VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Kremena V. Star, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Lynette M Sholl, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. RIGHT BREAST LUMPECTOMY: \u000aRIGHT EXCISION WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP. \u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA \u000aIN SITU AND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODES. \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE (Block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) \u000aMultifocal - No \u000aHistologic type - Lobular, see NOTE. \u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) (6 to 7 points) \u000aTubules - <10% (3 points) \u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate (2 points). Mitotic \u000acounts - 1 point \u000aExtensive intraductal component (EIC): Negative \u000aLymphovascular invasion (LVI) - Absent \u000aFinal Margins (invasive) \u000aNegative (> 0.3cm ) - superior, inferior, medial \u000aClose (0.1 to 0.3cm ) - lateral (0.1cm  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), posterior \u000a(0.2cm  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), anterior (0.2cm  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present \u000aTypes - Cribriform \u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent \u000aExtent of DCIS \u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks \u000aMargins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (> 0.3cm ) - Superior, inferior, medial, lateral, \u000aanterior \u000aClose (0.1 to 0.3cm ) - Posterior (0.1cm  blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present, see NOTE. \u000aLYMPH NODES \u000aSentinel lymph nodes - Negative (3 H&E levels examined) \u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0 \u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3 \u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia \u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) - Performed previously at BWH \u000aNOTE: \u000aImmunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following \u000astaining profile in lesional cells: \u000aNegative - e-cadherin \u000aThe immunohistochemical profile supports the above diagnosis. \u000aB. RIGHT SENTINEL NODE: \u000aPlease see part A. \u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests \u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance \u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the \u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the \u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such \u000aclearance or approval is not necessary. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None provided. \u000aOperation: Right lumpectomy after needle-localization; right sentinel node \u000abiopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Right breast lumpectomy, long suture - lateral; short - superior to \u000amammo. \u000aB/2) Right sentinel node biopsy for permanent section. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen with Ca++ wire, Ca++. OR called/ SR. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, labeled with the patient's name \u000aand MR number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast lumpectomy, long suture lateral, short superior to \u000amammo", consists of a lumpectomy specimen (7.3cm superior to inferior, 4.6cm \u000amedial to lateral, 2.5cm anterior to posterior). There is a wire entering \u000athis specimen from the anterior/inferior aspect. A long stitch designates the \u000alateral aspect of the specimen, and a short stitch designates superior aspect. \u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from inferior to superior to \u000areveal dense fibrosis throughout, and a small hemorrhagic area (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), located in the posterior lateral aspect of the specimen. A clip is \u000aidentified and removed. The entire specimen is submitted for histology. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Right breast lumpectomy, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contain the area marked with the clip. \u000aPart B, "#2. Right sentinel node biopsy for permanent section", consists of one \u000ayellow fragment of adipose tissue (12.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm ). Three candidate lymph \u000anodes are identified and entirely submitted for histology. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Right sentinel node biopsy, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aKST/mgd/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lynette M Sholl M.D., Electronically signed on Monday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 01,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12:54:43PM \u000a[report_end] 
