VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOGINO, SHUJI, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D. \u000a1) LEFT BREAST BIOPSY: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (blocks #1 and #4). \u000aSurgical resection margins are free of malignancy. \u000a2) LEFT BREAST BIOPSY, DESIGNATED "CORE BIOPSY CAVITY": \u000aBenign breast tissue with focal epithelial hyperplasia. \u000aApocrine metaplasia. \u000aSurgical margins are free of malignancy. \u000aNOTE: \u000aEvidence of a priopr biopsy is not seen (see NOTE below). \u000a3) LEFT BREAST BIOPSY, DESIGNATED "MASS": \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (block #20). \u000aApocrine metaplasia. \u000aSurgical margins are free of malignancy. \u000aNOTE: \u000aThese biopsies were performed to remove a myofobroblastoma previously diagnosed \u000aby core needle biopsy (BWH  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). The radiologic mass was not seen in \u000aspecimen radiography of all three specimens, and there were no gross \u000amass-forming lesions. There is no microscopic evidence of a biopsy site. \u000aClinical and radiologic correlation is suggested. \u000aThe case has been reviewed by Dr. S. Lester who concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Hx myofibroblastoma by core bx. \u000aOperation: L breast biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast mass. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000a1. L breast tissue - short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral. \u000a2. Left breast core biopsy cavity, sutures: long/lateral, short/superior. \u000a3. Left breast mass, long/lateral, short/superior. \u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: \u000a#1 & #2: No mass in specimen. Dr. E. Frost (EPF) \u000a#3: No clip in specimen. Dr. N. Smith (DNS) \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WU,DAVID,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, labeled with the patient's name \u000aand unit number. \u000aPart one, "#1", consists of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm  irregular, fibrofatty breast \u000atissue which has a short suture designating superior and a long suture \u000adesignating lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; \u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned to reveal a predominantly yellow lobulated fatty tissue admixed with \u000ascant thin white fibrous tissue in which a discrete lesion is not appreciated. \u000aRepresentative sections are submitted sequentially from superior to inferior. \u000aMicro 1: superior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 2: lateral margin to include posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 3: lateral margin to include anterior and posterior margins, 2 frags, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior medial margin, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro 6: inferior anterior margin, micro 1, RSS. \u000aMicro 7: inferior medial margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aPart two, "#2 left breast core biopsy cavity, suture marks long lateral, short \u000asuperior", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm  fibrofatty breast tissue with a \u000ashort suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The \u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral \u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to \u000alateral to reveal a yellow lobulated fatty tissue admixed with scant thin white \u000afibrous tissue in which a discrete mass is not appreciated. Representative \u000asections are submitted sequentially from lateral to medial. \u000aMicro 8: anterior lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior margin to include superior and inferior margins, 1 frag \u000aeach, ESS. \u000aMicro 11: lateral margin to include superior and inferior margin, 1 frag, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro 12: lateral margin to include inferior margin \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior margin to include lateral and medial aspects, 3 frags \u000atotal, RSS. \u000aMicro 15: posterior margin to include superior and inferior margins, 2 \u000afrags, ESS. \u000aPart three, "#3 left breast mass, short superior, long lateral", consists of \u000athree fibrofatty breast tissues in which the largest (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm ) has \u000abeen previously incised along the midline, bisecting the anterior, inferior, \u000aposterior aspects and has a short suture designating superior and a long suture \u000adesignating lateral. The larger tissue has been inked per pathology protocol \u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = \u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Sectioning the \u000alarger fragment reveals a predominantly yellow lobulated fatty tissue admixed \u000awith scant thin white fibrous tissue in which a discrete lesion is not \u000aappreciated. Representative sections are submitted sequentially from medial to \u000alateral. The additional breast tissues (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) are black-inked and serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable yellow \u000alobulated fatty tissue surface admixed with scant thin white fibrous tissue. \u000aRepresentative sections are submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire smallest breast tissue, 5 frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mid size breast tissue, 6 frags total, RSS. \u000aMicro 21: largest breast tissue, lateral margin to include inferior margin, \u000a2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 22: superior anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 23: posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 24: inferior margin to include the lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 25: medial anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000alm \u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
