VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Agoston Tony Agoston, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP: \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. \u000aCore needle biopsy site with gel pledgets, is present and is transected \u000aat the superior/medial margin. \u000aNote: The patient underwent a core needle biopsy for calcifications \u000ashowing ADH ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; 1/5/08). The clip marking this site was not seen in \u000athe specimen radiograph of this specimen or the subsequent superior margin \u000a(see below). The core needle biopsy has been transected between the two \u000aspecimens and, therefore, the clip may have been dislodged during surgery. \u000aClinical correlation is suggested. \u000aNo carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN: \u000aThe core needle biopsy site, with gel pledgets, is present at the old \u000amargin and is not present at the new margin. \u000aNote: No carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic examination of \u000athe specimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 59 year old post-menopausal woman with 3mm cluster of increasing \u000acalcifications on REMOVED_DATE mammogram in RUOQ. Core bx REMOVED_DATE = ADH. Previous \u000asurgery - BS-08- REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aOperation: R breast wire localized biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal R mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Right breast tissue, short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral, whip \u000astitch on chest wall margin --> mammo. \u000aB/2) Superior shaved margin, whip stitch on chest wall margin --> mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aSpecimen #1 - No clip present/wire intact. Discussed with Dr. Rhei by Dr. \u000aRitner. \u000aSpecimen #2 - No clip. DGS. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s \u000aname and medical record number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast tissue", consists of a wire localized breast excision \u000aspecimen (3.4cm SI, 3.0cm ML, 4.8cm AP) that is oriented with a short suture \u000adesignating superior, a long suture designating lateral, and a whipstitch \u000adesignating the chest wall margin/posterior. There is a wire entering on the \u000amedial aspect inferiorly and exiting on the medial aspect superiorly. The \u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. An accompanying radiograph demonstrates an intact wire with no \u000aclip present. There is a firm white fibrotic area (2.6cm SI, 2.2cm ML, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm AP) that abuts the superior, inferior, medial, lateral, and anterior \u000amargins, and is 0.5cm from the posterior margin. It contains the core biopsy \u000asite. The entire specimen is examined microscopically. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE frags per block, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin, 2 frags per block, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Serially sectioned specimen anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE frags per \u000ablock, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Superior shave margin", consists of a breast shave excision (3.5 x \u000a2.7cm  1.0cm SI) that is oriented with a whipstitch on a new superior margin \u000a(inked blue). The old margin is inked black. An accompanying radiograph shows \u000ano clip, and the case has been discussed with Dr. Rhei. There is a firm white \u000afibrotic area (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ) that abuts the old margin, and is 0.5cm \u000afrom the new margin. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entirely submitted specimen, REMOVED_DATE frags per block, ESS. \u000aTA/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a1/21/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
