emonstrates a tight cluster of calcifications adjacent to the \u000alocalization wire. The specimen was sectioned from medial to lateral and \u000aentirely submitted. The tissue consists of fibrous adipose tissue and the \u000acalcifications were localized to blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 5 frags, ESS (perpendicular) \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags each, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : wire localized sections with probable calcifications, 1 frag \u000aeach, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : lateral margin, 5 frags, ESS (perpendicular) \u000aPart B, was received in formalin and labeled "#2. New medial margin", and \u000aconsists of one piece of tan/pink tissue (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ). One surface of \u000athe tissue was inked orange by the surgeon. The new medial margin is re-inked \u000aorange, and the old surgical margin is inked black by the pathologist. The \u000aspecimen consists primarily of adipose tissue with no discreet lesions \u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : New Surgical margin, 3 frags, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : New surgical margin, 3 frags, ESS \u000aDM/cdm \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Derek K Marsee M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Derek K Marsee M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Derek K Marsee M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a7/13/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
