VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: George Lin, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY AND SENTINEL NODE \u000aBIOPSIES (Part A and Part C (including FSA): \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODES \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aTypes - Comedo, solid, cribriform, papillary, \u000aand clinging \u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present \u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent \u000aExtent of DCIS \u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks \u000aMargins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (> 0.3cm ) - Deep \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent \u000aLYMPH NODES \u000aSentinel lymph nodes - Negative (3 H&E levels examined) \u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0 \u000aNumber of nodes examined - 1 \u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia \u000aBiopsy cavity \u000aSkin with scar \u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) - Performed previously \u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY": \u000aBreast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia associated with \u000acalcifications and calcifications in benign epithelium. \u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change. \u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES" (including FSA): \u000aPlease see Part A. \u000aD. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, SKIN": \u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change. \u000aE. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, SKIN": \u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Hx of Hodgkin's with radiation CA Rt Brst. \u000aOperation: SNB Rt bilat mastex. \u000aOperative Findings: See op note. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: CA Rt Brst. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Right breast, short - superior, long - lateral 279 gm. \u000aB/2) Left breast, short - superior, long - lateral, 272 gm. \u000aC/3) Right sentinel lymph node - F.S. \u000aD/4) Right breast skin. \u000aE/5) Left breast skin. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "SENTINEL LYMPH NODE RIGHT" (INCLUDING FSA): \u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor. \u000aOR Consultation by: HEJIN P. HAHN, M.D., PH.D. \u000aResident: Agoston T. Agoston, M.D., PH.D. \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimens are received fresh in five parts, labeled with the patient's name \u000aand medical record number. \u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right breast, short-superior, long-lateral", consists of a \u000aright mastectomy specimen (270.0 g, 14.0cm medial to lateral, 12.0cm superior \u000ato inferior, and 3.8cm deep) with skin ellipse (8.0 x 2.2cm ), and everted \u000anipple (0.7cm in diameter x 0.4cm in height) with areola (2.3cm in \u000adiameter). The axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm  On the skin ellipse \u000aare two sutures with short designating superior and long designating lateral. \u000aOn the skin, there is a scar (1.4cm ) located 3.0cm lateral to nipple and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm to the nearest skin edge. No muscle is grossly identified. The deep margin \u000ais inked blue. Sectioning the specimen reveals an ill-defined fibrous area \u000a(2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm ) located in the lower outer aspect of the specimen, deep to \u000athe skin scar. The fibrous area comes to 0.2cm from the deep margin. No \u000aother mass lesions are grossly identified. No lymph nodes are grossly \u000aidentified. The breast tissue is approximately 5% fibrous and 95% adipose \u000atissue. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin scar, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous area deep to scar, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Axillary tail, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left breast, short-superior, long-lateral", consists of a \u000aleft mastectomy specimen (234.0 g, 12.0cm medial to lateral, 11.0cm superior \u000ato inferior, and 3.5cm deep) with skin ellipse (6.0 x 2.5cm ), and everted \u000anipple (0.8cm in diameter x 0.6cm in height) with areola (1.8cm in \u000adiameter). The axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.8cm  No muscle is \u000agrossly identified. The deep margin is inked blue. Sectioning the specimen \u000areveals no mass lesions. The breast parenchyma is approximately 5% fibrous and \u000a95% adipose tissue. In the same container is a separate fragment of \u000afibroadipose tissue (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ). No lymph nodes are grossly \u000aidentified in either the mastectomy specimen or separate fragment of \u000afibroadipose tissue. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Axillary tail, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Separate fragment of fibroadipose tissue, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Sentinel lymph node right", consists of a fragment of \u000apink/yellow soft tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ). The specimen is bisected and \u000aentirely submitted for frozen section as FSA. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Frozen section remnant A, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart D, labeled "#4. Right breast skin", consists of a skin ellipse (23.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm x 0.4cm deep with two fresh incisions measuring 6.5cm and 6.8cm ). The \u000a6.5cm incision is surrounded by blue dye and comes to 0.1cm to the nearest \u000askin edge. The 6.8cm incision comes to 0.3cm to nearest skin edge. Deep \u000aaspect of the specimen is inked blue. Representative sections are submitted \u000afor histologic evaluation. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 6.5cm incision with dye, multi frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 6.8cm incision, multi frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Tips, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart E, labeled "#5. Left breast skin", consists of a skin ellipse (11.3 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) which has the center portion excised in another elliptical shape (8.7 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) such that the inner aspect of the ellipse has been excised. The specimen \u000ais 0.5cm deep. The skin portion varies in width from REMOVED_DATE to 2.0cm  On one \u000aaspect of the ellipse, there is a fresh incision (5.0cm in length) on the \u000aportion of skin that measures 2.0cm in width. The incision comes to 0.5cm to \u000anearest skin edge. Representative sections are submitted for histologic \u000aevaluation. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Incision site, 5 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Portion of skin ellipse opposite portion with incision, 7 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Tips, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aGL/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
