VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR TWO MASSES: \u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA (blocks 6 and 7; levels examined). See note. \u000aIntramammary lymph node. \u000aNOTE: The area of ADH closely approaches a diagnosis of DCIS but is \u000adifficult to evaluate due to crush artifact. This area is close to \u000aan inked margin. Re-excision may be helpful to exclude an adjacent \u000aarea of DCIS. \u000aOne of the radiologic masses correlates with the lymph node. The \u000aill defined density may correlate with the dense area of stroma \u000aassociated with the ADH. \u000a(This case was reviewed by Dr. James Connolly and Dr. Susan Lester \u000awho concur with this interpretation.) \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 66 year old postmenopausal female not on ERT with RUOQ density on \u000a12/11/02 mammogram. 4mm solid lesion on ultrasound. Not amenable to core \u000abiopsy. \u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized biopsy \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast tissue \u000aRADIOLOGY: Masses in specimen. SK/JMS. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HASKELL,HENRY D.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received in one part, labeled with the patient's name, unit \u000anumber and #1. right breast tissue", and consists of three fragments of breast \u000atissue (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ). The \u000aspecimen is not oriented. Despite the fragmented nature of the specimen, all \u000afragments are inked black (these do not necessarily represent true margins). \u000aSectioning of the tissue reveals unremarkable breast tissue (approximately 80% \u000afat). The entire specimen is examined histologically. \u000aThe specimen radiograph reveals a lobulated density and a second ill defined \u000adensity at the tip of the localization wire. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  largest frag, 2 frags each, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  second largest fragment, 5 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  smallest fragment, 1 frag each, ESS \u000ahdh \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
