ived. Special studies \u000awere performed at the referring institution and reviewed at BWH show the \u000afollowing immunostaining profile in the lesion: \u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR - POSITIVE \u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR - POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /NEU - NEGATIVE (1+) \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 51 year old woman with stereotactic core needle biopsies for right \u000abreast calcifications. Block D contains the cores with calcifications. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by O'CONNELL,FIONNUALA,M.B.B.C.H.,B.A.O. \u000aReceived from Mazen Duwaji, M.D., Department of Pathology, Caritas Norwood \u000aHospital, 800 Washington Street, Norwood, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  are sixteen (16) slides \u000alabeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", sublabeled "A level 2", "A level 4", "B level 2", "B level \u000a4", C level 2", "C level 4", "D", "D recut 1", "D recut 2", "D recut 3". "D \u000alevel 2" through "D level 5", and "E level 2", "E level 4", corresponding to \u000aright breast obtained on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology \u000areport bearing the patient's name. \u000aReports to: \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST \u000a[report_end] 
