VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOGINO, SHUJI, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D. \u000a#1. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS: \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aFlorid ductal epithelial hyperplasia. \u000aIntraductal papilloma. \u000aApocrine metaplasia. \u000aMultiple cysts (up to 0.3cm ). \u000aSclerosing adenosis. \u000aThere is no evidence of invasive carcinoma or DCIS in the specimen, \u000aincluding the margins. \u000aNOTE: There is an intraductal papilloma with stromal sclerosis in the region of \u000athe mammographic density. \u000a#2. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aFlorid ductal epithelial hyperplasia. \u000aApocrine metaplasia. \u000aCalcifications are associated with benign breast epithelium. \u000aCompelx sclerosing lesion and sclerosing adenosis. \u000aMultiple cysts. \u000aCalcifications in the media of muscular artery. \u000aThere is no evidence of invasive carcinoma or DCIS in the specimen, \u000aincluding the margins. \u000aNOTES for both part #1 and #2: Levels were examined on blocks #5 and #11. \u000aSelected slides (#5, 11, 24, 28) have been reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast \u000aPathology Division. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 59 year old female with right breast 9:00 axis 1.3cm solid mass by \u000aU/S for which biopsy is recommended. Left breast UOQ 3mm punctate \u000acalcifications for which patient prefers excision. \u000aOperation: Bilateral wire localization excision \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass, left breast abnormal mammogram \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right breast wire excision \u000a#2) Left breast wire excision \u000aRADIOLOGY: Right specimen: Mass and wire. \u000aLeft specimen: Calcifications and wire. \u000aCalled to OR. Mylins Hughs. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KINDELBERGER,DAVID W.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right breast wire excision", consists of a single \u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (4.5cm from lateral to medial x 3.5cm \u000asuperior to inferior x 1.2cm anterior to posterior). There is metal \u000alocalizing wire embedded within the specimen. The specimen was inked by the \u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = \u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; \u000amedial = orange. The breast tissue approximately 60% fibrous and 40% adipose. \u000aThere are numerous small cysts measuring up to 0.1cm in diameter. There is a \u000asmall hemorrhagic focus (0.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.1cm ) corresonding to the location of \u000athe localizing wire. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral \u000aand entirely submitted for histologic analysis. Accompanying radiograph shows a \u000amass around the wire. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue, mult frags, ESS (the position of the \u000alocalizing wire corresponds to #3 and 4) \u000aPart two, labeled "#2. left breast wire excision", consists of a single \u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue measuring 7cm lateral to medial x 6.5cm \u000asuperior to inferior x 2.0cm anterior to posterior. There is a metal \u000alocalizing wire embedded within the specimen. The specimen was inked by the \u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = \u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; \u000amedial = orange. The breast tissue is approximately 40% fibrous and 60% \u000aadipose tissue. There is a focal area of fresh hemorrhage (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ) \u000acorresponding to the location of the localizing wire. No other lesions are \u000agrossly identified. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely sections \u000aare submitted for histologic analysis. Accompanying radiograph shows \u000acalcifications around the wire. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue, mult frags, ESS (#12-16, 23, 29 correspond \u000ato areas adjacent to the localizing wire) \u000adk \u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
