m the lateral \u000amargin, 3.2cm from the anterior margin, 2.0cm from the posterior margin, 1cm \u000afrom the superior margin and 1.6cm from the inferior margin. The remainder of \u000athe specimen consists of grossly unremarkable yellow/white, fibroadipose \u000atissue. There is an accompanying specimen radiograph, which demonstrates a \u000aclip and calcifications in the specimen. Representative sections, including \u000athe entire mass, are submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior and inferior margins, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice containing mass (mass in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Next slice also containing mass with mass in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 5 frags, \u000a` ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional representative sections, including possible \u000abiopsy site, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000amah/MMM \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Marian H Harris M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a5/3/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
