VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST BIOPSY: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, focally bordering on low grade ductal \u000acarcinoma in situ, present in 2 of 4 blocks (#1, #2) with marked cautery \u000aartifact, and extending to within 0.1cm of inked, cauterized margins. \u000aFibrocystic changes, proliferative. \u000aMicrocalcifications are present in association with benign ducts. \u000aNo invasive tumor. \u000aNOTE: The tissue shows extensive cautery and processing artifact which makes \u000ainterpretation of the atypical ductal changes difficult. However, in block #1 \u000aand #2 several ducts have features that are atypical and approach low grade \u000aductal carcinoma in situ. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aOperation: Left breast needle directed bx. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Calcifications left breast. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast mass. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1. LEFT BREAST TISSUE MASS": \u000aNo areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma. \u000aRADIOLOGY: The mass is in the specimen. \u000aC. DENISON M.D \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by MANTEL,MICHELLE HAVA,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in the frozen section, in one part, labelled \u000awith the patient's name, unit number and "left breast tissue mass", consists of \u000atwo fragments of unoriented yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x1.5cm  with needle localization wire in place. Cut \u000asection of yellow adipose tissue and left fibrous breast tissue, with no areas \u000agrossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma. The specimen is inked in black. \u000aMicros #1-4: Breast biopsy, multiple frags, ESS. \