0aNOTE: The invasive carcinoma and DCIS are adjacent to the prior biopsy site. \u000aThe smaller focus of invasion is distinct from the biopsy site and appears to \u000abe a separate area of invasion. Biopsy site changes are extensively present at \u000athe medial and deep margins. Cautery artefact at these margins makes them \u000adifficult to evaluate. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Cancer of right breast for re-excision and sentinel node bx. \u000aOperation: Re-excision right breast, sentinel node biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast ca. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Sentinel node right breast. \u000a2. Axillary contents, right. \u000a3. Tumor site right breast. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SHEN,JIAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1, sentinel node, right breast", is a yellow-tan \u000afibroadipose tissue fragment (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm ) containing four (4) potential \u000alymph nodes (largest being 0.8cm in diameter), which are entirely submitted. \u000aMicro 1: sentinel lymph node, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2, axillary contents, right", are multiple fragments of \u000ayellow-tan fibroadipose tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm in aggregate), which \u000acontains five (5) potential lymph nodes (ranging in size from 0.2cm to 0.4cm \u000ain diameter), which are entirely submitted. \u000aMicro 2: 5 potential lymph nodes, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aPart three, labeled "#3, tumor site, right breast", is a fragment of \u000afibroadipose tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ) with an attached skin ellipse (3.5 x \u000a0.5cm ). There is a well-healed surgical scar (1.5cm ) which is present on the \u000asurface of the skin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; \u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Cross sectioning of the \u000aspecimen reveals multiple areas of fibrosis (0.5cm to 0.9cm in diameter). \u000aThe entire specimen is submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  specimen from superior to inferior, 1 frag per cass., ESS. \u000ajis \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
