ins \u000amultiple cylindrical fibrofatty soft tissues (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm in aggregate). \u000aThe specimen is submitted in toto. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Contents of pink cassette labeled "A CA++", multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Contents of pink cassette labeled "B", multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "left breast site #2", consists of green cassettes, one labeled \u000a"A CA++" containing multiple cylindrical fibrofatty soft tissues (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.3cm in aggregate). The second green cassette is labeled "B" and contains \u000amultiple cylindrical fibrofatty soft tissues (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm in aggregate). \u000aThe specimen is submitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Contents of green cassette labeled "A CA++", multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Contents of green cassette labeled "B", multi frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000ajc/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 17,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11:51:27AM \u000a[report_end] 
