u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet \u000abeen determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor \u000acells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but \u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive. \u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity \u000ain >10% of tumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational \u000ause only. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: History of left breast, core biopsy REMOVED_MONTH 30th; tumor is ER positive \u000aPR positive, Her-2 neu positive. \u000aOperation: Left mammographical directed biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue (short stitch = superior margin, \u000along stitch = lateral margin). \u000aRadiology: Mass in specimen. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by IAFRATE,ANTHONY JOHN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one (1) part, labeled with the patient's \u000aname, unit number, and "left breast tissue, short stitch = superior, long \u000astitch = lateral", and consists of a single fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose \u000atissue (7.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 3.2cm ), with a single localization wire in place, and two \u000a(2) orienting sutures, a short suture designating superior, and a long suture \u000adesignating lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; \u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. A firm, white fibrotic \u000amass (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ) is identified. It is located 0.2cm from the green \u000ainked margin, 0.6cm from the red inked margin, 2cm from the yellow and \u000aorange inked margins, 1.1cm from the black inked margin, and 1.2cm from the \u000ablue inked margin. The remainder of the tissue consists of approximately 10% \u000awhite fibrous tissue, and 90% unremarkable adipose tissue. Adjacent to the \u000amass is an approximate 0.5cm area of hemorrhage, consistent with recent needle \u000abiopsy. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor and closest green and red margins, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 3 : tumor and black margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 4 : lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 5 : medial margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 6 : anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 7 : lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 8 : uninvolved breast tissue, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
