 = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Sectioning reveals a \u000acentral area of old hemorrhage, fibrosis and fat necrosis, grossly consistent \u000awith prior biopsy/excision site, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.8cm  The distances \u000aof this area to the nearest margins are as follows: 0.2cm to medial, 1.5cm \u000ato lateral, 0.3cm to inferior, 0.4cm to superior, less than 0.1cm to \u000aanterior and 0.3cm to posterior. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is \u000acomposed of almost exclusively lobulated adipose tissue without any additional \u000alesions. \u000aMicro 1&2: biopsy site and nearest medial margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 3: biopsy site and nearest lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 4: biopsy site and nearest inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 5: biopsy site and nearest superior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 6&7: biopsy site and nearest anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 8&9: biopsy site and nearest posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 10&11: additional representative biopsy site, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 12: representative uninvolved breast, 1 frag, RSS. \u000apj \u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
