VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: J. GREGORY KANE M.D. \u000aCASE: BG-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Elgida Radoncipi, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA) S/L "WIRE LOCALIZED RIGHT BREAST LESION, LONG LATERAL, SHORT SUPERIOR: \u000aPapilloma with focal atypical ductal hyperplasia confined to the \u000apapilloma, and associated microcalcifications. \u000aCysts, hyperplasia. \u000aBiopsy site changes. \u000aB) S/L "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE MEDIAL TO SPECIMEN #1, SUTURE ON ASPECT CLOSE TO \u000aSPECIMEN #1: \u000aBenign breast tissue with biopsy site changes. \u000aC) "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE INFERIOR TO SPECIMEN #1": \u000aCysts, florid hyperplasia and associated calcifications. \u000aBiopsy site changes. \u000aD) S/L "TISSUE FROM DIRECTLY UNDERNEATH NIPPLE" \u000aBenign breast tissue. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Microcalcifications and nodule right breast shows core - papilloma \u000awith atypia. Excision advised. \u000aOperation: Right wire localized breast resection \u000aOperative Findings: Nodular around wire \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast intraductal papilloma. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA. Wire localized right breast lesion (mass and calcifications adjacent to wire \u000asegment) long stitch lateral, short superior (to mammo) \u000aB. Right breast tissue medial to specimen #1 - suture on aspect closest \u000aC. Right breast tissue inferior to specimen #1 to specimen #1 \u000aD. Tissue from directly underneath nipple \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in four parts, each labeled with the patient's name \u000aand unit number. \u000aPart A, "#1.wire localized right breast lesion - long lat, short sup", consist \u000aof one fragment of yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring 6.1cm from medial to \u000alateral margin, 2.2cm from anterior to posterior margin, and 0.8cm from \u000asuperior to inferior margin. There is a short suture designating as superior \u000aand a long suture designating as lateral, per surgeon. The specimen is inked \u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. \u000aThere is a wire that enters the lateral margin and exits the posterior margin. \u000aThere is an attached mammogram showing a lesion that is close to the superior, \u000aposterior and inferior margins. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal \u000athe clip measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm abutting the posterior and inferior \u000amargin and is 0.2cm from the superior margin, 1.1cm from the anterior margin \u000aand greater than 1.0cm from the medial and lateral margin. No other gross \u000alesions are identified. The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral, posterior, superior and inferior margins, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Clip, anterior, posterior, superior and inferior margins, 2 frags, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior, posterior, superior and inferior margins, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior, posterior, superior and inferior margins, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior, posterior, superior, inferior and medial margins, 2 frags, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. R breast tissue medial to specimen #1, suture on aspect close to \u000aspecimen #1", consists of one fragment of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.8 x 0.8cm  There is a stitch designated as aspect closest to specimen #1, \u000aper surgeon. Half of the specimen closest to stitch is inked blue, and the \u000aother half is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal one \u000afocal discoloration measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm that abuts the blue-inked \u000amargin. The specimen is entirely submitted. There is an accompanying \u000aradiograph showing no lesion pacification. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Stitch half perpendicular section, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : lesional tissue, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Right breast tissue medial to specimen #1, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Black-inked margin, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aPart C, "#3. R breast tissue inferior to specimen #1", consists of one fragment \u000aof yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  The specimen is \u000aunoriented and entirely inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to \u000areveal a white cystic nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm abutting the margins. \u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Right breast tissue inferior to specimen #1, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Cyst, right breast tissue inferior to specimen #1, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart D, "#4. Tissue from directly underneath nipple", consists of one fragment \u000aof skin punch biopsy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm in depth. The specimen is \u000abisected and entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Tissue from directly underneath nipple, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aER:lc \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aWednesday August 12,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01:36:11PM \u000a[report_end] 
