ADIOLOGY: Ca++ and wire in specimen. (no signature on form) \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SMOUSE,JASON H.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the \u000apatient's name, unit number and "#1 tissue from left breast DCIS site, stitch: \u000along - lateral, short = superior", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.2cm portion \u000aof fibrofatty breast tissue and overlying tan skin ellipse (5.0 x 2.2cm ), a \u000alocalization wire, and accompanying radiograph and two sutures designated by \u000athe surgeon (long - lateral and short - superior). The specimen is received \u000apreviously inked according to pathology protocol for the evaluation of \u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; \u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. There is a 3.7cm in length, well-healed, \u000alinear scar on the skin ellipse which is at the nearest radial margin. The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral revealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.5cm  tan/white, indurated, ill-defined mass which is 0.5cm from the \u000aposterior margin, 0.9cm from the superior margin, 1.1cm from the anterior \u000amargin, 1.6cm from the inferior margin, 2cm from the medial margin and \u000agreater than 3.5cm from the lateral margin. Just lateral and anterior to the \u000amass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm  ill-defined, focally hemorrhagic focus with fat \u000anecrosis (? previous excision/biopsy site) which is subjacent to the \u000aaforementioned skin scar. This area comes to within 0.4cm of the posterior \u000amargin, 1.5cm of the superior margin, 1.6cm of the inferior margin and is at \u000aleast 2.5cm from the medial and lateral margins. The remaining breast tissue \u000aconsists of approximately equal amounts of yellow/tan, lobulated fat and \u000atan/white, focally cystic, dense fibrous stroma. The entire mass (probable \u000aprevious biopsy site and area of calcifications [corresponding with \u000aradiograph]) is submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast mass in relationship to margin, sequentially from medial to \u000alateral, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  probable previous biopsy/excision site to include relationship \u000awith all margins (submitted from medial to lateral), multi frags, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro 24: representative lateral margin nearest biopsy site, 2 frags, RSS. \u000adfi \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
