e (7.2 x 3.4cm ). \u000aThe upper middle portion of the breast has a semi-solid area (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) that was previously tatooed by the surgeon. This area is 1.8cm from the \u000askin surface and 2.8cm from the deep margin. The remaining breast parenchyma \u000aconsist of approximately 60% of white/tan fibrous tissue and approximately 40% \u000aof yellow/tan adipose tissue. The skin, nipple (1.2cm in diameter), and areola \u000a(2.2cm in diamter) are grossly unremarkable. Grossly, no skeletal muscle is \u000aidentified. One pink/tan lymph node (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ) is identified and \u000asubmitted. No other lesions are identified in the specimen. \u000aMicro 3: One bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Firm area and surrounding tatooed area, 6 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 10: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 11: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 12: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 13: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 14: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aPart 3, "Superior piece of breast", consists of a fragment of unoriented \u000awhite/yellow/tan soft tissue (6.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ). The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Superior breast tissue, 4 frags, ESS. \u000amjy \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
