o  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential bisected cross section, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential bisected cross section, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential bisected cross section, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential bisected cross section, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin, radially,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  multi frags,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Superior shave margin, stitch on new margin", consists of a \u000aportion of fibrofatty tissue (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm ), with a suture on one side, \u000adesignating the new margin. This new margin is inked blue, and the opposite \u000amargin is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal 95% \u000adense white fibrous tissue and 5% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no \u000adiscrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen radiograph reveals dense \u000atissue, without a specific lesion. The fibrous tissue extends to both the \u000ablue inked new margin and opposite black inked margin. The specimen is \u000asequentially submitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 unoriented end, radially, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags each;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : \u000a1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Opposite unoriented end, radially, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000acp/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a11/9/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
