r, long stitch \u000alateral, whipstitch on chest wall margin", and consists of a wire localized \u000aexcisional breast biopsy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.7cm with three stitches \u000adesignating the superior, lateral, and chest wall margins. A wire is present \u000ain the specimen. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates an area of \u000acentral hyperlucency adjacent to the wire and associated with a clip. The \u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. The lateral and medial aspects of the specimen were removed and \u000arepresentatively submitted as perpendicular sections. The remaining tissue is \u000aserially sectioned from lateral to medial such that the lateral aspect of the \u000aspecimen is represented in slice #1 and that the final medial margin is \u000arepresented in slice #11. Sectioning demonstrates a predominantly tan/white \u000afirm cut surface likely representing fibrosis or fibroadenoma which appears to \u000aabut the inferior margin, superior margin, and anterior margin. A clip is \u000aidentified in the specimen in slices #9 and #10 contain an area of tan/pink \u000afirm tissue, focal area of hemorrhage present in slice #9 and potentially \u000arepresents prior biopsy sites. All of the fibrous breast tissue is submitted \u000afor histological evaluation. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of slice #4 to include area of tan/white \u000afibrous nodule to green ink, blue ink, and red ink, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #9, trisected to include green, red, blue, black inks, 1 \u000afrag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #10, trisected, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6 partially sectioned to include an area of focal hemorrhage, \u000a1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #10, partially fragmented tissue, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, bisected, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, bisected, 1 frag per cassette, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Portion of slice #6 to include anterior/posterior/inferior margins, \u000a1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7 bisected, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional section of slice #4, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aSRK/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a6/30/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
