000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by prosector). Two \u000alocalizing wires enter the superolateral aspect of the specimen and at least \u000aone of the wires exits the inferior/anterior medial aspect of the specimen. \u000aThe specimen is received with a radiograph demonstrating the localizing wires \u000ain place adjacent to a clip and a focus of calcifications. Sectioning \u000ademonstrates a central hematoma (at least REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm ), with central \u000acavitation and chalky white fragments of foreign material compatible with \u000aGelfoam beads. The hematoma itself approaches within 0.2cm of the closest \u000asuperior margin, 0.2cm of the closest posterior margin, 0.4cm from the \u000aclosest lateral margin, 0.7cm from the closest inferior margin, 1.2cm from \u000athe closest medial margin, and 1.2cm from the closest anterior margin. There \u000aare no obvious masses, lesions, or other abnormalities grossly. The entire \u000aspecimen is submitted, sequentially from medial to lateral. The remaining \u000aspecimen is predominantly comprised of tan/yellow, focally hemorrhagic adipose \u000atissue. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen, sequentially from medial to lateral, with \u000aperpendicular medial margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and perpendicular lateral margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , multi frags, ESS. \u000aThe tissue of interest (tissue containing clip) is located in micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (section \u000awith clip) through approximately  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000adb/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a7/5/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
