VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Andrew G. Evans, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present \u000aTypes - Solid, cribriform \u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present \u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent \u000aExtent of DCIS \u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks \u000aMargins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (> 0.3cm ) - Medial, superior, anterior, posterior \u000aClose (0.1 to 0.3cm ) - Inferior (o.2cm  focal, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) \u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - Lateral (extensive, blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent \u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - Tis (DCIS) NX MX \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) - Pending \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 81 year old female with a history of a  REMOVED_CASE_ID  L breast biopsy, revealing \u000aLCIS and ADH. REMOVED_DATE mammogram demonstrates right lower/inner posterior \u000acalcifications not amenable to core biopsy. \u000aOperation: R breast wire localized biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal R mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) rt needle loc br tissue - short/sup, long/lateral, whip/chest wall margin. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aSpecimen contains the wire and calcifications. The OR was called by Dr. Latham \u000aat 11:00 am. RPL. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "Rt needle localization bx", and consists of an irregular fragment of \u000afibroadipose tissue (7.2cm M-L x 3.2cm S-I x 1.5cm A-P) with a short suture \u000adesignating superior, long suture designating lateral, and a whip stitch \u000adesignating chest wall margin per surgeon. The specimen is previously inked \u000aper pathology protocol, the specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; \u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is \u000areceived with a radiograph demonstrating a needle localization wire, which \u000aenters the inferior aspect of the specimen and exits through the superior \u000aaspect of the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned to exhibit 30% \u000awhite fibrous tissue to 70% yellow lobulated adipose tissue. No definitive \u000amasses or lesions can be grossly appreciated. The area of the needle \u000alocalization wire is slightly irregular and abuts the lateral margin. The \u000aspecimen is submitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Perpendicular lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast parenchyma sequentially submitted from lateral to medial \u000ato include area of interest ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), 1 frag in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Perpendicular medial margin, multi frags total, ESS. \u000ajc/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000aMonday August 17,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02:39:25PM \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for DCIS (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) NEGATIVE (1+) \u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following \u000acriteria: \u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the \u000acarcinoma is reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not \u000ayet been determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a \u000aportion of the membrane is positive. \u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of \u000atumor cells or moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in < 30% \u000aof tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% \u000aof tumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity. \u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests \u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance \u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the \u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the \u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such \u000aclearance or approval is not necessary. \u000aAddendum #1 by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aWednesday August 19,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02:57:48PM \u000a[report_end] 
