000aNo gross lesions identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Rt breast inferior margin, whip-stitch new margin", \u000aconsists of a concave portion of yellow/pink fibroadipose tissue (4.6 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.5cm ) with a whip-stitch along one surface designating "new margin" per the \u000asurgeon. The surface marked by the whip-stitch is inked blue and the opposing \u000aconcave, focally fibrotic/hemorrhagic surface (non-true margin) is inked black. \u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned, exhibiting predominantly fibrotic/focally \u000anecrotic, hemorrhagic tissue abutting the non-true margin and focally extending \u000ato the new margin. There is scant yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue. No \u000aother gross lesions identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast tissue, multi frags, ESS. \u000aDFI/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aMonday REMOVED_MONTH 21,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06:16:59PM \u000a[report_end] 
