graph which demonstrates a wire, clip and \u000aan ill-defined lesion with possible areas of microcalcification. Sectioning \u000areveals approximately 90% firm white fibrous tissue, with no obvious lesions. \u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aThe specimen is inked as follows: superior red, inferior green, anterior blue, \u000aposterior black, medial orange, lateral yellow. \u000aMicro sections: \u000aMicro 1: medial margin, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tissue submitted medial to lateral including superior inferior \u000aanterior and posterior margins, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 4: lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, "ECC", consists of hemorrhagic tan/pink tissue (0.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.1cm in \u000aaggregate). The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro 5: ECC, ESS. \u000aPart three, "EMC", consists of hemorrhagic tan soft tissue (2 x 2 x 0.4cm ). \u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  EMC, multiple frags, ESS. \u000aReports to: REILLY, RAYMOND, JOHN, M.B.B.C.H. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: ENDOCERVICAL CURETTINGS (ECC) OR BIOPSY \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: ENDOMETRIAL CURETTINGS (EMC) OR BIOPSY \u000a[report_end] 
