VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHARINE CARTER M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Marian H Harris, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, 9:00, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR AN ILL-DEFINED MASS AND A CLIP: \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (e.g. blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aColumnar cell change. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aEctatic lactiferous sinuses with periductal chronic inflammation. \u000aBiopsy site changes. \u000aNote: No invasive carcinoma or DCIS are seen after complete microscopic \u000aevaluation of the specimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: History of right mastitis during winter with mass at 9:00 by \u000aultrasound core biopsy REMOVED_DATE  This showed ectatic ducts and epithelial \u000ahyperplasia; there was question of radiologic/pathologic discordance. Patient \u000adeveloped hematoma from core biopsy - follow-up ultrasound REMOVED_DATE showed \u000ahematoma. Repeat follow-up mammograms and ultrasound REMOVED_DATE showed persistent \u000aabnormality by ultrasound - probably related to scarring, but wire localization \u000aexcisional right breast biopsy recommended to exclude malignancy. \u000aOperation: Right mammographically-directed breast biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass. Clip is felt to be right under skin and \u000amay not be with excised breast tissue. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) right peri-areolar tissue at 9 o'clock., short=superior, long=lateral. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aMass and clip in specimen (specimen US radiograph) - OR called. Dr. Twohig. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number, \u000aand "#1 - right breast tissue at 9:00, short suture/superior, long \u000asuture/lateral", and consists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to tan/white \u000afibroadipose tissue (6.4 f-i x REMOVED_DATE m-l x REMOVED_DATE a-pcm ), which is oriented per \u000asurgeon with two sutures as indicated. The specimen is inked per pro-sector \u000aaccording to the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. The specimen radiograph shows an ill-defined density traversed \u000aby the wire and a clip. The needle localization wire enters the inferior \u000aaspect of the specimen and exits the anterior aspect of the specimen. The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior into a total of \u000afifteen slices (slice one=superior, slice fifteen=inferior). In slices six \u000athrough ten there is an ill-defined, dense, white/pink, gritty fibrous lesion \u000a(1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ) traversed by the needle localization wire. The lesion \u000aexhibits multiple foci of hemorrhage (0.1-0.8cm in greatest dimension) and a \u000afew small simple cysts (ranging from REMOVED_DATE 4cm in greatest dimension) filled \u000awith clear serous fluid with adjacent areas of gritty yellow/tan fat necrosis. \u000aThe lesion comes to within 0.2cm of the posterior margin, 0.3cm of the \u000aanterior margin, 0.9cm of the medial margin, 1.0cm of the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the inferior margin, and 2.1cm of the superior margin. The clip is \u000aidentified within the tissue adjacent to the lesion in slice ten. \u000aThe remainder of the specimen is composed of approximately 80% dense white/tan \u000afibrous stroma and 20% yellow/tan adipose tissue. \u000aThe entire specimen is examined microscopically. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : ill-defined lesion sequentially submitted from superior to \u000ainferior (slices six through ten, respectively), clip \u000aidentified within tissue in Block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , including medial, \u000alateral, anterior and posterior margins, 1 frag in each, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slices three and four, superior margin closest to lesion, 2 \u000afrags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slices thirteen and fourteen, inferior margin closest to \u000alesion with dense fibrous stroma, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : remainder of tissue, mult frags, ESS. \u000almb/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a5/17/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
