 from the posterior margin, 1.2cm from the \u000asuperior margin, 2.2cm from the inferior margin, 0.5cm from the medial margin \u000aand 1.1cm from the lateral margin. There is an additional linear hemorrhage \u000a1.4cm in length inferior to the hemorrhagic cavity. The specimen was \u000asubmitted in its entirety in sections from medial to lateral. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen from medial to lateral, 20 frags, ESS \u000aNOTE: The hemorrhagic cavity is contained in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aThe linear hemorrhagic area is contained within cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aEUB/cdm \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Edilberto G Bauza M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a8/15/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
