VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, focally severe, arising in a background \u000acolumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions. \u000aCalcifications associated with atypical ductal hyperplasia and columnar \u000aalteration. \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread into ducts is also \u000apresent. \u000aFocus of sclerosing adenosis (block 5). Immunohistochemistry for p63 \u000aconfirms the presence of myoepithelial cells. \u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION, SPECIMEN LABELED "SUPERIOR BREAST TISSUE": \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia arising in columnar alteration of lobules with \u000aprominent snouts and secretions. \u000aThis case has been seen by Dr. A. Richardson, who concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 56 yo perimenopausal female, not on hormones, whose REMOVED_DATE \u000amammograms demonstrate LUOQ calcifications for which biopsy is \u000arecommended, which are not amenable to core biopsy. \u000aOperation: L breast wire localization excision. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal L mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Needle directed left breast tissue. Long lateral, \u000ashort superior, whip chest wall. \u000a2. Superior breast tissue (left). \u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcs in specimen. OR called. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HASKELL,HENRY D.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two containers, each labeled with the \u000apatient's name and unit number. \u000aThe first is further labeled "#1 left breast tissue". Received, previously \u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; \u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = \u000aorange, is a wire localized lumpectomy specimen (medial to lateral 4.5cm  \u000ainferior to superior 4.5cm  posterior to anterior 2.2cm ). No discrete nodule \u000aor mass lesion is found within the specimen. A specimen radiograph is \u000aperformed and all parts of the specimen containing radiographically evident \u000acalcification are submitted for histology. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  areas of calcification, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 14: inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aThe second part is labeled "#2 superior breast tissue left". Received fresh is \u000aan unoriented lump of breast tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm ). The surgical \u000amargin is inked black. The specimen is entirely submitted. The breast \u000aparenchyma contains no suspicious lesions. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior breast tissue left, 2 frags each, ESS. \u000ahdh \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
