rgin) and an adjacent area \u000aof numerous calcifications throughout the midportion of the specimen. The \u000aspecimen has been inked by the surgeon according to protocol for the evaluation \u000aof margins: black = posterior, blue = anterior, medial = orange, lateral = \u000ayellow, superior = red, inferior = green. There is a clip in a 1 x 1cm \u000aill-defined firm area of tissue that abuts the superior margin. The remainder \u000aof the specimen consists of predominantly fatty tissue with interspersed \u000astrands of fibrous tissue. No other gross lesions are present. The entire \u000aspecimen is submitted for microscopic examination sequentially from the lateral \u000amargin to the medial margin. \u000aCass REMOVED_DATE  Lateral margin, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aCass 3: Area of clip, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aCass REMOVED_DATE  Sequential sections from lateral to medial, 8 frags, ESS. \u000aCass REMOVED_DATE  Medial margin, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a1/7/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
