; \u000amedial/orange. The needle localization wire enters at the anteromedial aspect \u000aand exits superiorly. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to \u000amedial, revealing approximately 75% tan/white dense focally nodular fibrous \u000astroma admixed with 25% yellow lobulated adipose tissue. As confirmed by the \u000aaccompanying radiograph, two foci of calcification are present within the \u000aspecimen as well as the presence of a hookwire within the specimen. No other \u000agross lesions are identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast tissue, sequentially from lateral to medial, multiple \u000afrags, ESS. \u000aNote: Foci of calcification predominantly within  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as well as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000athrough  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aDFI/elw \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a3/30/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aImmunoperoxidase stains for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID / REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /p63 show the presence of basal cells. \u000aThe diagnosis remains UNCHANGED. \u000aAddendum #1 by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a3/31/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
