cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right axilla sentinel lymph node #1. \u000aB/2. Right axilla sentinel lymph node #2. \u000aC/3. Right breast wire localized lumpectomy *Short suture superior, long suture \u000alateral. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass and clip in specimen - wire intact. Report called to Dr. \u000aGolshan by Dr. Ritner REMOVED_DATE at 5:00 PM. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in parts, each labeled with the patient's name, \u000aunit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "Rt axilla sentinel lymph node #1", consists of an irregular \u000atan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue (3.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ). The \u000aspecimen is sectioned to reveal a well-circumscribed pink/tan smooth rubbery \u000anodule consistent with lymph node (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0. 5cm ). The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned and submitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 possible lymph node serially sectioned, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "Rt axilla sentinel lymph node #2", consists of an irregular \u000atan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ). The \u000aspecimen is sectioned to reveal a well-circumscribed pink/tan smooth rubbery \u000anodule consistent with lymph node (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ). The specimen is \u000atrisected, and submitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 3 frags, ESS. \u000aPart C, labeled "right breast wire localized lumpectomy short suture superior \u000along suture lateral", consists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of \u000afibroadipose breast tissue (3.8cm superior to inferior, 3.0cm medial to \u000alateral, and 1.5cm anterior to posterior). There is a short suture \u000adesignating the superior margin and a long suture designating the lateral \u000amargin. There is a needle localization wire entering through the lateral \u000aaspect of the specimen and exiting through the medial posterior aspect of the \u000aspecimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol (superior red, inferior \u000agreen, medial orange, lateral yellow, anterior blue, and posterior black) and \u000athe specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior. The cut surface \u000ais tan/yellow and homogeneous with a focal area of dense white ill-defined \u000afibrous tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ), which grossly abuts the lateral and \u000aposterior margins and comes within 0.4cm of the anterior margin, 1.0cm of the \u000amedial margin, 1.4cm of the superior margin, and 1.5cm of the inferior \u000amargin. Within the dense white fibrous tissue is a metallic clip. No \u000aadditional lesions are grossly identified. The specimen is submitted in its \u000aentirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections superior to inferior, blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to \u000ainclude fibrous area, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to include radiographed area with metallic clip, \u000a1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000asek/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
