VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s) \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Astrid Weins, M.D., Ph.D.; Tanya Rege, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS \u000aAND A CLIP, SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY, PALPABLE LYMPH NODE BIOPSY AND AXILLARY \u000aNODE DISSECTION (Part A (including  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), Part B (including FSB), \u000aPart C, Part D): \u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODES \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aSize - at least 2.5cm \u000aMultifocal - Yes (see note) \u000aHistologic type - Ductal \u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - III (Poor) (8 or 9 points) \u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points) \u000aNuclear grade - High (3 points) \u000aMitotic counts - 2 points \u000aEIC - Positive \u000aLVI - Present \u000aDermal LVI - Not applicable \u000aSkin invasion - Not applicable \u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable \u000aFinal Margins (invasive) \u000aNegative (> 0.3cm ) - Superior, anterior \u000aVery close(<0.1cm from margin)- Posterior, lateral, inferior, medial \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aTypes - Solid, cribriform \u000aNuclear grade - High \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present \u000aExtent of DCIS \u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks \u000aMargins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (> 0.3cm ) - Superior, lateral, anterior \u000aVery close(<0.1cm from margin)- posterior, inferior, medial \u000aLYMPH NODES \u000aSentinel lymph nodes - Positive (3 H&E levels examined) \u000aNumber of positive nodes - 2 (see NOTE) \u000aNumber of nodes examined - 5 \u000aAxillary lymph nodes - Positive \u000aNumber of positive nodes - 2 \u000aNumber of nodes examined - 16 \u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- REMOVED_DATE \u000aSize of largest metastatic focus - 0.7cm \u000aExtranodal extension - Present \u000a- Size <0.1cm \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aCore biopsy site \u000aFibroadenoma \u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID a MX (with multiple foci \u000aof invasion) \u000aNOTE: \u000aTumor is present as a 2.5cm mass with adjacent areas of DCIS including \u000amultiple satellite foci of invasive carcinoma. Evaluation for lymphovascular \u000ainvasion is difficult due to marked retraction artifact; however, two (2) \u000adefinitive foci of lymphovascular invasion are seen (blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). Slides \u000afrom Part C are also reviewed by Dr. D. Dillon (Breast Pathology Service) who \u000aconcurs. \u000aThe original frozen section report for part A reported a total of three (3) \u000apositive sentinel nodes. The tumor originally frozen as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is not present on \u000apermanent sections. After review of the original frozen section slides, the two \u000a(2) fragments that contained tumor in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  are interpreted as being from a \u000asingle lymph node. Consequently, two (2) of five (5) sentinel nodes are \u000apositive for tumor. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 60-year-old postmenopausal woman S/P L breast core bx REMOVED_DATE \u000arevealing poorly-differentiated Grade III/III IDC with LVI; high nuclear grade \u000aDCIS. \u000aOperation: L breast WL lumpectomy with 2 bracketing wires, SNB, SLAB, ? ALND. \u000aPREVIOUS SURGERY: REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; REMOVED_DATE BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; REMOVED_DATE BS-08- REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aOperative Findings: None specified. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: None specified. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Left sentinel node Hot + Blue REMOVED_DATE (FS). \u000aB/2) Palpable left lymph node Blue not hot (FS). \u000aC/3) Lt breast tissue (mammary); long - lateral; short - superior; Whipple - \u000achest wall margin. \u000aD/4) Lt Level 1 + 2 axillary lymph node. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++, clip and 2 wires in specimen - Ca++ may extend to margin. - \u000aE. P. Frost, MD. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT SENTINEL NODE" (FSA); \u000aOne of two (2) lymph nodes with METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aTwo of two (2) lymph nodes with METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "PALPABLE LEFT LYMPH NODE" (FSB): \u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA involving two (of two) lymph nodes. \u000aOR Consultation by: Lucian Chirieac, M.D. \u000aResident: SCOTT LOVITCH, M.D., PH.D. \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in four parts, each labeled with the \u000apatient's name and unit number. \u000aPart A, "Left sentinel node hot and blue", consists of multiple fragments of \u000ayellow adipose tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm in aggregate) within which four \u000atan/pink rubbery lymph node candidates are identified ranging REMOVED_DATE to 1.1cm in \u000agreatest dimension. The two largest lymph nodes are bisected (one node inked \u000ablue) and entirely submitted for frozen as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remaining two lymph nodes \u000aare entirely submitted for frozen as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Another lymph node candidate is \u000aidentified within the remaining fatty soft tissue (0.3cm in greatest \u000adimension). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One lymph node candidate, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart B, "Palpable left lymph node blue, not hot", consists of two tan/pink \u000alymph node candidates (0.4 and 0.6cm in greatest dimension) which are entirely \u000asubmitted for frozen as FSB. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : FSB remnant, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart C, "LT breast tissue", consists of an irregular portion of fibrofatty soft \u000atissue (7.0cm medial to lateral x 6.5cm superior to inferior x 3.5cm \u000aanterior to posterior) with two needle-localization wires in place (designated \u000aby prosector as #1 and #2). The first needle-localization wire was received \u000apartially removed and now only inserts through the inferior aspect of the \u000aspecimen with no exit. The second needle-localization wire enters through the \u000ainferomedial aspect of the specimen with no definitive exit. There is a long \u000astitch designating lateral, a short designating superior and a whipstitch \u000adesignating the chest wall margin. The accompanying specimen radiograph \u000adisplays a metallic clip in the area of interest. The specimen is inked by the \u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. \u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a \u000aprevious biopsy cavity focally surrounded by an indurated tan-white lesion (2.5 \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm ) located 0.4cm from the posterior margin, 0.8cm from the \u000ainferior margin, 1.4cm from the medial margin, 2.0cm from the anterior \u000amargin, 2.5cm from the lateral margin, and 3.8cm from the superior margin. \u000aNeedle-localization wire #1 goes directly through the area of interest. \u000aSurrounding the area of interest are multiple gritty-granular areas of ? \u000acalcification. Remaining breast parenchyma consists of approximately 80% \u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue and 20% dense white fibrous tissue. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, radially submitted, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Previous biopsy site, lesion and gritty/granular areas in \u000arelationship to closest margin sequentially submitted from superior to \u000ainferior, multi frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, radially submitted, 3 frags in each, RSS. \u000aPart D, "LT level #1 and #2 axillary lymph nodes", consists of multiple \u000aportions of yellow-red fatty soft tissue (11.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm in aggregate) \u000awithin which multiple tan-pink rubbery lymph node candidates are identified \u000aranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1.2cm in greatest dimension. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Three lymph node candidates in each, 3 frags in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Five lymph node candidates, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aJenC/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a7/22/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
