000amargins revealing 1. Medial margin - poorly differentiated grade III/III IDC, \u000ano LVI; intermediate nuclear grade DCIS with close margin; 2. Inferior margin \u000arevealing poorly differentiated grade III/III IDC with LVI + margin; \u000aintermediate nuclear grade DCIS with close margin. \u000aOperation: Left breast re-excision. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Left medial shave margin, whip stitch new margin plus scar. \u000aB/2. Inferior shaved margin, whip stitch new margin. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, labeled with the patient's name \u000aand medical record number. \u000aPart A, "left medial shaved margin, whipstitch new margin plus scar". The \u000aspecimen consists of two fragments of tissue, the first, a pink/white skin \u000aellipse (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm ) has no gross abnormalities. The second part is a \u000ayellow/red fatty breast tissue fragment (9.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ) that is oriented \u000aper surgeon with a whipstitch on the new margin (inked black). The old \u000aresection margin was inked blue. The specimen is sectioned to reveal no gross \u000aabnormalities. The entire specimen is submitted for review. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin ellipse, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of the specimen, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aPart B, "inferior shaved margin, whipstitch new margin". The specimen consists \u000aof one fragment of yellow/red fatty adipose tissue (7.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ), that \u000ais partially disrupted. The specimen is oriented per surgeon with a whipstitch \u000aon the new margin (inked black). The old resection margin was inked blue. The \u000aspecimen is uninked on the disrupted internal aspect of the specimen. The \u000aspecimen is submitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Marginal tissue, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER: 