astromal reaction, lying 6.0cm from the deep margin. Representative sections \u000afrom this mass, the deep margin underlying the mass, and all four quadrants are \u000asubmitted for histologic analysis. Dissection of the presumed axillary tail \u000areveals only two definite lymph nodes. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass, 1 frag/cass, RSS \u000aMicro 3: deep margin underlying mass, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper inner quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper outer quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower outer quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower inner quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS \u000aMicro 12: nipple, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 13: 2 lymph nodes, 2 frag, RSS \u000aPart two, "right breast (suture/tail)", consists of a right breast (26.4 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 5.7cm ) with skin (27.2 x 13.2cm ), nipple (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ), and small \u000aaxillary tail (8.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 3.2cm ). The deep surface is a smooth fascial \u000aplane. This plane is inked in black, and the specimen is serially sectioned to \u000areveal a cystic breast, but no gross mass lesions. Representative sections of \u000athe breast are submitted for histologic analysis. The axillary tail is \u000adissected for lymph nodes, and these are submitted for histologic analysis. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper inner quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower inner quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  outer upper quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper outer quadrant, 1 frag/cass, RSS \u000aMicro 22: nipple, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 23: 3 potential lymph nodes from small axillary tail, 3 frag, RSS \u000adwa \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000a[report_end] 
