VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Wai Chin Foo, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS: \u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU is \u000apresent in 3 of 18 blocks. \u000aSevere ductal atypia is associated with columnar cell change, mucin production, \u000aand calcifications. \u000aSevere ductal atypia is focally very close to (<0.1cm ) the medial margin \u000a(block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aSevere ductal atypia is 0.15cm from the inferior margin (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) and 0.25cm \u000afrom the superior margin (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aThe lateral, anterior and posterior margins are negative (>0.3cm ). \u000aCore biopsy site. \u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN: \u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU is \u000apresent in 6 of 9 blocks. \u000aSevere ductal atypia is associated with columnar cell change, mucin production, \u000aand calcifications. \u000aSevere ductal atypia is multifocally close to the new margin: (0.15cm  block \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; 0.2cm  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; 0.25cm  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; 0.3cm block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aCore biopsy site. \u000aC. RIGHT BREAST, "MARGIN BEYOND INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN": \u000aBenign breast tissue. \u000aNOTE: Selected slides were also reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast pathology, \u000awho concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: ADH, right breast. \u000aOperation: Wire-directed excision. \u000aOperative Findings: See OP note. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Preop: ADH. Postop: None provided. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right breast needle localized biopsy tissue. \u000aB/2. Inferior margin (blue used as outer edge). \u000aC/3. Margin beyond inferior shave at closed area. \u000aRADIOLOGY: First specimen ? abnormal on edge of specimen - possible few groups \u000aof calcs - reported to R.C. and more tissue being taken. MN  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and medical record number. \u000aPart A, "Right breast needle localized biopsy tissue," consists of a REMOVED_DATE g \u000alumpectomy specimen (A-P 4.9cm  S-I REMOVED_DATE  M-L 4.4cm ) with a localizing wire \u000aentering at the lateral margin and exiting at the medial margin. An \u000aaccompanying radiograph demonstrates a localizing wire, calcifications, and a \u000amass at the edge of the specimen. Specimen is sectioned, anterior to \u000aposterior, into seven slices (wire, slice 3). There is an ill-defined \u000awhite/yellow mass (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.8cm ), which extends from slices 3 to 6. The \u000amass grossly abuts the inferior and posterior margin and measures 0.9cm to the \u000amedial margin, 1.8cm to the superior margin, 3.6cm to the lateral margin, and \u000a1.5cm to the anterior margin. The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable. \u000aSpecimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, perpendicular, 4 frags per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin, perpendicular, 4 frags per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #1, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3 (wire), 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Inferior margin (blue used as outer edge)," consists of a REMOVED_DATE g \u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.1cm ) with a suture opposite to \u000aan inked surface (blue). No orientation information is provided. The cut \u000asurface demonstrates a tan/yellow, lobulated mass (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm ), which \u000aextends to the inked margin, with focal hemorrhage. Specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aPart C, "#3. Margin beyond inferior shave at closed area," consists of a REMOVED_DATE g \u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm ) with an inked surface \u000a(blue). No orientation information is provided. The cut surface is \u000aunremarkable. Specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE frags per cassette, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aWCF/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a3/14/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
