VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE DIRECTED BIOPSY: \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (blocks 2, 3, 6, and 8). Single cell necrosis is \u000apresent focally in tumor cells. No calcifications are seen in association \u000awith tumor. \u000aFibrocystic changes with cysts, apocrine metaplasia, and numerous \u000acalcium oxalate crystals (see note). \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia without atypia. \u000aFibroadenoma (0.3cm ). \u000aNOTE: The paraffin blocks were re-x-rayed and a cluster of calcifications was \u000aidentified in block #3. Step sections of this block revealed a cluster of \u000aapocrine cysts with calcium oxalate crystals. A single calcification was seen \u000ain block 6. Calcium oxalate crystals in cysts and in stroma were present in \u000astep sections. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: New right mammogram, clustered microcalcifications. \u000aOperation: Right needle directed breast biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast calcifications. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Right breast tissue. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST NEEDLE DIRECTED BIOPSY": \u000aNo areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma. \u000aFinal diagnosis deferred to permanent sections. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications in specimen. \u000aT. FRENNA M.D \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by JONES,DANIEL MORGAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aSpecimen received fresh, labelled with the patient's name and number only, \u000aconsists of a single fragment of yellow/tan fibrous fatty tissue with needle \u000alocalization wire in place (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ). The specimen is composed of \u000aunremarkable adipose and breast parenchyma with no areas grossly suspicious for \u000ainvasive carcinoma. \u000aThe blocks are re-x-rayed. A cluster of calcifications is identified in block \u000athree and a single calcification in block six. Additional levels are obtained \u000aon these blocks. \u000aMICROS REMOVED_DATE  Entire specimen, multi frags, 8 cass. \u000aReports to: DAVIS, SALLIE, KEENE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
