VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, MASTECTCOMY AND LEVEL I AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODE(S) \u000aSYNOPSIS: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aTypes - cribriform, micropapillary \u000aNuclear grade - low \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent \u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent \u000aExtent of DCIS \u000aNumber of blocks:total - 2:23 blocks \u000aFinal Margins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (>0.3cm ) - deep \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - present \u000aLYMPH NODES \u000aAxillary Lymph Nodes - negative \u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0 \u000aNumber of nodes examined - 4 \u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 0:4 \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia \u000aClips and core biopsy sites (x 2) \u000aFibroadenoma \u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium \u000aSeborrheic keratosis \u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis p REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  MX \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending \u000aNOTE: \u000aThe DCIS and much of the LCIS are associated with the previous core biopsy site \u000ain the outer portion of the breast. \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for DCIS (block 15): \u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE - LOW \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) - POSITIVE (2+) \u000aInterpretation: \u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the \u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet \u000abeen determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor \u000acells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but \u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive. \u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity \u000ain >10% of tumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational \u000ause only. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Hx DCIS right breast - see BWH core bx (4/28/03) positive DCIS and \u000apositive LCIS. \u000aOperation: Right mastectomy with removal level I lymphndoes. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast and level I lymph nodes, short = superior, \u000along = lateral. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by REIMANN,JULIE DYLAN REGAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "right breast, short superior, long lateral, plus level I lymph nodes", \u000aand consists of a 973-gram mastectomy specimen (25 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm ) with \u000aattached skin ellipse (23 x 16.5cm ) with areola (5.5 x 2.8cm ) and nipple \u000a(0.9 x 1.4cm ). There is a brown, pigmented area adjacent to the nipple on \u000athe skin ellipse (0.8 x 0.6cm ) that has the gross appearance of a seborrheic \u000akeratosis; there is no scar on the skin ellipse. The breast tissue is \u000acomposed of approximately 15% fibrous tissue, the rest is adipose tissue. \u000aThere are no grossly identifiable lesions. Radiographs taken by the \u000apathologist in the grossing room indicate two clips in the mastectomy \u000aspecimen, one located in the lower inner quadrant and the other located in the \u000alower outer quadrant. Sixteen (16) candidate lymph nodes are identified in \u000athe specimen, ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1.8cm in greatest dimension. \u000aMicro 1: fibrous tissue, slice 2 (most likely to be [inaudible] located in \u000athe inner lower quadrant), 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 2: fibrous tissue adjacent to the area in slicd 2 contained with clip, \u000a2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 3: fibrous tissue adjacent to the clip in slice 2, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 4: fibrous tissue adjacent to area of clip in slice 2, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 5: fibrous tissue adjacent to clip area and slice 2, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 6: fibrous tissue from upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue in outer lower quadrant (in area containing the \u000asecond clip), REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro 16: fibrous tissue from upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue with nipple and tissue deep to the nipple, 1 frag \u000aeach, RSS. \u000aMicro 20: 4 candidate lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 21: 4 candidate lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 22: 4 candidate lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 23: 4 candidate lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 24: skin with brown pigmented lesion, 1 frag, ESS. \u000ajdr \u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000a[report_end] 
