VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Travis J Hollmann, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aBiopsy site changes (see note). \u000aSclerosing adenosis with calcifications. \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aNote: The clip placed at the time of a prior core needle biopsy is not seen in \u000athe specimen radiograph. The biopsy site changes are close to, but not at, the \u000amedial and deep margins. Clinical correlation is suggested to ensure that the \u000aclip and the entire biopsy site has been removed. \u000aNo carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic evaluation of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, MEDIAL SHAVE MARGIN, WITH RADIOLOGIC CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (best seen in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aCalcifications are associated with ADH and with apocrine cysts and in lobules. \u000aNo biopsy site changes are seen. \u000aNote: No carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic evaluation of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, LATERAL SHAVE MARGIN: \u000aPredominantly fatty breast tissue. \u000aNo biopsy site changes are seen. \u000aNote: No carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic evaluation of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 63 year old female with abnormal right mammogram - ADH. REMOVED_DATE - \u000amammo right breast, scattered fibroglandular densities with greater than ten \u000agrouped heterogeneous calcs. REMOVED_DATE - right breast core biopsy - ADH, \u000aassociated with calcifications. \u000aOperation: Excisional biopsy. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) right breast tissue, short stitch=superior, long stitch=lateral, whip \u000astitch on deep margin. \u000aB/2) additional breast tissue, medial shave margin, stitch at med=whip stitch \u000aat new margin. \u000aC/3) additional breast tissue, lateral shave margin, whip stitch at lateral. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aSpecimen #1 - Calcifications circled \u000aSpecimen #2 Calcifications faint \u000aSpecimen #3 - No calcifications Dr. Jack Meyer. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patients \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "#1 - right breast tissue", consists of a single wire-localized \u000abreast excision specimen, which contains a long stitch designating lateral, a \u000ashort stitch designating superior, and a whip stitch designating the posterior \u000amargin (per the surgeon). The specimen is received with the localization wire \u000anot in the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen measures 1.6cm \u000aa-p, 4.6cm m-l, and 3.5cm s-i. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph, \u000awhich shows scant microcalcifications at the edge of the specimen. The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned into ten slices from lateral to medial, \u000arevealing parenchyma consisting of predominantly (75%) fatty tissue and \u000aapproximately 25% fibrous tissue. The specimen contains a centrally oriented \u000aarea of hemorrhage (slices five through seven), likely representing the prior \u000abiopsy site. The entire specimen is submitted for microscopic examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : lateral tip, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice two, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID + REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice three, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID + REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice four, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID + REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice five, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID + REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice six, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID + REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice seven, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice eight, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice nine and slice ten (smaller fragment), 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2 - additional right breast tissue", consists of a single \u000atan/pink breast excision specimen (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ), which contains a whip \u000astitch designating the new margin (per the surgeon). The specimen is \u000aaccompanied by a radiograph showing very faint calcifications. The specimen is \u000ainked as follows: blue=old margin, black=new margin (with whip stitch). The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned into twelve slices revealing approximately 90% \u000aadipose tissue and 10% fibrous tissue. After alignment with the radiograph, \u000athe microcalcifications likely reside in slices one through six. There is no \u000aevidence of discrete nodule or tumor. The entire specimen is submitted for \u000amicroscopic examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice one, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice two, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice three, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice four, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice five, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice six, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID + REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice seven, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID + REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice eight, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID + REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice nine, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice ten, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice eleven, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice twelve, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart C, labeled "#3 - additional right breast tissue", consists of a single \u000abreast excision specimen (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm ) with a whip stitch designating \u000athe new lateral shave margin (per the surgeon). The specimen is inked as \u000afollows: old=blue, while new=black (whip stitch). The specimen is serially \u000asectioned into twelve sections revealing approximately 90% fatty tissue and 5% \u000afibrous tissue. There is no evidence of discrete nodules, masses or gross \u000aabnormalities. The specimen radiograph does not reveal calcifications. The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for microscopic examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice one, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice two, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice three, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice four, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice five, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice six, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice seven, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice eight, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice nine, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice ten, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice eleven, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice twelve, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aTH/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a5/16/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
