000ainferior. The specimen is inked by the surgeon as follows: anterior = blue, \u000aposterior = black, medial = orange, lateral = yellow, superior = red, and \u000ainferior = green. The specimen appears to be focally disrupted at various \u000amargins (possibly due to excision or mammography). The entire specimen is \u000asubmitted. There is a single nodule (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ) present at the \u000aperiphery (lateral margin) of the mass that is pink/white and firm. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue, multiple frags each, ESS. \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
