er of the specimen is \u000acomposed 90% of fibrous tissue, including cyst formation, and 10% adipose \u000atissue. Two potential lymph nodes (0.6 and 0.9cm ) are identified in the \u000aadipose tissue designated at the axilla. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : nipple, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : breast tissue subjacent to nipple, multiple frags, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : axillary adipose tissue/potential lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : biopsy cavity and adjacent tissue, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMCC/jp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Martin C Chang M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Martin C Chang M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Russell K Dorer M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
