ATE (superior to inferior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior). \u000aOn the accompanying specimen radiograph, the specimen contains a localization \u000awire, dense calcifications, and a clip. The specimen is received with the wire \u000aremoved. \u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from medial (slice 1) to lateral (slice 9) \u000ainto nine slides. There is a 0.5cm hemorrhagic area adjacent to fibrous \u000atissue in slice 4. The remainder of the tissue consists of 50% fibrous tissue \u000aand 50% adipose tissue, that is entirely submitted in serial sections. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, perpendicular sections, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slices  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a7/5/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
