gin, 0.6cm of the superior and \u000ainferior margins, and 0.7cm of the posterior margin. A gray/white, cystic, \u000aill-defined area (2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm ) is present at the inferior aspect of the \u000acavity, grossly extending to the inferior, medial, anterior margins, and coming \u000ato within 0.4cm of the posterior margin, 0.7cm of the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the superior margin. The remaining breast tissue consists of \u000apredominantly golden yellow lobulated fat with scant fibrous stroma. The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted sequentially from superior to inferior. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : breast tissue, sequentially from superior to inferior, \u000agray/white ill-defined lesional tissue in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , multiple \u000afrags, ESS. \u000adfi/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Derek K Marsee M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
