low/tan fibroadipose tissue (4.7 M - L x REMOVED_DATE S - I x \u000a2.5 A - Pcm ) which exhibits two sutures per surgeon: Short equals superior \u000aand long equals lateral. Adherent to the anteromedial aspect of the specimen \u000ais a tan granular skin ellipse (1.7 x 0.6cm ) through which enters a \u000aneedle-localization wire. The wire tip is embedded within the specimen, with \u000ano clear exit site. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; \u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen was \u000apreviously radiographed, confirming the presence of an intact wire and \u000acalcification within the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from \u000alateral to medial. In the lateral aspect of the specimen, around the \u000aneedle-localization wire tip, is an ill-defined gritty yellow/tan firm lesion \u000a(1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ) corresponding to the area of calcifications as seen on the \u000aaccompanying radiograph. The ill-defined lesion is located 0.3cm from the \u000alateral margin, 0.3cm from the anterior margin, 0.6cm from the posterior \u000amargin, 1.5cm from the inferior margin, 0.4cm from the superior margin, and \u000a1.9cm from the medial margin. The remainder of the cut surface is composed of \u000ayellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue with minimal delicate white/tan fibrous \u000astroma. The specimen is entirely sequentially submitted from lateral to \u000amedial. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central specimen from lateral to medial (ill-defined \u000agritty lesion corresponding to calcifications in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin to include skin ellipse perpendicularly sectioned, \u000amulti frags, ESS. \u000alm/lp \u000aCASE NU