VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: George Lin, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (Block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; levels examined), see NOTE. \u000aIntraductal papilloma with florid epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine \u000ametaplasia, and associated calcifications. \u000aNOTE: There is one focus of LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (Block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) with lack of \u000aE-cadherin demonstrated by immunohistochemical staining. There is \u000afocal necrosis associated with the ductal hyperplasia in a duct \u000ainvolved by LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU. \u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who \u000aconcurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 59 year old female with history of left nipple discharge clear, \u000aabnormal breast MRI. \u000aOperation: 1. Left breast MRI guided excisional biopsy and duct excision. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: 1. Left breast nipple discharge. \u000a2. Left breast abnormal MRI. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA. Left breast MRI guided wire localized excisional biopsy and duct excision \u000a(stitch) short superior, long lateral - mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aWire & vague nodularity & some Ca++ in specimen. OR called /SR. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1. Left breast MRI-guided wire localized excisional biopsy and duct \u000aexcision stitch equals short superior, long lateral", and consists of an \u000airregular portion of fibrofatty tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm ), with a long suture \u000adesignating lateral, and a short suture designating superior. The specimen is \u000areceived with a radiograph showing the wire and calcifications within the \u000aspecimen. There is an inserted needle localization wire, which enters along the \u000amedial-inferior aspect, and does not exit the specimen. The specimen is inked \u000aper pathology protocol as superior red, inferior green, anterior blue, \u000aposterior black, lateral yellow and medial orange, and is serially sectioned to \u000areveal 60% yellow lobulated adipose tissue and 40% focally cystic white fibrous \u000atissue, with no discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen is \u000asequentially submitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections from anterior to posterior, with the \u000alocalized area as displayed on the accompanying radiograph in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin, radially, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aCP/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a9/8/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
