it number. \u000aPart one, labeled "Left breast tissue", consists of two (2) light blue \u000acassettes. One cassette is labeled "A-Ca++" and contains multiple, soft, \u000afragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm in aggregate). \u000aThe other blue cassette is labeled "B" and contains similar tissue fragments \u000a(1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm in aggregate). \u000aMicro 1: "A", multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 2: "B", multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, labeled "right breast tissue" consists of two (2) white cassettes. \u000aOne cassette is labeled "A Ca++" and contains multiple, soft, fragmented, \u000ayellow to white tissue cores (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm in aggregate). The other \u000awhite cassette is labeled "B" and contains similar tissue fragments (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 0.2cm in aggregate). \u000aMicro 3: "A", multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 4: "B", multi frags, ESS. \u000akks \u000aReports to: TWOHIG, LORRAINE, BERNADETTE, MB \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES) \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES) \u000a[report_end] 
