SCRIPTION: by LOMBARD,DAVID B.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one is labeled "#1 right breast tissue, short superior, long lateral, whip \u000astitch deep margin". The specimen consists of a mass of fibroadipose tissue \u000a(4.8cm superior to inferior x 4.2cm medial to lateral x 1.5cm anterior to \u000aposterior). Three sutures placed in the specimen by the surgeon denote in the \u000asuperior, lateral, and deep orientations to the specimen. In addition, the \u000aspecimen has been inked by the surgeon, presumably per pathology protocol for \u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; \u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. A wire is present in the \u000aspecimen which is removed. A specimen radiograph is taken and the clips as \u000awell as multiple areas of calcification are located. No tumor mass is grossly \u000aevident. Representative sections are submitted, including all areas of \u000acalcification identified on radiography. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  areas of calcification, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 4: area of clip, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional areas of calcification, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional fibrous areas of breast, multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart two is labeled "#2 left breast tissue, long lateral, short superior, whip \u000astitch deep margin". It consists of a mass of fibroadipose tissue (4.5cm \u000aanterior to posterior x 1.5cm medial lateral x 2.8cm superior to inferior). \u000aThree sutures are present in the specimen designating superior, lateral and \u000adeep margins of the specimen. A wire is also present in the specimen which is \u000aremoved. In addition, the specimen has been inked previously by the surgeon, \u000apresumably per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = \u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; \u000amedial = orange. A specimen radiograph is taken and the clip is identified and \u000aremoved. No discrete mass is present in the specimen which is serially \u000asectioned and entirely submitted for analysis. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  multi frags, ESS. The area of the clip is in micros 17&18. \u000adl \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
