\u000abiopsy cavity is sampled and generous sections are taken from the remainder of \u000athe breast. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire biopsy cavity including deep margin, REMOVED_DATE frags each \u000acassette, ESS. \u000aMicro 10: area of nodularity in the upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 11: additional section from inner upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections from the lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro 14&15: representative sections from the upper outer quadrant, 1 frag \u000aeach cassette, RSS. \u000aMicro 16&17: representative sections from the lower outer quadrant, 1 frag \u000aeach cassette, RSS. \u000aMicro 18: nipple, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 19: skin with scar, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aPart two, "mastectomy skin, left breast", received are four fragments of skin \u000aand underlying soft cutaneous tissue (6.7 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm in aggregate). \u000aRepresentative sections are submitted for histologic evaluation. \u000aMicro 20: skin from mastectomy site, 3 frags, RSS. \u000adwa \u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT \u000a[report_end] 
