tions are in the specimen. There is an area of \u000ahemorrhage (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ) located 0.3cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the inferior margin, 1.0cm from the lateral margin, 1.6cm from the \u000amedial margin, 1.0cm from the anterior margin, and 0.5cm from the posterior \u000amargin. The remainder of the specimen is composed of predominantly white/tan \u000afibrous tissue which grossly extends to all margins. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro #1: Lateral margin, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro #2: Inferior, superior, anterior, posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro #3: Inferior, anterior, posterior, superior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro #4: Anterior, superior, posterior margins, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro #5: Superior, inferior, anterior, posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro #6: Anterior, posterior, superior, inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro #7: Superior, inferior, anterior, posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro #8: Medial margin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000ajdr/ \u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
