ntral portion of the specimen adjacent \u000ato the localization wire. The specimen is sectioned into eight slices from \u000aanterior to posterior. A REMOVED_DATE cubic centimeter region consistent with the \u000aprevious biopsy site and containing the clip (slice #4) is identified 0.4cm \u000afrom the inferior margin, 0.6cm from the superior margin, 1.0cm from the \u000amedial margin, 1.1cm from the lateral margin, 1.6cm from the deep margin and \u000a1.6cm from the anterior margin. The remainder of the specimen consists 90% of \u000aunremarkable adipose tissue and 10% dense white fibrous tissue. Gross \u000aphotographs are taken. The specimen is submitted in its entirety for \u000ahistologic examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, 2 frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Deep margin, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aCEL/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 21,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12:03:58PM \u000a[report_end] 
