or/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A region of \u000ahemorrhagic, foreign material (2.3cm medial-lateral, 1.5cm \u000aanterior-posterior, 1.0cm superior-inferior) representing the clip site is \u000apresent. The foreign material abuts the anterior and inferior margins and is \u000a0.5cm from the superior, 1.1cm from the posterior, 1.4cm from the lateral \u000aand 1.5cm from the medial margins. A white/yellow, chalky, well-circumscribed \u000aregion is present (0.6cm anterior-posterior, 0.3cm superior-inferior, 0.4cm \u000amedial-lateral) is 0.3cm from the posterior, 2.0cm from the anterior, 0.9cm \u000afrom the inferior, 1.1cm from the superior, 0.9cm from the medial, and 1.5cm \u000afrom the lateral margins). The remainder of the breast parenchyma is \u000aapproximately 80% adipose and 20% fibrous tissue. The specimen is received \u000awith a radiograph showing a clip adjacent to the tip of a needle localization \u000awire. The entire specimen is submitted for histologic examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin (perpendicular), 4 frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential sections, each cross section submitted in two \u000acassettes with white/yellow mass in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and foreign material in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , \u000amass with respect to foreign material in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin (perpendicular), REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast parenchyma to include posterior and superior margins, 3 \u000afrags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aoob\u005cpab \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a2/11/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
