VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000a1. LEFT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY (205 GM): \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with severe atypia, single microscopic \u000afocus (0.2cm ) adjacent to prior biopsy cavity (block 13; levels examined) \u000a(see note). \u000aNo vascular invasion seen. \u000aFibrocystic changes, including sclerosing adenosis, apocrine metaplasia, \u000acysts, and microcalcification. \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, florid. \u000aOne (1) intramammary lymph node with no tumor present. \u000aNOTE: No infiltrating tumor is seen. All areas of fibrous breast \u000aparenchyma (excluding areas of adipose tissue) and the entire prior biopsy \u000acavity area was examined histologically. The area of atypical ductal \u000ahyperplasia was step sectioned. \u000a2. AXILLARY LYMPH NODES, LEVELS I AND II: \u000aNine (9) lymph nodes with no tumor present. \u000aFat necrosis, with suture granulomas, consistent with prior lymph node \u000abiopsy site. \u000aNo breast parenchymal structures are present in the axillary tissue. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Cancer of unknown primary, positive left axillary lymph node, \u000alobular in situ. Please check breast specimen carefully. \u000aOperation: Left modified radical mastectomy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue. \u000a2. Level 1 & 2 axillary lymph nodes. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HEVNER,ROBERT FRANCIS,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two (2) parts, each labeled with the \u000apatient's name and number. \u000aThe first part, labeled "#1 left breast", consists of a modified radical \u000amastectomy specimen (205 grams, 19.5cm left-right, 14.0cm superior-inferior, \u000a2.0cm anterior-posterior), with ellipse of pale tan skin (17.5cm left-right, \u000a5.8cm superior-inferior) containing an areola (3.0cm diameter) with nipple \u000a(1.2cm diameter) near the inferior skin ellipse margin, and a superiorly \u000alocated healed scar (2cm ) running from left to right, 2cm superior to the \u000aareola. Sectioning reveals a prior biopsy site (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm ) with \u000aslight fibrosis and fat necrosis evident grossly, located 0.3cm below the \u000askin with scar, 0.4cm from the deep resection margin, and greater than 2cm \u000afrom all other margins. The remainder of the breast is primarily adipose, with \u000afew areas of slightly fibrous tissue identified as well. The gross specimen \u000awas reveiwed with Dr. Lester. No areas suspicious for invasive carcinoma are \u000aidentified after extensive searching. All areas of gross fibrous parenchyma \u000aare submitted for histologic examination. \u000aMICRO REMOVED_DATE  Biopsy cavity in relation to skin and deep margin, RSS, (all of \u000agrossly visible biopsy cavity submitted), 3 frags, 3 cass. \u000aMICRO 4: Additional moderately fibrous tissue near biopsy cavity, RSS, \u000a2 frags, 1 cass. \u000aMICRO REMOVED_DATE  Moderately fibrous breast tissue in upper outer quadrant, RSS, \u000a4 frags, 4 cass. \u000aMICRO REMOVED_DATE  Moderately fibrous tissue in lower outer quadrant, RSS, 2 frags, \u000a2 cass. \u000aMICRO 11: Additional lower outer quadrant moderately fibrous tissue, RSS, \u000a1 frag, 1 cass. \u000aMICRO 12: Nipple, RSS, 1 frag, 1 cass. \u000aMICRO REMOVED_DATE  Slightly fibrous tissue in lower inner quadrant, RSS, 2 frags, \u000a2 cass. \u000aMICRO REMOVED_DATE  Slightly fibrous areas in upper inner quadrant, RSS, 3 frags, \u000a2 cass. \u000aMICRO 17: Additional slightly fibrous tissue from upper outer quadrant, \u000aRSS, 2 frags, 1 cass. \u000aThe second part, labeled "#3 level 1 & 2 axillary nodes", consists of a single \u000afragment of mainly yellow, fibroadipose tissue (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm ), containing \u000aseveral identified lymph nodes. \u000aMICRO REMOVED_DATE  Lymph nodes, RSS, 16 frags, 6 cass. \u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY \u000a[report_end] 
