 semi-circle is gray/white, fibrous tissue \u000aconsistent with biopsy cavity. The margins are inked as follows: deep margin, \u000ablack; inferior, green; and lateral, yellow. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Perpendicular margins, inferior and deep, ESS, multi frag, 4 cass. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Perpendicular margins, inferior and lateral, ESS, multi frag, \u000a2 cass. \u000aPart three is labeled "superior anterior posterior medial and lateral margin, \u000aright breast" and consists of an approximately oval-shaped fragment of \u000ayellow/gray, fibrofatty tissue (2.7 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm ) with yellow adipose tissue \u000aalong the superior margin, as designated by the surgeon, firm and gray fibrous \u000atissue within the biopsy cavity, and additional gray/brown fibrous tissue along \u000athe deep margin. The margins are inked as follows: deep margin, black; \u000alateral margin, yellow; superior margin, green; and lateral margin, red. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Perpendicular sections, right breast, ESS, multi frag, 4 cass. \u000aari \u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY \u000a[report_end] 
