VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.; Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.; Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND A MASS: \u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, partially involving an intraductal papilloma, \u000aassociated with the prior core needle biopsy site (blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; levels \u000aexamined) (see note). Immunoperoxidase studies for p63 demonstrate \u000amyoepithelial cells along the fibrovascular cores of the papilloma, supporting \u000athe above diagnosis. \u000aThe closest margin is superior (0.1cm ). The remaining margins are \u000a> 0.3cm  \u000aNOTE: The patient had a circumscribed mass that was diagnosed as an "markedly \u000aatypical cribriform proliferation involving a papillary lesion" on core needle \u000abiopsy ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aIn this excision, ADH is confined to a papilloma. No atypia is seen in the \u000asurrounding tissue, which is completely examined microscopically. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 56 year old female with right breast atypical papillary lesion, s/p \u000aimage-guided core biopsy. \u000aOperation: Not provided. \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast papillary lesion. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Right breast, wire localized excisional biopsy, short stitch/superior, \u000along stitch/lateral - to mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aCalled to OR; Clip, mass, and intact wire on radiograph and US. Dr. A. \u000aOdulate. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000amedical record number, and "#1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy, \u000ashort stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral", and consists of a soft tissue \u000aresection specimen (4.2cm medial to lateral x 3.5cm anterior to posterior x \u000a1.4cm superior to inferior) with a long suture marking the lateral margin and \u000ashort suture marking the superior margin. There is a wire entering the lateral \u000aside of the specimen and exits at the medial side of the specimen. An \u000aaccompanying radiograph shows a clip in the middle of the specimen at the site \u000aof an ill-defined mass and the adjacent to the localization wire. The specimen \u000ais inked per pathology protocol: superior/red, inferior/green, anterior/blue, \u000aposterior/black, lateral/yellow, and medial/orange. There is a tan/white \u000aill-defined fibrotic area (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ) that abuts the posterior, \u000ainferior, superior, lateral and medial margins and is 0.7cm from the closest \u000aanterior margin. The specimen is serially sectioned from posterior to anterior \u000ainto eleven slices (slice #1 represents posterior margin and slice #11 \u000arepresents anterior margin). A metal clip is recovered in slice #6. The \u000aentire specimen is examined microscopically. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #1, posterior margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2 and #3, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #8, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #9, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #19, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #11, anterior margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, \u000aESS. \u000aQY/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a3/26/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
