e marks the \u000asuperior aspect of the specimen, long suture marks the lateral aspect, and a \u000awhipstitch marks the deep (posterior) margin. The specimen measures 1.9cm \u000afrom lateral to medial, 2.2cm from superior to inferior, and 3.8cm from \u000aanterior to posterior. There is a single wire present in the specimen, which \u000aenters anteriorly. A radiograph shows the wire passing through an area of \u000acalcifications in an area of density and a clip adjacent to the wire. The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior into six slices, such \u000athat slice #1 includes the superior margin and slice #6 includes the inferior \u000amargin. There is a firm, well-circumscribed, pink/white mass, which measures \u000a1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm  This grossly abuts the anterior and inferior margins, is \u000alocated 0.2cm from the medial margin, 0.5cm from the lateral margin, 2.1cm \u000afrom the posterior margin, and 1.4cm from the superior margin. Re-radiography \u000aof the serially sectioned specimen indicates the presence of the clip. The \u000aentire specimen is submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #1 (superior margin), 9 frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, anterior, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, posterior, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, anterior, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, posterior, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, anterior including main mass, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, central tissue between mass and ill-defined nodularity, 1 \u000afrag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, posterior including area of ill-defined nodularity, 1 \u000afrag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, anterior including mass and clip site, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, central, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, posterior, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6 (inferior margin), perpendicular sections, 4 frags \u000aper cassette, ESS. \u000aSBL/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a6/27/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
