ghout the remainder of the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned \u000aand submitted for histologic evaluation. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 5, adjacent to wire A, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 6, wire A, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 7, wire A, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 8, wire A, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 9: portion of slice 9, wire A, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 10: portion of slice 9, wire A, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 10, adjacent to wire A, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 14, adjacent to wire B, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 15, wire B, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 16, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 19: portion of slice 4 containing cyst, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 20: portion of slice 4, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 11, fibrous tissue, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 12, fibrous tissue, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 13, fibrous tissue, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 27: slices 1&2, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 28: slice 3, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 29: slice 17, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
