perior margin, en face, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro #4: Inferior margin, en face, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro #5: Deep margin, en face, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro #6: Biopsy cavity with respect to superior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro #7: Biopsy cavity with respect to deep margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicros #8-9: Biopsy cavity, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro #10: Skin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aThe second part is labelled "level 1 lymh node" and consists of a tan/yellow \u000afragment of fibrofatty tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x 5 x 1.5cm  Eight lymph nodes \u000aare identified, the greatest 1.5cm in dimension. \u000aMicros #11-12: One lymph node per cass, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro #13: Four lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicros #14-15: One lymph node per cass, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LUMPECTOMY \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: AXILLARY NODES \u000a[report_end] 
