VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material \u000aProcedure Date: \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIA WONG M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM MASSACHUSETTS GENERAL HOSPITAL, BOSTON, MA: \u000aLEFT BREAST, INCISIONAL BIOPSIES ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; 1/12/09): \u000a3:00: \u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified \u000aBloom-Richardson grade II/III), is present measuring at least 1.0cm  \u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen. \u000aNo carcinoma in situ is seen. \u000aThe invasive carcinoma is present at the unoriented black margin over a broad \u000afront. \u000a2:00, LATERAL: \u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified \u000aBloom-Richardson grade II/III), measuring at least 1.3cm  \u000aNo definitive lymphovascular invasion is seen. \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present. \u000aThe invasive carcinoma is at the unoriented black margin over a broad front. \u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the following \u000aresults (not reviewed): \u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE \u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /NEU (IHC) NEGATIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /NEU (FISH) NOT AMPLIFIED (1.7/1.7 = 1.0) \u000a6:00: \u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified \u000aBloom-Richardson grade II/III), measuring at least 0.5cm  \u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen. \u000aNo carcinoma in situ is seen. \u000aThe invasive carcinoma is at the unoriented black margin over a broad front. \u000aLEFT MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; 2/10/09): \u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified \u000aBloom-Richardson grade II/III), is present in 9 of 9 blocks with an estimated \u000asize of 10.5cm  by report. \u000aBiopsy site changes are present. \u000aLymphovascular invasion is seen ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present. \u000aThe nipple is present grossly. \u000aThe invasive carcinoma is at the anterior and posterior margin over a broad \u000afront, with cautery on invasive carcinoma (> 1.0cm ). \u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the following \u000aresults (not reviewed): \u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE \u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /NEU (IHC) NEGATIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /NEU (FISH) NOT AMPLIFIED (1.9/1.75 = 1.1) \u000aMETASTATIC LOBULAR CARCINOMA is present in two (2) of eight (8) axillary lymph \u000anodes. Both metastatic deposits measure 0.4cm (macrometastases). Extensive \u000aextranodal extension is seen in 4 of 4 slides (at least 0.6cm ). \u000aNote: The patient has a history of a 1cm invasive lobular carcinoma of the \u000aleft breast in  REMOVED_CASE_ID  ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). One of three lymph nodes was \u000apositive for metastatic carcinoma. The histologic appearance of the current \u000acarcinoma is consistent with a recurrence. \u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th edition): rp  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID a. \u000aSKIN, LEFT CHEST WALL, REMOVED_DATE CM PUNCH BIOPSY FOR A PLAQUE AND A NODULE \u000a( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; 3/13/09): \u000aCHEST WALL PLAQUE: \u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA is present invading in the deep dermis and \u000asubcutaneous tissue measuring 0.3cm  The skin is not ulcerated. \u000aNo dermal lymphovascular invasion is seen. \u000aThe invasive carcinoma is at the black inked margin. \u000aCHEST WALL NODULE: \u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA in collagenous stroma. \u000aFragment of epidermis and superficial dermis with no carcinoma seen. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Prior left lumpectomy for ILC - increased thickening left breast. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: ILC, LCIS. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aConsult slides. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aReceived from Massachusetts General Hospital, Pathology Department, 55 Fruit \u000aStreet, Boston, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID , are sixteen (16) glass slides. \u000aThree (3) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", \u000acorresponding to A) left breast, 3:00, excision (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ) B) left \u000abreast, 2 o'clock, lateral, excision (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) C) left breast, 6:00 o'clock, excision (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ) performed on \u000a1/12/09, according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's \u000aname. \u000aThirteen (13) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through \u000a" REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", corresponding to A) left breast modified radical \u000amastectomy (17 x 10 x 3.7cm ) with attached axillary tail dissection (7.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 1.6cm ) B) additional axillary contents dissection (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ) \u000aperformed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing \u000athe patient's name. \u000aTwo (2) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", \u000acorresponding to A) skin, left chest wall plaque, punch biopsy (0.3 x 0.3cm ) \u000aB) skin, right chest wall nodule, biopsy (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm )performed on \u000a3/13/09, according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's \u000aname. \u000aThree (3) cytology slides are labeled "MN-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " \u000athrough " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", corresponding to a midline chest fine needle aspiration performed \u000aon REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying cytology report bearing the patient's \u000aname (outside diagnosis: non-diagnostic specimen). The cytologic preparations \u000awere not reviewed due to a lack of medical necessity. \u000aEight (8) cytology slides are labeled "MN-09-0 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " \u000athrough " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", corresponding to a left breast fine needle aspiration performed \u000aon REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the \u000apatient's name (outside diagnosis: no malignant cells identified). The \u000acytologic preparations were not reviewed due to a lack of medical necessity. \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 08,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 10:28:43AM \u000a[report_end] 
