VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: \u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR (3.5cm ), benign. \u000aThe stroma is moderately cellular with mild nuclear pleomorphism; mitoses \u000anumber up to 4 per 10 HPF; no stromal overgrowth is present. \u000aTumor comes to within 0.2cm of the anterior, 0.9cm of the posterior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the superior, 0.8cm of the inferior, 1.0cm of the medial, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the lateral margins. \u000aPrior core biopsy sties. \u000aBenign changes include intraductal papilloma; florid ductal hyperplasia; \u000afibrocystic change, including cysts and apocrine metaplasia; and \u000asclerosing adenosis; microfibroadenoma. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aOperation: Left breast biopsy \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast lump (short/superior; long/lateral) \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HENDERSON,JOEL M.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000aunit number and "#1. left breast lump, short superior, long lateral", \u000aaccompanied by a whole specimen radiograph, which shows a mass of tissue with a \u000alocalization wire in place, marking a central lobulated hyperdensity. The \u000aspecimen consists of a single fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (9.0 x \u000a6.0 x 3.0cm ). The specimen is marked with a short suture to indicate \u000asuperior, and a long suture to indicate lateral. The specimen is inked per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior \u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. \u000aSectioning reveals the specimen to contain a well-circumscribed, lobulated firm \u000atan/gray mass with architecture consistent with phylloids tumor (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a2.5cm ). This mass is 1.0cm from the medial, 2.5cm from the lateral, 0.8cm \u000afrom the superior, 0.8cm from the inferior, 1.0cm from the deep, and 0.5cm \u000afrom the anterior margins by gross examination. Incorporated into the \u000aanterolateral aspect of the mass is a hemorrhagic prior biopsy site (0.9cm \u000agreatest dimension), with a well-circumscribed fibrous edge. This is adjacent \u000ato focal hemorrhage and fat necrosis. No other lesions are identified in the \u000aremaining breast tissue, which consists of approximately 70% yellow adipose \u000atissue and 30% tan/white fibrous tissue. A portion of tumor is retained for \u000atumor banking. Additional representative sections are submitted for histologic \u000aexamination. Approximaly 30% of the specimen is submitted. \u000aMicro 1: lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass and superior margin, medial to lateral, 3 frags, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass and inferior margin, medial to lateral, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass and anterior margin, medial to lateral, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass at posterior margin, including biopsy cavity, 4 frags, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, perpendiculary sectioned, 3 frags, RSS \u000ajmh \u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
