VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aFOLKERTH, REBECCA, DUNN, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by FOLKERTH,REBECCA DUNN,M.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST BIOPSY, NEEDLE LOCALIZATION (INCLUDING FSA): \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, microscopic foci (blocks #3 & #4), \u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm in overall aggregate area, focally present \u000awithin <0.1cm of the inked margin (see NOTE). \u000aFibrocystic change, proliferative with sclerosing adenosis, intraductal \u000apapillomatosis. \u000aMicrocalcifications are present in association with benign and neoplastic \u000aepithelial elements. \u000aRIGHT BREAST BIOPSY: \u000aFibrocystic change, proliferative with intraductal papillomatosis, \u000asclerosing adenosis, and microcalcifications. \u000aNOTE: The LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is arising in a complex sclerosing lesion, \u000aand microscopic foci (less than 0.1cm in diameter) of invasion cannot be \u000aabsolutely excluded. Slides #3 and #4 have been received by Dr. S. Lester and \u000aat staff surgical pathology conference. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aOperation: Biopsy, right breast, needle localization. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast calcifications. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast biopsy (needle localization). \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000a1. RIGHT BREAST MASS AND NEEDLE (FSA): \u000a0.5cm nodule noted at one end of specimen (FSA). \u000aRepresentative section shows benign sclerosing lesion, a focus of \u000aintraductal papilloma, and microcalcifications. \u000aNo tumor present. \u000a2. RIGHT BREAST MASS: \u000aNo areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma. \u000aRADIOLOGY: No calcifications in specimen, T. Frenna, MD. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BADIZADEGAN,KAMRAN,M.D. \u000aThe specimen was received fresh, in two (2) parts, each labeled with the \u000apatient's name and unit number. \u000aThe first part, labeled "#1", consists of a single fragment of yellow \u000afibrofatty tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ) with a localization wire in place. \u000aThere is a single, 0.4cm  firm, tan area sampled in FSA. The remaining breast \u000aparenchyma is fibrotic and focally hemorrhagic with no discreet lesions. \u000aMicro 1: FSRA, ESS, 1 frag. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Remaining tissue, ESS, multi frag. \u000aThe next part, labeled "#2 right breast mass", consists of a single fragment of \u000afibrofatty tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ). The tissue is slightly fibrotic with \u000ano focal lesions. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Right breast mass, ESS, 3 frag. \u000akb \u000aReports to: HAIGH, LINDA, SANDERS M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
