hology demonstrated papillary Ca. History of left breast \u000abiopsy  REMOVED_CASE_ID  - atypical ductal and atypical lobular hyperplasia. BS 05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , \u000abreast; BC 05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , thyroid. \u000aOperation: (R) breast wire loc lumpectomy, SNM, SLNB; possible ALND \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: (R) breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Sentinel node (R) hot x 2 - FS. \u000aB/2. (R) breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, whip stitch \u000achest wall - FS - mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: The mass and wire are within the specimen. Dr. Gombos. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT HOT SENTINEL NODE  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " (FSA): \u000aTwo lymph nodes; negative for tumor. \u000aOR Consultation by: JONATHAN NEIL GLICKMAN, M.D., PH.D. \u000aResident: PAULA C. ABREU-E-LIMA, M.D. \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Sentinel node (R) hot sentinel node x 2", consists of one \u000ayellow/tan piece of fibroadipose tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ), containing two \u000alymph nodes (1.2cm and 1.0cm in greatest diameter). The larger lymph node is \u000ainked blue and bisected, and the smaller lymph node is inked orange. Both \u000alymph nodes are submitted in their entirely as FSA. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : FSA remnant, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast tissue", consists of a breast excision \u000aspecimen measuring 6.2cm lateral to medial, 6.5cm superior to inferior, and \u000a2.0cm anterior to posterior. The specimen has one long suture marking the \u000alateral margin and one short suture marking 