VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Esther Rhei M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Rachel E Factor, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Lucian Chirieac, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY: \u000aFibroadenoma (1.3cm ), with atypical ductal hyperplasia. \u000aBiopsy site, chronic inflammation, ruptured cysts with giant cell \u000aReaction. \u000aProminent apocrine metaplasia, adenosis, epithelial hyperplasia, and \u000alactational change. \u000aCalcifications associated with benign tissue. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aThis case was reviewed by the Breast Pathology Service. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 47 yr old female (L) breast mass increased in size over serial \u000amammograms. S/P core needle biopsy Lahey Clinic REMOVED_DATE  \u000aOperation: (L) breast wire loc biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal (L) mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000a#1 Lt breast mass; short superior, long lateral, to mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Specimen shows mass, clip + wire (ILLEGIBLE SIGNATURE) \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number, \u000aand "Lt breast", and consists of a 6.6-gm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.2cm  fibrofatty \u000atissue fragment, inked and oriented per surgeon as follows: The specimen is \u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange, and \u000awith sutures designating superior (short suture) and lateral (long suture) \u000amargins. A localizing wire enters anteriorly and exits the specimen \u000aposteriorly. Sectioning demonstrates a nodular, circumscribed, tan/white, firm \u000amass abutting the superior, inferior, lateral and medial margins and within REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the anterior, and posterior margins (mass) is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.9cm  Mass \u000ademonstrates multifocal hemorrhage (15% of nodule). Specimen is received with \u000aan accompanying radiograph, which demonstrates the localizing wire in place \u000awithin the specimen, in addition a 0.3-cm, metallic, radiologic clip within the \u000amass. The entire specimen is submitted \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross-sections from anterior to posterior \u000a(Slice with radiologic clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), 12 frags, ESS. \u000adb/MMM \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by David Wu M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
