ast #2, 11:00", in a yellow cassette, and consists \u000aof multiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in aggregate). \u000aMicro 2: Multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart three, labeled "right breast #3, 8:30", in a white cassette, and consists \u000aof multiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm \u000ain aggregate). \u000aMicro 3: Multi frags, ESS. \u000akks \u000aReports to: FROST, ELISABETH, PEPPERELL M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES) \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES) \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES) \u000a[report_end] 
