n, there is a firm well-defined gray/white mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.0 x 1.0cm  The edges of the lesion are ill-defined with a slight scalloped \u000aappearance. The closet superior margin is grossly within 1mm  The remaining \u000amargins distances are as follows: inferior margin 1cm  lateral margin 1.2cm  \u000amedial margin 4cm  posterior margin 1.5cm  and anterior margin 1.5cm  The \u000aremaining breast tissue is soft red/yellow fibroadipose tissue. The specimen \u000ais entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : The entire tumor and closest superior and inferior margin, \u000a3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining superior margin, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of breast excision specimen, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aSF/mmm/PES \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a10/5/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
