VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D. \u000a1) LEFT BREAST, QUADRANTECTOMY (INCLUDING FSA): \u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA present as two (2) discrete nodules measuring \u000a3.3cm and at least 0.4cm (see NOTE). \u000aThe larger tumor is poorly differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson \u000agrade II/III) and is not present at the surgical resection margins. \u000aThe smaller tumor is well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade \u000aI/III) (tubular carcinoma) and is present at ink in an en face section \u000aof the inferior margin (block #6). \u000aLymphovascular invasion is identified adjacent to the larger tumor. \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, comedo type, is present in association with the \u000alarger tumor, comprises ten per cent (10%) of the invasive tumor, and is \u000anot found away from the invasive tumor. \u000aIn-situ carcinoma is present in two of eight blocks (blocks #2, #6) and \u000ais not present at the margin. \u000aNOTE: The tumor masses were approximately 2cm from one another and are \u000ahistologically dissimilar; thus, they probably represent two distinct \u000aprimaries. This case was reviewed at departmental staff conference. \u000aTumor from the larger tumor was sent for hormone receptor and flow \u000acytometry analysis. \u000a2) AXILLARY LYMPH NODE: \u000aEleven (11) lymph nodes with no tumor seen. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Left core needle biopsy (showing infiltrating cancer). \u000aOperation: Left Quadrantectomy, Axillary lymph node dissection \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Quadrantectomy - left \u000a#2. Axillary lymph node \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST QUADRANECTOMY (FSA):" \u000aTumor 3.3cm in greatest dimension. \u000aInfiltrating ductal carcinoma by FS. \u000aTumor extends to within 0.3cm of the inked margin. \u000aTumor submitted for ERICA and flow cytometry. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHU,GERALD CHEN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1. Quadrantectomy - left", consists of a tan/yellow \u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (7.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm ) with attached skin ellipse \u000a(4.5cm x 0.3cm ). The specimen contains a long stitch which is designated as \u000aanterior-superior, and a short stitch which is designated anterior-inferior. \u000aThere is a firm, spiculated, white/tan/yellow mass (3.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ) which \u000ais closest to the deep margin (0.3cm ). The mass is also 0.5cm of the lateral \u000amargin, 2.7cm of the medial margin, 1.5cm of the superior margin, and 2.2cm \u000aof the inferior margin. The remainder of the breast contains white/tan breast \u000atissue with several blue-domed cysts. A portion of the tumor was submitted for \u000aintraoperative analysis as FSA. The FSR was submitted for ERICA. A \u000arepresentative section of the tumor was also submitted for flow cytometry. \u000aMicro 1, skin, 1 fragment, RSS. \u000aMicro 2, deep margin, perpendicular, 1 fragment, RSS. \u000aMicro 3, lateral margin, perpendicular, 1 fragment, RSS. \u000aMicro 4, medial, en face margin, 1 fragment, RSS. \u000aMicro 5, superior, en face margin, 1 fragment, RSS. \u000aMicro 6, inferior, en face margin, 1 fragment, RSS. \u000aMiro REMOVED_DATE  tumor, 2 fragments, RSS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2. axillary lymph node", consists of one fragment of \u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (8.5 x 6 x 3.5cm ). Thirteen lymph nodes are \u000aidentified within the specimen. \u000aMicro 9, 1 lymph node, 3 fragments, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  1 lymph node, 5 fragments, ESS. \u000aMicro 12, 1 lymph node, 2 fragments, ESS. \u000aMicro 13, 2 lymph nodes, 4 fragments, ESS. \u000aMicro 14, 2 lymph nodes, 3 fragments, ESS. \u000aMicro 15, 1 lymph node, 3 fragments, ESS. \u000aMicro 16, 2 lymph nodes, 4 fragments, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  1 lymph node, 8 fragments, ESS. \u000aReports to: EBERLEIN, TIMOTHY, JOSEPH M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION \u000a[report_end] 
