VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP: \u000aBreast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia, fibroadenoma (in region of \u000aprior biopsy site), columnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts \u000aand secretions, and apocrine metaplasia. \u000aCore biopsy site and clip identified. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: History of core biopsy at Brigham and Women's Hospital REMOVED_DATE \u000aof left breast, calcs showing ADH; clip left. \u000aOperation: Left mammographically-directed breast biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - left breast tissue - short/superior, long/lateral. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HAHN,HEJIN P.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "left breast tissue, long/lateral, short/superior", and consists of a piece \u000aof breast tissue (4.3cm from superior to inferior, 4cm from medial to \u000alateral, 1.7cm from anterior to posterior), with two orienting sutures, placed \u000aby the surgeon to indicate superior and lateral, and a wire that is protruding \u000afrom the medial and posterior surface. The specimen is accompanied by a \u000aradiograph which demonstrates a clip. The specimen is inked per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; \u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The \u000aspecimen is radiographed, revealing a clip in an ill-defined area of fibrous \u000atissue, abutting the posterior margin. The specimen is 95% grossly \u000aunremarkable adipose tissue, with no lesions grossly identified. Also received \u000ain the container is a detached fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (2.3x \u000a1.9 x 0.5cm ). Approximately 70% of the entire specimen is submitted serially \u000afrom superior to inferior. All fibrous tissue is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro #1+2: Superior margin, 4 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro #3+4: Slice with clip, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro #5-10: Serial slices inferior to clip slice, multiple frags, RSS. \u000aMicro #11+12: Inferior margin, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro #13: Detached fragment of tissue, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
