VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBOROWSKY, ALEXANDER, D., M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BOROWSKY,ALEXANDER D.,M.D. \u000a1. LEFT BREAST, POSTERIOR, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY (BLOCKS 1-9): \u000aBenign breast tissue. \u000aApocrine metaplasia, epithelial hyperplasia, cyst formation, and \u000asclerosing adenosis. \u000aPrevious biopsy site present. \u000aNo residual atypical ductal hyperplasia is identified. \u000a2. LEFT BREAST, ANTERIOR, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY (BLOCKS 10-21): \u000aBenign breast tissue. \u000aApocrine metaplasia, epithelial hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis, and \u000acolumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions. \u000aOxylate calcifications are seen in association with apocrine cysts. \u000aLevels examined. \u000a3. RIGHT BREAST, INFERIOR, SUPERIOR, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY (BLOCKS 22-29): \u000aBenign breast tissue. \u000aApocrine metaplasia, epithelial hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis, and \u000acolumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions. \u000aOxylate calcifications are seen in association with apocrine cysts. \u000aLevels examined. \u000a4. RIGHT BREAST, SUPERIOR, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY (BLOCKS 30-40): \u000aBenign breast tissue with dense fibrotic stroma. (See note). \u000aApocrine metaplasia, epithelial hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis, and cyst \u000aformation. \u000aSee note. \u000aNOTE: The fibrotic dense area roughly corresponds to the radiologic density \u000aseen in the specimen radiograph. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aOperation: Left and right needle localized breast biopsy. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast posterior. \u000a2. Left breast anterior. \u000a3. Right breast inferior. \u000a4. Right breast superior. \u000aRadiology: Calcifications and clip in specimens, left. \u000aRadiology: Calcifications in specimen #3 and #4..........J. Meyer, M.D. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WOLGAMOT,GREGORY M.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in four parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1, left posterior", consists of a single fragment of \u000afirm fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm  A short stitch is \u000apresent designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral. A separate \u000awire accompanies the specimen. Also accompanying the specimen is a radiograph \u000athat shows the wire and a clip within the specimen. The specimen is inked per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior \u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. \u000aFirm tissue is encountered throughout this specimen and is grossly present at \u000aall margins. The entire specimen is submitted for histologic analysis. \u000aMicro 1: inferior margin, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue progressing from inferior to superior, 1 frag each, \u000aESS. (Micro 4 has the tissue around the clip). \u000aMicro 9: superior margin, multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2, left anterior", consists of a single mass of \u000afibroadipose tissue measuring 8 x 5 x 1cm  A short stitch designates superior \u000aand a long stitch designates lateral. A wire is present in the specimen. \u000aAccompanying this specimen is radiograph that shows calcifications in the \u000aregion of the bend of the wire. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol \u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = \u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Firm areas of tissue \u000aare encountered adjacent to the deep and anterior margins. No masses are found \u000ain the region of the wire. Representative samples are submitted for histologic \u000aexamination. Approximately 60% of the specimen is submitted per histologic \u000aanalysis. \u000aMicro 10: medial margin, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tissue around wire, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  firm tissue adjacent to anterior margin (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ), \u000amulti frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 18: firm tissue adjacent to posterior margin, (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm ), \u000a3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative margins, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aPart three, labeled "#3, right breast inferior", consists of a single \u000amass of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm  A short suture \u000adesignates superior, and a long suture and the wire have fallen from the \u000aspecimen. Per Dr. Shirley's advice, the superior portion of the specimen is \u000ainked in yellow and the inferior is inked in black. A nodule of white firm \u000atissue (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ) is found adjacent to the inferior margin. The \u000aentire specimen is submitted for histologic examination. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  firm tissue adjacent to inferior margin, 2 frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aPart four, labeled "#4, right breast superior", and consists of a mass of \u000afibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm  A short stitch designates \u000asuperior, long stitch designates lateral, and a wire protrudes from the \u000asuperior lateral portion of the specimen. Firm white tissue is present at the \u000aanterior and posterior margin at the inferior portion of the specimen. The \u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral \u000a= yellow; medial = orange. 80% of the specimen is submitted for histologic \u000aanalysis. \u000aMicro 30: firm tissue at inferior pole, multi frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  firm tissue adjacent to margins, multi frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative margins, multi frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 40: superior pole, multi frags, RSS. \u000agmw \u000aReports to: SHIRLEY, ROBERT, LAWRENCE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
