ibrous area best seen in slice #3 and #4 measuring \u000a0.8 x 0.9cm and located 0.3cm to the medial margin, 0.7cm to the lateral \u000amargin, 0.5cm to the posterior margin, and 0.3cm to the anterior margin. \u000aThis area is located approximately 1.0cm from the superior margin and 2.5cm \u000afrom the inferior margin. Of note, the specimen was received pre-inked with \u000aaspects of the specimen only approximately correctly identified by the ink. \u000aSpecimen is submitted for histologic review in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #1, perpendicular sections, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7, perpendicular sections, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMDH/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
