hip stitch \u000adeep margin. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000aMR number, and "#1. Right breast tissue with short stitch superior, long \u000alateral, whip-stitch deep margin", and consists of a lumpectomy specimen (5.0 \u000acm medial to lateral, 4.0cm superior to inferior, 1.6cm anterior to \u000aposterior). A wire enters the specimen from the medial to lateral side. A \u000ashort stitch designates superior aspect, long designates lateral, and \u000awhip-stitch designates deep margin. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. \u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a fibrotic area abutting the \u000ainferior margin consistent with a core biopsy site (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm ). A \u000aclip is identified within the area of fibrosis immediately adjacent to the \u000ainferior margin. The entire specimen is submitted for histology. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lumpectomy, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contain the area of fibrosis described above. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contain area marked by the clip. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000akst/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on Thursday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 08,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05:44:11PM \u000a[report_end] 
