VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Kevin Golden, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP MARKING A PREVIOUS BIOPSY SITE \u000aAND CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU with ductal and lobular features, solid type (low to \u000afocally high nuclear grade), is present in 19 of 20 slides (see note). \u000aCalcifications are present in CIS. No necrosis is seen. \u000aThe CIS with the highest nuclear grade is adjacent to the prior core \u000aneedle biopsy site. \u000aCIS is < 0.1cm from the anterior, posterior, medial, lateral, and \u000ainferior margins. The superior margin is not well seen. \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for \u000aCIS (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE - LOW \u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu NEGATIVE (0) \u000aE-cadherin NEGATIVE \u000aNote: The patient underwent a prior core needle biopsy for \u000acalcifications that showed CIS with mixed features that was negative for ER, \u000aPR, and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). In this specimen, the CIS with the highest \u000anuclear grade is adjacent to the core site. In the remainder of the \u000aspecimen, there is extensive CIS. Although approximately 50% of the CIS could \u000abe classified as lobular carcinoma in situ, these areas are intermingled \u000awith foci with higher nuclear grade. The lower grade CIS shows more ER \u000apositivity than the higher grade CIS, but lacks PR. The absence of PR would \u000abe unusual for typical LCIS. This finding supports classifying all the CIS \u000aas the same process and as having mixed features. \u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th edition) Tis NX. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: DCIS, Right breast. \u000aOperation: Right partial mastectomy. \u000aOperative Findings: Specimen mammo with clip. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast DCIS. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Right breast tissue with wire. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications and clips are present in specimen radiograph. \u000aCalled to OR by Hesham Malik, MD. At 12;10 PM on Sept. 29,  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name \u000aand medical record number, and "Right breast mass". The specimen consists of a \u000awire localized excision (27.6-g; 5.5cm medial to lateral, 2.1cm superior to \u000ainferior, 5.1cm anterior to posterior). The specimen was inked per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; \u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. An accompanying \u000aspecimen radiograph reveals a wire and a clip associated with a density and \u000acalcifications within the center of the specimen. Other clips that appear \u000asurgical are present. There is a white/tan irregular firm mass (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) that is located in the area of the wire tip. This mass abuts the inferior \u000amargin and is 0.6cm from the superior margin, 1.5cm from the lateral margin, \u000a0.9cm from the medial margin, 1.5cm from the anterior margin, and 1.2cm from \u000athe posterior margin. The blocks are radiographed and the clip is in cassette \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The entire specimen is examined microscopically. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, 3 frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of specimen, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin, 3 frags each, ESS. \u000aKG/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a10/6/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
