VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Surgical margin \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Shakti Ramkissoon, M.D., Ph.D.; Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, SUPERIOR MARIGIN, RE-EXCISION: \u000aExcision site changes are present. \u000aNo residual carcinoma in situ seen. \u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis. \u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, INFERIOR MARGIN, RE-EXCISION: \u000aResidual CARCINOMA IN SITU with mixed features, solid type, (low and \u000aintermediate nuclear grade), is present in 7 of 7 blocks. \u000aNo necrosis or calcifications are associated with CIS. \u000aCIS is present at the inferior and lateral margins, and is < 0.1cm from the \u000amedial margin. \u000aExtensive excision site changes are present. \u000aNote: Immunohistochemical stains for ER and PR show the CIS is ER positive and \u000aPR negative ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aC. RIGHT BREAST, DEEP INFERIOR MARGIN, RE-EXCISION: \u000aResidual CARCINOMA IN SITU with mixed features, solid type, (low and \u000aintermediate nuclear grade), is present in 4 of 7 blocks. \u000aNo necrosis or calcifications are associated with CIS. \u000aCIS is focally present at the inferior margin and < 0.1cm from the anterior \u000amargin (see Note). \u000aExcision site changes are present. \u000aImmunohistochemical stains for ER and PR show the CIS is ER positive and PR \u000anegative ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aNote: The margins are difficult to evaluate due to specimen fragmentation and \u000aink leakage. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: DCIS; superior margin 2mm (close); inferior margin <1mm \u000aOperation: Right re-excision, partial mastectomy. \u000aOperative Findings: None specified. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Right breast biopsy(superior margin), standard ink on all margins. \u000aB/2) Right breast biopsy (inferior margin), standard ink on all margins. \u000aC/3) (Deep inferior margin), right breast biopsy, standard ink on all margins. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast biopsy, superior margin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a2.0cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by inks per surgeon. Please \u000anote: Specimen deviates from typical pathology breast inking protocol, and is \u000ainked as follows: Superior - red, inferior - green, anterior - blue, posterior \u000a- black, medial - yellow, lateral - orange (per operative report). Discrepancy \u000ahas been confirmed with the surgeon, who concurs. The inferior surface of the \u000aspecimen is comprised of a biopsy cavity wall; sectioning demonstrates fibrous \u000acyst and fat necrosis along with surface, without definitive additional \u000aabnormalities noted grossly. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial \u000a(yellow) to lateral (orange), with perpendicular medial margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and \u000aperpendicular lateral margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Tissue is held for further fixation prior \u000ato processing. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, perpendicular section, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Serial sections, medial to lateral, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, perpendicular section, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast biopsy, inferior margin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.4cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented with inks by the surgeon. The \u000aspecimen appears to be inked appropriately; however, blue and black ink cannot \u000abe definitively discerned. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for \u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by surgeon). The entire \u000asuperior surface of the specimen is comprised of a biopsy cavity wall; \u000asectioning reveals fibrosis and fat necrosis along this surface, without \u000adefinitive residual lesional tissue noted grossly. The entire specimen is \u000asubmitted, sequentially from presumed anterior to presumed posterior with \u000apresumed anterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and presumed posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen, presumably from anterior to posterior, multi \u000afrags, ESS. \u000aThe specimen will be held for further fixation prior to processing. \u000aPart C, "#3. Right breast biopsy, deep inferior margin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x \u000a3.8 x 1.4cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by the surgeon with \u000ainks. Please note: Only three definitive ink colors are discernible on the \u000aspecimen; red, green, and yellow. One broad surface appears to be comprised of \u000abiopsy cavity wall has been marked with red ink and is presumed superior. The \u000aopposing surface has been marked with green inked and is presumed to be new \u000ainferior margin. One edge of the specimen exhibits yellow ink, and is presumed \u000ato lateral, according to pathology breast inking protocol. There are no \u000adefinitive additional discernible colors on the specimen. Sectioning \u000ademonstrates fibrosis and fat necrosis along the biopsy cavity wall, with no \u000adefinitive residual lesional tumor noted grossly. The entire specimen is \u000asubmitted, sequentially from the yellow - inked edge (presumably lateral to \u000amedial), with perpendicular ends in micro cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen, sequentially firm yellow - inked edge, multi \u000afrags, ESS. \u000aPlease note: This specimen will be held for further fixation prior to \u000aprocessing. \u000aDB/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 11,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05:31:06PM \u000a[report_end] 
