beled with the patient's name \u000aand medical record number. \u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right total mastectomy - short stitch, superior and long \u000astitch, lateral", consists of a mastectomy specimen (915.0 grams, 24.0cm \u000asuperior to inferior, 23.0cm medial to lateral, 4.0cm anterior to posterior) \u000awith skin ellipse (8.5 x 3.2cm ) with areola (3.0 x 2.2cm ) and with everted \u000anipple (1.0cm in diameter x 0.8cm in height). There are two orienting \u000asutures with short superior and long lateral per surgeon. The deep aspect of \u000athe specimen is inked black. There is a cavity, which is opened to both the \u000adeep/posterior and anterior aspect of the specimen with an opening measuring \u000a3.2 x 2.2cm with the anterior-posterior dimension measuring 3.2cm  The \u000acavity is located in the central outer aspect of the specimen and is lateral to \u000athe lateral aspect of the skin ellipse. Sectioning the specimen reveals no \u000aother lesions. The specimen is approximately 10% fibrous and 90% adipose \u000atissue. In addition, there are separately received attached fragments of \u000afibroadipose tissue (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 3.2cm in aggregate). No lymph nodes or \u000askeletal muscle are grossly identified. The cavity is entirely submitted for \u000ahistologic evaluation. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial aspect of cavity with skin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior aspect of cavity, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior aspect of cavity with skin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag each, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral aspect of cavity with skin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast skin", consists of an ovoid donut-shaped \u000afragment of skin (outer ovoid dimension REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and inner ovoid dimension \u000a9.7 x 3.6cm  with width range, REMOVED_DATE to 1.1cm  and depth up to 0.6cm ). There \u000ais a well-healed linear scar (2.5cm ) that extends to skin edge. The deep \u000aaspect of the specimen is inked blue. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Scar, 5 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional representative sections of skin, 3 frag, RSS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aGL/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aWednesday February 25,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 08:21:50PM \u000a[report_end] 
