rior \u000ainferior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol \u000a(superior red, inferior green, lateral yellow, medial orange, anterior blue and \u000aposterior black) and inferiorly sectioned from anterior to posterior. There is \u000aa dense well-circumscribed fibrous nodule (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ) which abuts the \u000amedial and anterior margin, and is located 0.5cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the superior margin, 0.9cm from the posterior margin, and 2.2cm from \u000athe anterior margin. Remainder of the breast parenchyma is tan/yellow and \u000ahomogeneous with no additional lesions or areas of disruption identified. The \u000aspecimen is radiographed and displays a clip adjacent to the previously \u000adescribed lesion. The specimen is submitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections anterior to posterior block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to \u000ainclude nodules encrypt designated area, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Tan A Ince M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a12/26/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
