acent to the localization wire. The specimen is inked per pathology \u000aprotocol. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange. The tissue consists of dense \u000afibrous parenchyma (75%) and adipose tissue (25%). The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, perpendicular sections, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body to include area of calcifications in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , multi frags \u000atotal, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin, perpendicular sections, 4 frags, ESS. \u000almc/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 10,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04:48:54PM \u000a[report_end] 
