ion wire in place (entering at the \u000asuperior aspect). The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol \u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned from inferior to superior, exhibiting approximately equal proportions \u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue and white/pink, diffusely cystic (cyst \u000ameasuring up to 0.7cm in greatest dimension) fibrous stroma. As confirmed by \u000athe accompanying radiograph and radiology "calcs and wire are in specimen". \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast, fibrous tissue, sequentially from superior to inferior, \u000amulti frags, ESS. \u000aDFI/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM: \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including the margins. \u000aAddendum #1 by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
