rrounds the biopsy cavity with depth of REMOVED_DATE to 4.5cm in the \u000asuperior/posterior aspect of the specimen (3.0cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the posterior margin); 40% of the specimen consists of fibrous tissue. \u000aThe remainder of tissue consists of adipose tissue. Gross photographs are \u000ataken of the specimen. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, perpendicular sections, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, en face section, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy site in relation to inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy site, lateral aspect, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy site, medial aspect of site, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy site in relation to skin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy site, superior aspect, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy site, posterior aspect, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue surrounding biopsy site,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 frags,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , \u000a1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Area of wire localization for calcification, 2 frags \u000aeach, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Area lateral to wire localization site,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag, \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Area medial to wire localization site for calcification, \u000a1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral resection margin, perpendicular section, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial resection margin, perpendicular section, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Unoriented fragments of biopsy cavity, 