D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart 1, "left breast tissue", consists of four fragments of yellow/tan breast \u000atissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm in aggregate). No wire is identified. Sectioning \u000areveals 30% of the specimen is fibrous tissue. The specimen is inked and \u000aentirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS. \u000aPart 2, "additional left breast tissue", consists of three fragments of \u000atan/yellow fibroadipose soft tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm om aggregate). The \u000aspecimen is inked and entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Additional breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS. \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
