VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast biopsy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME -HELLEGERS \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Patricia A. R. Brunker, M.D., D. Phil.; Shakti Ramkissoon, M.D., \u000aPh.D. \u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and cribriform types, (high nuclear grade) with \u000anecrosis and calcifications. \u000aNo invasive carcinoma is seen. \u000aDCIS is present in six (6) of thirteen (13) blocks and involves an area \u000ameasuring up to 1.0cm on glass slide. \u000aThe closest margin is superior, 0.3cm (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). Other margins are >0.5cm \u000aaway. \u000aRadial scar, papilloma, florid hyperplasia and prior biopsy site are also \u000apresent. \u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone \u000areceptor, and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu will be performed and reported in an addendum. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 50 year old female s/p stereo core L (+) ADH REMOVED_DATE  surgical excision \u000arevealed columnar atypia but clip and evidence of prior biopsy not found. On \u000ascreening mammogram this year elevated microcalcs surg bed seen in recommended \u000afor re-excision. \u000aOperation: left wire localized breast biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast microcalcification. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Left breast tissue, short superior, long lateral suture - green = \u000ainferior, yellow = lateral, black = posterior, red = superior, blue = anterior, \u000aorange = medial. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen radiograph shows intact wire with clip, mass and \u000acalcifications. OR called at 3:12 pm. CW/SR. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1. Left breast tissue, short superior, long lateral", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x \u000a3.8 x 3.7cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating \u000asuperior (short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins. The specimen is \u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange \u000a(inked by surgeon). A localizing wire enters the lateral aspect of the \u000aspecimen and traverses medially. The specimen is received with a radiograph \u000ademonstrating the localizing wire in place within the specimen, adjacent to a \u000ametallic surgical clip. Sectioning demonstrates scarred-appearing tan/white \u000afibrous tissue involving 30% to 40% of the tissue, particularly along the \u000ainferior aspect, with fibrous tissue radiating to the inferior, anterior, \u000aposterior, and superior surfaces, within 0.7cm of the medial margin and 1.2cm \u000aof the closest lateral margin. The metallic clip is situated just lateral to \u000athis scarred area. There are no identifiable masses grossly. Remaining \u000aparenchyma is comprised of firm tan/yellow adipose tissue. The entire specimen \u000ais submitted, sequentially from lateral to medial, with perpendicular lateral \u000amargin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , perpendicular medial margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and section bearing \u000ametallic clip in micro cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Multi frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aDB/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a6/10/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (6/13/08) \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for DCIS: \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE-LOW \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) WEAKLY POSITIVE (EQUIVOCAL) (2+) \u000aNOTE: FISH analysis for amplification of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu may be helpful, if \u000aclinically warranted. \u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the \u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet \u000abeen determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a \u000aportion of the membrane is positive. \u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of \u000atumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of \u000atumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational \u000ause only. \u000aAddendum #1 by Tan A Ince M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
