VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000a"RIGHT BREAST MASS", BIOPSY: \u000aRuptured cyst lined by cells with both apocrine and squamous \u000ametaplasia with extensive chronic inflammation and granulation \u000atissue (1.0cm ) (see note). \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (block 1, levels examined). \u000aFibrocystic change with florid proliferation. \u000aSclerosing adenosis and complex sclerosing lesions associated \u000awith microcalcifications. \u000aNOTE: The presence of squamous metaplasia suggests "squamous \u000ametaplasia of lactiferous ducts". However, the absence of a \u000aforeign body giant cell reaction in response to keratin is \u000aunusual for this entity. \u000a(Clinical: patient with recurrent cyst near areola). \u000aReferences: \u000aAM J SURG 119:523 (70). \u000aAM J SURG 144:359 (82). \u000aS MED J 70:935 (77). \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Recurrent cyst, right breast. Ultra-sound shows "irregularity \u000ain wall of cyst". \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Tissue, right breast. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000a"RIGHT BREAST MASS": \u000aFibrofatty tissue with 1.0cm grossly benign cyst. \u000aNo areas grossly suspicious for invasive tumor. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WANG,PETER LINCOLN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aReceived fresh, labelled "right breast mass" is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm white/yellow \u000afragment of fibrofatty tissue mainly composed of white fibrous tissue, \u000acontaining a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cyst with thin yellowish wall containing cloudy \u000afluid. \u000aMicros #1-6: Right breast biopsy, ESS, multiple frags, 6 cass. \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
