VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000a1. RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY WIRE LOCALIZATION: \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia without atypia. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aNote: No radiologic calcifications were seen in this specimen after \u000aradiography by the radiology department. \u000a2. RIGHT BREAST SCAR TISSUE: \u000aSkin with cicatrix. \u000a3. RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY, ADDITIONAL TISSUE: \u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, present in two of six blocks (#12 \u000aand #13; levels examined) (see note). \u000aThe radiologic calcifications are identified in block #13 and are \u000aassociated with the area of atypical hyperplasia in this block. \u000aThe atypical ductal hyperplasia is within 0.1cm of the margin adjacent to \u000athe attached suture (marked with green ink). \u000aNote: The two foci of ADH measure less than 0.1cm in size. The focus in \u000ablock #12 has low grade nuclei and micropapillae. However, only one space \u000ais involved and the area measures less than 0.2cm  thus not warrenting a \u000adiagnosis of DCIS. \u000aThe radiologic calcifications were identified in this specimen after \u000aradiography by the radiology department. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 43 year old premenopasual female status post REMOVED_DATE right breast \u000aexcision and re-excision of ADH/DCIS, now with right breast \u000amammo CA+, not ammenable to core biopsy. \u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization partial mastectomy \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast wire partial mastectomy \u000ashort suture - superior \u000along suture - lateral \u000awhip stitch - chest wall \u000a#2. Right breast scar tissue \u000a#3. Right breast re-excision, partial mastectomy \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000a#3. RIGHT BREAST: \u000aBreast tissue with no gross evidence of invasive carcinoma. \u000aCalcifications seen on 2nd specimen; none seen on 1st. S. Harvey, M.D. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WENG,ANDREW PHILIP,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, "#1. right breast wire localized partial mastectomy", consists of a \u000asingle oriented fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (3cm from superior \u000ato inferior, 4.0cm from medial to lateral and 1.3cm from superficial to deep) \u000awith a needle localization wire in place. The specimen is oriented with three \u000astitches. The margins of the specimens are inked as follows: superficial blue, \u000adeep black, medial green, lateral yellow, superior red, and inferior orange. \u000aNo areas are identified which are grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma. \u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro 1, lateral margin, perpendicular sections, 3 fragments, ESS. \u000aMicro 2, medial margin, perpendicular sections, 2 fragments, ESS. \u000aMicro 3, inferior margin, perpendicular sections, 5 fragments, ESS. \u000aMicro 4, superior margin, perpendicular sections, 6 fragments, ESS. \u000aMicro 5, superficial margin, perpendicular sections, 5 fragments, ESS. \u000aMicro 6, deep margin, perpendicular sections, 6 fragments, ESS. \u000aPart two, "#2. right breast scar tissue", consists of a single oriented \u000atan/white skin ellipse (3 x 0.5cm excised to a depth of 1.1cm ) with a well \u000ahealed surgical scar (3cm ) which is longitudinally oriented with the specimen \u000aand is 0.1cm from the closest lateral margin. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro 7, right breast scar, 1 fragment, ESS. \u000aPart three, "#3. right breast re-excision partial mastectomy", consists of a \u000asingle fragment of oriented yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.5 x 2 x 0.5cm ) \u000awhich is oriented by a single stitch on one side. The side with the whip \u000astitch is inked in green and the remainder of the specimen is inked in black. \u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro 8, ends, perpendicular sections, 4 fragments, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  cross sections, multiple fragments, ESS. \u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN, PLASTIC REPAIR \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
