VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Stacey A. Simons, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, DUCT EXCISION FOR NIPPLE DISCHARGE: \u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, bordering on ductal carcinoma in situ, \u000apartially involving a papilloma (see note). \u000aIntraductal papillomas (largest 0.5cm ). \u000aDuctal epithelial hyperplasia. \u000aColumnar cell change. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aLevels examined. \u000aNote: The atypical ductal hyperplasia is present in one of fifteen blocks and \u000ais focally close (0.25cm ) to the posterior margin (see below for additional \u000amargin). \u000aSelected slides reviewed by Dr. S. Lester who concurs. \u000aLEFT BREAST, "NODULE AT POSTERIOR-LATERAL MARGIN", EXCISION: \u000aIntraductal papilloma (0.6cm ) with usual ductal hyperplasia. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 75 year old woman with left breast spontaneous nipple discharge. \u000aOperation: Left breast biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left nipple discharge. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) left breast tissue - green/ant, black/post, red/sup, blue/inf, orange/med, \u000ayellow/lateral. \u000aB/2) left breast nodule @ posterior-lateral margin. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname, unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "left breast tissue", and consists of a previously inked \u000aportion of fibrofatty tissue, which is received inked as follows: anterior \u000agreen, posterior black, superior red, inferior blue, medial orange and lateral \u000ayellow. The specimen measures 5.0cm from medial to lateral, 4.5cm from \u000ainferior to superior and 1.0cm from anterior to posterior. The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal approximately 70% yellow \u000alobulated adipose tissue, and 30% nodular white fibrous tissue, with no \u000adiscrete masses or lesions identified. The nodular fibrous tissue comes to REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial margin, 1.0cm from the lateral margin, 0.1cm from the \u000aposterior margin, 0.1cm from the anterior margin, 0.8cm from the inferior \u000amargin and 1.0cm from the superior margin. The specimen is submitted in its \u000aentirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, radially ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /3 frags;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /2 frags), ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross section, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left breast nodule posterolateral margin", consists of an \u000aunoriented tan-pink irregular soft tissue (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ). The specimen \u000ais inked black and bisected to reveal tan cut surface. The specimen is \u000asubmitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast nodule, bisected, 2 frags, ESS. \u000acp/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on \u000a6/20/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
