ening tissue between \u000athe two wires. The calcifications appear posterolateral, per radiograph. \u000aSectioning demonstrates tan/yellow lobulated adipose tissue (at least 85%), \u000aadmixed with unremarkable, granular, tan/white, fibrodense tissue, \u000apredominantly posterolaterally. There are no obvious masses, lesions or other \u000aabnormalities grossly. The entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from \u000alateral to medial, with perpendicular lateral margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , perpendicular \u000amedial margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the area of interest per localizing wires in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from lateral to \u000amedial, with perpendicular lateral margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , perpendicular medial margin in \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the area of interest per localizing wires in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , multiple frags \u000atotal, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aDB/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
