itive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity \u000ain >10% of tumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational \u000ause only. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aOperation: Excision of left breast mass \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast mass \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHEN,JEY-HSIN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen, received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and \u000a"left breast mass", is an unoriented tan/pink soft tissue (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm ). \u000aThe external surface is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to \u000areveal a lobulated pink/yellow color on cut surface. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - serial sections with ends taken perpendicularly, 11 frags, ESS. \u000aReports to: REILLY, RAYMOND, JOHN, M.B.B.C.H. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
