VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS: \u000aSingle focus (0.15cm ) of severely atypical ductal hyperplasia with \u000aassociated microcalcifications (block 2; present on original level \u000aonly; levels examined); this focus is present 0.22cm from posterior \u000aresection margin. \u000aFibrocystic changes including apocrine metaplasia, cyst formation, a \u000acomplex sclerosing lesion (0.6cm ) and collagenous spherulosis (benign). \u000aHemorrhage and granulation tissue consistent with FNA site associated with \u000aa cluster of benign cysts (0.6cm ). \u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, of breast pathology \u000aservice, who concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Left breast mass; patient with history of ADH in  REMOVED_CASE_ID ; \u000acurrently on Tamoxifen. \u000aOperation: Excision \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue - short suture superior, long suture \u000alateral \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE" (GROSS EXAMINATION ONLY): \u000aFibrous breast parenchyma with recent hemorrhage. \u000aNo gross evidence of neoplasia. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WOLGAMOT,GREGORY M.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number \u000aand "left breast tissue", and consists of a single portion of yellow/tan \u000afibroadipose tissue (2.5 x 2 x 1cm ) with a long and short orienting suture in \u000aplace. The specimen is diffusely fibrous and has a recent hemorrhagic tract in \u000athe center, but no gross evidence of invasive carcinoma. The specimen is inked \u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; \u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = \u000aorange. No frozen is performed, intraoperative gross exam only. The specimen \u000ais entirely submitted for histologic examination. \u000aMicro sections: \u000aMicro 1: medial pole, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  specimen, medial to lateral, multiple frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 6: lateral pole, multiple frags, ESS. \u000aReports to: SHIRLEY, ROBERT, LAWRENCE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
