 two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, "#1. R axillary sentinel node", consists of a tan rubbery lymph node \u000a(1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ), which is bisected and submitted in its entirety for \u000afrozen section as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast, stitch short superior, long lateral", consists of a \u000aright simple mastectomy (220 g, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.8cm ), with a long suture \u000adesignating lateral, and a short suture designating superior. There is an \u000aoverlying unremarkable tan skin ellipse (6.7 x 1.8cm ), with an unremarkable \u000anipple areolar complex (2.5 x 1.8cm ), with an everted nipple (1.5cm in \u000adiameter). The posterior margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially \u000asectioned to reveal a well-healed biopsy cavity (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm ), located \u000abetween the upper inner and lower inner quadrants. The cavity contains a \u000asurgical clip, and is 1.0cm from the closest black-inked posterior margin, and \u000ais located directly posterior to the nipple, 1.8cm  The remaining cut surface \u000adisplays 50% focally dense white fibrous tissue, and 50% yellow lobulated \u000aadipose tissue, with no additional discrete masses or lesions identified. No \u000alymph nodes are identified. Representative sections are submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy cavity, sequentially from lateral to medial, with the clip \u000aidentified in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue from upper outer quadrant, to include the posterior \u000amargin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue from lower outer quadrant, to include the posterior \u000amargin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : White fibrous tissue from lower inner quadrant, to include the \u000aposterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue from upper inner quadrant, to include the \u000aposterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 frags each, RSS. \u000acp/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
