VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aHORNICK, JASON, L., M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by HORNICK,JASON L.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS: \u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR (2.2cm ), low grade, with myofibroblastoma-like features. \u000aThe tumor is present at the lateral margin and is <0.1cm from the \u000aposterior, inferior, and superior margins. \u000aThe medial and anterior margins are negative for tumor (>0.3cm ). \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia. \u000aImmunohistochemical staining for PAN-K is negative in the spindle cells. \u000aNOTE: This case was also reviewed by Dr. J. Connolly (Breast Pathology \u000aService), who concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 43 year old nulliparous premenopausal female, not on hormones with a \u000afamily history of breast cancer in her mother and maternal aunt. \u000aright breast UOQ palpable mass with 2.5cm hypoechoic area on U/S not \u000aamenable to core biopsy. \u000aOperation: Right breast excisional biopsy \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast mass - short superior; long lateral \u000a(with stitch deep margin) \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHEN,JEY-HSIN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number \u000aand "#1. right breast, short superior, long lateral", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x \u000a2.5 x 2.0cm breast tissue with attached orienting sutures: a short stitch \u000amarking the superior surface and a long stitch marking the lateral surface. \u000aThe specimen is received inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of \u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; \u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from \u000alateral to medial surfaces, revealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm white/tan firm \u000afocally cystic well-circumscribed lesion abutting the superior, posterior and \u000ainferior surfaces and extends to within less than 0.1cm from the closest \u000ainferior, lateral, and 0.2cm from the closest medial margin. The specimen is \u000aentirely submitted. \u000aMicro 1: lateral margin, perpendicular, 5 frags ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections lateral to medial, 6 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, perpendicular, 8 frags, ESS \u000ajhc \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
