VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Paula C Abreu-e-Lima, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP: \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present. \u000aCalcifications are associated with benign epithelium, sclerosing adenosis, and \u000asmall cysts. \u000aThe prior core needle biopsy site is present. \u000aNote: No invasive carcinoma or DCIS are seen after microscopic examination of \u000athe specimen, including all fibrous tissue and margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Right breast atypical hyperplasia (lobular) on needle core biopsy for \u000acalcifications. \u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast atypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right breast wire localized biopsy, short suture superior long suture \u000alateral to mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aWire, clip, calcifications in specimen. Spoke with J. Carrigan in OR B. \u000aTownsend, M.D. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number, \u000aand "Right breast wire localized biopsy, short suture superior, long suture \u000alateral", and consists of a breast excision specimen (5.0cm from medial to \u000alateral x 3.4cm superior to inferior x 2.2cm from anterior to posterior) \u000acontaining a single localization wire and two sutures (per surgeon: short \u000asuture = superior, long suture = lateral). The specimen is inked per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; \u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The accompanying \u000aspecimen radiograph shows a single clip and the localization wire, both present \u000awithin a dense area containing microcalcifications. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm core biopsy \u000acavity, filled with beads and surrounded by areas of hemorrhage. It extends to \u000awithin 0.2cm of the anterior, 0.7cm of the inferior, 0.8cm of the posterior, \u000a1.1cm of the superior, 1.6cm of the medial, and 1.7cm of the lateral margin. \u000aNo masses are grossly identified. 95% of the specimen is submitted, including \u000aall fibrous tissue. The area containing the clip is placed in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Prior core biopsy site to anterior and inferior margins, 1 frag, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Core biopsy site to anterior, inferior, and posterior margins, \u000a1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Core biopsy site to anterior, inferior, and posterior margins, \u000a1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional core biopsy site, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue present in the specimen to include margins, \u000amulti frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining fibrous tissue, mult frags, ESS. \u000aPal/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a10/5/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
