he posterior margin. The remainder of the \u000abreast parenchyma is yellow/tan and fatty with no discrete lesions identified. \u000aGross photographs are taken. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic \u000aevaluation. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass to medial and anterior margins, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass to anterior, posterior, and lateral margins, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass to anterior, posterior, and lateral margins, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass to medial margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial and posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS (medial to lateral). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of specimen submitted medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE frags \u000aeach, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aTR/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a11/13/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
