VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aFLETCHER, CHRISTOPHER, D.M., M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by FLETCHER,CHRISTOPHER D.M.,M.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS: \u000aBreast parenchyma with atypical ductal hyperplasia, fibroadenoma (0.4cm ), \u000asclerosing adenosis, apocrine metaplasia, microscopic intraductal \u000apapillomas with associated squamous metaplasia. \u000aSecretory changes are present focally. \u000aThere is NO malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by FLETCHER,CHRISTOPHER D.M.,M.D. \u000aScarring and focal fat necrosis consistent with prior biopsy site are \u000aidentified in block #1, corresponding to the area of most striking atypical \u000aductal hyperplasia and sclerosing adenosis. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 52 y/o female s/p REMOVED_DATE core biopsy of palpable lump with no \u000amammogram correlate & subtle u/s mass revealing ADH & complex sclerosing \u000alesion. \u000aOperation: L breast wire localization excision. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast mass with ADH. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue with needle - suture marks long \u000alateral & color markings per path protocol. Short superior, whipstitch deep \u000amargin. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass is in the specimen. D.Smith \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LIN,JONATHAN H.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received in one part, labeled with the patient's name, unit \u000anumber and "#1 left breast tissue with needle, long lateral, short superior, \u000awhip stitch deep margin". The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; \u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is received \u000awith the accompanying radiograph that reveals a wire localization in place \u000aalong with a mass. The specimen consists of breast parenchymal tissue (3.5 x \u000a3.0 x 1.5cm ), received with two sutures that have been designated short \u000asuperior, long lateral and whip stitch = deep. Sectioning of the specimen \u000areveals a white, fibrotic area interspered with possible core biopsy site that \u000ameasure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm and appears to come to less than 0.5cm from the \u000agreen inked, red inked, yellow inked margins. No further lesions are \u000aidentified in the remaining breast parenchyma which consists entirely of \u000ayellow adipose tissue. The specimen is sectioned and entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area of fibrosis/core biopsy site, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remaining specimen, 9 frags, ESS. \u000ajhl \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
