VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST EXCISION, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU with atypical nuclei (intermediate to high \u000anuclear grade), extensive with associated calcifications. \u000aNOTE: The proliferation involves both ducts and lobules with reactive large \u000auniform cells with cellular adhesion consistent with lobular \u000adifferentiation. However, the nuclei are larger and more atypical than \u000ais usually seen in LCIS. The clinical behavior of this type of lesion \u000ais uncertain. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 53 year old postmenopausal female whose REMOVED_DATE mamograms \u000ademonstrate L breast calcifications for which wire localization \u000a& excision is recommended. \u000aOperation: L breast wire localization and excision. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: L abnormal mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. L left breast tissue - short stitch superior, long \u000alateral, stitch on deep margin. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++ in specimen. OR called @ 10:40 a.m. CG \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DAVID,FRANK SAMUEL,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000aunit number and "#1 left breast tissue", and consists of a single mass of \u000afibroadipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm  There is a localizing wire protruding \u000athe specimen, the specimen is oriented with a long suture and short suture \u000amarking the lateral and superior aspects, respectively. The specimen has been \u000ainked by the operating room for the evaluation of margins. The specimen is \u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; \u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = \u000aorange. The interior of the mass is grossly unremarkable, without any discrete \u000amasses or suspicious lesions. The mass is serially sectioned and entirely \u000asubmitted. A mammogram accompanied the specimen demonstrating the presence of \u000aa localizing wire and calcifications. \u000aMicro 1: lateral, ESS. \u000aMicro 2: medial, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, lateral to medial, ESS. \u000afsd \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
