4cm ), containing a surgical clip, as identified on the accompanying \u000aradiograph. The biopsy cavity is 0.4cm from the inferior margin, 2.5cm from \u000athe superior margin, 0.5cm from the lateral margin, 1.2cm from the medial \u000amargin, 1.0cm from the posterior margin and 2.5cm from the anterior margin. \u000aThe remaining cut surface displays 60% focally dense white fibrous tissue, and \u000a40% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no discrete masses or lesions \u000aidentified. The specimen is sequentially submitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections, from posterior to anterior, with the \u000abiopsy cavity in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the surgical clip identified in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag each, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000acp/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
