 \u000aaspect of the specimen and exiting the inferolateral aspect of the specimen. \u000aThe specimen was previously radiographed, confirming the presence of a clip \u000awithin the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral \u000ain the central/medial aspect of the specimen, there is a well-circumscribed \u000abulging tan granular solid mass (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ), which extends to the \u000ainferior and posterior margins, 0.3cm from the anterior margin, 0.7cm to the \u000asuperior margin, 0.4cm to the medial margin, and 1.3cm to the lateral margin. \u000aEmbedded within the nodular mass is a silver metal clip as consistent with \u000aprior core biopsy procedure. The remainder of the cut surface is composed of \u000agreater than 75% dense white/tan fibrous stroma and less than 25% yellow/tan \u000alobulated adipose tissue with no additional discrete lesions grossly \u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely sequentially submitted from medial to \u000alateral. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central specimen from medial to lateral (mass in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , clip in \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), 1 frag in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS. \u000aLM/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a4/4/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
