VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material \u000aProcedure Date: \u000aOrdering Provider: JUDY E GARBER M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM MASSACHUSETTS GENERAL HOSPITAL, BOSTON: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, TWO WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONS FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND TWO CLIPS \u000a( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; 1/02/09): \u000aSUBAREOLAR, PRESUMABLY FOR TWO CLIPS AND CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aRuptured large cyst with a densely hyalinized wall, associated with chronic \u000aactive inflammation (e.g. in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; multiple levels examined) (see \u000anote). \u000aCluster of apocrine cysts with mucin production (0.5cm ) (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aCore needle biopsy site changes. \u000aNote: The patient underwent two core needle biopsies at Baystate Health (their \u000anumber  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). One biopsy was performed under ultrasound for a \u000aretroareolar oval mass with calcifications. The biopsy was reported to show \u000a"mammary duct/cyst wall fragments". If this is a re-excision of that site, the \u000alarge ruptured cyst could correlate with the radiologic finding. There was a \u000asecond biopsy at 9:00 for calcifications that showed benign breast tissue \u000awithout calcifications. It is unclear whether or not this excision included \u000athat biopsy site or the location of the residual calcifications in this \u000aspecimen (i.e. associated with one or both clip sites or in another location). \u000aThe specimen was radiographed and the calcifications were identified in block \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . This is the block with the large cyst and a cluster of apocrine cysts. \u000aMultiple levels through the block do not reveal definitive calcifications. The \u000aspecimen was entirely submitted for histologic examination. \u000a12:00, PRESUMABLY FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aApocrine cysts with associated calcifications (calcium oxalate). \u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia. \u000aColumnar cell change. \u000aNo biopsy site changes are identified. \u000aNote: The specimen was radiographed with the calcifications identified in block \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Multiple levels were examined. The specimen was submitted entirely \u000afor microscopic examination. \u000aAccording to the original report, "atypical ductal hyperplasia of apocrine \u000acells" was present. There is a < 0.2cm focus of apocrine cysts with a partial \u000acribriform pattern in 2 of the 9 levels of block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (levels 7 and 8). Note \u000athat level 2 of this block was not sent for review. \u000aDiagnostic features of atypical ductal hyperplasia are not seen in the slides \u000asent for review. \u000aDr. Deborah Dillon reviewed this case and concurs with this interpretation. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Cyst and calcifications in the right breast. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: ADH. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aConsult slides. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aReceived from Massachusetts General Hospital, Pathology Department, 55 Fruit \u000aStreet, Boston, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID , are forty-vie (45) glass slides. \u000aThe slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", \u000a" REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", \u000a" REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through \u000a" REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", corresponding to A) right breast, subareolar, excision (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) B) right breast, 12 o'clock, excision (3.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm ) performed on \u000a1/2/09, according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's \u000aname. \u000aIncluded is a consultation report from the same hospital numbered \u000a"MS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and dated REMOVED_DATE  referring institution Baystate Center; their \u000aaccession number " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", bearing the patient's name. \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 27,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04:26:30PM \u000a[report_end] 
