VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aMUELLER, JAMES, D, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by MUELLER,JAMES D,M.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS: \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, ONE (1) FOCUS \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aSYNOPSIS: \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aSize - 0.7cm \u000aMultifocal? - no \u000aHistologic Type - ductal \u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - I (well) \u000aNuclear Grade - low \u000aEIC - positive \u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent \u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A \u000aSkin invasion - N/A \u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A \u000aFinal Margins (invasive) - \u000aNegative (no ink on the tumor - all other margins \u000aClose (tumor <0.1cm from margin) inferior \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aTypes - cribriform \u000aNuclear grade - low \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent \u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent \u000aExtent of DCIS \u000aNumber of blocks/total - 3:17 blocks \u000aFinal Margins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (>0.3cm ) - all other margins \u000aClose (0.1-0.3cm ) - inferior, lateral, superior \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia \u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID b pNx MX \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 2): \u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) - NEGATIVE (0) \u000aInterpretation: \u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the \u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet \u000abeen determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor \u000acells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but \u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive. \u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity \u000ain >10% of tumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational \u000ause only. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 50-year-old premenopausal female with prior history of biopsy with \u000aatypical lobular hyperplasia, + family history of breast cancer in \u000athe mother and maternal grandmother. Right breast UOQ 5mm mass \u000awith negative mammogram, U/S with 6mm mass for which a biopsy is \u000arecommended. \u000aOperation: Right breast mass excision. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right excisional breast biopsy. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMBARD,DAVID B.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000aunit number, and "#1, right breast biopsy", and consists of a mass of \u000afibroadipose tissue (3.5cm medial to lateral x 1.9cm anterior to posterior x \u000a1.5cm superior to inferior). The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for \u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; \u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Serial sectioning of the \u000aspecimen reveals it to consist of approximately 80% fibrous tissue and 20% \u000aadipose tissue. No discrete lesion is present. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted from lateral to medial. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  multi frags, ESS. \u000adl \u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
