VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D. \u000a1) RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE, BIOPSY (including FSA): \u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA, in one of two (1:2) lymph nodes (3 H&E \u000alevels examined). \u000aThe metastatic deposit measures <0.1cm in size (micrometastasis). \u000aNo extranodal invasion present. \u000aThe metastasis is not present at the surgical section. \u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN": \u000aRESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (intermediate nuclear \u000agrade), is present in two of two (2:2) blocks. \u000aNo necrosis or calcifications are seen. \u000aNOTE: Although cautery artifact makes evaluation of the margin difficult \u000aareas consistent with DCIS are <0.1cm from the new margin. \u000a3) SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, LATERAL SHAVE MARGIN": \u000aResidual DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU present in two of two (2:2) blocks, \u000aand <0.1cm from the new surgical resection margin. \u000aNo residual invasive carcinoma is identified. \u000a4) SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN": \u000aResidual DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, is present in one of two (1:2) blocks. \u000aNo residual invasive carcinoma is identified. \u000aNOTE: The fragment of tissue with the DCIS does not have black ink \u000aindicating the new margin. No DCIS is seen close to black-inked \u000atissue. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 50 year old female with 0.7cm grade 1, LVI-negative breast cancer, \u000apositive margins. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right axillary hot sentinel node > REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a#2) Right breast inferior shave margin - stitch on new margin \u000a#3) Right breast lateral shave margin - stitch on new margin \u000a#4) Right breast superior shave margin - stitch on new margin \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED #1. RIGHT AXILLARY HOT SENTINEL NODE > REMOVED_CASE_ID ", (FSA): \u000aLymph nodes negative for carcinoma. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SMOUSE,JASON H.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received in four parts, each labeled with the patient's name \u000aand unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right axillary hot sentinel node > REMOVED_CASE_ID ", consists of one \u000afragment of red/yellow/tan soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm with two \u000alymph nodes, larger (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm ), smaller (0.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm ). \u000aRepresentative sections of each node are submitted as FSA. The remainder of \u000athe tissue from the smaller node is inked in black to differentiate it from the \u000alarger node by the pathologist and the remainder of each node is submitted. \u000aMicro 1: FSA remnant, ESS \u000aMicro 2: 2 lymph nodes; 1 larger node bisected and 1 smaller node inked in \u000ablack, ESS \u000aPart two, labeled "2. right breast inferior shave margin, stitch on new \u000amargin", consists of one fragment of fibroadipose breast tissue measuring 3 x \u000a1.5 x 1cm  There is a stitch placed by the surgeon designating the new \u000amargin. The specimen is inked by the pathologist in black for the new margin \u000aand blue for the old margin, and serially sectioned. The interior of the \u000aspecimen consists of densely fibrous breast tissue. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  4 frags, RSS \u000aPart three, labeled "#3. right breast lateral shave margin, stitch on new \u000amargin", consists of one fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue consistent \u000awith breast tissue measuring 2 x 1 x 1cm  There is a stitch placed by the \u000asurgeon designated as the new margin which is inked in black by the \u000apathologist and the old margin is inked in blue by the pathologist. The \u000ainterior of the specimen consists of dense fibrous tissue with no discrete \u000amasses or lesions. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic analysis. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  7 frags, ESS \u000aPart four, labeled "#4. right breast superior shave margin - stitch on new \u000amargin", consists of one fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue consistent \u000awith breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0.7cm with a stitch placed by the \u000asurgeon designating the new margin. The new margin is inked in black by the \u000apathologist and old margin is inked blue. The interior of the specimen \u000aconsists of fibroadipose tissue with no discrete masses or lesions. The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histologic analysis. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  8 frags, ESS \u000ajs \u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
