VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  LYMPH NODE BIOPSY \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aMUELLER, JAMES, D, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by MUELLER,JAMES D,M.D. \u000a1) AXILLARY LYMPH NODES, LEVEL I AND II, RESECTION: \u000aThirteen (13) lymph nodes negative for tumor. \u000a2) INFERIOR SHAVED MARGIN OF RIGHT BREAST TISSUE: \u000aResidual DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, in 1:4 blocks, 0.3cm from the new \u000amargin (see note). \u000aFibrosis, foreign body giant cell reaction, and intraductal hyperplasia. \u000aNo invasive carcinoma identified. \u000aNOTE: The margin is difficult to evaluate due to cautery artifact, but the \u000aclosest approach of DCIS to the new (black ink) margin is 0.3cm (slide \u000a13, levels examined). \u000a3) LATERAL SHAVED MARGIN OF RIGHT BREAST TISSUE: \u000aResidual DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, in 2:5 blocks, 0.2cm from the new \u000amargin. \u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions. \u000aDuctal hyperplasia. \u000aForeign body giant cell reaction, fibrosis, and chronic inflammation. \u000aNo invasive carcinoma identified. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: See previous pathology. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Completion of axillary Level I and II node dissection. \u000a2. Inferior shaved margin of rt breast tissue, stitch on new margin. \u000a3. Lateral shaved margin of rt breast tissue, stitch on new margin. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HASKELL,HENRY D.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received in three containers, each marked with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aThe first is further labeled "#1 completion of axillary Level I and II node \u000adissection". Received fresh and fixed overnight in Bouin's are approximately \u000aten fragments of fibroadipose tissue (in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm ). The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned at 0.1cm and 22 possible lymph nodes are \u000alocated. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  2 frags each, 22 probable lymph nodes, ESS (differentially inked, \u000aorange, black). \u000aThe second specimen consists of a fragment of fibroadipose tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.0cm thick). One margin is indicated by the surgeon as the new margin with a \u000astitch. The new margin is inked blue and the old, black. There is no lesion \u000ain the interior which is suspicious for carcinoma. A second fragment is found \u000awithin the same container; it is not attached to the oriented specimen. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  oriented margin, 8 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 15: unattached specimen, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aThe third container is labeled "#3 lateral shaved margin of right breast \u000atissue, stitch on new margin". Received fresh is a mass of fibroadipose tissue \u000a(2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm deep). It is oriented by the surgeon with a suture. The \u000anew margin is inked blue and the old, black. There is no lesion in the \u000ainterior margin that is suggestive of malignancy. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral shaved margin, right breast tissue, multi frags, ESS. \u000ahdh \u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
