VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D. \u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: \u000aThere is no evidence of residual or invasive or in situ ductal carcinoma. \u000aHealing and old prior excision sites. \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. \u000aOne (1) intraparenchymal lymph node negative for tumor. \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D. \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is also present, adjacent to the prior excision \u000asite. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 50-year-old female with right breast cancer, +DCIS with margins. \u000aSee previous path. \u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right simple mastectomy, stitch marking long at \u000aaxillary tail, blue stitch at upper inner quadrant ADH \u000abiopsy site, current incision in upper outer quadrant. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KINDELBERGER,DAVID W.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1, right simple mastectomy", consists of a simple mastectomy specimen (19 \u000acm medial to lateral x 13.5cm superior to inferior x 2.0cm \u000aanterior/posterior). A skin ellipse is present on the specimen (17 x 6.5cm ) \u000awith a nipple (1.2cm in diameter). A blue suture marks a healed incision \u000aat the medial aspect of the specimen (1.0cm in length). A recent incision \u000a(2.1cm in length) is present at the lateral aspect of the skin ellipse (4.0cm \u000ato the nipple). Subjacent to the recent incision is a biopsy cavity (4.0cm in \u000agreatest dimension) that comes to within 0.1cm of the deep margin. No biopsy \u000acavity is evident subjacent to the blue suture. There is no gross evidence of \u000ainvasive malignancy at the biopsy site. The specimen appears to consist of \u000aapproximately 50% fibrous tissue and 50% fatty tissue. There is no evidence of \u000ainvasive malignancy anywhere within the specimen. Representative sections of \u000athe biopsy cavity, nipple, the biospy scars, and the remainder of the breast \u000aare submitted for microscopic analysis for permanent sections. Please note \u000athat approximately 50% of the biopsy cavity is submitted for microscopic \u000aanalysis. \u000aMicro 1: nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 2: scar marked by blue suture, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 3: recent biopsy scar, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000adk \u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY \u000a[report_end] 
