 from inferior the margin. The specimen contains \u000aapproximately 70% fibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted. An \u000aaccompanying mammograph shows minute calcification in the specimen, as \u000adocumented by the Radiologist. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue with anterior, lateral and posterior margins, \u000asuperior to inferior sections, 4 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue with anterior, medial, and posterior margins, \u000asuperior to inferior sections, mult frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior margin, perpendicular sections, mult frags, ESS \u000aMicro 11: inferior margin, perpendicular sections, mult frags, ESS \u000axh \u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
