VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DAVID I SOYBEL M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Michael H Roh, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA., B. - LEFT BREAST, EXCISION; WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS, A MASS \u000aAND A CLIP, AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY (2 SPECIMENS): \u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, AND NEGATIVE \u000aLYMPH NODE. \u000aSYNOPSIS: \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aSize - 2.2cm \u000aMultifocal - No \u000aHistologic Type - Ductal \u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III (Poor) \u000aNuclear Grade - High \u000aEIC - Negative \u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent \u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - Absent \u000aSkin invasion - Absent \u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A \u000aFinal Margins (invasive) - Negative (> 0.3cm ) anterior, posterior, \u000alateral, medial, inferior, superior. \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present \u000aTypes - Cribriform, micropapillary \u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present \u000aExtent of DCIS - DCIS is present a minor component of the \u000ainvasive carcinoma \u000aFinal Margins (DCIS) - Negative (> 0.3cm ), anterior, \u000aposterior, medial, lateral, inferior, \u000asuperior. \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent \u000aSENTINEL LYMPH NODES (3 H&E levels examined) - Negative \u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0 \u000aNumber of nodes examined - 1 \u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS: \u000aCore biopsy site, apocrine metaplasia, vessels with medial \u000acalcification, calcifications in benign epithelium and core biopsy site. \u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  MX \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Not provided. \u000aOperation: Left breast wire localized biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast CA. \u000aORGAN/TISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Left breast tissue - lateral orange, medial yellow. \u000aB/2. Left axillary sentinel lymph node  REMOVED_CASE_ID  counts. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass, clip and wire and ca++ are all seen in specimen radiograph. \u000aRobyn Birdwell, MD called to OR at 1:35 p.m. by RB \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe case is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's name \u000aand unit number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast tissue, lateral orange, medial yellow", consists of \u000abreast tissue measuring 7.3cm from medial to lateral, 5.5cm from superior to \u000ainferior, and 2.8cm from posterior to anterior. The medial aspect of the \u000aspecimen is inked yellow and is associated with a skin ellipse (2.8 x 1.0cm ). \u000aThere is a wire entering the skin at the medial surface. The lateral aspect of \u000athe specimen is inked orange. The superior surface is inked red and the \u000ainferior surface is inked green. The anterior margin is inked black and the \u000aposterior margin is inked blue. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph in \u000awhich the wire is associated with an ill-defined mass associated with \u000acalcifications and a clip. The tip of the wire is visualized exiting at the \u000ainferolateral aspect of the specimen. The specimen is bisected along the wire \u000ato reveal a clip in association with an ill-defined tan/white firm mass \u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm  The lesion is 0.6cm from the green-inked \u000ainferior margin. The lesion is grossly distant (greater than 2.0cm ) from the \u000asuperior, lateral, and medial margins. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass in association with inferior margin (the wire was passing \u000abetween these sections), 1 frag per cassette, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of lateral margin (orange), 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of skin and medial margin (yellow), 2 \u000afrags total, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of superior margin (red), 2 frags \u000atotal, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of anterior margin (black), 2 frags \u000atotal, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of posterior margin (blue), 2 frags \u000atotal, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional representative sections of mass, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Left axillary sentinel lymph node;  REMOVED_CASE_ID  counts", consists of a \u000asingle fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm  \u000aWithin this tissue, there is a single lymph node measuring 1.4cm in greatest \u000adimension. This node is bisected and entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Bisected sentinel lymph node, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aroh/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
