VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Michael H Roh, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: \u000aA single focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , levels examined). \u000aBreast parenchyma with interlobular fibrosis, adenosis, apocrine \u000ametaplasia, cysts, and focal fibroadenomatous changes. \u000aCalcifications are associated with benign epithelium. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aNote: Selected slide (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) was also reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, who \u000aconcurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 51-year-old female with abnormal mammogram, left breast. Previous \u000amammo REMOVED_DATE at Falmouth Hospital (2.5 x 1.5cm  new mass left breast left \u000aouter quadrant). REMOVED_DATE - left breast mammo - demonstrates suspicious \u000amammographic abnormality for which needle localization and biopsy are \u000arecommended. \u000aOperation: Left needle localized breast biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammo. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Left wire localized breast tissue - marking stitch short suture superior, \u000along stitch lateral, whip stitch in chest wall margin. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aArea of interest in specimen. Signed: C. Denison, M.D. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number, \u000aand "#1 Left wire localized breast tissue", and consists of an ovoid fragment \u000aof yellow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (5.4 s-i x REMOVED_DATE m-l x REMOVED_DATE a-pcm ), \u000awhich is oriented per surgeon with three sutures: short = superior, long = \u000alateral, whip stitch = chest wall margin. The specimen is inked per prosector \u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A \u000aneedle localization wire is received free-floating in the specimen container. \u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to exhibit \u000aapproximately 30% focally dense, tan/white fibrostroma extending to the \u000aanterior, posterior, superior and medial margin, and approximately 70% \u000ayellow/tan, lobulated adipose tissue. No discrete masses or lesions are grossly \u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely sequentially submitted from superior to \u000ainferior. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Specimen sequentially submitted from superior to inferior, \u000amultiple frags total, ESS. \u000aLMB/elw \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Michael H Roh M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Michael H Roh M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Michael H Roh M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a2/21/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
