erior \u000ato superior, 2.5cm anterior to posterior, 0.2cm medial to lateral) and \u000aextends to within 0.2cm of the deep margin, 3.4cm of the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the inferior margin, 4.0cm from the medial margin, and 6.1cm from the \u000alateral margin. There are two possible tan/brown lymph nodes in the lateral \u000amargin of the resection. \u000aMicro 1: Right breast deep margin with fibrous tissue, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Fibrous tissue, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro 4: Superior outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro 5: Inferior outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro 6: Superior inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro 7: Inferior inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro 8: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 9: Two lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS \u000aPart 2, "L breast - short superior long lateral", consists of a 510 gm left \u000asimple mastectomy specimen (22 x 15 x 3.2) with a white/tan skin ellipse (20.7 \u000ax 10.2cm ) without an attached axillary tail. The areola measure 2.2cm in \u000adiameter and the nipple measures 1.1cm in diameter and 0.9cm in length. There \u000ais a scar (1.1cm ) above the nipple, along the areola, from 9:00 to 12:00. \u000aThere is a biopsy cavity noted deep to the areola scar (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE c 0.9cm ). \u000aThe cavity is 3.5cm form the deep margin, 5.5cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the inferior margin, 7cm from the medial margin, 10.5cm from the \u000alateral margin, and 1cm from the anterior skin. 0.4cm inferior to the biopsy \u000acavity is a firm nodular area (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ). \u000aMicro 10: Inferior border of biopsy cavity, including firm, nodular area, 1 \u000afrag, RSS \u000aMicro 11: Deep border of biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 12: Superior border of biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 13: Anterior border of biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 14: Lateral border of biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 15: Medial border of bipsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 16: Biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 17: Deep margin deep to cavity, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 18: Nodular firm area, 1 frags, RSS \u000aMicro 19: Superior outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 20: Inferior outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 21: Superior inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 22: Inferior inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 23: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000a[report_end] 
