mber, \u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue wire-localized biopsy, short - superior, long - \u000alateral, whip stitch - chest wall margin", and consists of a previously inked \u000aand oriented wire-localized excision of breast tissue (4.5cm from superior to \u000ainferior, 3.9cm from medial to lateral, 1.6cm from anterior to posterior) \u000awith an embedded localization wire and three orienting sutures (short - \u000asuperior, long - lateral, whip suture - posterior/chest wall). An accompanying \u000aradiograph shows an embedded localization wire along a cluster of \u000acalcifications with a nearby surgical clip. Sectioning from medial to lateral \u000areveals no discrete lesions; however, the area around the embedded wire appears \u000aheterogenous with approximately 70% fibrous tissue admixed with minority of \u000aadipose tissue. The entire specimen is examined microscopically. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial with some inferior, 8 frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag each, ESS (wire-localized area in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags each, ESS, \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral with some superior, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aVKV/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
