itch denoting superior and long \u000astitch denoting lateral. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; \u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. \u000aSectioning the specimen superior to inferior reveals 30% of the tissue is \u000afibrous tissue. No masses are grossly identified. The specimen is \u000aentirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast with superior and posterior margins, mult frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast with inferior margin, mult frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast with medial, inferior margins, mult frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast with lateral margin, mult frags, ESS \u000aPart two, labeled "#2. superolateral left breast tissue", consists of a breast \u000aexcision (5.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ). The specimen is not oriented. The specimen is \u000ainked in black. Sectioning reveals 70% of the tissue is fibrous tissue. The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue, mult frags, ESS \u000axh \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
