VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Tanya Rege, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with associated calcifications, small focus, \u000apresent in one (1) of eleven (11) blocks. \u000aCalcifications in association with benign breast tissue. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aLEFT BREAST, INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN: \u000aBenign breast tissue. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 58-year-old female S/P L breast UO core Bxs on REMOVED_DATE at FH and \u000aread here REMOVED_DATE  revealing focal ADH; for excision. \u000aOperation: L breast WL bx. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Left breast tissue; short suture - superior; long - lateral; whip stitch \u000aat chest wall margin to mammo. \u000aB/2) Left breast inferior shaved margin; whip stitch - new margin to mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aA: Ca++ present, no clip, intact wire. (ILLEGIBLE signature). \u000aB: No Ca++, no clip (ILLEGIBLE signature). \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, labeled with the patient's name \u000aand medical record number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast tissue, short suture superior, long lateral, whip \u000astitch at chest wall margin", consists of one lumpectomy (14 grams post \u000afixation, 3.1cm superior to inferior, 5.5cm medial to lateral, 2.4cm \u000aanterior to posterior), oriented with three sutures (short-superior, \u000along-lateral, whip stitch-chest wall margin). The specimen is inked by the \u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange. A \u000alocalization wire is present and enters the medial aspect. \u000aAn accompanying radiograph demonstrates calcifications and an intact \u000alocalization wire. A hemorrhagic lesion/prior biopsy cavity (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) is present at the superior margin, 1.1cm to the inferior margin, 0.6cm to \u000athe anterior margin, 0.3cm to the posterior margin, 0.2cm to the medial \u000amargin, and 3.1cm to the lateral margin. A white/tan fibrous area (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 4.3cm ) is present at the lateral, superior, inferior, anterior, and \u000aposterior margins. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Left breast tissue, lateral to medial, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast inferior shave margin, whip stitch new margin", \u000aconsists of two lumpectomies (15.5 grams post fixation, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.9cm and \u000a6.4 grams post fixation, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ). Stitches are present on both \u000alumpectomies, designated new margin per surgeon (inked black). The remainder \u000aof the breast parenchyma is inked blue. An accompanying radiograph is \u000aunremarkable. The smaller lumpectomy is approximately 90% fibrotic. The \u000alarger lumpectomy is approximately 30% fibrotic. The remainder of the breast \u000aparenchyma is tan/yellow and unremarkable. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Smaller lumpectomy, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Larger lumpectomy, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aTR/mmm \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a3/10/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aFocal area of scarring is present and is consistent with prior biopsy \u000asite. \u000aThe diagnosis remains UNCHANGED. \u000aAddendum #1 by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a3/26/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
