VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: David C. Park, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS": \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia. \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, columnar cell hyperplasia, and apocrine \u000acysts with microcalcifications. \u000aNOTE: \u000aTwo areas containing a monomorphic ductal proliferation (ADH) are adjacent to \u000afoci of columnar cell hyperplasia. \u000aDr. Ince has reviewed selected slides and concurs with the diagnosis. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 54 y o woman with microcalcifications on screening not amenable to \u000astereotactic core. Recommended for bx. \u000aOperation: Right needle loc breast bx. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: R abnl mammo. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) R breast tissue (F.S.) \u000aRADIOLOGY: Hook wire and Ca++ in specimen. Called to OR HP 15:09. \u000a- Peters  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue", and consists of an irregular portion of \u000afibrofatty tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm ), which is received previously inked per \u000apathology protocol as anterior blue, posterior black, superior red, inferior \u000agreen, medial orange and lateral yellow. There is an inserted needle \u000alocalization wire, which enters along the superior - medial aspect, and exits \u000aalong the inferior aspect. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal 50% \u000adense white focally nodular fibrous tissue, and 40% yellow lobulated adipose \u000atissue, with no discrete m