VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGRANTER, SCOTT, R., M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GRANTER,SCOTT R.,M.D. \u000aSKIN, LEFT BREAST, PUNCH BIOPSY: \u000aAtypical perivascular and interstitial lymphocytic infiltrate \u000aWORRISOME FOR A T-CELL LYMPHOPROLIFERATIVE DISORDER. \u000aImmunostains reveal the majority of cells are reactive for T-cell markers \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . There is a mixture of both  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  reactive cells. \u000aOnly a minority of cells are reactive for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Scattered cells are \u000areactive for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aNOTE: The presence of atypical cells within the infiltrate is somewhat \u000aworrisome for a T-cell lymphoproliferative disorder; however, the \u000apresence of mixed  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  reactive cells would argue against \u000athis diagnosis. The differential diagnosis includes \u000ahypersensitivity reactions, gyrate erythemas, and connective tissue \u000adisease. Clinical correlation is needed. A repeat biopsy to \u000aobtain fresh tissue for immunomarker and gene rearrangement studies \u000ais advised if deemed clinically appropriate. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 58-year-old white female with REMOVED_DATE month history of asymptomatic \u000adiscrete 3-8cm erythematous macules on breasts, inframammary region, inguinal \u000acreases and bilateral groin. No scale seen. \u000aOperation: 3mm punch. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Rule out CTCL versus large plaque parapsoriasis. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Skin, left breast. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HENDERSON,JOEL M.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit \u000anumber, and consists of a punch biopsy of tan/white smooth skin (0.2cm \u000adiameter, 0.3cm depth), which is inked and submitted entirely. \u000aMicro 1: 1 frag, ESS. \u000akks \u000aReports to: O'SULLIVAN-HUNNEWELL, REBECCA \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT \u000a[report_end] 
