VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST,NOS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCRUM, CHRISTOPHER, PAUL, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CRUM,CHRISTOPHER PAUL,M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS": \u000aFibrocystic change proliferative. \u000aMicrocalcifications noted in association with benign epithelium. \u000aIntraductal papilloma (1). \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE MEDIAL TO PREVIOUS RESECTION": \u000aFibrocystic change proliferative. \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by CRUM,CHRISTOPHER PAUL,M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE MEDIAL TO PREVIOUS RESECTION": \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (see comment). \u000aCOMMENT: This case was targeted for quality assurance and re-evaluated \u000awith levels of the original tissue blocks. The levels reveal the presence \u000aof atypical lobular hyperplasia in a few ducts. The classical histologic \u000acriteria for lobular carcinoma in situ are not met. However, because of the \u000ainvolvement of several lobules and the presence of intraductal extension, the \u000arisk of concurrent or subsequent breast neoplasia is similar to that associated \u000awith LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU. No invasive carcinoma is identified. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Microcalfications on mammogram. Resection recommended. Wire \u000alocalization carried out. \u000aOperation: Left breast resection \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast abnormal mammogram \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue with microcalcifications \u000a2. Left breast tissue medial to previous resection \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000a#1."Left breast tissue with microcalcifications: \u000aReceived is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm  portion of fallopian tube with a \u000awire tip localizing microcalcifications. Breadloafing does not \u000areveal any evidence of invasive tumor. \u000a(Gross only). \u000aFibrocystic changes. No evidence of invasive tumor. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications in specimen. \u000aJ. Meyer, M.D. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KRAUS,MADELEINE,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received in 2 parts. \u000aPart 1, labeled "left breast tissue with microcalcification", is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.7cm  portion of fallopian tube with a wire tip localizing \u000amicrocalcification. Breadloafing does not reveal any evidence of invasive \u000atumor. \u000aSection code: \u000aMicro 1 and 2 - tissue near wire tip, ESS, multiple fragments, 2 cassettes \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - left breast biopsy (specimen #1), ESS, multiple fragments, \u000a4 cassettes. \u000aPart 2, received fresh, labeled "#2 left breast tissue medial to previous \u000aresection", is a single mass of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  \u000aMicro 7 - specimen #2, ESS, 2 fragments, 1 cassette. \u000aReports to: KANE, J.GREGORY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST,NOS \u000a[report_end] 
