VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED RIGHT BREAST TISSUE: \u000aINFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA (1.0cm ), grade 1 of 3, associated with an \u000aextensive intraductal component. See note. \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (grade 2 nuclear features), \u000apresent within and adjacent to the invasive tumor and comprising \u000aapproximately 30% of the tumor mass. See note. \u000aBoth invasive and in situ carcinoma extend to inked margins. \u000aNo definite lymphatic/vascular invasion is identified. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED RIGHT BREAST TISSUE MEDIAL TO LESION: \u000aFocally cauterized breast parenchyma; no tumor identified. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED RIGHT BREAST TISSUE LATERAL TO LESION: \u000aFocally cauterized breast parenchyma; no tumor identified. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED RIGHT BREAST TISSUE SUPERIOR TO LESION: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED AXILLARY CONTENTS: \u000aFifteen lymph nodes; no tumor present. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED SKIN PAPILLOMA: \u000aSquamous papilloma. \u000aNOTE: A second focus of ductal carcinoma in situ (associated with \u000amicrocalcifications) is identified away from the main tumor \u000amass and is associated with focal invasion. This most likely \u000arepresents a separate synchronous lesion. A portion of the main \u000atumor mass was submitted for ERICA. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Suspicious nodule plus another area of microcalcifications, both in \u000athe upper aspect of the right breast. \u000aOperation: Breast resection after 2 wire localizations \u000aClinical Diagnosis: ?Breast carcinoma \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue (FS) \u000a2. Right breast tissue medial to lesion \u000a3. Right breast tissue lateral to lesion \u000a4. Right breast tissue superior to lesion \u000a5. Right axillary contents \u000a6. Skin papilloma \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000a1.0cm  gritty nodule present at an inked margin; grossly suspicious for \u000ainvasive carcinoma. \u000aFinal diagnosis pending microscopy. A portion is submitted for ERICA. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications and mass in specimen. \u000aC. Denison, M.D. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HASEGAWA,SUSAN LYNN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aReceived fresh, in the OR, labeled "#1 right breast tissue", is a 10 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. mass of fatty tissue with two loose needle localization wires attached. \u000aThe specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  \u000anodule which is gritty and grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma. The \u000anodule is present at in inked margin. A portion of this tissue is frozen for \u000aERICA analysis. No additional suspicious nodules are grossly identified. \u000aMicro 1 - remaining grossly suspicious nodule \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - breast tissue surrounding the grossly suspicious nodule. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - ESS, breast biopsy \u000aIn saline, labeled "right breast tissue, medial to lesion", is an aggregate of \u000afocally hemorrhagic fatty tissue fragments which are unoriented and measure REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 2 x 0.4cm  \u000aMicro 14 - ESS, breast tissue medial to lesion \u000aIn saline, labeled "right breast tissue, lateral to lesion", is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm aggregate fatty tissue with no orientation provided. \u000aMicro 15 - ESS, tissue lateral to lesion \u000aIn saline, labeled "right breast tissue, superior to lesion", is an aggregate \u000aof fatty tissue fragments measuring REMOVED_DATE x 4 x 1cm  No orientation is \u000aprovided. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - ESS, breast tissue superior to lesion \u000aIn saline, labeled "axillary contents", is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm mass of fatty \u000atissue which is dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes measuring up to 2cm \u000ain greatest dimension. The larger lymph nodes are predominantly fatty. One \u000asection from each identified lymph node is submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - one representative section from each identified lymph node \u000aIn saline, labeled "skin papilloma", is a 5mm tan hemorrhagic fragment which \u000ais bisected. \u000aMicro 23 - ESS, skin papilloma \u000aReports to: KANE, J.GREGORY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
