medial to lateral, and 2.5cm from anterior to posterior). The specimen \u000ais received inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of \u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; \u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen contains a wire, protruding \u000afrom the inferior/anterior portion of the specimen. The specimen is \u000aaccompanied by a radiograph which shows a wire and an area of \u000amicrocalcifications. Serial sectioning reveals that the specimen is 40% firm, \u000awhite fibrous tissue. No lesions are grossly identified. The entire specimen \u000ais submitted serially from inferior to superior. \u000aMicro 1: Inferior margin, perpendicular, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Serial sections, multiple frags, ESS \u000aMicro 8: Superior margin, perpendicular, 2 frags, ESS \u000aPart 2, "Right breast superior upper outer quadrant microcalcifications", \u000aconsists of a piece of breast tissue (4cm from medial to lateral, 2.5cm from \u000asuperior to inferior, and 1.5cm from anterior to posterior). The specimen is \u000areceived inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of \u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; \u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen contains a hook wire which \u000aruns along the lateral aspect of the specimen. The specimen is accompanied by \u000aa radiograph which demonstrates a wire and a focal area of \u000amicrocalcifications. Serial sectioning reveals that the specimen is 80% firm, \u000awhite fibrous tissue. No lesions are grossly identified. The entire specimen \u000ais submitted serially from medial to lateral. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Medial margin, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Serial sections, multiple frags, ESS \u000aMicro 17: Lateral and posterior margin, perpendicular, 2 frags, ESS \u000ahph \u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
