VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA/1. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aColumnar cell change. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aNOTE: Selected slides were reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, Breast Pathologist, \u000awho concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Micro calcs left breast. \u000aOperation: Localized excision. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Tissue, left breast. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Wire and calcification in specimen. OR called SC/SR. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "tissue, left breast", and consists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to \u000apink/tan fibroadipose tissue (4.6 M/L x REMOVED_DATE A/P x REMOVED_DATE S/Icm ). The specimen is \u000ainked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/ orange. There is one needle-localization wire in place which enters \u000athe inferolateral aspect of the specimen and exits the posterior medial aspect \u000aof the specimen. The specimen was previously radiographed (per radiologist \u000a"wire and calcifications in the specimen, OR called"). The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral to exhibit approximately 60% \u000adense/lumpy white/tan fibrous tissue and 40% yellow/lobulated adipose tissue. \u000aThe dense fibrous tissue extends to the medial, anterior, posterior, superior, \u000aand inferior margins, and is traversed by the needled-localization wire \u000a(corresponds to the circled area of calcification on specimen radiograph). No \u000adiscrete masses or lesions are identified. The specimen is entirely \u000asequentially submitted from medial to lateral. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, perpendicular resection, 4 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central specimen (fibrous tissue in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), 1 frag in \u000aeach, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, perpendicular resection, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000almc/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on \u000a2/21/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
