ferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. \u000aContained within the specimen is a single localization wire corresponding to an \u000aarea of calcifications on the accompanying specimen radiograph. \u000aThe specimen is composed predominantly of fibrous tissue with focal cystic \u000achanges. The entire specimen is submitted for microscopic examination. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Right breast tissue in serial sections from inferior to superior, \u000alikely calcifications in Micro REMOVED_DATE  multiple frags, ESS. \u000amcc \u000aReports to: SHOJI, BRENT, T. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
