short suture) and lateral (long suture) \u000aportion of the specimen. The attached REMOVED_DATE x 3.1cm tan/white skin is almost \u000aentirely comprised of a REMOVED_DATE x 2.9cm areola and central unremarkable 1.2cm \u000anipple. Immediately lateral to and abutting the lateral quater of the nipple \u000ais a 1.4cm curve of linear tan/white discoloration, likely scar. Deep surface \u000acomprised of a smooth fascial plain (inked black). The specimen is sectioned, \u000arevealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm fibromembranous, retracted area in the right \u000aupper radial quadrant (? Prior biopsy cavity), 0.5cm from the deep margin. In \u000aaddition, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm cystic lesion filled with a thick \u000atan/yellow amorphous material, 1.6cm lateral to the previously described \u000alesion and 0.9cm from the deep margin in this area (right upper radial \u000aquadrant). Remaining specimen is comprised of extremely dense granular fibrous \u000atissue (maximally 8.5cm  medial to lateral), with occasional dilated ducts \u000afilled with a deep tan yellow fluid. There are no additional discreet masses. \u000aDense fibrous tissue comprises at least 60% of specimen. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, possible lateral scar, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Possible cavity ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is closest to deep margin), 5 frags, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 0.4cm cyst, lateral to possible cavity, with closest deep \u000amargin, 3 frags, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central breast, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS \u000aNOTE: Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  are sequential representative sections from irregular \u000afibrous dense tissue (medial to lateral) \u000aPart B, "#2. L breast tissue, marking stitch short superior, long lateral", \u000aconsists of a 217 gm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.9cm left mastectomy specimen. The \u000aattached REMOVED_DATE x 3.4cm tan/white ovoid skin is almost entirely comprised of a \u000a3.0cm diameter, areola and central 1.2cm everted, unremarkable nipple. There \u000aare no scars grossly. Deep surface is comprise of a smooth fascial plain \u000a(inked black). The specimen is sectioned, revealing diffusely dense, granular, \u000acystic fibrous tissue (maximally 11.0cm  medial to lateral), with occasional \u000adilated ducts filled with a thick, tan/yellow fluid. Closest overlying freely \u000amobile deep margin is within 0.2cm of the dense fibrous tissue. There are no \u000adiscreet lesions grossly. Fibrous tissue comprises of at least 60% of the \u000aspecimen. There is scant grossly uninvolved fibrous tissue. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential representative sections from lateral to medial ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is \u000alateral most fibrous tissue,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is upper outer quadrant,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is \u000alower outer quadrant,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is central breast,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is lower inner \u000aquadrant,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is upper inner quadrant,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is medial most fibrous \u000atissue), multiple frags, RSS \u000aDB/cdm \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Peter M Sadow M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a9/26/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
