VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Paul A. VanderLaan, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aNo residual atypical hyperplasia seen. \u000aCore biopsy site changes. \u000aCalcifications in cysts and adenosis. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aFibroadenoma (0.5cm ). \u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 48-year-old female with right breast atypical ductal hyperplasia not \u000aassociated with calcifications - S/P image-guided biopsy. \u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast ADH. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right breast localized wire excisional biopsy - short superior, long \u000alateral -S. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and Ca++ present. - C. Denison, MD \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1. Right breast localized excisional Bx, short sup/long lateral", and \u000aconsists of an irregular portion of yellow lobulated fibrofatty tissue (2.5 x \u000a2.0 x 1.0cm ), with a long suture designating lateral, and a short suture \u000adesignating superior. There is an inserted needle localization wire, as \u000adisplayed in the accompanying radiograph, which enters along the inferior \u000amargin, and traverses the length of the specimen and exits at the \u000asuperior-posterior margin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol, by \u000athe prosector as anterior blue, posterior black, superior red, inferior green, \u000alateral yellow, and medial orange. The specimen is serially sectioned to \u000areveal a well-healed biopsy cavity (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ), less than 0.1cm from \u000athe anterior margin, 0.2cm from the posterior margin, 0.2cm from the medial \u000amargin, 0.7cm from the lateral margin, 1.5cm from the inferior margin, and \u000a1.3cm from the superior margin. As displayed in the accompanying radiograph, \u000aa surgical clip is identified within the cavity along with a wire. The cavity \u000ais surrounded by white fibrous tissue, and yellow adipose tissue, with no \u000adiscrete masses or lesions identified. The remaining cut surface displays 60% \u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 40% white fibrous tissue, with no \u000aadditional discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen is sequentially \u000asubmitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin, radially sectioned, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections from inferior to superior, with the \u000acavity in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , the surgical clip identified in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the area of concern on \u000athe accompanying radiograph in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, radially sectioned, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aCP/mgd/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aWednesday May 13,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 09:50:53AM \u000a[report_end] 
