h no discrete masses \u000aor lesions grossly identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin and focally dense fibrous tissue, 4 frags in each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional fibrous tissue, RSS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast tissue, 685 g", consists of a 685-g specimen consists \u000aof multiple fragments of yellow/tan to tan/pink fibroadipose tissue and brown \u000awrinkled skin (19.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 5.5cm in aggregate). The fragments are sectioned \u000ato exhibit approximately 40% focally dense/lumpy white/tan fibrous tissue and \u000a60% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue with no discrete masses or lesions \u000agrossly identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin and focally dense fibrous stroma, 4 frags in each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional fibrous tissue, RSS. \u000almb/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a2/28/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
