 number. \u000aPart 1, "right needle localized breast biopsy", consists of a needle localized \u000abreast excision (5.5cm from anterior to posterior, 2.8cm superior to \u000ainferior, and 2.0cm medial to lateral). No wire in the specimen. The specimen \u000ais inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = \u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; \u000amedial = orange. No biopsy site is grossly identified. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted. An accompanying radiograph shows no calcification in the specimen \u000aas documented by the radiologist. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Superior, inferior, lateral, and medial margins, multiple frags, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro 9: Anterior margin, perpendicular sections, multiple frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Posterior margin, perpendicular sections, multiple frags, ESS. \u000aPart 2, "#2 right breast posterior tissue", consists of one piece of tan/yellow \u000afibroadipose soft tissue (12.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm ). The specimen is not oriented. \u000aThe specimen is inked in black and entirely submitted. An accompanying \u000aradiograph shows calcifications in the specimen as documented by the \u000aradiologist. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Posterior breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS. \u000axh \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
