VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR A CLIP: \u000aSmall focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia. \u000aPrior core biopsy site changes are noted in multiple sections \u000a(blocks 8-10). \u000aNo in-situ or invasive carcinoma is identified. \u000aThe inked surgical margins of resection were examined microscopically. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Core biopsy-diagnosed DCIS of left breast \u000aOperation: Lt. needle-directed core biopsy \u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS, L. breast \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: L. breast tissue with mammo \u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: \u000aClip is in the specimen. \u000aD. Smith, MD \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by OH,KIRSTINE YUNG-TING,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, accompanied by a mammogram, and labeled with \u000athe patient's name, unit number, and "1) left breast tissue", and consists of a \u000awire-localization with a clip in the specimen. The specimen consists of an \u000aellipse of skin (4.4 x 1.7cm ) with underlying fibrofatty adipose breast tissue \u000a(5.6cm superior to inferior, 6.0cm medial to lateral, 5.5cm anterior to \u000aposterior). There is a short suture orienting to superior and a long stitch \u000aorienting to lateral. The specimen is inked, by the surgeon, per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; \u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from inferior to superior to reveal a central \u000aarea of fibrous breast tissue within the fatty component (approximately 20% of \u000athe specimen) with associated recent hemorrhage. A metal clip is identified in \u000aone area. No obvious mass or DCIS is identified. All of the fibrous tissue is \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro 1: inferior margin, multi frag, RSS \u000aMicro 2: superior margin, 2 frag, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior margin, 1 frag/cass, RSS \u000aMicro 5: anterior/skin margin, 2 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 6: lateral margin, 2 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 7: medial margin, 2 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 8: section of core site with clip, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of fibrous tissue, REMOVED_DATE frag/cass, ESS \u000adam \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
