l extension. \u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition):  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID c  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (sn) \u000aLEFT BREAST, STEREOTACTIC BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS (08: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 09/24/08): \u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA with lobular features, moderately differentiated \u000a(modified Bloom-Richardson grade II/III), measuring at least 0.4cm in size in \u000athis limited specimen. \u000aNo lymphovascular invasion identified in this limited specimen. \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type, (low nuclear grade), without necrosis or \u000acalcifications. \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with calcifications. \u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the following \u000aresults (reviewed): \u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE (95%) \u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE (95%) \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /NEU 0/NEGATIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (FISH) 1.8/EQUIVOCAL (by report) \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: LCIS in the right breast \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right Br ILC and LCIS; left Br IDLC \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aConsult slides. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aReceived from Jordan Hospital, Pathology Department, 275 Sandwich Street, \u000aPlymouth, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID , are thirty-two (32) glass slides. \u000aNine (9) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled "1", "3", "(+)ctrl/ER", \u000a"(+)ctrl/PR", "(+)ctrl/ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  HercepTest", "(+)ctrl/Ki-67", "(+)ctrlp53" and "Neg \u000aControl"( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), corresponding to a right breast core biopsy (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm ) \u000aperformed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the \u000apatient's name. \u000aSeventeen (17) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  1", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  1", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a1", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  1", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  1", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  1", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3", " REMOVED_ACCESSI