n. On \u000asection, there is white fibrous tissue (20% of the specimen) running along the \u000alateral margin towards the anterior pole. The remainder of the specimen is \u000acomposed of unremarkable, focally hemorrhagic, yellow lobulated adipose tissue. \u000aThe path of the wire and wire localized area is submitted in micros one to \u000athree. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial and is \u000aentirely submitted. The specimen radiograph as read by radiology shows \u000acalcifications localized by the wire. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  wire, localized area, 3 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of fibrous portion of specimen, 5 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, lateral to medial, 12 frags, ESS \u000assa \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
