serially sectioned to reveal firmly adipose \u000atissue with an area of lobulated, cystic, well-circumscribed tissue (1.5cm in \u000alongest dimension) which is grossly consistent with fibroadenoma. \u000aRepresentative sections are taken of the specimen and submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area of breast consistent with fibroadenoma, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro 4: uninvolved breast, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2, right breast tissue", consists of skin and breast \u000atissue, weighing  REMOVED_CASE_ID  grams, and measures 54 x 35 x 5cm in depth. There are \u000aeight (8) separate fragments of fibroadipose tissue and one (1) separate \u000afragment of skin measuring 26 x 11cm  There is a brown-pigmented portion of \u000athe skin, 0.4cm in length, which is located 0.6cm from the nearest skin \u000aellipse edge. This skin ellipse edge is inked in black, and the lesion is \u000asectioned and representative segments are submitted. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned to reveal fibroadipose tissue (approximately 10% of which is fibrous \u000atissue, and the rest is adipose tissue). There are no lesions grossly \u000aidentified. \u000aMicro 5: brown-pigmented lesion on skin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous breast tissue, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS. \u000aPart three, labeled "#3, left breast tissue", consists of skin and attached \u000abreast tissue weighing 3,070 grams. There are thirteen (13) pieces of tissue in \u000aall; ten of which are fibroadipose tissue, one of which is a large piece of \u000afibroadipose tissue with attached skin, measuring 53 x 13 x 5cm deep, and two \u000a(2) fragments of skin, measuring 17cm and 24cm in length. There are no \u000aidentifiable skin lesions, grossly. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, multi frags, ESS. \u000ajdr \u000aReports to: ORGILL, DENNIS, PAUL M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY \u000a[report_end] 
