. \u000aThere is a needle localization wire entering the lateral aspect of the \u000aspecimen. The specimen radiograph shows the wire and a small cluster of \u000acalcifications. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol (blue equals \u000aanterior, black equals posterior, red equals superior, green equals inferior, \u000ayellow equals lateral, and orange equals medial). The specimen is serially \u000asectioned from lateral to medial to show parenchyma with focally dense \u000atan/white fibrous tissue (45%). There is a cystic space 0.2cm in greatest \u000adimension, 0.1cm from the anterior margin, 1.0cm from the inferior margin, \u000a0.2cm from the superior margin, 1.4cm from the posterior margin, 1.5cm from \u000athe medial margin, and 2.1cm from the lateral margin. The remaining \u000aparenchyma consists of tan/yellow adipose tissue. The entire specimen is \u000aexamined microscopically. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Specimen sequentially sectioned from lateral to medial, \u000amulti frags, ESS. \u000aDRD/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a7/26/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
