sis. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 45 year old woman with architectural distortion on screening mammogram \u000aright separate complex cystic lesion incidental found on right which had \u000aaspiration and returned atypia; on clinical exam had single poor clear \u000adischarge from left nipple. \u000aOperation: Right needle localization, breast biopsy two lesions left duct \u000aexcisional biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left nipple discharge, right abnormal mammogram. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000a1. Mass in specimen. EP Frost, MD \u000a2. Architectural distortion and calcification in specimen. EP Frost, MD \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right breast tissue cystic lesion short suture superior, long lateral. \u000aB/2. Right breast tissue architectural distortion short suture superior, long \u000alateral. \u000aC/3. Left breast duct suture in on the duct. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "right breast tissue cystic lesion, short suture superior, long \u000alateral", consists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose \u000abreast tissue (3.5cm superior to inferior, 2.8cm medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm anterior to posterior) with a short suture designating superior margin, and \u000aa long suture designating lateral margin. There is a needle localization wire \u000ain place which enters through the lateral aspect of the specimen and exits \u000athrough the medial posterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen has been \u000apreviously inked per pathology protocol (superior red, inferior green, medial \u000aorange, lateral yellow, anterior blue, posterior black) and is serially \u000asectioned from superior to inferior. The cut surface is tan/yellow and \u000ahomogenous with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting \u000aapproximately 20% of the breast parenchyma. No discrete lesions are grossly \u000aidentified. The specimen is submitted in its entirety. The specimen is \u000areceived with a radiograph which shows a wire and a density in the specimen. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections superior to inferior, 1 frag each, ESS, \u000ablock  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to include designated area in specimen radiograph. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "Right breast architectural distortion, short superior, long \u000alateral", consists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose \u000abreast tissue (3.8cm anterior to posterior, 2.8cm superior to inferior, and \u000a2.4cm medial to lateral) with a short suture designating the superior margin, \u000aand a long suture designating the lateral margin. There is a needle \u000alocalization wire in place which enters through the superior aspect of the \u000aspecimen and exits through the inferior aspect of the specimen. The specimen \u000ahas been previously inked per the surgeon per pathology protocol (anterior \u000ablue, posterior black, superior red, inferior green, medial orange, lateral \u000ayellow) and is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior. There are focal \u000aareas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting approximately 90% of the \u000abreast parenchyma. No discrete lesions or areas of disruption are grossly \u000aidentified. The specimen is submitted in its entirety. The specimen is \u000asubmitted in its entirety. The specimen is received with a radiograph which \u000ashows a wire, calcifications and an area of architectural distortion in the \u000aspecimen. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, 4 frags, ESS, \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections anterior to posterior, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to \u000ainclude area designated per specimen radiograph, 