VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CHRISTINE M DENISON M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Justine A Barletta, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 11 G STEREOTACTRIC VACUUM-ASSISTED CORE NEEDLE \u000aBIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified \u000aBloom-Richardson grade II/III), measuring at least 0.25cm in size in this \u000alimited specimen. \u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen. \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present. \u000aCollagenous spherulosis with associated calcifications. The focus of \u000acollagenous spherulosis has pagetoid involvement by LCIS (See Note) \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma: \u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE \u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /NEU NEGATIVE (0) (SEE NOTE) \u000aNOTE: Lack of E-cadherin confirms the presence of LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU. \u000aKerative/ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  immunohistochemical stains highlight the examined cells \u000ain the focus of collagenous spherulosis. CEA is negative in this focus. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHISTORY: 48 year old with new tight cluster of Ca++s L UOQ ~ 9mm REMOVED_DATE \u000aAdditional, more faint, Ca++s in mid upper breast ~ 15mm posterior to main \u000agroup. \u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING: \u000a1. Left: non-palpable calcifications. \u000aLOCATION: \u000a1. Left: upper outer. \u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY: \u000a1. 11G stereotactic, vacuum-assisted. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Left breast cores - A/tissue with Ca++s; B/remainder of tissue - 2 green \u000acassettes. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit \u000anumber, and "left breast", and consists of cores of fibroadipose tissue, \u000areceived in two green cassettes with green lids, labeled "A Ca++" (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.3cm ), and "B" (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ). The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Left breast "cassette A" cores, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Left breast green "cassette B" cores, multi frags, ESS. \u000adb/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a9/19/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
