VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Consult slides \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAY HARRIS M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  CALNAN \u000aResident: Russell K Dorer, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM MASSACHUSETTS GENERAL HOSPITAL, BOSTON, MA: \u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; 4/15/05): \u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, HIGH GRADE (10cm  by report). \u000aSeparately submitted "final shaved margin" (part B) shows focal atypical ductal \u000ahyperplasia and a 0.3cm focus of fibroadenomatoid change (0.6cm from \u000ablack-inked margin, designated ?new true surgical margin?). \u000aNOTE: This is a highly cellular tumor with marked stromal overgrowth and \u000anuclear pleomorphism, a high mitotic rate (at least REMOVED_DATE hfps) and extensive \u000atumor necrosis. By report, immunohistochemical studies performed at the \u000areferring institution (not reviewed) show that the tumor cells are positive for \u000avimentin and negative for wide spectrum keratin, keratin, keratin 903, smooth \u000amuscle actin, desmin, HMB-45, MART-1, and S-100. By report, tumor cells are \u000aalso negative for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor and Her2/neu. By \u000areport, electron microscopy was attempted, but was non-contributory. \u000aThe ?final shaved margin? is described as a ?hollow shell? of tissue. By \u000areport, the outer aspect was inked black and represents the ?new true surgical \u000amargin.? The width of this margin is not specifically indicated in the outside \u000areport, but appears on the slides to measure at least 0.5cm to over 1.0cm  \u000aClinical correlation is suggested for best determination of distance to the \u000afinal margins. \u000aLEFT BREAST, FINE NEEDLE ASPIRATION (MN-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; 4/13/05): \u000aCytologic preparations not reviewed due to lack of medical necessity. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Left breast mass. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: ?Phyllodes tumor vs carcinoma. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aConsult slides. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aReceived from Massachusetts General Hospital, Pathology Department, Boston, MA \u000a REMOVED_CASE_ID , are forty-six (46) glass slides. \u000aThirty-four (34) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", \u000a" REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", \u000a" REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through \u000a" REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", corresponding to a left breast excision (10.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 5.0cm ) \u000aperformed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing \u000athe patient's name. \u000aTwelve (12) cytology slides are labeled "MN-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " \u000athrough " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", corresponding to a left breast fine needle aspiration performed \u000aon REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying cytology report bearing the patient's \u000aname. \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Deborah A Dillon M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
