VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aSclerosing adenosis with numerous calcifications. \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. \u000aIntraductal papillomas. \u000aAprocrine cysts. \u000aFibroadenoma. \u000aNote: No malignancy is seen after complete microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aLEFT BREAST, "ADDITIONAL TISSUE INFERIOR BIOPSY SITE": \u000aSclerosing adenosis with numerous calcifications. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aNote: There was a gross nodule adjacent to a designated suture. This \u000anodule corresponds to an area of sclerosing adenosis ("nodular adenosis"). \u000aNo malignancy is seen after complete microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Calcifications - Left. Hepatitis C. \u000aOperation: Left breast biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalcifications in left breast. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left needle directed breast mass. \u000a2. Additional tissue inferior biopsy site. Stitch marked side is adjacent. \u000aWhat is nodule adjacent to the stitch? \u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Calcifications and hook wire in specimen..........DR \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PADERA,ROBERT F.,JR.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1, left needle directed breast biopsy", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x \u000a3.4 x 0.9cm breast biopsy specimen. The specimen is received with a wire that \u000ahas become largely removed from the mass. The specimen is received with two (2) \u000aorienting sutures. A double long suture is present indicating lateral and a \u000adouble short suture is received indicating superior. The specimen is inked per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior \u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. \u000aAn area of calcifications is identified adjacent to the superior and posterior \u000amargins measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  The remainder of the breast parenchyma \u000ais composed of largely adipose tissue with bands of fibrous tissue running \u000athroughout. No other discrete lesions are identified. The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned and entirely submitted from lateral to medial. \u000aA specimen radiograph is received which shows an area of calcifications and a \u000ahookwire. \u000aMicro 1: lateral tips, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, submitted from lateral to medial, \u000amulti frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial tip, 10 frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2, additional tissue inferior", consists of a single \u000afragment of tan-white fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  The \u000aspecimen is received with a single stitch indicating a nodule of interest in \u000athe specimen. As the specimen contains only one stitch, it cannot be oriented. \u000aTherefore, the entire outer aspect of the specimen is inked black. The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned. The area marked by the stitch contains a \u000awhite-tan firm nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm that is located adjacent to \u000aa thin walled cyst containing clear fluid, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm  \u000aThese structures are present adjacent to the inked resection margin. The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted. \u000aMicro 13: region of nodule, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 14: remainder of specimen, 4 frags, ESS. \u000arp \u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
