s identified. The \u000aspecimen has been previously inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for \u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; \u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. \u000aAn accompanying radiograph shows the specimen with the wire localization needle \u000anear a site of a small group of microcalcifications. \u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from a lateral to medial, revealing \u000apredominantly white-yellow adipose tissue with very minimal amount of fibrous \u000atissue, with no masses or lesions suggestive of malignancy, which are grossly \u000aidentified. The entire specimen is submitted. \u000aMicro 1: lateral perpendicular margins, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right wire localized breast biopsy from lateral to medial, \u000a1-2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 12: medial perpendicular margins, multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2, left needle directed breast biopsy", consists of a \u000afragmented, unoriented left wire localized breast biopsy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm in aggregate; two (2) fragments are connected by a very small \u000aportion of tissue and contain a needle localization wire. This larger fragment \u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm  The smaller detached fragment measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 1.0cm  \u000aAn accompanying radiograph shows the specimen to be intact, with a wire \u000alocalization needle at the site of a small cluster of microcalcifications. \u000aThe specimen is inked in black and serially sectioned to reveal predominantly \u000ayellow adipose tissue with a very small amount of white fibrous tissue, with no \u000amasses or lesions suggestive of malignancy grossly identified. The specimen is \u000aradiographed and the slices containing microcalcifications are entirely \u000asubmitted; representative sections of the detached fragment are also submitted. \u000aApproximately 30% of the entire specimen is examined microscopically. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast wire localized biopsy, containing calcifications, \u000amulti frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 20: detached fragment, 4 frags, RSS. \u000aNOTE: Slices containing the microcalcifications are submitted in micro 17 \u000athrough 19. \u000alcl \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
