section of breast tissue \u000aclosest to the curled wire edge is inked yellow and closest to the bent wire \u000aedge is inked blue. The remainder of the specimen is inked black. The main \u000aspecimen has a central friable dark brown area closest to the blue-inked margin \u000a(1.2 x 1.1cm ). Additionally, separate fragments of fibroadipose tissue \u000aaccompany the main specimen (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm in aggregate). The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned and submitted entirely. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Wire localized specimen, serially sectioned from blue to yellow \u000amargin, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Unoriented separate fibroadipose tissue frags, multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Medial specimen", consists of a firm yellow/tan/red fragment of \u000afibroadipose tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ). An accompanying specimen radiograph \u000ademonstrates the tissue fragment with a centrally located MRI clip. No other \u000acalcifications are identified. The specimen is inked black and is serially \u000asectioned. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen serially sectioned, 3 frags each, ESS. \u000aKRI/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a10/31/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
