VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA (best seen on deeper levels of block #8), \u000aassociated with histologic and radiologic calcifications. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aScattered calcifications are associated with atrophic breast \u000aepithelium. \u000aNOTE: A specific breast core needle biopsy site is not seen. However, the \u000aclip marking the site was removed in the specimen. The needle biopsy was \u000aperformed four months previously and the site may have healed. \u000aThe area of ADH in this specimen is associated with the cluster of \u000amicrocalcifications that were localized by the radiologist. \u000aAll margins are inked and exmained histologically and no carcinoma is \u000aseen. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 48 year old female with history of core posterior calcifications for \u000aADH REMOVED_DATE (see previous report) marked with clip and radiology report. \u000aOperation: Left needle localization x 2 \u000aOperative findings: 2 areas of calcifications \u000aClinical Diagnosis: ADH - left breast \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast - clip marked area of old core biopsy \u000aMAMMOGRAM: Clip and calcifications are in seen in specimen - Dr. Jack Meyer. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by MAGI GALLUZZI,CRISTINA,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number \u000aand "left breast tissue", and consists of a segment of breast tissue measuring \u000a8 x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm  49g. Two needle wires are inserted in the specimen. The \u000aspecimen is received inked by the surgeon. The specimen is inked for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; \u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Sections of margins are \u000asubmitted for microscopic examination. Also received is the corresponding \u000amammogram demonstrating a clip and calcifications. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned to show two white/gray, poorly defined, firm areas measuring REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.5 x 0.6cm and REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0.5cm  respectively in proximity to the wires. A \u000a0.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.1cm cavity is present in the center of the larger area \u000adescribed, possibly representing a core biopsy. Ninety percent of the specimen \u000aincluding all fibrous tissue is submitted. \u000aThe blocks and remaining tissue are radiographed. The cluster of \u000acalcifications seen in the specimen radiograph are in block #8. No other \u000aclustered calcifications are seen. The clip is not seen. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  larger area described, 11 frags, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  smaller area described, 9 frags, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  other margins or resection, 3 frags, RSS \u000acmg \u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
