dial to lateral direction. A \u000awire enters at the intersection of the superior and lateral margins. \u000aSectioning into thirteen slices reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm nodule at the \u000asuperior/lateral aspect of the specimen, 0.1cm from the closest lateral \u000amargin. The nodule spans slices #3 -#6. Representative sections are submitted \u000afor histologic analysis. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior tip, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Tan/brown nodule, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Serial sections of the specimen, 1 frag each ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  has 2 frags), \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior tip, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast mass with wire", consists of a soft tissue \u000afragment, previously inked per the pathology protocol for the evaluation of \u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; \u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange, which measures 4.1cm in the superior to \u000ainferior direction, 3.9cm from medial to lateral direction, and 2.4cm in the \u000aanterior to posterior direction. The specimen is received with a wire separate \u000afrom the tissue. Sectioning into ten slices revealed a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm \u000atan/brown nodule abutting the posterior margin. The lesion encompasses slices \u000a#6-#8. Representative section is submitted for histologic analysis. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior tip, 7 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Serial sections, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Tan/brown nodule, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior aspect of the specimen, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior tip, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aCJD/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 26,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03:07:39PM \u000a[report_end] 
