VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: RAYMOND J REILLY MB,BCH,BAO \u000aCASE: BG-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Eric L Snyder, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Michelle S Hirsch, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A CLIP MARKING A PRIOR \u000aCONE NEEDLE BIOPSY SITE": \u000aSEVERLEY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, associated with columnar cell \u000achange with atypia (blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; levels excision), is present in \u000atwo of eight (2:8) slides (See NOTE). \u000aThe atypical areas are close to the prior biopsy site and are associated \u000awith calcifications. \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aBiopsy site changes are present. \u000aNOTE: Two of the foci of ADH closely approach a diagnosis of ductal \u000acarcinoma in situ, and are present < 0.1cm from the unoriented resection \u000amargin (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , best seen on the original HE level and level 3). \u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. S. Lester (Breast Pathology Service) who \u000aconcurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Extensive atypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass, needle localization \u000aRadiology report: Hookwire and clip in specimen. Called to O.R by MPO. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aRight breast needle localization \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patients name, unit \u000anumber, and "right breast needle localization", and consists of a single \u000aunoriented fragment of soft, yellow to pink/tan, fibroadipose tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 1.0cm ), accompanied by a needle. The specimen radiograph reveals a central \u000adensity and a clip, but no calcifications. Upon sectioning, the specimen has \u000amultiple focal hemorrhages (largest 0.2cm in greatest dimension) as well as a \u000acentral area of pale/tan fibrotic tissue (0.3 x 0.2cm ), located 0.2cm from \u000athe nearest margin. The specimen is entirely inked in black and serially \u000asectioned and submitted in 8 cassettes. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - right breast, ESS. \u000aCK \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Eric L Snyder M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Review by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a2/11/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
