VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D. \u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aSYNOPSIS: \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aSize - 0.9cm \u000aMultifocal - yes \u000aHistologic Type - mixed ductal and lobular \u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate) \u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate \u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent \u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - absent \u000aSkin invasion - absent \u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - absent \u000aFinal Margins (invasive) - \u000aNegative (>0.3cm ) - lateral, anterior, medial \u000aClose (0.1-0.3cm ) - superior (focal, 0.2cm ) \u000aVery close (<0.1cm from margin)- inferior (multifocal), posterior (focal) \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aTypes - cribriform \u000aNuclear grade - intermediate \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present \u000aExtent of DCIS \u000aNumber of blocks:total - 7:22 blocks \u000aFinal Margins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (>0.3cm ) - posterior, superior, anterior, medial \u000aVery close (<0.1cm ) - inferior (multifocal), lateral \u000a(multifocal) \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia \u000aSkin with scar \u000aSkeletal muscle \u000aPapilloma with atypia \u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions \u000aBiopsy site \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously \u000a2) RIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION: \u000aBenign breast tissue with biopsy cavity. \u000aSkin with scar. \u000aFibrocystic changes with cysts. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000a3) RIGHT BREAST WITH SKIN, RE-EXCISION: \u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change. \u000a4) RIGHT BREAST, AXILLARY CONTENTS: \u000aEight (8) lymph nodes with no tumor present. \u000aNOTE: Positive lymph nodes were present in a prior specimen ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: DCIS & invasive cancer, rt brst. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS & invasive cancer, R breast. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Tumor site, R breast. \u000a2. DCIS site superior aspect, R breast. \u000a3. Dog ear of skin, R breast. \u000a4. Axillary contents. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications within specimen. \u000a(radiology report is not initialed by radiologist) \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,MARTIN C,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in four parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "right breast tumor site", consists of an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm \u000abreast biopsy with two localization wires in place, a short suture marking \u000asuperior, and a long suture marking lateral. An accompanying specimen \u000aradiograph demonstrates two small clusters of calcification. The specimen is \u000areceived inked for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = \u000ablue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. \u000aThere is an irregular segment of tan skin measuring 0.7cm in length and \u000aranging in width from REMOVED_DATE to 3.0cm  A longitudinal, well-healed surgical scar \u000a(2.0cm ) is present. Close to the larger cluster of calcification is a REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.5cm hemorrhagic area consistent with prior biopsy site. Two remarkably \u000ahard, irregular areas (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ) are present \u000aclose to the prior biopsy cavity site located approximately 0.8cm apart. The \u000alarger of the areas is located 0.1cm from the inferior, 1.0cm from the \u000asuperior, and 1.5cm from the posterior margin. The smaller of the two hard \u000aareas is located 0.2cm from the inferior and 1.5cm from the superior margin. \u000aThe lateral, medial, and anterior margins are located greater than 1.5cm from \u000athe clusters of calcification and hard areas. The remainder of the specimen \u000ais composed of 30% fibrous tissue and 70% adipose tissue with no other gross \u000aabnormality present. \u000aMicro 1: larger hard area, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 2: smaller hard area, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 3: superior margin closest to smaller hard area, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  probable biopsy cavity, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue surrounding larger hard area, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue surrounding smaller hard area, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 18: medial margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro 21: superior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 22: skin with scar, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aPart two, "DCIS site sueprior aspect, R breast", consists of a single fragment \u000aof breast tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE (depth) x 0.9cm ) oriented with a short suture for \u000asuperior and a long suture for lateral. The specimen is received inked per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior \u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. \u000aThere is a skin ellipse (4.0 x 1.0cm ) containing a 3.0cm  well-healed \u000asurgical scar. The specimen is composed of 85% of adipose tissue with no \u000agross abnormalities present. The specimen is submitted from medial to lateral \u000ain its entirety. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  DCIS site, rt breast, multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart three, "dog ear of skin, right breast", consists of a triangular piece of \u000askin and subjacent adipose tissue (2.6 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm in depth). The skin is \u000atan in color with no gross abnormalities. \u000aMicro 35: skin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aPart four, "axillary contents", consists of a single fragment of adipose tissue \u000a(5.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.4cm ). Six lymph nodes averaging 0.4cm in size are present. \u000aTwo potential lymph nodes, mostly replaced by adipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE \u000aand 1.2cm in greatest dimension, are also present. \u000aMicro 36: 7 potential lymph nodes, 7 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  1 potential lymph node, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro 39: 1 potential lymph node, 2 frags, ESS. \u000amcc \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN, PLASTIC REPAIR \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION \u000a[report_end] 
