an adjacent cavity (3 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). Surrounding area of fibrosis is present in this area. This large biopsy \u000asite is located underneath the skin scar, partially becoming part of deep \u000aexcisional margin. The deep margin is inked. Representative sections are \u000asubmitted. No lymph nodes are identified within the specimen. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity with closest margin, 4 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 5: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 6: inner outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 7: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 8: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 9: skin with scar, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 10: nipple, 2 frags, RSS. \u000ajis \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000a[report_end] 
