VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST MASS, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS: \u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA (block 6; levels examined)(see NOTE). \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia and apocrine metaplasia. \u000aFibroadenoma, 0.8cm  \u000aStromal reaction consistent with the prior core needle biopsy site. \u000aNOTE: \u000aThere is a lobular unit (0.2cm ) filled with a population of cells with \u000amarkedly pleomorphic nuclei. Although not sufficient for a diagnosis of DCIS, \u000athe degree of pleomorphism is unusual for ADH; partial involvement of a lobule \u000aby DCIS is favored. This area is 0.1cm from the lateral margin. This area \u000adoes not correlate with the radiologic mass. \u000aThis case was reviewed at staff Surgical Pathology conference. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 1.5cm mass, core biopsy showed fibroadenoma; strong family history \u000a(per Pathology resident). \u000aOperation: Lt breast needle localization. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Lt breast mass. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Lt breast tissue, long lateral, short superior. \u000aMAMMO: Mass and hookwire in specimen. DR \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BROWNE,TARA-JANE,MB,BCH,BAO \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number \u000aand "#1 left breast tissue, short superior, long lateral". The specimen \u000aconsists of one piece of tissue (6.5 x 3 x 0.7cm in depth). There is one \u000ashort stitch indicating the superior margin and one long stitch indicating the \u000alateral margin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; \u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen contains a \u000asingle piece of wire in place. There is an accompanying radiograph which shows \u000athat the wire is localized to an area that corresponds to a mass. The mass is \u000afirm and tan-colored, measuring approximately 1.5cm in its greatest diameter. \u000aThe specimen is submitted in its entirety for histological analysis. \u000aMicro 1: superior margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 2: inferior margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 3&4: uninvolved breast, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue including mass area, 13 frags, ESS. \u000arfi \u000aReports to: WHANG, EDWARD, E. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
