he specimen is inked (The \u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange). The localization wire enters the specimen in the lateral \u000aaspect and leaves the specimen in the superior anterior aspect. Specimen is \u000asectioned from anterior to posterior to show a parenchyma consisting of \u000atan/white fibrous tissue that is focally cystic with focal calcifications, \u000aalong with tan/yellow lobulated adipose tissue. No other lesions are grossly \u000aidentified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Specimen sectioned with perpendicular section of anterior aspect \u000ain  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and perpendicular section of posterior aspect in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , multi frags, \u000aESS. \u000aDRD/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a4/25/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
