VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D. \u000aCASE: BG-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Briana Gleason, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Marisa R Nucci, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION": \u000aHealing biopsy site. \u000aSkin with cicatrix. \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aNo residual phyllodes tumor identified. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "UTERUS WITH LEFT TUBE AND OVARY" (861g): \u000aEndometrium: \u000aProliferative endometrium. \u000aMyometrium: \u000aAdenomyosis. \u000aLeiomyomata (intramural and subserosal, up to 9.5cm ). \u000aSerosa: \u000aNo significant pathologic change. \u000aLeft fallopian tube: \u000aPeritubal adhesions. \u000aLeft ovary: \u000aCystic follicles. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "CERVIX (PORTION OF)": \u000aSquamous metaplasia. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Re-excision left breast phyllodes tumor excision site. \u000aOperation: Re-excision left breast biopsy site, TAH/LSO \u000aOperative Findings: \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Phyllodes tumor left breast, menorrhagia/fibroids \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000a1. Re-excision left breast biopsy site \u000a2. Uterus with left tube and ovary \u000a3. Cervix (portion of) \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in 3 parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "re-excision left breast biopsy site", consists of a breast \u000aexcision specimen (7.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 4.8cm ) with a skin ellipse (5.6 x 1.1cm ). The \u000aspecimen has been previously inked by the surgeon in five colors (red = \u000asuperior, green = inferior, black = posterior, orange = medial, and yellow = \u000alateral); the skin represents the anterior margin. There is a biopsy cavity \u000a(2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.9cm ) with surrounding areas of fat necrosis and focal \u000ahemorrhage. The biopsy cavity is located 1.2cm from the closest superior \u000amargin, 1.6cm from the closest posterior margin, 2.9cm from the closest skin \u000amargin, 2.5cm from the closest medial margin and 2.3cm from the closest \u000alateral margin and 2.8cm from the closest inferior margin. The breast \u000aparenchyma is composed of approximately 80% fibrous tissue and 20% adipose \u000atissue. Representative sections of biopsy cavity and each margin are \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - biopsy cavity superior margin, 5 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - biopsy cavity posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - medial margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - skin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aPart B, labeled "uterus, with left tube and ovary", is a 861-gram hysterectomy \u000aspecimen (17 x 12 x 11cm ) with attached left ovary (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ) and \u000aleft fallopian tube (4.2cm in length by 0.8cm in diameter), and portion of \u000athe right fallopian tube (4.7cm in length by 0.6cm in diameter). The \u000acervical margin (3.9 x 3.7cm ) has a red, granular appearance. The \u000aendocervical canal (2.2cm in length) has a tan herringbone appearance. The \u000aendometrial cavity (2.9cm from cornu to cornu and 4.1cm in length) is grossly \u000adistorted by approximately ten subserosal and intramural fibroids (up to 9.5cm \u000ain diameter). The cut surface of the leiomyomata is white and whorled, without \u000aareas of hemorrhage or necrosis. The myometrium is thickened (maximum thickness \u000aof 3.2cm ). The left fallopian tube is patent and has a fimbriated end. The \u000aovary contains multiple corpora albicantia. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - anterior cervical margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - posterior cervical margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - LUS, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - anterior endometrium, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - posterior endometrium, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - serosa, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - representative sections of large leio, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - right fallopian tube segment, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - left fallopian tube fimbria cross sections, 5 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - ovary, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aPart C, labeled "cervix", consists of two fragments of ectocervix with \u000aglistening, white mucosa (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm in aggregate). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - representative sections of each fragment, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Briana Gleason M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Marisa R Nucci M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
