rior revealing a fibrofatty breast parenchyma \u000awith no discrete masses or lesions. The specimen consists of 30% fibrous \u000atissue and 70% adipose tissue. The area of calcifications are entirely \u000asubmitted for histologic evaluation. 100% of the specimen is submitted \u000afor histologic evaluation. A single area of hemorrhage is identified and \u000alocated equidistant between the anterior and posterior margins measuring 0.5cm \u000ain greatest dimension and is 0.2cm from the lateral margin and greater than \u000a0.5cm from all other margins. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area of calcification, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 6: potential core biopsy site, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of fibrous tissue, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, ESS \u000ajs \u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
