VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCORSON, JOSEPH, M., M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CORSON,JOSEPH M.,M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "INFERIOR RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY", EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: \u000aFibrocystic change, with a single focus of atypical lobular hyperplasia \u000a(block 6, levels examined). \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "SUPERIOR RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY", EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: \u000aFibroadenomas (two, each 0.7cm ). \u000aFibrocystic change. \u000aRIGHT BREAST TISSUE AND SKIN, REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY (600 G): \u000aSkin, subcutaneous and mature adipose tissue with no significant \u000apathologic change. \u000aLEFT BREAST TISSUE AND SKIN, REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY, 630 G: \u000aSkin, subcutaneous tissue with no significant pathologic change. \u000aBenign breast tissue. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 36 year old female with right mammo showing upper outer quadrant 7mm \u000adensity, not ameneable to needle aspiration. Left inner quadrant \u000a13mm density, core biopsy on REMOVED_DATE showing fibroadenoma. \u000aOperation: Right breast double wire localization of mammo densities. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast upper outer quadrant. \u000a#2. Right breast lower inner quadrant. \u000a#3. Right breast tissue and skin. \u000a#4. Left breast tissue and skin. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. INFERIOR RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY": \u000aNo areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. SUPERIOR RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY": \u000a2 nodules (0.7cm and 0.7cm ) grossly consistent with fibroadenoma. \u000aSPECIMEN RADIOGRAPHS: Representative densities in specimen #1 and 2. WK \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ZEMBOWICZ,ARTUR , M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, all labeled with the patient's \u000aname and number. \u000aPart one, "inferior right breast biopsy", consists of a single not oriented \u000afragment of yellow/tan fibrofatty tissue with needle wire in place (4 x 3 x 1 \u000acm). No areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma are present. \u000aMICRO #1-8: Inferior right breast biopsy, ESS, 9 frags. \u000aThe second part, "superior right breast biopsy", consists of a single not \u000aoriented tan/yellow fragment of fibrofatty tissue with needle wire in place \u000a(7.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm ). There are two well-circumscribed white nodules, bulging \u000aon cross section, grossly consistent with fibroadenoma. The remaining breast \u000atissue consists of adipose and adipose tissue and 20% of tan fibrous breast \u000atissue. There are no areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma. \u000aMICRO #9 and 10: Nodules, ESS, 3 frags. \u000aMICRO #11-15: Fibrous breast tissue, ESS, 8 frags. \u000aThe third part, "right breast tissue and skin", consists of 600 gram reduction \u000amammoplasty specimen composed of unremarkable irregularly shaped fragments of \u000askin, subcutaneous tissue and adipose tissue with strands of fibrous breast \u000atissue (less than 20% of specimen). The entire specimen measures 20 x 15 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. There are no areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma or \u000ainflammatory process. \u000aMICRO #16 and 17: Skin, subcutaneous tissue and breast tissue, RSS, 2 frags. \u000aThe fourth part, "left breast tissue and skin", consists of 630 grams reduction \u000amammoplasty specimen consisting of grossly unremarkable irregularly shaped \u000afragments of skin, subcutaneous and adipose tissue measuring 25 x 20 x 4cm in \u000aaggregate. The specimen is extensively sectioned to reveal no areas grossly \u000asuspicious for invasive carcinoma or any inflammatory process. Fibrous breast \u000atissue comprises less than 5% of the total specimen. \u000aMICRO #18: Left breast tissue and skin, RSS, 2 frags. \u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY \u000a[report_end] 
