VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aBreast tissue with focal atypical lobular hyperplasia, epithelial \u000ahyperplasia, and fibrocystic changes including sclerosing adenosis, \u000aapocrine metaplasia, cysts, and fibroadenomatoid stromal changes. \u000aCalcifications are present in benign epithelium. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 47 year old woman with R breast new microcalc, perimenopausal \u000a(-) FH. \u000aOperation: Rt needle directed breast bx. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Rt breast mammogram abnormality. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Rt breast bx - stitch short superior, long lateral. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++ in specimen. J. Leung, MD \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BUNDOCK,ELIZABETH A.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000aunit number and "rt breast bx", and consists of an oriented portion of \u000afibroadipose tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm ) with a localization wire in place and \u000aone short and one long suture present, placed by the surgeon to designate short \u000aand superior, respectively. An accompanying specimen radiograph is received \u000aand is reported as "calcium in specimen", signed J Leung, MD. The specimen is \u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; \u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = \u000aorange. The specimen is sectioned at 3mm intervals from medial to lateral, \u000arevealing 90% adipose tissue and 10% white fibrous tissue including cysts. No \u000afirm areas suspicious for invasive carcinoma are identified. The specimen is \u000aentirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 10 frags, ESS. \u000aeab \u000aReports to: LOCKHART, DIANE, CATHERINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
