VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCRUM, CHRISTOPHER, PAUL, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CRUM,CHRISTOPHER PAUL,M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST BIOPSY": \u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA (blocks 5-7) within 0.1cm of an inked \u000aresection resection margin, but not present at the resection margin. \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, extensive (10 of 11 blocks). \u000aNo vascular invasion seen. \u000aSCLEROSING INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMATOSIS. \u000aFibrocystic change, proliferative, extensive with atypical ductal \u000ahyperplasia. \u000aNOTE: \u000aA paraffin block will be sent for estrogen receptor analysis. The tumor \u000ais too diffusely and infiltrating for meaningul analysis by flow \u000acytometry. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: REMOVED_DATE NFDR for nipple galactoschezia "florid IDH and atypical lobular \u000aH". Now has adjacent asymmetrical thickening, FNA "atypical ductals". \u000aOperation: Left breast resection \u000aOperative findings: Dense breast tissue \u000aClinical Diagnosis: FCD with H, rule out more \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast resection - FS with ER and PR if indicated \u000aSingle tag - lateral and double tag-cephalad \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000a"Left breast": \u000aEpithelial proliferation and sclerosis, suggestive of ductal \u000apapilloma. \u000aDrs. Shulman/Welch \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HERMANOWSKI-VOSATKA,ANNE,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and "mass left \u000abreast", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm  breast mass with focal \u000ahemorrhage but no discrete mass, except for a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  tan/white, \u000aill-defined indurated area. This area is frozen in part. (FSA) \u000aMicro 1 - FSRA, ESS, 1 frag, 1 cass. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - indurated area in vicinity, RSS, 3 frags, 3 cass. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - lateral margin, ESS, multiple frags, 3 cass. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - medial portion, RSS, multiple frags, 2 cass. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - cephalad portion, RSS, multiple frags, 2 cass. \u000aNOTE: 75% of the biopsy is submitted. \u000aReports to: SHIRLEY, ROBERT, LAWRENCE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
