VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  LUMPECTOMY \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST BIOPSY SITE TISSUE": \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, two residual microscopic foci (blocks \u000a#5 and 6), with pagetoid ductal involvement. \u000aFibrocystic change, proliferative. \u000aSclerosing intraductal papillomatosis. \u000aFibroadenoma, microscopic. \u000aFat necrosis, fibrosis, and foreign body giant cell reaction \u000aconsistent with previous biopsy site. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT AXILLARY NODES LEVEL I": \u000aSix (6) lymph nodes; no tumor present. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT AXILLARY NODES LEVEL II": \u000aTen (10) lymph nodes; no tumor present. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Re-excision for ? margins and axillary dissection for staging. \u000aOperation: Left lumpectomy and axillary biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast biopsy site tissue (a) double stitch toward \u000askin, (b) single stitch cephala. \u000a2. Left axillary nodes level I. \u000a3. Left axillary nodes level II. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen, received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "left breast biopsy site tissue, (a) double stitch for skin, \u000a(b) single stitch cephalad", consists of one fragment of fibro fatty measuring \u000a7.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm with a single stitch denoting the portion of specimen \u000atowards the skin and a double stitch denoting the cephalad directions. In the \u000asuperior, posterior portion of the specimen, a 1.0cm in greatest dimensions \u000abiopsy cavity with organizing clot and fat necrosis is identified which is \u000alocated a minimum of 0.3cm from the margin. There are no areas grossly \u000asuspicious for infiltrating carcinoma identified. The remainder of the breast \u000aparenchyma consists of white firm rubbery tissue with numerous small cyst \u000ameasuring up to 0.4cm in greatest dimensions. \u000aSection Code: \u000aMicro #1-4 - breast tissue biopsy cavity, 4 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro #5-10 - additional representative breast tissue, multiple frags, RSS. \u000aPart two, labeled "left axillary nodes level I", consists of two fragments of \u000afibrofatty tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm in the aggregate within which \u000aare identified approximately six (6) tan lymph nodes ranging in sizes from REMOVED_DATE \u000ato 1.6cm in maximum dimensions. \u000aMicro #11-12 - level I left axillary node, multiple frags, RSS. \u000aPart three, labeled "left axillary nodes level II", consists of one fragment \u000aof fibro fatty tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm within which are identified \u000aapproximately twelve (12) tan lymph nodes ranging in sizes from REMOVED_DATE to 1.0cm \u000ain greatest dimensions. \u000aMicro #13-15 - left axillary nodes level II, multiple frags, RSS. \u000aReports to: SHIRLEY, ROBERT, LAWRENCE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LUMPECTOMY \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY \u000a[report_end] 
