VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST RE-EXCISION TISSUE" (47 GM): \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia. See note. \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aSclerosing adenosis, papillomatosis, calcifications in benign epithelium, \u000acysts, apocrine metaplasia. \u000aBiopsy cavity, extensive fat necrosis and foreign body giant cell reaction \u000ato polarizable foreign material. \u000aNOTE: The atypical changes are focallly worrisome for papillary DCIS \u000a(block 19), but the changes do not fulfill strict criteria. (Levels \u000aexamined.) \u000a(The case has been reviewed with Dr. Susan Lester of the Breast \u000aPathology Service.) \u000a( \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aOperation: Re-excision left breast biopsy site \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast atypical ductal hyperplasia \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left re-excisional breast tissue \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PADERA,ROBERT F.,JR.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000aunit number and "#1. left breast re-excisional tissue", and consists of a 47g \u000amass of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.4cm  The specimen has \u000abeen inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = \u000ayellow; medial = orange. There is a biopsy cavity present within the mass of \u000atissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm  This biopsy contains red/brown blood \u000aclot and is partially cystic. Surrounding the biopsy cavity are bright yellow \u000anodules measuring up to 0.8cm consistent with fat necrosis. The biopsy cavity \u000ais located 1.5cm from the inferior margin, 0.9cm from the superior margin, \u000a0.4cm from the anterior margin, 0.6cm from the posterior margin, 0.6cm from \u000amedial margin, and 1.1cm from the lateral margin. The remainder of the \u000abreast is composed primarily of adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted from lateral to medial. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast re-excisional tissue, mult frags, ESS \u000arp \u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
