S DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the \u000apatient's name, unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "left breast #1", and consists of two orange cassettes \u000acontaining cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.2cm in aggregate), which are submitted in toto. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Contents of orange cassettes, multi frags in each, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "left breast #2", and consists of two yellow cassettes \u000acontaining multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues \u000a(1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ), which are submitted in toto. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Contents of yellow cassettes, multi frags in each, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aJC/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Friday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 13,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04:17:45PM \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (3/17/09): \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for \u000ainvasive carcinoma (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) EQUIVOCAL (2+) \u000aNOTE: Normal epithelium shows appropriate immunoreactivity for estrogen and \u000aprogesterone receptors. \u000aFISH analysis for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu will be performed; results will be reported in an \u000aaddendum. \u000ainvasive carcinoma (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) NEGATIVE (0) \u000aNOTE: Normal epithelium shows appropriate immunoreactivity for estrogen and \u000aprogesterone receptors. \u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following \u000acriteria: \u000aHormone receptor analysis: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not \u000ayet been determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor \u000acells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but \u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive. \u000aEquivocal (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in \u000a>10% of tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in \u000a>30% of tumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational \u000ause only. \u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH \u000a17,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04:54:32PM \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (3/24/09) \u000aFISH was performed by Clarient using the PathVysion HER-2 DNA Probe Kit with \u000athe following (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aResults: NOT AMPLIFIED \u000aHER-2/CEP-17 ratio = REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of HER-2 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average centromere 17 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aREFERENCE RANGE: \u000aNOT AMPLIFIED HER-2/CEP-17 ratio < REMOVED_DATE \u000aEQUIVOCAL HER-2/CEP-17 ratio REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE \u000aAMPLIFIED  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /CEP-17 ratio 