VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s) \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Paul A. VanderLaan, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODES (including FSA): \u000aPlease see Part B. \u000aB. LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY (910g): \u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODES \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aSize - 1.7cm and 1.5cm  two (2) distinct foci \u000aMultifocal - Yes (see note) \u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - III (Poor) (8 or 9 points) \u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points) \u000aNuclear grade - High (3 points) \u000aMitotic counts - 3 points \u000aEIC - Negative \u000aLVI - Present \u000aDermal LVI - Absent \u000aSkin invasion - Absent \u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable \u000aFinal Margins (invasive) \u000aVery close(<0.1cm from margin)- Superficial anterior @ 12 o'clock \u000a(0.1cm ) \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aTypes - Comedo, solid, cribriform \u000aNuclear grade - High \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present \u000aNumber of blocks/total - 6:13 blocks \u000aMargins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (> 0.3cm ) - Posterior \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent \u000aLYMPH NODES \u000aSentinel lymph nodes - Negative (3 H&E levels examined) \u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0 \u000aNumber of nodes examined - 1 \u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 0:1 \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aBiopsy cavity \u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - p REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID c  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  MX \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) - Pending \u000aNOTE: There are two (2) distinct foci of invasive ductal carcinoma present, the \u000alarger in the upper inner quadrant at 9:30 and measuring 1.7cm  and the second \u000ain the upper midline at 12:00 and measuring 1.5cm  The two (2) foci are \u000aapproximately 7.0cm apart. \u000aC. MASTECTOMY SKIN: \u000aSkin and subcutis, negative for tumor. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: CA of Lt breast, 2 foci. \u000aOperation: SNB, Lt ax; Lt total mastex implant. \u000aOperative Findings: See op note. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: CA of Lt breast, 2 foci. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Left axillary sentinel lymph node (FS). \u000aB/2) Left breast (to FS Rm for tissue bank). \u000aC/3) Mastectomy skin. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1. SENT. LN, LT AX" (FSA): \u000aLymph node, negative for tumor \u000aOR Consultation by: LYNETTE MARIE SHOLL, M.D. \u000aResident: KEVIN GOLDEN, M.D., PH.D. \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThis is a specimen received fresh, in three parts, all labeled with the \u000apatient's name and medical record number. \u000aThe specimen, Part A, "#1. Left axillary sentinel lymph node", consists of one \u000afragment of yellow/tan fatty tissue (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ) with one palpable \u000alymph node. The specimen is bisected and entirely submitted as frozen section \u000aA. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Frozen section A remnant, bisected, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aThe specimen, Part B, "#2. Left breast", consists of a 910-gram simple \u000amastectomy with a tan/pink skin ellipse (14.5 x 4.0cm ), areola (4.5cm ), and \u000aeverted nipple (1.2cm ). The specimen overall measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6.0cm  \u000aThe specimen is oriented per the surgeon such that a short stitch designates \u000asuperior and a long stitch designates lateral. The skin ellipse is grossly \u000aunremarkable with any notable masses, lesions or scars. A blue dye is noted \u000aabout the areolar region. The deep margin is a smooth fascial plane, and was \u000ainked black. The specimen was serially sectioned from medial to lateral to \u000areveal two discrete masses. The first mass (mass #1) is located in the upper \u000ainner quadrant at 9:30, measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm  and abuts the superficial \u000amargin (inked blue). This mass is an irregular firm tan/white color, and is \u000alocated 4.0cm from the deep resection margin. The second mass (mass #2) is \u000alocated in the central breast at 12 o'clock, measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm  and \u000ais located 2.0cm from the deep resection margin, and approximately 7.0cm away \u000afrom mass #1. This mass also is a firm white/tan color with somewhat irregular \u000aborders. The intervening tissue between the two masses is grossly normal. \u000aEach mass has a notable previous biopsy cavity site with a clip identified. \u000aThe remainder of the lobulated yellow breast tissue is grossly normal, and has \u000aapproximately 20% scattered white fibrous tissue running through the lobulated \u000afatty tissue. Representative sections of the tumors and the normal breast were \u000asubmitted for tissue banking. Representative sections are submitted for \u000ahistology. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass #2 to superficial margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass #1 with clip, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass #1 lateral to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Area lateral to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Area medial to mass #2, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass #2 with clip and biopsy cavity, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass #2 lateral to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Area just lateral to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant deep to mass #1, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aThe specimen, Part C, "#3. Mastectomy skin", consists of three strips of \u000apink/tan skin and subcutis (15.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  and REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.5 x 0.4cm ). No masses, lesions, or scars are noted in the skin strips. \u000aRepresentative cross sections are submitted for histology. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mastectomy skin, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aPVA/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on Thursday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 16,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05:31:54PM \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (4/20/09) \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma, mass # 1, upper inner quadrant (block \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) EQUIVOCAL-HETEROGENEOUS (1-2+) \u000aInvasive carcinoma, mass # 2, central (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) NEGATIVE (0) \u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen \u000aand progesterone receptors. \u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following \u000acriteria: \u000aHormone receptor analysis: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not \u000ayet been determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor \u000acells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but \u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive. \u000aEquivocal (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in \u000a>10% of tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in \u000a>30% of tumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational \u000ause only. \u000aAddendum #1 by James L Connolly M.D., Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH \u000a20,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01:57:37PM \u000a[report_end] 
