) and a \u000aneedle localization wire in placed (entering at the superolateral aspect and \u000aexiting at the superior aspect). The specimen is inked by the surgeon per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange. \u000aThe specimen is accompanied by a radiograph, which exhibit a few scattered \u000acalcifications and a hookwire in placed. The specimen is serially sectioned \u000afrom superior to inferior, exhibiting approximately 75% tan/white dense, \u000afocally cystic fibrous stroma and 25% yellow lobulated adipose tissue. No \u000aother gross lesions identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast tissue sequentially from superior to inferior (probable \u000acalcifications in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), multi frags, ESS. \u000adl/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on \u000a8/15/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
