tified within 0.1cm of the inferior margin, 0.5cm of the superior \u000amargin, 0.7cm of the deep margin, 1.3cm of the anterior margin and greater \u000athan 1.5cm from the medial and lateral margins. A clip is identified in the \u000aspecimen adjacent to the mass. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is \u000acomposed of approximately 60% fibrous tissue and 40% adipose tissue. The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue with multiple margins, serially submitted \u000afrom lateral to medial, mult frags, ESS \u000aNOTE: The section with the clip is cut transversely and entirely submitted in \u000acassettes 11 and 12. \u000amsh \u000aReports to: SHOJI, BRENT, T. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
