 on REMOVED_DATE \u000aat 9:05 p.m.), "surgeon tried to reach Radiology unsuccessfully and decided \u000athat x-ray is not necessary (wire in mass) - specimen fixed and processed for \u000apathology." The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial. In the \u000alateral/central aspect of the specimen, there is a poorly delineated irregular \u000acystic/gelatinous tan mass (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ) which is traversed by the \u000aneedle localization wire. The mass comes within 0.5cm of the superior margin, \u000a0.4cm of the inferior margin, 0.5cm of the posterior margin, 0.7cm of the \u000aanterior/skin margin, 0.4cm from the lateral margin, and 1.3cm at the medial \u000amargin. The remainder of the cut surface is composed of approximately 90% \u000ayellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue and 10% delicate white/tan fibrous stroma \u000awith no additional discrete lesions identified. The specimen is entirely \u000asequentially submitted from lateral to medial. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central specimen from lateral to medial (mass in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), multi \u000afrags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS. \u000aLMB/mmm \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a7/3/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aSurgical addendum: \u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Deborah Dillon and Dr. Susan Lester, Breast \u000aPathology Service, who concur. \u000aAddendum #1 by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
