he \u000acentral aspect of the breast extending laterally (upper outer quadrant), \u000afocally extending to the slightly puckered deep margin 0.5cm deep to the \u000aaforementioned skin scar. Probable synthetic suture material is present within \u000ahemorrhagic cavitary portion of the lesion. The remaining breast tissue \u000aconsists predominately of yellow/tan lobulated fat with scant tan/white fibrous \u000astroma. No lymph nodes are identified within the lateral aspect of the \u000aspecimen. No other gross lesions are identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple and scar contiguous with biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy cavity and scar, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy cavity (white stellate area), in relationship to puckered \u000adeep margin (sequentially from medial to lateral), 5 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant (away from lesion), 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aDfi/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Patricia A. R. Brunker M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
