VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOGINO, SHUJI, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D. \u000a1. RIGHT BREAST; MAMMOPLASTY (244 GM): \u000aBreast tissue with a single focus of LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (LCIS) \u000a(<0.1cm )(block 2). \u000aDystrophic calcifications (up to 2.4cm ) in stroma and fibroadenomatous \u000astromal changes. \u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change. \u000aNOTE: The nuclear grade of the LCIS is slightly higher than that typically \u000aseen. Selected slide (#2) has been reviewed by D. S. Lester. \u000a2. LEFT BREAST, MAMMOPLASTY (94G): \u000aBenign breast tissue and skin with no significant pathologic change. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Status post gastric bypass for morbid obesity, now with skin laxity. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Skin laxity. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Right breast 240 gm \u000a1) Left breast tissue 90 gm. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BUNDOCK,ELIZABETH A.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart 1, "right breast tissue", consists of a 244 gm, 18 x 9 x 3cm aggregate of \u000ahemorrhagic fibrofatty breast tissue and multiple fragments of tan/pink \u000aunremarkable skin. Serial sectioning of the breast tissue reveals three \u000agray/yellow to red focally hemorrhagic, indurated, calcified nodules (ranging \u000afrom REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm ). The remaining tissue consists of \u000aapproximately equal amounts of white/tan, lumpy fibrous stroma and yellow/tan, \u000alobulated fat. No other lesions are grossly identified. \u000aMicro 1: Calcified nodules, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Skin and breast stroma, 4 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional tissue, 8 frags, RSS. \u000aPart 2, "left breast tissue", consists of a 94 gm, 10 x 9 x 2cm aggregate of \u000atan/pink unremarkable skin and fibrofatty breast tissue fragments. Sectioning \u000aof the breast tissue reveals approximately equal amounts of yellow/tan, \u000alobulated fat and tan/white, lumpy fibrous stroma. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Skin and breast stroma, 4 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Additional tissue, 3 frags, RSS. \u000adfi \u000aReports to: BREUING, KARL, HEINZ M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY \u000a[report_end] 
