000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange per surgeon. The majority of the \u000aspecimen is adipose tissue with focal fibrosis. The specimen is submitted in \u000atoto for microscopic examination. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue, 18 frags, ESS. \u000aSpecimen #2, labeled "left breast re-excision", consists of a fragment of \u000afibrofatty tissue (8 x 5 x 2.5cm ). This is unoriented and the external \u000asurface of this tissue is inked black. The specimen is sampled to include all \u000athe fibrous tissue. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  re-excision, left breast, 7 frags, RSS. \u000amab \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
