VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRENN, THOMAS, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRENN,THOMAS,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP MARKING AN AREA OF BIOPSIED \u000aCALCIFICATION: \u000aFocal ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, associated with microcalcifications . \u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions with \u000acalcifications. \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aCysts and microcalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aCore biopsy site changes present. \u000aNOTE: \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aCase reviewed with Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 69 year old female with abnormal mammogram, S/P core biopsy right \u000abreast with atypical ductal hyperplasia. Plus rheumatoid arthritis with gold \u000atreatment on methotrexate, hypertension, headache, S/P right breast biopsy T+A. \u000aOperation: Right breast needle localization biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - right breast tissue -- mammo. \u000aRadiology: Clip in specimen, D. Smith, M.D. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BROCK,JANE E.,M.B.,B.S.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name and \u000aunit number and "right breast localized needle biopsy", and consists of an \u000aunoriented wire localized lumpectomy specimen (4.5cm x 3.5cm x 1.0cm ). The \u000aspecimen is received with a radiograph which demonstrates a wire, a clip, and \u000aa mass lesion in the center of the specimen. The specimen is inked blue. \u000aSectioning reveals a core biopsy site (0.4cm x 0.5cm x 0.5cm ) which is \u000asurrounded by a small rim of fibrous hemorrhagic tissue. The closest margin to \u000athe core biopsy site is 0.3cm  The lumpectomy is approximately 90% adipose \u000atissue. The remainder is composed of strands of fibrous tissue which are \u000aunremarkable. The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro #1+2: Breast tips, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro #3+4: Biopsy cavity, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro #5-9: Remainder of specimen, 6 frags, ESS. \u000ajeb/ \u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
