ormal mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right sentinel lymph nodes. \u000a#2. Right needle directed breast biopsy. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by NASCIMENTO,ALESSANDRA F.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two (2) parts, each labeled with the \u000apatient's name and unit number. \u000aPart #1, "right sentinel lymph nodes," consists of two (2) fragments of \u000atan/white fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0.8cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. Two (2) candidate lymph nodes are identified within the specimen, and \u000aentirely submitted for histologic examination. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  1 lymph node, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro 3 : 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart #2, labeled "right needle directed breast biopsy," consists of a \u000afragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm  \u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation \u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = \u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Within the specimen, there is a \u000aneedle loc. No mammogram is received with the specimen. On sectioning, a \u000atan/white, ill-defined firm area is identified measures REMOVED_DATE x 5 x 1cm  The \u000aill-defined area is grossly at the blue ink, black ink, yellow ink, green ink, \u000aand red ink. It is 0.7cm from the orange ink. Representative sections of the \u000aspecimen are submitted for histologic examination. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, including tissue around wire (micros 15 through \u000a19), 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
