VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Agoston Tony Agoston, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP MARKING A CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY \u000aSITE: \u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, cribriform pattern, bordering on ductal \u000acarcinoma in situ, is present as a 0.2cm focus in 1 of 13 blocks (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; \u000alevels examined) (see note). The ADH is adjacent to the prior core needle \u000abiopsy site. This area of ADH is present at the deep margin (with cautery \u000aon the ADH; < 0.1cm area). The cells are positive for estrogen and \u000aprogesterone receptors and negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu. \u000aAdditional foci of ADH associated with columnar cell change are present. \u000aNote: The ADH closely approaches a diagnosis of low grade ductal \u000acarcinoma in situ. However, due to the very limited extent classification \u000aas ADH is favored. \u000aThe entire specimen was examined microscopically, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 75 year old female with right breast atypical ductal hyperplasia. \u000aS/p image-guided core biopsy at Faulkner Hospital ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast ADH. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Right breast wire-localized excisional bx; short suture - superior, long \u000asuture - lateral. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen has wire, clip, mass. OR called. Dr. Sughra Raza. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and medical \u000arecord number, and consists of one part. \u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy", consists \u000aof a REMOVED_DATE gram specimen (4.0cm SI, 3.5cm ML, 3.0cm AP) is oriented with a \u000ashort suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The \u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. A wire enters the specimen superomedially and exits \u000ainferolaterally. A radiograph demonstrates the specimen associated with wire, \u000aclip, and a mass. The specimen is sectioned along the plane of the wire into \u000asix slices, with the medial/inferior margin as slice #1 and the \u000asuperior/lateral margin as slice #6. There is a wire and clip between slices 2 \u000aand 3 associated with core biopsy site changes and an irregular firm white \u000afibrous area (3.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm ) present in all slices. The firm white \u000afibrous area abuts the superior and lateral margins, and is 0.2cm from medial, \u000a0.5cm from inferior, 1.1cm from anterior, and 0.8cm from posterior margins. \u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted for histologic examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial/inferior margins (slice #1), perpendicular sections, 2, 2, \u000a1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, 1 frag per block, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, 1 frag per block, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, 1 frag per block, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, 1 frag per block, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6 (superior/lateral margin), perpendicular sections, 3 \u000afrags per block, ESS. \u000aTA/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Monday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 22,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04:52:39PM \u000a[report_end] 
