VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Soft tissue biopsy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Cheryl Adackapara, M.D. \u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, "TISSUE BEHIND NIPPLE": \u000aBreast tissue with lactiferous sinuses. \u000aNote: No carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic evaluation of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aLEFT BREAST, 4:00, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR AN INTRADUCTAL MASS: \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (e.g. block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; levels examined). \u000aIntraductal papilloma (2.3cm ). \u000aNote: No carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic evaluation of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, who concurs with this \u000ainterpretation. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 51 year old postmenopausal woman with left spontaneous bloody nipple \u000adischarge and left breast U/S on REMOVED_DATE revealing intraductal mass at 4:00 - \u000aexcision recommended. \u000aOperation: L breast wire localized terminal duct excision. \u000aOperative Findings: None specified. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: None specified. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Tissue behind nipple, left breast. \u000aB/2) Left breast tissue; short stitch - superior; long - lateral; whip stitch \u000aon deep margin; blue bowtie on divided ducts (mammo) \u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen x-ray and ultrasound - Dilated duct with intraductal mass \u000aand hookwire are within specimen. - Dr. Eva Gombos. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Tissue behind nipple left", consists of an unoriented REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm fragment of cauterized fibroadipose tissues, inked and embedded \u000ain toto. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left breast tissue (short stitch superior, long lateral, \u000awhip stitch deep margin, blue bowtie on 'divided ducts'", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x \u000a5.5 x 2.3cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating \u000asuperior (short suture), lateral (long suture), and deep (whip stitch) margins. \u000aA blue bowtie is present on the anterior/medial/inferior surface designating \u000a"divided ducts". A localizing wire enters the inferior aspect of the specimen \u000aand traverses superiorly. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by surgeon). The specimen \u000ais received with a radiograph demonstrating the localizing wire in place within \u000athe specimen adjacent to an encircled abnormality (dilated duct with \u000aintraductal mass, per radiology). Sectioning demonstrates a firm tan/white \u000acircumscribed lobulated lesion (intraductal) in the area of the localizing \u000awire, at least REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm  and within 0.1cm of closest inferior \u000amargin, 0.1cm of the closest anterior margin, 0.4cm of closest posterior \u000amargin, 0.5cm of the closest inferior margin, 0.6cm of the closest medial \u000amargin, and remote (greater than 1.5cm ) from the lateral margin. Remainder of \u000athe specimen is comprised of 30-40% tan/white fiber-dense tissue. The entire \u000aspecimen is submitted for microscopic examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : En face sutured divided duct end (1mm in thickness), 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, multi frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nodular lesion, sequentially from medial to lateral, multi frags, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Intervening uninvolved appearing fibrous tissue between lesion and \u000alateral margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Perpendicular lateral margin, multi frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of specimen, mult frags, ESS. \u000aDB/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
