VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU. \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aNOTE: Calcifications are associated with LCIS in this biopsy, as well as \u000awith benign epithelium. The association of LCIS with calcifications is an \u000aunusual finding. Given the absence of necrosis or lumens, the association \u000amay not be specific and be due LCIS involving areas with pre-existing \u000acalcifications. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Microcalcs, rt brst. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Rt needle loc. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications in specimen. OR called. LBT \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KINDELBERGER,DAVID W.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number \u000aand "right needle loc", and consists of a single fragment of yellow/pink/tan \u000afibroadipose tissue (2.2cm from superior to inferior x 3.5cm from anterior to \u000aposterior x 1.4cm from medial to lateral). There is an attached fragment of \u000askin, comprising the anterior surface of the specimen (1.9 x 1.1cm ). A metal \u000alocalizing wire is embedded within the specimen. The specimen has been inked \u000aby the surgeon in six colors per pathology protocol for the evaluation \u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = \u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is diffusely fibrous \u000awith multiple hemorrhagic foci, the largest measuring 0.4cm in diameter. No \u000aother lesions are grossly identified. The specimen is entirely submitted for \u000ahistologic evaluation from posterior to anterior. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast mass, 9 frags, ESS. \u000aAn accompanying radiogram demonstrates the presence of calcificiations and a \u000alocalizing wire within the specimen. \u000adk \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
