VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHARINE CARTER M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Rachel E Factor, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST TISSUE WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION 3:00: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia associated with columnar cell change (blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aand  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , multiple levels examined). \u000aApocrine metaplasia. \u000aFibroadenoma (0.8cm ). \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, apocrine cysts, sclerosing adenosis. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: History of nodule, left breast at 2 o'clock (0.8cm ), history of \u000aprior breast biopsy for fibroadenoma. \u000aOperation: Left mammographically directed breast biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Left breast tissue at 3 o'clock, short=superior, long=lateral. \u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: \u000aThe mass, hook and wire are in the specimen. Called to OR. \u000a---unsigned \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1. Left breast tissue at 3 o'clock, short superior, long lateral to \u000amammo", consisting of an irregular tan/yellow to tan/white fibrofatty portion \u000aof breast tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm ) that has a long suture marking lateral \u000aand short suture marking superior. The prosector concurs and notes that there \u000ais an ill-defined mass subjacent to the localization wire. Specimen is inked \u000a(the specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange) and sectioned from inferior to superior. The localization wire \u000aenters the specimen in anterior/inferior aspect. Cut surface shows a \u000atan/white, firm nodule (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ) that abuts the posterior aspect, is \u000a1.6cm from the lateral aspect, 0.7cm from the medial aspect, 1.7cm from the \u000aanterior aspect, 1.3cm from the superior aspect and 2.1cm from the inferior \u000aaspect. This tan/white nodule is surrounded by focally dense tan/white, \u000afocally cystic fibrous tissue that is primarily concentrated at the posterior \u000aaspect (40% of the parenchyma), while the remaining parenchyma consists of \u000atan/yellow, focally hemorrhagic lobulated fat. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nodule to medial, anterior and posterior margins, 2 frags total, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nodule to posterolateral and anterior margins, 2 frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin, multi frags total, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, multi frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sections of random fibrous tissue, multi frags, RSS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aDRD/jp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a11/20/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a11/29/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
