VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aPATIENT: JUDI-ANNE FOLEY \u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION RE-EXCISION AND CLIP FOR MICROCALCIFICATIONS: \u000aSmall focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia (block # REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), adjacent to the biopsy \u000asite. \u000aCore biopsy site changes. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Cluster of microcalcs, Rt breast -> ADH \u000aOperation: Right breast wire directed excisional biopsy \u000aOperative Findings: Not given \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalcs R breast ->ADH \u000aRADIOLOGY CONSULTATION: \u000aWire and clip within specimen. No residual calcifications. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000a#1 - Tissue from right breast. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number, \u000aand "tissue from Rt breast", and consists of a portion of fibrofatty breast \u000atissue (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ) with a localization wire in place (entering at the \u000aanterior aspect and exiting at the posterior). The specimen is inked per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. \u000aSections from anterior to posterior reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm cavity \u000acontaining tan, synthetic, gelatinous beads with peripheral hemorrhage, coming \u000ato within 0.1cm of the anterior margin, 0.2cm of the superior and inferior \u000amargins, 0.6cm of the lateral and medial margins, and 0.7cm of the posterior \u000amargin. A clip is present within the gelatinous beads at the anterior-most \u000aaspect of the cavity, and the wire traverses the lesion. The accompanying \u000aspecimen radiograph confirms the presence of a wire and clip in the tissue. No \u000aresidual calcifications are noted on the accompanying radiograph. The remaining \u000abreast tissue consists of yellow lobulated fat with scant fibrous stroma. The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histologic examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS \u000aDFI/jp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Ann K Folkins M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a8/2/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
