VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D. \u000a1. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, STITCH AT AXILLARY TAIL": \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis, cysts, and \u000aapocrine metaplasia. \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a2. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BERAST, STITCH AT AXILLARY TAIL": \u000aFocal Atypical lobular hyperplasia, epithelial hyperplasia, \u000asclerosing adenosis, cysts, and microcalcifications associated \u000awith benign epitheliium. \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000aFive (5) lymph nodes with no tumor seen. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Family history of breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast, stitch at axillary tail. \u000a2. Right breast, stitch at axillary tail (please look at nodes \u000amarked with stitch in axillary tail). \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1, left breast, stitch at axillary tail", consists of a 209 \u000agram simple mastectomy specimen (19.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm ), which bears a tan skin \u000aellipse (3.5 x 2.5cm ), which contains an unremarkable areola (2.2cm ) and \u000anipple (1.5cm ). No scar is identified. There is a stitch to denote an axillary \u000atail; however there does not appear to be a distinct axillary tail present. \u000aThe deep margin is a smooth fascial plane with skeletal muscle present (7.5 x \u000a0.6 x 0.3cm ); the deep margin is inked in black and the specimen is serially \u000asectioned to reveal a firm, but not hard, multinodular area (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) along the superior mid to inner portion of the breast; this area is \u000aapproximately 1.0cm from the deep and 1.0cm from the anterior margins. No \u000aareas or nodules suspicious for tumor are identified. Representative sections \u000aof the firm, multinodular area are submitted. Two (2) possible lymph nodes \u000aare identified in the area designated with a stitch as axillary tail. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  firm, multinodular area of fibrous breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 5: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 6: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 7: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 8: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 9: nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 10: 2 possible lymph nodes, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 11: additional soft tissue with possible lymph node candidate, 1 frag, \u000aRSS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2, right breast, stitch at axillary tail", consists of a \u000a213 gram, right simple mastectomy specimen (18.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm ), which bears \u000aa tan skin ellipse (4.0 x 2.5cm ) with an unremarkable areola (2.4cm ) and \u000anipple (1.5cm ). No scar is identified. There is a stitch to denote the \u000aaxillary tail. The deep margin is a smooth fascial plane with skeletal muscle \u000apresent (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ); it is inked in black and the specimen is \u000aserially sectioned to reveal firm, white fibrous tissue with multiple domed \u000acysts that range in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0.3cm  There is an area of firm, but \u000anot hard, multinodular white fibrous tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm ), which is REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the deep margin and 0.9cm from the anterior margin. The remainder of \u000athe specimen is comprised of unremarkable white fibrous tissue and adipose \u000atissue; no masses or lesions suspicious for tumor are identified. Five (5) \u000alymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to \u000a2.0cm in greatest dimension and are entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of white fibrous tissue, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 15: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 16: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 17: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 18: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 19: nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 20: largest lymph node bisected, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  1 lymph node each bisected, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 23: 2 intact lymph nodes, 1 frag, ESS. \u000alcl \u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000a[report_end] 
