VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DAVID JACOBSEN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Stacey A. Simons, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aColumnar cell change lining mucinous cysts, associated with \u000acalcifications, adjacent to the prior core biopsy site. \u000aApocrine cysts and benign breast tissue with calcifications. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aNOTE: This case was also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester (Breast Pathologist), who \u000aconcurs with this interpretation. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None provided. \u000aOperation: None provided. \u000aOperative Findings: None provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: None provided. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Left breast tissue, suture: short is superior, long stitch posterior \u000a(deep) - to mammo at 10:20. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aCalcs, clip and wire all contained in specimen. OR notified. \u000aDr. Elman/Dr. Frost \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name \u000aand unit number, and "#1. Left breast tissue, short stitch is superior, long \u000astitch is posterior (illegible)", and consists of one breast wire loop excision \u000a(6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm overall), received with a wire entering at the \u000aanterolateral aspect and exiting at the posteromedial aspect. The specimen is \u000aaccompanied by a radiograph, which has been marked by the radiologist to show a \u000awire calcification and clips all within the specimen. The specimen has been \u000ainked by the surgeon with a short stitch to indicate the superior aspect and \u000athe long stitch indicates the posterior/deep aspect, and has been inked by the \u000apathology resident. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specific dimensions of the \u000aspecimen after inking are as follows: 2.0cm S-I; 6.4cm A-P; 4.8cm M-L. The \u000aspecimen is sectioned from posterior to anterior and the tip of the wire is \u000alocated in slice #4. There is a firm white mass located in slices #6 through \u000a#12 (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ), which is marginally excised at the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the superior margin, 0.8cm from the inferior margin, 1.9cm from the \u000alateral margin, 1.3cm from the anterior margin and 1.1cm from the posterior \u000amargin. \u000aThe mass is white and homogenous, and relatively well-circumscribed with \u000apunctate areas of old hemorrhage. The remainder of the excised tissue is \u000agreater than 98% yellow lobulated adipose tissue with only scattered fibrous \u000astrand. The specimen is sectioned into 17 slices. The entire mass and all \u000afibrous tissue is submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Part of slice #5 (S, M, I), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6 bisected (S, M, I, L, ?P), 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Portion of slice #7 to include mass (S, M, I), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Part of slice #8 to encompass mass (S, M, I, ?P), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Part of slice #9 to encompass mass (S, M, I), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Part of slice #10 to encompass mass (S, M, I), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Part of slice #11 to encompass mass (S, I), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Part of slice #12 bisected to encompass mass (S, I, L), 2 frags, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Part of slice #13A and #13B to encompass mass versus fibrous \u000atissue (S, I), 4 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Closest anterior margin from slice #14, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Closest posterior margin from slice #3, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue from slice #14 and #15, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue from slice #15, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aNote: The clip is not grossly seen, but by measurement should appear in slice \u000a#7 or #8. \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a11/3/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
