east with grossly identified \u000amicrocalcifications in micro 1, multiple frags, ESS. \u000aThe second part of the specimen, labeled "#2 upper inner quadrant left breast", \u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue with hemorrhage \u000aand cystic areas measuring up to 0.3cm in greatest dimension, with no areas \u000agrossly suspicious for infiltrating carcinoma identified. \u000aMICRO REMOVED_DATE  Upper inner quadrant left breast mass, radiographically identified \u000acalcifications in micros REMOVED_DATE  multiple frags, ESS. \u000aReports to: DAVIS, SALLIE, KEENE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
