VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JUDY E GARBER M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER INNER QUADRANT, MRI GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A \u000a1.8 CM AREA ENHANCEMENT: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform and solid types (intermediate to high \u000anuclear grade), with focal calcifications, is present involving sclerosing \u000aadenosis and a fibroadenoma. An immunohistochemical study for p63 and \u000acytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID / REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  confirms the presence of myoepithelial cells in DCIS. No \u000anecrosis is seen. \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with \u000athe following results for DCIS (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) EQUIVOCAL (1+ to 2+) \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHISTORY: 50 year old female with a history of left breast LCIS and ADH in  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). Also with 3 sisters diagnosed with breast cancer. Now with new \u000aarea of abnormal enhancement in the right upper inner breast. \u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING: \u000a1. Right: 1.8cm  nonpalpable, regional and non-mass forming. \u000aLOCATION: \u000a1. Right: upper inner \u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY: \u000a1. MRI \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000a1. MRI cores - Green top/white bottom \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit \u000anumber, and "right breast", consists of two white cassettes with green lids, \u000aeach containing multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft \u000atissues (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm in aggregate), which are submitted in toto. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Contents of white cassettes with green lids, multi frags in each, \u000aESS. \u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following \u000acriteria: \u000aHormone receptor analysis: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not \u000ayet been determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% \u000aof tumor cells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor \u000acells but only a portion of the membrane is positive. \u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in >30% of tumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for \u000ainvestigational use only. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aJC/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 17,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11:32:41AM \u000a[report_end] 
