000awhite fibrous tissue. The specimen is inked in black and entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential sections to breast tissue, multi frags each, ESS. \u000aPart B, "left additional breast tissue", consists of one piece of breast tissue \u000a(3.6 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm ). The specimen contains three short tan sutures at \u000aopposing ends of the specimen, which all have the same length and are not \u000afurther designated. Sections through the specimen show yellow lobulated \u000aadipose tissue, intermixed with white fibrous areas. There is also a small \u000ahemorrhagic cyst (0.2cm ). The specimen also contains areas of hemorrhage (up \u000ato 0.7cm ). The accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates two small \u000aill-defined radiodense lesions. The entire specimen is inked in black and \u000aentirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential sections through the specimen, 2 frags each ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), 1 frag each ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aSs:lc \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
