0astellate, poorly circumscribed area with focal hemorrhage and a focal cyst-like \u000aspace (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ) which is present 0.3cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the inferior margin, 0.8cm from the lateral margin, 1.2cm from the \u000asuperior margin, 1.6cm from the posterior margin and 1.8cm from the overlying \u000askin. This area is associated with chalky yellow discoloration grossly \u000aconsistent with fat necrosis. The specimen is otherwise approximately 60% \u000atan/white fibrous tissue and 40% yellow fatty tissue. Approximately 95% of the \u000aspecimen including all margins and the stellate area are submitted for \u000amicroscopic examination. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue from superior to inferior, multi frags, RSS. \u000arlr \u000aReports to: SHOJI, BRENT, T. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
