VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Christopher P. Elco, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, MASS WITH WIRE": \u000aBreast parenchyma with calcifications in association with \u000abenign epithelium, core biopsy site, and columnar cell changes. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Hx ALH on core bx. \u000aOperation: Exc. left breast mass. \u000aOperative Findings: None specified. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Left breast mass with wire. \u000aRADIOLOGY; Clip, calcifications and intact wire present in specimen image. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "Left breast mass with wire", and consists of an irregular tan/yellow \u000alobulated portion of fibroadipose breast tissue (3.8cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm anterior to posterior, and 2.2cm superior to inferior) with a short suture \u000adesignating the superior margin, and a long suture designating the lateral \u000amargin. Please note that the sutures are not designated on the form 86, \u000ahowever, the surgeon has designated the sutures in the operation report. There \u000ais a needle-localization wire in place which enters through the medial superior \u000aaspect of the specimen and exits through the lateral inferior aspect of the \u000aspecimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol (superior red, inferior \u000agreen, medial orange, lateral yellow, anterior blue, and posterior black) and \u000ais serially sectioned from medial to lateral. There is an irregular tan/white \u000agranular defect consistent with previous biopsy cavity (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ) \u000awithin which there is a silver metallic clip, and is located 0.4cm from the \u000ainferior margin, 0.9cm from the superior margin, 0.5cm from the anterior \u000amargin, 1.3cm from the posterior margin, 1.2cm from the lateral margin, and \u000a2.8cm from the medial margin. There is a focal area of dense white fibrous \u000atissue surrounding the previous biopsy cavity which constitutes approximately \u000a40% of the breast parenchyma. No discrete lesions are grossly identified. The \u000aspecimen is submitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections, medial and lateral, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to \u000ainclude biopsy cavity with metallic clip, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aSEK/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM: \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aAddendum #1 by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
