ngth. Sectioning demonstrates an \u000aill-defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.2cm area of fibrosis and fat necrosis, abutting the \u000asuperior, inferior, medial, and lateral margins, and within 0.5cm of the \u000aclosest posterior margin, and 1.0cm of the closest anterior margin. There is \u000ano obvious residual tumor identified grossly. The remaining specimen is \u000acomprised of unremarkable-appearing fibrous tissue (40% of the specimen), \u000aadmixed with lobulated tan/yellow adipose tissue. The entire specimen is \u000asubmitted, sequentially from anterior to posterior, with perpendicular anterior \u000amargin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and perpendicular posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential sections from anterior to posterior, multiple frags, \u000aESS. \u000aDB/mmm \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on \u000a5/22/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
