men is received previously inked by the surgeon in \u000aaccordance with the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. Ink is reapplied to the surfaces. An accompanying specimen \u000aradiograph demonstrates the shaft of the wire and a clip localized to an \u000airregularly-shaped, radio-dense mass. Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  \u000arelatively well-delineated, firm, white mass with a central biopsy site and \u000aclip located within 0.1cm of the posterior margin, 1.2cm from the superior \u000amargin, 1.1cm from the inferior margin, 0.3cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the lateral margin, and 0.9cm from the medial margin. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial and lateral margin, perpendicular, 2 frags each, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 6, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 7, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 8, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 9, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 10, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aVKV/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
