 sublabeled "1 1" through "1 3", \u000a"1 3 (2)" through "1 3 (6)", "1 4", "1 5", "1 5 (2)" and "1 6", corresponding \u000ato right breast needle localization biopsy (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm ) performed on \u000a7/37/97, according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's \u000aname. \u000aNine (9) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled "1 1" through "1 9", \u000acorresponding to right breast needle localization biopsy (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ) \u000aperformed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing \u000athe patient's name. \u000aFifteen (15) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled "1 1" "LEV #3 1 1", \u000a"1 2", "LEV #2 1 1", "LEV #2 1 2", "LEV #3 1 2", "2 1", "LEV #2 2 1", "LEV #3 2 \u000a1", "2 2", "LEV #2 2 2", "LEV #3 2 2", "2 3", "LEV #2 2 3" and "LEV #3 2 3", \u000acorresponding to 1) left breast core needle biopsies with calcifications 2) \u000aleft breast core needle biopsies without calcifications performed on REMOVED_DATE  \u000aaccording to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name. \u000aReports to: SHULMAN, LAWRENCE, NATHAN M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST \u000a[report_end] 
