VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR A CLIP MARKING AN AREA OF \u000aCALCIFICATIONS: \u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions \u000a(CAPSS) with atypia is present (see note). \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia is present. \u000aA biopsy site is present. \u000aNote: The areas of CAPSS show enlarged hyperchromatic nuclei and poor \u000aorientation towards the basement membrane. No malignancy is seen after \u000acomplete microscopic examination of the specimen, including margins. \u000aSENTINEL LYMPH NODE #1: \u000aOne lymph node with no tumor seen (3 H&E levels examined). \u000aSENTINEL LYMPH NODE #2: \u000aOne lymph node with no tumor seen (3 H&E levels examined). \u000aRIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION: \u000aRESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified \u000aBloom-Richardson grade II/III), 0.7cm in size, is present adjacent to the \u000aprior biopsy site. Calcifications are associated with the invasive \u000acarcinoma. \u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen. \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and cribriform types (low nuclear grade) \u000ais present associated with the invasive carcinoma and focally adjacent to \u000athe invasive carcinoma in 4 of 13 slides (EIC negative). No necrosis is \u000aseen. Focal calcifications are present. \u000aThe invasive carcinoma is not present at the margin. DCIS is < 0.1cm \u000afrom the inferior and lateral margins as small foci (each < 0.1cm ). \u000aNote: The patient had a prior excision revealing a 2.5cm carcinoma (BWH \u000aconsultation  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). Immunoperoxidase and FISH studies were performed \u000aon this specimen. \u000aThe DCIS is low grade and has a resemblance to lobular carcinoma in situ \u000ain the foci adjacent to the invasive carcinoma. However, these areas are \u000avery similar to the clearcut DCIS present and are best classified as DCIS. \u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  p REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  MX. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Left breast atypia, right breast cancer. \u000aOperation: Left needle directed breast biopsy, right lumpectomy, right \u000asentinel lymph node biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast needle directed lumpectomy, long/lateral, \u000ashort/superior. \u000a2. Sentinel lymph node #1. \u000a3. Sentinel lymph node #2. \u000a4. Right lumpectomy (re-excision right breast ca), \u000along/lateral, short/superior. \u000aRadiology: Clip is in specimen. Dr. Jessica Leung \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,BRIAN S.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fixed, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1, left breast needle directed lumpectomy", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.6cm specimen with two orienting sutures in the lateral and superior aspects \u000aand a localization wire within the specimen. The specimen is inked per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = \u000ablue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely from medial to lateral. \u000aThe specimen radiograph reveals a clip and the localization wire. The area of \u000athe clip is submitted in block 3. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lumpectomy, 10 frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2, sentinel lymph node #1", consists of a single fragment \u000aof yellow-tan soft tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  One lymph node is \u000aidentified with a maximum dimension of 1.3cm  \u000aMicro 9: 1 lymph node, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aPart three, labeled "#3, sentinel lymph node #2", consists of a single fragment \u000aof yellow fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  One lymph node is \u000aidentified with a maximum dimension of 1.8cm  \u000aMicro 10: 1 lymph node bisected, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart four, labeled "#4, right lumpectomy, re-excision of right breast cancer", \u000aconsists of a fragment of yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring 6 x 5 x 2cm \u000awith an attached skin ellipse measuring 3.0cm in length x 0.6cm in width with \u000aa well-healed surgical scar measuring 1.5cm in length. Two orienting sutures \u000aindicate superior and lateral orientations. The specimen is inked per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior \u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. \u000aSerial sectioning reveals a biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm  which \u000ais surrounded by scar tissue and is 0.5cm from the nearest lateral, 0.6cm \u000afrom nearest deep, 0.5cm from nearest anterior, 1.4cm from nearest superior, \u000a1.5cm from nearest inferior, and 2.1cm from nearest medial margin. \u000aAll fibrous tissue (approximately 80% of the specimen) is submitted for \u000ahistologic examination. \u000aMicro 11: biopsy cavity nearest lateral margin, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 12: biospy cavity nearest superior and anterior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 13: biopsy cavity nearest posterior margin, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 14: biospy cavity nearest inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 15: biopsy cavity nearest medial margin, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional biopsy cavity, 2 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of fibrous tissue, mult frags, ESS. \u000absc \u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
