VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCORSON, JOSEPH, M., M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CORSON,JOSEPH M.,M.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST BIOPSY, WIRE LOCALIZED: \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, single 2mm focus (block #12). \u000aFibrocystic change with microcysts, apocrine metaplasia and birefringent \u000acrystalloid material present in ductal lumina, see note. \u000aAdenosis with clear cell change. \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. \u000aMedial sclerosis and calcification of a vessel. \u000aNOTE: This crystalloid material apparently correlates with the radio-opaque \u000amaterial seen in the specimen mammogram as well as that seen in our X-ray of \u000athe paraffin blocks. No conventional microcalcifications are seen. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aOperation: Needle directed left breast biopsy. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue and wire. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE AND WIRE": \u000aFibrocystic changes. \u000aNo areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma. \u000aFinal diagnosis deferred to permanent sections. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcification in specimen. D. Smith, MD \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KUTOK,JEFFREY LORNE,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in the frozen section room, labeled with the \u000apatient's name, unit number and "left breast tissue and wire", and consists of \u000aone portion of yellow/red fibroadipose tissue (7.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ) with needle \u000alocalization wire in place. The specimen is received unoriented. The specimen \u000ais inked and sectioned revealing multiple blue domed cysts measuring up to REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in greatest diameter, and firm tan/pink breast parenchyma with admixed \u000ayellow fatty tissue. No areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma. \u000aThe tissue blocks are X-rayed to localize microcalcifications. \u000aMICRO #1-12: Serial cross sections of specimen perpendicular to margins, mult \u000afrags, ESS, 12 cass. \u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
