ed in black and a representative \u000asection is submitted. \u000aMicro 1: left nipple and areolar, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aPart two, labeled "Right nipple and areolar", consists of a single fragment \u000aof pink/tan skin, consists of a nipple and areolar. The skin measures REMOVED_DATE x \u000a2.0 x 0.2cm and the nipple measures REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm  The base of the skin is \u000ainked in black and the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted. \u000aMicro 2: right nipple and areolar, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aPart three, labeled "Right breast tissue", consists of multiple fragments of \u000awhite/yellow fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm in aggregate. \u000aThe specimen is fragmented and no margin is evident. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue, multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart four, labeled "Left breast tissue", consists of multiple fragments of \u000apink/yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm in aggregate. \u000aThe specimen is fragmented and the no margin is evident. The specimen is \u000aentirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue, multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart five, labeled "Left breast implant", consists of a clear breast implant \u000a(12.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 6.0cm ) with no tears or leaks. The external surface is smooth \u000aand there is no tissue attached. Gross exam only. \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST IMPLANT \u000a[report_end] 
