VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Kevin Golden, M.D., Ph.D.; Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, associated with columnar cell change with flat \u000aatypia with calcifications, is present (best seen in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; levels \u000aexamined). \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aNote: The entire specimen was examined microscopically, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 50 year old woman with new calcifications on screening mammogram. \u000aOperation: R needle localization breast biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: R abnormal mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) R breast tissue - mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aCalcifications in specimen - wire intact. Discussed with Dr. Lockhart. JAR \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "needle localized bx", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.8cm excision of \u000afibroadipose tissue, oriented by ink per surgeon. The specimen is inked per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A \u000alocalizing wire enters the anterolateral aspect of the specimen and exits \u000amedially. The specimen is received with a radiograph demonstrating the \u000alocalizing wire in place within the specimen and the area of calcifications at \u000athe medial edge. Sectioning demonstrates cystic tan/white fibrodense tissue \u000a(at least 80% of the specimen), admixed with unremarkable-appearing soft, \u000alobulated tan/yellow adipose tissue (less than 20%). There are no obvious \u000amasses, lesions, or other abnormalities grossly. The entire specimen is \u000asubmitted, sequentially from medial to lateral, with perpendicular medial \u000amargin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , perpendicular lateral margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen, sequentially, multi frags, ESS. \u000adb/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a7/17/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
