VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Stefan Kraft, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER INNER, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA, with pagetoid spread (best seen in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aCalcifications are associated with lobules. \u000aNote: No malignancy is seen after complete microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 47 year old premenopausal female with LUI breast calcifications on \u000amammo REMOVED_DATE - not amenable to core biopsy. \u000aOperation: L breast WLBX. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Left breast tissue short equals superior, long equals lateral, whip \u000astitch on deep margin (to mammo). \u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications and intact hookwire are in the center of the \u000aspecimen. Eva Gombos, MD. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1. Left breast tissue long - lateral, short - superior, whipstitch on \u000adeep margin", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.4cm excision of fibroadipose \u000atissue, received oriented with sutures designating superior (short suture), \u000alateral (long suture), and deep (whipstitch) margins, in addition to inking by \u000athe surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. A localizing wire enters the specimen superior/anterior \u000asurface, and exits medial/inferiorly. Specimen is received along with a \u000aradiograph demonstrating the localizing wire in place centrally within the \u000aspecimen, adjacent to a small focus of calcifications. Sectioning demonstrates \u000adense tan/white fibrous tissue (60-70% of the specimen), admixed with \u000aunremarkable tan/yellow soft, lobulated adipose tissue. There are no obvious \u000amasses, lesions or other abnormalities grossly. The entire specimen is \u000asequentially submitted from lateral to medial, with perpendicular lateral \u000amargin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , perpendicular medial margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and area of interest (per \u000alocalizing wire) in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen, sequentially from lateral to medial, \u000amulti frags, ESS. \u000aDB/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a10/30/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
