ere are focal areas of hemorrhage. The specimen is radiographed, and \u000athe slice containing the clip is identified and submitted in cassettes #8 and \u000a9. No discrete lesions or masses are identified. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral perpendicular margin, mult frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast wire localized biopsy, from lateral to medial, 1 frag \u000aeach, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial perpendicular margin, 2 or 3 frags each, ESS \u000alcl \u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
