well circumscribed dense pearly white mass REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in greatest dimension grossly consistent with a fibroadenoma. The remainder \u000aof the breast tissue is largely fatty with no areas grossly suspicious for \u000ainvasive tumor. A portion of the dense lesion is frozen as FSB. Fatty areas \u000aare trimmed from the specimen and the remainder is entirely submitted. \u000aMICRO #8: FSR B, 1 frag, ESS, 1 cass. \u000aMICRO #9-15: 6 frags, RSS, 6 cas. \u000aMICRO #16: FSRA, retrieved from reproductive endocrinology lab, ESS, 1 frag, 1 \u000acass. \u000aNote: The frozen section remnant A was submitted to the reproductive \u000aendocrinology lab for potential ERICA studies. This block was retrieved and \u000aprocessed for histologic examination. No ERICA was perfomed. \u000aReports to: SMITH, BARBARA, LYNN M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
