VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s) \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Andrew G. Evans, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, DOUBLE WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A BIOPSY SITE, A CLIP AND \u000aMICROCALCIFICATIONS AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSIES (THREE SPECIMENS, INCLUDING \u000aFROZEN SECTIONS): \u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson \u000agrade II/III) (tubule score=2, nuclear score=3, mitoses score=1, total=6), is \u000apresent as two foci, each 0.2cm in size (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; deeper levels; block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aTwo additional foci of MICROINVASION are present, < 0.1cm in size (slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aand  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is present. \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and cribriform types (high nuclear grades), \u000awith necrosis and microcalcifications, is associated with and away from the \u000ainvasive carcinoma (13 of 41 blocks; EIC positive). \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aA core needle biopsy site is present. \u000aThe superior, inferior, medial, lateral, anterior, and posterior margins are \u000anegative for invasive carcinoma, including the foci of microinvasion. \u000aDCIS is multifocally present < 0.1cm from the inferior, medial, and lateral \u000amargins. The superior, anterior, and posterior margins are negative for DCIS \u000a(> 0.3cm ). \u000aTwo sentinel lymph nodes are negative for carcinoma (3 H&E levels for each \u000alymph node are examined). \u000aNote: The patient underwent a prior core needle biopsy for \u000acalcifications which revealed DCIS with microinvasion that was positive for \u000aER and PR and negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu. Immunoperoxidase studies will be \u000aperformed on the larger area of invasion in this excision and reported in \u000aan addendum. \u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th edition):  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID a  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (sn) \u000awith additional foci of invasion. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 58 year old female postmenopausal with family history of 2 paternal \u000aaunts with breast cancer, personal risk factors of nulliparity and history of \u000aADH. REMOVED_DATE screening mammogram demonstrates L calcifications. REMOVED_DATE \u000astereotactic core biopsy revealed comedo DCIS with microinvasion. \u000aOperation: L breast wire-localized lumpectomy with 2 bracketing wires, L \u000asentinel lymph node mapping, biopsy and possible axillary dissection. \u000aPREVIOUS SURGERY: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aOperative Findings: None provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast DCIS wide excision. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Left sentinel node hot and blue (F.S.) \u000aB/2) Left sentinel node hot not blue (F.S.). \u000aC/3) Left breast tissue; short stitch - superior; long - lateral, whip stitch \u000achest wall margin (mammo). \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. LEFT SENTINEL NODE HOT AND BLUE" (FSA): \u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. LEFT SENTINEL NODE HOT NOT BLUE" (FSB): \u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor. \u000aOR Consultation by: Alessandra F. Nascimento, M.D. \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname, medical record number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Left sentinel node, hot and blue". The specimen consists of one \u000ayellow fibroadipose tissue (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm ) containing a single lymph node \u000a(1.7cm in greatest dimension), which was bisected and entirely submitted for \u000afrozen section examination as FSA. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : FSA, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Non-frozen tissue, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Left sentinel node, hot not blue". The specimen consists of one \u000ayellow fibroadipose tissue fragment (2.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ) containing one lymph \u000anode (0.9cm in greatest dimension), which was bisected and entirely submitted \u000afor frozen section examination as FSB. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : FSB, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Non-frozen tissue, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart C, "#3. Left breast tissue, short stitch superior, long lateral, \u000awhip-stitch chest wall margin". The specimen consists of a single portion of \u000aadipose tissue (5.8cm superior to inferior, 6.5cm medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm anterior to posterior), which is oriented by a short stitch on the superior \u000aaspect of the specimen, a long stitch on the lateral aspect of the specimen, \u000aand a whip-stitch on the posterior aspect of the specimen, which is designated \u000aby the surgeon as chest wall margin. Two wire needles are protruding from the \u000aspecimen, one from the lateral superior aspect of the specimen and the other \u000afrom the medial inferior aspect of the specimen. The tissue is accompanied by \u000aa radiograph, which demonstrates a clip in an area of irregular density \u000aconsistent with biopsy cavity, calcifications, and two hookwires present on \u000aopposite side aspects of the specimen. The accompanying report reads "calcs \u000aclip and two wires. Called to OR by Lisa Zorn on REMOVED_DATE at 3:50 P.M. to \u000aDr. Rhei". The wire at the inferior medial aspect of the specimen inserts \u000awithin an area of focal hemorrhage and diffuse irregular nodularity (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 1.0cm ). Within this area at least three firm white calcified nodules (0.2 \u000acm in greatest dimension) are identified. This area is within 0.3cm to the \u000amedial margin and 0.5cm to the inferior margin, and greater than 1.0cm to \u000aeach remaining margin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The wire entering from the \u000asuperior lateral aspect of the breast, terminates at the anterior inferior \u000aportion (designated wire #2) traversing in area of breast tissue extensively \u000amarked with blue ink. A focal nodularity (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ) is found within \u000athe center the specimen, 2.5cm from the posterior margin, the nearest \u000aresection margin. The second focal nodularity (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ) is found \u000awithin the anterior aspect of the specimen, 0.7cm from the medial resection \u000amargin. At the inferior surface of the specimen, focal firm nodules and white \u000afirm tissue covering an area of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm is identified. \u000aApproximately 60% of the specimen is submitted for microscopic analysis, and \u000athe remaining tissue is all unremarkable fibroadipose tissue. The cut sections \u000aand the non-submitted tissues are both radiographed for subsequent \u000aidentification of the clip. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior/medial areas of calcifications and nodularity, 1 frag \u000aeach, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Adjacent areas examining the medial posterior and inferior margin, \u000aincluding clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Area of nodularity adjacent to posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Areas of nodularity adjacent to the medial margin, 1 frag each, \u000