VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia in region showing prior biopsy site changes. \u000aCalcifications are associated with ADH and benign epithelium. \u000aApocrine metaplasia and cysts. \u000aFour (4) lymph nodes negative for tumor. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Multiple areas of ADH, left breast, several operations. \u000aOperation: Total mastectomy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast ca. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast (see any low nodes ?), short suture = \u000asuperior, long suture = lateral. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PADERA,ROBERT F.,JR.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1, left breast, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral", and consists \u000aof a 325 gram, 15 x 12 x 2.0cm left simple mastectomy containing an eccentric \u000atan-white REMOVED_DATE x 4.5cm wrinkled skin ellipse, with a 2.5cm tan-white areola \u000aand an inverted REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm tan-pink nipple. The skin contains three (3) \u000acurvilinear well-healed scars (3.0cm - lower - inner, 2.2cm - lower - outer, \u000a1.5cm - lower - central) and a short stitch denoting superior and a long \u000astitch denoting lateral. The deep margin is inked black and the specimen is \u000asectioned to reveal a 6.5cm focally lumpy to rubbery fibrosed area subjacent \u000ato the aforementioned skin scars. The remaining parenchyma contains \u000aapproximately 40% tan-white dense, focally lumpy, focally cystic fibrous \u000atissues admixed with approximately 60% tan-yellow lobulated, focally \u000ahemorrhagic fat. The cyst range in size from up to 0.4cm and contains a \u000aserosanguineous to pus-like fluid. No invasive lesions are grossly \u000aidentified. Four (4) possible lymph nodes are identified ranging from 0.2cm \u000aup to 1.1cm in greatest dimension. Representative sections are submitted as \u000afollows. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of fibrosed tissue subjacent to skin scar \u000afrom medial to lateral, 10 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of upper outer quadrant, 2 frags each, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of lower outer, 2 frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of inner upper quadrant, 2 frags each, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of lower inner quadrant, 2 frags each, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of each skin scar, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro 17: representative radial section of nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 18: 4 possible lymph node candidates, 4 frags, ESS. \u000akks \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION \u000a[report_end] 
