ior to posterior \u000ainto twelve sections. The clip was recovered in the sixth section. The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histologic review. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 1 and 2, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 3 and 4, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 5, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 6 (clip), 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 7, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 8, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 9, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 10, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 11, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 12, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMDH/mmm \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a8/25/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
