ly 60% adipose and 40% fibrous tissue. The specimen is \u000aentirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : medial margin, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : central portion of specimen with prior biopsy site in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000athrough  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , multiple frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : lateral margin, multiple frags, ESS. \u000aBGL/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Briana Gleason M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aResident Review by Briana Gleason M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a7/14/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
