itch laterally and a whipstitch on the deep margin. The specimen is \u000ainked by the surgeon per pathology protocol (superior equals red, inferior \u000aequals green, anterior equals blue, posterior equals black, medial equals \u000aorange, yellow equals lateral), and measures 3.6cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm medial to lateral and 1.7cm anterior to posterior. A needle-localization \u000awire enters the lateral aspect of the specimen but does not exit. A radiograph \u000aon centricity shows a wire which localizes both a clip and a mass. The \u000aspecimen is fixed overnight and serially sectioned to reveal 90% fatty tissue \u000aand 10% fibrous tissue. A well-circumscribed, tan mass (0.6cm in greatest \u000adimension) is present in the lateral aspect of the specimen, just distal to the \u000alocalization wire tip. The specimen has been entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Complete coronal section, including mass and tip, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Complete coronal section, anterior to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (mass in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), 1 \u000afrag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior aspect of the specimen, perpendicular, multi \u000afrags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Complete coronal section, posterior to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), 1 \u000afrag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior aspect of the specimen, perpendicular, multi \u000afrags total, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aAQU/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R 