 REMOVED_DATE x 0.4) which is; 0.3cm to superior, 1.8cm to inferior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm to anterior, 0.4cm to posterior, 0.8cm from the medial and 0.9cm from the \u000alateral resection margin. A clip is identified at the anterior margin, 0.2cm \u000afrom the nodule. The specimen is entirely submitted for histology. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, perpendicular, 3 frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, perpendicular, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of specimen (clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aAL/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a8/28/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
