VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST MASS - ANTERIOR": \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (LCIS) with focal pagetoid spread, involving \u000afour (4) of four (4) blocks. \u000aScattered calcifications are present, but are not specifically associated \u000awith the LCIS. \u000aCysts. \u000aSee NOTE. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST MASS - POSTERIOR": \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (LCIS) with focal pagetoid spread, involving \u000athree (3) of four (4) blocks. \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. \u000aAdenosis. \u000aScattered calcifications are present, but are not specifically associated \u000awith the LCIS. \u000aCysts. \u000aSee NOTE. \u000aNOTE: This case was reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who \u000aconcurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 2 areas of microcalcifications - left breast removed. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast mass - anterior \u000a2. Left breast mass - posterior \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KINDELBERGER,DAVID W.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in 2 parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart 1, sublabeled "left breast mass - anterior", consists of a single, \u000aunoriented fragment of yellow/pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). A single metal localizing wire is embedded within the specimen. An \u000aaccompanying radiograph demonstrates the presence of microcalcifications and a \u000alocalizing wire within the specimen. The external surface of the specimen is \u000ainked black. Sectioning reveals a single cyst (0.3cm in maximum dimension) \u000athat abutts the inked margin. No other gross lesions are identified. The \u000aspecimen is composed of approximately 60% adipose tissue and 40% fibrous \u000atissue. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic evaluation. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - left breast mass (anterior), 6 frags, ESS. \u000aPart 2, sublabeled "left breast mass - posterior", consists of a single, \u000aunoriented fragment of yellow/pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). A metal localizing wire is embedded within the specimen. An accompanying \u000aradiograph demonstrates the presence of microcalcifications and a localizing \u000awire within the specimen. The external surface of the specimen is inked blue. \u000aSerial sectioning reveals no areas of hemorrhage, necrosis, or other grossly \u000aapparent lesions. The specimen is composed of 50% fibriod and 50% adipose \u000atissue. The entire specimen is submitted for histologic evaluation. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - left breast mass (posterior), 9 frags, ESS. \u000aReports to: REILLY, RAYMOND, JOHN, M.B.B.C.H. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
