,ADY,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts labeled with the patient's name and \u000aunit number. \u000aThe first specimen labeled "1 left directed breast biopsy-upper wire", is a REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm white/yellow, fibrous fatty tissue with a wire in place. There \u000ais a 0.5cm area of firmness consistent with calcifications seen on mammogram. \u000aSection code: \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left needle directed breast biopsy-upper wire, ESS, multiple \u000afragments, 3 cassettes. \u000aThe second specimen labeled "2 left needle directed breast biopsy-lower wire", \u000ais a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm white/yellow fibrous fatty tissue with a wire in place. \u000aA 0.4cm area of punctate firmness consists of a calcifications as seen on the \u000amammogram. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left needle directed breast biopsy-lower wire, ESS, multiple \u000afragments, 4 cassettes. \u000aNote: No micro #6 submitted. \u000aReports to: KANE, J.GREGORY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
