d fragment \u000aof yellow/tan soft tissue (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ) with one needle localization \u000awire in place. The specimen is inked black. Sections showing remarkable \u000afibroadipose tissue with no areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma. \u000aMicro sections: \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, "anterior lower left breast", consists of one unoriented fragment of \u000ayellow/tan soft tissue (3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ) with one needle localization wire in \u000aplace. The specimen is inked black and section showed a linear area of \u000aindurated hemorrhagic tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ), possibly representing a \u000abiopsy needle biopsy tract. There are no areas grossly suspicious for invasive \u000acarcinoma. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  multiple frags, ESS. \u000aReports to: KANE, J.GREGORY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
