le and ill-defined mass. \u000a2. Right: 11mm  palpable and ill-defined mass. \u000aLOCATION: \u000a1. Right: 12:30 \u000a2. Right: upper inner 1:00 \u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY: \u000a1. 14G Ultrasound \u000a2. 14G Ultrasound \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. - Blue cassette \u000aB/2. - Pink cassette \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the \u000apatient's name and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled " REMOVED_CASE_ID  position right breast", consists of multiple yellow-white \u000afibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm ), which are received in a \u000ablue cassette. The specimens are submitted in toto. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "Right breast site #2 pink cassette", consists of multiple \u000ayellow-white fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm ), which are \u000areceived in a pink cassette. The specimens are submitted in toto. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Multi frags, ESS. \u000aCP/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a8/7/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for the DCIS, Block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : \u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) POSITIVE (3+) \u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen \u000aand progesterone receptors. \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for the DCIS, Block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : \u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) Positive (3+) \u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen \u000aand progesterone receptors. \u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the \u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet \u000abeen determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a \u000aportion of the membrane is positive. \u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of \u000atumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of \u000atumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational \u000ause only. \u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a8/11/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
