VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Lymph node biopsy (non-heme) \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Shuji Ogino, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY, AND AXILLARY NODE \u000aDISSECTION (3 SPECIMENS) (INCLUDING  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aINVASIVE MUCINOUS CARCINOMA AND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODE(S). \u000aSYNOPSIS: \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aSize - 1.2cm \u000aMultifocal - No \u000aHistologic Type - Mucinous (colloid), Ductal. Tumor is \u000acomposed of 100% mucinous component. \u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - I (well) \u000aNuclear Grade - Low to focally intermediate \u000aEIC - Negative \u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent \u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - Absent \u000aSkin invasion - Absent \u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A \u000aFinal Margins (invasive) - Negative (> 0.3cm ) deep \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present \u000aSENTINEL LYMPH NODES - Negative \u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0 \u000aNumber of nodes examined - 2 \u000aAXILLARY LYMPH NODES: - Negative \u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0 \u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3 (one lymph node in breast specimen (C) \u000aand two nodes in axillary specimen (A). \u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS: \u000aApocrine metaplasia, columnar hyperplasia, core biopsy site, skin with \u000ascar, calcifications in benign epithelium. \u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID c p REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  MX \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 70 year old female REMOVED_DATE - left breast excision biopsy - wire \u000aloc/"LCIS" and ALH with pagetoid spread around ducts/calcs associated with \u000abenign epithelium; REMOVED_DATE - left breast ultrasound-guided core biopsy - \u000a"invasive mucinous cancer", well-diff - BR I/III - no lymphovascular invasion, \u000ano carcinoma in-situ. ER/PR+ - Her2Neu-. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) left axillary tissue. \u000aB/2) left sentinel lymph nodes (fs). \u000aC/3) left breast. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2 - LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE(S)" ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes; no tumor present. \u000aOR Consultation by: WILLIAM ROBERT WELCH, M.D. \u000aResident: JUSTINE BARLETTA, M.D. \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patients \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "#1 - left axillary tissue", consists of two irregular \u000afragments of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (4.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm in aggregate), \u000acontaining two pink/tan firm lymph node candidates (1.8cm and 2.3cm in \u000agreatest dimension, respectively), which are entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : one lymph node candidate serially sectioned, multiple frags, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : one lymph node candidate serially sectioned, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B is received in the frozen section room, labeled "#2 - left sentinel \u000alymph nodes", and consists of two fragments of pink/yellow soft tissue (3.0cm \u000aand 3.2cm in greatest dimension, respectively), which exhibit two pink/tan \u000alymph node candidates (2.2cm and 2.3cm in greatest dimension, respectively). \u000aThe larger lymph node was previously bisected and entirely frozen as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with \u000athe second lymph node candidate also previously bisected and frozen as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart C, labeled "#3 - left breast", consists of a 440 gram left simple \u000amastectomy specimen (16.5 m-l x REMOVED_DATE s-i x REMOVED_DATE a-pcm ) with an attached \u000atan/white, wrinkled skin ellipse (13.5 x 4.3cm ) with a central tan/pink \u000aeverted nipple (1.0cm in diameter) and tan areola (3.0 x 2.8cm ). Per \u000asurgeon, the specimen exhibits two sutures (short suture superior, long suture \u000alateral). Located 1.4cm inferolateral to the nipple is a well-healed linear \u000ascar (4.2cm in length). The superomedial aspect of the areola exhibits a \u000awell-healed retracted curvilinear scar (3.2cm in length). The deep margin \u000a(inked black) is predominantly a smooth fascial plane with a central, focally \u000adisrupted blue/green dyed (? sentinel node mapping procedure) area (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. At \u000aapproximately 12 o'clock (at the junction of the upper/inner and upper/outer \u000aquadrant), there is an indurated tan/pink, lobulated, poorly delineated mass \u000a(1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ), which comes to within 1.3cm of the black-inked deep \u000amargin. Within the central portion of the mass is a yellow/tan \u000amucinous/gelatinous focus (0.8cm in greatest dimension). Located 4.9cm \u000ainferolateral to the aforementioned mass is a poorly delineated firm tan/white \u000avaguely nodular fibrous lesion (? biopsy cavity from prior excision procedure, \u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ), which comes to within 0.3cm of the black-inked deep \u000amargin. \u000aThe remainder of the specimen is composed of approximately 30% dense, nodular, \u000alumpy, tan/white fibrous stroma and approximately 70% yellow/tan lobulated \u000aadipose tissue with multiple foci of blue/green discoloration as consistent \u000awith prior node mapping procedure. \u000aWithin the most-lateral breast tissue, one pink/tan rubbery intramammary lymph \u000anode candidate (0.9cm in greatest dimension) is identified. An axillary tail \u000ais not present. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : nipple and areola with curvilinear scar, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : deep margin closest to mass, 12 o'clock, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : mass 12 o'clock sequentially submitted from lateral to \u000amedial (sections to exhibit greatest dimension of mass), 3 \u000afrags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : ill-defined vaguely nodular lesion, inferolateral to mass to \u000ainclude deep margin, 1 frag in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : grossly unremarkable intervening tissue between 12 o'clock \u000amass and inferolateral lesion, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : dense/lumpy fibrous stroma, upper/outer quadrant, 4 frags, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : dense/lumpy fibrous stroma, upper/inner quadrant, 4 frags, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : dense/lumpy fibrous stroma, lower/outer quadrant, 4 frags, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : dense/lumpy fibrous stroma, lower/inner quadrant, 4 frags, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : one bisected lymph node candidate, 2 frags, ESS. \u000almb/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Ann K Folkins M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Shuji Ogino M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a2/6/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
