VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D. \u000a1. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS: \u000aBenign breast tissue with focal chronic inflammation. \u000aFibrocystic change with apocrine metaplasia. \u000aLymph node(s) with no significant pathologic change. \u000a2. RIGHT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: \u000aBenign breast tissue with acute and chronic inflammation, \u000afibrosis, and fat necrosis. \u000a3. RIGHT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOSY: \u000aBenign breast tissue with suppurative granulomatous inflammation, \u000aand acute and chronic inflammation. \u000aResults of special stains will be reported as an addendum. \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM OF REMOVED_DATE  \u000aGram, fungal (MSS), and acid-fast stains are negative for organisms. \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM OF REMOVED_DATE  \u000aA Steiner stain is negative for cat scratch bacilli. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 36 year old female with long history of mastitis US REMOVED_DATE multiple \u000ahypoechoic mass in right breast. Core biopsy REMOVED_DATE of mass at 4 o'clock \u000aright breast - acute and chronic abscess. \u000aOperation: #1) Right breast wire localized breast biopsy \u000a#2) I&D of 2 sites of right breast, ? with 1/4" NL gauge \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right breast mass (upper outer quadrant) - short \u000asuture/superior; long suture/lateral; whipstitch suture is at deep margin \u000a#2) Inferior 6 o'clock breast tissue (mass) \u000a#3) Medial 4 o'clock breast tissue right \u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen......Dr. Frost \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BRENN,THOMAS,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "right breast mass upper outer quadrant", consists of two \u000afragments of firm tan/pink fibroadipose tissue. The small fragment measures \u000a1.7 x 1 x 0.5cm  The second fragment is oriented by the surgeon with a short \u000astitch designated superior, a long stitch designated lateral and a whipstitch \u000adesignated deep margin. There is a localization wire in place and an \u000aaccompanying radiograph for orientation of the mass. The larger \u000afragment measures 3cm from lateral to medial, 5cm from superior to inferior \u000aand 0.9cm from anterior to posterior. The specimen is inked per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; \u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The \u000aspecimen consists of 80% of dense white/pink fibrous tissue and 20% adipose \u000atissue. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  largest fragment breast biopsy submitted from inferior to \u000asuperior, mult frags, ESSs \u000aMicro 11: smaller fragment of breast biopsy, 2 frags, ESS \u000aPart two, labeled "inferior 6 o'clock breast tissue mass", consists of one \u000aunoriented fragment of tan/pink fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. The specimen is inked black, serially sectioned and entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, mult frags, ESS \u000aPart three, labeled "medial 4 o'clock breast tissue right", consists of two \u000afragments of tan/pink fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1cm in \u000aaggregate. The fragments are inked black, and entirely submitted. \u000aMicro 15: breast tissue, 3 frags, ESS \u000atb \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY \u000a[report_end] 
