VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY": \u000aBreast parenchyma with atypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid \u000aspread, intraductal papillomas, apocrine metaplasia, and cysts. \u000aGiant cell reaction consistent with prior surgical procedure. \u000aFocal fibroadenomatous change. \u000aThe entire specimen was submitted for histological analysis. \u000aSelected slides from the case were reviewed with Dr. Susan Lester, \u000aBreast Pathology, who concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 40 year-old premenopausal female with a history of granulomatous \u000amastitis. Now with right breast nodularity without mammogram or ultrasound \u000acorelate for which she prefers excision. \u000aOperation: Right breast excisional biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast excisional biopsy. \u000aShort suture superior. \u000aLong suture lateral. \u000aWhip stitch on deep margin. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SANTAGATA,SANDRO,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen was received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000amedical record number, "#1. Right breast excisional biopsy", and consists of \u000atwo fragments of fibroadipose tissue. The smaller which is unoriented measures \u000a2.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm and is inked black, serially sectioned and entirely \u000asubmitted. The second main breast excision specimen measures 5.4cm from \u000asuperior to inferior, 4.4cm from medial to lateral, 2.0cm from anterior to \u000aposterior, and is marked by the surgeon with a short suture indicating the \u000asuperior margin and long suture indicating the lateral margin. The specimen is \u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; \u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = \u000aorange. On section, the specimen is friable and is composed predominately of \u000aadipose tissue with a firm fibrous area abutting the deep margin (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.7cm ). The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic analysis. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Smaller fragment (inked black), 7 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 4: Larger fragment, fibrous area to lateral/inferior margin, 2 frags, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro 5: Fibrous area -posterior, inferior, lateral margins, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Additional fibrous area to margins, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Remainder of specimen, multiple frags, ESS. \u000assa \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
