y: Pt is s/p cre bx at Faulkner REMOVED_DATE  poorly differentiated \u000ainvasive ductal cancer, (+) LVI, ER (+), PR (+), Her 2 neu (-). \u000aOperation: Left partial mastectomy and left axillary lymph node dissection. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left axillary nodes. \u000a2. Left partial mastectomy - breast tissue @ REMOVED_DATE o'clock. \u000aShort superior, long lateral. Inked per pathology protocol. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KINDELBERGER,DAVID W.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and medical record number. \u000aPart one, "#1 left axillary node", consists of a single fragment of yellow/tan \u000afibroadipose tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.4cm ). There are approximately 22 lymph \u000anodes embedded within the specimen, ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm up \u000ato REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm  The lymph nodes are dissected free of surrounding \u000aadipose tissue and entirely submitted for histologic evaluation. \u000aMicro 1: largest lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 2: second lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 3: 6 lymph nodes, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 4: 6 lymph nodes, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 5: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 6: 3 lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, "#2 left partial mastectomy", consists of a single fragment of \u000afibroadipose tissue (7.0cm from superior to inferior x 6.4cm from medial to \u000alateral x 4.0cm from anterior to posterior). A short black suture was placed \u000aby the surgeon to indicate the superior margin and a long black suture was \u000aplaced by the surgeon to indicate the lateral margin. The specimen is inked by \u000athe surgeon in six colors per pathology protocol for the evaluation of \u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; \u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. There is a small fragment of skin with scar \u000aattached to the specimen (5.4cm from lateral to medial x 1.3cm superior to \u000ainferior). The skin has been covered with ink such that definitive \u000aidentification of a surgical scar is not possible. There is a large, \u000awhite/tan, firm, poorly circumscribed mass (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm ). The mass \u000aappears to come within 1cm of the medial margin, 1.3cm of the anterior (skin) \u000amargin, 2.0cm of the lateral margin, 1.8cm of the superior margin, 1.9cm of \u000athe inferior margin and appears to abut the posterior margin. Representative \u000asections are submitted for histologic evaluation. \u000aMicro 7: posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 8: anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 9: medial margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 10: lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 11: superior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 12: inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 13: nodule, 3 frags, RSS. \u000adk \u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000a[report_end] 
