le mastectomy specimen \u000ameasuring 17cm from lateral to medial by 17.5cm from superior to inferior by \u000a1.9cm from anterior to posterior. A short black suture is placed by the \u000asurgeon to indicate the superior aspect of the specimen, and a long black \u000asuture is placed by the surgeon to indicate the lateral aspect of the specimen. \u000aThere is a pink/tan skin ellipse measuring 15cm from lateral to medial by 5cm \u000afrom superior to inferior, containing an eccentrically placed nipple (1.4 x \u000a1.4cm ), surrounded by areolar tissue (2.4 x 2.5cm ). A biopsy cavity is \u000aidentifed (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ) which approaches to within 0.4cm of the deep \u000amargin. No additional lesions are grossly identified. The breast parenchyma \u000ais composed of approximately 70% adipose and 30% fibrous tissue. No lymph \u000anodes are identified. Representative sections are submitted for histologic \u000aevaluation. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Biopsy cavity and deep margin, 2 frag, ESS \u000aMicro 3: Upper outer quadrant sample, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 4: Lower outer quadrant sample, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 5: Upper inner quadrant sample, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 6: Lower inner quadrant sample, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 7: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS \u000aPart 2, "Right breast tissue" consists of 426 g right simple mastectomy \u000ameasuring 19cm from lateral to medial by 19cm from superior to inferior by \u000a2.2cm from anterior to posterior. A short black suture was placed by the \u000asurgeon to indicate the superior aspect of the specimen and a long black suture \u000awas placed by the surgeon to indicate the lateral aspect of the specimen. \u000aThere is a pink/tan skin ellipse measuring 14cm from lateral to medial by REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from superior to inferior. It contains a centrally placed nipple (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) surrounded by areolar tissue (2.3 x 2.3cm ). No lesions are grossly \u000aidentified. The breast parenchyma is composed of approximately 60% adipose and \u000a40% fibrous tissue. No lymph nodes are identified. No lesions are grossly \u000aidentified. Represenative sections are submitted for histologic evaluation. \u000aMicro 8: Upper outer quadrant sample, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 9: Lower outer quadrant sample, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 10: Upper inner quadrant sample, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 11: Lower inner quadrant sample, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro 12: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS \u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000a[report_end] 
