ast tissue cores are received in a white \u000acassette marked "B". The specimen is submitted in toto. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Cassette "A", multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Cassette "B", multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, "Right breast 1:15 site #2", consists of multiple tan/white to \u000atan/yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue cores (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm in \u000aaggregate). A portion of the breast tissue cores are received in a brown \u000acassette marked "A. Ca+2", an additional portion of breast tissue cores are \u000areceived in an additional brown cassette marked "A. Ca+2" and the remainder of \u000athe breast tissue cores are received in a brown cassette marked "B". The \u000aspecimen is submitted in toto. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Cassette "A. Ca+2", multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional cassette marked "A CA+2", multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of breast tissue cores cassette "B", multi frags, ESS. \u000aSEK/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a11/5/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
