VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s) \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Astrid Weins, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY ANS SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY (parts A and \u000aB including  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and FSB): \u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA AND INVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES, TWO \u000aFOCI, LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU AND MESTASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODE \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aSize - 2.5cm and > 5cm \u000aMultifocal - Yes (see note) \u000aHistologic type - Lobular and Mixed Ductal and Lobular \u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) (6 to 7 points) \u000aTubules - 10 to 75% (2 points) to < 10% (3 points) \u000aNuclear grade - Low (1 point) to Intermediate (2 points) \u000aMitotic counts - 1 point \u000aEIC - Negative \u000aLVI - Present \u000aDermal LVI - Absent \u000aSkin invasion - Absent. Invasive carcinoma extends into \u000anipple and is present in stroma around lactiferous ducts. \u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Present \u000aFinal Margins (invasive) \u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - Medial, deep, anterior \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU -Absent \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU -Present \u000aSentinel lymph nodes - Positive (3 H&E levels examined) \u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1 \u000aNumber of nodes examined - 1 \u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- REMOVED_DATE \u000aSize of largest metastatic focus - 0.12cm \u000aExtranodal extension - Absent \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aALH \u000aCore biopsy site (x2) \u000aSkeletal muscle \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) - Pending \u000aNOTE: Tumor is present as two distinct foci. There is an invasive lobular \u000acarcinoma present throughout the 2.5cm mass in the medial part of the specimen \u000ain the upper inner quadrant ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). This tumor extensively infiltrates skeletal \u000amuscle extending to margins. The other focus has mixed ductal and lobular \u000afeatures and involves two grossly identified 1.5cm nodules in the mid-upper \u000aouter quadrant as well as all tissue between the two nodules (2 \u000acm).Additionally, all the tissue submitted between the larger 2.5cm gross mass \u000a(invasive lobular carcinoma) and the two smaller gross masses (cumulatively 5 \u000acm) are also involved by invasive carcinoma with mixed features. The overall \u000aexact size of the carcinoma with mixed features is difficult to determine, but \u000aexceeds 5cm ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aThe micrometastasis [ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID mi(sn)] is seen on deeper levels in the sentinel node \u000a(block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , level 2) and is not present in the original frozen section slides. \u000aMorphologically, it is favored that the metastasis is from the tumor with mixed \u000aductal and lobular features. \u000aDr. D. Dillon, Breast Pathology, has reviewed selected slides and concurs. \u000aC. CORE BIOPSY SITE: \u000aSkin with scar. \u000aD. MEDIAL PECTORAL MUSCLE: \u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, invading skeletal muscle. \u000aCarcinoma is focally present at medial, anterior, and posterior margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 54 year old post menopausal woman s/p REMOVED_DATE right breast, core \u000abiopsy, UIQ revealing moderately differentiated grade II/III ILC; no LVI, no \u000aCIS. \u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy, SNM, SLNB, ? ALND, RECON. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right sentinel node hot and blue. \u000aB/2. Right breast short superior, long lateral bow tie firm medial margin. \u000aC/3. Core biopsy site. \u000aD/4. Medial pectoral muscle short medial long superior. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. RIGHT SENTINEL NODE" ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2, 3, 4): \u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. RIGHT BREAST" (FSB): \u000aInvasive carcinoma involves the medial and deep margins. \u000aCarcinoma shows extensive infiltration of skeletal muscle. \u000aOR Consultation by: JASON L. HORNICK, M.D., PH.D. \u000aResident: GEORGE LIN, M.D., PH.D. \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and medical record number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Right sentinel node, hot and blue", consists of one fragment of \u000afibroadipose tissue (4.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm ), containing one large fatty lymph node \u000a(3.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm ), sliced in four sections and submitted in the frozen \u000asection room as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnants, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of fibroadipose tissue, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast, short superior, long lateral, bowtie, firm medial \u000amargin", consists of a radical mastectomy specimen (900-g, 20.0cm from medial \u000ato lateral, 20.0cm from superior to inferior, 6.5cm from anterior to \u000aposterior). A patch of muscle is located on the deep margin at the medial \u000aaspect of the specimen (10.5cm from superior to inferior, 3.5cm from medial \u000ato lateral and 1.0cm from anterior to posterior), which is inked orange and \u000amarked with a bowtie per the surgeon. The deep margin is inked black, the \u000aanterior margin is inked blue. Sectioning of the specimen reveals \u000aapproximately 90% lobulated yellow adipose tissue and 10% white, firm fibrous \u000atissue. The anterior surface displays a white/tan skin ellipse (11.5 x 4.3cm ) \u000awith a 3.0cm nipple-areolar complex, including an everted nipple (1.0cm in \u000adiameter). \u000aAt the medial aspect of the specimen, located at the interface of fibroadipose \u000atissue and skeletal muscle, there is a white, firm, ill-defined, spiculated \u000amass (up to 2.5cm in greatest dimension, ill-defined) present. A \u000arepresentative section of this mass is submitted in the frozen section room as \u000aFSB. This mass (#1), located in the upper inner quadrant, is grossly present \u000aat the deep skeletal muscle margin and the medial margin, 5cm from the \u000aanterior margin and approximately 7.0cm from the nipple-areolar complex. Mass \u000a#1, including surrounding firm fibrous tissue and skeletal muscle, is entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aAdditional ill-defined, firm, white areas (? additional masses, both measuring \u000aapproximately 1.5cm in greatest dimension, found 2.0cm apart from each other) \u000aare found in the mid to upper outer quadrant, located approximately 5cm from \u000amass #1, 1.5cm from the posterior/deep, > 3.0cm from the anterior margin \u000a(mass #2) as well as 3.5cm from the NA complex, and in the mid to lower outer \u000aquadrant, located 1.5cm from the deep and at least 4.5cm from the anterior \u000amargin as well as 4cm from the NA complex (mass #3). \u000aNo other lesions or masses are identified. Approximately 80-90% of the firm, \u000awhite fibrous tissue are submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : FSB remnant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass #1, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass #2, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass #3, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple-areolar complex, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue between mass #1 and mass #2, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue between mass #2 and mass#3, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aPart C, "#3. Core needle biopsy site", consists of a fragment of tan/white firm \u000atissue (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm ). The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Core biopsy site, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart D, "#4. Medial pectoral muscle, short medial, long superior", consists of \u000aa fragment of skeletal muscle (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ). The specimen is inked as \u000afollows: Anterior - blue, posterior - black, and medial - orange. The \u000aspecimen is sectioned from medial to lateral and is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Serial sections, multi frags each, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aAWE/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aMonday REMOVED_MONTH 06,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01:47:29PM \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (4/7/09): \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for \u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) NEGATIVE (1+) \u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for E-cadherin is