\u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the following \u000aresults for ADH (reviewed): \u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE \u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE \u000aNote: The ADH consists of low grade nuclei forming a cribriform pattern in a \u000a0.1cm area and was originally classified as DCIS. Given the small size of the \u000alesion, classification as ADH is favored. However, excision would be helpful \u000ato exclude an adjacent area of DCIS. \u000aThe type of lesion biopsied is not stated. Radiologic correlation is necessary \u000ato ensure the biopsies are representative of the targeted lesion. \u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Deborah Dillon, who concurs wit this \u000ainterpretation. \u000aLEFT BREAST, CORE BIOPSIES ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; 10/14/08): \u000aPapilloma. \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aBenign epithelium with associated calcifications. \u000aNote: The type of lesion biopsied is not stated. Radiologic correlation is \u000anecessary to ensure the biopsies are representative of the targeted lesion. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aConsult slides. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aReceived from Lahey Clinic, Pathology Department, 41 Mall Road, Burlington, MA \u000a REMOVED_CASE_ID , are fifty-one (51) glass slides. \u000aFifteen (15) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  1" through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a3", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  1" through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  1" through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  1" through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3" and " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a1" through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3", corresponding to a left breast core biopsies A) well #12 \u000awith calcifications (1.5 x 1cm ) B) well #3 with (1.58 x 1cm ) C) well #6 with \u000acalcifications (0.8 x 0.5cm ) D) well #9 with calcifications (1.5 x 0.4cm ) E) \u000acenter well with calcifications (0.8 x 0.4cm )1.58 x 1cm ) C) well #6 with \u000acalcifications (0.8 x 0.5cm ) D) well #9 with calcifications (1.5 x 0.4cm ) E) \u000acenter well with calcifications (0.8 x 0.4cm ) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according \u000ato the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name. \u000aTwenty-three (23) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through \u000a" REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ER", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PR", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  UNC-Ms" and " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", corresponding \u000ato a left breast excision (5 x 4 x 3cm ) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the \u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name. \u000aSeven (7) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3-1", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3-3", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aER", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PR", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  UNC-Ms", " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3-1" and " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3-3", corresponding to a right \u000abreast core biopsy (2.5cm ) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying \u000apathology report bearing the patient's name. \u000aSix (6) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3-1" through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3-3" \u000aand " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3-1" through " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3-3", corresponding to a left breast core biopsy (2.5 \u000acm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report \u000abearing the patient's name. \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed