VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY: \u000aFibroadenoma (0.4cm ). \u000aBiopsy cavity with repair reaction. \u000aNo residual tumor seen. \u000aThirteen axillary lymph nodes with no tumor seen. \u000aLEFT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY: \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (block 14). \u000aFibroadenoma, (0.9cm ). \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. \u000aFibrocystic changes. \u000aBiopsy cavity with repair reaction. \u000aNine axillary lymph nodes with no tumor seen. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aOperation: Bilateral modified radical mastectomy with tissue expanders. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast with axillary tail (short stitch=superior; \u000along stitch=lateral). \u000a2. Left breast/axillary node dissection (short stitch=superior; \u000along stitch=lateral). \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 RIGHT BREAST/AXILLARY NODES": \u000aSpecimen examined in frozen section room, revealing previous biopsy cavity \u000a(2.7cm ) with no residual invasive carcinoma grossly identified. \u000aNo charge to patient. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2 LEFT BREAST/AXILLARY NODES": \u000aMastectomy specimen with axillary tail. \u000aA 1.7cm biopsy cavity with no gross evidence of residual tumor. \u000aNo charge to patient. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BENJAMIN,RICHARD JOHN,M.B.,CH.B.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received in two (2) parts, fresh, in the frozen section room, \u000aeach labeled with the patient's name and unit number. \u000aSpecimen's part one, labeled "right breast/axillary nodes", consists of a right \u000abreast containing a skin ellipse, with attached fatty tissue and \u000aaxillary tail. Grossly the entire specimen measures REMOVED_DATE x 28 x 2cm and \u000aweighs 560 grams. The skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 4.3cm and has a nipple and \u000aareola present; the nipple measures 1.4cm in diameter and the areola, 2.5cm  \u000aA 4cm  well healed scar is present on the lateral border of the areola. \u000aThe axillary tail measures 8 x 8 x 1cm  On incision, no gross residual tumor \u000awas present. The previous biopsy cavity was identified measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.5cm  extending to within 0.3cm of the deep margin. Muscle tissue is \u000apresent on the posterior surface of the breast, measuring REMOVED_DATE x 5cm  \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Cavity, 2 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 3: Scar, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Nipple and cavity, 2 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 6: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 7: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 8: Right upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 9: Right lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Right axillary lymph nodes, 12 frag, RSS. \u000aSpecimen's part two, labeled "left breast/axillary node (short=supeior; \u000along=lateral)", is received fresh in the frozen section room and weighs 535 \u000agrams and measures, grossly, 28 x 19 x 3cm  The specimen consists of a left \u000abreast, complete with axillary tail and skin ellipse. The skin ellipse \u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x 4.5cm and has a central nipple with a diameter of 1.4cm \u000asurrounded by a 2.7cm diameter areola. On the medial border of the areola, \u000ais a 3.7cm well healed scar. The axillary tail measures 9 x 6 x 2cm  On \u000aincision, no tumor was grossly present; however, a biopsy cavity was found \u000asurrounded by fat necrosis. The biopsy cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm and \u000ais situated 1.2cm from the deep margin. \u000aMicro 13: Left breast biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 14: Left biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 15: Left breast scar, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 16: Left nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 17: Medial superior quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 18: Medial inferior quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 19: Left lateral superior quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Left lower outer quadrant, 2 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Left axillary lymph nodes, 10 frag, RSS. \u000arjb \u000aReports to: EBERLEIN, TIMOTHY, JOSEPH M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000a[report_end] 
