VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ELISABETH P FROST M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Peter M Sadow, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, LOWER INNER, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN \u000aIRREGULAR MASS: \u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade \u000aI/III), measuring at least 0.3cm in size in this limited specimen. \u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen. \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type, (low nuclear grade) is present. \u000aNo necrosis or microcalcifications are associated with DCIS. \u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone \u000areceptor, and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu will be performed and reported in an addendum. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHISTORY: 71 year old female with irregular mass left LIQ on MRI, mammo +4s. \u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING: \u000a1. Left: 6mm  non-palpable and irregular mass. \u000aLOCATION: \u000a1. Left: lower/inner. \u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY: \u000a1. 14G Ultrasound. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Left breast in one blue cassette. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit \u000anumber, and "left breast", and consists of a single blue cassette labeled with \u000athe word "left". The blue cassette is labeled "left", and contains multiple \u000atan/yellow tissues that aggregate to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Blue cassette labeled left contents, multi frags, ESS. \u000apf/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a5/2/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) NEGATIVE (1+) \u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the \u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet \u000abeen determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a \u000aportion of the membrane is positive. \u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of \u000atumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of \u000atumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational \u000ause only. \u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
