VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNOSE, VANIA, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NOSE,VANIA,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION WIRE-LOCALIZATION (SPECIMEN 1): \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aSYNOPSIS: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Cribiform, clinging, apocrine \u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate to high \u000aCalcification with DCIS - Present \u000aNecrosis with DCIS - Absent \u000aMargins DCIS: \u000aNegative: - Superior, lateral, posterior \u000aClose (0.1cm ): - Medial and inferior: multifocal \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - present \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia \u000aBiopsy cavity \u000aSkin with scar \u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium \u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously \u000aNOTE: \u000aSkin with seborrheic keratosis. \u000aDr. Susan Lester concurs. \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATION (SPECIMEN 2): \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aOther findings: Atypical ductal hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis, fibroadenoma \u000aand calcifications in benign epithelium. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: DCIS left breast microcalcification, left breast. DCIS, resected, but \u000aclose margins. \u000aOperation: Left breast wire localized excision. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS, left breast; microcalcifications, left breast. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Site of DCIS, left breast to FS. \u000a2. Area of microcalcifciations, left breast. Suture short margin. Long \u000alateral. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++ in specimen - site #1, UOQ posterior. epf \u000aCA++ in specimen - site #2, anterior. epf \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHEN,JEY-HSIN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aReceived fresh in the Frozen Section Room in two parts, each labeled with the \u000apatient's name and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "site of DCIS, left breast", is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm breast \u000aexcisional biopsy specimen consisting of a tan/pink skin ellipse (4 x 0.7cm ), \u000aexcised to a depth of 4.0cm  The specimen is oriented with a short suture on \u000athe skin edge designating the superior surface and a long suture designating \u000athe lateral surface. The specimen is received with a wire which accompanies a \u000aradiograph confirming the placement of the wire in the specimen which inserts \u000ainto the anterolateral surface and exits at the posterior surface. The \u000aspecimen is received inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; \u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. The posterior surface of the specimen is \u000acomprised of fibrous tissue consistent with a biopsy cavity. The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned from inferior to superior (skin) revealing a firm \u000atan/pink/yellow area abutting the biopsy cavity extending to the medial, \u000ainferior, posterior surfaces. The entire specimen is submitted with the area \u000aof microcalcifications potentially in micros REMOVED_DATE \u000aMicro 1&2: inferior-most slice, perpendicular, 7 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial slices from inferior to superior, 13 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior-most slice including skin, perpendicular, 14 frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, labeled " #2 area of microcalcification, left breast suture long \u000alateral, short superior", is a breast excisional biopsy (5 x 4 x 1.5cm \u000aoriented with a short suture designating the superior surface and a long \u000asuture designating the lateral surface. The specimen contains a wire with \u000aaccompanying radiograph confirming the placement of the wire in the specimen \u000awhich enters the specimen at the medial surface and extends out of the \u000aspecimen at the lateral surface. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol \u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = \u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is \u000abisected with the anterior portion containing the wire. The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned lateral to medial and is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior half of the specimen containing the wire, serial \u000asections from lateral to medial with microcalcifications contained potentially \u000ain micros REMOVED_DATE  \u000aMicro 19: lateral-most slice, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections from lateral to medial, 7 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 27: medial-most slice, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior half of the specimen, serial sections from lateral to \u000amedial: \u000aMicro 28: lateral-most slice, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections from lateral to medial, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 35: medial-most slides, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS. \u000ajhc \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
