VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D. \u000a1. LEFT SKIN LESION MEDIAL EXCISION SITE: \u000aSkin with scar and foreign body giant cell reaction. \u000aSeborrheic keratosis. \u000a2. LEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aSYNOPSIS: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aTypes - cribriform, apocrine \u000aNuclear grade - low-intermediate \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent \u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent \u000aExtent of DCIS \u000aNumber of blocks:total - 2:20 blocks \u000aFinal Margins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (>0.3cm ) - inferior, medial, lateral, anterior, \u000aposterior \u000aClose (0.2cm ) - superior (focal, block #17) \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - present \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread \u000aBiopsy cavity \u000aSkin with scar \u000aFibroadenoma \u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pNX MX \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: DCIS of left breast. Still has close margins. Skin lesion adjacent \u000ato former incision medial breast. \u000aOperation: Left breast re-excision, excision of skin lesion \u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS left breast \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left skin lesion medial incision site \u000a#2) Re-excision left breast DCIS site - short superior; \u000along lateral \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHEN,JEY-HSIN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1. left skin lesion medial incision site", consists of a \u000apink/tan skin ellipse (1.8 x 0.4cm  excised to a depth of 0.4cm ). The \u000aspecimen is unoriented and the soft tissue resection margin is inked black. \u000aThere is a slightly raised area of pink/tan skin (0.6cm ), similar in to color \u000ato surrounding skin, which extends to within 0.1cm of the skin edge. The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted. \u000aMicro 1: tips, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections, 6 frags, ESS \u000aPart two, labeled "#2. re-excision left breast DCIS site short superior, long \u000alateral", consists of an oriented left breast lumpectomy specimen (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a2.0cm ) with attached pink/tan skin ellipse (3.8 x 1.1cm ) oriented with a \u000ashort stitch marking the superior surface and a long stitch marking the lateral \u000asurface. The specimen is inked orange and green by the surgeon at the medial \u000aand inferior margins, respectively, and the remaining surfaces are inked per \u000athe histologic evaluation margins (skin is at the anterior surface, and biopsy \u000acavity located at the superior surface): posterior = black; anterior = blue; \u000asuperior = red; lateral = yellow. The skin contains a well-healed linear scar \u000a(3.0cm ). The specimen is serially sectioned from posterior to anterior \u000arevealing approximately 70% white/tan/pink lobular tissue which extends to all \u000aof the soft tissue resection margins. The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posteriormost section, perpendicular, 14 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections from posterior to anterior, 17 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anteriormost section, perpendicular, including skin with scar, 18 \u000afrags, ESS \u000ajhc \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
