st scar, multi frag, ESS \u000aPart two, "2) left breast tissue (whip stitch=new margin)", consists of a \u000asingle fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm ) with a \u000astitch on one surface indicating the new anterior margin. The surface opposite \u000athe new margin is pink/tan and fibrotic, consistent with an old biopsy site. \u000aThere are no masses or nodules within the specimen. The new margin is inked in \u000ablue, and the entire specimen is submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Left breast tissue, including new anterior margin, 1 frag/cass, \u000aESS \u000aPart three, "3) deep nodule, left breast", consists of a single unoriented \u000afragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm ). The entire \u000aspecimen is inked black. Within the specimen, there is a firm, white, fibrotic \u000aarea (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ). There are no other nodules or masses. This fibrous \u000aarea is ill-defined and appproaches the inked black resection margin by 0.1cm  \u000aThe entire specimen is submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Deep nodule, left breast, multi frag, ESS \u000ajch \u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
