VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Astrid Weins, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE LOCALIZED REEXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aNo residual DCIS identified. \u000aBreast tissue with atypical lobular hyperplasia and calcifications in \u000abenign epithelium. \u000aBiopsy cavity changes. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 54 year old premenopausal woman S/P REMOVED_DATE R breast WL exc revealing \u000aintermediate grade DCIS with close lateral and inferior margins. \u000aOperation: R breast WL re-excision. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Rt breast abnormal mammo. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) rt breast tissue, short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral, whip stitch \u000aon chest wall margin -- mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aCalcifications, hook and wire in specimen. Called to Dr. Rhei by DGS at 2:55 \u000apm. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and medical \u000arecord number, and "#1. Right breast tissue, short stitch/superior, long \u000astitch/lateral, whip stitch on chest wall margin.", and consists of one wire \u000alocalized excision (6.0cm medial to lateral, 6.0cm superior to inferior, and \u000a4.0cm from anterior to posterior). The specimen is oriented with a short \u000astitch designated superior, a long stitch designated lateral and a whip stitch \u000aon the chest wall margin per the surgeon. The specimen is inked per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; \u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The accompanying \u000aradiograph is examined. There is an excision cavity present in the specimen \u000a(3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm depth). There is a localization wire entering the specimen \u000ain the prior excision cavity. The orientation of the wire cannot be clearly \u000aidentified as it is partially dislocated, but it appears to be entering the \u000aspecimen on the lateral aspect. Upon sectioning, the specimen contains \u000aapproximately 40% fibrous and 60% adipose tissue. The fibrous tissue is \u000apredominantly located adjacent to superior and anterior margins (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a2.0cm ) as well as surrounding the prior excision cavity. The fibrous tissue \u000ais entirely submitted from medial to lateral. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial and inferior margins, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Small anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior and posterior margins, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior and lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral, superior, and posterior margins, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aAWE/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a9/24/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
