or/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is extremely \u000afriable and begins to fall apart immediately upon receipt in surgical \u000apathology. The specimen radiograph is reviewed and reveals no discrete biopsy \u000aclip but does reveal localization wire entering specimen in association with \u000aseveral areas of calcification. Localization wire is identified in the \u000aspecimen and removed. The specimen is approximately 90% fibrous and 10% fatty. \u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted from medial to lateral. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior/inferior/anterior/posterior margins, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aSEI/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lynette M Sholl M.D., Electronically signed on Monday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 25,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 09:33:35AM \u000a[report_end] 
