VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000a1, 2) RIGHT BREAST AND AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE, WIRE-LOCALIZATED \u000aBIOPSY FOR A MASS AND A CLIP AND SENTINEL LYMPH NODE BIOPSY: \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA. \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU. \u000aNEGATIVE SENTINEL LYMPH NODE(S). \u000aSYNOPSIS: \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aSize - 1.2cm \u000aMultifocal? - No \u000aHistologic Type - Ductal \u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) \u000aNuclear Grade - Intermediate \u000aEIC - Negative \u000aLymphovascular invasion - No definite lymphovascular invasion \u000ais identified. \u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A \u000aSkin invasion - N/A \u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A \u000aFinal Margins (invasive) \u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - Anterior, medial, superior, lateral \u000aClose (<0.1cm from margin) - Posterior (focal; block #2) \u000aPositive (ink on tumor) - Inferior (broad; block #3) \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aTypes - Cribriform, papillary \u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present \u000aExtent of DCIS \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU is present as a minor component of the \u000ainvasive tumor. \u000aFinal Margins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (>0.3cm ) - Superior, medial, lateral, anterior, \u000ainferior \u000aClose (0.1-0.3cm ) - Posterior (focal,block #2) \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent \u000aLYMPH NODES \u000aSentinel lymph nodes (3 H+E levels examined) \u000aNumber of positive nodes: 0 \u000aNumber of nodes examined: 2 \u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia \u000aCysts \u000aApocrine metaplasia \u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium \u000aPrior core biopsy site \u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID c p REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  MX \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 56 year old female with right breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right wire (local excision) breast (short/superior; \u000along/lateral) \u000a#2) Right sentinel node biopsy \u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass and clip in specimen. JL \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BUNDOCK,ELIZABETH A.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right wire local excision breast", consists of a portion \u000aof fibroadipose tissue (7.5 x 5 x 2cm ) with a localization wire and two \u000asutures (short to designate superior, long to designate lateral) in place. The \u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral \u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is sectioned serially at 3mm \u000aintervals from medial to lateral to reveal tissue which is 75% rubbery white \u000afibrosis which extends to the inferior, medial and posterior margins, is 0.4cm \u000afrom the superior margin, and more than 1cm from the lateral margin. The clip \u000ais found in the lateral aspect of a firm white mass (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ) which \u000ais apparent on the accompanying specimen radiograph. The mass extends to the \u000adeep and inferior margins and is located 1.2cm from the superior, 2cm from \u000athe anterior, and 2cm from the lateral margin. The mass is submitted \u000aentirely in series in cassettes one through four. Representative sections of \u000athe remaining fibrous tissue and margins are submitted. The specimen is also \u000areceived with a specimen radiograph which is reported as mass and clip in \u000aspecimen. A separate specimen radiograph is taken in pathology to localize the \u000aclip in the sectioned specimen. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass surrounding clip, clip in #4, 5 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of dense fibrosis (approximately 75%), 8 \u000afrags, RSS \u000aPart two, labeled "#2. rt sentinel node biopsy", consists of one fragment of \u000ayellow/tan adipose tissue (2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ) which contains one lymph node (0.6 \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ). \u000aMicro 10: 1 lymph node, 1 frag, ESS \u000aeab \u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE \u000a[report_end] 
