ATE x 3.8cm ) in which the two wires are \u000alocalized and in which the clip is identified. The fibrous area grossly extends \u000ato the superior margin, 0.5cm from the inferior margin, to the posterior \u000amargin, 2.0cm from the anterior/skin margin, to the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial margin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is yellow/tan \u000agrossly unremarkable adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMICRO #1 and 2: Medial margin, 3 frags in each cass, ESS. \u000aMICRO #3-5: Lateral and inferior margins, 3 frags in micro #3, 2 frags in \u000amicros #4 and 5, ESS. \u000aMICRO #6: Area containing clip with inferior and superior margins, 1 frags, \u000aESS. \u000aMICRO #8: Superior margin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMICRO #9: Superior and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMICRO #10: Anterior/skin, superior, inferior margins, 1 frags, ESS. \u000aMICRO #11: Anterior, medial, inferior margins, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMICRO #12: Superior, inferior margins, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMICRO #13: Anterior, superior, inferior margins, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMICRO #14: Anterior, superior, inferior margins, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMICRO #15: Anterior and superior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMICRO #16: Inferior and posterior margins, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMICRO #17: Anterior, superior, inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMICRO #18: Inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMICRO #19: Posterior margins, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMICRO #20: Posterior and inferior margins, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMICRO #21: Posterior, inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMICRO #22: Posterior margin, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMICRO #23: Inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS. \u000ajdr \u000aReports to: SHOJI, BRENT, T. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
