VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. LEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS; \u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR (4.1cm ), low-grade. \u000aMitoses number 1 per 10 HPF's. \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present within the tumor. \u000aThe stroma is moderately cellular with moderate nuclear pleomorphism. \u000aNo necrosis is seen. \u000aNo heterologous elements are seen. \u000aMinimal stromal overgrowth is present. \u000aBiopsy site changes are present. \u000aThe tumor is well circumscribed with pushing margins. \u000aThe tumor is 0.1cm from the posterior margin, and the other resection \u000amargins are free of tumor by at least 0.5cm  \u000aB. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS (SUPERIOR WIRE): \u000aIll-defined mass (2.5cm ) consisting of adenosis, biopsy site changes, \u000aand adipose tissue. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aNote: Radiologically, the lesion appeared to be hamartoma. \u000aC. LEFT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aMucinous cysts. \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. \u000aCalcium oxalate is present. \u000aNote: There is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the \u000aentire specimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Left breast phyllodes tumor, left breast hamartoma with \u000acalcifications, new left breast calcifications. \u000aOperation: Left breast wide excision of phyllodes; left breast wide local \u000aexcision of superior wire, hamartoma; and, left breast wire localized excision \u000aof inferior wire calcifications. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: left breast phyllodes tumor; left breast hamartoma; and, \u000aleft breast calcification. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1 - left breast phyllodes tumor (breast bank/research), stitch = \u000ashort/superior, long/lateral. \u000aB/2 - left breast wire loc (superior wire), stitch = short/superior, \u000along/lateral (to mammo). \u000aC/3 - left breast wire loc (inferior wire), stitch = short/superior, \u000along/lateral (to mammo). \u000aRADIOGRAPHY REPORT: Specimen #2: Mass in specimen (checked with ultrasound). \u000aSpecimen #3: Calcifications in specimen. C. Denison, M.D. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient?s \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "#1 - left breast wide excision of phyllodes tumor, stitch = \u000ashort/superior, long/lateral", consists of one breast excision specimen (6.3 x \u000a6.0 x 3.0cm ) with two orienting sutures. The specimen is inked per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; \u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen \u000acontains a well-circumscribed papillary tan mass (4.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm ), which is \u000aless than 0.1cm from the deep margin, 0.5cm from medial margin, 0.5cm from \u000athe superior margin, 1.0cm from the anterior margin, and 1.0cm from the \u000alateral margin. Approximately 40% of the specimen is submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : medial margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : anterior margin, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : superior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : tumor, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2 - left breast wire localized biopsy (superior wire)", \u000aconsists of one breast excision specimen (5.5cm superior to inferior, 3.5cm \u000aanterior to posterior, and 2.7cm medial to lateral) with two orienting sutures \u000aand one intact needle localization wire. The specimen is inked per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; \u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The localization \u000awire enters superiorly and exits inferiorly. An accompanying specimen \u000aradiograph demonstrates a density with irregular borders at the end of the \u000aneedle localization wire. The specimen contains an irregular heterogeneous \u000amass (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.8cm ), which is composed of focally cystic tan/white soft \u000atissue with focal hemorrhage. The mass grossly extends to the inferior, \u000aanterior, medial, and lateral margins. The mass is 0.9cm from the posterior \u000amargin and 2.5cm from the superior margin. The remainder of the specimen is \u000acomposed of approximately 80% adipose tissue and 20% fibrous tissue. The \u000aspecimen is sectioned into eleven slices, and the mass is present is slices \u000aseven through eleven. Approximately 60% of the specimen is submitted, \u000aincluding all slices containing the mass and any slices containing fibrous \u000atissue. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : superior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice seven with mass, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice eight with mass, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice nine with mass, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice ten with mass, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : inferior margin with mass in level 11, 8 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : fibrous tissue in level 5, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : fibrous tissue in level 6, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aPart C, labeled "#3 - left breast wire loc biopsy (inferior wire)", consists of \u000aone breast excision specimen (3.9cm medial to lateral, 3.5cm anterior to \u000aposterior, and 1.9cm superior to inferior) with two orienting sutures and one \u000aneedle localization wire entering laterally and exiting superomedially. An \u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a small cluster of three \u000acalcifications present in the center of the needle localization wire. The \u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. The specimen is sectioned into seven slices from medial to \u000alateral (0.4cm each), and there is an area of dense fibrous tissue (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 0.9cm ) in the center of the needle localization wire. The dense fibrous \u000atissue grossly abuts the inferior and anterior margins, and is 0.3cm from the \u000asuperior margin, 1.0cm from the posterior margin, 1.5cm from the medial \u000amargin, and 0.9cm from the lateral margin. The specimen contains no other \u000amasses, and is composed of approximately 90% adipose tissue. The dense fibrous \u000atissue is present in slices four, five and six. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : level one (medial margin), 6 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : level two, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : level three, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : level four with fibrous tissue, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : level five with fibrous tissue, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : level six with fibrous tissue, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : level seven, 7 frags, ESS. \u000aAF/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Ann K Folkins M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a11/7/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
