ying specimen radiograph \u000awhich is reported as "Clip is seen in radiograph specimen" and signed by L. \u000aFrost. The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal tissue \u000awhich is 60% white fibrosis with a hemorrhagic focus surrounding the clip. \u000aThe fibrotic areas extend to the margin of excision. No areas are grossly \u000asuspicious for invasive carcinoma. The specimen is entirely submitted in \u000aseries. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 10 frag, ESS (NOTE: clip is in block #7) \u000aeab \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
