low soft tissue; the first fragment, which measures \u000a1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm is unoriented, is inked in black, and serially sectioned to \u000areveal unremarkable white fibrous tissue, and a small amount of what appears to \u000abe pink tissue consistent with prior biopsy site. The second detached \u000afragment, is also unoriented, and contains fragments of skin (2.5 x 0.5cm  \u000aexcised to a depth of 1.2cm ). The skin ellipse has been longitudinally cut \u000afrom one edge to a length of 1.5cm  No scar is definitively identified. The \u000adeep margin is inked in black, the specimen serially sectioned, and entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast posterior shave margin, 2 or 3 frags, ESS \u000aMicro 6: detached soft tissue fragment, 6 frags, ESS \u000aMicro 7: skin ellipse tips of second detached fragment, 3 frags, ESS \u000aMicro 8: detached soft tissue fragment of skin, mult frags, ESS \u000alcl \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
