, unit number, \u000aand "#1. R breast tissue with needle wire tags long equals lateral, short \u000aequals superior, whip equals chest wall", consists of an irregular portion of \u000afibrofatty tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm ), with a long suture designating lateral, \u000aa short suture designating superior, and a whipstitch designating chest wall \u000amargin (posterior). The specimen is received previously inked per pathology \u000aprotocol as anterior blue, posterior black, superior red, inferior green, \u000amedial orange and lateral yellow. There is an inserted needle localization \u000awire, which enters along the anterior-lateral margin, and does not exit the \u000aspecimen. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a hemorrhagic biopsy \u000acavity (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ), 0.8cm from the superior margin, 0.8cm from the \u000ainferior margin, 0.6cm from the anterior margin, 0.5cm from the posterior \u000amargin, 0.8cm from the lateral margin and 2.0cm from the medial margin. The \u000abiopsy cavity is surrounded by dense white fibrous tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm ), \u000apredominantly at the inferior-posterior aspect, coming to less than 0.1cm from \u000athe inferior margin, less than 0.1cm from the posterior margin, 0.8cm from \u000athe anterior margin, 1.5cm from the superior margin, 0.7cm from the lateral \u000amargin, and 1.8cm from the medial margin. The remaining cut surface displays \u000a98% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 2% white fibrous tissue, with no \u000aadditional discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen is sequentially \u000asubmitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, radially. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections, bisected, with the biopsy cavity in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , \u000a1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections, bisected, with the surgical clip, and \u000athe biopsy cavity identified in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections, bisected, with the biopsy cavity in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , \u000a1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential bisected cross sections, with the biopsy cavity in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , \u000a1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross section, bisected, with the dense fibrous \u000atissue in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross section, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000acp/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a4/18/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
