VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Dick Guang-Iong Hwang, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION": \u000aBreast tissue with focal atypical ductal hyperplasia, \u000aepithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, and cysts. \u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aFocal fibrosis consistent with old core biopsy site. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 50-year-old premenopausal female with left breast mammogram on \u000a2/18/08, showing a few scattered benign-appearing microcalcifications in left \u000abreast. History of papilloma, REMOVED_DATE core biopsy - excision recommended. \u000aOperation: Left breast core biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: Not given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Left breast tissue (short superior, long lateral - whipstitch deep margin. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aSpecimen contains wire and clip. Signature: (ILLEGIBLE) \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1. Left breast tissue, short superior, long lateral, whipstitch deep \u000amargin", consists of an irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), with a long suture designating lateral, and short suture designating \u000asuperior, and a whipstitch designating the deep margin. There is an inserted \u000aneedle localization wire, which enters along the lateral margin, and exits \u000aalong the medial margin. The specimen is received previously inked per \u000apathology protocol as anterior blue, posterior black (deep margin), superior \u000ared, inferior green, lateral yellow, and medial orange. The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned to reveal a potential hemorrhagic biopsy cavity (0.4 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.3cm ), less than 0.1cm from the superior margin, less than 0.1cm from the \u000amedial margin, 1.0cm from the lateral margin, 1.0cm from the inferior margin, \u000a1.0cm from the lateral margin, 2.0cm from the anterior margin, and 1.5cm \u000afrom the posterior margin. A surgical clip is identified within the potential \u000ahemorrhagic biopsy cavity. The remaining cut surface displays 90% focally \u000adense white fibrous tissue, and 10% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no \u000aadditional discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen is sequentially \u000asubmitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, radially, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections from anterior to posterior, with the \u000aclip identified in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin, radially, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000acp/elw \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
