d, located 0.6cm to the superior \u000amargin, 3.2cm inferior, 2.9cm medial, 1.7cm lateral, 0.9cm anterior, and \u000a0.5cm posterior. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. No lesions, masses, or areas of \u000ahemorrhage are associated with the clip. The specimen has approximately 20% \u000afibrous and 80% adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted for \u000ahistologic evaluation. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin with slices inferior to superior, 3 frags in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and \u000a5 frags in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin with anterior/posterior with slices medial lateral \u000aand clip area in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin with slices going superior inferior, REMOVED_DATE frags \u000aeach, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin with anterior and posterior with slices going \u000alateral medial, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aGL/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
