imen container. \u000aThe specimen was previously radiographed. The specimen is serially sectioned \u000afrom medial to lateral to exhibit approximately 80% very dense white/tan \u000afibrous stroma and approximately 20% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. A \u000ametal clip is identified within a hemorrhagic/cystic focus (0.6 x 0.5cm ) in \u000athe central specimen, with an adjacent area of hemorrhagic gritty probable fat \u000anecrosis (0.4cm in greatest dimension). No discrete masses or lesions are \u000agrossly identified. The specimen is entirely sequentially submitted from \u000amedial to lateral. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : sequential from medial to lateral (clip in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) multi frags \u000atotal, ESS. \u000aLMB/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Briana Gleason M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a2/3/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
