VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: EVA D. GOMBOS M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Revised Report ********** Resident: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN IRREGULAR REMOVED_DATE CM MASS: \u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified \u000aBloom-Richardson grade II/III), measuring at least 0.5cm in size in this \u000alimited specimen. \u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen. \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type, (intermediate nuclear grade) is present. \u000aStromal nodule with associated calcifications. \u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone \u000areceptor, and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu will be performed and reported in an addendum. \u000aReport has been revised to correct a typographical error. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Left breast mass (1.3cm ), s/p prior benign biopsy of the left breast. \u000aOperation: \u000aOperative Findings: \u000aClinical Diagnosis: \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000a10 core samples of left breast mass in a pink cassette. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit \u000anumber, and "left breast", in a pink cassette, and consists of ten soft, \u000afragmented, yellow to white fibrofatty tissue cores (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm in \u000aaggregate). The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Left breast, 10 frags (4 frags in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and 6 frags  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), ESS. \u000aMah/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aSurgical Addendum: \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) - NEGATIVE (1+) \u000aInterpretation: \u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the \u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet \u000abeen determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor \u000acells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only \u000aa portion of the membrane is positive. \u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% \u000aof tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in \u000a>10% of tumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational \u000ause only. \u000aResident Review by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAmendment #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a2/3/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
