VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRENN, THOMAS, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRENN,THOMAS,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST MASS AT 3:30, BIOPSY: \u000aFibrodenoma (1.5cm ). \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000aRIGHT BREAST MASS AT 12:30, BIOPSY: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia involving and confined within the \u000afibroadenoma (MLE). \u000aFibroadenoma (1.8cm ). \u000aNOTE: \u000aThe significance of finding ADH within a fibroadenoma is unknown. \u000aCase reviewed with Dr. A. Richardson, Breast Pathology. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 32 yo female with a prior history of bilateral fibroadenomas \u000awith 2 right breast masses for which she prefers excision. \u000aOperation: R breast wire localized bx x2. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal R U/S. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Rt 3:30 breast mass (long lateral, short superior, whip \u000astitch chest wall fascia). \u000a2. Rt 12:30 breast mass (long lateral, short superior, whip stitch \u000adeep margin). \u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass seen in specimen #1. ds \u000aMass seen in specimen #2. ds \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SADOW,PETER MARK,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts labeled with the patient's name and \u000aunit number. \u000aPart one, "#1 rt 3:30 breast mass, long lateral, short superior, whip stitch \u000achest wall fascia". There is a needle localization and a radiograph submitted \u000aby Radiology. The excision biopsy measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm  The specimen \u000ais inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. According to the radiograph, the mass is in the inferior \u000aportion of the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to \u000amedial and the entire specimen is submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  3:30 breast mass, lateral to medial, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, "#2 12:30 breast mass, long lateral, short superior, whip stitch deep \u000amargin", consists of a tan/pink excision specimen of fibrofatty breast tissue, \u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm  There are sutures which have been placed by the \u000asurgeon marking the short stitch superior and long stitch lateral and deep \u000amargin with whip stitch. The specimen came with a wire localized and a \u000aradiograph submitted. The wire was not in the specimen upon receipt. The \u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. Upon sectioning, there is a tan/white, circumscribed lesion \u000awhich abuts the yellow-inked lateral margin (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ). The mass is \u000a0.2cm away from the inferior margin, 0.3cm from the deep margin, 1.8cm from \u000athe superior margin, 2.5cm away from the anterior margin and is 1.8cm from \u000athe medial margin. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial \u000aand entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast mass 12:30, lateral to medial, 11 frags, ESS. \u000apes \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
