nt's name, unit \u000anumber, and "left breast mass", and consists of an unoriented yellow/tan/white, \u000afocally cauterized to hemorrhagic portion of fibroadipose tissue (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.2cm ). Specimen is inked and serially sectioned, exhibiting a predominantly \u000awhite/tan, focally cystic fibrous stroma admixed with scant adipose tissue. No \u000aother gross lesions identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast tissue, multi frags, ESS. \u000adfi/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a5/24/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
