m to \u000alateral, 0.9cm to posterior, 1.5cm to superior and remote (more than 2.5cm ) \u000ato inferior. The remaining breast parenchyma is 20% composed of white fibrous \u000atissue, to 80% of yellow lobulated adipose tissue. The entire specimen is \u000aexamined microscopically. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, perpendicular, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4 ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to include area of hemorrhage), 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5 ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to include area of hemorrhage), 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #8, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #9, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #10, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aSTS/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a6/19/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
