VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s) \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Elizabeth A. Steensma, M.D.; Martin C Chang, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR MRI ENHANCEMENT AND A CLIP, LATERAL \u000aMARGIN RE-EXCISION AND SENTINEL LYMPH NODES (A, B, AND C: 3 SPECIMENS): \u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson \u000agrade II/III), measuring 0.2cm (slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen. \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (intermediate to high nuclear grade), is \u000apresent in 6 of 18 blocks in the main excision, focally associated with core \u000abiopsy site changes. \u000aDCIS is associated with calcifications and necrosis. \u000aInvasive carcinoma is present at least 0.3cm from all margins. \u000aIn the main excision (part B), DCIS is present <0.1cm from the lateral margin \u000aand >0.3cm from all other margins. No carcinoma is seen in the separately \u000asubmitted "lateral shave margin" (part C). \u000aSkin with no carcinoma seen. \u000aTwo sentinel lymph nodes with no carcinoma seen (0/2). \u000aCalcifications present in association with benign epithelium. \u000aNOTE: This carcinoma could be classified as AJCC (6th edition)  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID a  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (sn) MX. \u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu will be performed and reported in an addendum. \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR MRI ENHANCEMENT AND A CLIP (D: 1 \u000aSPECIMEN): \u000aSclerosing adenosis (0.5cm ) present adjacent to biopsy site changes. \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, columnar cell changes, apocrine cysts and \u000acalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: The patient with CA Lt breast with separate area of abnormal MRI. \u000aOperation: SNB - left, wire-directed excision two areas, left breast. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer. \u000aORGAN/TISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Sentinel lymph nodes -> FS room. \u000aB/2. Tissue left breast (cancer site) long stitch lateral, short stitch \u000asuperior -> mammo via FS room. \u000aC/3. Lateral shave margin, long lateral, short superior. \u000aD/4. Area of MRI abnormal -> mammo via FS room (I did not ink #4 - if there is \u000aCA or DCIS, she will need mastectomy and margin won?t count). \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000a#2. Intact hookwire and mass with clip are within the specimen. Calcifications \u000aare also seen. Dr. Gombos. \u000a#4. Please submit entire specimen for histology; MRI-guided LOC. Incidentally \u000aseen are calcifications. Dr. Gombos. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE(S)" ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes negative for carcinoma. \u000aOR Consultation by: JONATHAN NEIL GLICKMAN, M.D., PH.D. \u000aResident: ONAME O. BURLINGAME, MD, PHD \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Sentinel lymph nodes", consists of two lymph nodes, one with blue \u000adye (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ) and one that is white/tan (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ). Each \u000alymph node is bisected, and the blue-dyed lymph node is entirely submitted as \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the tan/pink lymph node is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Tissue left breast (CA site) long lateral, short superior", \u000aconsists of a wire-localized lumpectomy specimen (5.4cm anterior to posterior, \u000a5.2cm medial to lateral, 1.8cm superior to inferior) with a localization wire \u000apresent, entering the lateral aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked by \u000athe surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/ orange. A tan/pink skin ellipse (3.5 x 0.9cm ) is present along the \u000aanterior surface. A white/tan, firm mass-like area (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ) is \u000apresent less than 0.1cm from the superior, less than 0.1cm from the medial, \u000a0.4cm from the inferior, 2.9cm from the medial, 2.7cm from the posterior, \u000aand 1.9cm from the anterior margin. This area is adjacent to the localization \u000awire and per the specimen radiograph, coincides with the clip. Representative \u000asections (including all fibrous tissue and greater than 95% of the specimen) \u000aare submitted for histology. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior/superior margin, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of fibrous tissue submitted sequentially from \u000aposterior to anterior (area of interest in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin including skin, perpendicular, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aPart C, "#3. Lateral shave margin, long lateral, short superior", consists of a \u000atissue specimen (3.5cm anterior to posterior, 2.9cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm medial to lateral) with an attached tan/pink skin ellipse (2.2 x 1.2cm ) \u000athat has been surgically cut at one edge. The specimen is inked by the surgeon \u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange. \u000aThe specimen is sectioned to reveal an area of tan/white firm fibrosis (1.1 x \u000a0.9 x 0.7cm ) that directly abuts the medial, superior, and inferior margins, \u000aand is 2.2cm from the anterior, 0.1cm from the posterior, and 1.2cm from the \u000anearest inferior margin. The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior and superior margin, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of posterior margin, superior, medial, lateral, and \u000ainferior margin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior, medial, lateral, and inferior margins, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior, anterior, medial and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aPart D, "#4. Area of MRI Abn" consists of one portion of blue-stained \u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.6cm ) with a localization wire in \u000aplace. An area of dense white fibrosis (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm ) is present, \u000adirectly abutting the peripheral resection margin. A clip is present in the \u000aadipose tissue, directly adjacent to the area of fibrosis. The specimen is \u000areceived with an accompanying radiograph and is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : MRI abnormality, multi frags, ESS. \u000aEAS/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSurgical Addendum: (1/30/07) \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE - LOW \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) NEGATIVE (0) \u000aInterpretation: \u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the \u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet \u000abeen determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor \u000acells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only \u000aa portion of the membrane is positive. \u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% \u000aof tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in \u000a>10% of tumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational \u000ause only. \u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a1/30/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
