VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aHORNICK, JASON, L., M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by HORNICK,JASON L.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR MICROCALCIFICATIONS: \u000aFibroadenoma with stromal calcifications. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000a2) ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR TISSUE: \u000aFibroadenoma. \u000aCalcifications in association with benign breast epithelium. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Right breast microcalcifications \u000aOperation: Right needle localized breast biopsy \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalcifications right breast \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Right breast specimen with wire - mammo \u000a2) Additional anterior tissue - mammo \u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: \u000aCalcifications in specimen #1. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SCHMIDT,JASON F.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart 1, "R breast specimen with wire", consists of a breast excision specimen \u000acomposed of two fragments of tissue (5.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) without orienting sutures. Within the larger portion of tissue there is an \u000aembedded localization wire. Accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a \u000asingle breast lumpectomy specimen with an embedded localization wire adjacent \u000ato a cluster of microcalcifications. The specimen has been previously inked by \u000athe surgeon and is presumed to be oriented as follows: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. \u000aThe surface of the larger portion of tissue has areas of red, yellow, blue, \u000agreen, and black ink as wells as a focus of uninked tissue. The surface of \u000athe smaller portion of tissue has areas of black, blue, and orange ink as well \u000aas a focus of uninked tissue. No discrete lesions or masses are identified. \u000aThe specimen is composed primarily of yellow, lobulated adipose tissue \u000a(approximately 95%) with interwoven strands of tan/white fibrous tissue (5%). \u000aThe specimen is submitted in its entirety for microscopic examination. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Larger portion of tissue from lateral to anterior, 19 frags \u000a(slices bisected in 3-11), ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Smaller portion of tissue, 2 frags each, ESS. \u000aPart 2, "2 Additional Anterior Tissue", consists of consists of a breast shave \u000amargin specimen (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm ) without orienting sutures. An \u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates no lesions or \u000amicrocalcifications. The surface of the specimen has been previously inked \u000ablack and blue by the surgeon. The specimen is composed primarily of yellow, \u000alobulated adipose tissue (approximately 80%) and focal areas of tan/white \u000afibrous tissue (approximately 20%). No discrete lesions are identified. \u000aRepresentative sections are submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Additional anterior tissue, 6 frags, ESS. \u000ajfs \u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
