VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Paul A. VanderLaan, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Lynette M Sholl, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. LEFT BREAST, BIOPSY AFTER NEEDLE LOCALIZATION: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia. \u000aIntraductal papilloma with atypia. \u000aBiopsy site changes. \u000aMultiple levels examined. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: ADH and papilloma on core. \u000aOperation: Left. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Left breast biopsy after needle localization (long = lateral, short = \u000asuperior). \u000aRADIOLOGY: Lesion in center of specimen and wire/OR called. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, medical record \u000anumber, and "#1. Left breast biopsy after needle localization, long lateral \u000ashort superior". The specimen consists of an REMOVED_DATE gram fragment of breast \u000atissue that is oriented per the surgeon such that a short suture designates \u000asuperior and a long suture designates lateral. The specimen measures 6.5cm \u000amedial to lateral, 7.0cm anterior to posterior, and 3.1cm superior to \u000ainferior. Accompanying the specimen is a mammogram demonstrating a wire \u000alocalizing a clip and an irregularly bordered REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm lesion. The wire is \u000aseen to enter the specimen at the superior/lateral/anterior aspect, but does \u000anot exit the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned from medial to lateral to reveal approximately 90% unremarkable \u000ayellow lobulated fatty tissue and 10% firm white fibrous tissue with \u000ahemorrhage. The lesion localized by the wire and clip measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in total. The lesion is located 4.1cm to the lateral margin, 1.4cm to the \u000amedial margin, 0.6cm to the superior margin, 0.9cm to the inferior margin, \u000a3.1cm to the anterior margin, and 1.6cm to the posterior margin. The clip is \u000aidentified in a small hemorrhagic biopsy cavity (0.6 x 0.3cm ) and the tissue \u000awith the clip is located in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . All of the lesion and fibrous tissue \u000ais submitted for histology. In total approximately 25% of the specimen is \u000asubmitted for histology. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 2 perpendicular fragments, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial aspect of lesion, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Previous biopsy cavity with clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Closest anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Closest posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral end of lesion, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : White fibrous tissue at anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Area of hemorrhage near inferior margin, 1 frag per cassette, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, perpendicular section, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000apva/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lynette M Sholl M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 10,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04:55:01PM \u000a[report_end] 
