regular border. \u000a2. Left (site #2): Non-palpable on breast imaging, non-mass forming, \u000asegmental and heterogeneous. \u000aLOCATION: \u000a1. Left (site #1): upper/inner. \u000a2. Left (site #2): lower/outer. \u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY: \u000a1. Left (site #1): 9G MRI and vacuum-assisted. \u000a2. Left (site #2): 9G MRI and vacuum-assisted. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Left breast core biopsy (site #1) in one green top/white bottom cassette. \u000aB/2) Left breast core biopsy (site #2) in one blue top/white bottom cassette. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the \u000apatient's name, unit number. \u000aPart A, "green top, white bottom, site #1, left breast, REMOVED_DATE  9:40 a.m.", \u000aconsists of multiple yellow focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty tissues (aggregating \u000a5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ), which are received in four white cassettes with green top. \u000aThe specimen is submitted in toto. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 white cassette with green top, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 white cassette with green top, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 white cassette with green top, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 white cassette with green top, multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, "blue top, white bottom, site #2, left breast, REMOVED_DATE  9:40 a.m.", \u000aconsists of multiple yellow focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty tissues (aggregating \u000a4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ), which are received in three white cassettes with blue top. \u000aThe specimens are submitted in toto. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 white cassette with blue top, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 white cassette with blue top, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 white cassette with blue top, multi frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000acp/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below