VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Elizabeth A. Steensma, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY SITE WITH A CLIP \u000aAND CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, \u000apresent in 6 of 13 blocks, predominantly present adjacent to the prior core \u000aneedle biopsy site (blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) (see note). \u000aNo necrosis is associated with ADH. Rare calcifications are present. \u000aThe ADH is < 0.1cm from the anterior margin (multifocal), inferior margin \u000a(focal, one block), and posterior margin (focal, one block). The superior, \u000amedial, and lateral margins are > 0.3cm from the ADH. \u000aColumnar cell hyperplasia with flat atypia. \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for ADH \u000a(block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu WEAKLY POSITIVE (2+) \u000aNote: This is a difficult lesion to classify. The ADH arises in an area of \u000acolumnar cell change with atypia. The cells have an apocrine appearance and in \u000asome areas the cells form cribriform spaces. Although the architectural \u000afeatures are insufficient for a diagnosis of DCIS, the proximity to the margins \u000ais of concern for possible adjacent DCIS. \u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Andrea Richardson, who concurs with this \u000ainterpretation. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 54-year-old woman with right microcalcifications on screening \u000amammogram, status post stereo core biopsy positive for ADH. \u000aOperation: Right needle localization breast biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right abnormal mammogram. \u000aORGAN/TISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right breast tissue, red superior, orange medial, blue anterior, lateral \u000ayellow, inferior black, posterior green. \u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Clip and intact hookwire and rare punctate calcifications \u000aseen in specimen. - Dr. Birdwell. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part labeled with the patient's name unit \u000anumber and "#1. Right breast tissue", and consists of an oriented biopsy \u000aspecimen (4.6cm superior to inferior, 1.9cm anterior to posterior, 3.7cm \u000amedial to lateral) with a wire localization needle present. The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned into seven slices from medial to lateral. The localization \u000aneedle is located within slice #3, however, no gross abnormalities are noted. \u000aThe remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of approximately 90% fibrous \u000atissue and 10% adipose tissue. A radiograph was received with the specimen \u000ademonstrating a clip and intact wire and rare punctate calcifications; the \u000aspecimen is re-radiographed and entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast tissue serially submitted, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS. \u000aEAS/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a9/15/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
