VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Tanya Rege, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, SUPERIOR, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aBenign breast tissue with calcifications. \u000aNote: No malignancy is seen after complete microscopic examination of \u000athe specimen, including margins. \u000aLEFT BREAST, LATERAL, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR ARCHITECHTURAL \u000aDISTORTION: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and cribriform types, (low nuclear \u000agrade), with rare calcifications, is present in 4 of 11 blocks (blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000ato  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aDCIS is close to the medial (0.1cm ) and lateral (0.1cm ) margins. \u000aSuperior, inferior, anterior, posterior, and medial margins are negative for \u000aDCIS (> 0.3cm ) \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present. An immunoperoxidase study \u000aconfirms the absence of immunoreactivity for e-cadherin. (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) \u000aBenign breast tissue with calcifications. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aSclerosing adenosis. \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with \u000athe following results for DCIS (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) NEGATIVE (0) \u000aNote: A specific histologic correlate for the architectural distortion \u000adetected radiologically is not seen. The entire specimen was examined \u000amicroscopically. The DCIS appears to be an incidental finding. \u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th edition) Tis NX. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 56 year old woman with past medical history of severe ADH R breast, \u000asister with breast cancer at age 50, found to have microcalcifications on left \u000ascreening mammogram. On surgical prep with placement wires; radiologist also \u000anoted architectural distortion, which they also recommended for biopsy. \u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localized biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None specified. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Left breast superior microcalcification (mammo). \u000aB/2) Left lateral architectural distortion (mammo) \u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen #1 - wire and calcifications - OR called. Dr. Sughra \u000aRaza. \u000aSpecimen #2. Left breast architectural distortion (mammo), in specimen. Dr. \u000aDianne Georgian-Smith. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Left breast superior microcalcifications", consists of a \u000a5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures \u000adesignating superior (short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins. The \u000aspecimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of \u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; \u000alateral/yellow; medial/ orange. The localizing wire enters the medial aspect \u000aof the specimen and traverses posterolaterally. The specimen is received with \u000aa radiograph demonstrating the localizing wire in place within a small cluster \u000aof calcifications centrally. Cut surfaces demonstrate a band of \u000afibromembranous tissue at the lateral end of the specimen that is maximally REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in greatest dimension and occupies 20% of the total specimen. There are no \u000adiscrete lesions grossly. The entire specimen is sequentially submitted from \u000amedial to lateral, with the likely area of calcifications in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000athrough  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (per radiograph). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen, sequentially from medial to lateral, multiple \u000afragments, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Lateral architectural distortion", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 2.8cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating \u000asuperior (short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins. The specimen is \u000ainked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/ orange. Localizing wire enters the lateral aspect of the specimen and \u000aexits medially. The accompanying radiograph demonstrates the localizing wire \u000ain place adjacent to a faint central area of distortion. Sectioning \u000ademonstrates at least 90% tan/white soft, lobulated fibrous tissue without \u000adiscrete masses, lesions, or other abnormalities grossly. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen, sequentially, multi frags, ESS. \u000aDB/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a10/29/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
