VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Leona A. Doyle, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION": \u000aPrior excision/biopsy site changes. \u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium. \u000aApocrine metaplasia and cysts. \u000aColumnar cell change. \u000aNo residual DCIS. \u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 52 year old woman with multiple breast biopsy in past. History of ADH. \u000aExcision wire loc. REMOVED_DATE showed DCIS in lateral sample with close middle and \u000alateral margins. Second site biopsied same dated showed atypical hyperplasia. \u000aOperation: Left breast re-excision partial mastectomy. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast DCIS. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Left breast tissue - short stitch superior, long stitch lateral. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and medical \u000arecord number, and "#1. Left breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch \u000alateral", and consists of a 21 g lumpectomy specimen (3.1cm medial to lateral, \u000a5.1cm superior to inferior, and 2.6cm anterior to posterior). The specimen \u000ais received oriented with short stitch designating superior aspect and long \u000astitch lateral aspect, and inked by surgeon per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is an attached skin \u000aellipse on the lateral surface (3.1 x 0.4cm ) with no gross lesions. There is \u000aan excision cavity (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ) which is present 0.2cm to superior \u000amargin, 0.5cm to medial margin, 0.6cm to lateral and anterior margins, 1.1cm \u000ato posterior margin, and 2.7cm to the inferior margin. Surrounding the \u000aexcision cavity, there is firm fibrous tissue and focal fat necrosis extending \u000aover an area of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.6cm  focally present at the anterior, inferior, \u000aposterior and superior margins, 0.6cm to lateral margin and 0.4cm to the \u000amedial margin. The entire specimen is submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Excision cavity and closest margins, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining margins, multi frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aLDO/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 03,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11:20:56AM \u000a[report_end] 
