VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Wai Chin Foo, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS: \u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, low grade, (3.9cm ) \u000aStroma is moderately cellular, and stromal overgrowth is present. \u000aMitoses number up to 2 per 10 hpfs. \u000aNo necrosis is present. \u000aNo heterologous elements are present. \u000aThe tumor has predominantly pushing borders but with focal infiltration into \u000aadipose tissue. \u000aTumor is extensively present at the lateral margin, very close to (<0.1cm ) the \u000asuperior and medial margins, 0.1cm from the inferior and posterior margins, \u000aand 0.4cm from the anterior margin. \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia involves the tumor. \u000aNOTE: Case also reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, breast pathology service, who \u000aconcurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aClinical History: A 34-year-old female with right breast mass, core biopsy \u000areveals fibroadenoma. \u000aOperation: Right breast excisional biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast fibroadenoma. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right breast excision biopsy short suture superior, long suture lateral. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit \u000anumber, and "right breast excision biopsy short suture superior, long suture \u000alateral ", and consists of a portion of tan/pink/yellow fibroadipose tissue \u000a(4.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.2cm ) with two orienting sutures ("short - superior; long - \u000alateral"). The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of \u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; \u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from \u000aanterior to posterior, exhibiting a white/pink, rubbery, encapsulated, \u000alobulated mass (3.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ) which extends to the superior, lateral \u000amargin, 0.1cm of the inferior margin and medial margins. The remaining tissue \u000aconsists of tan/white fibrous stroma. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast tissue, (sequentially from anterior to posterior), multi \u000afrags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aDFI/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a3/3/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
