VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Elizabeth A. Steensma, M.D.; Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS: \u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA is present (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; multiple levels examined). \u000aFibroadenoma (0.5cm  see note). \u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine cysts and calcifications present in \u000aassociation with benign epithelium. \u000aNOTE: This case is reviewed in conjunction with the previous core needle \u000abiopsy. Findings are best interpreted as fibroadenoma. No histologic features \u000aof phyllodes tumor are seen (see previous core needle biopsy reviewed at BWH as \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aImmunohistochemistry for p63 demonstrates intact myoepithelium in a sclerotic \u000alobule (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 51-year-old woman with density on screening mammogram, ultrasound \u000acore biopsy positive fibroepithelial proliferative lesion with adenosis, could \u000anot rule out phyllodes tumor. \u000aOperation: R breast needle localization. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast abnormal mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Rt breast, right tissue - stitch short superior and long lateral. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Spoke with Dr. Lockhart; intact hookwire and hypoechoic lesion are \u000acontained within the specimen, confirmed on US. - Rachna Madan. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue, stitch short - superior, long - lateral", and \u000aconsists of a portion of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (4.6 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm ) \u000awith two orienting sutures (short - superior; long - lateral) and a hookwire in \u000aplaced (entering at the lateral aspect and exiting anteriorly). The specimen \u000ais inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/ orange. The tissue is serially sectioned from medial to lateral, \u000aexhibiting a tan/white, papillary, nodular to cystic lesion (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), which grossly extends to the anterior margin, comes to within 0.1cm of \u000athe inferior margin, 0.6cm of the superior margin, 1.0cm of the posterior \u000amargin, 1.0cm of the lateral margin, and approximately 3.0cm of the medial \u000amargin. Approximately 0.9cm medial and posterior to the aforementioned \u000alesion, is a unilocular smooth, white clear fluid filled cyst (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). There is dense fibrous tissue adjacent to both lesions. The specimen is \u000aaccompanied by a radiograph, which is examined by radiology, confirming an \u000a"intact hookwire and hypoechoic lesion" present within the specimen. Entirely \u000asubmitted for histologic examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast tissue, sequentially from medial to lateral, multi frags, \u000aESS. \u000aPapillary cystic lesion in micros  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aCystic smooth wall lesion in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aDFI/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
