 ). The specimens are serially sectioned to reveal 50% yellow \u000alobulated adipose tissue, and 50% dense white fibrous tissue, with no discrete \u000amasses or lesions identified. Representative sections of the skin and fibrous \u000atissue are submitted. \u000aAfter examination of the initial 2 blocks of tissue, the specimen was \u000are-examined grossly and 8 additional representative blocks of tissue were \u000asubmitted for histologic analysis. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin and fibrous tissue, 3 frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional breast tissue, multi frags, RSS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left breast tissue", consists of multiple yellow lobulated \u000airregular portions of fibrofatty tissue, with overlying and separately received \u000atan wrinkled unremarkable skin fragments (615 grams, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm ). \u000aThe specimens are serially sectioned to reveal 50% yellow lobulated adipose \u000atissue, and 50% dense white fibrous tissue, with no discrete masses or lesions \u000aidentified. Representative sections of the skin and fibrous tissue are \u000asubmitted. \u000aAfter examination of the initial 2 blocks of tissue, the specimen was \u000are-examined grossly and 8 additional representative blocks of tissue were \u000asubmitted for histologic analysis. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin and fibrous tissue, 3 frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional breast tissue, multi frags, RSS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000acp/elw \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a7/31/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
