VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast biopsy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Christian J. Davidson, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED: LEFT BREAST SUPERIOR (UIQ), EXCISION FOR \u000aCALCIFICATIONS: \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread. \u000aColumnar Cell hyperplasia with associated calcifications and atypia. \u000aApocrine metaplasia. \u000aPapilloma with epithelial hyperplasia. \u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED: INFERIOR AND POSTERIOR LEFT BREAST TISSUE, EXCISION \u000aFOR TWO CLUSTERS OF CALCIFICATIONS. \u000aCalcifications associated with columnar cell change. \u000aFocus of fat necrosis suggestive of prior biopsy site changes. \u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. D. Dillon of the Breast Pathology service, \u000awho concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: CA of lt breast. Now with 3 newly recognized clusters of calcs. \u000aOperation: Wire-directed excision. \u000aOperative Findings: See Op Note. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Three newly recognized clusters of calcs. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) tissue, left breast - 'superior' (UIQ) - mammography. \u000aB/2) inferior and posterior left breast tissue - mammo (wire with pigtail is \u000ainferior, short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral). \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aSpecimen #1: Ca++ in specimen/OR called - DGS. \u000aSpecimen #2: Two (2) clusters of Ca++/OR called - DGS. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and medical record number. \u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Tissue, left breast - "superior" (UIQ) - mammography", \u000aconsists of one wire-localized breast excisional biopsy with a short stitch \u000adesignating superior and a long stitch designating lateral. The wire enters \u000athe specimen at the superior aspect of the lateral margin. The entire specimen \u000ameasures 3.4cm superior to inferior, 1.4cm anterior to posterior, and 5.5cm \u000amedial to lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. Sectioning of the specimen into \u000aeight slices reveals a white/tan, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm mass consistent with the \u000aarea marked by the radiologist. The mass is in slices #3, #4, and #5. No \u000aother masses or abnormalities are noted. The entire specimen is submitted for \u000ahistologic analysis. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #1 (medial tip), perpendicular sections, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, 1 frag total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #8 (lateral tip), 3 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Inferior and posterior left breast tissue", consists of \u000aone wire-localized breast excisional biopsy measuring 4.6cm superior to \u000ainferior, 1.6cm anterior to posterior, and 4.9cm medial to lateral. The \u000ashort stitch has been designated superior, the long stitch lateral, and the \u000awire with the pigtail inferior (per the surgeon). Two wires exit/enter the \u000aspecimen. The pigtailed wire enters the specimen at the junction of the \u000aanterior and inferior margins. The other wire enters the specimen at the \u000ajunction of the anterior and superior margins, while it exits at the junction \u000aof the superior and medial aspects. The specimen is inked per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; \u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is \u000asectioned from lateral to medial into nine slices. The radiograph received \u000awith the specimen has two areas of microcalcification circled. The first \u000amicrocalcification area is marked by the pigtail wire and is seen in slices #3 \u000aand #4, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  This area of microcalcification comes \u000awithin 0.3cm of the medial margin. It otherwise is far from the other \u000amargins. The area of calcification marked by the straight wire is seen in \u000aslices #6, #7, and #8, as a white/tan REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm lesion. The lesion \u000agrossly extends to the superior, anterior, and medial margins. No other \u000alesions are grossly identified. The entire specimen is submitted for \u000ahistologic analysis. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #1 (lateral margin), perpendicular, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #8, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #9 (medial margin), perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aCJD/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed \u000aon Friday February 20,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03:51:32PM \u000aA. ADDENDUM FOR SPECIMEN DESIGNATED: LEFT BREAST SUPERIOR (UIQ), EXCISION FOR \u000aCALCIFICATIONS: \u000aIn addition to the findings mentioned above, there is also a single focus of \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (Block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aB. ADDENDUM FOR SPECIMEN DESIGNATED: INFERIOR AND POSTERIOR LEFT BREAST \u000aTISSUE, EXCISION FOR TWO CLUSTERS OF CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aTwo foci of calcifications are identified in this excision. One focus is \u000aassociated with the biopsy site changes and the second focus is associated with \u000athe area of columnar cell change. \u000aAddendum #1 by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aFriday February 20,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06:48:26PM \u000a[report_end] 
