VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOGINO, SHUJI, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D. \u000a1) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT WIRE LOCALIZATION": \u000aColumnar hyperplasia with epithelial atypia and calcifications. \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with calcifications. \u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE, SUPERIOR MEDIAL SHAVE MARGIN": \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with calcifications. \u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aNOTE: The case was reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, Breast Pathology, who \u000aconcurs. \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aCore biopsy site is present (block #4). \u000aThe diagnosis remains unchanged. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Left abnormal mammogram status post stereotactic core \u000abiopsy showing CAPSS and ALH. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left wire localization, short superior, long lateral \u000awhip stitch deep margin. \u000a#2. Left breast tissue, superior medial shaved margin, \u000awhip stitch new margin. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RUCKER-SCHMIDT,RACHEL L.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, sublabeled "Left wire localized breast biopsy, short stitch superior, \u000along stitch lateral, whip stitch deep margin", consists of a wire localized \u000abreast excision specimen (3.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm ) which includes two sutures placed \u000aby the surgeon to designate the superior and lateral margin of the specimen. \u000aThe specimen is received previously inked by the surgeon as follows: red = \u000asuperior, green = inferior, blue = anterior, black = posterior, yellow = \u000alateral, and orange = medial. The specimen contains a localization wire, but \u000ano radiograph accompanied the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned \u000afrom medial to lateral to reveal dense fibrotic tan/white tissue admixed with \u000agolden yellow fatty tissue (approximately 75% fibrous tissue and 25% fatty \u000atissue) which is centrally hemorrhagic. No gross masses are identified. The \u000aspecimen is entirely serially submitted for microscopic examination. \u000aMicro 1: Medial and inferior margin, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Remainder of specimen, multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, sublabeled "Left breast tissue - superior medial shave margin, whip \u000astitch new margin", consists of a breast shave excision specimen (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.1cm ) which contains a suture placed by the surgeon to designate the new \u000amargin. This new margin is inked in black and the old margin is inked in blue. \u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal no gross masses. The specimen is \u000aapproximately 50% dense fibrous tissue and 50% yellow adipose tissue. The \u000aentire specimen is submitted for microscopic examination. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Superior medial shave margin, 2 frags each, ESS. \u000arlr \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
