VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES) \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, 4:00, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A WELL \u000aCIRCUMSCRIBED MASS WITH MIXED ECHOGENICITY: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (best seen on additional deeper levels) \u000a(see note). \u000aPseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia (PASH). \u000aAdenosis with columnar cell change. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aNote: ADH is best evaluated with excision. PASH can be associated with \u000aradiologic densities, but the histologic findings are not specific for a \u000amass forming lesion. Radiologic correlation is suggested to ensure that \u000athe biopsies are representative of the radiologic lesion. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, 9:30, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A CIRCUMSCRIBED \u000aMASS WITH MIXED ECHOGENICITY AND CYSTIC SPACES: \u000aPASH (see note). \u000aAdenosis with columnar cell change. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aNote: PASH can be associated with radiologic densities, but the \u000ahistologic findings are not specific for a mass forming lesion. \u000aRadiologic correlation is suggested to ensure the biopsy is representative \u000aof the radiologic lesion. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Left solid, mixed echogenic mass, well circumscribed at 4:00. \u000aRight solid, mixed echogenic mass with multiple cystic spaces, circumscribed at \u000a9:30. \u000aOperation: 11 G Stereotatic. \u000aOperative findings: Left breast mass. Right breast mass. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral solid masses. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast - pink cassette. \u000a#2. Right breast - Green cassette. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WITKIEWICZ,AGNIESKA K.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the \u000apatient's name, unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "Left breast", in a pink cassette, and consists of multiple, \u000asoft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm in \u000aaggregate). \u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, labeled "Right breast", in a green cassette, and consists of \u000amultiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm in \u000aaggregate). \u000aMicro 2: Multi frags, ESS. \u000adf \u000aReports to: BABAGBEMI, TOKUNBO M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES) \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES) \u000a[report_end] 
