VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, NEEDLE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS: \u000aConsistent with mammary hamartoma (6.4cm maximum dimension); see NOTE. \u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia (block #3) and atypical lobular \u000ahyperplasia (block #1). \u000aFibroadenoma (block #30; 0.5cm ). \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aLEFT BREAST, NEEDLE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS: \u000aConsistent with mammary hamartoma (4.8cm maximum dimension); see NOTE. \u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia (block #12). \u000aCore biopsy site changes. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aNOTE: \u000aThe lesions on both sides are histologically similar. The masses are relatively \u000awell circumscribed, with dense stroma with extensive pseudomyelomatous stromal \u000ahyperplastic changes (PASH), multiple cysts, and distorted lobules. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aOperation: Bilateral needle directed breast biopsies. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral abnormal mammograms. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000a#1. Rt needle directed breast biopsy - mammo stitches short superior, long \u000alateral. \u000a#2. Lt needle directed breast biopsy - mammo stitches short superior, long \u000alateral. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,PRISCILLA S.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "Right needle directed breast biopsies - stitch short \u000asuperior, long lateral", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm fibrofatty breast \u000atissue with a localizing wire in place and an accompanying radiograph. There \u000ais a short suture designating superior and long suture designating lateral. \u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral \u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned (12 slices) to \u000areveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm dense white fibrous tissue, with diffuse cystic \u000achanges, which extends to all margins. The remaining parenchyma is yellow \u000alobulated fatty tissue. Representative sections are submitted sequentially \u000afrom medial (slice 1) to lateral (slice 12) as follows: \u000aMicro 1: Fibrous tissue to medial margin (slice 1), 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 2: Fibrous tissue to anterior margin (slice 2), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 3: Fibrous tissue to superior margin (slice 3), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 4: Fibrous tissue to anterior/inferior margin (slice 4), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 5: Fibrous tissue to inferior margin (slice 5), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 6: Fibrous tissue to anterior margin (slice 6), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 7: Fibrous tissue to anterior margin (slice 7), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 8: Fibrous tissue to posterior margin (slice 9), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 9: Fibrous tissue to posterior/inferior margin (slice 10), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 10: Fibrous tissue to lateral margin (slice 12), 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Additional fibrous tissue, multi frags, RSS. \u000aPart two, labeled "Left needle directed breast biopsy - stitch short superior, \u000along lateral", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.9cm fibrofatty breast tissue with \u000aa localizing wire in place and an accompanying radiograph. There is a short \u000asuture designating superior and long suture designating lateral. The specimen \u000ais inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = \u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; \u000amedial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned (16 slices) to reveal a \u000atan/white dense fibrous mass with diffuse fibrocystic changes (4.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) which grossly extends to all margins, except for the lateral margin (2cm \u000aaway). Representative sections are submitted sequentially from medial (slice \u000a1) to lateral (slice 16) as follows: \u000aMicro 11: Fibrous tissue to medial margin (slice 1), 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 12: Fibrous tissue to superior margin (slice 2), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 13: Fibrous tissue to superior, anterior, posterior margin (slice 4), 1 \u000afrag, RSS. \u000aMicro 14: Fibrous tissue to anterior and posterior margins (slice 5), 1 frag, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro 15: Fibrous tissue to anterior margin (slice 6), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 16: Fibrous tissue to anterior margin (slice 7), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 17: Fibrous tissue to superior, anterior, posterior margins at area of \u000awire (slice 9), 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 18: Fibrous tissue to inferior, anterior, posterior margins (slice 10), 1 \u000afrag, RSS. \u000aMicro 19: Fibrous tissue to inferior, anterior, posterior margins (slice 11), 1 \u000afrag, RSS. \u000aMicro 20: Uninvolved lateral margin (slice 15-16), 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Additional fibrous tissue, multi frags, RSS. \u000alm \u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
