VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR A DENSITY: \u000aEXTENSIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present. \u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA is present (levels examined; best seen in \u000adeeper levels of block 5). \u000aRuptured cyst with chronic inflammation and histiocytic response. \u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aNote: There are two small areas (each measuring less than 0.1cm ) \u000asuspicious for microinvasion (blocks 5 and 15). These areas are only \u000apresent on the original slides and are not present on the deeper levels. \u000aThese areas were reviewed at the staff conference. Although suspicious \u000afor microinvasion, a definitive diagnosis cannot be made. \u000aNo definitive invasive carcinoma or DCIS are seen after complete \u000amicroscopic evaluation of the specimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: History of lobular cancer in situ in the right breast. \u000aOperation: Left needle directed breast biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left abnormal mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast wire localization biopsy. \u000aMammography report: Lesion and wire are in the specimen. E.P.Frost. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by MAGI GALLUZZI,CRISTINA,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000aunit number, and "left breast wire, localization biopsy", and received together \u000awith the specimen is a specimen radiograph showing a poorly defined hyper-dense \u000aarea with adjacent needle wire. The specimen consists of a segment of \u000afibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm and weighing 36 grams. The \u000awire is present in the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol \u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = \u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The cut surface of \u000athe specimen shows a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm yellow-gray, poorly defined firm area. \u000aFew cysts and hemorrhage are present in the area. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm \u000ayellow-tan, round firm nodule is present in the center of the area described. \u000aThe nodule is 0.5cm from the inferior and anterior margin, 0.7cm from the \u000aposterior margin, 2.0cm from the superior margin, 2.2cm from the lateral \u000amargin and 3.2cm from the medial margin. The area is described is at the \u000aposterior, superior, inferior and anterior resection margins. Scattered area \u000aof possible fat necrosis are present in proximity to the lateral portion of the \u000apoorly defined area. The entire specimen is submitted for microscopic \u000aevaluation. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  nodule described, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  parenchyma adjacent to the nodule, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  poorly defined area, multi frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  possible areas of fat necrosis, 4 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 17: medial resection margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 18: lateral resection margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of tissue, mult frags, ESS. \u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
