VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Jane E Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION BIOPSY FOR MICROCALCIFICATIONS: \u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia in association with \u000amicrocalcifications, present adjacent to core biopsy site \u000achanges, best seen in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a(Levels examined.) \u000aColumnar cell change. \u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium and cysts. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aNOTE: \u000aDr. D. Dillon (Breast Pathology Service) reviewed the case and concurs with the \u000adiagnosis. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Right breast calcifications and atypical ductal hyperplasia on \u000astereotactic core biopsy. \u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized biopsy x2 wires. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast calcifications; right breast atypical ductal \u000ahyperplasia. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000a(1) Right breast wire-localized biopsy x2 wires; short suture - superior; long \u000asuture - lateral. \u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: \u000aCalcifications/clip/both distal hook wires, all included. \u000a- A. Huang/ R. Birdwell \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number, \u000aand "1. Right breast wire-localized biopsy x2 wires, short suture - superior, \u000along suture - lateral", and consists of a wire-localized breast excision [4.2 \u000acm from superior to inferior, 4.1cm from lateral to medial, 2.2cm from \u000aanterior to posterior]. The specimen is received with 2 wires, which enter \u000asuperiorly and exits inferoposteriorly. The specimen has two orienting \u000asutures. The specimen is received with a radiograph, which demonstrates a clip \u000aand two wires and multiple microcalcifications. The specimen is inked per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. \u000aSectioning reveals approximately 40% firm, fibrous tissue with numerous, small \u000acysts [up to 0.2cm in greatest diameter], located mostly inferiorly. A core \u000abiopsy site is identified [0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ], which is located 1cm from the \u000alateral margin, 0.8cm from the posterior margin, 1.2cm from the anterior \u000amargin, 1.4cm from the superior margin, 2.8cm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the inferior margin. The clip is not seen. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted, with the core biopsy site in Micros  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The specimen is \u000asubmitted from superior to inferior. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast excision, multiple fragment, ESS. \u000ajeb/MMM \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Jane E Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a3/23/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
