VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ISHA A MUSTAFA M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Stephanie Schulte, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Massimo F Loda, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY": \u000aBenign breast tissue with fibrosis and biopsy site changes. \u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aOperation: Left breast wire localized breast biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast atypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Left breast biopsy, short superior, long lateral. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aWire, clip, incidental calcs are in the specimen. Called to OR. D/W Dr. \u000aRaza. D/W. Mimi, OR nurse. Arnold, resident. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1. Left breast biopsy short superior, long lateral", and consists of a \u000a6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.8cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, which exhibits a 3.7cm \u000adefect along the lateral aspect (1.5cm in depth) extending from the anterior \u000ato the posterior surface. The localizing wire enters anteriorly and is exposed \u000ain the area of this defect. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for \u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen was inked by the \u000aprosector, to avoid the previously described defect, which likely does not \u000arepresent true surgical margin. Sectioning demonstrates dense tan/white \u000alobulated fibrous tissue (25-30% of the specimen). There is a \u000awell-circumscribed tan/pink REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm nodule, likely consistent with \u000aintraparenchymal lymph node, which is marked by a surgical clip, in the area of \u000athe localizing wire. The specimen is received along with an accompanying \u000aradiograph demonstrating the localizing wire and clip in place within the \u000aspecimen, along with incidental calcifications in this area. \u000aThe presumed lymph node is 0.1cm from the closest anterior margin, 0.4cm from \u000athe closest medial margin, at least 1.4cm from the closest inferior margin, \u000aand 1.9cm from the closest posterior margin. The distance to the nearest true \u000alateral margin cannot be determined, due to the previously mentioned defect. \u000aThe closest inked lateral surface is within 0.8cm  The entire specimen is \u000asubmitted sequentially from inferomedial to superolateral, with area of \u000ainterest in micro-cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and tissue with surgical clip in micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen, sequentially submitted, multi frags, ESS. \u000aNOTE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID inferior, medial;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID posterior, inferior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID medial, inferior, \u000aposterior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID medial, anterior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID medial, inferior, anterior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID medial, \u000aposterior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID medial, anterior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID medial, anterior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID posterior, superior, \u000aanterior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID posterior, medial;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID superior, posterior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID superior, \u000aposterior, lateral;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID superior, posterior, lateral;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID superior, anterior; \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID superior, anterior, lateral;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID lateral;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID superior, anterior, lateral. \u000aDB/mmm \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Massimo F Loda M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
