nal biopsy, short superior, long \u000alateral", consists of wire-localized breast excision (4.4cm superior to \u000ainferior, 5.1cm medial to lateral, 1.3cm anterior to posterior) with a short \u000astitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral. The \u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. An accompanying radiograph demonstrates a localization wire \u000aentering the superolateral aspect of the specimen and exiting the medial aspect \u000aof the specimen with few calcifications scattered in the specimen. The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior in nine slices to \u000areveal a red/brown hemorrhagic area (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ) with associated firm \u000afibrous tissue in slices #1 through #3 and is located less than 0.1cm from the \u000amedial margin, 2.3cm from the lateral margin, grossly abuts the posterior \u000amargin, 0.4cm from the anterior margin, grossly abuts the superior margin, and \u000a2.0cm from the inferior margin. The specimen is entirely submitted for \u000ahistological examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, perpendicular, 13 frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Specimen from superior-inferior, multi frags, ESS (micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000acorrespond to one slice transected in half.) \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin, perpendicular, 7 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, "right breast, medial margin", consists of two soft tissue fragments \u000a(3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm in aggregate) that are previously inked blue on one aspect \u000aand black on the other aspect of the specimen per surgeon. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, perpendicular, 7 frags each, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aDP/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on Tuesday \u000aFebruary 10,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06:11:55PM \u000a[report_end] 
