VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Oname O. Burlingame, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP MARKING A CORE \u000aSITE: \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU. \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (best seen adjacent to core site; block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aColumnar cell change. \u000aIntraductal papillomas. \u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast epithelium. \u000aNOTE: No invasive cancer or disease seen after complete microscopic evaluation \u000aof the specimen. \u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who \u000aconcurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 52-year-old female with abnormal right mammogram, REMOVED_DATE \u000amammogram - right breast - "heterogeneous calc in UOQ" - demonstrates \u000asuspicious abnl - REMOVED_DATE - right breast core biopsy - "adenosis with \u000acolumnar cell change and atypia, including micro papillae, with calcifications \u000a(atypia best excised). \u000aOperation: R breast WL Bx. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. R breast tissue, stitches; short superior, long lateral, whip chest wall. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aCalled to Dr. Rhei, 2:45 pm. Calcs & intact wire in specimen. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen, Part A, is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit \u000anumber, and "#1. R breast tissue", and consists of a breast excision specimen \u000a(4.2cm superior-inferior, 3.7cm anterior-posterior, 1.8cm medial-lateral) \u000awith a short stitch indicating the superior margin, a long stitch indicating \u000athe lateral margin and a whip stitch indicating the chest wall margins \u000a(posterior, black). A localization wire enters the specimen at the \u000ainferior-anterior aspect and exits at the posterior margin. The specimen is \u000areceived previously inked, per pathology protocol for the evaluation of \u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; \u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The breast parenchyma is 50% fibrous and 50% \u000aadipose tissue. A clip is identified next to the localization wire. No \u000alesions or masses are identified. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph \u000asharing a clip, scattered calcifications and an intact wire in specimen. The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned, approximately superior to inferior and entirely \u000asubmitted for histologic examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, perpendicular, submitted approximately posterior \u000ato anterior, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential sections from superior to inferior with wire in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , \u000aclip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and complete sections in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; \u000a1-3 frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin, perpendicular, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aOOB/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a4/6/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
