he wire was removed prior to sectioning. The external \u000asurface of the fragment was inked in black. The fragments are yellow/tan \u000afibroadipose tissue. The largest piece, with the wire needle, shows an open \u000acavity at the needle site. Cut sections reveal a white fibrous area with \u000afocal hemorrhage (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm ). No mass is grossly identified. The \u000aentire specimen is submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Left breast tissue, REMOVED_DATE frag/cass, ESS \u000atlp \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
