ted calcifications are within the specimen. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Lt breast needle localization ", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a2.2cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented with sutures designating \u000asuperior (short suture), lateral (long suture), and chest wall (whipstitch) \u000amargins. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of \u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; \u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by surgeon). A localizing wire enters the \u000asuperior aspect of the specimen and exits the inferior aspect. Specimen is \u000areceived with a radiograph demonstrating localizing wire in place within an \u000aill-defined central area of scattered calcifications. Note: Calcifications \u000aappear to extend to at least one edge of the specimen. Sectioning demonstrates \u000a30-40% tan/white lobulated fibrous tissue without obvious masses, lesions or \u000aother abnormalities grossly. Entire specimen is sequentially submitted from \u000asuperior to inferior following further fixation. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen, multi frags, ESS (perpendicular superior margin \u000ain  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and perpendicular inferior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. L axillary skin mass", consists of a 1.3cm shaved \u000averrucous lesion with a 0.1cm base. Base is inked, specimen is sectioned and \u000aentirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags, ESS. \u000aDB/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated 