am. Wire and tissue \u000apresent ? wire within an oval small mass by US. Dr. Robyn Birdwell. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patients \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast tissue", consists of one fragment of fibroadipose \u000atissue measuring 4.0cm from superior to inferior margin, 3.1cm from medial to \u000alateral margin and 1.9cm from anterior to posterior margin. There is a short \u000asuture designated as superior, long suture designated as lateral, whip stitch \u000adesignated as deep and a blue bowtie designated as the divided duct. The \u000aspecimen was inked by surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of \u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; \u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is a wire entering through the lateral \u000ainferior margin. The specimen radiograph shows the wire and a vague dense area \u000acircled by the radiologist. No definitive mass lesion is seen. \u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from anterior (blue tie) to posterior \u000a(perpendicular to the blue tie) to reveal 10% fibrous tissue and 90% adipose \u000atissue. No mass is grossly identified. The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial, superior and anterior margins, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial, superior and anterior margins, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Bisected anterior, medial, superior and inferior margins, 2 \u000afrags, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Bisected superior, inferior, anterior and posterior margins,2 \u000afrags, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Wire tip, bisected to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , posterior and inferior margins, 1 \u000afrag, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Bisected to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , superior, posterior and lateral margins, 1 \u000afrags, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Wire tip, bisected to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , lateral and inferior margins \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Bisected to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , superior, posterior and lateral margins \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral, inferior and superior margins, 2 frags, ESS \u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast tissue behind nipple", consists of one fragment of \u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  The entire \u000aspecimen is submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Left breast tissue behind nipple, 1 frag, ESS \u000aECH/cdm \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Eric C Huang M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a2/27/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
