. The FDA has determined that such \u000aclearance or approval is not necessary. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHISTORY: 54 year-old with new solid mass LI 30 axis \u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING: \u000a1. Left: irregular mass. \u000aLOCATION: \u000a1. Left: upper outer \u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY: \u000a1. 14G Ultrasound \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000a1. 14G Ultrasound Left breast - Pink cassette 9:50 am time in formalin \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in one part, labeled with the patient's \u000aname, unit number and "left breast", consists of a pink cassette which contains \u000amultiple irregular tan-pink fibrofatty tissue cores (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.1cm in \u000aaggregate) which are submitted in toto. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Tissues received in pink cassette, multi frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aLMC/ajb \u000aInterpretation: \u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following \u000acriteria: \u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the \u000acarcinoma is reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet \u000abeen determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a \u000aportion of the membrane is positive. \u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of \u000atumor cells or moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in < 30% \u000aof tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 30% \u000aof tumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate immunoreactivity. \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Friday \u000aFebruary 05,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01:52:14PM \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (2/10/10) \u000aFISH was performed by Clarient using the PathVysion HER-2 DNA Probe Kit with \u000athe following (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aResults: NOT AMPLIFIED \u000aHER-2/CEP-17 ratio = 1 \u000aThe average of HER-2 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average centromere 17 copies per cell: 2 \u000aREFERENCE RANGE: \u000aNOT AMPLIFIED HER-2/CEP-17 ratio < REMOVED_DATE \u000aEQUIVOCAL HER-2/CEP-17 ratio REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE \u000aAMPLIFIED  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /CEP-17 ratio > REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by Amy Ly M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday February 11, \u000a REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 10:08:39AM \u000a[report_end] 
