yellow, medial orange. No orienting sutures are present. The specimen measures \u000a4.8cm medial to lateral, 4.8cm superior to inferior, and 1.6cm anterior to \u000aposterior. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a localization \u000awire entering the specimen and associated with both a metal clip and a cluster \u000aof calcification of the medial aspect of the specimen. The localization wire \u000aenters the specimen laterally and extends to the medial aspect. The \u000alocalization wire is associated with firm fibrous breast parenchyma with \u000ahemorrhage and biopsy site changes and a small metallic clip, extending over an \u000aarea of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm  which is present at the inferior margin, 0.8cm to \u000athe medial margin, 0.5cm to the posterior margin, 0.6cm to the anterior \u000amargin, 1.0cm to the lateral margin, and 2.7cm to the superior margin. The \u000aremaining breast parenchyma is 50% fibrous and 50% adipose tissue with no \u000aadditional gross lesions identified. The entire specimen is submitted to \u000ainclude the clip site and closets margins and all remaining tissue. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast parenchyma surrounding clip site (clip located in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) \u000ato include closest inferior and anterior margins, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Closest lateral margin, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Deep and inferior margins, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining anterior margin, 2 frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining medial margin, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining breast parenchyma, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aLDO/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed \u000aon Tuesday February 24,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04:50:49PM \u000a[report_end] 
