margins, and approximately 40% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. \u000aA small metal clip is identified within the dense fibrous tissue in the \u000ainferior portion of the specimen. No discrete masses are identified. The \u000aspecimen is entirely sequentially submitted from inferior to superior. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin perpendicularly sectioned, 3 frags in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central specimen to include dense/nodular/cystic fibrous tissue \u000a(clip identified within tissue in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), 1 frag in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags total, \u000aESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aLMB/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a2/21/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
