VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000a#1 RIGHT AXILLARY HOT SENTINEL NODE (INCLUDING FSA): \u000aOne (1) lymph node with no tumor seen (3 H&E levels examined). \u000a#2 RIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION: \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present. \u000aBiopsy site with reprair reaction. \u000aNOTE: No residual invasive carcinoma is seen after microscopic \u000aexamination of the specimen including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 59 yo surgically postmenopausal female who recently discontinued \u000ahormone replacement therapy whose REMOVED_DATE screening mammogram demonstrates \u000aa R breast UOQ increased density. S/p REMOVED_DATE (R) breast excision \u000arevealing 4-5cm infiltrating lobular carcinoma with positive margins. \u000aOperation: R breast re-excision, sentinel node biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. R axillary hot sentinel node, >500 - FS. \u000a2. R breast re-excision partial mastectomy. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1) R AXILLARY NODE HOT SENTINEL": \u000aLymph node; no tumor present. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RIVERA,MIGUEL N,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, labeled with the patient's name, \u000aand unit number. \u000aPart one is labeled "right axillary sentinel node". The specimen consists of a \u000asingle fragment of yellow fatty soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  The \u000aspecimen is bisected and one-half is submitted as FSA. \u000aMicro 1: FSA remnant and non frozen remnant (inked black), 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 2: additional fat, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart two is labeled 'right breast re-excision partial mastectomy". The \u000aspecimen consists of a single fragment of fibroadipose tissue measuring 5cm \u000afrom medial to lateral, 4.5cm from superior to inferior and 6.5cm from \u000aanterior to posterior. The anterior aspect of the skin ellipse (2.2 x 0.3cm ) \u000ahas a well healed scar (1.9cm in length). The specimen is inked by the \u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = \u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; \u000amedial = orange. Two (2)cm deep to the scar there is an area consistent with \u000abiopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm  This area is adjacent to the \u000amedial margin and the superior margin. The area is 3cm from the inferior \u000amargin, 3.5cm from the lateral margin, 2cm from the anterior margin (skin) \u000aand 3.2cm from the posterior margin. Representative sections are submitted \u000afor histologic evaluation. \u000aMicro 3: skin to biopsy cavity (anterior margin), 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire biopsy cavity with closest margin (superior and medial), 10 \u000afrags, ESS. \u000aMicro 10: additional superior and medial margins, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 11: additional anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 12: posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 13: inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 14: lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aNOTE: The specimen is approximately 70% fat and 30% fibrous tissue. All \u000afibrous tissue has been submitted. \u000amir \u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000a[report_end] 
