VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Peter M Sadow, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aSYNOPSIS: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present \u000aTypes - Solid, comedo and cribriform \u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate to high \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - No \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Yes \u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent \u000aExtent of DCIS - REMOVED_DATE blocks \u000aFinal Margins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (>0.3cm) - Anterior, posterior, medial, lateral, superior, inferior \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU Absent \u000aOTHER FINDINGS: \u000aBiopsy site changes with dystrophic calcifications \u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis (DCIS) p REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  MX \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Left breast DCIS, S/P needle core biopsy for calcification. \u000aOperation: Left breast wire localized lumpectomy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast DCIS. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1 - left breast mass with wire - short suture/superior; long suture/lateral \u000a(mammo). \u000aRADIOGRAPHY REPORT: Clip, calcifications wire are in specimen. Called to OR. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number, \u000aand "#1 - left breast mass", and consists of a left breast excision specimen, \u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.8cm  There are two sutures that are placed by the \u000asurgeon, one designating the superior portion of the specimen, and one \u000adesignating the lateral portion of the specimen. There is a wire entering into \u000athe superior portion of the specimen, adjacent to the superior suture. The \u000aspecimen is received with a radiograph, which shows a wire, a clip and \u000acalcifications within the tissue. The specimen is inked by the pathology \u000aresident according the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. Upon section, the specimen is mostly yellow, lobulated, fatty \u000abreast tissue. There are focal areas of white dense fibrosis, in addition to \u000agel beads placed at the site of the former needle core biopsy. The specimen is \u000aradiographed to reveal a clip and calcifications. Due to fibrosis present \u000athroughout the excision specimen, the specimen is serially sectioned and \u000aentirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : breast excision, serially sectioned, 1 frag in each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : breast excision with calcifications localized by \u000aradiograph, \u000a1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : non-calcified half of slice from  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : breast, slice with clip, 1 and 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice with additional calcifications, 1 frag in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : remainder of breast specimen, serially sectioned, 1 frag in \u000aeach, ESS. \u000aPES/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a9/26/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
