VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (block 4, levels examined) (see NOTE). \u000aMicrocalcifications are present in association with atypical ductal \u000ahyperplasia and benign epithelium. \u000aFibrous breast tissue with foreign material in histiocytes, suggestive of \u000aa remote biopsy site. \u000aNOTE: The specimen radiograph did not reveal definite calcifications. \u000aClinical correlation is suggested. \u000aThe area of atypical ductal hyperplasia approaches a diagnosis of ductal \u000acarcinoma in situ. However, due to the small size and the qualitative \u000afeatures of the proliferation, atypical ductal hyperplasia is favored. \u000aThe atypical ductal hyperplasia is 0.2cm from the margin. The atypical \u000aductal hyperplasia is 0.2cm from the margin. The atypical ductal \u000ahyperplasia appears to be adjacent to a prior healed biopsy site. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Microcalcifications in patient with history of ADH bordering \u000aon DCIS in  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aOperation: Right needle directed breast bx. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalcifications in the right breast. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Tissue from right breast. \u000aRADIOLOGY: No calcifications visible in specimen. Dr. Christian notified. \u000aC.Dension, MD \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000aunit number and "tissue from right breast", and consists of a right wire \u000alocalized biopsy specimen (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ) with a localization wire. An \u000aaccompanying radiograph shows a specimen with the localization wire, but no \u000amasses or microcalcifications are identified. The unoriented specimen is inked \u000ain black and serially sectioned to reveal approximately 50% white fibrous \u000atissue with a small area of firmness (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm ) which is present in \u000aone slice. The remainder of the specimen is comprised predominantly of \u000aunremarkable adipose tissue and the specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right wire localized breast biopsy, 1, 2, or 3 frags, ESS. \u000aPlease note: the area of firmness is submitted in cassette #2. \u000alcl \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
