VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "TISSUE FROM LEFT BREAST PRIMARY SPECIMEN": \u000aDuct ectasia with inspissation, calcifications, and periductal \u000afibrosis. \u000aSclerosing apocrine adenosis, adenosis, and epithelial hyperplasia. \u000aHealing biopsy site. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LATERAL SHAVE MARGIN": \u000aSclerosing apocrine adenosis. \u000aSclerosing adenosis and associated calcifications. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Micro Calcs, left breast. \u000aOperation: Left breast wire directed excisional biopsies x 2. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Micro Calcs, left breast. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Tissue from left breast - primary specimen. Wire \u000awith double coil = medial. \u000a#2. Tissue from left breast - lateral shave margin. REMOVED_DATE \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SPRINGER,KIMBERLEY M.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen was received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1. Tissue from left breast - primary specimen", consists of \u000aa REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm fragment of breast tissue, previously inked by the surgeon \u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; \u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = \u000aorange. There are two wires in the specimen that are seen in close proximity \u000ato a clip and calcifications on the accompaning radiograph. There are several \u000afibrous areas with serous fluid filled cyst in the breast parenchyma but no \u000adiscrete masses. The clip is located at the inferiomedial border and an \u000aadditional radiograph shows the clusters calcifications approximately 0.5cm \u000afrom the posterior, 0.9cm from the superior, 0.5cm from the lateral, 0.8cm \u000afrom inferior, and greater than 2.0cm from the anterior and medial margins. \u000aThe remaining breast tissue approximately 40% fibrous. The fibrous tissue is \u000aentirely submitted. \u000aMicro 1: Section with clip, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Microcalcifications, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Remaining margins, multi frags, RSS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2. Tissue from left breast lateral shave margin", consists \u000aof a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm fragment of breast tissue that has been inked by the \u000asurgeon in red (superior), yellow (lateral), and green (inferior). The old \u000amargin is inked blue for reference only. There is some dense white fibrous \u000atissue at the lateral and inferior margins. The entire specimen is submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Lateral shave margin, multi frags, ESS. \u000akms \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
