VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s) \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS (specimen B) AND SENTINEL NODE \u000aBIOPSIES (including  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) (specimen A): \u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODES \u000aSYNOPSIS: \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aSize - 1.8cm \u000aMultifocal - no \u000aHistologic Type - ductal \u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - I (well) \u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate \u000aEIC - negative \u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent \u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - absent \u000aSkin invasion - absent \u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A \u000aFinal Margins (invasive) - \u000aNegative (>0.3cm ) - anterior, posterior, superior, \u000ainferior, medial, lateral \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aTypes - cribriform \u000aNuclear grade - intermediate \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent \u000aExtent of DCIS \u000aDCIS is present as a minor component of the invasive carcinoma \u000aFinal Margins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (>0.3cm ) - anterior, posterior, superior, \u000ainferior, medial, lateral \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent \u000aLYMPH NODES \u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - negative (3 HE levels examined) \u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0 \u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3 \u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 0:3 \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia \u000aColumnar hyperplasia \u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change \u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID c p REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (sn) MX \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - ER and PR performed previously; HER-2 \u000apending \u000aSUPERIOR SHAVED MARGIN (specimen C): \u000aBreast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia, columnar hyperplasia, and \u000aapocrine metaplasia. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aINFERIOR SHAVED MARGIN (specimen D): \u000aBreast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia, columnar hyperplasia, and \u000aapocrine metaplasia. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 61 year old with hx of R breast ADH '99, now with L breast ca, \u000a12/27/05 L breast core needle bxs - IDL mod diff II/III - no def LVI, no def \u000aIS, ER/PR positive, Her2/neu positive \u000aOperation: None given \u000aOperative Findings: None given \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast ca \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000a1/A Left sentinel lymph nodes (fs) \u000a2/B Left breast primary tumor site \u000a3/C Superior shaved margin, suture superior \u000a4/D Inferior shaved margin \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1. LEFT SENTINEL NODE" ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aThree lymph nodes with no tumor seen. \u000aOR Consultation by: DAVID MICHAEL DORFMAN, M.D., PH.D. \u000aResident: PATRICIA A. R. BRUNKER, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patients \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, "#1 left sentinel lymph nodes," consists of two fragments of red-yellow \u000asoft tissue (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm ). The smaller fragment \u000acontains a single lymph node candidate, which is bisected and frozen as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aLarger fragment contains two additional lymph node candidates (each 1.2cm in \u000agreatest dimension). Each candidate is bisected, one is frozen as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the \u000aother is entirely frozen as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : non frozen tissue, multiple frags, ESS \u000aPart B, "#2 left breast primary tumor site," consists of an excision of \u000afibroadipose tissue (7.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 4.5cm ) with sutures designating superior \u000a(short suture), lateral (long suture), and deep (whip stitch) margins \u000a(confirmed per surgeon's operative report). The specimen is inked per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; \u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is an \u000aattached light tan skin ellipse (5.7 x 1.7cm ) on the anterior aspect of the \u000aspecimen. A localizing wire enters the specimen superolaterally and is embedded \u000awithin an ill-defined firm tan-white mass (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm ) with associated \u000afocal hemorrhage and fat necrosis consistent with prior biopsy. The mass is \u000alocated 0.6cm from the closest inferior margin, 1.3cm from the closest \u000asuperior margin, and is remote (>2cm ) from the medial, lateral, anterior, and \u000aposterior margins. The remaining specimen demonstrates occasional tan-white \u000afibro-dense bands (40%) with associated tan-yellow soft, lobulated adipose \u000atissue. There are no additional lesion or abnormalities grossly. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : mass and closest inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : mass and closest superior margin, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : closest posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : closest anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : closest lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : closest medial margin, additional (uninvolved) fibrous tissue, 3 \u000afrags, RSS \u000aPart C, "#3 superior shaved margin, suture superior," consists of an excision \u000aof fibroadipose tissue (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.3cm ) with a suture designating superior. \u000aThe superior surface has been previously inked blue by surgeon; the opposing \u000asurface is inked black by prosector. Sectioning demonstrates predominantly \u000aunremarkable soft yellow lobulated adipose tissue with occasional dense \u000atan-white fibrous tissue (<10%). There are no masses. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : representative sections (1 percm in greatest dimension, to \u000ainclude majority of fibrous tissue), 7 frags, ESS \u000aPart D, "#4 inferior shaved margin, suture superior," consists of an excision \u000aof fibroadipose tissue (5.7 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm ) with a suture designating superior. \u000aThe superior surface has been inked black by prosector; the opposing surface \u000a(inferior) has been previously inked blue by surgeon. Sectioning demonstrates \u000apredominantly unremarkable tan-yellow lobulated adipose tissue (70%) with dense \u000atan-white fibrous tissue (30%). The fibrous tissue is focally cystic but \u000aotherwise unremarkable. There are no masses. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : multiple frags, RSS \u000aDB/jp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Ann K Folkins M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a2/3/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: \u000aAn immunoperoxidase study was performed with the following result for invasive \u000acarcinoma (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu WEAK AND FOCAL (1+) \u000aNote: Studies on the patient's prior core needle biopsy revealed that the \u000acarcinoma was positive for estrogen and progesterone receptors ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aIn this prior specimen, the study for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu was reported to be 2+ and FISH \u000ashowed the lowest limit considered amplification (a ratio of 2.0). In this \u000aspecimen, there is only focal and weak immunoreactivity for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu. \u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
