and no discrete mass. \u000aPosterior and inferior surfaces of the specimen are disrupted; definitive \u000asurgical margin cannot be accurately assessed in these areas due to disrupted \u000anature of specimen. Sectioning demonstrates only focal fibrous tissue \u000a(maximally 0.8cm ) in the area of the localizing wire tip (there are not \u000adiscrete lesions grossly). The remaining specimen is soft, lobulated adipose \u000atissue with occasional focal hemorrhage (localizing wire tracked) and no \u000adiscrete abnormalities. The specimen is entirely submitted sequentially from \u000alateral to medial with tissue surrounding localizing wire tip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen, sequentially from lateral to medial, multiple \u000afrags, ESS. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - lateral, posterior, inferior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - lateral, anterior, posterior, superior; \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - anterior, posterior, superior, inferior,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - anterior, posterior, \u000asuperior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - inferior, anterior, posterior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - anterior, posterior, \u000asuperior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - anterior, posterior, inferior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - superior, anterior, \u000aposterior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - superior, anterior, posterior, medial;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - medial, superior, \u000aposterior. \u000aDB/elw \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Michael H Roh M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a12/19/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
