VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Reduction mamoplasty \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIAN J PRIBAZ M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Elizabeth A. Steensma, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE" (530 gm): \u000aBenign breast tissue with apocrine metaplasia and \u000acystic changes. \u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change. \u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE" (700 gm): \u000aBenign breast tissue with apocrine metaplasia and \u000acystic changes. \u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change. \u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS": \u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aSYNOPSIS: \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aSize - 0.6cm (measured off glass slide) \u000aMultifocal - no \u000aHistologic Type - ductal \u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - I (well) \u000aNuclear Grade - low \u000aEIC - negative \u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent \u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A \u000aSkin invasion - N/A \u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A \u000aFinal Margins (invasive) - \u000aClose (0.1-0.3cm ) - radial (0.2cm ) (unoriented specimen) \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aTypes - cribriform \u000aNuclear grade - low \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent \u000aExtent of DCIS \u000aNumber of blocks:total - 2:8 blocks \u000aFinal Margins (DCIS) \u000aClose (0.1-0.3cm ) - radial (0.2cm ) (unoriented specimen) \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aBiopsy cavity \u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID b pNx MX \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending \u000aNOTE: \u000aSelect slides were reviewed with Dr. A. Richardson of the Breast Pathology \u000aService, who concurs. Dr. Pribaz notified of diagnosis by E-mail at 2 PM on \u000a11/1/06. \u000aD. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT EYELID, LESION": \u000aDermal fibrosis with sparse perivascular chronic inflammation and pigment \u000aincontinence. \u000aThe changes are non-specific. \u000aClinical correlation is recommended. \u000aMultiple levels examined. \u000aThe case is also reviewed at the Dermpath Division Consensus Conference. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Routine bilateral reduction mammoplasty. Separate excision of right \u000abreast lump - from side of previous MRI-guided wire-localized biopsy in \u000aREMOVED_MONTH  REMOVED_CASE_ID . Xanthoma-like lesion right upper eyelid. \u000aOperation: Bilateral breast reduction, excision. \u000aOperative Findings: Right breast lump, excision RT eye lesion. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right breast tissue. \u000aB/2. Left breast tissue. \u000aC/3. Right breast lump. \u000aD/4. Right eyelid lesion. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname, unit number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast tissue", and consists of a 530-gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a4.0cm aggregate of hemorrhagic, yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue and multiple \u000afragments of tan/pink, grossly unremarkable skin. The breast tissue consists \u000aof approximately 70% yellow, lobulated adipose tissue and 30% tan/white, \u000afocally cystic to dense fibrous stroma. No other gross lesions identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin and breast stroma, 4 frags total, RSS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast tissue", and consists of a 700-gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm aggregate of hemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue and multiple fragments of tan, \u000agrossly unremarkable skin. The breast tissue consists of approximately 75% \u000ayellow, lobulated adipose tissue and 25% tan/white focally cystic fibrous \u000astroma. No other gross lesions are identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin and breast stroma, 4 frags total, RSS. \u000aPart C, "#3. Right breast lump", and consists of an unoriented portion of \u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.7 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm ). The specimen is inked \u000ablack and serially sectioned, to exhibit REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm  which grossly \u000acomes to within 0.3cm of the nearest radial margin. The surrounding tissue is \u000atan/white, fibrotic, and focally necrotic. The remaining tissue consists \u000apredominantly of yellow, lobulated adipose tissue with focal pink/tan fibrous \u000astroma. No other gross lesions are identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast tissue, multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart D, "#4. Right eyelid lesion", and consists of an unoriented, tan skin \u000aellipse (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE excised to a depth of 0.2cm ). A definitive lesion is not \u000agrossly identified. The specimen is inked and bisected. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000adfi/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a11/1/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for carcinoma (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) NEGATIVE (1+) \u000aInterpretation: \u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the \u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet \u000abeen determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor \u000acells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only \u000aa portion of the membrane is positive. \u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% \u000aof tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in \u000a>10% of tumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational \u000ause only. \u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a11/3/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: \u000aA paraffin block of invasive carcinoma was sent for the genomic health oncotype \u000aDX Breast Cancer Assay with the following results (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aRecurrence Score = 17 \u000aPatients with a Recurrence Score of 17 in the clinical validation study had an \u000aAverage Rate of Recurrence at 10 years of 11% (95% CI: 8% - 14%). \u000aAddendum #2 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
