sue, \u000aoriented by sutures designating superior (short suture) and lateral (long \u000asuture) margins. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by prosector). The \u000alocalizing wire enters the anterior aspect of the specimen and traverses \u000aposteriorly. The specimen is received with an accompanying radiograph \u000ademonstrating the localizing wire in place within the specimen, in an area of \u000ascattered calcifications. Specimen is sectioned from superior to inferior, \u000arevealing patchy fibro dense tissue involving at least 40% of the specimen and \u000aabutting all margins. There are no discrete masses, lesions or other \u000aabnormalities grossly. Entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from \u000asuperior to inferior, with perpendicular superior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and \u000aperpendicular inferior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The area of interest for localizing \u000awire in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen, sequentially submitted from superior to \u000ainferior, multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart B is labeled "#2. Right breast tissue short stitch superior long lateral", \u000aand consists of an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.4cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue, oriented \u000aby sutures designating superior (short suture) and lateral (long suture) \u000amargins. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of \u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; \u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by prosector). The localizing wire enters \u000athe lateral aspect of the specimen and traverses superomedially. Specimen is \u000areceived with a radiograph demonstrating localizing wire in place within the \u000aspecimen adjacent to a small calcification (central specimen). Specimen is \u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral (19 total slices), revealing \u000aoccasional fibro dense tissue (48-50% of specimen), abutting all margins and \u000awithout discrete masses, lesions or other abnormalities grossly. \u000aRepresentative tissue is submitted, to include entire central portion of \u000aspecimen. Approximately 60% of tissue is submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, #3, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #8, 2 frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #9, 2 frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #10, 2 frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #11, 2 frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #12, 2 frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #13, 2 frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #14, 4 frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #15, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #16, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #17, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #19 (lateral margin), 4 frags, RSS. \u000aNote: Area of interest for localizing wire in approximately  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aDB/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
