VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Stephanie Schulte, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED FOR CALCIFICATIONS": \u000aBreast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia, columnar cell changes, \u000aand calcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aSmall focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None specified. \u000aOperation: L needle-localized breast biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None specified. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram, L breast mass. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) L breast tissue, short - superior, long - lateral --> Mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++ and wire intact in specimen / DGS. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1. L breast tissue short superior, long lateral", and consists of an \u000aovoid fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.9cm ), which is \u000aoriented per surgeon with two sutures: Short equals superior, long equals \u000alateral. There is one needle localization wire in place entering the lateral \u000aaspect of the specimen and exiting at the medial aspect of the specimen. The \u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. The specimen was previously radiographed, confirming the \u000apresence of calcification and an intact needle localization wire within the \u000aspecimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to exhibit \u000aapproximately 90% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue and 10% delicate focally \u000acystic pink/tan fibrous stroma. No discrete masses or lesions are identified. \u000aThe needle localization wire transverses the tissue adjacent to the probable \u000aarea of calcifications as identified on the accompanying radiograph. The \u000aspecimen is entirely sequentially submitted from medial to lateral. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central specimen from medial to lateral with area of probable \u000acalcification in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , multi frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, 3 frags in each, ESS. \u000aLM/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM: \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy, including margins. \u000aAddendum #1 by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
