VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Matthias D. Hofer, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA/1. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION - SHORT SUPERIOR, \u000aLONG LATERAL": \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia adjacent to core site. \u000aCalcifications associated with columnar cell change. \u000aCore biopsy site changes are present at the medial margin of the specimen, see \u000anote. \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000aA double stain with p63 and keratin highlight the myoepithelial layer \u000aunderlying lobules. \u000aNote: The core biopsy site is not completely excised. The focus of atypical \u000aductal hyperplasia is located immediately lateral to the core biopsy site. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Left breast atypical ductal hyperplasia on core biopsy for \u000acalcifications. \u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast ADH on core needle biopsy. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Left breast wire-localized excision - short superior, long lateral. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip, 2 wires and calcs in specimen - d/w J. Jones by M. Noroozian. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen was received fresh with the patient's name and unit number and \u000a"#1. Left breast wire localized excision - short superior, long lateral". The \u000aspecimen consists of a wire localized breast excision specimen measuring 3.2cm \u000a(S-I) x 3.7cm (M-L) x 1.7cm (A-P). Two wires enter the specimen at the \u000alateral (yellow) aspect. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned from medial to lateral into seven slices. The medial aspect is \u000adesignated as slice #1. There is one area of firmness measuring 0.3cm  most \u000apredominantly located in slices #1 through #4 that comes to within 0.2cm to \u000athe anterior aspect, 0.8cm to the posterior aspect, 0.6cm to the superior \u000aaspect, 2.0cm to the inferior aspect, approximately 3.5cm to the medial \u000aaspect and approximately 1.5cm to the lateral aspect. No other gross \u000aabnormalities can be identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #1 (medial aspect), perpendicular sections, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7 (lateral aspect), perpendicular sections, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMDH/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a6/19/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aSurgical addendum: \u000aThe focus of ADH is best seen on the slide containing the immunohistochemical \u000astain. \u000aAdditional levels are examined. \u000aThe diagnosis remains unchanged. \u000aAddendum #1 by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a6/20/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
