VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBROWN, FELIX, MARCEL, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia and atypical lobular hyperplasia involving \u000aa complex sclerosing lesion (radial scar). \u000aNOTE: Because of preoperative clinical or radiologic concern regarding the \u000apossibility of tumor, the margins of this specimen were inked, sampled, and \u000aexamined microscopically. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, SUPERIOR MARGIN: \u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia. \u000aNo tumor seen. \u000aSKIN TAG, RIGHT AXILLA: \u000aFibroepithelial polyp. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aOperation: Right needle localized breast biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue with wite. \u000a2. Right beast superior margin. \u000a3. Skin tag, right axilla. \u000aMammogram - architectural distortion in specimen.. J.L. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DINH,QUINN QUEYEN-BAO,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1, right breast tissue with wire", consists of an oriented \u000aright breast excision with wire localizations for abnormal mammogram (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 2.0cm ). The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation \u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = \u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The cross sections reveal an area of \u000aextended irregular fibrosis (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ). The nearest margins of this \u000aregion of fibrosis: less than 0.5cm from the superior margin, less than REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the inferior margin, less than 0.1cm from the anterior margin, greater \u000athan 1.5cm from the posterior margin, greater than 2.5cm from the lateral \u000amargin and greater than 2.5cm from the medial margin. This area of fibrosis \u000aconsists of approximately 20% of the breast parenchyma, the remaining consists \u000aof yellow adipose tissue. The region of fibrosis is entirely submitted with \u000arespect to closest margins. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast parenchyma with fibrosis (entirely submitted) with respect \u000ato superior, inferior, and anterior margins, 7 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional breast sampling with respect to medial and lateral \u000amargins, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2, right breast superior margin", consists of a right \u000abreast excision, oriented (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm ) and (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm ). \u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation \u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = \u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Cross sectioning reveals yellow \u000alobulated breast parenchyma with no gross evidence of lesion. Representative \u000asections of tissue with respect to inked margins are submitted. \u000aFifty to sixty percent (50-60%) of breast parenchyma and soft tissue are \u000asampled. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast superior margin excision, 5 frags, RSS. \u000aPart three, labeled "#3, skin tag, right axilla", consists of a punch biopsy \u000awith attached skin (0.6 x 0.3cm  excised to a depth of 0.4cm ). The deep soft \u000atissue margin is inked black and the specimen was entirely submitted. \u000aMicro 15: skin tag, bisected, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT \u000a[report_end] 
