adiograph reviewed). The specimen is serially sectioned from \u000alateral to medial to exhibit approximately 50% dense/nodular white/pink fibrous \u000astroma and 50% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. The clip is identified \u000awithin dense fibrous stroma in the posterolateral aspect of the specimen with \u000aassociated hemorrhage and gritty yellow/tan palpable fat necrosis, coming to \u000awithin 0.2cm of the posterior margin and 0.7cm of the lateral margin. No \u000adiscrete masses or lesions are grossly identified. The clip and circled area \u000aof calcifications correspond to the track of the needle localization wire \u000atowards the lateral aspect of the specimen. The specimen is sequentially \u000asubmitted from lateral to medial. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin perpendicular sections, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central specimen (clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , area of palpable calcifications in \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), multi frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS. \u000aLMB/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a8/1/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
