VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME . SAUVEUR \u000aResident: Andrew M. Quinn, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. LEFT BREAST TISSUE, RE-EXCISION (25.0g): \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (4 blocks), arising amid a background of columnar \u000acell change and atypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aSeparate foci of calcification in benign breast tissue. \u000aIntraductal papilloma (0.2cm ). \u000aScattered areas of acute and chronic inflammation, fat necrosis, and foreign \u000abody giant cell reaction, consistent with prior excisional biopsy site. \u000aScar with mild chronic inflammation and foreign body giant cell reaction. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aNOTE: \u000aDr. A. Richardson, Breast Pathology Service, also reviewed this case and \u000aconcurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 56 y/o female S/P REMOVED_DATE L breast well-localized biopsy of \u000acalcifications revealing low-grade DCIS with a close anterior margin; ER/PR (+) \u000aHer-2/neu (-). \u000aOperation: L breast wire-localized re-excision. \u000aOperative Findings: None provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast DCIS. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Left breast tissue, short suture - superior; long label whip stitch on \u000achest wall margin and scar anterior. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in a container, labeled with the patient's \u000aname, medical record number, and "#1. Left breast tissue, short suture \u000asuperior, long lateral whipstitch on chest wall margin and scar anterior", and \u000aconsists of a left breast re-excision (25.0 grams), which is oriented by the \u000asurgeon with a short stitch superiorly, a long stitch laterally, and a \u000awhipstitch on the chest wall. The surgeon has inked the specimen per pathology \u000aprotocol (anterior equals blue, posterior equals black, superior equals red, \u000ainferior equals green, medial equals orange and lateral equals yellow), and \u000ameasures 4.4cm superior to inferior, 5.2cm medial to lateral and 3.8cm \u000aanterior to posterior. A linear scar (2.2cm long) extends from the anterior \u000asurface. A needle localization wire enters the anteroinferior aspect of the \u000aspecimen and exits anteromedially. Also extending from the anteroinferior \u000asurface is a retained needle localization wire tip. Also received are two \u000aneedle localization wires, which are not in the specimen. An x-ray on \u000acentricity shows a needle localization wire and a retained wire tip as \u000adescribed above, as well as two needle localization wires not in the specimen. \u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a prior biopsy cavity (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), which abuts the anteroinferior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is \u000a70% fat and 30% fibrous. The specimen has been entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Scar, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice through wire localization site, including previous biopsy \u000acavity, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice anterior to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , bisected, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior surface, perpendicular sections, 7 frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice lateral to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , bisected, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice lateral to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , bisected, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice lateral to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , bisected, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice lateral to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice lateral to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral surface, perpendicular sections, 2 frags each, ESS. \u000aPlease note that the long axis of the specimen extended from its anterior \u000asurface to its lateral surface. \u000aAQU/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on Wednesday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 30,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06:54:52PM \u000a[report_end] 
