tly of fatty tissue. \u000aThe posterior portion of the specimen consists of white fibrous tissue (up to \u000a2.5cm in greatest dimension). No lesions grossly suspicious for malignancy \u000aare present. The specimen is entirely submitted from anterior to posterior. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue, multi frags, ESS. \u000adl \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
