node - FS (neg for tumor). \u000aB/2. Primary tumor site, left breast - mammo. \u000aC/3. Superior shaved margin. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and mass within specimen. A. Goldkamp. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000a1. SPECIMEN LABELED "SENTINEL LYMPH NODE" ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aLymph node(s), negative for tumor. \u000aOR Consultation by: William Robert Welch, M.D. \u000aResident: Vinodh Pillai, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname, unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "left sentinel lymph node", consists of an irregular pink/tan \u000asmooth rubbery fragment of soft tissue consistent with lymph node (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.2cm ). The specimen is bisected and each half is submitted in its entirety \u000afor frozen section evaluation ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). The specimen is submitted in \u000aits entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Frozen section remnant  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Frozen section remnant  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "primary tumor site left breast", consists of an irregular \u000atan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose breast tissue (5.8cm medial to \u000alateral, 4.5cm anterior to posterior, and 2.4cm superior to inferior) with a \u000ashort suture designating the superior margin, and long suture designating the \u000alateral margin per the surgeon's OP report. There is a needle localization \u000awire, which enters through the lateral aspect of the specimen, and exits \u000athrough the inferior posterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen has been \u000ainked per pathology protocol (superior red, inferior green, medial orange, \u000alateral yellow, anterior blue, and posterior black) per the surgeon. There is \u000aan ill-defined dense white fibrous focally hemorrhagic area consistent with \u000aprevious biopsy cavity (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm ) within which there is a silver \u000ametallic biopsy clip. The biopsy cavity comes within 0.3cm from the superior \u000amargin, 0.5cm from the inferior margin, 0.5cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the anterior margin, 2.0cm from the lateral margin, and 1.5cm from \u000athe medial margin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is tan/yellow and \u000ahomogeneous with no additional lesions or areas of disruption grossly \u000aidentified. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections medial to lateral, blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to \u000ainclude biopsy cavity,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to include metallic clip, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aPart C, labeled "superior shave margin", consists of an irregular tan/yellow \u000alobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm ). There is a \u000asuture designating the superior margin and the surface has been previously \u000ainked red per the surgeon. The opposite surface is irregular tan/yellow to \u000ared/brown, ragged, and concave consistent with "old margin" (black). The cut \u000asurface is tan/yellow and homogeneous with no discrete lesions grossly \u000aidentified. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags, ESS. \u000aSEK/mgd/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed \u000aon Wednesday August 26,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01:03:50PM \u000a[report_end] 
