edle localization wire is present within the specimen, \u000aand an accompanying radiograph shows the needle localization wire adjacent to \u000aan area of microcalcifications. Serial sectioning reveals a tan to white, \u000afibrous cut surface with a minimal amount of admixed adipose tissue. The \u000aspecimen is approximately 80% fibrous tissue and 20% adipose tissue. No \u000alesions are grossly identified. The specimen is entirely submitted for \u000amicroscopic examination. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial slices of specimen from lateral to medial, multi frags, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro 9: inferior margin, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS.lrl \u000alrl \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
