, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : "B", multi frags, ESS. \u000acp/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 14,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05:50:17PM \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for DCIS (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) NEGATIVE (0) \u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following \u000acriteria: \u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the \u000acarcinoma is reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet \u000abeen determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor \u000acells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but \u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive. \u000aEquivocal (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in \u000a>10% of tumor cells or moderate to strong complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in < 30% of tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in \u000a>30% of tumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate immunoreactivity. \u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests \u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance \u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the \u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the \u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such \u000aclearance or approval is not necessary. \u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 15,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05:26:25PM \u000a[report_end] 
