VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST EXCISION WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU. \u000aSYNOPSIS: \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA - not present \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aType - Cribriform \u000aNuclear grade - Low \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent \u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent \u000aExtent of DCIS \u000aSize (max area in one block) - 0.2cm \u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE block \u000aEstimated overall size - 0.2cm \u000aFinal Margins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (>0.3cm ) - All margins (closest deep and inferior \u000aapprox 0.5cm ) \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia \u000aIntraductal papilloma \u000aSclerosing adenosis \u000aCysts \u000aApocrine metaplasia \u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium \u000aCore biopsy \u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: History of DCIS left breast (marked by area and clip, marked by wire \u000a#2). Radiologist also concerned about additional calcifications \u000aanterior to clip and about 2cm (marked by wire #1). \u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS left breast \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast tissue (short = superior, long = lateral) \u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and 2 hook wires in specimen. Calcifications near wire #1 not \u000adefinitely seen in specimen. These findings were communicated to Dr. Carter. \u000aDIR. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SMOUSE,JASON H.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number \u000aand "#1. left breast tissue", and consists of a single breast excision mass \u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x 5 x 4cm which has been inked by the surgeon per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; \u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. A long \u000asuture designates the lateral side and a short stitch designates the superior \u000aside are present. There are two localizing wires present in the specimen. \u000aThere is a small skin ellipse measuring 3cm in length and 0.5cm in greatest \u000awidth, excised to a depth of 5cm  Two localizing wires penetrate through the \u000askin ellipse. The skin is unremarkable. A radiograph accompanies the specimen \u000adesignating that two localizing wires and a clip are in the specimen. \u000aLocalizing wire #2 marks the area of the clip and localizing wire #1 marks the \u000aarea of calcifications anterior to the clip about 2cm  which were \u000asubsequently not seen in the specimen after resection. The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned from superior to inferior revealing 80% dense fibrous \u000atissue diffusely present throughout the specimen with core needle biopsy site \u000achanges and small cysts measuring from 0.1cm up to 0.3cm in diameter. There \u000aare no discrete masses or lesions noted. The sections are radiographed by the \u000apathologist revealing that the clip is in the specimen. The clip is removed \u000aby the pathologist. The specimen is submitted from inferior to superior and \u000a100% of the fibrous tissue is submitted. 90% of the specimen is submitted for \u000ahistologic evaluation. \u000aMicro 1: inferior margin, mult frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous breast tissue, inferior to superior (core biopsy site \u000achanges in #10,12,14; area of clip in #14; representative \u000asections of skin in #20), mult frags, RSS \u000ajs \u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
