VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Scott Lovitch, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, MASTECTOMY" (706g): \u000aLobular carcinoma in situ with pagetoid spread (best seen \u000aon slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aApocrine metaplasia with cyst formation. \u000aNo invasive carcinoma (including deep margin). \u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, MASTECTOMY" (536g): \u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aSize - 0.8cm (measured off slide), associated \u000awith prior biopsy site \u000aMultifocal - No \u000aHistologic type - Ductal \u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - III (Poor) \u000aNuclear grade - High \u000aEIC - Absent \u000aLVI - Absent \u000aDermal LVI - Absent \u000aSkin invasion - Absent \u000aFinal Margins (invasive) \u000aNegative (> 0.3cm ) - Deep \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aTypes - Cribriform, micropapillary \u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present \u000aExtent of DCIS \u000aNumber of blocks/total - 2:11 blocks \u000aMargins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (> 0.3cm ) - Deep \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aCore biopsy site \u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition):  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID b Nx MX. \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) - Performed previously \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: S/p right lumpectomy + AX LN D -> s/p XRT, now with recurrent right \u000abreast Ca on core bx s/p L reduction mammoplasty. \u000aOperation: Right total mastectomy, L prophylactic mastectomy. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Left breast - stitch @ 12 o'clock \u000aB/2. Right breast - stitch @ 12 o'clock. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThis case has two parts. Each is received unfixed, labeled with the patient's \u000aname and medical record number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast stitch at 12 o'clock", and consists of a 706-gram \u000abreast, without axillary fat, oriented by a stitch placed at 12 o'clock on the \u000aellipse of skin (9.5 x 5.0cm ). The breast tissue (19.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 7.0cm ) is \u000acomposed of approximately 60% soft yellow lobulated fat diffusely admixed with \u000amoderately firm, focally cystic, centrally lumpy white fibrous parenchyma. \u000aThere is no indication of nodularity, induration, or grittiness in the \u000aparenchyma. The deep margin is composed of a thin fibrous fascia which we \u000amarked with black ink. The skin surface is tan and soft with a central, 1.2cm \u000aeverted nipple and a surrounding 3.5cm dark brown areola. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative, firm, lumpy and cystic breast tissue, 3 frags, \u000aRSS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast", and consists of a 536-gram breast, without axillary \u000acontents. It is oriented by a suture designating 12 o'clock attached to the \u000aedge of the ellipse of skin (10.5 x 5.0cm ) which has a central, 1.2cm everted \u000anipple surrounded by a 3.0cm in diameter dark brown areola. The breast tissue \u000a(15.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm ) is composed of approximately 70% soft yellow lobulated \u000afat admixed with predominantly centrally located, firm, rubbery white fibrous \u000aparenchyma containing vaguely lumpy areas and cyst, but no evidence of \u000ainduration or nodularity at the center of the breast. The upper outer quadrant \u000ademonstrates a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7.0cm gray solid mass with central hemorrhage and \u000ascattered surrounding necrosis. Dense fibrosis radiates from the mass in a \u000astellate pattern. The mass contains a small clip identified on a radiograph. \u000aThe mass is 2.0cm from the deep margin which is composed of a thin fibrous \u000afascia which we marked with black ink. The lateral most portion of the breast, \u000aat the deep margin, demonstrates a dense fibrous, well-healed scar (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.0cm ). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sections with clip, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Section of tumor adjacent to clip, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Deep margin near tumor, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Scarred area in lateral portion at deep margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000adf/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a8/15/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: \u000aFISH was performed by USLABS using the PathVysion HER-2 DNA Probe Kit with the \u000afollowing results for the right breast invasive carcinoma (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aResults: NOT AMPLIFIED \u000aHer-2/cen 17 ratio = REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of Her-2/neu copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of cen 17 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe cutoff point for assessing HER-2/neu gene amplification is a ratio of REMOVED_DATE \u000aNote: Immunoperoxidase studies on the prior core needle biopsy showed 2+ \u000aequivocal positivity for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu. \u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
