VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR TWO DENSITIES: \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. See note 2. \u000aHyalinized cysts with calcification, chronic inflammation, and hemosiderin \u000aladen macrophages. \u000aNOTE 1: The breast tissue is largely adipose tissue with focal areas of \u000adense stroma, possibly correlating with the mammographic densities. The \u000aentire specimen is examined histologically, including margins. \u000aNOTE 2: A few foci of lush hyperplasia border on atypical (e.g., block 11; \u000aDr. Welch); level sections do not disclose changes that would meet \u000astrict criteria for ADH (Dr. Lester). \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 66-year-old postmenopausal female whose recent mammogram \u000ademonstrated a right breast focal opacity and ultrasound demonstrates \u000a2 adjacent 5mm nodules, recommended for excisional biopsy. \u000aOperation: Right breast double wire localization excision. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast biopsy. \u000aRadiology: Masses are in the specimen. D. Smith, M.D. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,BRIAN S.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh and labeled with the patient's name and unit \u000anumber and consists of a single REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm mass of fibroadipose tissue. \u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral \u000a= yellow; medial = orange. There is a long stitch and a short stitch marking \u000athe lateral and superior aspects respectively and two (2) wires in the \u000aspecimen. The specimen is serially sectioned. The central portion of the \u000aspecimen has several areas of firm, white glistening tissue corresponding to \u000athe lesions seen radiographically. The largest area measures REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm  \u000aThe remaining portion of the specimen consists almost entirely of yellow \u000aadipose tissue, which appears unremarkable. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aThe specimen radiograph is reviewed and reveals two wires and two vague \u000aradiologic densities. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  central portion of specimen including radiographic lesion, \u000a12 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior portion of specimen, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior portion of specimen, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of the specimen, mult frags, ESS. \u000aNote: There is no cassette #18. \u000absc \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
