he evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. Specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal \u000aa probable core biopsy site with old hemorrhage. This area is abutting the \u000amedial margin, greater than 4.0cm from the lateral margin, 0.9cm from the \u000ainferior margin, greater than 1.0cm from the superior margin, 1.1cm from the \u000aanterior margin and greater than 1.0cm from the posterior margin. The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histology. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Left breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aARL/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a10/17/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
