8cm anterior to posterior and \u000a0.9cm medial to lateral. Sectioning along the superior-inferior axis, lateral \u000amultiple small yellow/light brown fluid-filled cysts measuring up to 0.2cm in \u000alargest dimension. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is mostly composed \u000aof tan fibrotic tissue. \u000aMicros REMOVED_DATE  serial sections of specimen from superior to inferior, 11 frags \u000atotal, ESS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2 right breast tissue, medial shave margin", consists of a \u000asingle fragment of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm with one \u000acauterized surface and one surface that has been inked orange by the surgeon. \u000aSectioning reveals a mostly fibrotic parenchyma with some adipose tissue, and \u000ano gross lesions. \u000aMicros REMOVED_DATE  entire specimen, 9 frags total, ESS. \u000apj \u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
