VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A PALPABLE MASS: \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, present as multiple foci in 12 of 19 blocks. \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies for e-cadherin are performed and show absent or \u000aonly weak immunoreactivity (blocks 12 and 15; see note). \u000aFibroadenoma(s) (present in three blocks, measuring up to 0.5cm in size). \u000aFibrosis and traumatic neuromas, consistent with the history of prior \u000abreast biopsies. \u000aNote: Focally, the LCIS has a more solid pattern. No definite \u000acribriforming is present. In the absence of strong e-cadherin positivity, \u000athis carcinoma in situ is best classified as LCIS. \u000aDr. Stuart Schnitt also reviewed selected slides and concurs with this \u000ainterpretation. \u000aNo invasive carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic examination of \u000athe specimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: History of benign breast biopsies. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast mass. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue. Marking stitch - short superior, \u000along lateral. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WITKIEWICZ,AGNIESKA K.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000amedical record number and "#1 right breast tissue, marking stitch short \u000asuperior, long lateral", and consists of a single fragment of fibroadipose \u000atissue (5.5 x 4 x 2cm ). The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; \u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The breast parenchyma has \u000amultiple areas of vague nodularity (largest 1cm ) but no discrete masses or \u000anodules can be grossly identified. The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior to superior, mult frags, ESS. \u000afm \u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
