VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNASCIMENTO, ALESSANDRA, F., M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NASCIMENTO,ALESSANDRA F.,M.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (719 GM): \u000aFibroadenoma (0.8cm ). \u000aBenign breast tissue with focal epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine \u000ametaplasia, ectatic ducts, and dense fibrous stroma. \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (810 GM): \u000aRESIDUAL LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU. \u000aThe deep resection margin is negative for tumor. \u000aSclerosing adenosis, apocrine metaplasia, ectatic ducts, dense fibrous \u000astroma. \u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions. \u000aIntraductal papilloma (0.2cm ). \u000aBiopsy cavity with foreign body giant cell reaction. \u000aSkin with cicatrix. \u000aAJCC staging (6th edition,  REMOVED_CASE_ID ): Tis (LCIS) Nx Mx. \u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester (breast pathology service), who \u000aconcurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Hx of LCIS + mutiple benign biopsies. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1). Left breast 730 gm. \u000a2). Right breast 820 gm. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHEN,JEY-HSIN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aReceived in two parts, both of which are received fresh, labeled with the \u000apatient's name and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "left breast short stitch superior, long stitch lateral", is \u000a0a 719-gram REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.5cm simple mastectomy with a short suture \u000adesignating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The tan skin \u000aellipse (15.0 x 8.5cm ) has an eccentric nipple/areolar complex (4.5 x 4.5cm \u000awith a central everted nipple 1.7cm ). No scar is grossly appreciated. The \u000adeep fascial plane, devoid of skeletal muscle, is inked black. The specimen \u000ais serially sectioned to reveal, a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm well-delineated \u000atan/white granular slightly gritty mass which comes to within 2.0cm of the \u000adeep margin. The remaining parenchyma (approximately 40% specimen) is dense \u000awhite fibrous tissue, with diffuse fibrocystic disease, coming to within 0.5cm \u000aof the deep margin (with a largest measurement of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm ) subjacent \u000ato the overlying scar. The remaining 60% is yellow lobulated fatty tissue. \u000aLymph nodes are not grossly appreciated. Representative sections are submitted \u000aas follows: \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro 3: deep margin associated with mass, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 4: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 5: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 6: lower outer quadrant to include 1.0cm cyst, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 7: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 8: nipple and skin with scar, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 20: additional skin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aPart two, labeled "right breast", is an 810-gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm simple mastectomy with a short suture designating superior and a long suture \u000adesignating lateral. The tan surfacing skin ellipse (17.0 x 7.0cm ) displays \u000aan eccentric nipple/areolar complex (4.5 x 4.0cm  with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm \u000aeverted nipple). Located 8.0cm lateral to the nipple is a well-healed linear \u000ascar (3.2cm in length) which abuts the superior and inferior skin margins. \u000aThe deep fascial plane, with scant skeletal muscle, is inked black. The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned to reveal contiguous with the overlying scar, \u000apredominantly within the upper outer quadrant, a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm area of \u000afibrous tissue containing two cavities (0.8cm and 3.0cm in greatest \u000adimension) and a stellate fibrous area (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ) with the largest \u000acavity coming to within 3.0cm of the deep margin. The remaining parenchyma, \u000ais 60% dense white fibrous tissue with diffuse fibrocystic disease, which is \u000aassociated with the aforementioned cavity/stellate area, coming to within REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the deep margin, and is predominantly within the upper portion of the \u000aspecimen. The remaining 40% of the parenchyma is yellow lobulated fatty \u000atissue. Lymph nodes are not grossly appreciated. Representative sections are \u000asubmitted as follows: \u000aMicro 9: nipple and skin with scar, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 10: closest deep margin in relation to associated with cavity, 1 frag, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  larger cavity to include smaller cavity, 1 frag in each, RSS. \u000aMicro 13: smaller cavity to stellate area, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  stellate fibrous tissue, 1 frag in each, RSS. \u000aMicro 16: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 17: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 18: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 19: upper outer quadrant, 1.0cm away from cavity, 1 frag, RSS.` \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue surrounding cavities, 5 frags, RSS. \u000alm \u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000a[report_end] 
