ed "A ca++" and contains multiple, soft, fragmented, yellow \u000ato white tissue cores (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm in aggregate). The other cassette \u000ais labeled "B" and contains similar tissue fragments (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm in \u000aaggregate). \u000aMicro 3: tan cassette labeled "A ca++", multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 4: tan cassette labeled "B", multi frags, ESS. \u000akks \u000aReports to: SEDGWICK, EMILY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES) \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES) \u000a[report_end] 
