ecimen, and adjacent to the tip of the localization wire. Sectioning \u000areveals the specimen to be composed of approximately 60% dense tan/white \u000afibrous tissue, predominantly in the inferolateral aspect of the specimen, with \u000afocal hemorrhage consistent with prior biopsy procedure in slices six through \u000anine. The localization clip is identified in slice 8, and the cluster of \u000acalcifications is identified radiographically in slice 6. No grossly evident \u000amass lesions are identified. The specimen is sliced from inferior to superior, \u000aand the specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 1 (inferior), sliced perpendicularly, 10 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 2, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 3, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 4, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 5, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 6 (calcifications in cassette 11), 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 7, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 8 (clip in micro 15), 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 9, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 10, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 11, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 12, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro 25: slice 13, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro 26: slice 14 (superior), sliced perpendicularly, 8 frags, ESS \u000ajmh \u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
