en \u000ain the inferior aspect of the specimen. There is a metal clip inserted \u000aadjacent to the entry point of the needle-localization wire in the superior \u000aportion of the specimen. The specimen is inked in six colors "per pathology \u000aprotocol" with superior red, inferior green, anterior blue, posterior black, \u000amedial orange and lateral yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from \u000ainferior to superior. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a possible \u000aprevious biopsy site located in the mid portion of the specimen surrounded by \u000aan area of recent hemorrhage that measures over an area REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  \u000aAlso noted throughout the specimens are multiple smooth-lined cysts ranging \u000afrom REMOVED_DATE up to 0.6cm in greatest dimension. There is no discrete mass, lesion \u000aor nodule associated with the specimen grossly. The approximate specimen \u000acomposition is 85% diffuse dense white fibrous tissue and 15% unremarkable \u000ayellow adipose tissue. \u000aThe specimen is submitted entirely sequentially from inferior to superior. \u000aNote also the area that contains the clip and the area of architectural \u000adistortion is in cassette 16, 17 and 18. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin perpendicularly sectioned, 3 frags per \u000acassette each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One full thickness \u000asectioned divided into two pieces, 1 frag per cassette each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin perpendicularly taken with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 frags, \u000aESS,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000acp/ag