ures 0.4cm in diameter and is adjacent to the medial margin, \u000a0.2cm from the posterior margin, and 0.8cm from the superior margin. The \u000asecond area of firmness is 1cm away from the first one and is adjacent to the \u000aposterior margin, 1cm from the medial margin, and 2cm from the superior \u000amargin. This area measures 0.3cm in diameter. The remainder of the tissue \u000aconsists of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted for histologic analysis from superior to inferior. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire specimen submitted from superior to inferior margins. The \u000aareas of firmness are contained in cassettes REMOVED_DATE \u000amir \u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
