oned from lateral to medial revealing predominantly \u000awhite, rubbery, focally gritty breast parenchyma, with no discrete lesions or \u000amasses identified. The specimen is radiographed. The slide containing the \u000aclip is identified, and is submitted in cassette #12. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral perpendicular margins, 3 frags each, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast wire localized biopsy from lateral to medial, 1 or 2 \u000afrags each, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial perpendicular margin, 3 or 4 frags, ESS \u000alcl \u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
