an/white, focally cystic, \u000afibrous stroma. No other lesions are grossly identified. \u000aMicro 1: skin and breast stroma, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 2: breast stroma, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast, additional sections, mult frags, RSS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2 right breast tissue", consists of a  REMOVED_CASE_ID -gram, 25 x 22 x \u000a4cm aggregate of hemorrhagic, fibrofatty breast tissue and multiple fragments \u000aof tan irregular skin. Serial sectioning of the breast tissue reveals \u000aapproximately 60% yellow/tan lobulated fat and 40% tan/white to red, focally \u000ahemorrhagic, focally cystic, fibrous stroma. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  tan/white, \u000arubbery, circumscribed, fibrous nodule is identified within the stroma \u000aconsistent with a fibroadenoma. No other lesions are grossly identified. \u000aThe breast is re-examined grossly and additional sections were submitted. \u000aMicro 3: skin and circumscribed fibrous nodule, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 4: breast stroma, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast, additional sections, mult frags, RSS. \u000adfi \u000aReports to: HERGRUETER, CHARLES, A. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY \u000a[report_end] 
