VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Benjamin J-C Chen, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. RIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread and involving \u000aareas of sclerosing adenosis. \u000aColumnar cell change. \u000aSclerosing adenosis with associated microcalcifications. \u000aPapilloma (0.3cm ). \u000aImmunohistochemical studies performed at BWH show that E-Cadherin \u000ais absent in the areas of atypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aA double p63/ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID / REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  highlights an intact myoepithelial layer. \u000aMargins were inked and evaluated in examination of the specimen \u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests \u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance \u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the \u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the \u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such \u000aclearance or approval is not necessary. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 46 yo woman found on screening mammogram, REMOVED_DATE demonstrates new area \u000amicrocalcs close to prior biopsy site which show ALH. \u000aOperation: R wire localized breast biopsy \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided \u000aClinical Diagnosis: R abnl mammogram \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. R breast tissue - short superior, long lateral \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aCa++ + wire/DG \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000aunit number \u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast tissue", consists of a 5.0cm (anterior to posterior) \u000ax 2.6cm (superior to inferior) x 1.9cm (medial to lateral) breast biopsy \u000aspecimen with a white/tan skin ellipse (5.0 x 2.0cm ) overlying the inferior \u000aand anterior aspects and a localization wire in place. The specimen is \u000aoriented with a short suture marking superior, a long suture marking lateral, \u000aand inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates scattered \u000acalcification in the center of the specimen adjacent to the localization wire. \u000aAdditional calcification is seen near the lateral margin at the level of the \u000alocalization wire which enters the posterior aspect of the specimen. The \u000aspecimen is composed of greater than 90% dense white fibrous tissue and is \u000asubmitted in its entirety for histological examination. \u000aCalcifications are present in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (posterolateral) and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a(central). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin, perpendicular sections, 3 frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Cross sections (posterior to anterior), REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, perpendicular sections, 3 frags each, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aCEL/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed \u000aon Monday REMOVED_MONTH 27,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 09:37:33PM \u000a[report_end] 
