ial. Gross diagnosis: Medical \u000adevice consistent with breast implant. No sections. \u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast implant". It consists of a 14.0cm  600 mL tissue \u000aexpander bearing the words "McGhan Style 133FV, lot  REMOVED_CASE_ID ". The external \u000asurface is lightly blood-stained. It is composed of finely granular, intact \u000asynthetic membrane and filled with clear watery fluid. Gross diagnosis: \u000aMedical device consistent with breast implant. No sections. \u000aPart C, "#3. Right breast skin". It consists of two strips of soft tan \u000aunremarkable skin (9.0 x 1.0cm and REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ). They are excised to an \u000aaverage depth of 1.2cm  Subjacent tissue is composed of soft yellow lobulated \u000afat and a central layer of dense fibrous tissue suggestive of scar. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 3 frags, RSS. \u000aPart D, "#4. Right breast capsule". It consists of a dense rubbery fibrous \u000amembrane. It is irregularly shaped (15.0 x 9.0cm ) and averages 0.3cm in \u000athickness. One surface is smooth and glistening. The opposite side is almost \u000aentirely covered by adherent, soft, rubbery fibrous tissue and fat. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Membrane, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aPart E, "#5. Left breast skin". It consists of a 9.0cm strip of tan skin, \u000aranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0.6cm in width. It is excised to a greatest depth of REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. The subjacent tissue is composed of soft yellow fat and dense fibrous \u000atissue as seen in the scar. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 3 frags, RSS. \u000aPart F, "#6. Left breast capsule". It consists of a dense rubbery \u000afibromembranous segment of tissue with an intact, saccular shaped (13.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm x 0.5cm in average thickness). One surface is smooth, pink and glistening. \u000aThe opposite side is uniformly covered by a thin layer of shaggy fibrous tissue \u000aand fat. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Membranous tissue, 2 frags, RSS. \