VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Stefan Kraft, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST MASS, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION: \u000aFibroadenoma (1.7cm ) with epithelial hyperplasia. \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia. \u000aColumnar cell change with flat epithelial atypia and associated with \u000acalcifications. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aCore biopsy site is present. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aNOTE: Selected slides were reviewed by Dr. S. Lester and Dr. A. Richardson who \u000aconcur with the diagnosis. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: History of phyllodes tumor excision  REMOVED_CASE_ID ; remnant mass in area. Rule \u000aout phyllodes versus fibroadenoma. \u000aOperation: Right needle loc bx. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right breast mass needle loc oriented to path (mammo). \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aMass in center of specimen with hookwire - d/w Shoji by Noroozian. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit \u000anumber, and "right breast mass needle loc", consists of an irregular tan/pink \u000ato tan/yellow fibrofatty breast tissue (5.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm ) that has been \u000apreviously inked by the surgeon. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol \u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen was previously \u000aradiographed (per radiologist, "mass in center of specimen with hooked wire"). \u000aThe prosector concurs and notes that the needle localization wire is either \u000aadjacent to or runs through a well-circumscribed somewhat lobulated mass. The \u000aneedle localization wire enters the medial anterior aspect of the specimen and \u000aleaves at the lateral posterior aspect. Specimen is sectioned from the medial \u000ato lateral aspect to show a tan/white, well-circumscribed mass (1.7cm in max. \u000adim.) whose cut surface has focal punctate hemorrhage. The mass is 0.3cm from \u000athe inferior aspect, 0.4cm from the posterior aspect, 0.8cm from the superior \u000aaspect, 0.7cm from the inferior aspect, 1.3cm from the lateral aspect, and \u000a2.4cm from the medial aspect. The mass is surrounded by focally dense \u000atan/white to tan/pink fibrous tissue (30%), along with tan/yellow lobulated \u000aadipose tissue. This fibrous tissue may have possible focal calcifications. \u000aNo other lesions are grossly identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Specimen serially sectioned with perpendicular sections of medial \u000aaspect in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , perpendicular sections of lateral aspect in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and \u000amass in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , multi frags total, ESS. \u000adrd/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on \u000a4/12/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
