VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Agoston Tony Agoston, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CLACIFICATIONS AND A CLIP: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform and solid types (low nuclear grade), \u000apresent \u000aas two foci (0.5 and 0.2cm ) in two (2) of eleven blocks (11). \u000aNo necrosis or associated microcalcifications are identified. \u000aColumnar cell hyperplasia with focal atypia. \u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with columnar cell hyperplasia and \u000aapocrine \u000acysts. \u000aPrior biopsy site changes are present. \u000aDCIS is 0.1cm from the lateral margin (inked yellow, focal, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) and \u000a0.15 \u000acm from the inferior margin (inked green, focal, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aAll other margins are negative for carcinoma (>0.3cm ). \u000aThis carcinoma would be best classified as AJCC (6th edition) Tis NX. \u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone \u000areceptor, and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu will be performed and reported in an addendum. \u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who \u000aconcurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 51 year old female with abnormal mammo = atypical hyperplasia ductal L \u000abreast on core bx. \u000aOperation: L breast wire localized. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) left breast tissue - short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral --> mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aIntact wire, clip and scattered Ca++ in specimen. Banu Oner, M.D. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number, \u000alabeled "#1. Left breast tissue", and consists of a wire localized excisional \u000abiopsy (2.0cm SI, 5.5cm ML, 3.5cm AP) that is oriented with a short suture \u000adesignating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The specimen is \u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A \u000awire enters on the anterior/medial aspect, and the radiograph demonstrates a \u000awire, calcifications and a clip in the specimen. There is a firm white \u000afibrotic area (1.5cm SI, 1.7cm ML, 2.5cm AP) that abuts the superior, \u000ainferior, lateral, anterior and posterior margins, and a 3.5cm from the medial \u000amargin. A core biopsy site is identified, but no clip is found. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Serially sectioned specimen from medial to lateral, multi frags, \u000aESS. \u000aNote: The clip is likely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  based on the radiograph. \u000aTA/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a12/21/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for DCIS (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) NEGATIVE (0) \u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the \u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet \u000abeen determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a \u000aportion of the membrane is positive. \u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of \u000atumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of \u000atumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational \u000ause only. \u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
