VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Scott Lovitch, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia. \u000aBiopsy cavity. \u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium. \u000aThere is no residual DCIS seen upon microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aNOTE: Selected slides were also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology \u000aService, who concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Hx L DCIS with close inferior and lateral margins --> re-excision. \u000aOperation: Left breast re-excisional biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None specified. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Left breast re-excision biopsy; short stitch - superior, long stitch - \u000alateral. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in a single container labeled with the patient's \u000aname, medical record number, and "#1. Left breast reexcision biopsy, short \u000astitch superior, long stitch lateral". It consists of a single left breast \u000aexcision specimen without localization wire which measures 6.0cm from medial \u000ato lateral, 4.5cm from superior to inferior, and 3.5cm from anterior to \u000aposterior. A short suture marks the superior aspect of the specimen and a long \u000asuture marks the lateral aspect. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol \u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is a skin ellipse which \u000ais present on the anterior surface and measures REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm and 0.2cm in \u000adepth. It contains a well-healed, linear scar which measures 2.5cm in length \u000aand extends to within 0.7cm of the medial tip of the ellipse, 1.4cm of the \u000alateral tip, and 0.6cm of either side. The specimen is serially sectioned \u000afrom medial to lateral in 9 slices such that slice #1 represents the medial \u000amargin and slice #9 represents the lateral margin. In the center of the \u000aspecimen, there is a seroma cavity filled with unremarkable red/brown fluid. \u000aThis measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm and extends to within 0.9cm of the anterior \u000amargin/skin ellipse, 1.1cm of the superior margin, 1.1cm of the inferior \u000amargin, 2.1cm of the posterior margin, 0.9cm of the medial margin, and 1.6cm \u000aof the lateral margin. The fibrous tissue surrounding the seroma cavity is \u000apalpably firm and has a granular texture. This firm, fibrous tissue abuts the \u000asuperior, posterior, and inferior margins and extends to within 0.1cm of the \u000alateral margin, 0.5cm of the medial margin, and 0.5cm of the anterior margin. \u000aAt the periphery of the fibrous tissue, several small cysts are identified \u000awhich measure 0.4cm in greatest dimension and contain serous fluid. The \u000aentire specimen is submitted for microscopic examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, perpendicular sections, REMOVED_DATE frags per cassette, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin ellipse at medial margin, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #8, 1 frag per cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, perpendicular sections, REMOVED_DATE frags per cassette, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral tip of skin ellipse, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aSBL/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a2/12/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
