odule (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ) located 0.2cm \u000afrom the anterior margin, 0.5cm from the posterior margin, 0.5cm from the \u000asuperior margin, 1.0cm from the inferior margin, 1.2cm from the lateral \u000amargin, and 2.5cm from the medial margin. Remainder of the breast parenchyma \u000ais tan/yellow and homogenous with no additional lesions or areas of disruption \u000agrossly identified. The specimen is submitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections, medial to lateral block ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to \u000ainclude lesion block,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  adjacent to clip as seen on mammogram), 1 frag \u000aeach, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aPlease note block #15 does not have intact inked margins. \u000asek/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a4/9/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
