 central scar. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol \u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = \u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange and contains two \u000asutures: long = lateral and short = superior. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned from medial to lateral and entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - left breast tissue, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aPart 2, "uterus, cervix, both tubes and ovaries", is a 72g specimen including \u000auterus (8 x REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm ), right fallopian tube (5cm in length by 0.4cm in \u000adiameter), right ovary (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ), left fallopian tube (4.5cm in \u000alength by REMOVED_DATE cn in diameter) and left ovary (2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ). The exocervix \u000a(3 x 2.8cm ) is covered by smooth, glistening, white mucosa. The external os \u000ais slit-like and measures REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm  The endocervical canal (3cm in \u000alength) has a tan herringbone mucosa. The endometrial cavity (2.5cm from \u000acornu to cornu, 2.5cm in length) has a tan/pink hemorrhagic endometrium (0.2 \u000acm in average thickness). The myometrium measures 1.5cm in maximum thickness. \u000aThe serosa is dull and there are no adhesions. Both fallopian tubes are patent \u000aand have fimbriated ends without paratubal cysts. Both ovaries have a \u000acribriform, glistening, tan surface. \u000aMicro 10 - anterior cervix, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 11 - posterior cervix, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 12 - LUS, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - anterior endometrium, REMOVED_DATE f each cass, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - posterior endometrium, REMOVED_DATE f each cass, ESS. \u000aMicro 22 - left ovary & fallopian tube, 4 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 23 - right ovary & fallopian tube, 4 frags, RSS. \u000aReports to: FARHAD, SAHBA M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: UTERUS W/ OR W/O ADNEXA- OTH THAN NEPLAST OR PROL \u000a[report_end] 
