VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D. \u000a1) LEFT BREAST, LATERAL, NEEDLE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A NODULE: \u000aIntraductal papillomas (multiple; up to 0.5cm in size), some with \u000aapocrine change and associated calcifications. \u000aFibrocystic changes including epithelial hyperplasia, cysts, and \u000aapocrine change. \u000aThe entire specimen is submitted for analysis; margins examined \u000amicroscopically. \u000a2) LEFT BREAST, MEDIAL, NEEDLE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aFibrocystic changes including epithelial hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis, \u000aintraductal papillomas, cysts, and apocrine change. \u000aNumerous calcifications associated with benign breast epithelium. \u000aHealing core biopsy site. \u000aThe entire specimen is submitted for analysis; margins examined \u000amicroscopically. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: REMOVED_DATE US showing a solid mass at 3 o'clock. On REMOVED_DATE (consult \u000aslides -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) of the left breast wire localization excision for \u000acalcifications shows atypical ductal hyperplasia associated with calcifications \u000aand lobular carcinoma in situ. \u000aOperation: Left needle localized breast biopsy \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammo left, lobular carcinoma in situ left breast \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left lateral needle localized breast biopsy \u000a(short/superior; long/lateral) \u000a#2) Left medial needle localized breast biopsy (short/superior; long/lateral) \u000aRADIOLOGY: #1) Nodule in specimen. JL \u000a#2) Calcifications in specimen. JL \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMBARD,DAVID B.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1. left lateral needle loc breast biopsy, one large, one \u000asmall x 2 pieces", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm portion of fibrofatty \u000abreast tissue with a needle localization in place and two sutures present \u000a(short/superior and long/lateral per the surgeon). A radiograph accompanies \u000athe specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation \u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = \u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned \u000arevealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm white/tan, ill-defined, indurated mass which \u000acomes to within 0.1cm of the posterior margin, 0.2cm from the anterior \u000amargin, 0.4cm from the inferior margin, 1.9cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the lateral margin, and 2.5cm from the medial margin. Focal \u000ahemorrhage and granular to cystic fibrous stroma surround the mass. The \u000aremaining breast tissue consists of predominantly tan/yellow lobulated fat and \u000afocally cystic fibrous stroma. Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.8 x 0.4cm tan/yellow irregular rubbery soft tissue fragment, within two \u000atubular structures are identified. The specimen is bisected and entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue (sequentially from lateral to medial), mult frags, \u000aESS (#3 and 4 contain the mass) \u000aMicro 8: additional tubular soft tissue, 2 frags, ESS \u000aPart two, labeled "#2. left medial needle loc breast biopsy, long lateral, \u000ashort superior", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm portion of fibrofatty breast \u000atissue with an accompanying radiograph, needle localization wire, and two \u000asutures (short superior, long lateral per the surgeon). The specimen is inked \u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; \u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = \u000aorange. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior, \u000arevealing approximately 50% tan/white, cystic, dense fibrous stroma with focal \u000ahemorrhage (predominantly adjacent to needle localization wire) and 50% \u000ayellow/tan lobulated fat. The specimen is re-radiographed and the \u000acalcifications are identified. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue (sequentially from superior to inferior), mult \u000afrags, ESS (calcifications are identified in blocks REMOVED_DATE  \u000apredominantly within 9,10 and 11) \u000adfi \u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
