lip in specimen. SMS/SR. \u000aSpecimen #3, No clip in specimen discussed with Dr. Matory. \u000aSpecimen #4, No clip. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LIN,JONATHAN H.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in four parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1, left breast upper inner quadrant, short/superior, \u000along/lateral" is a breast biopsy specimen received with two (2) orienting \u000asutures designated short/superior and long/lateral by the surgeon along with \u000aone (1) wire in place. The breast biopsy measures 6cm from medial to lateral, \u000a4.2cm from anterior to superior and anterior to posterior and 1.6cm from \u000asuperior to inferior. The breast biopsy consists of greater than 80% yellow \u000aadipose tissue. There is an irregular area of white fibrosis measuring 0.9cm \u000ain greatest dimension that appears to approach to within 0.5cm of the green \u000ainked margin. There is a also a 0.6cm clear fluid filled cyst that appears to \u000aapproach to within 0.2cm of the green inked margin. The entire specimen is \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast biopsy specimen, 25 frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2, left breast, lower inner quadrant, short/superior, \u000along/lateral", consists of a breast biopsy specimen oriented by two (2) sutures \u000adesignated as short/superior, long/lateral by the surgeon along with the wire \u000ain place measuring 6.8cm from medial to lateral, 4.5cm from anterior to \u000aposterior and 1.2cm from superior to inferior. The specimen is inked per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior \u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. \u000aThe specimen consists approximately of 80% yellow adipose tissue, and the \u000aremaining tissue may consist of possible skeletal muscle admixed with bands of \u000airregular white fibrous tissue. A definite biopsy site is not identified. The \u000aclip is not grossly identified. The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower inner quadrant breast biopsy serially sectioned from \u000alateral to medial, entirely submitted, 23 frags, ESS. \u000aPart three, labeled "#3, left breast, long lateral, short superior", consists \u000aof a breast biopsy specimen received with two (2) sutures designated \u000along/lateral by the surgeon measuring 6.9cm from medial to lateral, 2.5cm \u000afrom anterior to posterior and 1.9cm from superior to inferior. The specimen \u000ais inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = \u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; \u000amedial = orange. The specimen consists of 80% of yellow adipose tissue, and a \u000adiffuse area of white fibrosis (1.5cm in greatest dimension) appears to \u000aimmediately abut both the green and red inked margins. The specimen is \u000aentirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast biopsy specimen #3, serially sectioned and entirely \u000asubmitted from lateral to medial, 12 frags, ESS. \u000aPart four, labeled "#4, left breast, re-excision upper quadrant, long/lateral, \u000ashort superior", consists of a breast biopsy specimen received with two sutures \u000adesignated short/superior, long/lateral by the surgeon. The specimen is inked \u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; \u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = \u000aorange and measuring 1.5cm from medial to lateral, 3.0cm from superior to \u000ainferior, and 2.9cm from anterior to posterior. The specimen consists of 80% \u000aadipose tissue with possible interspersed areas of fibrosis in the remaining \u000atissue. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic examination. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  re-excision breast biopsy specimen, 7 frags, ESS. \u000ajhl \u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
