or/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. \u000aThe localizing wire enters laterally and traverses the specimen medially. The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral, revealing 30-40% \u000atan/white focally hemorrhagic fibrous tissue, which is grossly unremarkable \u000awith the exception of a 0.5cm palpably firm tan/white nodule (? Cyst), 0.3cm \u000afrom the closest medial margin, 0.4cm from the closest anterior margin, 0.8cm \u000afrom the closest superior margin, 0.3cm from the closest inferior margin and \u000a1.5cm from the closest posterior margin and greater than 2cm from the closest \u000amedial margin. There are no additional abnormalities. The entire specimen is \u000asubmitted, sequentially from medial to lateral. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen, sequentially from medial to lateral \u000a(wire tip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; nodule in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), multiple frags, ESS. \u000aDB/mmm \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a4/21/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
