VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aSevere atypical ductal hyperplasia, bordering on DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000a(blocks 6 & 7; levels examined), present < 0.1cm from the posterior \u000amargin. \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present. \u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions and \u000aatypia. \u000aApocrine metaplasia and cysts. \u000aSclerosing adenosis. \u000aCalcifications associated with atypical ductal hyperplasia and with \u000abenign epithelium. \u000aNOTE: Selected slides have been reviewed by Dr. Stuart Schnitt who \u000aconcurs with the interpretation of ADH bordering on DCIS. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 52 year old postmenopausal female on HRT, whose REMOVED_DATE mammograms \u000ademonstrated a 1cm right breast UOQ cluster of calcifications, not amenable to \u000acore biopsy. \u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization excision \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast mass (short stitch/superior; long/lateral; \u000awhip stitch/deep margin) \u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications in specimen. J. Meyer,MD \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PADERA,ROBERT F.,JR.,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000aunit number and "#1. right breast mass". The specimen is received with a wire \u000ain place. The specimen is received with two orienting sutures. A double long \u000asuture indicates lateral and double short suture indicates superior. The \u000aspecimen has been inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; \u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen measures \u000a6.5cm from medial to lateral, 4.2cm from superior to inferior, and 1.2cm \u000afrom anterior to posterior. Serial sectioning of the breast reveals an area of \u000afirm fibrous tissue that is adjacent to the posterior margin over a length of \u000a2.8cm measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm in the other dimension. This fibrous area is \u000ainvolving the inferior margin, comes to within 0.2cm of the superior margin, \u000awithin 0.6cm of the anterior margin, 1.2cm from the medial margin, and 1.5cm \u000afrom the lateral margin. This area corresponds to the calcific density seen on \u000athe specimen radiograph. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely \u000asubmitted for histologic evaluation. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast mass, mult frags, ESS (the area of calcifications \u000aon the radiograph is primarily in blocks 5-12) \u000arp \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
