VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME -AVELLINO \u000aResident: Joanna A Gibson, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. RIGHT BREAST EXCISION, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia, adenosis, \u000aapocrine metaplasia, and calcifications associated with \u000abenign epithelium. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION: \u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia, columnar cell changes, and \u000acalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aCore biopsy site changes. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: R breast mass. \u000aOperation: R needle localized breast bx. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast mass. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1 - R beast bx - mammo. \u000aB/2 - additional R breast tissue - mammo. \u000aRADIOGRAPHY REPORT: Wire in first specimen. No clip seen in first or 2nd \u000aspecimen, and Dr. Iglehart was called. Dr. Raza, M.D. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "right breast biopsy", and consists of a wire localized breast \u000aexcision specimen, measuring 1.5cm superior to inferior, 2.5cm medial to \u000alateral, and 3.8cm anterior to posterior. The specimen has two undesignated \u000asutures, which are designated by pathology as follows: short=superior, \u000along=lateral. The specimen is inked in the pathology department per the \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A \u000alocalization wire protrudes from the medial surface. The specimen is received \u000awith a radiograph showing the wire and calcifications within the specimen. The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned into eight slices from anterior to posterior, \u000aand shows 50% adipose tissue admixed with white firm fibrous tissue. The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histological examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : anterior margin, perpendicular fragments, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : serial sections from anterior to posterior, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : posterior margin, perpendicular fragments, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "additional right breast tissue", and consists of an unoriented \u000asmall breast excision (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm ). White bead-like foreign material \u000ais embedded in the tissue at one end. The entire specimen is inked and \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : additional right breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS. \u000aJGI/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Joanna A Gibson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a10/17/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
