VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Michael H Roh, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR A CLIP: \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU. \u000aExtensive atypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread and focally \u000ainvolving adenosis (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aCore biopsy site. \u000aIntraductal papilloma (0.5cm ) with epithelial hyperplasia and focal \u000ainvolvement by LCIS. \u000aColumnar cell changes. \u000aApocrine metaplasia. \u000aImmunohistochemical studies for p63/ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID / REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and E-cadherin \u000aconfirm the presence of myoepithelial cells surrounding foci \u000aof LCIS with loss of E-cadherin expression. \u000aNOTE: \u000aThis case has been reviewed by Dr. Deborah Dillon, Breast Pathology Service, \u000awho concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Core biopsies with LCIS and atypical papilloma. \u000aOperation: Needle localized left breast biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammo. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) left breast wire localized biopsy, short stitch/superior, long \u000astitch/lateral - fs room mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aClip in specimen with wire. OR called 12:40. LBT \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number, \u000aand "left breast wire localized biopsy", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm \u000aovoid fragment of fibrofatty tissue with two orienting sutures: short \u000astitch=superior, and long stitch=lateral. The margins are inked according to \u000athe pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. \u000aThere is a needle localization wire in situ, which enters at the medial aspect. \u000aThere is also a 2cm defect at the medial margin. The specimen is also \u000aaccompanied by two identical x-rays with a circled area of interest around a \u000asmall metal clip. There is a pink sheet with a notation "clip in specimen with \u000awire. OR called at 12:40". The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to \u000alateral showing the tip of the wire to terminate at the lateral margin. The \u000acut surface shows a pale pink/white fibrous tissue with a moderate amount of \u000afat and the mid-portion of the specimen shows a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  somewhat \u000acircumscribed area containing friable radiopaque injected material along with \u000athe metal clip. There is also adjacent focal fresh hemorrhage. The injected \u000aarea corresponds to the circled area of interest on the radiograph and is \u000alocated 0.2cm from the posterior margin, 0.5cm from the inferior margin, and \u000a0.5cm from the anterior margin. A mass lesion is not seen. The specimen is \u000aentirely submitted from medial to lateral, respectively in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : perpendicular medial margin, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : medial breast tissue, 2 frags and 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : area of interest with all surrounding margins, 1 frag each, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : area of interest with tissue containing metal clip, 1 frag, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : lateral breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : perpendicular lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000awp/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a4/11/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
