ogy protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. A specimen radiogram accompanies the specimen demonstrating \u000athe wire, clip, and calcifications within the specimen. The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral demonstrating a white/yellow firm \u000aarea with irregular borders (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm ) extending to the posterior, \u000ainferior, and superior margins, 1.6cm of the anterior surface, less than REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the medial surface, and 1.2cm of the closest lateral surface. A clip \u000ais identified within the fibrous area in slice #5. The remainder of the \u000abreast tissue is comprised of 80-90% adipose tissue and grossly unremarkable. \u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #1, medial most, perpendicular, 9 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #2, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #3, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #4, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #5 with clip contained in micro 11, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #6, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #7, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #8, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #9, lateral most, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS. \u000ajhc \u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
