VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Astrid Weins, M.D., Ph.D.; Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.; Deborah A Dillon, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION: \u000aBiopsy site changes with ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA, sclerosing adenosis with \u000amicrocalcifications, apocrine cysts with cyst rupture and columnar cell change. \u000aSpecial studies performed at BWH demonstrate the following profile in atypical \u000alobular hyperplasia: \u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE \u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /NEU NEGATIVE (0) \u000aE-CADHERIN NEGATIVE \u000aNOTE: Findings support the above diagnosis. Slides also seen by Dr. Deborah \u000aDillon (Breast Pathology), who concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 48 year old woman, S/P L breast UOQ core biopsy REMOVED_DATE revealing ALH \u000awith recommendation for excision. Previous surgery: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aOperation: L breast WL bx. \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) left breast tissue, short suture/superior, long/lateral, whip stitch on \u000adeep margin --> mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aMR - clip and intact wire in specimen. Called to Dr. Rhei in OR by Dr. Yeh. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen was received fresh in one part, and labeled with the patient's \u000aname, medical record number and "#1. Left breast tissue, short suture superior, \u000along lateral, whip stitch on deep margin - mammo.", The specimen consists of \u000aone lumpectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm and weighing 18 g \u000apostfixation. The lateral aspect is designated with a long stitch, the \u000asuperior with a short stitch and the deep margin with a whip stitch. There is \u000aa wire entering the specimen on its inferior aspect and exiting the specimen \u000abetween anterior and medial aspect. The specimen is previously inked by the \u000asurgeon. It was accompanied by a radiology report reading "MR clip and intact \u000awire in specimen." The specimen was sectioned to reveal a biopsy cavity (1.5 x \u000a1.0 x 0.5cm ) present 0.5cm from the medial, 0.5cm from the posterior, 1.5cm \u000afrom the inferior, 0.8cm from the superior, 2.0cm from the lateral and 2.0cm \u000afrom the anterior margins. It is surrounded by firm, white fibrous tissue with \u000asporadic hemorrhagic areas. The specimen was entirely submitted from medial to \u000alateral. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lumpectomy specimen, sectioned from medial to lateral, 1 to 4 \u000afrags, each, ESS. The biopsy cavity is present in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , the \u000aclip is found in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aAWE/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
