VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS: \u000aFibrocystic changes with dense interlobular fibrosis. \u000aFocal mild epithelial hyperplasia (3). \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present involving one (1) duct; levels \u000aexamined. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 51 yo female, not on hormones, family history of breast cancer in \u000athe mother (46). REMOVED_DATE mammograms demonstrate a 1cm irregular density in the \u000ainferior R breast without ultrasound correlate, too faint for core biopsy. \u000aOperation: R breast wire localization excision. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal R mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: S/L right breast tissue, short stitch - sup; long stitch - \u000alat; whip - deep margins. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Representative tissue present. C.Denison, MD \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CULPEPPER,KELIEGH S.,M.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000aunit number and "right breast tissue, short stitch super, long lateral, whip \u000adeep margin", and consists of two pieces of fibroadipose tissue, the larger \u000apiece measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm  It is received inked by the surgeon per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior \u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. A \u000awire is present which inserts at the border of the inferior lateral margin. A \u000ashort stitch is present in the red inked area, a whip stitch is present in the \u000ablack inked area, no long stitch is identified. A second piece of fibroadipose \u000atissue is present that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm  This one appears to have \u000asome yellow and some black as well as green ink. A radiograph is included \u000awhich demonstrates a wire in place. A portion on the radiograph is circled \u000awhich corresponds to red inked portion of the specimen. The tip of the wire \u000ainserts at the opposite end towards the inferior part of the specimen. Upon \u000asectioning the specimen is approximately 80% adipose tissue. In the superior \u000aregion of the specimen, there is a large area of fibrous tissue. In the \u000ainferior portion of the specimen where the wire localized, there are no \u000agrossly appreciable lesions. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior portion of breast tissue, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 16: loose portion of fibroadipose tissue, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aksc \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
