e evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; \u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. On the specimen \u000aradiograph, the area of the clip is potentially abutting the anterior margin of \u000athe specimen and the area of residual calcification is potentially abutting the \u000aposterior margin of the specimen. The specimen is bisected along the \u000alocalization wire. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm tan firm area of possible \u000aprior biopsy site. The firm area abuts the anterior margin, and is located REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the superior, 0.4cm from the medial 0.3cm from the inferior, 1.0cm \u000afrom the anterior, and 1.7cm from the lateral margin. The entire specimen is \u000asubmitted for microscopic analysis. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral aspect of the specimen, perpendicular sections, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Specimen serially sectioned from medial to lateral (full \u000acalcifications in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; possible core biopsy site in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial aspect of the specimen, perpendicular sections, ESS. \u000aSK/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a7/18/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
