00aindicate the deep margin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; \u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Cut section reveals a \u000alarge cavity (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ) with adjacent areas of hemorrhage measuring \u000a0.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm  The specimen is serially sectioned \u000afrom superior to inferior and entirely submitted for histological evaluation. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast mass from superior to inferior, multi frags, ESS. \u000aAn accompanying radiograph demonstrates calcifications within the specimen and \u000aa single localizing wire. \u000adk \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
