ults reported in an \u000aaddendum. \u000aNOTE: The CIS in both biopsies has areas of slightly higher nuclear grade than \u000atypically seen in classic LCIS. No necrosis or calcifications are associated \u000awith the CIS. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHISTORY: Site #1: Site 54 y. o. with strong family hx of breast cancer. Now \u000a7-mm mass with indistinct and angular margin LLIQ, 7:00, 3cm from the nipple. \u000aAdditional site of concern 7:00, 8cm from the nipple = biopsy site #2 (see \u000apage 2). \u000aSite #2: 54 with strong family hx breast cancer. new vague focal density \u000aposterior LLIQ with subtle distortion, shadowing on U/S @ 7:00, 8cm from \u000anipple. Additional 7-mm mass @ 7:0, N+3cm = biopsy site #1 (see page 1) \u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING: \u000a1. Left: 7-mm, Nonpalpable and irregular mass. \u000a2. Left: ~5mm  Nonpalpable, architectural distortion and ? ill-defined mass. \u000aLOCATION: \u000a1. Left: lower inner \u000a2. Left: lower inner \u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY: \u000a1. 14G Ultrasound \u000a2. 14G Ultrasound \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Biopsy site #1: 1:00 p.m. in formalin, 7:00 N+3 lesion round mass with \u000aangular margin. - 1 blue cassette. \u000aB/2. Biopsy site #2: vague mass density LLIQ + arch. distort/? mass on U/S \u000a7:00 N+8cm  in formalin @ 1:30 p.m. - 1 pink cassette. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the \u000apatient's name, unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "left breast", consists of a blue cassette containing multiple \u000acylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm in \u000aaggregate), which are submitted in toto. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Contents of blue cassette, multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "left breast #2", consists of a pink cassette containing \u000amultiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.3cm in aggregate), which are submitted in toto. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Contents of pink cassette, multi frags, ESS. \u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone \u000areceptor, and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis \u000ausing the following criteria: \u000aHormone receptor analysis: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not \u000ayet been determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% \u000aof tumor cells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor \u000acells but only a portion of the membrane is positive. \u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in >30% of tumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for \u000ainvestigational use only. \u000aJC/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 17,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04:50:39PM \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (11/23/09) \u000aFISH was performed by Clarient using the PathVysion HER-2 DNA Probe Kit with \u000athe following (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aResults: NOT AMPLIFIED \u000aHER-2/CEP-17 ratio = REM