VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s) \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-10- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Elgida Radoncipi, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES (including FSA): \u000aSee part B \u000aB. LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY FOR ENHANCING AREA ON MRI AND CLIPS AND \u000aSENTINEL NODE BIOPSY (PARTS A AND B): \u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, 2 FOCI, LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU AND \u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODES. \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aSize - 1.7cm and 0.9cm ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) \u000aMultifocal - Yes (see note) \u000aHistologic type - Lobular \u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) (6 to 7 points) \u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points) \u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate (2 points) \u000aMitotic counts - 1 point \u000aEIC - Not applicable \u000aLVI - Absent \u000aDermal LVI - Absent \u000aSkin invasion - Absent \u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable \u000aFinal Margins (invasive) \u000aClose (0.1 to 0.3cm ) - 0.2cm from deep ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present \u000aLYMPH NODES \u000aSentinel lymph nodes - Negative (3 H&E levels examined) \u000aExtranodal extension - Absent \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aCore biopsy sites \u000aColumna cell changes \u000aCalcifications in benign breast epithelium \u000aAJCC Classification (7th edition):  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID c  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (sn) Mx. \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) - Performed previously at BWH \u000aA double stain for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID / REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and p63 was performed for the final diagnosis. \u000aNOTE: \u000aTwo (2) foci of invasive lobular carcinoma are identified, measuring 1.7cm on \u000aslide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and 0.9cm on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , associated with LCIS and core biopsy site \u000achanges. \u000aC. LEFT MASTECTOMY, SKIN: \u000aSkin and subcutaneous tissue, negative for tumor. \u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests \u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance \u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the \u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the \u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such \u000aclearance or approval is not necessary. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 54 year-old postmenopausal female, not on hormones with family history \u000anotable for 2 sisters with breast cancer. REMOVED_DATE MMG supplemented with u/s \u000ademonstrates a L LIQ mass + architectural distortion. REMOVED_DATE core biopsy of \u000athe mass demonstrates DCIS, architectural distortion revealed grade II, ER/PR \u000apositive  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /Neu negative invasive lobular carcinoma. REMOVED_DATE core biopsy of \u000aan MRI enhancing mass revealed grade II ER/PR positive her 2 neu negative ILC \u000aOperation: L simple mastectomy, sentinel node mapping, biopsy + possible \u000aaxillary dissection with time expander reconstruction \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided \u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast cancer, ATTN: specimen must be radiographed by \u000apathology prior to processing 3 clips to identify \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA. Left sentinel node hot & blue FS \u000aB. Left breast short suture superior, long lateral \u000aC. Left mastectomy skin \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1. LEFT SENTINEL NODE, HOT AND BLUE" (FSA): \u000aLymph node, negative for tumor. \u000aOR Consultation by: William Robert Welch, M.D. \u000aResident: Paul A. VanderLaan, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A is labeled "#1. Left sentinel node hot and blue", and consists of \u000ayellow/tan aggregate of fatty tissue with a blue lymph node (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). The lymph node was bisected and entirely submitted for frozen section \u000aexamination as FSA. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of fibrofatty tissue, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart B is labeled "#2. Left breast, short suture superior, long lateral", and \u000aconsists of a 960-gram simple mastectomy specimen (25.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 6.0cm ) with \u000awhite/tan skin ellipse (12.5 x 4.6cm ). The deep margin is inked black and \u000agrossly no muscle tissue is identified. The specimen is serially sectioned \u000afrom medial to lateral to reveal three biopsy site cavities each associated \u000awith a clip. The first clip is located in the lower inner quadrant \u000aapproximately 7 o'clock and designates an ill-defined white/tan area (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 0.5cm ), 0.5cm from the closest deep margin. This area is entirely \u000asubmitted for microscopic examination ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). The second clip is found within \u000athe biopsy cavity (0.3cm in diameter), located in the lower inner quadrant at \u000aapproximately 7 o'clock, anterior to the first clip approximately 4.0cm away \u000afrom the first clip, and 3cm for the deep margin. The biopsy cavity and \u000asurrounding fibrous tissue are entirely submitted for microscopic \u000aexamination( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). The third biopsy cavity (0.7cm in diameter) with clip is \u000aidentified in the upper inner quadrant and is filled with organizing red/tan \u000aclot. The clip marks an ill-defined white/tan fibrotic area (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), 2.0cm from the closest deep margin. This is entirely submitted for \u000amicroscopic examination in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (the more medial slice), and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (the \u000amore lateral slice). The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of \u000aapproximately 50% fibroadipose tissue and 50% fibrofatty tissue. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : First biopsy site, 1 frag in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Second biopsy site, 1 frag in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Third biopsy site, 1 frag in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aPart C is labeled "#3. Left mastectomy skin", and consists of a fragment of \u000askin, 17.0cm in length, excised to a depth of 1.0cm  composed of fibrofatty \u000atissue. Representative sections are submitted for microscopic examination \u000agrossly. There is no evidence of any tumor infiltration. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aERV/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 20,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06:50:55PM \u000a[report_end] 
