VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aCONSULT SLIDES AND PARAFFIN BLOCKS FROM HALLMARK HEALTH, LAWRENCE MEMORIAL \u000aHOSPITAL, MEDFORD, MA: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : REMOVED_CASE_ID ; 11/1/02): \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, is present as a 0.4cm focus in two of six \u000ablocks (E and F; levels examined) (see note). Calcifications are \u000aassociated with ADH. This area is 0.1cm from the closest margin. \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread. \u000aComplex sclerosing lesions (radial scars). \u000aNote: The area of ADH consists of a cluster of ductal spaces lined by \u000acolumnar cells with occasional bridges and micropapillae. The findings \u000aare insufficient for a diagnosis of DCIS. \u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Andrea Richardson who concurs with this \u000ainterpretation. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides and paraffin blocks. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PREISINGER,ELIZABETH ANN,M.D. \u000aReceived from Lawrence Memorial Hospital, Pathology Department, 170 Governors \u000aAvenue, Medford, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID , are six (6) slides and two paraffin blocks. \u000aThe slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled "A" and "B"( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), \u000acorresponding to a left breast wire needle localization biopsy (4.8 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a2.0cm ) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report \u000abearing the patient's name (original diagnosis: "Focus of atypical \u000apapillomatosis bordering on DCIS, atypical lobular hyperplasia"). The blocks \u000aare labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled "E" and "F". \u000aIncluded is a consultation report from Boston Medical Center, Boston, MA; their \u000aaccession number " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", dated REMOVED_DATE  referring to the above case \u000anumbered " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " from Lawrence Memorial Hospital, Medford, MA; bearing the \u000apatient's name (outside diagnosis: "Focal atypical ductal and atypical lobular \u000ahyperplasia"). \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST \u000a[report_end] 
