en is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1. Left breast and axillary contents, stitch on axillary tail", consists \u000aof a left modified radical mastectomy ( REMOVED_CASE_ID  g, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5.5cm ). There is \u000aa suture designating the axillary tail (10.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm ). There is an \u000aoverlying tan/pink skin ellipse (27.0 x 21.0cm ), with a pink-white well healed \u000airregular scar (4.0 x 1.3cm ). The scar is 3.5cm lateral to the \u000anipple-areolar complex (5.0 x 4.0cm ), located at the 3 o'clock position. \u000aThere is an unremarkable everted nipple (1.3cm in diameter). The posterior \u000amargin is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a \u000awhite-yellow, focally hemorrhagic ill-defined irregular mass (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), 4.0cm from the closest black-inked deep margin. The mass is located \u000abetween the upper inner and upper outer quadrants, and is 8.0cm superior to \u000athe nipple, at the 12 o'clock position. The remaining cut surface displays 30% \u000afocally dense white fibrous tissue, and 70% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, \u000awith no additional discrete masses or lesions identified. Multiple lymph nodes \u000aare identified within the axillary tail region, ranging from 0.4cm  to 2.5cm \u000ain greatest dimension. The lymph nodes are selectively bisected, to reveal \u000atan-pink cut surfaces. Representative sections are submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple and well-healed scar, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : White-yellow focally hemorrhagic mass at the 12 o'clock position, \u000asequentially from medial to lateral, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Corresponding black-inked posterior margin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Dense white fibrous tissue from the upper outer quadrant, to \u000ainclude the posterior margin at  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 frags 