VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCIBAS, EDMUND, SAULIUS, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CIBAS,EDMUND SAULIUS,M.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, CENTRAL DUCT EXCISION: \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (blocks 10, 14, and 15). \u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent apocrine snouts, with \u000aatypia. \u000aFibrocystic change, with apocrine cysts, papillomatosis, florid \u000acolumnar and ductal hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis, and complex \u000asclerosing lesions. \u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aFibroadenoma (block 10). \u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson who concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: History of left breast ca. Status post left central duct excision \u000a2/26/03 with LCIS. History of lobular carcinoma in situ left breast. \u000aOperation: Right breast central duct excision. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right nipple discharge. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast central duct excision. \u000aStitch markings = short suture superior, long suture lateral. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by REIMANN,JULIE DYLAN REGAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1. Right breast central duct excision with stitch markings", and \u000aconsists of one yellow/tan fragment of soft tissue (4.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm ) with a \u000ashort stitch marking superior and a long stitch marking lateral. The specimen \u000ais inked by the pathologist per pathology protocol for the evaluation of \u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; \u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned \u000amedially to laterally to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm cyst surrounded by \u000awhite/tan fibrous tissue, which grossly extends to the anterior margin, to the \u000aposterior margin, to the medial margin, 1.5cm from the superior margin, and \u000ato the inferior margin, and 2.3cm from the lateral margin. There is a second \u000awhite/tan firm illdefined area (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ) located at the lateral \u000amargin, at the posterior margin, 2.5cm from the medial margin, 1.0cm from \u000athe anterior margin, at the inferior margin, and at the superior margin. The \u000aremainder of the specimen is composed of approximately 40% fibrous tissue and \u000athe rest is adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro 1: Cystic lesion with medial, anterior, posterior, inferior margins, 1 \u000afrag, ESS. \u000aMicro 2: Area adjacent to first lesion with posterior, anterior, superior \u000amargin, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 3: Area adjacent to cystic lesion with medial, anterior, posterior, \u000ainferior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 4: Area adjacent to cystic lesion with anterior, posterior, superior, 1 \u000afrag, ESS. \u000aMicro 5: Fibrous tissue nearest to cystic lesion with medial, anterior, \u000aposterior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 6: Fibrous tissue near cystic lesion lesion with superior, anterior, \u000aposterior margins, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 7: Fibrous tissue near cystic lesion with posterior, medial margins, 2 \u000afrags, ESS. \u000aMicro 8: Fibrous tissue near cystic lesion with medial, anterior, posterior, \u000asuperior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 9: Medial, anterior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 10: Second lesion with lateral, superior, posterior margins, 2 frags, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro 11: Second lesion with posterior, lateral, inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 12: Second lesion with inferior, posterior margin, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 13: Second lesion with lateral, superior, posterior, anterior margins, 1 \u000afrag, ESS. \u000aMicro 14: Fibrous tissue adjacent to second lesion with inferior, posterior, \u000alateral margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 15: Anterior, posterior, inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 16: Anterior, posterior, superior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 17: Superior, anterior, posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 18: Inferior, posterior, lateral margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro 19: Inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS. \u000ajdr \u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
