 The \u000aspecimen is inked in the pathology department per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. Serial sectioning demonstrates \u000afibrous tissue without discrete nodules. Approximately 20% of the specimen is \u000aadipose tissue. The specimen is entirely and serially submitted for histologic \u000aevaluation. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : left breast tissue, medial to lateral, 10 frags, ESS. \u000aPab/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Patricia A. R. Brunker M.D., D. Phil., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
