/green; \u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral \u000ato medial, revealing a white/tan, focally cystic, ill-defined fibrous area (3.2 \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm ), which extends to the inferior, posterior, anterior, medial, \u000aand lateral margins and comes to within 0.1cm of the superior margin. The \u000aneedle-localization wire traverses this area and coincides with the \u000aaccompanying radiograph and confirmation per radiology. The remaining breast \u000atissue consists of yellow/tan, lobulated fat. No other gross lesions are \u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely submitted sequentially from lateral to \u000amedial. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : breast tissue sequentially from lateral to medial, multiple \u000afrags, ESS \u000aDFI/jp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Marianna B Ruzinova M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Thomas Brenn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a11/28/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
