VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Marianna B Ruzinova, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.; Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION OF MASS, UPPER OUTER \u000aQUADRANT": \u000aBreast tissue with LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, atypical lobular \u000ahyperplasia, columnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and \u000asecretions, and epithelial hyperplasia involving a nodular area \u000aconsistent with hamartoma (~2.3cm ). \u000aCore bx site changes. \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU and atypical lobular hyperplasia is extensive \u000awithin the lesion. \u000aNOTE: Focally, the CARCINOMA IN SITU exhibits high-grade nuclei and \u000aindividual cell necrosis. However, immunohistochemical stain for \u000ae-cadherin is negative for these cells. \u000aB. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION OF LESION AT 5:30, \u000aSTITCH MARKING, SHORT EQUALS SUPERIOR, LONG EQUALS LATERAL": \u000aBreast tissue with portion of intraductal papilloma, epithelial \u000ahyperplasia and apocrine fibrocystic changes. \u000aCore biopsy site changes at lateral end of specimen. \u000aMicrofibroadenoma (0.6cm ). \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 52-year-old female with left breast mass x2. \u000aOperation: Left breast-guided wire localized excision with biopsy x2. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass x2. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Left breast wire-localized excision of mass, upper outer quadrant. \u000aStitch marking, short equals superior long equals lateral, prosection mammo. \u000aB/2. Left breast wire-localized excision of lesion at 5:30, stitch marking, \u000ashort equals superior, long equals lateral. \u000aRADIOLOGY: ? density on x-ray plus clip present; hypoechoic mass vs lobule on \u000aU.S. of specimen. MN  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aNo clip in specimen. ? mass seen on U.S.. d/w Dr. J. Jones, NM  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast wire-localized excision mass, upper outer quadrant, \u000ashort superior, long lateral", consists of a firm tan/white to tan/yellow \u000afibrofatty portion of breast tissue (2.6 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.6cm ) short suture marking \u000asuperior and long suture marking lateral. The specimen is previously \u000aradiographed (per radiologist "? density on x-ray, positive clip present \u000ahypoechoic mass versus lobule on ultrasound of specimen"). The prosector \u000aconcurs and notes that a clip and a mass are within the specimen (the specimen \u000ais inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange). \u000aThe localization wire enters the specimen at the lateral posterior aspect. The \u000aspecimen is sectioned from the lateral to medial aspect show a parenchyma \u000aconsisting lobulated tan/white to tan/pink, dense, focally cystic fibrous \u000atissue (98% of specimen) with focal calcification (98%) with scant tan/yellow \u000alobulated fat. The clip is identified. No other lesions are grossly \u000aidentified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Specimen serially sectioned with the section that contains the \u000aclip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , multi frags total, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast wire-localized excision of lesion at 5:30, stitch \u000ashort equals superior, long equals lateral", consists of an irregular tan/pink \u000ato tan/yellow fibrofatty breast tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ). The specimen has \u000aa short suture marking superior and long suture marking lateral. The specimen \u000ais previously radiographed (per radiologist "no clip in specimen, ? mass seen \u000aon ultrasound. Discussed with Dr. Jones". The prosector concurs and notes \u000athat there is no clip found in the specimen, and that the specimen appears to \u000abe made up of lobulated large tissue. The new localization wire enters the \u000aspecimen in the lateral aspect and exits the specimen at the posterior medial \u000aaspect. The specimen is sectioned from the mediolateral aspect to show a cut \u000asurface consisting of tan/pink fibrous tissue (50%) with tan/yellow lobulated \u000afat. Fibrous tissue is focally cystic and has focal application. No other \u000alesions are grossly identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Specimen is serially sectioned and submitted, multi frags, ESS. \u000aDRD/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
