p \u000ais identified in the center of the specimen adjacent to the localization wire. \u000aNo definitive masses or lesions identified. The outer surface of the specimen \u000ais inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned and sequentially \u000asubmitted in its entirety. The specimen is received with a radiograph and \u000aradiograph report stating that a clip and wire are seen within the specimen. \u000aThe radiograph shows a clip present within the specimen adjacent to the \u000alocalization wire. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Side margin (perpendicular), 5 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Serial sections sequentially submitted with clip site in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 complete cross sections in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and 1 complete cross section in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , incomplete cross section in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Side margin, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Additional Rt breast tissue", consists of an unoriented \u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm ) made up of approximately \u000a95% and 5% fibrous tissue with one focus of recent hemorrhage. No definitive \u000amasses or lesions are identified. The outer surface is inked black, and the \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted for histologic \u000aexamination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Side margin (perpendicular), 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Complete cross sections, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Side margin (perpendicular), 4 frags, ESS. \u000aOOB/md/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
