VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Leona A. Doyle, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. LEFT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE LOCALIZED FOR A CLIP: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) \u000aBiopsy site changes \u000aColumnar cell changes with cysts and flat epithelial atypia. \u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for final diagnosis. \u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. J. Brock, Breast Pathology Service, \u000awho concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 74 year old woman, S/P REMOVED_DATE L breast wire bxs revealing ADH with \u000aexcision recommended. \u000aOperation: L breast wire loc bx. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left abnormal mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) left breast tissue, short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral, deep \u000astitch/wide. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aClip and intact wire are present in specimen. Dr. Yeh phoned to Dr. Rhei in OR \u000a- 10:55 am. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, and medical \u000arecord number, and "#1. Left breast tissue short stitch/superior, long \u000astitch/lateral and deep stitch/wide", and consists of a 39.0-gram breast \u000aexcision (3.0cm superior to inferior, 6.0cm medial to lateral, and 2.5cm \u000aanterior to posterior) with orienting sutures designating superior, lateral and \u000adeep aspects. The specimen is inked by surgeon per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is disrupted at \u000athe deep and superior aspects. An accompanying specimen radiography \u000ademonstrates a localization wire entering the specimen and is associated with a \u000ametal clip and single calcification. There is an area of fat necrosis and \u000afibrosis (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ) extending to the medial and superior margins and \u000a0.6cm to the inferior margin, greater than 1.0cm from the lateral inferior \u000aand deep margins. This area is associated with a metallic clip and the wire. \u000aIn addition, there is a separate firm circumscribed nodule (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), 0.2cm to the superior aspect. The remaining breast parenchyma comprises \u000aless than 5% fibrous tissue and greater than 95% of adipose tissue. An area of \u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm surrounding the biopsy site is submitted in \u000aaddition to the second nodule and all fibrous breast parenchyma. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire area surrounding biopsy site to include closest margins, \u000a1-2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Second nodule, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining margins, REMOVED_DATE frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining fibrous tissue, multi frags, ESS. \u000aLDO/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000aWednesday February 11,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03:33:40PM \u000a[report_end] 
