mined) \u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0 \u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3 \u000aOTHER FINDINGS Columnar cell changes \u000aADH \u000aCore biopsy site \u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition):  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID b s REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Mx with two foci of invasion. \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (on  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) (ER, PR,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) - Pending \u000aNOTE: Double stain performed (p63,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID / REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  demonstrates \u000aloss of myoepithelial cells in the invasive component. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 62 year old woman with DCIS documented in 2 quadrants by stereotactic \u000acore biopsy for microcalcifications. Clips placed in L UIQ + L UOQ. \u000aOperation: Left SLN biopsy, left simple mastectomy. \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast DCIS. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) SLN L. \u000aB/2) SLN #2. \u000aC/3) SLN #3. \u000aD/4) L breast, suture on tail of Spence. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 - SLN" ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aLymph node negative for tumor. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2 - SLN #2" (FSB): \u000aLymph node negative for tumor. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#3 - SENTINEL NODE #3" (FSC): \u000aNegative for tumor. \u000aOR Consultation by: VANIA NOSE, M.D., PH.D. \u000aResident: ANNA LAURY, M.D. \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in four parts, labeled with the patient's name \u000aand unit number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Sentinel lymph node #1", consists of one fragment of soft tissue \u000a(2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ). The specimen was bisected and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aand  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Sentinel node #2", consists of one fragment of red/yellow \u000afibroadipose tissue (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ). The specimen was bisected and \u000aentirely submitted as FSB. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : FSB remnant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart C, "#3. Sentinel node #3", consists of one fragment of fibroadipose tissue \u000a(1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ). The specimen was bisected and entirely submitted as FSC. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : FSC remnant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart D, "#4. Left breast", consists of a 686-g simple mastectomy specimen with \u000astitch designating the tail (22.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 4.5cm ) with attached skin ellipse \u000a(4.1 x 3.5cm ). One clip (#1) is found in the upper inner quadrant with an \u000aill-defined fibrotic area (10.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 4.8cm ), 4.0cm from the deep margin \u000a(inked in black) is a smooth fascial plane with no skeletal muscle attached. A \u000asecond clip was found in the outer upper quadrant an ill-defined fibrotic area \u000a(3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ), located 4.5cm from the deep resection margin. An ill \u000adefined tan/white firm area (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ) in the lower outer quadrant is \u000a3cm from the closest deep resection margin, 4.5cm from the clip #1, 3cm from \u000athe clip #2. No additional lesion is identified. The remainder of the breast \u000aparenchyma is predominantly white and yellow fibroadipose tissue. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Clip #1 site, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Clip #2 site, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Firm area in the lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Closest deep margin to clip #1 site, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Closest deep margin to clip #2 site, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of fibrotic firm area in lower outer quadrant, multi \u000afrags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Closest deep margin to lower outer quadrant firm area, 1 frag, \u000aRSS. \u000aLC/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher D. M. Fletcher M.D. FRCPath, Electronically \u000asigned on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block d12): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) NEGATIVE (0) \u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen \u000aand progesterone receptors. \u000aInterpretation: \u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the \u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet \u000abeen determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a \u000aportion of