0% fibrous tissue, the \u000arest is adipose tissue. A radiograph is taken by the pathologist and the clip \u000ais located. The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro 1: medial margin, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro 2: medial and inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro 3: medial and inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro 4: medial and inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro 5: medial, inferior and posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro 6: anterior and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro 7: superior, posterior and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro 8: superior, anterior margins, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro 9: superior, posterior and inferior margins, 1 frag, (this \u000afragment contains the clip), ESS \u000aMicro 10: superior, posterior, and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro 11: inferior, posterior and superior margins, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro 12: superior, anterior, and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro 13: posterior and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro 14: lateral and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro 15: lateral and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS \u000aNOTE: (micros 5 through 10 contain core biopsy site) \u000ajdr \u000aReports to: GOLSHAN, MEHRA M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
