rior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior)cm \u000abreast biopsy with a localization wire in the specimen container. An \u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates calcifications and wire in the \u000aspecimen. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The parenchyma consists of \u000aapproximately 80% adipose tissue and 20% white fibrous tissue without gross \u000alesions. The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 8 frags, ESS. \u000amah \u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
