00acm superior to inferior, 2.5cm anterior to posterior, and 3.5cm medial to \u000alateral. There is one wire in the specimen in the lateral/superior portion. \u000aThe superior portion of the specimen is almost entirely fibrous tissue, whereas \u000athe remaining 60% of the specimen is a mix of roughly 60% adipose and 40% \u000afibrous tissue. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : superior portion of specimen with clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag in \u000aeach, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : anterior, posterior and medial margins with fibrous tissue, \u000a1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : inferior margin, 1 frag in each, RSS. \u000a(NOTE: approximately 50% of the specimen and 75% of the fibrous tissue is \u000asubmitted.) \u000aPart B, labeled "#2 - additional left breast tissue" and consists of one \u000afragment of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 4 x 1.1cm  Half of the surface is \u000ainked in black, and the other half is inked in yellow by the surgeon. A biopsy \u000asite with gel-foam is identified in the central portion of the specimen \u000aabutting the black-inked margin. The gel-foam comes to within 0.4cm of the \u000ayellow-inked margin. The remainder of the cut surface consists entirely of \u000ayellow adipose tissue. The biopsy site cavity is submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : additional left breast tissue, 1 frag in each, RSS. \u000a(NOTE: approximately 60% of the specimen and 100% of the fibrous tissue have \u000abeen submitted.) \u000aESN/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a5/16/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
