VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BG-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Oname O. Burlingame, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Christopher P Crum, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP: \u000aColumnar cell change is present. \u000aThe prior core biopsy site is present, transected along the anterior margin. \u000aCalcifications are present in benign breast tissue. \u000aNote: The patient underwent a prior core needle biopsy for calcifications that \u000ashowed atypical ductal hyperplasia. No residual ADH is seen. The specimen was \u000aentirely submitted for histologic review, including margins. \u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, who concurs with this \u000ainterpretation. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Left breast atypical ductal hyperplasia, s/p image-guided core biopsy. \u000aOperation: Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: Not given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast atypical ductal hyperplasia. \u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Clip, soft tissue mass, and intact hookwire in specimen. \u000aDr. Small and Dr. Raza. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aLeft breast wire localized excisional biopsy (short superior, long lateral) \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen, received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and \u000a"#1. Lt breast wire localized excisional Bx (short superior, long lateral)", \u000aconsists of a yellow/tan, oriented breast biopsy specimen (3.3cm \u000asuperior-inferior, 2.8cm medial-lateral, 1.2cm anterior-posterior) with a \u000along surgical stitch indicating the lateral margin, a short surgical stitch \u000aindicating the superior margin, and a needle localization wire that enters the \u000aspecimen at the inferior lateral/anterior corner and exits the specimen at the \u000amiddle medial/posterior border. The specimen radiograph shows the wire and a \u000aclip within an ill-defined density. The specimen is inked per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; \u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is \u000asectioned parallel to the wire (approximately inferior to superior) into eleven \u000asections. No discrete masses are identified. No clip is identified. The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histologic evaluation serially from the \u000ainferior to the superior margins. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior most tissue, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy site and clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , wire in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of the specimen, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aOOB/am \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher P Crum M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a12/20/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
