VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP MARKING AN AREA OF BIOPSIED \u000aCALCIFICATIONS: \u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, associated with columnar and \u000asecretory type changes, is present predominantly adjacent to the prior \u000acore needle biopsy (best seen in the original slide of block 10 and \u000ablock 8) (see note). The ADH is immunoreactive for estrogen and \u000aprogesterone receptors and negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (1+). Calcifications are \u000aassociated with ADH. No necrosis is seen. \u000aNote: The entire specimen, including margins, was examined \u000amicroscopically. The areas of ADH of most concern are not close to \u000amargins (> 0.3cm ). \u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. James Connolly and Dr. Andrea \u000aRichardson who concur with this interpretation. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 50 year old female with an abnormal routine mammogram on REMOVED_DATE with \u000arepeat examination positive. She was referred to Dr. Iglehart for stereotactic \u000abx - REMOVED_DATE - which showed columnar alteration of lobules with atypia. Now \u000afor L needle localization. No family history of breast or GYN carcinoma. \u000aOperation: L needle loc breast mass excision. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram, L breast. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: L breast mass with needle loc. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and wire in place. OR called. Dr. Raza \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SANTAGATA,SANDRO,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000aunit number, and "L breast needle loc tissue", and consists of a 36-gram \u000abreast excision specimen that is marked by the surgeon with a long suture \u000aindicating the lateral position and a short suture indicating the superior \u000aposition. The specimen measures 5.9cm from anterior to posterior, 3.8cm from \u000amedial to lateral, and 2.2cm from superior to inferior. There is a wire \u000aentering the specimen at the anterior/lateral portion. The deep breast is \u000acomposed predominantly of 50% fibrous tissue and has a nodular focal area \u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm that is 0.6cm from the superior, 1.1cm from the \u000alateral, 0.8cm from the medial, 1.9cm from the inferior and 1.3cm from the \u000aanterior and 2.5cm from the posterior margins. There is a focal area of \u000ahemorrhage corresponding to the path of the wire used for localization. The \u000abreast parenchyma is diffusely nodular and no other remarkable lesions are \u000anoted. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of \u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = \u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is sectioned serially \u000afrom posterior to anterior and is entirely submitted. Micros 8 & 9 contain \u000afirm nodular areas. \u000aThe specimen radiograph is reviewd and reveals a clip, the localization wire, \u000aand two large solitary calcifications. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections from posterior to anterior, 29 frags, ESS. ssa \u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
