VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Michael A. Seidman, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aBreast tissue with focal epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, \u000acalcifications associated with benign breast epithelium, and \u000aextensive biopsy site changes. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the entire \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 39-yr-old woman found to have two nodules and separate area \u000amicrocalcifications on screening right mammogram. Two nodules had U/s core - \u000abenign. Microcalcifications had stereotactic cores at Faulkner Hospital and \u000aresulted as ADH. Recommended for surgical biopsy. \u000aOperation: Right wire localized breast biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right abnormal mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right breast tissue and wire - stitches: Short superior, long lateral. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name, \u000amedical record number, and "#1. Right breast tissue and wire -stitches: short \u000asuperior, long lateral", and consists of a partial mastectomy specimen (3.6cm \u000amedial to lateral, 2.9cm superior to inferior, 2.6cm anterior to posterior). \u000aThe specimen radiograph is reviewed on Centricity. Localization wire and two \u000abiopsy clips are identified and removed. Two sutures indicating superior and \u000alateral as per the surgeon are identified and removed. The specimen is \u000aapproximately 60% fibrous and 40% fatty, with fibrous tissue distributed \u000airregularly throughout the specimen. Site of prior biopsy, corresponding to \u000alocation of biopsy clips, is identified and consists of several firm, cystic, \u000acalcified lesions (0.2-0.4cm in diameter). Biopsy site and irregular tissue \u000ais submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Remaining tissue is also submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy site, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining tissue, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aSEI/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aFriday REMOVED_MONTH 16,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 07:14:21AM \u000a[report_end] 
