VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A CLIP: \u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL PROLIFERATION (see note). \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present. \u000aCalcifications are present in association with atypical epithelium and with \u000abenign epithelium. \u000aBiopsy site changes (see note). \u000aNOTE: Cytologic and architectural atypia are sufficient in multiple small foci \u000a(<0.1cm each) to warrant a diagnosis of ductal carcinoma in situ. These small \u000afoci are arising in a background of extensive columnar cell hyperplasia, \u000acolumnar cell hyperplasia with atypia and atypical ductal hyperplasia, present \u000ain seven of seven blocks. The close intermingling of these histologic changes \u000asuggests that they are part of the same biological process. Slides also \u000areviewed by Dr. Stuart Schnitt and Dr. Susan Lester, who agree with this \u000ainterpretation. \u000aHighly atypical epithelium is present within and adjacent to the previous core \u000aneedle tract and appears to have an absent or incomplete myoepithelial cell \u000alayer on immunohistochemistry for keratin/p63. Artifactual displacement of the \u000aatypical epithelium related to the previous core needle biopsy is favored. \u000aA spectrum of atypia is seen very close to multiple margins, ranging from foci \u000awith features of DCIS (inferior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), atypical ductal hyperplasia (posterior; \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), (superior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), to columnar cell hyperplasia with severe atypia (medial; \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), (anterior;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th edition) Tis NX MX. \u000aLEFT BREAST, SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN: \u000aSeverely ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA is present in three of three blocks, \u000afocally involving a papilloma. \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present. \u000aCalcifications are present in association with atypical epithelium and with \u000abenign epithelium. \u000aNOTE: Insufficient red ink is present for confident evaluation of the new \u000asuperior margin. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: ADH with microcalcs left breast. \u000aOperation: L needle localized breast biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: ADH with microcalcs - left breast \u000aRADIOGRAPHY REPORT: \u000a#1 - clip in specimen; #2 - wire in specimen. \u000aDr. Elman. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1 - tissue from left breast \u000aB/2 - left breast tissue, superior shave. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "#1 - tissue from left breast", consists of a breast excision \u000aspecimen, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm in overall dimensions. The specimen is \u000areceived inked by the surgeon. Yellow ink is not present. An accompanying \u000aradiograph shows a clip. No lesions are grossly identified. Eighty (80%) \u000apercent of the breast parenchyma is fibrous, and 20% is adipose tissue. The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : breast containing clip, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : additional breast parenchyma, multiple frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2 - left breast tissue, superior shave", consists of a breast \u000aexcision specimen previously inked by the surgeon with a needle localization \u000awire in place. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  An accompanying \u000aradiograph shows calcifications and a needle wire in place. The new margin is \u000ainked red. The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : breast, multiple frags, ESS. \u000aKEL/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Kevin B Long M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Kevin B Long M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Kevin B Long M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Review by Deborah A Dillon M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
