VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. LEFT BREAST, TISSUE": \u000aBenign breast tissue. \u000aMultiple blood vessels with intramural medial calcification. \u000aOne (1) lymph node with no significant pathologic change. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "ANTERIOR MEDIAL SHAVE MARGIN": \u000aFocus of atypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aExtensive calcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000aNOTE: Portion of the case reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, who concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 69 yo female s/p REMOVED_DATE mammograms with L breast UIQ 11:00 axis \u000acalcifications for which biopsy is recommended, not amenable to \u000acore biopsy. \u000aOperation: L breast WL excision. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: L mammographic calcification. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue - short stitch superior, long stitch \u000alateral, whip stitch chest wall margin. \u000a2. Anterior medial shave margin - whip stitch on new margin. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen 1: Wire and a few ca++. \u000aSpecimen 2: Few more calcs. OR called./sr \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SANTAGATA,SANDRO,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, labeled with the patient's name \u000aand medical record number. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1 left breast tissue short superior, long lateral, whip \u000astitch on chest wall margin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm breast excision \u000aspecimen that was marked by the surgeon with a long suture indicating the \u000alateral pole and a short suture indicating the superior pole. There is a \u000alocalizing wire at the edge of the specimen through the inferior margin and \u000alocalizes a radiopaque lesion as noted on the radiograph. The radiograph also \u000aindicates there are some calcifications along the putative superior margin. \u000aThe specimen was six-inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; \u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. On sectioning the wire \u000alocalized area is hemorrhagic and composed of fibrous tissue. The superior \u000aarea of the specimen contains foci of firm tissue consistent with \u000acalcifications. The specimen is serially sectioned from inferior to superior \u000aand entirely submitted. \u000aMicro 1: inferior margin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro 2: path of wire, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen from inferior to superior, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2 anterior medial shave margin", consists of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.6cm breast excision specimen with a whip stitch placed by the surgeon \u000aindicating the new margin (inked blue). The old margin is focally cauterized \u000awith areas of focal hemorrhage (inked black). The radiograph reveals multiple \u000adiffuse calcifications and two nodules present in apparent fibrous tissue. The \u000afibrous area measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm and extends to involve both the \u000ablue-inked and black-inked margins. The specimen is serially sectioned and \u000aentirely submitted. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous area with calcifications, 10 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, focally fibrotic, 4 frags, ESS. \u000assa \u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
