PECIMEN LABELED "SENTINEL LYMPH NODE(S) LT" ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aTwo lymph nodes negative for tumor. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CARLSON,JOSEPH WOODWARD,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "left sentinel nodes biopsy", consists of two pink/tan lymph \u000anodes (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ). The first node is bisected and \u000aentirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The second node is bisected and entirely submitted \u000aas  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro 1:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro 2:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 1 frag, ESS \u000aMicro 3:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 1 frag, ESS \u000aPart two, labeled "#2. left breast mass", consists of a left breast excision \u000aspecimen (2.3cm superior to inferior, 5.5cm medial to lateral, 6.0cm \u000aanterior to posterior). The anterior edge of the specimen has a skin ellipse \u000a(5.2cm in length x 2.4cm in width) with a scar (3.4cm in length) running \u000adown its superior aspect. There are two sutures in the skin ellipse which have \u000abeen designated by the surgeon (short superior, long lateral). Additionally \u000atwo needle localization wires enter the specimen. The first enters in the \u000acenter of the skin ellipse and exits on the medial edge of the specimen. The \u000asecond enters at the inferior/anterior/lateral edge of the specimen and does \u000anot exit. A specimen radiograph accompanies the tissue which indicate wires \u000aand calcifications in the spcimen. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior \u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibroadipose tissue, 100% of fibrous tissue submitted, 30 frags, \u000aRSS \u000ajoc \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
