VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ELOF ERIKSSON M.D.,PH.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, CAPSULE": \u000aBreast with dense fibrous tissue and associated \u000acalcifications, consistent with implant capsule. \u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, SILICONE IMPLANT #2, #3": \u000aGross examination only. \u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, SILICONE IMPLANT": \u000aGross examination only. \u000aD. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, CAPSULE": \u000aBreast with dense fibrous tissue and associated \u000acalcifications, consistent with implant capsule. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aOperation: Removal of bilateral breast implant capsulectomies, bilateral breast \u000are-augmentation. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right breast capsule. \u000aB/2. Right breast silicone implant #2, #3 (for ID only). \u000aC/3. Left breast silicone implant (for ID only). \u000aD/4. Left breast capsule. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patients \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, "Right breast capsule", consists of a cystic fragment of pink fibrous \u000atissue (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ). The wall thickness averages 0.2cm  The external \u000asurface is pale pink and the inside lining is pink, roughened, with extensive \u000acalcification and little sticky residue. Representative sections are submitted. \u000aThe specimen is fixed and decalcified prior to processing. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 3 frags, RSS. \u000aPart B, "Right breast silicone implant", consists of a ruptured breast \u000aprosthesis (10.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ). There is an abundant amount of yellow, sticky \u000amaterial and multiple chalky, calcified fragments. The specimen is consistent \u000awith a silicone implant and is for gross examination only. \u000aNote: Gross photographs are taken. \u000aPart C, "Left breast silicone implant", consists of a ruptured breast \u000aprosthesis (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm ). There is an abundant amount of pale yellow, \u000asticky material and multiple minute, calcified fragments. The specimen is \u000aconsistent with a silicone implant and is for gross examination only. \u000aNote: Gross photographs are taken. \u000aPart D, "Left breast capsule", consists of a collapsed pink, discoid, cystic, \u000arubbery tissue (9.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ). The external surface is pale pink with a \u000asmall amount of attached fat. The inside lining is pink, roughened, with \u000amoderate calcification. Further examination shows a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm attached \u000afragment of dense white tissue. Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aThe specimen is fixed and decalcified prior to processing. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Capsule, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Capsule with adjacent breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast tissue, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aWP/elw \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Kevin B Long M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
