areport, keratin immunostains revealed rare (< 10) keratin positive cells \u000a(slides not sent for review). \u000aNOTE: The core needle biopsy site is in the center of the carcinoma and \u000athe gross size is likely an accurate post-biopsy size. However, \u000acorrelation with the radiologic size may be helpful to determine the best \u000asize for staging. \u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th edition)  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID b NO (sn) (i+) \u000aMX with reported single cells seen in a lymph node by \u000aimmunohistochemistry. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by YANG,TAO,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aReceived from Massachusetts General Hospital, Pathology Department, Boston, MA \u000a REMOVED_CASE_ID , are thirty-one (31) slides. \u000aOne (1) slide is labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled "A", corresponding to a \u000aright breast, 10:00, core biopsy (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE  and REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm ), according to \u000athe accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name. \u000aThirty (30) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled "A" through "DD", \u000acorresponding to A-J) right breast lumpectomy (4.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.1cm ) K-N) right \u000aaxillary sentinel lymph node excision (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm ) O-R) right breast, \u000afinal anterior, excision (1.4 x 1.8cm  and 2 x 2 x 1.6cm in aggregate) S-U) \u000aright breast, final superior, excision (two fragments: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm  and \u000a2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ) V) right breast, final lateral, excision (2.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) W-X) right breast, final medial shaved margin, excision (2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm ) \u000aY-Z) right breast, final deep shaved margin, excision (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm ) AA-DD) \u000aright breast, final I, excision (5 x 2 x 0.7cm ) performed on REMOVED_DATE  \u000aaccording to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name. \u000aReports to: BURSTEIN, HAROLD, JOHN M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST \u000a[report_end] 
