VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNASCIMENTO, ALESSANDRA, F., M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NASCIMENTO,ALESSANDRA F.,M.D. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (226g): \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU. \u000aComplex sclerosing lesion. \u000aFibroadenoma (0.3cm ). \u000aFibrocystic changes including apocrine metaplasia, cysts and epithelial \u000ahyperplasia. \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy at the deep margin of resection. \u000aLEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (346 g): \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, focally present 0.1cm from the deep margin. \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread. \u000aFibroadenomatous change, cysts, apocrine metaplasia, epithelial \u000ahyperplasia and microcalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aNOTE: This case was reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, breast pathology service, \u000awho concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: DCIS on left side, LCIS ADH on both sides. \u000aOperation: Bilateral simple mastectomies. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000a1) Right breast, stitch on lateral side. \u000a2) Left breast, stitch on lateral side. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by GIBSON,JOANNA A,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, labeled with the patient's name \u000aand unit number. \u000aPart 1, "Right breast - stitch on lateral side", consists of a 336 gram, REMOVED_DATE x \u000a15.5 x 3.2cm right simple mastectomy specimen to include the following: \u000atan/pink skin ellipse (9.8 x 5.2cm ), tan/pink, diffusely nodular to lobulated \u000aareola (3.3 x 3.2cm ), slightly inverted nipple (1.2cm in diameter), and a \u000astitch at the lateral aspect of the breast. Approximately 1.7cm superior and \u000alateral to the areola is a tan/pink, well-healed scar (3.3cm in length). The \u000adeep/fascial plane is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned from \u000alateral to medial, revealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.8cm  tan/white, stellate, fibrous \u000alesion that is present between the upper outer and upper inner quadrants, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the deep margin, and 2.0cm subjacent to the aforementioned skin scar. \u000aThe remaining breast tissue consists of approximately equal proportions of \u000ayellow/tan, lobulated fat and dense, tan/white, cystic fibrostroma with foci of \u000aa yellow, friable substance exuding from the duct. The lateral aspect of the \u000abreast is carefully sectioned, and no lymph nodes are identified. \u000aMicro 1: Inverted nipple and areola, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 2: Skin scar. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Stellate lesion in relation to deep margin, 2 frags total, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Additional sections of stellate lesion and adjacent fibrostroma, 2 \u000afrags, RSS. \u000aMicro 7: Upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 8: Upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 9: Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 10: Lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aPart 2, "Left breast - stitch on lateral side" consists of a 346 gram, 17 x \u000a16 x 2.5cm left simple mastectomy specimen to include the following: \u000atan/pink skin ellipse (11.5 x 4.5cm ), tan/pink, diffusely lobulated \u000aareola (3.5 x 3.5cm ), slightly inverted nipple (1.4cm in diameter), and a \u000asingle stitch at the lateral aspect. Approximately 0.2cm superior to the \u000aareola is a tan/pink, well-healed linear scar (3.5cm in length). There is a \u000aslightly puckered defect (2.5 x 2.2cm ) at the deep margin, located at the \u000acentral aspect of the breast, which is inked red and overinked blue. The \u000aremaining deep/fascial plane is inked black and the specimen is serially \u000asectioned from medial to lateral, revealing a tan/white, fibrotic, focally \u000astellate lesion (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm ), with central hemorrhage, 0.2cm subjacent \u000ato the aforementioned deep margin defect. The remaining breast stroma adjacent \u000ato and extending througout the breast is tan/white, dense, with diffuse cystic \u000achange and slightly nodular. No lymph nodes are identified at the lateral \u000aaspect. \u000aMicro 11: Nipple and areola, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 12: Skin scar and subjacent breast stroma, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Stellate lesion and associated deep margin, 3 frags total, RSS. \u000aMicro 16: Stellate lesion to include focal hemorrhage and adjacent stroma, \u000a1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 17: Additional stellate lesion, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 18: Upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 19: Upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 20: Lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 21: Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000adfi \u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE \u000a[report_end] 
