VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D. \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS (#1): \u000aBenign breast tissue with a fibroadenoma, columnar alteration of lobules \u000awith prominent snouts and secretions, epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine \u000ametaplasia and ectatic ducts. \u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS (#2): \u000aBreast tissue with focal atypical lobular hyperplasia involving a \u000afibroadenoma (0.3cm  block 8). \u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: H/O of ADH R breast lumpectomy  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aOperation: Left needle localization, breast biopsy  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast mass. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - L breast wire localized biopsy (short/superior, \u000along/lateral, stitch/medial wire. \u000a#2 - L breast wire localized biopsy (short stitch/superior, long/lateral, \u000alateral/wire). \u000aRadiograph reports: Mass in both medial and lateral specimens. Dr. J. Meyer \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHEN,JEY-HSIN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000aReceived fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's name and unit \u000anumber. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1 - left breast localized biopsy medial wire", consists of \u000aa yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm ), oriented by a short \u000asuture designating the superior surface, and a long suture designating the \u000alateral surface. In place is a wire that enters the specimen at the superior \u000asurface, directed inferiorly. The specimen is inked per the pathology protocol \u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned from medial to lateral, revealing a white/yellow/pink lobulated area \u000a(2.5cm ) extending to the superior, inferior, posterior surfaces, and to within \u000a0.9cm of the anterior surface, 0.1cm of the lateral surface, and 0.2cm of \u000amedial surface. The lobulated area has irregular borders and comprises \u000aapproximately 40% to 50% of the specimen. The remainder of the breast \u000aparenchyma is comprised of 90% adipose tissue, grossly unremarkable. The \u000aentire specimen is submitted. \u000aMicro #1: Lateral resection margin, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro #2: Medial resection margin, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro #3-7: Remainder of specimen, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2 - left breast wire localized breast biopsy, lateral \u000awire", consists of a yellow/tan fibrofatty tissue (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm ), \u000aoriented by a short stitch marking the superior surface, and long stitch \u000amarking the lateral surface. In place is a wire directed into the specimen at \u000athe lateral surface and which exits the specimen at the superior, medial, and \u000aposterior surfaces. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to \u000alateral, revealing a yellow/tan color on the cut surface, involving \u000aapproximately 80% of the specimen, grossly unremarkable. The entire specimen \u000ais submitted. \u000aMicro #8: Medial-most margin, bisected, perpendicular, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro #9: Lateral-most section, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro #10+11: Remaining sections, 3 frags, ESS. \u000ajhc/ \u000aReports to: GOLSHAN, MEHRA M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
