; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned from medial to lateral. No discrete lesions are identified. The \u000atissue is composed of tan/white fibrous tissue (40%) and yellow, lobulated \u000aadipose tissue (60%). No clips are grossly identified. The specimen is \u000aentirely submitted from medial to lateral. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  10 frag, ESS \u000ajfs \u000aReports to: LOCKHART, DIANE, CATHERINE M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
