VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Addended Report *********** \u000aResident: Scott Lovitch, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aSYNOPSIS: \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aSize - 0.3cm \u000aMultifocal - No \u000aHistologic Type - Ductal \u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - I (well) \u000aNuclear Grade - Low \u000aEIC - Negative \u000aLymphovascular invasion - Negative \u000aFinal Margins (invasive) - \u000aNegative (>0.3cm ) - Anterior, Lateral, Superior, Inferior \u000aClose (0.1-0.3cm ) - Posterior (0.1cm  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) \u000aVery close (<0.1cm from margin)- Medial (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aTypes - Solid, Cribriform \u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent \u000aExtent of DCIS \u000aNumber of blocks:total - 3:10 blocks \u000aFinal Margins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (>0.3cm ) - Lateral, Superior, Inferior \u000aClose (0.1-0.3cm ) - Anterior (0.1cm  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) \u000aPosterior (0.3cm  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) \u000aMedial (0.1cm  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aPapilloma \u000aSclerosing adenosis, fibroadenoma \u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID a Nx MX \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Increase in Ca++ L breast, S/P R br bx --> LCIS. \u000aOperation: L needle loc core br bx. \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnl L mammo. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) left breast mass, short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral --> mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aCalcifications contained in specimen. Findings called to OR by Dr. MacLean. \u000aDr. Frost. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in a container labeled with the patient's name \u000aand medical record number. It consists of a single wire-localized breast \u000aexcision specimen which measures 3.4cm from superior to inferior, 4.1cm from \u000amedial to lateral, and 1.0cm from anterior to posterior. A short suture marks \u000athe superior aspect of the specimen and a long suture marks the lateral aspect \u000aof the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is a single wire present \u000ain the specimen, which enters anterolaterally midway between the superior and \u000athe inferior margins and exits posteromedially. A radiograph is provided along \u000awith the specimen, which shows the wire and calcifications associated with the \u000amid portion of the wire in the center of the specimen. The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned into eight slices from the superior to the inferior margin \u000a(slice #1 superior, slice #8 inferior). In slices #4 and #5, there is a cyst \u000ameasuring 0.2cm in diameter. This is located 0.5cm from the anterior margin, \u000a0.3cm from the posterior margin, 1.5cm from the lateral margin, 1.8cm from \u000athe medial margin, 1.7cm from the superior margin, and 1.5cm from the \u000ainferior margin. There are punctate calcifications surrounding the cyst. No \u000amasses are identified. The specimen has been discussed with Dr. Richardson. \u000aThe entire specimen is submitted for microscopic examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Cyst with anterior, posterior, and medial margins, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of slice #5 containing calcifications and lateral margin, 1 \u000afrag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin (slice #1), multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin (slice #8), multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of the specimen, serially sectioned from superior to \u000ainferior, 2 frags per cassette, ESS. (Cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains sections of slice \u000a#4 containing cyst and calcifications). \u000aSBL/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a8/6/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) NEGATIVE (1+) \u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the \u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet \u000abeen determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a \u000aportion of the membrane is positive. \u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of \u000atumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of \u000atumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity. \u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational \u000ause only. \u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
