s a localization and a \u000amass contained within the specimen. Serial sections reveal a rubbery tan/pink \u000anodular mass (2.2cm ) contained within the specimen and extending to within \u000aless than 0.1cm of the resection margin. Contained within the mass is a \u000awhite/tan cystic area (0.4cm ) which extends to within 0.2cm of the resection \u000amargin. The remainder of the tissue is yellow/orange, fatty and grossly \u000aunremarkable (approximately 40% of the specimen). The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : left breast, lateral, serial sections from tip of needle to \u000aproximal \u000aportion of needle, with mass contains in blocks REMOVED_DATE  14 frags, \u000aESS \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. left breast mass medial", consists of a tan/orange/yellow \u000arubbery soft tissue (2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ). The specimen is unoriented and the \u000aexternal surface is inked black. A needle traverses through the specimen along \u000aits short axis. An accompanying radiograph demonstrates a localization wire \u000aand mass contained within the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned \u000afrom tip of the wire extending proximally revealing a firm white/tan mass (2.0 \u000acm) which extends to within less than 0.1cm of the resection margin. The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : serial sections, 5 frags, ESS \u000aPart C, labeled "#3. re-excision left breast", consists of an unoriented \u000ayellow/tan rubbery soft tissue (3 x 2 x 1.2cm ). An accompanying radiograph \u000ademonstrates a clip contained within the specimen. The external surface is \u000ainked blue and the specimen is serially sectioned along its long axis revealing \u000aa white/tan calcified cyst (0.3cm ) in an otherwise unremarkable breast. The \u000aparenchyma is comprised of approximately 40% pink/tan fibrous tissue, the \u000aremaining 60% comprised of unremarkable yellow/orange adipose tissue. A clip \u000ais 