t, simple mastectomy specimen (161-gm, 14 x 13 x 2cm ), to include tan/pink \u000askin ellipse (7.0 x 2.5cm ), tan/brown areola (2.9 x 2.3cm ), tan/pink everted \u000anipple (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ) and a single stitch at "the axillary tail". The \u000adeep margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned from medial \u000ato lateral, revealing an area of white/tan, dense, fibrous tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a3.0cm ) within the central breast, focally extending to the lateral aspect and \u000aextending to the deep margin. No lesions consistent with invasive carcinoma \u000aare identified. The remaining breast tissue consists of approximately equal \u000aproportions of yellow/tan, lobulated fat and tan/white, fibrous stroma. No \u000alymph nodes are identified at the lateral aspect of the breast. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper/outer quadrant (including dense fibrous area), 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant (including dense fibrous area), 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower/inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper/inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional, dense, fibrous lesion (central breast), 1 frag, RSS. \u000adfi/MMM \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Samuel G Katz M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
