VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Consult slide(s) \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-04- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM HALLMARK HEALTH, LAWRENCE MEMORIAL CAMPUS, MEDFORD, MA: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; 2/26/04): \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, CORE BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; 9/16/04): \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with calcifications. \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; 9/28/04): \u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA bordering on DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, \u000acribriform and micropapillary types, (low nuclear grade), in 10 of 23 blocks \u000aassociated with calcifications and focal necrosis. \u000aThe atypical hyperplasia/in situ carcinoma is at margin of resection. \u000aBiopsy cavity. \u000aOne intramammary lymph node with no tumor seen. \u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the following \u000aresults (reviewed): \u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR - POSITIVE \u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR - POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /NEU - NEGATIVE (0) \u000aNOTE: The excision shows multiple foci of severely atypical ductal \u000aproliferation that is difficult to precisely classify. There is significant \u000acytologic atypia and micropapillary and focal cribriform architecture, although \u000athe architecture is never quite fully developed. The differential includes \u000asevere ADH and low grade DCIS. Drs. Richardson, Lester and Dillon have \u000areviewed the case and the consensus is that some foci reach criteria for DCIS. \u000aThere are highly atypical foci at least bordering on DCIS that are less than \u000a0.1cm from margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aOperation: Not provided. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aReceived from Hallmark Health, Lawrence Memorial Campus, Pathology Department, \u000a170 Governors Avenue, Medford, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID , are forty-three (43) slides. \u000aTwelve (12) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID blabeled "A" through "L", corresponding \u000ato a left breast wire needle localized biopsy (4.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm )performed on \u000a2/26/04 \u000aAccording to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name. \u000aThree (3) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled "A  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", "B  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and "C \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ", corresponding to a right breast stereotactic core biopsy for \u000acalcifications (4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the \u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name. \u000aTwenty-eight (28) slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled "A", "A(SPLIT", \u000a"B" through "H", "H (+)CTRL/ER", "H (+)CTRL/PR", "H NEG CONTRL", "I", "J", "J \u000aER", "J PR", "J NEG CONTROL" and "K" through "U", corresponding to a right \u000abreast wire needle localized excision for a mass (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm ) performed \u000aon REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the \u000apatient's name. \u000aIncluded is a consultation report from Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center, \u000aBoston, MA; numbered "04- REMOVED_CASE_ID M" and dated REMOVED_DATE  referring to all the cases \u000alisted above, bearing the patient's name. \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aGross Dictation by Brian S Chang M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aMicroscopic/Diagnostic Dictation by Brian S Chang M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Review by Deborah A Dillon M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a12/14/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
