east carcinoma. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA. Right sentinel lymph nodes (FS). \u000aB. Right breast (short superior, long lateral). \u000aC. Left breast (short superior, long lateral). \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1. RIGHT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES" ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aTwo lymph nodes; no tumor present. \u000aOR Consultation by: WILLIAM ROBERT WELCH, M.D. \u000aResident: SAMUEL G KATZ, M.D., PH.D. \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right sentinel lymph nodes", consists of one fragment of \u000ayellow/tan soft tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ). Two candidate lymph nodes are \u000adissected from the specimen (1.6cm and 1.9cm in maximum dimension, \u000arespectively). The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast", consists of a 454 gm simple mastectomy \u000aspecimen (17.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm ) with attached nipple areola complex (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) with areola (5.5 x 4.0cm ) and everted nipple (0.6 x 1.2cm in diameter), \u000aand attached separate white/tan skin ellipse (4.0 x 0.5cm ), which contains a \u000a3.6cm well-healed surgical scar. The deep margin is composed of unremarkable \u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue and is inked black. The specimen is oriented \u000awith a long suture indicating lateral and a short suture indicating superior. \u000aThere is an area of blue dye (3.5 x 3.5cm ) directly inferior to the nipple \u000aareola complex and a second area of blue dye (4.0 x 4.5cm ) surrounding the \u000aseparate skin ellipse. The second are of blue dye extends into a white/tan \u000arubbery fibrous area (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm ) located in the lower outer quadrant \u000a1.6cm from the deep margin, and is grossly consistent with a prior biopsy \u000asite. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is composed of approximately 20% \u000afibrous tissue the rest is adipose tissue. Approximately 90% of the fibrous \u000aarea and representative sections of the rest of the specimen are submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous area in lower outer quadrant, REMOVED_DATE frags in each, RSS. \u000aNote:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains closest deep margin. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant, fibrous tissue, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant, fibrous tissue, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant, fibrous tissue, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple and skin with scar, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Left breast", consists of a 268 gm simple mastectomy \u000aspecimen (17.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 3.2cm ) with attached nipple areola complex (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) with areola (3.8 x 2.8cm ) and everted nipple (0.6cm x 0.8cm in \u000adiameter). There is a long suture indicating lateral, and a short suture \u000aindicating superior. The deep margin is composed of grossly unremarkable \u000ayellow-tan fibroadipose tissue and is inked black. There is a white-tan fibrous \u000aarea (2.6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm ) located in the upper outer quadrant 1.5cm from the \u000adeep margin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is composed of \u000aapproximately 20% fibrous tissue and the rest adipose tissue. 2 candidate \u000aintramammary lymph nodes are identified, each measuring 0.3cm in maximum \u000adimension. The entire fibrous area and representative sections of the remainder \u000aof the specimen are submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous area in upper outer quadrant, 1 to 2 frags in each, ESS \u000a[Note: closest deep margin contained in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ] \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 candidate lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 2 frags, ESS \u000aJDR/abjpMMM \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aMicroscopic/Diagnostic Dictation by Julie D.R. Reimann M.D., Ph.D., on \u000a1/13/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
