t number, and "L breast", and consists of an irregular fragment of \u000afibroadipose tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ) with a needle-localization wire \u000aentering the anterior aspect of the specimen with no definitive exit, and an \u000aaccompanying radiograph demonstrating multiple punctate calcifications. There \u000ais a short stitch designating superior, long stitch designating lateral, and a \u000awhipstitch designating the chest wall margin per surgeon. The specimen is \u000ainked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/ orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior \u000aand unremarkable fibrofatty cut surface with approximately 95% white fibrous \u000atissue, to 5% yellow lobulated adipose tissue. The specimen is submitted in \u000aits entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Perpendicular superior margin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast sequentially submitted from superior to inferior to include \u000aarea of needle-localization wire ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), multi frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Perpendicular inferior margin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aJenC/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 10,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11:00:49AM \u000a[report_end] 
