_DATE x 0.6cm ). There is a \u000ashort stitch placed per surgeon to designate the superior position and a long \u000astitch placed per surgeon to designate the lateral position. The specimen is \u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. \u000aThe cut surface reveals an 80% fibrous parenchyma with a dense focus of fat \u000anecrosis consistent with prior excision site (located 0.2cm from the posterior \u000amargin, 0.4cm from the anterior margin, 0.4cm from the lateral margin, 0.6cm \u000afrom the medial margin, 0.8cm from the superior margin and 1.2cm from the \u000ainferior margin). The specimen is entirely submitted for microscopic analysis. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin perpendicularly sectioned, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Section with prior excision site including medial, lateral, anterior \u000aand posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Successive sections, 2 frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin, 5 frags, perpendicularly sectioned, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left medial shave margin, whipstitch new margin", consists \u000aof one yellow/tan fragment of fibroadipose tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ). There \u000ais suture placed per surgeon to designate the new margin. The corresponding \u000asurface is inked black. The old margin is inked red. The sectioned surface is \u000apredominantly fibrous in composition. The specimen is entirely submitted for \u000amicroscopic analysis. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : New left medial shave margin, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aSWY/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed 