ior black, medial orange, lateral yellow, superior red, \u000ainferior green. Two localization wires are entering the specimen at superior \u000amargin. The tissue is sectioned along the localization wires to reveal two \u000aclips. The medial clip is inserted in the middle of a round tan solid firm \u000aarea consistent with biopsy site measuring 0.8cm in diameter. This area \u000ameasures 0.3cm from superior, 0.3cm from anterior, 1.2cm from posterior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from medial, 5.0cm from lateral, and 0.8cm from the inferior surgical \u000aresection margins. The lateral clip is placed in another area consistent with \u000abiopsy site measuring, which measures 1.0cm in diameter and is 1.0cm lateral \u000ato the first nodule. This nodule measures 0.1cm from superior, 1.0cm from \u000ainferior, 3.0cm from lateral, 2.5cm from medial, REMOVED_DATE from the anterior, and \u000a1.0cm from posterior surgical resection margins respectively. Ill-defined, \u000amoderately rubbery, tan, fibrous tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm  extends \u000afrom the lateral nodule to the posterior and lateral surgical resection \u000amargins. The tissue is totally submitted as follows: \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial nodule, 1 frag in each cassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial surgical resection margin, sectioned perpendicular to \u000athe margin, 8 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : The lateral nodule and corresponding margins, 1 frag in each \u000acassette, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag in each cassette, tissue between the nodules and \u000acorresponding margins, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral extension of fibrous tissue from the lateral nodule to \u000alateral surgical resection margin. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior surgical resection margin. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aJBE/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on \u000a8/7/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
