VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Paul A. VanderLaan, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP: \u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA. \u000aCalcifications in normal breast epithelium and columnar cell change. \u000aOther findings: \u000aFibroadenoma (0.6cm ). \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. \u000aPrevious biopsy site identified (See FH  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  core biopsy for \u000acalcifications). \u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Suspicious biopsy with ALH and PASH. \u000aOperation: Right needle loc. breast biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: Not given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right breast tissue (FS room - mammo). \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aClip near wire in specimen. Signature: CR \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and medical \u000arecord number, and "#1. Right breast tissue", and consists of a 14.75-g \u000alumpectomy specimen with a wire localizing a clip as seen on the accompanying \u000amammogram. The specimen is received six-inked by the surgeon in the OR in a \u000astandard fashion, such that red is superior, green is inferior, yellow is \u000alateral, orange is medial, blue is anterior and black is posterior. The \u000aspecimen measures 2.6cm anterior to posterior, 2.4cm superior to inferior, \u000aand 3.9cm medial to lateral. The wire enters the specimen on the anterior \u000a(blue) aspect of the specimen, and does not exit the specimen. The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral in eleven slices. The specimen has a \u000acentral hemorrhagic cavity (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm ) that is located 0.3cm to the \u000aclosest resection margin (superior). The clip is found in the central \u000ahemorrhagic cavity, and is located in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Aside from the central \u000ahemorrhagic cavity, the breast parenchymal tissue is composed of approximately \u000a60% white firm fibrous tissue, and 40% yellow lobulated fatty tissue. The \u000aentire specimen is submitted for histology. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #1, medial end, perpendicular sections, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6 with clip, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #8, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #9, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #10, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #11, lateral end, perpendicular sections, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000apva/elw \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 11,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 10:37:43AM \u000a[report_end] 
