dial/ orange. \u000aAn accompanying specimen radiograph displays a silver metallic clip adjacent to \u000athe needle localization wire. The specimen is sliced from lateral to medial \u000ainto twelve slices to reveal a silver metallic clip in slice 7. The clip is \u000alocated within a firm poorly circumscribed tan-white mass (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ) \u000alocated abutting the posterior margin, 0.2cm from the inferior margin, 0.5cm \u000afrom the anterior margin, 1.3cm from the superior margin, 1.5cm from the \u000alateral margin, 1.7cm from the medial margin. The mass is located in slices 5 \u000athrough 9. The specimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 1, lateral margin, perpendicular sections, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 2, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 3, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 4, 1 frag in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 5, 1 frag in each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 6, 1 frag in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 7 (with clip), 1 frag in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 8, 1 frag in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 9, 1 frag in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 10, 1 frag in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 11, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice 12, medial margin, perpendicular sections, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aLMC/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on Friday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 09,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06:32:30PM \u000a[report_end] 
