VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Kristin S. Ricci, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP: \u000aColumnar cell change. \u000aBreast parenchyma with biopsy site changes. \u000aNo atypical ductal hyperplasia identified. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 48 year-old premenopausal woman s/p R B UOQ core bx REMOVED_DATE revealing \u000aADH best evaluated by excision. \u000aOperation: R B WL bx. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA. Right breast tissue long = lateral, short = superior, whip stitch on deep \u000amargin \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aSpecimen; mass, clip wire in. OR called/SR. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue, long equals lateral, short equals superior, whip \u000astitch on deep margin", consists of an ovoid yellow/tan breast excision \u000aspecimen (6.0 M-L x REMOVED_DATE S-I x REMOVED_DATE A-Pcm ) oriented per surgeon as follows: \u000aShort equals superior, long equals lateral, whip stitch equals deep margin. \u000aThere is one needle localization wire in place, entering the superolateral \u000aaspect of the specimen and exiting the posterolateral aspect of the specimen. \u000aThe specimen was previously radiographed, confirming the presence of a mass, \u000aclipped and wire within the specimen. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange. \u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial. In the central \u000aspecimen, there is a well-delineated pink/tan nodular lesion (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) which grossly extends to the superior margin, 0.1cm from the \u000aposterior/deep margin, 0.6cm from the anterior margin, 0.7cm from the medial \u000amargin, 1.0cm from the inferior margin, and 1.2cm from the lateral margin. A \u000asmall amount of clip is identified within the mass. \u000aThe remainder of the cut surface is composed of approximately 15% delicate \u000awhite/tan fibrous tissue and 85% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. No \u000aadditional discrete lesions are identified. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central specimen to include mass with superior, anterior, and \u000aposterior/deep margin sequentially submitted from lateral to medial, 1 frag in \u000aeach, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior and additional deep margin closest to mass, 1 frag in \u000aeach, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, perpendicular sections, multi frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of the specimen, mult frags, ESS \u000aLMB/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a8/30/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
