umpy, focally cystic fibrous stroma with \u000amultiple punctate areas of hemorrhage (ranging from 0.2cm to 0.4cm in \u000agreatest dimension), which extends to all surgical margins, and approximately \u000a40% grossly unremarkable yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. No discrete \u000amasses or lesions are identified. The specimen is entirely sequentially \u000asubmitted from anterior to posterior. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : (micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  = 1 bisected slice), multi frags total, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left breast specimen #2, long lateral, short superior", \u000aconsists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to pink/tan fibrofatty tissue (3.8 \u000acm M-L x 3.2cm A-P x 2.2cm S-I), which is oriented per surgeon as follows: \u000ashort = superior, long suture = lateral. The specimen was previously inked per \u000asurgeon as follows per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. There is one needle localization wire in place, which enters \u000athe lateral aspect of the specimen and exits the medial aspect of the specimen. \u000aPlease note that a radiograph is not received with the specimen. The specimen \u000ais serially sectioned from lateral to medial to exhibit approximately 80% very \u000adense lumpy tan/white fibrous stroma, which extends to all surgical margins and \u000aapproximately 20% unremarkable yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. Within the \u000adense fibrous stroma, there are multiple areas of hemorrhage (ranging from REMOVED_DATE \u000acm to 0.7cm in greatest dimension), the largest of which may represent areas \u000aassociated with prior core biopsy procedure verses dilated hemorrhagic ducts. \u000aNo discrete masses or lesions are identified. The specimen is entirely \u000asequentially submitted from lateral to medial. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : (micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  = 1 bisected slice), core biopsy site verses dilated \u000ahemorrhagic ducts in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , multi frags total, ESS. \u000aPlease note that the needle localization wire traverses the dense hemorrhagic \u000afibrous stroma. \u000aLmb/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Lynette M Sholl M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Lynette M Sholl M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Lynette M Sholl M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
