 0.5cm in the area where the wire was present, but does \u000anot grossly abut any inked margins. This hemorrhagic area is 2.4cm from skin. \u000aThe entire specimen was submitted for review lateral to medial. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral portion of specimen, 4 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of specimen, lateral to medial, 1 frag each, \u000aRSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 3 frags each, RSS. \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aKG/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
