ect. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: Posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned to reveal white, multinodular mass, located 0.2cm from the medial \u000amargin and measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm  including soft and necrotic spots. \u000aThe specimen is radiographed to locate a clip, which is found in Slide 2 of the \u000aspecimen. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Specimen sectioned from medial to lateral aspect with mass \u000ain  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 6 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, sublabeled "2. Superior margin, stitch on new margin", consists of one \u000a(1) fragment of fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm with a stitch \u000aplaced to indicate the new margin. The new margin is inked black, and the old \u000amargin is inked blue, and the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : New margin, 6 frag, ESS. \u000aMRU/mmm \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Marianna B Ruzinova M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a10/17/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
