sue. No other gross lesions are identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Tract, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining tissue, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2 Central nipple skin", consists of two tan/pink, lobulated to \u000airregular soft tissues (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ). The larger \u000asoft tissue is grossly consistent with skin. This tissue is inked blue and \u000abisected. The remaining tissue is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Probable skin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional soft tissue, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aDFI/elw \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Eric C Huang M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a2/27/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
