rs \u000aat the junction of the lateral and inferior margins. Sectioning the specimen, \u000ain a medial to lateral direction, into eleven slices reveals that the specimen \u000ais 90% adipose tissue. The clip is seen in slice #6. A white/tan lesion is \u000aseen slices #4 and #5, and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  The closest extension \u000aof the mass to a margin is 0.6cm (anterior green - inked margin). The entire \u000aspecimen is submitted for histologic analysis. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #1 (medial margin), 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #8, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #9, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #10, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #11 (lateral margin), 2 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000achd/elw \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 06,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02:42:11PM \u000a[report_end] 
