00asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned from superior to inferior to exhibit 95% yellow lobulated \u000aadipose tissue and 5% fibrous tissue. The fibrous tissue abuts the inferior \u000aaspect of the specimen and exhibits hemorrhage (consistent with needle \u000alocalization wire placement). No masses or lesions are grossly appreciated. \u000aRepresentative sections are submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body, sequentially submitted from superior to inferior, multi \u000afrags total, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Perpendicular inferior margin to include area designated by \u000aneedle localization wire, 2 frags in each, ESS. \u000aJenC/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 21,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05:28:10PM \u000a[report_end] 
