VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Christopher P. Elco, M.D., Ph.D.; Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP: \u000aColumnar cell change. \u000aApocrine metaplasia. \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. \u000aFibroadenomatoid nodule (0.4cm ). \u000aCalcifications in benign breast epithelium. \u000aCore biopsy site changes, extending to the posterior resection margin. \u000aNote: The patient underwent a prior core needle biopsy for calcifications that \u000arevealed atypical ductal hyperplasia ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). There is no malignancy or \u000aadditional foci of ADH seen upon microscopic examination of the entire \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 41 year-old woman s/p L breast UOQ core biopsies REMOVED_DATE revealing ADH \u000a- excision recommended. \u000aOperation: L breast WL bx. \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA. Left breast tissue short suture superior, long lateral, whip stitch on deep \u000amargin to mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aTargeted calcifications and the clip contained in the specimen. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name \u000aand unit number, and "#1. Left breast tissue", and consists of a single breast \u000aexcision specimen (3.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm ) containing a short suture designating \u000athe superior margin and a long suture designating lateral margin. The specimen \u000acontains a single wire, which enters the specimen at the lateral surface and \u000aexits at the superior surface. The specimen is received with an accompanying \u000aradiograph demonstrating a central clip adjacent to the previously described \u000awire and focal calcifications. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol \u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The superior and inferior \u000aaspects of the specimen are removed and submitted entirely as perpendicular \u000asections. The remaining tissue is serially sectioned from inferior to superior \u000ato reveal a central tan/white lesion (likely prior biopsy site, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), which is present 0.4cm from the lateral margin, 0.1cm to the posterior \u000amargin, 0.6cm to the medial margin, 0.4cm to the anterior margin, 1.5cm from \u000athe superior margin, and 1.0cm from the inferior margin. The specimen is \u000aentirely submitted for histological examination. The clip and associated \u000atissue is in Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, perpendicular sections, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Serial sections of the specimen, multi frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aSRK/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a7/29/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
