 SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) right sentinel node - hot + blue (fs). \u000aB/2) sentinel node R - hot + blue. \u000aC/3) right breast - short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 - RIGHT SENTINEL NODE - HOT + BLUE" (FSA): \u000aLymph node; negative for tumor. \u000aOR Consultation by: William Robert Welch, M.D. \u000aResident: Elizabeth Morgan, M.D. \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname, unit number. \u000aPart A is received in the frozen lab for intraoperative consultation and \u000alabeled, "right sentinel node hot and blue", consists of a fragment of \u000ayellow/tan firm soft tissue with attached fat consistent with a lymph node (1.7 \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm overall). The lymph node measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  The \u000alymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FSA. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : FSA remnant, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, "right sentinel node hot and blue", consists of a tan/yellow irregular \u000afibrofatty tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ) which exhibits a tan/pink lymph node \u000a(2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ) which is bisected and entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart C, "right breast", consists of a 378-g right simple mastectomy specimen \u000a(19.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm ) with a white/tan skin ellipse (12.0 x 5.0cm ) which \u000aexhibits a tan areola (2.5 x 2.5cm ) and an everted nipple (1.5 x 1.5cm ). \u000aThere is a tan/pink well-healed scar (0.3 x 0.2cm ) located 1.5cm from the \u000anipple. The deep margin is intact and no skeletal muscle is identified; 1.0cm \u000adeep to the scar is an ill-defined hemorrhagic area with focal areas of fat \u000anecrosis (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm ) located 12 o'clock, 2.8cm from the deep margin. \u000aThere is a silver metallic clip identified within the area. The remainder of \u000athe breast parenchyma is predominantly white and firm fibrous tissue (80%) and \u000ayellow fatty tissue (20%). The most lateral tissue is palpated; however, no \u000alymph nodes are identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Hemorrhagic area to scar, 1 frag in each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of hemorrhagic area to include area to deep margin in \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag in each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant, 4 frags total, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags in each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant, 2 frags in each, RSS. \u000almc/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aMonday REMOVED_MONTH 28,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05:40:10PM \u000a[report_end] 
