D_ACCESSION_ID  (sn) MX (with multiple foci of \u000ainvasion) \u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) - Performed previously at BWH \u000aNOTE: Two (2) distinct foci of invasive lobular carcinoma are seen. The \u000asmaller focus is well-differentiated. An E-cadherin immunostain demonstrates \u000aloss of membranous staining in both invasive and in-situ lobular carcinoma. In \u000athe main excision specimen, the biopsy cavity is 0.1cm from the lateral \u000amargin. However, the separately submitted final lateral margin is evaluated in \u000aPart C. \u000aC. LEFT BREAST, LATERAL SHAVE MARGIN: \u000aBreast tissue, negative for tumor. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 70 year old female with a history of ADH, REMOVED_DATE mammogram \u000asupplemental with L U/S demonstrates a 1cm solid mass. REMOVED_DATE core biopsy \u000arevealed grade II IDC ER+, PR low +, Her2/neu 2+, FISH not amplified. \u000aOperation: Left breast wire localized lumpectomy, sentinel node mapping, biopsy \u000aand possible level I and II dissection. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Left sentinel lymph node - hot and blue x 2. \u000aB/2. Left breast tissue - short stitch superior/long stitch lateral/whip stitch \u000ain chest wall margin to mammo/tissue bank. \u000aC/3. Left breast lateral shave margin, whip stitch new margin. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES, HOT AND BLUE" ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes negative for tumor. \u000aOR Consultation by: Jeffrey Fred Krane, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aResident: Leona A. Doyle, M.D., Cheryl Adackapara, M.D. \u000aRADIOLOGY: Intact wire, with mass and clip present. J. Wang/C. Denison \u000aIntact wire with mass and clip present. J. Wang/C. Denison \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each part labeled with the \u000apatient's name and medical record number. \u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Left sentinel lymph node hot and blue x2", consists of two \u000afragments of tan/red fibroadipose tissue (4.6 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.3cm ), each containing one firm blue lymph node, the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.0 x 0.5cm  with extensive fatty replacement. The largest lymph node is \u000abisected and entirely submitted in the frozen section room as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a(each containing one-half). The smaller lymph node (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ) is \u000aentirely submitted in the frozen section room as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remnant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Non-frozen fibroadipose tissue, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch \u000alateral, whip stitch chest wall margin", consists of a wire localized excision \u000a(9.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm ), oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch designated \u000asuperior, a long stitch designated lateral, and a whip stitch designated chest \u000awall margin. The specimen is previously inked by the surgeon and is oriented \u000ain the frozen section room. The wire is removed after reviewing the specimen \u000aradiograph. Please note: As described in the frozen section room, the whip \u000astitch is found on the blue (anterior) rather than the black (posterior) aspect \u000aof the specimen. This discordance was discussed with the surgeon in the frozen \u000asection room. The specimen is also difficult to orient as the ink has \u000aextensively run on the specimen. \u000aA solid white/tan mass (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ) is identified 0.1cm from the \u000alateral, 0.5cm from the superior, 2.0cm from the posterior, 2.0cm from the \u000aanterior, 3.5cm from the medial and 4.5cm from the inferior margin. A biopsy \u000acavity containing a clip is identified within the lesion. The clip is removed. \u000aA portion of the tumor was taken for protocol REMOVED_DATE in the frozen section \u000aroom. The specimen is submitted from superior to inferior with the biopsy \u000acavity in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Approximately 60% of the specimen are submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, 2 frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy cavity to lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior + medial margin near biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of inferior, medial, posterior and \u000alateral margins, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior and medial margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Left breast lateral shave margin - whip stitch new \u000amargin", consists of a disrupted fragment of fibroadipose tissue (18.0 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000aup to 1.5cm ). According to the specimen label, the specimen is supposed to be \u000aoriented with a whip stitch designated as new margin. However, this stitch is \u000anot found attached to the specimen, thus orientation is not possible. The \u000aspecimen is inked black in its entirety and serially sectioned. Note: The \u000amain, more solid portion of the specimen is submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , \u000aattached fibroadipose tissue is found in cassettes REMOVED_DATE \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Serial sections, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aawe/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aFriday May 29,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12:17:25PM \u000a[report_end] 
