VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Shakti Ramkissoon, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY": \u000aBenign breast and adipose tissue with columnar cell changes and cystic changes. \u000aThe margins are evaluated for the diagnosis. \u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, POSTERIOR MARGIN": \u000aSeverely atypical papillary lesion extending to margins (see NOTE). \u000a(Levels examined.) \u000aNOTE: \u000aSevere atypia is present within a papillary lesion, extending to inked and \u000acauterized margins. Re-excision is suggested to exclude DCIS. \u000aImmunohistochemistry for p63/ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID / REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  supports the above diagnosis. \u000aThe case was reviewed by Dr. Dillon, Breast Pathology Service, who agrees. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 69 y/o female with right breast, papillary lesion with atypia on \u000aimage-guided core biopsy. \u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None specified. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: right breast abnormal mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) R wire-localized excisional bx (mammo). \u000ab/2) Rt posterior margin, rt breast (mammo). \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000a#1. Wire is seen within the specimen. \u000a#2. Mass is within the specimen. - Dr. Gombos. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "Right excision biopsy wire localization short superior, long \u000alateral", consists of an irregular tan-yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose \u000abreast tissue (2.8cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE anterior to posterior, and 0.5cm \u000asuperior to inferior) with a suture designating the superior margin, and long \u000asuture designating the lateral margin. There is a new localization wire \u000aplaced, which enters through the inferior aspect of the specimen, exiting \u000athrough the lateral aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked per \u000apathology protocol (superior red, inferior green, medial large, lateral yellow, \u000aanterior blue, posterior black) and serially sectioned from medial to lateral. \u000aThe cut surface is tan-yellow homogenous with no discrete lesions grossly \u000aidentified. There is a scant amount of fibrous tissue present, which \u000aconstitutes less than 1% of the breast parenchyma. The specimen is submitted \u000ain its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : The new margin, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections medial to lateral,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  2 frags each, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "Right posterior margin Rt breast", consists of an unoriented \u000atan-yellow to tan-white lobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.2cm ). The specimen is inked, serially sectioned, and there are focal areas \u000aof dense white fibrous tissue, which constitutes approximately greater than 95% \u000aof the breast parenchyma. No discrete lesions are grossly identified. The \u000aspecimen is trisected, and submitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 3 frags, ESS. \u000aSEK/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by 