VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast biopsy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Joanna A Gibson, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST EXCISION, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A CLIP: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia present in 2 of 14 blocks (2 microscopic foci  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aand  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aCore biopsy site with dystrophic calcifications. \u000aThis case has been reviewed by Dr. Deborah Dillon, Breast Pathologist, who \u000aconcurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: ADH on core biopsy. \u000aOperation: Right breast needle localization excisional biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast atypical ductal hyperplasia. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) right breast bx after needle localization -> mammo, short=superior, \u000along=lateral per Dr. Iglehart via phone call REMOVED_DATE @ 11:35 am (dfi). \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aClip in specimen with adjacent hematoma. OR called 10:15 LBT. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number, \u000aand "#1 - right breast biopsy after needle localization", and consists of a \u000aportion of yellow/red lobulated, fibroadipose tissue (4.6 x REMOVED_DATE x 3.1cm ) with \u000atwo orienting sutures ("short stitch=superior; long stitch=lateral"), and a \u000aneedle localization wire in place (entering at the inferior aspect). The \u000aspecimen is inked by the pro-sector according to the pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned from lateral to medial, revealing a hemorrhagic cavity (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.7cm ), which is 0.2cm from the superior and anterior margins, 0.5cm from \u000athe posterior margin, 1.0cm from the lateral margin, 0.8cm from the medial \u000amargin, and 1.2cm from the inferior margin. The needle localization wire \u000aterminates within the cavity. The accompanying radiograph confirms the \u000apresence of a clip within the specimen, adjacent to the hematoma (per \u000aRadiology). The remaining breast tissue consists of approximately 80% yellow \u000alobulated adipose tissue and 20% tan/white, focally dense fibrous stroma. No \u000aother gross lesions are identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : breast tissue sequentially from lateral to medial with area \u000aof clip in micros  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , multiple frags, ESS. \u000adfi/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
