o lateral, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm superior to inferior, and 3.8cm anterior to posterior) with a short suture \u000adesignating the superior margin and a long suture designating the lateral \u000amargin. There is a needle localization wire in place, entering through the \u000alateral anterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology \u000aprotocol (superior red, inferior green, lateral yellow, medial orange, anterior \u000ablue, and posterior black) and is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. \u000aThere is an irregular hemorrhagic lesion with surrounding dense white fibrous \u000atissue (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ) located 0.6cm from the superior margin, 2.2cm \u000afrom the inferior margin, 1.0cm from the posterior margin, 2.4cm from the \u000aanterior margin, 1.4cm from the lateral margin, and 2.4cm from the medial \u000amargin. There is a metallic clip located within the hemorrhagic lesion \u000acorrelating with the radiograph received with the specimen. Remainder of the \u000abreast parenchyma is tan/yellow and homogeneous with no additional lesions or \u000aareas of disruption identified. Representative sections are submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire biopsy cavity and surrounding breast parenchyma, blocks \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to include slice with the metallic clip, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Uninvolved breast parenchyma, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aSEK/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
