r to posterior, 2.5cm superior to inferior). The specimen is oriented \u000awith a long stitch designating lateral, and a short stitch designating superior \u000aas per surgeon. The specimen is inked as follows: superior-red, \u000ainferior-green, anterior-blue, posterior-black, medial-orange and \u000alateral-yellow. The specimen contains a localization wire entering the medial \u000aaspect of the specimen and exiting the inferior lateral aspect of the specimen. \u000aThe specimen radiograph reviewed in centricity shows a wire, clip and \u000acalcifications in the specimen. The specimen contains a tan/white/red \u000ahemorrhagic area (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ) consistent with a previous biopsy site, \u000alocated 0.1cm from the inferior margin, 0.2cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the superior margin, 1.9cm from the anterior margin, 0.5cm from the \u000alateral margin, and 1.5cm from the medial margin. A clip is identified in the \u000acentral portion of this lesion, in the posterior aspect of the specimen. The \u000aremainder of the specimen is composed of 20% fibrous tissue and 80% adipose \u000atissue. The specimen is entirely submitted to include perpendicular sections \u000aof all margins. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast biopsy entirely submitted medially to laterally, with the \u000aarea containing the clip in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. \u000aDIL/mgd/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 10,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03:43:18PM \u000a[report_end] 
