clip with surrounding calcifications in the specimen. The specimen is \u000asectioned into eight slices, from inferior to superior, and it consists of \u000aapproximately 90% fibrous tissue and 10% adipose tissue. There is a collection \u000aof gel-foam beads (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm ) in slices five and six, which grossly \u000aabuts the anterior margin, and is 1.2cm from the posterior margin, 0.6cm from \u000athe lateral margin, 1.3cm from the medial margin, 2.4cm from the inferior \u000amargin, and 0.9cm from the superior margin. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice one, 7 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice two, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice three, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice four, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice five with gel-beads, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice six with gel-beads, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice seven, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : slice eight, 8 frags, ESS. \u000aAF/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a6/13/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
