ip, which is \u000awithin the specimen. There are associated calcifications more towards the \u000aanterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned in \u000athirteen slices going medial to lateral. The clip is identified in slice #6 \u000aand is located from margins as follows: 0.7cm superior, 0.7cm inferior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm anterior, 1.9cm posterior, 1.9cm medial, and 2.4cm lateral. Associated \u000awith the clip are biopsy site changes (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ) located from margins \u000aas follows: 0.2cm superior, 0.4cm inferior, 0.4cm anterior, 0.8cm \u000aposterior, 1.8cm medial, and 1.5cm lateral. No distinct mass is associated \u000awith the clip other than the biopsy site changes. The specimen is \u000aapproximately 20% fibrous and 80% adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted for histologic evaluation. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #1, medial margin perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6, anterior aspect, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6, posterior portion with clip, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7, anterior portion with biopsy site changes, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7, posterior aspect with biopsy site changes, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #8, anterior aspect with biopsy site changes, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #8, posterior aspect with biopsy site changes, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #9, anterior aspect with biopsy site changes, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #9, posterior aspect with biopsy site changes, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 