VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHARINE CARTER M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Rachel E Factor, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION: \u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA is present. \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present. \u000aCalcifications present in association with benign epithelium and stroma. \u000aBiopsy site changes are present. \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: History of abnormal right mammogram, history of 0.75-cm area of \u000acalcifications, right upper central breast core biopsy at BWH, REMOVED_DATE showed \u000aADH; clip left area is in location of an old biopsy site. \u000aOperation: Right mammographically directed breast biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aRight breast tissue at 12 o'clock (short superior, long lateral). \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aMass, clip + wire in specimen. Phoned to Dr. Carter in OR. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "right breast tissue at 12 o'clock, short superior and long lateral", and \u000aconsists of an irregular, tan/yellow, lobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue \u000a(6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.4cm ) with a needle localization wire in place and a short \u000asuture designating the superior margin and a long suture designating the \u000alateral margin. The specimen is received with radiograph, which designates a \u000aprevious biopsy site marked with a clip. The specimen is inked (superior - \u000ared, inferior - green, lateral - yellow, medial - orange, anterior - blue, and \u000aposterior - black) and is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior. There \u000ais a hemorrhagic cavity surrounded by dense white fibrous tissue consistent \u000awith previous biopsy site (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ) which is 0.7cm from the lateral \u000amargin, 0.8cm from the medial margin, 1.5cm from the inferior margin, 1.8cm \u000afrom the superior margin, 2.8cm from the posterior margin, and 2.6cm from the \u000aanterior margin. Subjacent to the cavity is a metallic clip. The remainder of \u000athe breast parenchyma is tan/yellow and homogeneous with focal areas of dense \u000awhite fibrous tissue constituting approximately 50% of the breast parenchyma. \u000aNo additional areas of disruption or lesions are identified. Entirely \u000asubmitted for histologic evaluation. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy cavity/subjacent clip, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy cavity, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Subjacent fibrous tissue, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional fibrous tissue, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of tissue. 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aSEK/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
