cm in aggregate). The second pink cassette, "B", contains multiple \u000ahemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue cores (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm in aggregate). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : "A CA++", multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : "B", multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, "left breast site #1", and contains two green cassettes. The first \u000agreen cassette, "A CA++", contains multiple yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue \u000acores (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm in aggregate). The second green cassette, "B", \u000acontains multiple focally hemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue cores (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.3cm in aggregate). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : "A CA++", multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : "B", multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart C, "left breast site #2 (brown)", and contains two brown cassettes. The \u000afirst brown cassette, "A CA++", contains multiple tan/yellow fibroadipose \u000atissue cores (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm in aggregate). The second brown cassette, \u000a"B", contains multiple yellow/tan focally hemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue cores \u000a(2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm in aggregate). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : "A CA++", multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : "B", multi frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000adfi/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a12/20/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: \u000aAccording to Dr. Durfee, the left breast biopsy from site #2 is from the upper \u000ainner breast. \u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
