VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHERINA ZABICKI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, MRI-GUIDED WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR \u000aSEGMENTAL ENHANCEMENT": \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, involving sclerosing adenosis and mucinous \u000aspherulosis. \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies confirm the absence of e-cadherin and presence \u000aof myoepithelial cells (p63 and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID / REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), supporting the above diagnosis. \u000aIntraductal papillomas with florid epithelial hyperplasia. \u000aCysts with rupture and chronic inflammation. \u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium. \u000aNOTE: The entire specimen was examined microscopically, including the margins. \u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, NIPPLE-SPARING MASTECTOMY": \u000aBenign breast tissue with columnar cell hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis, \u000afibroadenomatoid change, and cystic changes. \u000aBiopsy cavity with repair reaction. \u000aThe deep margin is free of tumor. \u000aNo residual phyllodes tumor present. \u000aNOTE: \u000aThe case has been reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service) who \u000aconcurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 8cm left phyllodes tumor, abnormal right breast MRI enhancement. \u000aOperation: L simple mastectomy. R NL lumpectomy. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast phyllodes tumor, abnormal MRI right breast. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right breast tissue to mammogram. \u000aB/2. Left breast - short stitch superior, long stitch lateral (0.525 kg). \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aMRI guided localization of (separately) enhancing tissue. Calcs, tissue + \u000aintact hookwire in specimen. MN  REMOVED_CASE_ID  REMOVED_DATE \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname, unit number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast tissue", and consists of a portion of white/tan \u000afibroadipose tissue (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm ). The needle localization wire in \u000aplace (ensuring at the medial aspect and exiting at the anterolateral aspect). \u000aThe specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation \u000aof margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; \u000alateral/yellow; medial/ orange. \u000aNo suture is present on the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from \u000alateral to medial, exhibiting approximately 70% white/tan, focally cystic to \u000agranular fibrous stroma admixed with 30% yellow, lobulated adipose tissue. The \u000aaccompanying radiograph and radiology confirmed: "MRI-guided localization of \u000aenhancing tissue calcs, tissue and intact hookwire in specimen MN". The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast tissue sequentially from lateral to medial, multi frags, \u000aESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast short stitch superior, long stitch lateral", and \u000aconsists of a simple mastectomy specimen (488 grams; REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm ) \u000awithout an overlying skin/nipple areolar complex. Two orienting sutures are \u000apresent ("long suture - lateral; short suture - superior"). The deep margin is \u000ainked black and the specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. \u000aThere is a white/tan, firm, fibrotic area (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm ), grossly \u000aconsistent with a previous biopsy site, which grossly comes within 0.5cm of \u000athe deep margin, between the upper outer and lower outer quadrants. There is \u000afocal fat necrosis adjacent to the aforementioned lesion. The remaining breast \u000atissue consists of approximately 70% yellow, lobulated adipose tissue and 30% \u000atan/white dense fibrous stroma. No other gross lesion is identified. The \u000alateral breast tissue is dissected and no lymph nodes identified. \u000aAlso, received in the same container are few fragments of yellow, lobulated, \u000agrossly unremarkable fibroadipose tissue (9.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm in aggregate). \u000aTissue is sectioned. No gross lesion is identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy cavity in relation to deep margin, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional fibrous tissue adjacent to cavity, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central breast fibrous stroma, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional breast tissue, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aDFI/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a3/26/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
