emonstrates a localization wire \u000aentering the posteromedial aspect of the specimen. (The localization wire is \u000aloosely attached to the specimen). The specimen is serially sectioned from \u000amedial to lateral to reveal a well-circumscribed focally cystic nodule (1.8 x \u000a1.2 x 0.8cm ) and is located 0.1cm to the medial margin, 1.0cm from the \u000alateral margin, 0.2cm from the inferior margin, 0.1cm from the superior \u000amargin, 0.1cm from the posterior margin, and 0.1cm from the anterior margin. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, perpendicular, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Specimen serially sectioned from medial to lateral (micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  1 \u000aslice bisected, micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  corresponds to area of clip), multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, perpendicular, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aDCP/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a2/27/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
