VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME -MORHUN \u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, MASTECTOMY: \u000aAtypical ductal epithelial hyperplasia with scant microcalcifications. \u000aDuctal epithelial hyperplasia. \u000aFibroadenoma (0.22cm ). \u000aSclerosing adenosis. \u000aApocrine cysts. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins \u000aRIGHT BREAST, MASTECTOMY: \u000aBiopsy site changes. \u000aFlorid ductal epithelial hyperplasia. \u000aFibroadenoma (1.2cm ). \u000aSkeletal muscle, negative for tumor. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Right pleomorphic LCIS with 1mm micro invasion. \u000aOperation: Bilateral mastectomy with insertion tissue expanders. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000a#1. Left breast short stitch superior, long lateral, 140 gms. \u000a#2. Right breast short superior, long lateral 110 gms \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and medical record number. \u000aPart 1, labeled "#1. Left breast short stitch superior, long lateral", and \u000aconsists of a left simple mastectomy specimen (16.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ) with a \u000awhite/tan skin ellipse (6.5 x 3.0cm ). There is a 1.2cm nipple located at the \u000acenter of the skin ellipse with a 3.0cm wrinkled areola around it. No biopsy \u000acavity is grossly identified. 80% of the breast tissue is composed of an \u000aill-defined tan/white/pink fibrotic area occupying the entire inner upper, \u000ainner lower, and the medial half of the upper outer and lower outer quadrants. \u000aThe fibrotic area abuts the black-inked deep resection margin. No surgical \u000ascar is grossly identified on the skin ellipse. The specimen is searched \u000acarefully but no lymph nodes identified. The gross specimen is reviewed by Dr. \u000aBennett. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple in relation to underlying fibrotic tissue, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : The lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : The upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : The lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : The outer upper quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast, short superior, long lateral", and consists of a \u000amastectomy specimen (14.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.8cm ) with a tan/white skin ellipse (5.0 x \u000a3.5cm ) containing a 1.0cm diameter nipple at the center and 2.5cm wrinkled \u000aareola around the nipple. The deep resection margin is covered by fibrous \u000afascia with a shallow rent (1.5 x 1.0cm ) at the center of the deep resection \u000amargin, 4.0cm from the lateral resection margin, 3.5cm from the medial \u000aresection margin, 6.5cm from the superior resection margin and 8.0cm from the \u000ainferior resection margin. A tan/pink well-circumscribed firm nodule (1.2 x \u000a0.7 x 0.6cm   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) is present at 1 o'clock and is 3.0cm from the nipple. This \u000anodule is adjacent to a tan/white firm irregular-shaped fibrotic area (1.0 x \u000a1.0 x 1.0cm ) laterally. Both the nodule and adjacent fibrotic area are less \u000athan 0.2cm grossly from the deep resection margin (inked black). 0.8cm \u000ainferior-laterally to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is a second, ill-defined tan/gray firm mass (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 0.6cm   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) that is 1.5cm from the nipple.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is less than 0.3cm from the \u000aclosest deep resection margin in the area the aforementioned rent on deep \u000aresection margin. The skin and underlying /neighboring breast tissue at 3 \u000ao'clock (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ) appears hemorrhagic/granular, consistent with old \u000asurgery/biopsy site. The rest of the specimen is composed about 60% fibrous \u000atissue and 40% adipose tissue. No lymph nodes are identified after carefully \u000asearching. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple in relation to the skin at 3 o'clock, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Rest of the hemorrhagic/granular skin and subcutaneous tissue at 3 \u000ao'clock, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Well-circumscribed nodule at 1 o'clock ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) in relation to surround \u000afibrous tissue and black-inked deep resection margin, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the fibrous tissue in between (the well-circumscribed \u000anodule side inked blue), 2 frags, 1 frag in each block, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID :  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 3 frags, 1 frag in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and 2 frags in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : The outer lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : The outer upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : The inner lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : The inner upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aqy/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on \u000a5/24/ RE