VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material \u000aProcedure Date: \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Jane E Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM MOUNT AUBURN HOSPITAL, CAMBRIDGE, MA: \u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; 4/23/07): \u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, is present \u000aas a 0.15cm focus (by report, in one of 9 blocks; block 3) (see note). The \u000aADH is adjacent to the prior core needle biopsy site. \u000aCalcifications are present within ADH. However, the majority of the \u000acalcifications are present in benign epithelium. \u000aThe ADH is < 0.1cm from an unoriented margin. \u000aNote: The ADH consists of a population of cells with apocrine change and \u000anuclear atypia, forming small cribriform spaces. Although the lesion \u000aapproaches a diagnosis of DCIS, given the very small size, classification as \u000aADH is favored. Due to the proximity to the margin, re-excision to evaluate \u000athe adjacent tissue would be of value. \u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Deborah Dillon, who concurs with this \u000ainterpretation. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Left abnormal mammogram. A prior core needle biopsy at Mount Auburn \u000aHospital (their number MS 07-402) for calcifications was reported to show ADH \u000aassociated with calcifications. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: CIS and ADH. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aConsult slides. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aReceived from Mount Auburn Hospital, Pathology Department, 330 Mt. Auburn \u000aStreet, Cambridge, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID , are fourteen (14) glass slides. \u000aThe slides are labeled " REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID " and sublabeled "1 3", "1 6", "2 3", "2 6", "2 \u000a8", "3 3","4 2", "4 3", "4 8", "5 2 E-CAD", "5 3", "6 2"( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) and "6 4", \u000acorresponding to a left breast wire needle localized excision for \u000amicrocalcifications (4 x 4 x 0.8cm ) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the \u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name. \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a7/10/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
