VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Kevin Golden, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST", PROPHYLACTIC SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: \u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia, columnar change, \u000aapocrine metaplasia, sclerosing adenosis, intraductal papilloma, \u000aand microcalcifications present in association with benign epithelium. \u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST", SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: \u000aBenign breast tissue with columnar change, apocrine metaplasia, \u000asclerosing adenosis, and calcifications associated with benign \u000aepithelium (both in association with and away from the prior biopsy \u000asite). \u000aBiopsy site changes. \u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the \u000aspecimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 60 y. o. woman with microcalcs, seen on screening mammogram at Mt. \u000aAuburn Hosp. Surgical biopsy at Mt. Auburn Hosp REMOVED_DATE read as DCIS. Second \u000aopinion at BWH, read as borderline DCIS. Pt discussed Dr. Talivera. Repeat \u000adigital mammogram, right at Mt. Auburn Hosp showed suspicious microcalcs. \u000aOperation: Left breast simple mastectomy; right breast prophylactic simple \u000amastectomy. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast DCIS. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Right breast, stitches on tail. \u000aB/2) Left breast, long stitch on axillary tail, short stitch on documented \u000acancer. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aNote: Abrupt end of dictation. \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and medical record number. \u000aThe specimen, Part A, "#1. Right breast - stitch on tail", consists of a simple \u000abreast mastectomy specimen on the right. The specimen weighs 96 grams and \u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.6cm  There was a stitch tied on at the axillary \u000atail. There is an attached skin ellipse, measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1.8cm and nipple \u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm  There were no scars present on the skin. The deep \u000amargin consisted of smooth, glistening fascia and was inked black. Upon serial \u000asectioning, there were no specific pathologic changes, and there was 85% \u000aadipose tissue and 15% dense white fibrous tissue. Approximately 80% of the \u000afibrous areas are submitted for review. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of fibrous tissue, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fragments of axillary tail, multi frags, RSS. \u000aThe specimen, Part B, "#2. Left breast and axillary tail, long stitch on \u000aaxillary tail, short stitch on documented cancer", consists of left mastectomy \u000aspecimen . The specimen weighs 92 grams and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm  \u000aThere was a skin ellipse on the surface measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm with a nipple \u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm  There are no scars or retractions seen on the skin. \u000aThe deep margin shows smooth fascia, no skeletal muscle and was inked black. \u000aThere was a firm nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm that is located 2.3cm from the \u000adeep margin and 0.9cm from the skin, adjacent to which are biopsy site \u000achanges, measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  These changes are located 2.1cm from the \u000adeep margin and 0.5cm from the skin. There is an additional nodule, measuring \u000a0.5 x 0.6cm  measuring 1.0cm from the deep margin and 1.1cm from the skin. \u000aApproximately 80% of the tissue was submitted for evaluation, including the \u000aentirety of both nodules and the biopsy site. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : First mentioned area with stitch, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional nodule, 1 frag each ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : UOQ, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : UIQ, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : LOQ, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : LIQ, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Axillary tail, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMDH/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a7/20/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
