00awith a clip and a hyperdense region in the middle of the specimen. The \u000aspecimen was serially sectioned medial to lateral into nine slices and \u000arevealing a dense fibrous mass surrounded by adipose tissue along with changes \u000aconsistent with prior biopsy site. The mass measures approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. The specimen is located approximately 0.6cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the posterior margin, 2.2cm from the inferior margin and 0.8cm from \u000athe superior margin. The mass is located approximately 1.5cm from the lateral \u000amargin and 2.0cm from the medial margin. The mass is located primarily in \u000aslices #4, #5 and #6. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic \u000asection. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Perpendicularly sliced lateral margin, 4 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #8, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Perpendicular sections of medial margin, multi frags, ESS. \u000aThis case was reviewed with Dr. Jane E Brock, fellow in breast pathology. \u000aMDH/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
