f the wire as well \u000aas two tight areas of calcification away from the wire near the inferior \u000amargin. The specimen is inked by the surgeon as follows: Red equals superior, \u000aorange equals medial, yellow equals lateral, green equals inferior, blue equals \u000aanterior, black equals posterior. There is a brown, focally hemorrhagic core \u000abiopsy site (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ) with surgical clip that abuts the medial and \u000aanterior and lateral margins, is 1.3cm to the inferior margin, is 0.6cm to \u000athe posterior margin, and is 0.2cm to the superior margin. There is also a \u000awhite, fibrotic area (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ) that abuts the inferior and lateral \u000amargins. The remainder of the specimen consists of adipose tissue. The \u000aspecimen is sectioned medial to lateral and the entire specimen is sequentially \u000asubmitted for histologic evaluation. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast excision specimen, sequentially sectioned from medial to \u000alateral,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  = area of clip,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  = fibrotic area ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /2 frags each, \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /1 frag each), ESS. \u000aEM/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
