e chest wall margin. The \u000aspecimen measures 2.0cm superior to inferior, 2.1cm medial to lateral, and \u000a2.5cm anterior to posterior. The specimen is received inked by the surgeon in \u000athe OR per pathology protocol, with red superior, green inferior, black \u000aposterior, blue anterior, orange medial, and yellow lateral. Accompanying the \u000aspecimen is a radiograph illustrating a wire entering the anterior aspect of \u000athe specimen, but not exiting the specimen. This wire is localizing a presumed \u000aprevious biopsy cavity, but no clip is identified on the radiograph. There is \u000aalso an area of calcifications that were not targeted. The specimen is fixed, \u000aserially sectioned from posterior to anterior, to reveal approximately a 50% \u000afirm white fibrous tissue and 50% yellow lobulated fatty tissue composition. \u000aNo clip is noted in the specimen. The entire specimen is submitted for \u000ahistology. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin, perpendicular sections, 5 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Serially sections from posterior to anterior, 1 frag per cassette, \u000aESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, perpendicular sections, 3 frags per cassette, \u000aESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000apva/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on Monday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 06,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05:08:56PM \u000a[report_end] 
