VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Skin bx cyst, tag, or debridement \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHERINA ZABICKI CALVILLO M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST SCAR": \u000aSkin with scarring. \u000aFibroadipose tissue with scarring and foreign body giant cell reaction to \u000apolarizable material consistent with suture. \u000aResidual breast tissue is present. \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE #1" (including FSA): \u000aOne (1) Lymph node negative for tumor. \u000aThree (3) H&E levels examined. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST": \u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aRadial scar with epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, and \u000asclerosing adenosis associated with microcalcifications. \u000aIntraductal papilloma with epithelial hyperplasia. \u000aSkin and nipple with no significant pathologic change. \u000aNOTE: The microcalcifications identified on imaging (by report) likely \u000acorrelate to the extensive adenosis identified in this specimen. A "negative" \u000abiopsy of this area was reportedly performed, but no biopsy site changes are \u000aidentified. Clinical correlation is suggested. \u000aThis portion of the case was also reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology \u000aService, who concurs. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE #2" (including FSB): \u000aOne (1) lymph node negative for tumor. \u000aThree (3) H&E levels examined. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST SKIN TISSUE": \u000aSkin and subcutaneous tissue with no significant pathologic change. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 52 y o female with history of left breast CA presenting today for 