aple. The specimen are serially sectioned to reveal \u000aunderlying yellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no discrete masses or lesions \u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin and underlying adipose tissue from container labeled "#1. \u000aLeft breast scar", 3 frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin and underlying adipose tissue from container labeled "#1. Left \u000abreast scar cont B", 2 frags, RSS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right axillary sentinel lymph node #1", consists of an \u000airregular portion of yellow lobulated adipose tissue (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ), in \u000awhich a thin rubbery lymph node is identified (2.0cm ). The lymph node is \u000abisected, and is submitted in its entirety for frozen section as FSA. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : FSA remnant, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Right breast stitch, long lateral, short superior", \u000aconsists of a right mastectomy ( REMOVED_CASE_ID  grams, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6.0cm ), with a long \u000asuture designating lateral, and a short suture designating superior. There is \u000aan overlying, unremarkable nipple-areolar complex (5.5 x 4.0cm ), with an \u000aeverted nipple (1.4cm in diameter). The posterior margin is inked black and \u000athe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a pink, chalky yellow stellate \u000aarea (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ), within the lower inner quadrant, 5.0cm inferior to \u000athe nipple at the 6 o'clock position and 3.5cm from the black inked posterior \u000amargin. The remaining cut surface displays 50% dense white, focally nodular \u000aand cystic fibrous tissue, and 40% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no \u000aadditional discrete masses or lesions identified. No lymph nodes are \u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Dense white fibrous tissue from upper outer quadrant to include \u000athe posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Dense white fibrous tissue from lower outer quadrant, to include \u000athe posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Dense white fibrous tissue from lower inner quadrant, with the \u000aposterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the stellate area in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , mult frags RSS \u000a(stellate area, ESS). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Dense white fibrous tissue from upper inner quadrant, to include \u000aposterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , mult frags, RSS. \u000aPart D, labeled "#4. Right axillary sentinel lymph node #2", consists of an \u000airregular portion of yellow lobulated adipose tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ), in \u000awhich a pink/tan rubbery lymph node is identified (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ), which \u000ais bisected and submitted in its entirety for frozen section as FSB. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : FSB remnant, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart E, labeled "#5. Rt breast skin tissue", consists of multiple irregular \u000aportions of tan/pink unremarkable skin fragments with underlying fibrofatty \u000atissue (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm ). The specimens are serially sectioned \u000ato reveal underlying yellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no discrete masses \u000aor lesions identified. Representative sections are submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags each, RSS. \u000aCP/mmm \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on \u000a12/17/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
