VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Anna Laury, M.D.; Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR FOUR MASSES: \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aRadial scar (slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aSclerosing adenosis. \u000aColumnar cell change and apocrine cysts. \u000aFibroadenoma (0.4cm ). \u000aCalcifications in normal breast tissue. \u000aNote: There is no malignancy seen after complete microscopic examination of \u000athe specimen, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 64 year old female with abnormal MRI and ultrasound of the right \u000abreast, possible complex cyst. \u000aOperation: #1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast abnormal ultrasound. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. right breast, abnormal u/s (to mammo). Documented by surgeon as short \u000asuperior, long lateral. \u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: 4 possible nodules with wire. OR called. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "right breast, abnormal ultrasound", and consists of a oriented portion of \u000afibrofatty tissue that measures 3.9cm from medial to lateral, 2.6cm from \u000aanterior to posterior, and 1.5cm from superior to inferior dimensions. The \u000aspecimen is received with orientation as follows: Short superior, long lateral \u000aas documented by the surgeon. The specimen is received with a \u000aneedle-localization wire and accompanying radiograph. The localization wire \u000aenters the specimen on the lateral aspect and exits on the medial aspect. Also \u000anoted are two clips inserted on the suture material with one clip on the \u000asuperior suture and two clips on the lateral suture. The accompanying \u000aradiograph displays four lesions that will be designated as follows. The \u000alesion located next to the needle entry site will be designated lesion #1, the \u000asecond lesion located immediately medial to first described lesion will be \u000adesignated lesion #2, the lesion adjacent to the needle exit site will be \u000aconsidered lesion #3, the lesion at the most superior deep portion of the \u000aspecimen will be considered lesion #4. The specimen is inked in six colors per \u000apathology protocol as follows: Superior red, inferior green, anterior blue, \u000aposterior black, medial orange, and lateral yellow. Sectioning reveals \u000amultiple smooth lined cysts ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0.3cm in greatest dimension. \u000aLesion #1, cyst is filled with dark red semisolid fluid. Cyst #2 is also \u000afilled with dark red semisolid fluid. Lesion #4 grossly appears to be \u000acomprised of dense white fibrous tissue. Lesion #3 displays a single smooth \u000alined cyst and 0.2cm in greatest dimension partially filled with dark red \u000asemisolid fluid. There are also two small nodules located in the medial aspect \u000aof the specimen, REMOVED_DATE and 0.3cm in greatest dimension that come to within less \u000athan 0.1cm of the inked posterior margin. Sectioning displays the approximate \u000acomposition of being 80% to 85% dense white fibrous tissue with 15% diffuse \u000aunremarkable yellow adipose tissue. The entire specimen is examined \u000amicroscopically. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral perpendicular margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lesion #1 submitted entirely with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Both the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  lesion with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Third described lesion submitted entirely with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  1 frag, ESS. \u000apf/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a3/3/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
