 (4.2 S-I x REMOVED_DATE M-L x REMOVED_DATE A-Pcm ) which is oriented per surgeon as \u000afollows, short equals superior, long equals lateral, whipstitch equals chest \u000awall margin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation \u000aof margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; \u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. A needle-localization wire is not present \u000awithin the specimen or the specimen container. The specimen was previously \u000aradiograph, confirming the presence of calcification in the periphery of the \u000aspecimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to exhibit \u000aapproximately 90% yellow/tan adipose tissue and 10% delicate pink/tan fibrous \u000astroma. No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, perpendicularly suctioned, multi frags in \u000aeach, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central specimen from lateral to medial (probable area of \u000acalcification in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Inferolateral shaved margin, whip stitch new margin", consists of \u000aan irregular multifocally disrupted fragment of yellow/tan breast tissue (3.8 x \u000a3.0 x 1.5cm ). Per surgeon, one surface of the specimen exhibits a whipstitch, \u000adesignating the new true margin (inked black per prosector). The opposite \u000anon-sutured surface is inked blue (blue does not equal true margin). A \u000aneedle-localization wire is received separately free-floating within the \u000aspecimen container. The specimen was previously radiographed, with no masses \u000aor calcifications identified. The specimen is serially sectioned to exhibit \u000agreater than 90% yellow/tan adipose tissue and less than 10% pink/tan fibrous \u000astroma which extends to the black inked new true margin. No discrete masses or \u000alesions are grossly identified. Also received in the specimen container are \u000atwo irregular fragments of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm \u000ain aggregate) with unremarkable cut surfaces. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Shave margin, multi frags total, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Separate tissue fragment, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aLM/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
