which enters through the inferior aspect of the specimen and exits through the \u000aanterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol \u000a(superior/red, inferior/green, medial/orange, lateral/yellow, anterior/blue, \u000aand posterior/black) and is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. There \u000ais a focal ill-defined dense white fibrous area (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm ) which \u000aabuts the anterior, posterior, and inferior margins, comes within 0.4cm from \u000athe superior margin, 2.8cm from the medial margin, and 1.5cm from the lateral \u000amargin. The remainder of the cut surface is tan/yellow and homogenous with no \u000adiscrete lesions grossly identified. The specimen is submitted in its \u000aentirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections of blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to include focal dense \u000awhite fibrous areas corresponding to areas of calcification on the specimen \u000aradiograph, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000asek/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (9/02/08): \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy including examination of margins. \u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
