VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, mastectomy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Tanya Rege, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, PROPHYLACTIC TOTAL MASTECTOMY" ( REMOVED_CASE_ID g): \u000aBreast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia, apocrine cysts, \u000aand giant cell reaction with hemosiderin-laden macrophages \u000aconsistent with a ruptured cyst. \u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aSkeletal muscle with no significant pathologic change. \u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor (0:1). \u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "NON-SENTINEL LYMPH NODES, BIOPSY": \u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor (0:1). \u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT MASTECTOMY SCAR, EXCISION": \u000aSkin and subcutis, negative for tumor. \u000aD. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT MASTECTOMY SKIN, EXCISION": \u000aSkin and subcutis, negative for tumor. \u000aE. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT MASTECTOMY SKIN, EXCISION": \u000aSkin and subcutis, negative for tumor. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: History of contralateral breast cancer - elevated risk L breast \u000acancer. \u000aOperation: L prophylactic total mastectomy, bilat breast reconstruction, DIEP \u000aFlaps. \u000aOperative Findings: Normal-appearing breast - 2 nodes in tail of breast. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: History of right breast cancer. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) left breast - short/superior, long/lateral ( REMOVED_CASE_ID ). \u000aB/2) non-sentinel nodes (tail of breast). \u000aC/3) rt mastectomy scar. \u000aD/4) left mastectomy skin. \u000aE/5) right mastectomy skin. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in five parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast short superior, long lateral,  REMOVED_CASE_ID ", consists of a \u000aleft simple mastectomy ( REMOVED_CASE_ID  g, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6.0cm ), with a long suture \u000adesignating lateral, and a short suture designating superior. There is an \u000aoverlying tan-pink irregular skin (6.7 x 4.7cm ), displaying focal areas of \u000ablue dye, consistent with sentinel node dye. There is an unremarkable nipple \u000aareolar complex (3.8 x 3.5cm ), with a slightly inverted nipple (1.2cm in \u000adiameter). The posterior margin is inked black and the specimen is serially \u000asectioned to reveal 60% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 40% focally dense \u000awhite fibrous tissue, with no discrete masses or lesions identified. A \u000atan-pink possible rubbery lymph node is identified within the upper outer \u000aquadrant (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ). Representative sections are submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant dense white fibrous tissue, with the \u000aposterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Dense white fibrous tissue from lower outer quadrant, to include \u000athe black-inked posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Dense white fibrous tissue from upper inner quadrant, to include \u000athe posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Dense white fibrous tissue from lower inner quadrant, to include \u000athe posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 2 frags each, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Tan-pink lymph node from upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart B, "#2. Nonsentinel node", consists of two tan-pink rubber lymph nodes \u000a(0.5cm  and 1.2cm ), which are submitted in toto. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart C, "#3. RT mastectomy scar", consists of a tan-pink unremarkable wrinkled \u000airregular skin (13.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ). A discrete mass or lesion is not \u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 4 frags, RSS. \u000aPart D, "#4. Left mastectomy skin", consists of two tan-pink irregular wrinkled \u000aportions of skin (measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ). The \u000asecond described portion of skin displays a pink vesicle (0.4cm ). No \u000aadditional discrete masses or lesions are identified. Representative sections \u000aare submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Unremarkable tan-pink irregular skin, 3 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Tan-pink skin with vesicle (inked blue), 2 frags, RSS (vesicle ESS). \u000aPart E, "#5. Right mastectomy skin", consists of an unremarkable irregular \u000atan-pink skin (17.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE (depth)cm ). A discrete mass or lesion is not \u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 frags, RSS. \u000acp/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a6/20/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
