rior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. A radiograph demonstrates a localization wire entering the \u000aanterior aspect of the specimen and exiting the posterior aspect of the \u000aspecimen, designating a surgical clip at a prior biopsy site. Grossly the \u000asurgical clip is 0.5cm from the anterior margin, 0.8cm from the superior \u000amargin, 0.7cm from the inferior margin, 2.5cm from the posterior margin, \u000agreater than 1.0cm from the medial and lateral margins. A gross lesion at the \u000asite of the surgical clip is not seen. The tissue consists of 80% dense \u000afibrous tissue and 20% adipose tissue. The specimen is submitted entirely. \u000aGross photographs of the specimen are taken. The location of the tissue blocks \u000ais recorded on a specimen diagram. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial resection margin, radially sectioned, multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Serial sections of breast from medial to lateral, surgical clip \u000ain  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral resection margin, radially sectioned, multi frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aKRI/lp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
