VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Kremena V. Star, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. RIGHT BREAST: \u000aCalcifications in benign breast epithelium. \u000aBenign breast tissue with columnar cell changes. \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000aB. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES (including FSA): \u000aThree lymph nodes, negative for tumor (0:3). \u000aC. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES (including FSB): \u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor (0:1). \u000aD. LEFT BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU \u000aTypes - Solid, cribriform \u000aNuclear grade - High \u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent \u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present \u000aExtent of DCIS \u000aEstimated overall size - 0.2cm \u000aNumber of blocks/total - 2:23 blocks; adjacent to prior \u000abiopsy site \u000aMargins (DCIS) \u000aNegative (> 0.3cm ) - Deep resection margin \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present \u000aLYMPH NODES - Please see Parts B and C \u000aOTHER FINDINGS \u000aCore biopsy site \u000aFibroadenoma (6mm ) \u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): Tis  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (including parts B & C) MX. \u000aNOTE: Part D was reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who \u000aconcurs. \u000aE. RIGHT BREAST, OLD SCAR: \u000aFibrosis and fat necrosis with foreign body giant cell reaction. \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000aF. ADDITIONAL SKIN MARGIN, LEFT BREAST SITE: \u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change. \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 53 y/o premenopausal female with a history of L breast LCIS & ALH. \u000aMammogram REMOVED_DATE demonstrates a 6-mm LUOQ cluster of calcifications. REMOVED_DATE \u000astereotactic core biopsy revealed solid and cribriform, ER/PR (+) her 2/Neu(-) \u000aDCIS (LCIS was in LLOQ). \u000aOperation: L simple mastectomy, sentinel lymph node biopsy with possible Level \u000aI & II dissections; R prophylactic mastectomy. \u000aPREVIOUS SURGERY: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aOperative Findings: None provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast DCIS. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Right breast - Stitch, short - superior; long - lateral. \u000aB/2) Left sentinal lymph node (hot ^ not blue) - FS. \u000aC/3) Left sentinel lymph node (hot & blue) - F.S. \u000aD/4) Left breast - stitch, short - superior; long - lateral. \u000aE/5) Old scar, right breast. \u000aF/6) Additional skin margin, left breast site. \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE" (FSA): \u000aThree lymph nodes, negative for tumor. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#3. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE" (FSB): \u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor. \u000aOR Consultation by: Alessandra F. Nascimento, M.D. \u000aResident: Paul A. VanderLaan, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in six parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast - stitch short superior - long lateral", consists of \u000aa 360 gram simple mastectomy specimen (17.5cm superior to inferior, 19.9cm \u000amedial to lateral, 1.5cm anterior to posterior), areolar complex (7.4 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), and an inverted nipple (1.1 x 1.1cm ). The deep resection margin is lined \u000aby fascia, which is focally disrupted and inked black. The specimen consists \u000aof 50% breast tissue and 50% adipos