VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s) \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Leona A. Doyle, M.D.; Stephanie Schulte, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. RIGHT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE (1), EXCISION (INCLUDING FSA): \u000aOne (1) lymph node, negative for carcinoma (3 H&E levels examined). \u000aB. RIGHT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE (2), EXCISION (INCLUDING FSB): \u000aOne (1) lymph node, negative for carcinoma (3 H&E levels examined). \u000aC. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR TWO CLIPS: \u000aEpithelial cells with nuclear ATYPIA are present within ducts and lobules (see \u000anote). \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present. \u000aBiopsy site changes are present at the site of the clip (posterior/medial; see \u000anote). \u000aMinute focus of biopsy site change present at the anterior/lateral margin (see \u000anote). \u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aD. ADDITIONAL INFEROMEDIAL TISSUE, EXCISION: \u000aEpithelial cells with nuclear ATYPIA are present within ducts and lobules (see \u000anote). \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present. \u000aBiopsy site changes are not seen. \u000aE. ADDITIONAL INFEROLATERAL TISSUE, EXCISION: \u000aEpithelial cells with nuclear ATYPIA are present within ducts and lobules (see \u000anote). \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present. \u000aBiopsy site changes are not seen. \u000aNote: By report, the patient had a 0.6cm well-differentiated invasive ductal \u000acarcinoma diagnosed in the right breast in REMOVED_MONTH  REMOVED_CASE_ID  (ER/PR positive, Her2/neu \u000anegative) with no lymphovascular invasion. Following re-excision with negative \u000amargins and one negative sentinel lymph node in May  REMOVED_CASE_ID , the patient underwent \u000aradiation therapy. By report, MRI in REMOVED_MONTH  REMOVED_CASE_ID  demonstrated two MRI \u000aabnormalities in the right breast (one of which was located anterior to the \u000ascar from her prior excision) and a 0.6cm mass in the left breast, for which \u000athe patient underwent core needle biopsies in REMOVED_MONTH  REMOVED_CASE_ID . By report, the \u000amass in the left breast was a fibroadenoma. By report, in the right breast, one \u000asite showed a 0.3cm well-differentiated invasive ductal carcinoma (ER/PR \u000apositive, Her2/neu negative) and the other site showed atypical ductal \u000ahyperplasia (slides reviewed at Faulkner Hospital as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). By report, an \u000aAtec bar clip was placed at the site of the atypical ductal hyperplasia and an \u000aOmega clip was placed at the site of the invasive ductal carcinoma. \u000aSpecimen radiograph of the current excision demonstrated one of the targeted \u000aclips (Atec clip). Two additional excisions were taken (see below, parts D and \u000aE), neither of which demonstrated the second targeted Omega clip. \u000aBy report, no clips were seen on the post-operative mammogram and it appears \u000amost likely that the second clip (marking the site of the invasive ductal \u000acarcinoma) fell out or was suctioned out during surgery. The second clip was \u000anot identified grossly in the resected specimen or in radiographs of the blocks \u000aof the entirely submitted specimen. \u000aBiopsy site changes are present in the area of the first clip (as identified on \u000aspecimen radiograph and gross examination) in the medial/posterior portion of \u000athe specimen (blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). Biopsy site changes are present as small foci \u000a(0.1cm each) at the anterior/lateral margin (blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  level 10). \u000aMultiple levels have been examined. Whether this represents the site of the \u000aprevious excision or the second clip cannot be determined with certainty. \u000aImmunohistochemistry for E-cadherin confirms absence of membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in lobular carcinoma in situ, with retention of \u000aimmunoreactivity for estrogen receptor and progesterone receptor. Additional \u000afoci showing intraductal epithelial cells with nuclear atypia are present (e.g. \u000ablocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). Recent radiation therapy limits the \u000ainterpretation of these changes. Architectural complexity is not present and \u000adiagnostic features of DCIS are not seen. Representative slides also seen by \u000aDr. Susan Lester, who concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Not provided \u000aOperation: Not provided \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Not provided \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right sentinel node (1) (count 122) \u000aB/2. Right sentinel node (2) (count 386) \u000aC/3. Right breast tissue with wire \u000aD/4. Additional inferomedial tissue (green/true inferior margin; \u000aorange/medial margin - approaches areola-mammo) \u000aE/5. Additional inferolateral tissue (green/inferior; yellow/lateral \u000aadjacent to skin - mammo) \u000aO.R. CONSULTATION: \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. RIGHT SENTINEL NODE (1)" (FSA): \u000aOne lymph node - negative for tumor. \u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. RIGHT SENTINEL NODE (2)" (FSB): \u000aOne lymph node - negative for tumor. \u000aOR Consultation by: Lucian Chirieac, M.D. \u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or \u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed \u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto. \u000aRADIOLOGY COMMENT: \u000aC/3: Targeted clip in specimen - second targeted clip at site of IDC is NOT in \u000aspecimen. DW/JR - Dr. Lesnikoski. \u000aD/4: Two additional, specimens do not show targeted clip which marked \u000ainvasive cancer site. Please look for bx site changes and invasive ca/JR \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in five parts, each labeled with the patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right sentinel node #1", consists of a single tan-yellow \u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ) with a single lymph node \u000a(0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ). The lymph node is entirely submitted as FSA. The \u000aremaining tissue is entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining adipose tissue, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right sentinel node #2", consists of a single fragment of \u000aadipose tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ) with a single lymph node (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). The lymph node is entirely submitted as FSB. Remaining tissue is \u000aentirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : FSB remnant, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining adipose tissue, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Right breast tissue with wire", consists of a single \u000abreast excision specimen (12 g, 4.0cm superior to inferior, 3.8cm medial to \u000alateral and 0.9cm anterior to posterior). The specimen is received previously \u000ainked by surgeon for the evaluation of margins, posterior black, anterior blue, \u000amedial orange, lateral yellow, superior red and inferior green. No orienting \u000asutures are present. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a \u000alocalization wire entering the specimen and associated with a single metallic \u000aclip. Grossly, the wire enters anteriorly and extends to the posteromedial \u000aaspect of the specimen. In this area, a metallic clip is located in \u000aassociation with focal hemorrhage and fat necrosis over an area of less than \u000a0.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.1cm  0.2cm to posterior margin and 0.4cm to the medial margin, \u000a0.4cm to anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE to lateral margin, and remote from the superior \u000aand inferior margins. The surrounding breast parenchyma is firm, rubbery and \u000afibrous with no discrete lesions identified. Also described within the \u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph, the second area of interest is situated at \u000athe lateral aspect of the specimen. In this area there is no clip and no \u000adefinite biopsy site changes or discrete masses grossly. The breast parenchyma \u000ahas a similar firm rubbery texture to the remaining breast parenchyma. The \u000aentire specimen is serially sectioned and submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Breast parenchyma around clip (clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) to include closest \u000amargins (posterior and medial in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , anterior  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterolateral breast parenchyma, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining breast tissue, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS. \u000aPart D, labeled "#4. Right additional inferomedial margin, green marks to \u000ainferior margin, orange marks medial margin approaching areola", consists of a \u000asingle fragment of tan-pink fibroadipose tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ) \u000awith one surface previously inked by surgeon, half green and half orange. The \u000aopposite smoother surface is received uninked and is inked black by prosector. \u000aNo discrete lesions are identified. The specimen is serially sectioned and \u000aentirely submitted. Note: \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : New inferomedial margin, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS. \u000aPart E, labeled "#5. Right additional inferolateral tissue, green inferior, \u000ayellow lateral adjacent to skin", consists of a single fragment of tan-pink \u000afibroadipose tissue (6.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ) with one surface inked green and \u000ayellow by surgeon and opposite smoother surface received uninked and inked \u000ablack by prosector. No discrete lesions are identified. The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned and entirely submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : New inferolateral margin, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aldo\u005cpab \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 04,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01:51:06PM \u000a[report_end] 
