VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Christian J. Davidson, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: \u000aColumnar cell change, intraductal papilloma, apocrine metaplasia, and small \u000acysts, with scattered microcalcifications, see NOTE. \u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis. \u000aNOTE: The patient is s/p a core needle biopsy for calcifications which revealed \u000aALH and calcifications associated with benign epithelium (this was the \u000adiagnosis on review at BWH see  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; but reported as ADH & ALH on \u000ainitial outside hospital pathology review). Per Radiology report available in \u000aLMR (BWH; 06/17/09), residual calcifications are not present at the site of \u000abiopsy and the clip marking the presence of a biopsy site was noted to be 4cm \u000ainferior to the site of biopsied calcifications. In this current excision which \u000aaimed to re-excise the prior biopsy site (but not the clip), no biopsy site \u000achanges are seen. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 48-year-old female with right breast atypical lobular hyperplasia \u000aafter image guide core biopsy. \u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast atypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short suture superior, long \u000asuture lateral - mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aThe area of prior biopsy and intact wire are in the specimen. \u000aCalled to Dr. Golshan in OR by Dr. Yeh, 12:05 pm. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThis case consists of one part, and is received fresh and clearly labeled with \u000athe patient's name and medical record number. \u000aSpecimen A, labeled "#1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short \u000asuture superior, long suture lateral-mammo", and consists of one wire \u000alocalized breast excisional biopsy measuring 2.5cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm medial to lateral, and 1.6cm anterior to posterior. A short suture \u000adesignates the superior margin and a long suture designates the lateral margin \u000a(per the surgeon). A localization wire enters at the superior margin and exits \u000aat the inferior margin. A radiograph received with the specimen shows that the \u000athickened area of wire is in a radiodense (fibrous) region of the specimen. \u000aSectioning through the specimen reveals 70% fibrous and 30% adipose tissue. \u000aThe fibrous tissue abuts all margins. No discrete masses or lesions are noted. \u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: \u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; \u000amedial/orange. The entire specimen is submitted for histologic analysis. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : The entire specimen sectioned superior to inferior (with superior \u000aperpendicular in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and inferior perpendicular in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), multi frags total, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000achd/elw \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 23,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02:51:13PM \u000a[report_end] 
