 submitted for histological examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 lymph nodes each, 2 frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining fat, multi frags, ESS. \u000aPart B is labeled "#2. Right breast short superior, long lateral", and consists \u000aof a breast tissue oriented by short suture superiorly and long suture \u000alaterally. A posterior surface is identified, which is inked black. There is \u000ano attached skin. The specimen measures 22.5cm medial to lateral, 20.2cm \u000asuperior to inferior and 6.2cm anterior to posterior. There is an area of \u000adeficit (12.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.9cm ) at the inferolateral margin anteriorly consistent \u000awith history of prior surgeries. The specimen is composed of less than 5% \u000afibrous stroma. No lesions are grossly identified. Representative sections \u000aare taken for histological examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous stroma, 1 frag each, RSS. \u000aPart C is labeled "#3. Right breast skin", and consists of two tan/white skin \u000afragments with attached soft tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). No lesions or scars are identified. A representative section is \u000asubmitted from each piece. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Right breast skin, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aPart D is labeled "#4. Subareolar tissue", and consists of fibroadipose tissue \u000a(2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ). The tissue contains fibrous stroma. This entire \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histological examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Subareolar tissue, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-10- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aVIP/am \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday \u000aFebruary 10,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04:26:35PM \u000a[report_end] 
