VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Cheryl Adackapara, M.D.; Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS: \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present within a cellular fibroadenoma \u000a(3.8cm ) and in adjacent breast tissue. An immunoperoxidase study for \u000acytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID / REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and p63 confirms the presence of myoepithelial cells in \u000aareas of LCIS (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aImmunohistochemical studies are performed at BWH with the following \u000aresults for LCIS: \u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) NEGATIVE (1+) \u000aE-cadherin NEGATIVE \u000aNote: There is extensive LCIS throughout the fibroadenoma. Although some \u000aareas have a nuclear grade slightly higher than typical for LCIS, the \u000apresence of ER and PR and absence of e-cadherin supports classification of \u000aas LCIS. \u000aThe entire specimen was examined microscopically, including margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Right breast fibroepithelial lesion with atypical hyperplasia on prior \u000acore needle biopsy ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy. \u000aOperative Findings: Not provided. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast fibroepithelial lesion. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) right wire localized excisional biopsy - short suture/superior, long \u000asuture/lateral. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aSpecimen - mass and wire - OR called. Dr. Raza. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number \u000aand "right breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short suture/superior, long \u000asuture/lateral", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE (superior to inferior) x REMOVED_DATE x (medial \u000ato lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior)cm breast biopsy with a localization \u000awire in place and a short suture marking the superior margin and a long suture \u000amarking the lateral margin. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a \u000amass in the central portion of the specimen associated with the localization \u000awire. The wire enters at the lateral aspect of the specimen with no visible \u000aexit point. The specimen is inked for the evaluation of margins per pathology \u000aprotocol: Posterior equals black, anterior equals blue, superior equals red, \u000aanterior equals green, lateral equals yellow, and medial equals orange. The \u000aspecimen is sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a tan/white firm \u000alobulated mass (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.6cm ) which is present at the superior, inferior, \u000aanterior, lateral and medial margins, and is 0.3cm to the closest posterior \u000amargin. The remainder of the specimen consists of dense fibrous tissue. The \u000aentire specimen is submitted for histological evaluation from superior to \u000ainferior. Gross photographs of the specimen are taken. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Contains the closest superior margin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Contains the closest lateral and posterior margins. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Contains the closest medial and anterior margins and consists of \u000aone bisected portion of tissue. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Consists of one bisected slice of tissue. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Consists of one bisected slice of tissue. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Consists of the closest inferior margin. \u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following \u000acriteria: \u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the \u000acarcinoma is reported as follows: \u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive \u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet \u000abeen determined. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor \u000acells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but \u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive. \u000aEquivocal (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in \u000a>10% of tumor cells or moderate to strong complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in < 30% of tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in \u000a>30% of tumor cells. \u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result. \u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate immunoreactivity. \u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests \u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance \u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the \u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the \u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such \u000aclearance or approval is not necessary. \u000aCAD/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 07,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 10:54:45PM \u000a[report_end] 
