n. Opposite the new margin is a portion of biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  lined by tan-red granular soft tissue. The new margin is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal predominately white fibrous tissue surrounding the biopsy cavity and the abutting black-inked. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with the biopsy cavity in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and " right breast inferior margin," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm irregular, oriented breast tissue with a double short stitch designating the nipple and 3 single stitches designating the posterior inferior margin, now inked black. The opposite side of the tissue is surfaced by yellow shaggy fatty tissue and tan-pink soft tissue with focal fat necrosis. The specimen is serially sectioned from nipple to opposite end to reveal predominately white fibrous tissue surrounding the irregular surface of the biopsy cavity, and extending to the black-inked margin. The specimen is entirely submitted from nipple to opposite end in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, " right breast deep margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm oriented breast tissue with a stitch designating new margin, now inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Gross Dictation by Nicole Ann Belsley M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Nicole Ann Belsley M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The ductal carcinoma in-situ tumor cells stain faintly for estrogen receptor protein. The ductal carcinoma in-situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. See note. Note: These