sary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Rosemary Tambouret,MD Signed On: 06 MAY 04 at 17:36 *** HER-2 Addendum *** RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast (Left, block B): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates HER-2/neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. Added by: Rosemary Tambouret,MD Signed On: 06 MAY 04 at 17:36 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left breast biopsy" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm irregular tan-yellow to pink lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue with a long suture designating the lateral aspect and a short suture designating the superior aspect. The superior aspect is inked blue, the inferior-black, the medial-green and lateral-yellow. The specimen is sequentially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal a tan-yellow to pink lobulated unremarkable cut surface. The specimen is entirely and sequentially submitted from anterior to posterior in cassettes A-E with the anterior margin in cassette A and the posterior margin in cassette E and the area denoted by the localization wire in cassettes B-C. Gross Description by: JENNIFER NASH Resident: ANDRAS SCHAFFER, MD,PhD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART : BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY 
