 determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 29 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13:07 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "sentinel node axilla level 1" are 2 tan-pink lymph nodes, REMOVED_DATE and 1.8cm  with minimal attached tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue. Both nodes are bisected and submitted entirely as A and B, respectively. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast lumpectomy, short superior, long lateral" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.7cm portion of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue with 2 stitches designating the superior and lateral margins. The posterior margin is inked black, the anterior blue, the medial yellow, and the lateral orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm indurated gray-white stellate mass, which comes to 0.1cm from the anterior, 0.2cm from the posterior, 1.0cm from the lateral, 1.3cm from the inferior, 1.3cm from the medial, and 2.5cm from the superior margins. The remaining cut surface is 5% gray-white fibrous and 95% tan-yellow lobular fibroadipose tissue. Representative sections are submitted as follows: C: Superior margin, radially sectioned. D-F: Tumor submitted entirely from superior to inferior. G: Inferior margin, radially sectioned. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final margin inferior-lateral half of cavity" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm aggregate of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue fragments with no orientation. The fragments are serially sectioned and entirely submitted as H-N. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final margin superior-medial half of cavity, short superior, long lateral" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm portion of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue with 2 black stitches designating the superior and lateral margins. The posterior margin is inked black, the anterior blue, the superior orange, and the inferior yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a well-defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm gray-white rubbery area, which comes to within 0.2cm from the anterior, 0.9cm of the posterior, 0.9cm from the superior, 1.5cm of the inferior, 1.5cm from the lateral, and 4.3cm from the medial margins. The remaining cut surface shows focal areas of dense gray-white fibrosis up to 30%. No other gross abnormalities are identified, and representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as follows: O-Q: Fibrous tissue, with medial margin as O. R-S: Lesion, entirely submitted T: Lateral margin. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional deep margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm portion of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue with no orientation, which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as U-V. Gross Description by: STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident: DI TIAN, MD, PhD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. Francis James Mcgovern, M.D. Barbara Ann Penn, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL NODE LEVEL I), EX PART B: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C: BST(LFT INFEROLATERAL HALF OF CAVITY),FINAL SHAVE PART D: BST(LFT SUPEROMEDIAL HALF OF CAVITY), FINAL SHAVED PART E: BREAST (LEFT), DEEP MARGIN 
