IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. SEE NOTE. BREAST (RIGHT, "LATERAL MARGIN"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. SEE NOTE. NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast tissue" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue incised prior to receipt. A long suture designates the lateral aspect and a short suture the superior aspect of the specimen. The long axis of the specimen runs from anterior to posterior. The specimen is inked as follows: superior blue, inferior black, medial green, and lateral yellow. Sectioning reveals a firm, tan-white nodule, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm  The nodule abuts the inferior and medial margins of the specimen and extends to 0.4cm from the superior margin, 0.3cm from the lateral margin, and more than 1cm from the anterior and posterior margins of the specimen. Sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior tip of specimen.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior tip of specimen.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sections through the mass demonstrating proximity to the inked margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Section taken away from the mass from the posterior aspect of the specimen. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast posterior" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a suture designating the true margin. The true margin is inked. The specimen is sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty tissue and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast superior" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a suture designating the true margin. The true margin is inked. The specimen is sectioned to reveal a ill defined area of dense breast parenchyma, which abuts the margin. This area is approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm and has a tan-yellow appearance. The specimen is submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast anterior" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm fibrofatty tissue, which has a suture designating the true margin. The true margin is inked. The specimen is sectioned to reveal predominantly adipose tissue with an area of dense breast parenchyma measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.1cm  which abuts the margin. The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast medial" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a suture designating the true margin. The true margin is inked. The specimen is sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma. A small area of dense breast parenchyma measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm abuts the margin. The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast inferior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm piece of fibrofatty tissue which has a suture designating the new true margin. The new true margin is inked black and the specimen is serial sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma which is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast lateral" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a suture designating the true margin. The true margin is inked. The specimen is sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty tissue and is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: # 1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) HER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation: The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows: Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) Show strong (3+) over overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: # 2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals (139) to chromosome 17 signals (125) in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. Results at or near the cutoff point (ranging from REMOVED_DATE - 2.2) should be interpreted with caution. Addendum #2 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART : BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONBREAST (RIGHT, "POSTERIOR MARGIN"), 
