XAMINED. BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA, THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY (see note #2). BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS; MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED (see note #2). BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL LATERAL MARGIN), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA, THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY (see note #2). BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL DEEP MARGIN), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA; THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL ANTERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: SKIN, NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED. NOTE #2: The resection margins of the specimens were inked and microscopically evaluated. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled Mildred Flynn, #178-08-24, and "right breast biopsy with needle loc" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm unoriented tan-pink portion of fibrofatty tissue with a wire in place which is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm stellate firm gray-white lesion which abuts the inked margin. The specimen is submitted in its entirety in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to include the lesion in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received are 7 additional containers which are labeled Mildred E. Flynn, #178-08-24. Received fresh, labeled "right axillary lymph nodes", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm portion of tan-red fibrofatty tissue, which is sectioned to reveal firm tan-red areas possibly representing lymph nodes. These areas are entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast final medial", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm portion of tan-red fibrofatty tissue with a black stitch along 1 aspect. The stitched aspect is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal focal hemorrhage and dense gray-white fibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast final superior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm portion of gray-white to tan-red fibrofatty tissue with a black stitch along 1 aspect. The stitched aspect is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal hemorrhage and focally dense gray-white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities. The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast final lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm portion of focally hemorrhagic gray-white to tan-yellow fibrofatty tissue with a black stitch along 1 aspect. The stitch aspect is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal hemorrhage and focally dense gray-white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities. The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast final inferior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm portion of hemorrhagic fibrofatty tissue with a black stitch along 1 aspect. The stitched aspect is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities. The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Also received in the specimen container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm aggregate of hemorrhagic tan-red fibrofatty tissue with no orientation. The remaining tissue is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast final deep", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm portion of hemorrhagic tan-red fibrofatty tissue with no orientation. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue, and the specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast final anterior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm portion of tan-pink fibrofatty tissue partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm tan skin. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . 