nimal amount of tan-white rubbery fibrous tissue. No discrete lesions are identified. Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, "left breast", is an  REMOVED_CASE_ID  gm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5.5cm aggregate of red-yellow fibroadipose tissue fragments. Multiple fragments are partially surfaced by tan-pink grossly unremarkable wrinkled skin. The fragments are serially sectioned to reveal focally hemorrhagic yellow lobulated adipose tissue with minimal areas of tan-white rubbery fibrous tissue. No discrete lesions are identified. Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 11,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 08:09:39PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: #1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The ductal carcinoma in-situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The ductal carcinoma in-situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. See note. Note: Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: - The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) - Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) - Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) - The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test?s accuracy and precision. Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 15,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 10:54:48AM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Breast (Right), Mammoplasty PART B: Breast (Left), Mammoplasty [report_end] 
