ED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5.5cm mastectomy specimen, with a suture designating "6 o'clock", and multiple fragments of detached fibroadipose tissue, aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm  The overlaying REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm ellipse of skin appears unremarkable. The nipple and areola appear unremarkable. The anterior margin is inked blue, and the posterior margin is inked black. The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm area of multinodular, slightly firm, tan-yellow area, which extends to 2.0cm from the posterior margin, and 2.0cm from the anterior margin. There are additional scattered yellow, chalky and slightly firm areas in the entire breast. The surrounding tissue is yellow and fatty. Lymph nodes are not detected in the lateral tissue. The following representative sections are submitted:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Tan-yellow, and slightly firm area in superior breast at 12 o'clock.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin at 12 o'clock.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Outer lower quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inner lower quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inner upper quadrant, with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the posterior margin. Received fresh, labeled "right breast", is a 22 x 19 x 5.5cm mastectomy specimen, with a suture designating 12 o'clock. The overlaying REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm ellipse of skin appears unremarkable. The nipple and areola appear unremarkable. The anterior margin is inked blue, and the posterior margin is inked black. The specimen contains multiple tan-yellow, chalky and slightly firm areas throughout the breast parenchyma, with the largest 1 measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm  located in the superior breast at 12 o'clock. There are additional tan-white, irregular and slightly firm areas throughout the breast parenchyma, up to 1.5cm in greatest dimension. The surrounding tissue is yellow and fatty. Lymph nodes are not detected in the lateral tissue. The following representative sections are submitted:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Outer breast at 9 o'clock.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Outer upper quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior breast at 12 o'clock, with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the posterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inner upper quadrant at areas that are tan-white and slightly firm, with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the posterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inner lower quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central breast.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional representative sections. Received fresh, labeled "left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x 6.0cm tan-white skin ellipse, excised to a depth of 4.0cm  There is an 18.0cm well-healed linear scar on the skin surface. The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal focal tan-yellow, chalky to slightly firm areas adjacent to the deep resection margin. No masses are identified. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Deep margin, containing slightly firm areas.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin, with scar. Received fresh, labeled "right breast", are multiple fragments of tan-white skin ellipse, aggregating to 23 x 10.0cm  excised to a depth of 2.5cm  A 15.0cm well-healed linear scar is identified on 1 fragment. The specimen is sectioned to reveal focal tan-white, to yellow and slightly firm areas, with no definitive masses identified. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Focal tan-white, and slightly firm areas in fibroadipose tissue.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Skin, with scar. INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1; (RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA. Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M.D., on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 10,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02:05:15PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. Amendment #1 by Dennis Sgroi M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 17,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03:58:52PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Lymph Node (Right Axilla, "Sentinel"), Excision PART B: Breast (Left), Simple Mastectomy PART C: Breast (Right), Simple Mastectomy PART D: Skin (Left Breast), Excision PART E: Skin (Right Breast), Excision PART F: Cryostat Frozen Section (slide only) [report_end] 
