ct. The defect is entirely submitted in A-F. At the medial aspect of the specimen, adjacent to the anterior margin, 0.4cm from the lateral margin, 0.5cm from the medial margin, and 0.1cm from the posterior margin is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm irregular fibrotic area with adjacent focal hemorrhagic areas. This area is entirely submitted in G-J. The remainder of the parenchyma is grossly unremarkable. Also received in the same container, are two portions of fibroadipose tissue that are unoriented. The first measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm  It is inked black, serially sectioned to reveal a mostly fatty parenchyma with focal fibrotic areas. It is entirely submitted in K-N. The second unoriented fragment measuers REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  It is inked black, serially sectioned, and submitted entirely in O-P. The remainder of the main specimen is submitted in HH-TT. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "sentinel node hot and blue, left axilla  REMOVED_CASE_ID ", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm lymph node with attached adipose tissue. It is sectioned, and submitted entirely in Q-T with T being fat. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional lateral margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm portion of unoriented fibroadipose tissue. It is serially sectioned, and submitted entirely in U-X. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved superior half of cavity", are multiple fragments of unoriented fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm in aggregate. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in Y-CC. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved inferior half of cavity", are multiple fragments of unoriented fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm in aggregate. The specimen is sectioned, and submitted entirely in DD-GG. Resident: 