VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE: 05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON: 05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14:51 CLINICAL DATA: {None Provided} =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LET), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, GRADE 3, REMOVED_DATE CM, FOCALLY EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS AND TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN SEVERAL FOCI. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11:44 =============================================================================== *** RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. See note. Note: In this laboratory, we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way (paraffin sections) and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay. 91% of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay. 96% of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay. When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections, the predictive value of a positive result was 97% and the predictive value of a negative result was 95%. In this laboratory, we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay. Sixty-five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay, and 98% of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors. Added by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13:53 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast mass" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue, inked and sectioned to reveal a 1.4cm pink-tan, firm mass approaching the inked margin. A representative section is frozen as FX #1, now in cassette A. The remainder is submitted entirely in cassettes B through J. Resident: DANIELLE ELLIOTT, M.D. *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1, BREAST MASS, LEFT: INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA. O.R. Resident: HENRY DONG, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Eugene F. Ruffolo, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Charles Mason Ferguson, M.D. PART : LEFT BREAST EXCISIONAL BIOPSY \u000a[report_end] 
