gnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received are five containers, which are all labeled Doreen McMahon, #107-86-61. Received fresh, labeled "left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm left simple mastectomy specimen. There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm oval tan-white skin on the anterior aspect with a centrally located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm unremarkable nipple. The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black. Please note that the breast is unoriented. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an indurated, hemorrhagic central area (hemorrhagic area #1) measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm  The cut surface is dark red to tan-yellow. Area #1 is located 6.2cm from the posterior and 2.5cm from the anterior soft tissue margin. Located 8.0cm from area #1 is a REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm separate hemorrhagic area (#2), located 5.0cm from the posterior and 0.6cm from the anterior soft tissue. There is also an additional hemorrhagic area #3 located 1.5cm from the hemorrhagic area #1, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm  coming to 0.5cm from the anterior and 4.0cm from the posterior margin, respectively. Within the fibrotic rubbery dense parenchyma a well-delineated rubbery REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm nodule is identified, located 3.7cm from area #1, 0.5cm from the anterior soft tissue margin and 1.7cm from the posterior margin). No other obvious masses, lesions or biopsy sites are grossly appreciated. Multiple cystic structures measuring up to 0.7cm in thickness are identified exuding pasty tan-brown material and clear tan-brown fluid. At the periphery no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated. Representative sections are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire hemorrhagic area #1 with closest anterior and posterior resection margins taken radially.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire hemorrhagic area #2 with overlying anterior and posterior closest resection margins taken radially.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire hemorrhagic area #3 to closest anterior and posterior resection margins taken radially.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Well-delineated rubbery tan-white nodule with closest posterior and anterior margins taken radially.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of dense fibrous parenchyma sequentially submitted from one oriented aspect to the opposing. The specimen was re-examined and multiple additional tissue sections submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled "left sentinel node #1-227", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm lymph node with attached fat which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled "left breast sentinel node #2-55", is a rubbery REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm tan-pink lymph node. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled "right breast", is an unorientated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm right simple mastectomy specimen. On the anterior surface there is an oval REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm portion of skin with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm unremarkable nipple. No scar is grossly appreciated. The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a focally hemorrhagic solid to cystic area (area #1)with tan-yellow hemorrhagic material measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm and coming to 3.5cm from the posterior and 3.2cm from the anterior. Located 1.0cm from area #1 is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm additional hemorrhagic solid to cystic area (#2) coming to 4.5cm from the posterior margin and 3.2cm from the anterior margin, respectively. The remaining parenchyma consists of dense white fibrous parenchyma with multiple cystic structures averaging 0.3cm containing dark brown fluid. Along the periphery no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated. No obvious biopsy cavities are grossly identified. Representative sections are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire hemorrhagic area #1, submitted with overlying posterior margin taken radially.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire hemorrhagic area #2 with overlying posterior margin taken radially.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of fibrous parenchyma sequentially submitted from one aspect to the opposing. Received fresh, labeled "217 right sentinel node", are two rubbery tan-pink lymph nodes with attached fat measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  The smallest lymph node is submitted in toto in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the largest bivalved in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Amendment #1 by Kristina Braaten M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"227), EXCISION PART C: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"55), EXCISION PART D: BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART E: LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"217), EXCISION [report_end] 
