VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE: 03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON: 03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16:10 CLINICAL DATA: {None Provided} =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY: DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU IN THE REGION OF THE BIOPSY CAVITY. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA). HEALING BIOPSY SITE. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Invasion of the stroma, blood vessels and lymphatic vessels is not seen. The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor. LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLA): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 17 OF 17 LYMPH NODES. SEE NOTE. NOTE: The results of keratin staining of the lymph nodes will be reported in an addendum. LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLA, "HIGHEST"): UNREMARKABLE FAT. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08:29 =============================================================================== *** IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR KERATIN LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLA): The lymph nodes do not stain for keratin. Added by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14:35 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast," is a 275 g, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm unoriented right mastectomy specimen, which includes a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm right axillary tail, and which is partially covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm skin ellipse. The skin ellipse includes a central 2.5cm areola with nipple, as well as a 2.3cm in length curvilinear, well-healed scar, located 1.5cm medial to the nipple. The remainder of the skin is diffusely tan-white and otherwise unremarkable. The deep resection margin is a smooth plane. The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a prior REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm biopsy site, characterized by sulfur yellow discoloration, fibrosis, and old hemorrhage. The biopsy site is immediately subjacent to the epidermal scar, and approaches to within 0.8cm of the superior margin, 0.9cm of the deep inked margin, 1.5cm of the inferior margin, and is distant from the lateral and medial margins. The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of mature, lobular, yellow, adipose tissue, with intercollating, think, fibrous bands. The axillary tail is explored for lymph nodes; several lymph nodes are identified. Section Code: A: biopsy site, scar, and deep inked margin. B-C: biopsy site with deep inked margin and superior margin. D: biopsy site with inferior margin. E: random fibrous breast parenchyma. F: nipple. G-J: lymph nodes. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "higher axillary node," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm piece of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue, containing a lymph node. The specimen is submitted entirely in K. Resident: JAMES J. TIESINGA, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Charles Mason Ferguson, M.D. G. Gregory Gallico III, M.D. PART A: RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B: LYMPH NODE (HIGHEST RIGHT AXILLA) \u000a[report_end] 
