 PARENCHYMA, THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT "FINAL I"), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA, THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Diagnosis by: Dennis Sgroi, M.D. Signed On: 20 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 07:53 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast lumpectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.1cm yellow and tan fibrofatty soft tissue fragment penetrated by a localization needle. There is a long stitch marking the inferior aspect of the tissue. There is a short stitch marking the deep aspect of the tissue. The external surface shows no gross abnormalities. The specimen is inked according to protocol: superior - blue, inferior - black, medial - green, lateral - yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a 1 x 1 x 0.6cm  tan-white, ill-defined area with a hemorrhagic component which may represent the tract of the needle. The lesion abuts the lateral and inferior margin and is 0.7cm from the medial margin and 1cm from the superior margin. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A-J with the lesion in cassettes E-I with closest margins. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right axillary sentinel", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm lymph node with scant attached fibrofatty tissue. The specimen is sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes K-N. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right breast final anterior", are four unoriented, fibrofatty, tan-yellow, soft tissue fragments ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1.8cm in diameter and aggregating to 2 x 2 x 1.6cm  The specimens are submitted entirely in cassettes O-R. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast final superior", are two yellow-tan fibrofatty soft tissue fragments, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm  The black suture marking the new margin on each fragment. The new margin is inked black and the specimens are serially sectioned. One fragment is submitted entirely in cassettes S and T. The other fragment is submitted entirely in cassette U. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast final lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm tan-yellow, fibrofatty, soft tissue fragment. There is a suture marking the new margin. The new margin is inked black, the specimen is serially sectioned, and submitted entirely in cassette V. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast shaved margin, final medial", is a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm fibrofatty, yellow-tan, unremarkable soft tissue fragment. There is a suture marking the new margin. The new margin is inked black, the specimen is sectioned, and submitted entirely in cassette W-X. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast final deep", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  yellow-tan, unremarkable fibrofatty tissue fragment. There is a suture marking the new margin. The new margin is inked black, the specimen is sectioned, and submitted entirely in cassettes Y-Z. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final I", is a 5 x 2 x 0.7cm  unremarkable, yellow-tan, fibrofatty tissue fragment. There is a suture marking the new margin. The new margin is inked black, the specimen is serially sectioned, and submitted entirely in cassettes AA-DD. Resident: MINDY J. HULL, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: LYMPH NODE(RIGHT AXILLA,SENTINEL),EXCISION PART C: BREAST(RIGHT,FINAL ANTERIOR),EXCISION PART D: BREAST(RIGHT,FINAL SUPERIOR),EXCISION PART E: BREAST(RIGHT,FINAL LATER