l cysts up to 0.2cm in diameter. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes E, F, and G. Labeled "right medial", is a 78 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm fibroadipose tissue with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 4.4cm skin ellipse, and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm detached fragment of yellow fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable fatty adipose tissue. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes H through J. Labeled "left central", is a 140 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm yellow fatty fibroadipose tissue fragment. The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal grossly breast tissue. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes K through M. Labeled "left medial", is a 165 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5.0cm aggregate of fibroadipose tissue fragments. The largest of which is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm skin ellipse. The is inked and serially sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable fatty adipose tissue. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes N through P. Labeled "left lateral" is a 260 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7.0cm yellow fibroadipose tissue with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 7.0cm skin ellipse. The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal white fibrous breast tissue with focal cyst up to 0.5cm in diameter. Representative sections are submitted in Q through T. Resident: HOWARD CHANG, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Michael J Yaremchuk, M.D. PART A: RIGHT BREAST, CENTRAL, MAMMOPLASTY PART B: RIGHT BREAST, LATERAL, MAMMOPLASTY PART C: RIGHT BREAST, MEDIAL, MAMMOPLASTY PART D: LEFT BREAST, CENTRAL, MAMMOPLASTY PART E: LEFT BREAST, MEDIAL, MAMMOPLASTY PART F: LEFT BREAST, LATERAL, MAMMOPLASTY \u000a[report_end] 
