rea, medial to lateral, denoted by wire. I: Uninvolved parenchyma. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast inferior" are 2 fragments of unoriented fibrofatty tissue, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm each. The larger fragment is pierced by a needle localization wire. Both fragments are inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a parenchyma composed of 80% adipose and 20% fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions. Representative sections are submitted. J-L: Larger fragment, area denoted by needle localization wire. M: Smaller fragment. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast additional inferior" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm fragment of unoriented fibrofatty tissue, inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a parenchyma composed 50% of fibrous firm gritty and 50% adipose tissue. Representative sections are submitted as N-P. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast final specimen" are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm  representative sections are submitted as Q-S. Resident: SOHEIL DADRAS, MD, PHD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT SUPERIOR), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST (LEFT INFERIOR), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C: BREAST(LEFT INFERIOR),ADDITIONAL PART D: BREAST (LEFT FINAL SPECIMEN), EXCISION 
