DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.8cm biopsy cavity which is open and extends to within 1.0cm of the superior lateral resection margin and to within 1.0cm of the lateral resection margin. There is a fragment of unremarkable skeletal muscle on the lateral, deep aspect of this area; a suture designates the area involved previously by granular cell tumor. The biopsy cavity extends medially under the skin surface and into the breast tissue to within 4.0cm of the medial margin. The remaining breast parenchyma is scant, fibrous, white-pink septa running through unremarkable fibroadipose tissue. Section Code: A: nipple and areolar complex. B-E: representative radial sections of biopsy cavity with superior margin and skeletal muscle (area near long silk suture). F,G: representative radial sections of biopsy cavity with lateral margin. H-K: representative biopsy cavity. L-O: representative breast tissue. P-T: axillary lymph nodes. Resident: Mark vanGorder, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Susan E Briggs, M.D. Simon Kaspar Ashiku, M.D. PART : BREAST (LEFT) \u000a[report_end] 
