ds the axillary tail and inferior is an irregular stellate area approximating an inked margin as submitted in H. Examination of the axillary tail reveals seven possible lymph nodes ranging in dimension from 0.4cm to 2.0cm  These lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes I through M. Additional sections of breast parenchyma are submitted in N through Q. Resident: Jo-Ann E. Haney, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Herbert Charles Hoover Jr., M.D. Allan Enrique Pineda, M.D. PART : LEFT BREAST AND AXILLARY CONTENTS \u000a[report_end] 
