osis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received unfixed, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast mass" is a portion of fibrofatty tissue with a localization wire, a long suture designating lateral aspect, and a short suture designating the superior aspect. The specimen measures 2.8cm from medial to lateral, 1.8cm from superior to inferior, and 1.3cm from anterior to posterior. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior blue, posterior black, superior green, and inferior yellow. The tissue contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm white irregular firm area, containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm focally hemorrhagic cavity filled with fragments of white amorphous material. This firm area is less than 0.1cm from the posterior margin, less than 0.1cm from inferior margin, 1.0cm from the anterior margin, 0.8cm from the superior margin, 0.8cm from the lateral margin, and 0.5cm from the medial margin. The specimen is submitted in its entirety as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin (en face).  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections, from lateral to medial ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains white firm area and hemorrhagic biopsy cavity).  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin (en face). Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast margin medial" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm tan-yellow to white, hemorrhagic, irregular, portion of unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue with a suture designating the new margin. The side with the suture is inked, and the specimen is submitted in its entirety as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast margin superior" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm tan to yellow, lobulated, glistening, irregular, portion of unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue with a suture designating the new 