r aspect of the specimen. The long axis is medial to lateral and the specimen is inked as follows: anterior-blue, posterior-black, superior-green and inferior-yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the long axis from lateral to medial margins to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm diffusely hemorrhagic, indurated cavity surrounded by a focally hemorrhagic parenchyma. The cavity measures 1.1cm from the posterior margin, 2.0cm from the inferior margin, 1.2cm from the superior margin, 3.0cm from the lateral margin, 2.2cm from the medial margin and grossly appears to abut on to the anterior margin. The adjacent parenchyma consists of white to gray, firm, nodular and somewhat cystic fibrous material. The remaining parenchyma is uninvolved. Representative sections are submitted. Section Code:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : En face section of the lateral margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Hemorrhagic cavity with superior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Hemorrhagic cavity with posterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Hemorrhagic cavity with superior and posterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Parenchyma adjacent to cavity.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Parenchyma away from cavity.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : En face section of the medial margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining breast parenchyma. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "sentinel node left axillary #1," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm pink tan, ovoid possible lymph node, which is bisected and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and " sentinel node, left axillary #2," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm pink tan, ovoid possible lymph node, which is bisected and submitted entirely is cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION PART B: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL" #1), EXCISION PART C: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL" #2), EXCISION 
