r portion is inked blue and a specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm stellate, area of retraction, 0.4cm from the deep margin and 2.2cm from the skin. The remaining surface of the tan-pink, multinodular parenchyma displays moderate dense fibrous tissue, with approximately 80% of the specimen composed of fibrous tissue. No discrete masses are identified. The stellate areas is located towards the 12 o'clock portions of specimen. There is an additional REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm gray, slightly discolored stellate area of retraction, in the 6 o'clock portion of the specimen, 0.5cm from the deep margin. The surfaces surrounding this area are tan and rubbery, suggestive of previous biopsy site. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Described stellate area.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections, submitted sequentially from lateral to medial, with the second described stellate area in cassettes 6 and 7. Also received in the same container, separately from the main specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.8cm synthetic, round, material which contains clear, thick, tenacious material, consistent with silicone. The number "225", is along one aspect. Photographs are taken. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and " left breast", is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm simple mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm circular, tan skin, which displays a central os, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm everted nipple, with surrounding REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm unremarkable areola. There is a suture designated as 6 o'clock. The deep aspect of the specimen displays a REMOVED_DATE x 10.5cm ovoid, smooth, glistening area, consistent with a capsule. The deep margin is inked black, the anterior aspect is inked blue and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal dense, pink, multinodular fibrous surfaces, which comprise approximately 80% of the specimen. No 