tioned from lateral to medial revealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x approximately 0.3cm stellate area with central hemorrhage consistent with previous biopsy site. The remainder shows predominantly yellow adipose tissue admixed with scant (less than 5%) white fibrous tissue. More solid yellow areas are present. The tissue of the medial margin is solid and yellow. Representative sections submitted from medial to lateral. B-D: Medial margin. E-U: Representative cross sections medial to lateral. W: Lateral margins. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "medial border of left breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm portion of yellow-white fibroadipose tissue which is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette X. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left axillary contents" is an 11 x 4 x 3.5cm portion of adipose tissue containing several apparent lymph nodes. The lymphoid tissue is dissected away and entirely submitted. Y-Z: Together, one lymph node bisected. AA-BB: Each, one lymph node bisected. CC-GG: Lymph nodes and fat. Resident: STACEY L. MIKESELL, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1 (HIGH MEDIAL MARGIN): LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU. O.R. Resident: JEROME T. O'CONNELL JR., MD O.R. Diagnosis by: CHIN-LEE WU, MD, PhD O.R. Consulting Pathologist(s): EDI BROGI, MD, PhD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Michael Ned Margolies, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT HIGH MEDIAL MARGIN), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (LEFT), RE-EXCISION PART C: BREAST (LEFT MEDIAL BORDER), EXCISION PART D: LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLA), EXCISION \u000a[report_end] 
