VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery, WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist: None Frozen Section Resident: None Frozen Section Consultant(s): None Consulting Pathologist(s): None Assigned Resident/Path: Rema A Rao, M.D., B.S. Reports To: MICHELLE C SPECHT, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: ADH for excisional biopsy. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (RIGHT MEDIAL), EXCISION: 1. FOCAL SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS AND EXTENDING TO <0.1 CM FROM THE POSTERIOR MARGIN. 2. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. NOTE: Immunostains for calponin, smooth muscle myosin heavy chain, p63 and cytokeratin do not disclose evidence of invasive carcinoma. Multiple levels examined. BREAST (RIGHT INFERIOR LATERAL), EXCISION: 1. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). 2. FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA WITH CALCIFICATIONS. 3. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS. 4. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. BREAST (RIGHT SUPERIOR MEDIAL DEEP), EXCISION: HEALING BIOPSY SITE. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast biopsy with needle loc right medial", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm oriented fibrofatty breast tissue with the short stitch that designates the superior aspect and a long stitch designating the lateral aspect. There is a thin wire penetrating the tissue from the anterior to posterior aspect. The specimen is inked as follows: superior-blue, inferior-black, medial-green and lateral-yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal a tan-yellow fatty cut-surface, with a REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm tan-red area of hemorrhage that appears to abut the inferior margin and is located 0.4cm from the lateral margin, 1.4cm from the superior margin and 1.5cm from the medial margin. The rest of the cut surface appears unremarkable. Sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior end (radial section).  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior end (radial section).  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body of the specimen entirely (from anterior to posterior). Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast biopsy with needle loc inferior lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm fatty tissue, with the long stitch denoting the lateral aspect and the short stitch denoting the superior aspect. There is a needle wire that appears to penetrate the tissue from the posterior to the anterior aspect. The specimen is oriented and inked as follows: superior-blue, inferior-black, medial-green, and lateral-yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0.1cm tan-pink, firm gritty lesion that is located 0.1cm from the medial margin, 0.6cm from the inferior margin, 0.5cm from the superior margin and 1.1cm from the lateral margin. There are few areas of hemorrhage noted on the cut surface. The rest of the cut surface appears tan, pale-white to fatty. Specimens are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior end (radial section).  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior end (radial section).  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body of the specimen entirely from anterior to posterior. Please note section  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains the gritty lesion. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast biopsy superior medial deep", is a REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm unoriented breast tissue which is entirely inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a fatty cut surface with a REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm tan-pink gritty lesion that is located at the inked resection margin. Entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Gross Dictation by Rema A Rao M.D., B.S., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Rema A Rao M.D., B.S., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (RIGHT MEDIAL ), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (RIGHT INFERIOR LATERAL), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (RIGHT SUPERIOR MEDIAL DEEP), EXCISION 
