VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE: 07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON: 07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11:19 CLINICAL DATA: 44 year old woman with strong family history of breast cancer, status post reduction mammoplasty at MGH in REMOVED_DATE  revealing DCIS of right breast. Patient currently undergoing right modified radical mastectomy and prophylatic left mastectomy. Long stitch lateral. Short stitch superior. Double stitch axillary tail (low axillary node). =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY: 1. LOBULAR CARCINOMA-IN-SITU WITH PAGETOID SPREAD INCLUDING INVOLVEMENT OF LACTIFEROUS SINUSES, 4 MICROSCOPIC FOCI (BLOCKS S AND BB) (SEE NOTE). NOTE: The margins are free of lobular carcinoma-in-situ. 2. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES INCLUDING ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, FIBROSIS, CYST FORMATION, AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA. 3. BIOPSY SITE WITH FAT NECROSIS, CHRONIC INFLAMMATION, HEMOSIDERIN, AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION. 4. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 14 OF 14 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES. BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY WITH LIMITED LYMPH NODE DISSECTION: 1. BIOPSY CAVITY WITH FIBROSIS, FAT NECROSIS, CHRONIC INFLAMMATION, AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION. 2. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES INCLUDING FIBROSIS, MICROCYST FORMATION, AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS. 3. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 10 OF 10 LYMPH NODES. Diagnosis by: Elizabeth Bailey, MD Signed On: 17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08:23 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast" is a 635 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm left mastectomy specimen with a limited axillary tail, and covered only by a REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm nipple, and with stitches indicating orientation. Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an unremarkable fatty breast. No biopsy cavity grossly identified. No frozen done. Section Code: A-B: Left breast, medial aspect, representative sections. C-D: Left breast, superior aspect, representative sections. E-F: Left breast, inferior aspect, representative sections. G-H: Left breast, lateral aspect, representative sections. I-J: Left breast, nipple, representative sections. W: Left axillary lymph nodes. X-Y: Left breast, ? calcific area. Z: Left breast, mid, representative section. Labeled "right breast and axillary contents" is a 615 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm attached tail and covered only by a REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm nipple. The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal predominantly fatty cut surface with some prominent white fibrous streaks in the inferior and lateral portions of the breast. No biopsy cavity grossly identified. No regions grossly suspicious for carcinoma identified. Exploration of the axillary contents reveals eleven lymph nodes, with a greatest overall dimension of 1.9cm  Section Code: K: Right breast, representative section. L: Right breast, medial aspect, representative section M-N: Right breast, superior aspect, representative sections. O-P: Right breast, inferior aspect, representative sections. Q-R: Right breast, lateral aspect, representative sections. S-T: Right breast, nipple, representative section. U-V: Right axillary lymph nodes. AA-CC: Right breast. Resident: DARRYL E. PALMER-TOY, MD, PhD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** GROSS DIAGNOSIS: BREAST LEFT: NO LESIONS SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA. O.R. Resident: JAMES J. TIESINGA, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Austin L. Vickery, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. G. Gregory Gallico III, M.D. James Allen, M.D. PART A: RIGHT BREAST AND AXILLARY CONTENTS PART B: LEFT BREAST AND LIMITED AXILLARY CONTENTS \u000a[report_end] 
