 margin is inked yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm tan-red area consistent with previous biopsy site, which comes to 0.1cm of the anterior, 0.1cm of the medial, 1.0cm of the posterior, 1.9cm of the lateral, 0.7cm of the inferior, and >2cm of the superior margins of the specimen. The remaining cut surface displays focally dense gray-white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities. Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with the superior end (radially sectioned) as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , the inferior margin (en face) as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the entire biopsy cavity as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled "additional cephalad margin", is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm portion of gray-white to tan-red fibrofatty tissue. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm red-orange area consistent with previous biopsy site surrounded by chalky yellow discoloration consistent with fat necrosis. Also noted is focally dense gray-white fibrous tissue. No discrete lesion or other gross abnormality is identified. The specimen is entirely submitted  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: Breast (Right), Excision PART B: Breast (Right Additional Cephalad Margin), Excision [report_end] 
