ions of fibrous stroma G: Fibrous tissue to anterior H,I,K,L: Representative of fibrous tissue J,BB: Hard stellate area. Y-AA,CC-HH: Representative sections from the fibrous areas. M: Lymph nodes N: 1 trisected lymph node O-Q: Whole lymph nodes R-S: Whole lymph nodes T: Whole lymph nodes Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional axillary tissue left breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm aggregate of adipose tissue which contains multiple tan-red rubbery to tan-white firm fatty lymph nodes ranging from 0.2cm to 1.0cm in greatest dimension. Representative sections are entirely submitted as follows: U: Whole lymph nodes V: Whole lymph nodes W: Whole lymph nodes X: Bisected lymph node Gross Description by: LORI MARINI Resident: RESIDENT-FREE SERVICE (SMN) =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B: LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLA), EXCISION 
