VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE: 10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON: 10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12:48 CLINICAL DATA: Re-excision in a patient with a history of phyllodes tumor. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION: ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, FEW MICROSCOPIC FOCI. HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF PHYLLODES TUMOR. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16:39 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "Right breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.5cm breast re-excision specimen which includes a REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm skin ellipse with centrally located 2.0cm well-healed scar. The outer surface of the specimen is tan-pink, shaggy, and irregular. The surgeon has previously transected the eccentrically located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm biopsy cavity in area subjacent to the skin ellipse and also on the undersurface of the specimen. The outer surface of the specimen is inked black with one face yellow on black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an irregular rim of tan to yellow firm fibrotic parenchyma and a rim of fibrosis and fat necrosis which surrounds the biopsy cavity and extends to multiple inked resection margins. The biopsy cavity itself lies within 0.2cm of the closest inked resection margin. Section Code: A: ends. B: closest inked resection margin. C-F: representative sections around biopsy cavity. G-M: additional suspicious areas. Gross Description by: Timothy R. Quinn, MD Resident: EDI BROGI, MD, PhD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Susan E Briggs, M.D. PART : RIGHT BREAST MASS \u000a[report_end] 
