ock  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, SENTINEL # REMOVED_CASE_ID ), EXCISION: METASTATIC MAMMARY CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE (SEE TABLE #2). LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLA), DISSECTION: METASTATIC MAMMARY CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 11 LYMPH NODES (SEE TABLE #2). TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS #2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES (BOTH SPECIMENS) TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES: 2 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED: 12 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0.02cm or less (isolated tumor cells): 0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases >0.02cm to 0.2cm (micrometastases): 0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases >0.2cm (macrometastases): 2 (including a 1.9cm node replaced by tumor) Extracapsular extension: Present (slight) Other forms of axillary involvement: None By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled Janet Burns, #224-22-01, and "left breast biopsy", is a portion of fibrofatty tissue, with an inserted needle localization wire, with one suture designating medial and two sutures designating superior. There is an accompanying radiograph. The specimen measures 8.0cm from medial to lateral, 6.0cm from superior to inferior and 1.7cm from anterior to posterior. There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 2.3cm tan skin ellipse on the anterior / lateral aspect of the specimen, displaying diffuse blue dye, consistent with sentinel node dye. The specimen is inked anterior blue, posterior black, superior green, and inferior yellow and is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm irregular ill defined white-tan firm mass. This mass is 0.3cm from the anterior margin, 1.0cm from the posterior margin, 1.0cm from the inferior margin, 2.5cm from the superior margin, 1.8cm from the medial margin and 1.2cm from the lateral margin. There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm firm white area extending superiorly, in communication with the mass. This firm area is <0.1cm from the superior margin, 2.0cm from the inferior margin, 0.8cm from the posterior margin, 1.5cm from the anterior margin, 1.8cm from the medial margin and 1.3cm from the lateral margin. A vertical clip is identified within the first described mass. The remaining cut surface displays predominantly yellow lobulated adipose tissue with focal areas of white fibrous tissue with no additional masses or lesions identified. Representative sections are sequentially submitted from medial to lateral as follows: Section Code:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial end (en face).  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections from medial to lateral, with one bisected section in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with the entire mass in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with the entire firm area extending from the mass in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral end (en face).  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional sections of the margins. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled Janet Burns, #224-22-01, and "left axillary sentinel node biopsy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm portion of tan-pink fibrofatty tissue which is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm tan-pink lymph node. The lymph node is entirely submitted for frozen section as FX#1, now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled Janet Burns, #224-22-01 and "left axillary contents", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm aggregate of tan-yellow lobulated fibrofatty tissue. Upon dissection, multiple lymph nodes are identified, ranging from 0.1cm to 1.9cm in maximum dimension. The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Three lymph node candidates.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Five lymph node candidates.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Two lymph node candidates.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One bisected lymph node candidate.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One bisected lymph node candidate. INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION # 1; LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL # REMOVED_CASE_ID ), EXCISION: POSITIVE FOR METASTATIC CARCINOMA. Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: #1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein. Focally, the tumor cells show moderate (2+) overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) HER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation; the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows: Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) Show strong (3+) overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test?s accuracy and precision. Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART : BREAS