VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE: 09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON: 09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17:42 CLINICAL DATA: Left breast cancer, DCIS =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), MASTECTOMY: DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, HIGH GRADE, SPANNING AT LEAST 1 CM, IN THE REGION OF THE BIOPSY SITE. MUCOCOELE-LIKE LESIONS WITH MUCIN EXTRAVASATION IN THE STROMA HEALING BIOPSY SITE. SEBORRHEIC KERATOSIS. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Invasion of the stroma, blood vessels and lymphatic vessels is not seen. The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor. LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLA): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 10 OF 10 LYMPH NODES. LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLA, SEPARATELY SUBMITTED): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 14 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08:52 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Two specimens are received fresh, each labeled with the patient's name and unit number. Designated "left breast," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen, with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6.5cm skin ellipse containing an unremarkable nipple-areolar complex at the superior border. The posterior surface is inked black, the superior anterior surface blue, and the inferior anterior surface green. There are multiple flesh colored papules, ranging in size from 0.2cm up to 0.4cm in greatest dimension, scattered over the skin ellipse. In addition there is a 5.5cm curvilinear well healed scar, located 3.5cm inferior and lateral to the nipple-areolar complex. The scar on the skin ellipse is 0.9cm from the inferior border of the skin ellipse. Cross sectioning reveals no definite biopsy cavity. There is a large area, 7.0cm in largest dimension, area of dense white fibrous tissue with scattered yellow discolored areas and microcysts. This abnormal tissue averages 0.6cm from the deep margin. There is a 0.9cm in largest dimension firm tan-white nodule, located in the medial aspect of the tissue, 0.3cm from the inferior anterior margin, and 0.6cm from the deep margin. A representative section of this nodule is in A. Representative sections of fibrous and cystic areas are in B-G. Representative sections of tissue beneath the scar are in H-J. Representative sections of skin papules are in K. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm portion of axillary tail attached to the specimen, with an axillary node designated by a long stitch. The axillary tail is dissected for lymph nodes, which are submitted in L-P. Cassette N contains sections of a single node. Further representative sections of the breast tissue are in Q-S. Designated "left breast lymph node, additional axillary tissue," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm aggregate of fatty tissue, containing several soft lymph nodes. The lymph nodes are fully submitted in T. Resident: KRISTINA M. BRAATEN, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), MASTECTOMY PART B: LYMPH NODES, LEFT AXILLA \u000a[report_end] 
