rially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm tan, granular ovoid area of packing material, abutting the anterior margin, 0.4cm from the deep and inferior margins, 1.3cm from the lateral margin, and greater than 1.5cm from the remaining two margins. Within this area a clip is identified. The remaining cut surface consists of yellow, lobulated adipose tissue with minimal white fibrous tissue. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Radial sections to medial margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential sections from medial to lateral, with slices containing the clip in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Radial sections to lateral margin. Gross Dictation by Michael R Tan, on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Dennis Sgroi M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Christine Garcia M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The in-situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The in-situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Addendum by Atul K Bhan M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART : BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION 
