. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number,and "right breast 2 o'clock" are two portions of rubbery and partly yellow adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  The smaller specimen is submitted entirely in cassette K. The larger specimen is bivalved and submitted entirely in cassette L. Resident: HEIKE VARNHOLT, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST(RIGHT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST(RIGHT 2:00),EXCISION 
