d nodule as I-J. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast final deep", are 3 irregular portions of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue which aggregates to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm  No orientation is provided, the fragments are serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue and entirely submitted as K-L. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast final lateral", is an irregular REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm portion of gray-white to tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue with no orientation. One surface shows diffusely hemorrhagic dense gray-white fibrous tissue with yellow-orange areas consistent with fat necrosis. This aspect is inked blue, the alternate aspect black. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as M-N. Gross Description by: STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident: RESIDENT-FREE SERVICE (JHE) =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), RE-EXCISION PART B: BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL DEEP MARGIN) PART C: BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL LATERAL MARGIN) 
