VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery Unit MEEI MRN: REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-2 Results To: KEVIN S. HUGHES, M.D. Signed Out by: Ronald Balassanian, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: The patient is a 42 year old woman with calcifications in the right breast and a history of LCIS by core biopsy. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: A. BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION 1. EXTENSIVE INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMATOSIS WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS. 2. EXTENSIVE FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. 3. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH APOCRINE METAPLASIA, SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS. 4. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. See note. Note: Sections reveal extensive intraductal papillomatosis which is focally distorted and fragmented by scarring and granulation tissue from the healing biopsy site. The areas of papillomatosis extend to the margin of resection in multiple foci. In addition, the papillomatosis is confluent with areas of usual ductal hyperplasia and fibrocystic change. A panel of immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin, p63, myosin and calponin were performed on slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The immunostaining pattern highlights the myoepithelial layer and supports the diagnosis. An immunohistochemical stain for e-cadherin performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is positive in ductal cells and does not show evidence of lobular carcinoma in-situ. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh labeled Maryann Radley, #257-45-78 only, is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.6cm yellow-tan fragment of fibroadipose tissue, received with a needle localization wire in place and accompanied by a radiograph. The specimen is received with a long suture denoting the lateral aspect, a short suture denoting the anterior aspect, and a bowtie suture denoting the cephalad aspect. Specimen is inked for orientation as follows: Anterior blue, posterior black, superior green and inferior yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal yellow lobulate adipose tissue with scant areas of dense white tan focally nodular rubbery fibrous tissue throughout with multiple cystic structures throughout. The specimen is entirely submitted sequentially from lateral to medial as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral end, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial end, en face. Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday August 20,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01:16:20PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART : Breast (Right), Excision [report_end] 
