VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-3 Results To: KEVIN S. HUGHES, M.D. Signed Out by: David C Wilbur, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: Right breast biopsy. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION: FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA IN THE BACKGROUND OF FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES SHOWING MULTIPLE FOCI OF FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA. NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. NOTE: Foci of atypical ductal hyperplasia are present less than 0.1cm from the inferior, superior, and lateral margins. BREAST (RIGHT SUPERFICIAL), EXCISION: FOCUS OF ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA WITHIN A COMPLEX SCLEROSING LESION. BACKGROUND OF FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FOCI OF FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA AND INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA. NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. NOTE: The focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia is present 0.2cm from an inked margin, but due to lack of specimen orientation, if cannot be determined if this represents a true resection margin. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received are 2 containers which are labeled Mary H. Cucchiara, #289-14-80. Received fresh, labeled "right breast biopsy with needle localization", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.8cm portion of tan-red fibrofatty tissue, with a localization wire in place. A short stitch designates the anterior margin, a bowtie stitch designates the superior margin, and a long stitch designates the lateral margin. There is a REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm disrupted defect, which communicates with the anterior margin. The inferior margin is inked black, the superior blue, the medial green, and the lateral yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal a poorly delineated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm central hemorrhagic area, with associated fat necrosis, consistent with previous biopsy site. Within this region, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm firm nodule, which comes to 0.6cm of the superior margin, 1.0cm of the inferior margin, 0.8cm of the lateral margin, 1.5cm of the medial margin, and >2cm of the anterior and posterior margins. Within this nodule is a silver metal clip. No other gross abnormalities are identified, and the specimen is entirely submitted from anterior to posterior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with the anterior margin, en face, as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , the posterior margin, en face, as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the entire firm nodule as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled "superficial tissue", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm portion of tan-red fibrofatty tissue, with no orientation. The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal diffuse hemorrhage, with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm hemorrhagic cavity, surrounded by chalky yellow discoloration, consistent with fat necrosis. This area is firm, with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm indurated, gray-white nodule at 1 end, which abuts the ink. The specimen is entirely submitted, with the ends, en face, as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the body as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The indurated nodule is in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by David C Wilbur M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 09,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03:42:36PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Breast (Right), Excision PART B: Breast (Right Superficial), Excision [report_end] 
