VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Updated Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-2 Results To: BARBARA LYNN SMITH, M.D. Frozen Section Pathologist: Maylee Hsu, M.D. Frozen Section Resident: Veronica Klepeis, M.D., Ph.D. Signed Out by: Melinda J Lerwill, M.D. ********** Addended Report *********** Reason for Addendum #1: Additional Tissue Processed CLINICAL DATA: Right breast CA, 2 abnormal areas mammo: IDC (superior) and flat atypia (inferior). FINAL DIAGNOSIS: LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLA, SENTINEL), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 LYMPH NODES (0/2). NOTE: Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin on three tissue levels per block support the above interpretation. BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION: 1. FOCAL FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA AND ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. 2. FOCAL LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA). 3. HEALING BIOPSY SITES. 4. RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED. NOTE: The remainder of the inferior biopsy site will be submitted and results reported in an addendum. BREAST (RIGHT, DEEP FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, INFERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, SUPERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA CANNOT BE ENTIRELY EXCLUDED, SEE NOTE. NOTE: Thermal artifact limits evaluation. BREAST (RIGHT, MEDIAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: FOCUS SUGGESTIVE OF LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU), SEE NOTE. NOTE: Thermal artifact limits evaluation. BREAST (RIGHT, LATERAL FINAL MARGIN), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab labeled Frances Connors, #242-40-78 and "right axillary sentinel node", are 2 fibrofatty soft tissue fragments measuring 3 x 3 x 1cm and 2 x 2 x 0.5cm  One is bisected and frozen entirely as FX #1, now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The 2nd is frozen as FX #1A, now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled Frances Connors, #242-40-78, and "right breast lump", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.2cm irregular portion of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue, which has been previously inked blue at the anterior aspect. The specimen has a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral. The specimen is received with 2 needle localization wires in place and a specimen radiograph. The specimen is inked as follows: Anterior - blue, posterior - black, medial - green, lateral - yellow and serially sectioned from superior to inferior. Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm firm, gray-yellow cavity, which contains spongy tan-pink material, which extends to within 0.4cm of the medial, 2.3cm of the lateral, 2.1cm of the anterior, and 2.0cm of the posterior margin. The nodule measures >3cm from both the superior and inferior margins. Identified approximately 2cm inferior to the main lesion is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm cavity, which extends to within 0.5cm of the anterior, 3.8cm of the posterior, 1.6cm of the lateral, 1.5cm of the medial, >5cm of the superior and >2.5cm from the inferior margin. The remainder of the cut surface consists of lobulated tan-yellow fat with a moderate amount of interspersed gray-white fibrous tissue and focal areas of hemorrhage. No other masses or lesions are grossly identified. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior end, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior end, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire larger cavity (superior), with section containing clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of fibrous tissue between the 2 lesions.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of the smaller inferior lesion (majority of lesion submitted).  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of fibrous tissue away from 2 lesions. Received are 5 containers, which are all labeled Frances Connors, #242-40-78. Received in formalin, labeled "right breast deep final shaved margin", are multiple unoriented fragments of fibroadipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm  sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast inferior final shaved margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue, which is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast superior final shaved margin", are 2 unoriented fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm  serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast medial final shaved margin", are multiple unoriented fragments of fibroadipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm  serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast lateral final shaved margin", are 3 unoriented fragments of fibroadipose tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm  serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1 & #1A; (RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN REMOVED_DATE LYMPH NODES. Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on Friday February 06,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06:08:10PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: Remainder of inferior biopsy site from main lumpectomy specimen The remainder of the inferior biopsy site is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; these sections do not reveal evidence of carcinoma. The above diagnosis remains unchanged. Addendum #1 by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday February 12,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06:00:52PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Lymph Node (Right Axilla, "Sentinel"), Excision PART B: Breast (Right), Excision PART C: Breast (Right,Deep Final shaved margin), Excision PART D: Breast (Right, Inferior Final shaved margin), Excision PART E: Breast (Right, Superior Final shaved margin), Excision PART F: Breast (Right, Medial [report_end] 
