VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery Unit MEEI MRN: REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-1 Results To: KEVIN S. HUGHES, M.D. Resident: Christopher K Hysell, M.D. Signed Out by: Elena F Brachtel, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: Complex cystic mass in right breast. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION: 1. ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, FOCALLY SEVERE, WITH CALCIFICATIONS. (SEE NOTE). 2. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH NUMEROUS CYSTS, SOME RPTURED, APOCRINE METAPLASIA AND DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA (USUAL TYPE). 3. SCLEROSING ADENOSIS WITH SCATTERED CALCIFICATIONS. NOTE: Atypical ductal hyperplasia cells are negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /6 by immunostain, while usual ductal hyperplasia cells are positive. Two foci of severe atypical ductal hyperplasia span about 0.15cm each and are away from the margins ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 16). Another small focus of severe atypical ductal hyperplasia is less than 0.1cm from the posterior margin, but disappears on deeper tissue sections; multiple levels examined ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). BREAST (RIGHT, ADDITIONAL MARGIN), EXCISION: 1. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH NUMEROUS CYSTS, SOME RUPTURED, APOCRINE METAPLASIA. 2. SCLEROSING ADENOSIS WITH SCATTERED CALCIFICATIONS. (SEE NOTE). 3. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA) NOTE: Lobular neoplasia cells are negative for E-cadherin. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received are two containers which are all labeled Luz Morales, #242-48-18. Received in formalin, labeled "right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.2cm excisional breast specimen. The surgeon orients the specimen by denoting the lateral aspect with a long stitch, the superior aspect with a bowtie, and the anterior margin with a short stitch. The specimen?s long axis is in the medial to lateral direction. The specimen is inked as follows: posterior-black, anterior-blue, superior-green, inferior-yellow. Sectioning reveals multiple cysts, individually measuring REMOVED_DATE to 0.7cm in greatest dimension and most concentrated near the medial aspect of the specimen. The parenchyma also shows white fibrous areas and a focal area which is darker yellow in color which is 0.6cm in greatest dimension. No solid masses are noted. The specimen is submitted entirely as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : En face lateral margin submitted in two cassettes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : En face medial resection margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Section between medial margin and beginning of cystification.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sections of greatest cystification with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing cyst and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the corresponding margins.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Continued representative sampling approaching lateral margin. Included in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is the described yellow discoloration. Received in formalin, labeled "additional lateral margin", is an unoriented fatty specimen which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm  Section reveals tan-yellow spongy tissue with focal cysts up to 0.2cm in greatest dimension. No solid masses are noted. The outer surface is inked black and the specimen is entirely sequentially submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART : BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONBREAST (RIGHT, ADDITIONAL MARGIN), E 
