rgin of the specimen is inked blue, the posterior margin black, the superior margin green, and the inferior margin yellow. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm ill-defined, slightly firm, gray-white nodule, which extends to within 0.5cm of the anterior margin, 2.1cm of the inferior margin, 2.1cm of the superior margin, >2.5cm of both the medial and lateral margins and abuts the posterior margin. There is a clip identified within the nodule #1. The surrounding tissue appears gray-white to tan-yellow and fibrofatty. There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm separately received portion of nodular gray-white fibroadipose tissue, which is sectioned to reveal a metallic clip #2. The following representative sections are submitted:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral end, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body of specimen, submitted sequentially from lateral to medial, with the lesion entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the sectioning containing the clip #1 in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial end, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire separately received portion of tissue containing clip #2. Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 21,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06:06:17PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART : Breast (Right), Excision [report_end] 
