IN. NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. BREAST (LEFT, ANTERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. BREAST (LEFT, LATERAL MARGIN), EXCISION: ISOLATED FOCUS OF INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITHIN HEALING BIOPSY SITE. CARCINOMA IS >0.2 CM FROM THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN. NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. BREAST (LEFT, INFERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: UNREMARKABLE BREAST PARENCHYMA. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. BREAST (LEFT, MEDIAL MARGIN), EXCISION: UNREMARKABLE BREAST PARENCHYMA. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. BREAST (LEFT, SUPERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: UNREMARKABLE BREAST PARENCHYMA. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. LYMPH NODE (NON-SENTINEL LEFT AXILLA), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE (0/1). GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled Leticia Sanchez, #253-21-12 and "left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm excision specimen with a needle localization wire in place and accompanied by a radiograph. The specimen is unoriented, and is inked entirely black. The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm firm, tan-gray lesion which is <0.1cm from the closest black inked margin. No metal clip is identified. The specimen is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with the firm lesion in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received are 10 containers, which are all labeled Leticia Sanchez, #253-21-12. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled patient's name and unit # and "left axillary sentinel node" are 2 lymph node candidates measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm  The lymph node candidates are bivalved and entirely frozen as FX #1 and FX #1A, respectively, now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast additional lumpectomy", are 2 unoriented yellow lobulated fibroadipose fragments, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  Both fragments are inked black, serially sectioned and submitted in toto in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "deep margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a suture designating the final margin. This aspect is inked black, the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "anterior margin", are 2 yellow lobulated fibroadipose fragments measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  Each fragment bears a suture designating the final margin. The surfaces are inked black, the specimens are serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "lateral margin", are 2 yellow lobulated fibroadipose fragments measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  Each fragment bears a suture designating the final margin. The surfaces are inked black, the specimens are serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "inferior margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue, with a suture designating the final margin. The surface is inked black, the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "medial margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm fibrofatty soft tissue, with a suture designating the final margin. The surface is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "superior margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch designating the final margin. The stitch is inked black, the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "non-sentinel node, left axilla", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm tan-pink soft tissue, which is bisected and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1; (LEFT SENTINEL NODE, SMALLER): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1A; (LEFT SENTINEL NODE, LARGER): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Final Diagnosis by David C Wilbur M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 01,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11:51:14AM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Breast (Left), Excision PART B: Lymph Node (Left Axilla, "Sentinel"), Excision PART C: Breast (Left Additional), Excision PART D: Breast (Left,Deep Margin), Excision PART E: Breast (Left,Anterior Margin), Excision PART F: Breast (Left,Lateral Margin), Excision PART G: Breast (Left,Inferior Margin), Exc [report_end] 
