ulated mass, measuring 0.7cm from the superior margin, 1.5cm from the inferior margin, 0.4cm from the posterior margin, 0.4cm from the lateral margin, 0.7cm from the anterior margin, and 0.8cm from the medial margin. A small metal pigtail clip and a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm hemorrhagic cavity are present directly adjacent to the previously described mass, measuring 0.7cm from the superior margin, 1.2cm from the inferior margin, 0.2cm from the lateral margin, abutting the posterior margin, 0.9cm from the medial margin and 2.0cm from the anterior margin. The remainder breast parenchyma is predominantly fatty with few fibrous streaks. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior end margin, radial.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior end margin, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire mass with closest margins with clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Uninvolved parenchyma. Received in formalin, labeled "right breast additional lumpectomy", are 3 unoriented portions of pink and yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm  2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable adipose tissue with no masses or lesions identified. The specimen is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with 1 fragment in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 1 fragment in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the largest fragment in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast final superior", are 2 oriented portions of yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm and 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm with stitches on one aspect indicating the new margins which are now inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with the smaller fragment in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the larger fragment in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast inferior", is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1.2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one aspect indicating the new margin which is now inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast final medial", is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one aspect indicating the new margin which is now inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  &  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast final lateral", are 2 oriented portions of yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm and 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm with stitches on one aspect indicating the new margins which are now inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with the smaller fragment in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the larger fragment in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast final deep", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm portion of yellow fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one aspect indicating the new margin which is now inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast final anterior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm portion of yellow fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one aspect indicating the new margin which is now inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1 & #1 DEEP; (RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Fellow Review by Ritu Ghai M.D., on Tuesday August 11,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02:06:46PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday August 12,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02:13:31PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: #1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. Focally, the tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: - The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) - Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) - Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) - The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) HER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation; the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows: - Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) - Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) - Show strong (3+) overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 30% of tumor cells) These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test?s accuracy and precision. Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday August 12,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03:25:15PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON #2: RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals (102) to chromosome 17 signals (101) in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. The results at or near the cutoff point (ranging from REMOVED_DATE - 2.2) should be interpreted with caution (Equivocal Amplification). Reference: Journal of Clinical Oncology 25:118-145,  REMOVED_CASE_ID . Addendum #2 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on Friday August 14,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01:08:21PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Lymph Node (Right Axilla, "Sentinel" REMOVED_CASE_ID ), Excision PART B: Breast (Right), Excision PART C: Breast ( Additional Right), Excision PART D: Breast (Right, Superior Final Margin), Excision PART E: Breast (Right, Inferior Final Margin), Excision PART F: Breast (Right, Medial Final Margin), Excision [report_end] 
