in, 0.6cm from the posterior margin, 1.2cm from the superior margin, and greater than 2.0cm from the inferior margin. The remaining breast parenchyma consists of unremarkable white-yellow fibroadipose tissue with diffuse hemorrhage. The specimen is submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior resection margin, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior resection margin, radially.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lesion, entirely.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Grossly uninvolved breast, inferior to the lesion. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and " right breast excision", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm excision specimen with a needle localization wire, a short suture denoting the superior surface, and a long suture denoting the lateral surface. The long axis is from anterior to posterior. The specimen is inked as follows: superior-green, lateral-blue, medial-black, inferior-yellow. The specimen is sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal a poorly circumscribed firm, stellate white-gray mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.9cm  The central portion of this lesion contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm firm tan-yellow gritty area. The lesion has a hemorrhagic periphery. This mass abuts the superior, lateral, medial, and inferior margins and is 0.4cm from the anterior margin and 0.6cm from the posterior margin. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, radially .  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior resection margin, radially.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of mass, with firm areas in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Grossly uninvolved breast posterior to lesion. Gross Dictation by Joshua Kish M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Joshua Kish M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (RIGHT), EX