ly submitted (see section code). A representative section of the nipple is submitted (see section code). Representative sections of the indurated white areas of the breast parenchyma are submitted (see section code). Section Code: C: Nipple D-F: Indurated areas G-H: Lymph nodes I-O: Indurated areas Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast" is a 16 x 10 x 5cm mastectomy specimen. It is covered by an ellipse of skin which measures 13 x 5cm  The nipple and areola are grossly unremarkable. A representative section of the nipple is submitted (see section code). Four surgical sutures are in place on the medial aspect of the areola, possibly designated a previous biopsy site. The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal a 0.2cm firm, white nodule which is 1cm from the deep margin, grossly suspicious for tumor. A representative section is frozen as FX #2, now in cassette P. The rest of the breast is similar to the changes describe in the left breast. Representative sections of the indurated areas are submitted (see section code). Additional sections from the firm area (frozen section) are submitted in cassette V. Further random sections are submitted(see section code). The axillary portion of the specimen is dissected and multiple lymph nodes are identified which are entirely submitted (see section code). Section Code: P: Frozen section #2 Q-U: Representative indurated areas V: Firm nodule W-X: Additional sections Y-Z: Lymph nodes ZZ: Nipple. Resident: JEROME T. O'CONNELL JR., MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1: BREAST (RIGHT, NODULE), EXCISION: FLORID INTRADUCTAL PROLIFERATION, FAVOR BENIGN; NO STROMAL INVASION IDENTIFIED. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #2: BREAST (RIGHT): SCLEROSING PAPILLOMA, THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. GROSS DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), MODIFIED RADICAL MASTATECTOMY: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. NO INVASIVE TUMOR IS SEEN ON GROSS EXAMINATION. O.R. Resident: SAMANTHA J. PULLIAM, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: John H. Eichhorn, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B: BREAST (LEFT) and LYMPH NODE (AXILLA) PART C: BREAST ("RIGHT NODULE") \u000a[report_end] 
