L" #950), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE (0/1) . (SEE NOTE). NOTE: Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the above interpretation. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL" #23), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE (0/1). (SEE NOTE). NOTE: Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the above interpretation. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL" #53), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE (0/1) . (SEE NOTE). NOTE: Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the above interpretation. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL" #281), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE (0/1) . (SEE NOTE). NOTE: Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the above interpretation. NOTE: This report is amended with a clarified specimen designation (two specimens had been originally accessioned as "left breast excision" only, without detailed designation). The change was discussed with Dr. K. Hughes by phone REMOVED_DATE  The remainder of the report is unchanged. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received are 7 containers, which are all labeled Eileen Ballard Sarcone, #261-27-68. Received fresh and labeled "left breast partial mastectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue containing a needle localization wire. The specimen is oriented by a single stitch designating the anterior margin, a long stitch designating the lateral margin, and a bowtie stitch designating the cephalad margin. The long axis of the specimen is anterior to posterior. The lateral surface of the specimen is partially disrupted and re-approximated prior to inking. The specimen is inked as follows: Superior - blue, inferior - black, medial - green, lateral - yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the long axis to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm firm and fibrous, stellate tan-white region with a pink center, located 1.5cm from the superior margin, 0.2cm from the inferior margin, 0.2cm from the medial margin, 0.3cm from the lateral margin, 2.2cm from the posterior margin, and 1.2cm from the anterior margin. Also present is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm focally nodular and partially cystic area within the posterior region of the specimen. The specimen is entirely submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Firm, stellate mass, including medial, lateral and inferior margin, entirely submitted, with region of clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  section bisected.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of focally nodular and partially cystic area near posterior region.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional sections.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of specimen. Received fresh and labeled "left breast biopsy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.8cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with 2 needle localization wires in place. The specimen is oriented by a single short stitch designating the anterior margin, a long stitch designating the lateral margin, and a bowtie stitch designating the cephalad margin. The long axis of the specimen is superior to inferior. The specimen is inked as follows: Anterior - blue, posterior - black, medial - green, lateral - yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm well-defined, firm, white lesion (lesion #1), located <0.1cm from the lateral margin, <0.1cm from the anterior margin, 0.8cm from the posterior margin, 0.7cm from the medial margin, 0.8cm from the