VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: WACC 2 Frozen Section Pathologist: None Frozen Section Resident: None Frozen Section Consultant(s): None Consulting Pathologist(s): None Assigned Resident/Path: Aleksandr Vasilyev, M.D. Reports To: MICHELE ANNETTE GADD, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: Core biopsy - FEL (low grade phyllodes versus cellular fibroadenoma). FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION: ATYPICAL FIBROEPITHELIAL NEOPLASM, SUSPICIOUS FOR LOW-GRADE PHYLLODES TUMOR (0.7 CM); ALL RESECTION MARGINS NEGATIVE (SURGICAL CLEARANCE FOCALLY < REMOVED_DATE CM) (SEE NOTE). ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, SCATTERED FOCI, FOCALLY ASSOCIATED WITH CALCIFICATION. PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES, INCLUDING SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. NOTE: The fibroepithelial lesion has increased periglandular specialized stromal cellularity, stromal atypia, and stromal mitotic activity (1-2 mitosis per 10 hpf), compared to a fibroadenoma. In addition, the glands in the lesion are dilated and show ductal hyperplasia. The tumor is largely well-circumscribed, with only a focal area suggestive of slight infiltration. These features are suspicious for a low-grade phyllodes tumor. However, in the absence of significant stromal expansion, frond-like architecture, or gland to stromal architectural heterogeneity, the features are felt to be insufficient for an unequivocal diagnosis of phyllodes tumor. This lesion may have some potential for recurrence and follow-up is recommended. Case reviewed in consultation with Dr. Koerner. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF NEOPLASIA. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast lump", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.9cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue which is unoriented. The external surface is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a diffusely fibrous tissue with small pinpoint areas of focal hemorrhage. The specimen is submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , along the long axis. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast final shaved margin", are multiple fragments of fibrofatty tissue, aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm  which are submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (LEFT, SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION 
