-circumscribed tan-white to pink gelatinous firm tumor, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 8.5cm  with focal areas of hemorrhage, polypoid projections, and blood-filled cysts (0.2 to 0.5cm in greatest dimension). The tumor comes to 2.0cm of the posterior margin and 3.2cm of anterior margin. The skin and posterior skeletal muscle are grossly uninvolved by the tumor. Axillary lymph nodes are not identified along the edge of the specimen. The remaining breast parenchyma is largely fatty and grossly uninvolved by the tumor. A-B: Tumor to posterior margin with the closest approach in cassette A. C: The closest anterior margin (radial section). D: Tumor to skin surface. E: The closest posterior skeletal muscle (radial section). F-G: Representative sections of the cystic areas of the tumor. H-L: Representative sections of the polypoid areas of the tumor. M-N: Representative sections of the gelatinous areas of the tumor. O: A representative section of the hemorrhagic areas of the tumor. P-R: Representative sections of the solid areas of the tumor. S-T: Tumor to surrounding fatty tissue. U-V: Two additional representative sections of the largely fatty uninvolved breast parenchyma. W: The 0.5cm skin papule, bisected. X: The 0.7cm skin papule, bisected. Y: The 1.5cm skin papule, bisected. Resident: TAI-YUAN LIN, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Kevin S. Hughes, M.D. PART : BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY 
