ting lateral. The specimen is received with a needle localization wire in place, and accompanied by a specimen radiograph. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior - blue, posterior - black, superior - green, inferior - yellow, and serially sectioned from medial to lateral. Sectioning reveals a lobulated, tan-yellow, fatty cut surface. The specimen is entirely submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial end, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body of specimen.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral end, en face. Received fresh, labeled "left breast biopsy", is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm  irregular portion of tan-yellow, fibroadipose tissue with a short stitch designating superior, a long stitch designating lateral and a needle localization wire in place. The specimen is received with a specimen radiograph. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior - blue, posterior - black, superior - green, inferior - yellow, and is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a lobulated, tan-yellow, fatty cut surface with interspersed areas of hemorrhage and fibrous tissue. No discrete masses or lesions are identified. The specimen is submitted entirely as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial end, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body of specimen submitted partially from medial to lateral.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral end, en face. Fellow Review by Ritu Ghai M.D., on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 11,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05:32:21PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M.D., Electronically signed on Saturday REMOVED_MONTH 12,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01:07:34PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Breast (Right),