ral with medial end margin radially in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , lateral end margin radially in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and lesion entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled "left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue oriented with a long stitch lateral and a short stitch superior. There is a needle localization wire in the same container but separate from the specimen. The long axis is medial to lateral, and the specimen is inked as follows: Superior - blue, inferior - black, anterior - green, posterior - yellow. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm prior biopsy cavity present at the superior posterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral, no lesions are grossly identified. The specimen is submitted entirely from medial to lateral with medial end margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , radially and lateral end margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , radially. Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: Breast (Right), Excision PART B: Breast (Left), Excision [report_end] 
