VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: UpdatedType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-04- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-04- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery, WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist: None Frozen Section Resident: None Frozen Section Consultant(s): None Consulting Pathologist(s): None Assigned Resident/Path: Pavan K Auluck, M.D., Ph.D. Reports To: MICHELE ANNETTE GADD, M.D. ********** Addended Report *********** Reason for Addendum #1: Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA: History of DCIS and recent diagnosis of invasive ductal carcinoma. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION: INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA. SEE TABLE #1. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU. SEE TABLE #1. ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS # 1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm (gross measurement) Grade: 1 Lymphatic vessel invasion: Not identified. Blood vessel invasion: Not identified. Margin of invasive carcinoma: Positive focally at the lateral and superior margins of the specimen. Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0.1cm from the lateral-posterior and anterior margins of the specimen focally. Location of ductal carcinoma in-situ: Within the region of the carcinoma. Grade of ductal carcinoma in-situ: 1 Margin of ductal carcinoma in-situ: Positive focally at the superior margin of the specimen. Ductal carcinoma in-situ also extends to less than 0.1cm from the lateral margin of the specimen focally and to 1mm from the anterior margin focally. Stains for receptors: Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . BREAST (LEFT MEDIAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, LATERAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: SMALL FOCUS OF ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. BREAST (LEFT SUPERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: 1. INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION, WHICH MEASURES SLIGHTLY LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM TO THE DESIGNATED "NEW" MARGIN. 2. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, ONE FOCUS (<1MM), WITHIN THE REGION OF THE INVASIVE CARCINOMA, WHICH IS >0.2CM FROM THE DESIGNATED "NEW" MARGIN. BREAST (LEFT, INFERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: SMALL FOCUS OF INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION, WHICH IS >0.2 CM FROM THE DESIGNATED "NEW" MARGIN. MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED. BREAST (LEFT, DEEP FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE. NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.4cm breast excision specimen with a short stitch marking superior aspect and a long stitch marking its lateral aspect. There is a needle localization wire entering the specimen on its anterior side which is marking an area of radiographic density. The long axis of the specimen is superior-inferior. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior=blue, posterior=black, medial=green, lateral = yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to its long axis to reveal a white stellate fibrous area in the vicinity of the needle localization wire. This stellate area measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm and comes to within 0.5cm of the posterior margin, 0.4cm of the anterior margin, 0.7cm of the medial margin, and 0.3cm of the lateral margin. Photographs are taken of this area. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Stellate area to nearest anterior/posterior/medial and lateral margins.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin of the specimen.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin of the specimen. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left axillary sentinel node" is a yellow-red REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a previously bivalved tan-gray REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x0.5cm lymph node at one end. It is entirely frozen as FX#1, now  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "medial" is a piece of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm with a single stitch marking the new margin. The new margin is inked black, serially sectioned and submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "lateral" are two fragments of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm respectively. Each piece of tissue has single stitch demarcating the new margin which is inked black. The specimens are serially sectioned and submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "superior" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a single stitch demarcating the new margin. The new margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "inferior" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a single stitch demarcating the new margin. The new margin is inked black, and the opposite surface is inked blue (because the stitch is loosely attached). The specimen is serially sectioned, submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "deep" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a single stitch demarcating the new margin. The new margin is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned and is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1: (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINAL NODE): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Gross Dictation by Pavan K Auluck M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Pavan K Auluck M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. In some areas, the tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Addendum by Atul K Bhan M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION PART B: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (LEFT,MEDIAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION PART D: BREAST (LEFT,LATERAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION PART E: BREAST (LEFT,SUPERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION PART F: BREAST (LEFT,INFERIOR FINAL 
