VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist: None Frozen Section Resident: None Frozen Section Consultant(s): None Consulting Pathologist(s): None Assigned Resident/Path: Melinda J Lerwill, M.D. Reports To: MICHELE ANNETTE GADD, M.D. JONATHAN MICHAEL WINOGRAD, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: History of granulomatous mastitis and family history of breast cancer. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: 1. FOCAL LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). 2. FOCAL MILDLY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. 3. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: 1. ABSCESS WITH GRANULOMATOUS INFLAMMATION. SEE NOTE. 2. FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. 3. FOCAL LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA). 4. MAMMARY DUCT ECTASIA. 5. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. NOTE: Organisms are not identified on PAS, GMS, AFB, Fite, Warthin-Starry, and Brown and Hopps stains. "LYMPH NODE" (LEFT AXILLA), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA WITH FOCAL CHRONIC INFLAMMATION. LYMPH NODE IS NOT IDENTIFIED. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch at 12 o'clock. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm irregular portion of tan unremarkable skin which has a REMOVED_DATE x 2.3cm defect that is consistent with previous nipple site. There is a 6.0cm in length well healed scar 2.2cm from the defect. The anterior is inked blue, and the posterior is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. The cut surface reveals tan-yellow to pink fibrofatty breast tissue with a few cysts. No discrete masses or lesions are identified. Sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections from upper outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections from lower outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections from central region to include posterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section from lower inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections from upper inner quadrant. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm tan irregular portion of skin. The skin shows a REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm defect which is consistent with previous nipple site. Five well healed scars are noted on the skin ranging from 1.0cm in length to 6.0cm in length. The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black, and the specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. The cut surface reveals a centrally located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm white, fibrotic, focally hemorrhagic yellow area. This area is 6.5cm from the nearest posterior margin. The remaining breast tissue is tan-yellow to pink, unremarkable fibrofatty tissue with no masses or discrete lesions identified. Sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections from yellow area.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections from upper outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections from lower outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections from upper inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections from lower inner quadrant. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left axillary node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm tan-pink soft tissue which is serially sectioned and submitted in its entirety in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Gross Dictation by Heather Burton, on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART C: LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLA), EXCISION 
