 from the medial margin, 0.3cm from the lateral margin, and 0.3cm from the anterior margin. The nodular area is located 0.6cm from the superior end and 2.0cm from the inferior end. The remaining breast parenchyma predominantly consists of tan to white, fibrotic to tissue, surrounded by a thin rim of adipose tissue. The specimen is submitted entirely from superior to inferior in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with the superior end in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the inferior end in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The nodular area (harboring a clip) is in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with "left breast additional margin", are several fragments of tan-pink, soft tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm  The tissue is unoriented and sectioned to reveal an unremarkable cut surface. The tissue is entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (LEFT, ADDITIONAL MARGIN), EXCISION [report_end] 
