 (medial portion) B: Biopsy cavity and nearest resection margin (lateral portion) C: Additional biopsy cavity D-E: Skin with scar F-G: Fibrotic areas. Labeled "highest axillary nodes" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue, dissected to reveal a lymph node that is entirely submitted in cassette H. Labeled "left lower axillary content" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue. Several lymph nodes are dissected and entirely submitted in cassettes I and J. Labeled "left high axillary content" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue. Three lymph nodes are dissected and entirely submitted in cassette K. Resident: RUBEN D. CARRASCO, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Susan E Briggs, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), RE-EXCISION PART B: LYMPH NODES (LEFT LOWER AXILLA) PART C: LYMPH NODES (LEFT HIGHER AXILLA) PART D: LYMPH NODE (HIGH AXILLARY), EXCISION 
