VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE: 11 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON: 11 MAY 98 at 10:27 CLINICAL DATA: {None Provided} =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), MASTECTOMY: RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, SCATTERED SMALL FOCI, WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION. (SEE NOTE). HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY. NOTE: The resection margin is free of tumor. BREAST (LEFT "ADDITIONAL"): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT), MAMMOPLASTY: SCLEROSING ADENOSIS. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 OF 4 LYMPH NODES. Diagnosis by: Joseph Misdraji, MD Signed On: 15 MAY 98 at 18:02 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left breast" is an unoriented left mastectomy specimen which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6.5cm with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 5.0cm tan skin ellipse with a central unremarkable nipple areolar complex. There is a healing curvilinear 6.0cm incision located 1.2cm from the nipple areolar complex. The specimen is inked black. There is a suture designating the deep part of the old biopsy cavity. Sectioning beneath the aforementioned incision reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm cystic biopsy cavity which contains a small amount of soft yellow friable material. The biopsy site is surrounded by dense white, firm indurated parenchyma and is located 2.0cm from the closest deep sutured resection margin. The biopsy cavity is located within 0.8cm of the closest anterior resection margin. The adjacent parenchyma has focal bright yellow tissue measuring up to REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  The remaining breast tissue is composed predominantly of dense white fibrous tissue with focal, firm nodularity. A few small blue cysts are also identified within the parenchyma. Section code: A-B: Biopsy cavity in relation to closest suture deep margin; C: Biopsy cavity in relation to closest anterior margin; D: Biopsy cavity in relation to overlying skin; E-F: Parenchymal changes adjacent to biopsy site; G-H: Representative nodular fibrous tissue from remaining breast; No lymph nodes were identified from the mastectomy specimen. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "more left breast tissue" are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm  One fragment is surfaced by an unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm tan skin ellipse. Sectioning through the specimens reveals an unremarkable parenchyma with no discrete lesions. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes I-J. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right breast tissue" are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6.0cm and weighing 500 grams. The largest fragment measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm  A few of the portions have overlying unremarkable portions of tan skin. Sectioning reveals moderate amounts of dense fibrous tissue. No discrete lesions are noted. Three lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  Representative sections of the fibrous parenchyma are submitted in cassettes K-O. Representative sections from each lymph node are submitted in cassette P. Additional sections of the breast tissue are submitted in Q-U. Gross Description by: JANINE L. DUDAC Resident: HOWARD CHANG, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Susan E Briggs, M.D. John Edmund Mayer Jr., M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), MASTECTOMY PART B: BREAST (LEFT "ADDITIONAL") PART C: BREAST (RIGHT) MAMMOPLASTY 
