at the central upper-outer quadrant. The specimen is inked as follows: posterior - black, anterior - blue. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a lobulated tan-yellow fatty cut-surface with an abundant amount of interspersed dense grey-white fibrous tissue with focal cystic areas, consistent with fibrocystic change. There is also a fibrous, scarred appearing area at the superior aspect of the specimen which may represent the site of prior mammoplasty. No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified. The lateral aspect of the specimen is palpated; one possible lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm is identified. Representative sections are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of breast, submitted from medial to lateral.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One possible lymph node, intact. Received fresh, labeled "left breast additional lateral margin", are two irregular portions of tan-yellow to focally cauterized fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm  Also received within the container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE m portion of red-brown, blood clot. The larger portion of tissue is black, the smaller portion of tissue is inked blue. Sectioning reveals a lobulated tan-yellow fatty cut-surface. No discrete masses or lesions are identified in either portion of tissue. Representative sections are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections larger portion of tissue.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire smaller portion of tissue. Received in formalin, labeled Kathleen O?Brien, #302-01-18 and "left breast skin", are two strips of tan, wrinkled, hair-bearing skin with underlying yellow, lobulated adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  The specimens are serially sectioned to reveal a single firm, cystic structure within the larger specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  The smaller specimen is remarkable for a partially ragged, brown-red surface, possibly consistent with muscular tissue. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with representatives of the largest specimen, to include the cystic area in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the smaller specimen in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B: BREAST (LEFT,ADDITIONAL LATERAL MARGIN), EXCISION PART C: SKIN (LEFT BREAST), EXCISION [report_end] 
