VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-1 Results To: MICHELE ANNETTE GADD, M.D. Resident: Rajni V Mandal, M.D. Signed Out by: Melinda J Lerwill, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: Atypical ductal hyperplasia. Family history. Prophylactic bilateral mastectomy. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: 1. FOCAL MILD DUCTAL ATYPIA. 2. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. 3. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 3 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES. BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: 1. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). 2. FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. 3. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. 4. HEALING BIOPSY SITE REACTION. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received are two containers, which are all labeled Dawn Cushing, #302-54-86. Received fresh, labeled "right breast", is a 630 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm simple mastectomy specimen, containing a REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm tan ellipse of skin with a REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm unremarkable areola and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm unremarkable nipple. There is a stitch designating the "12 o'clock" aspect per the surgeon. The anterior surfaces are inked blue, and the posterior surfaces are inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm pale firm fibrous area in the upper outer quadrant of the specimen, which is 3.0cm away from the posterior margin and 2.0cm away from the anterior margin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is diffusely nodular and firm, with cysts ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm in diameter. Sections are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin, radially sectioned.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of fibrotic and firm parenchyma.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Possible axillary tail lymph nodes. Received fresh, labeled "left breast", is a 410 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch denoting the 6 o'clock aspect for the surgeon. Also present is an attached REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm ellipse of tan skin, containing a REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm unremarkable tan areola and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm unremarkable nipple. The anterior surfaces are inked blue, and the posterior surfaces are inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm white puckered area, in the upper outer quadrant of the breast, and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm cavity surrounded by areas of firm tissue, 0.2cm from the closest posterior margin and 4.0cm from the anterior margin. The former described area of puckering is 0.8cm from the closest posterior margin and 5.5cm from the anterior margin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is diffusely nodular and cystic, with cysts ranging in size from 0.2cm to 0.4cm  Sections are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant area of puckering.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial deep firm tissue/cavity with areas surrounding cavity.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Section of most lateral portion of breast; no lymph nodes are identified.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm unremarkable aggregate of adipose tissue. Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY [report_end] 
