VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: UpdatedType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery, WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist: None Frozen Section Resident: None Frozen Section Consultant(s): None Consulting Pathologist(s): None Assigned Resident/Path: Salima Shaikh, M.D. Reports To: BARBARA LYNN SMITH, M.D. ********** Addended Report *********** Reason for Addendum #1: Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA: Bilateral MRI abnormalities, atypia on right core biopsy, no biopsy yet on left side. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION: ATYPICAL COLUMNAR CELL HYPERPLASIA (MILD ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA), FEW FOCI (SEE NOTE). HEALING BIOPSY SITE. FIBROADENOMA. FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS. NOTE: Results of an E-cadherin stain to exclude a small focus of lobular neoplasia will be reported in an addendum. The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated. BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION: ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, FEW FOCI, INCLUDING FOCUS OF SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA (SEE NOTE). FOCAL PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA IN THE VICINITY OF THE CLIP. NOTE: The focus of severely atypical ductal hyperplasia spans 0.1cm  is unrelated to the location of the clip, and is present 0.1cm from the anterior margin. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast biopsy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm irregular yellow-white fibrofatty tissue, with a localization wire in place, which is oriented at the to the superior and lateral aspects. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior blue, posterior black, superior green, and inferior yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm hemorrhagic cavity, which comes to within 0.2cm of the anterior margin, 0.3cm of the inferior margin, 0.4cm of the posterior and superior margins, 0.5cm of the medial margin, and 0.8cm from the lateral margin. On opening this cavity, a cylindrical piece of metal is identified. The specimen is submitted in its entirety sequentially from medial to lateral in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with en face margins in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and cavity within blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast biopsy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm irregular yellow-white fibrofatty tissue, with a short stitch designating superior, and a long stitch designating lateral. There is a localization wire in place, which enters in through the lateral-anterior aspect. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior blue, posterior black, superior green, and inferior yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a cut surface consisting of a white rubbery fibrous tissue and minimal lobulated adipose tissue. A cylindrical portion of the metal is identified within the specimen. The specimen is submitted in its entirety sequentially from medial to lateral in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with en face margins in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the area of the piece of metal in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Gross Dictation by Michael R Tan, on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Salima Shaikh M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: Additional immunohistochemistry results. Note: An E-cadherin stain performed on the right breast specimen does not reveal evidence of lobular neoplasia. Addendum #1 by Kristina Braaten M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION 
