nding to other resection margins. Small cysts, 0.2cm to 0.5cm in diameter, some containing clear, watery fluid others brown fluid, are found scattered within the tumor mass. SECTION CODE G: Tumor at posterior resection margin. H-K: Additional sections of the tumor. L: Section of fibrous area away from the main tumor mass. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number and "left breast specimen" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm aggregate of yellow, fibroadipose tissue fragments. No grossly obvious breast tissue or lymph nodes are identified. Representative sections of more fibrous portion of the specimen is submitted in cassettes M and N. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number and "right breast specimen" is a 7 x 7 x 4.0cm aggregate of yellow to tan, fibroadipose tissue fragments. No grossly identifiable structure is found in the specimen. Representative sections of the fibrous tissue is submitted in cassette O and P. Resident: HOWARD CHANG, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Susan E Briggs, M.D. James Warren May Jr., M.D. PART A: LEFT MASTECTOMY PART B: RIGHT MASTECTOMY PART C: BREAST TISSUE (LEFT) PART D: BREAST TISSUE (RIGHT) \u000a[report_end] 
