VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-2 Results To: MICHELE ANNETTE GADD, M.D. Frozen Section Pathologist: Esther Oliva, M.D. Frozen Section Resident: Olga Kolman, M.D. Signed Out by: Ronald Balassanian, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: The patient is a 50 year old woman with invasive breast cancer in the right breast. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLA, "SENTINEL," #394), EXCISION: METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN ONE OF THREE LYMPH NODES (1/3) (see Table #1 and note). LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLA CONTENTS), DISSECTION: METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA PRESENT IN 6 OF 19 LYMPH NODES (see Table #1 and note). TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS #1 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES AND SENTINEL LYMPH NODES Total number of positive lymph nodes: 6 Total number of lymph nodes examined: 19 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0.02cm or less (isolated tumor cells): 0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases > 0.02cm to 0.2cm (micrometastasis): 1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases >0.2cm (macro-metastases): 5 Method of detection: Both hematoxylin and eosin and cytokeratin immunohistochemistry. Extracapsular extension: Slight Other forms of axillary involvement: Lymphatic vessels and blood vessels Note: Keratin positive tumor cells are identified on six  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/CAM REMOVED_DATE immunostained levels. BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: 1. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE 2. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. 3. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. (See note) Note: The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL ANTERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: 1. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MILD DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, USUAL TYPE. 2. SKIN WITH SCAR. 3. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. 4. SKIN WITH SCAR AND CHRONIC INFLAMMATION. 5. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. (See note) Note: The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL INFERIOR ANTERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: 1. ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS. (See note) 2. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. 3. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. Note: The ADH is present in a single small focus measuring less than 0.2cm and located less than 0.1cm from the inked margin of resection. Multiple levels were examined. The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. BREAST (RIGHT POSTERIOR), EXCISION: 1. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MILD DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. 2. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. 3. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled Karen Dost, #305-45-85 and "right axilla sentinel lymph, #394", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue, which is dissected and palpated to reveal three candidate lymph nodes. The largest lymph node is bisected and submitted for Frozen Section as FX #1, now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remaining tissue is submitted in toto in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received are five containers, which are all labeled Karen Dost, #305-45-85. Received in formalin, labeled "right breast final inferior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm portion of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the new margin. The surface containing the stitch is inked black; specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast anterior final", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm portion of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the new margin. Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm tan-brown skin ellipse excised to a depth of 0.4cm  The overlying tan-brown skin contains a 0.6cm well-healed scar. The specimen is inked black, serially sectioned, and submitted entirely as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire fibroadipose tissue, serially sectioned.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Tip, skin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body, skin ellipse. Received in formalin, labeled "right breast inferior-anterior final margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm portion of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the new margin. The surface containing the stitch is inked black. The opposite surface is fibrotic and hemorrhagic. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast posterior tissue", are two unoriented portions of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  The specimens are serially sectioned and submitted entirely as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Smaller fragment, serially sectioned.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Larger fragment, serially sectioned. Received in formalin, labeled "right axillary contents", is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm aggregate of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue which 20 whole lymph nodes dissected ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  All lymph nodes are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Six whole lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Four whole lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Four whole lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Three whole lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Two whole lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Largest lymph node, serially sectioned. INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION # 1; RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE: POSITIVE FOR CARCINOMA. Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: Lymph Node (Right Axilla, "Sentinel", #394), Excision PART B: Breast (Right, Final Inferior Margin), Excision PART C: Breast (Right, Final Anterior Margin), Excision PART D: Breast (Right, Final Inferior Anterior Margin), Excision PART E: Breast (Right Posterior), Excision PART F: Lymph Nodes ( [report_end] 
