 seen on the CK immunostained slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). Extracapsular extension: None. Other forms of axillary involvement: None. NOTE: The metastatic focus is not present in frozen tissue section. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MARGIN SUPEROLATERAL), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA; THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. (SEE NOTE). NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA; THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. (SEE NOTE). NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MARGIN MEDIAL), EXCISION: FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA, SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA) (SEE NOTE). HEALING BIOPSY SITE. NOTE: An e-cadherin supports a diagnosis of lobular neoplasia (atypical lobular hyperplasia). BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MARGIN LATERAL), EXCISION: HEALING BIOPSY SITE; THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MARGIN DEEP), EXCISION: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA). FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA; MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled Antoinette Delvecchio, #306-29-76 and "left breast lump", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm unoriented portion of yellow lobulated soft tissue with a separately received localization wire. The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ill-defined, white, gritty mass with white packing material coming to 0.1cm from the black-inked margin. The specimen is submitted entirely from one end to the other as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID end margin, en face;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID mass;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID uninvolved parenchyma;  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID second end margin. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled Antoinette Delvecchio, #306-29-76 and "left axillary sentinel node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm tan-yellow soft tissue. The specimen is bivalved and frozen entirely as FX#1 and #1A, now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  respectively. Received are 5 containers which are labeled Antoinette Delvecchio, #306-29-76. Received in formalin, labeled "left breast, final margin, superolateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm portion of yellow lobulated soft tissue with a suture designating the new true margin. The new true margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast, final margin, inferior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm portion of yellow lobulated soft tissue with a suture designating the new true margin. The new true margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast, final margin, medial", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm portion of yellow lobulated soft tissue with a suture designating the new true margin. The new true margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast, final margin, lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm portion of yellow lobulated soft tissue with a suture designating the new true margin. The new true margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast, final margin, deep", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm portion of yellow-red soft tissue with a suture designating the new true margin. The new true margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1 & 1A; LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: 1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. Rare tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) HER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation; the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows: Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) Show strong (3+) overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test?s accuracy and precision. Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: 2 RESULTS