ith the patient's name, unit number and "sentinel node #3 (100)" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm lymph node with surrounding adipose tissue, which is bivalved and submitted entirely in cassette M. Resident: HEIKE VARNHOLT, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Kevin Hughes,MD PART A: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL #1), EXCISION PART B: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL #2), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART D: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL #3), EXCISION 
