VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: UpdatedType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-1 Results To: MICHELE ANNETTE GADD, M.D. Resident: Aleksandr Vasilyev, M.D. Frozen Section Pathologist: Gregory Y Lauwers, M.D. Frozen Section Resident: Christopher J Nero, M.D. Signed Out by: John H Eichhorn, M.D. ********** Addended Report *********** Reason for Addendum #1: Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization (FISH) Results CLINICAL DATA: Core with invasive lobular carcinoma. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLARY, SENTINEL, #1), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 NODE. SEE NOTE 1. THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED. NOTE 1: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLARY, SENTINEL, #2), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 NODE. SEE NOTE 2. THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED. NOTE 2: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLARY, SENTINEL, #3), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 NODE. SEE NOTE 3. NOTE 3: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. BREAST (RIGHT), WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION: INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA. SEE TABLE. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE: REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm (slide measurement). GRADE: 2. LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION: Not identified. BLOOD VESSEL INVASION: Not identified. MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA: Invasive carcinoma extends to < 0.1cm from the anterior, posterior, superior and inferior margins of the specimen along broad fronts. STAINS FOR RECEPTORS: Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (Her-2 only). BREAST (RIGHT, SUPERIOR, FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), ORIENTED EXCISION: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. SEE NOTE 4. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. NOTE 4: The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated. BREAST (RIGHT, INFERIOR, FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), ORIENTED EXCISION: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). SEE NOTE 5. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. SMALL DUCT PAPILLOMA. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA. NOTE 5: By immunoperoxidase techniques, the lobular neoplastic cells are negative for e-cadherin. The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated. BREAST (RIGHT, MEDIAL, FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), ORIENTED EXCISION: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. SEE NOTE 6. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. NOTE 6: The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated. BREAST (RIGHT, LATERAL, FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), ORIENTED EXCISION: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA). SEE NOTE 7. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. NOTE 7: The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated. BREAST (RIGHT, ANTERIOR, FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), ORIENTED EXCISION: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA). SEE NOTE 8. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. NOTE 8: The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated. BREAST (RIGHT, DEEP, FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), ORIENTED EXCISION: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). SEE NOTE 9. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA. NOTE 9: The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled Medb Sichko, #309-01-69 and "right sentinel node #1", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm tan-yellow lymph node which is frozen entirely as FX#1, now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled Medb Sichko, #309-01-69 and "right axillary sentinel node #2", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm red-tan potential lymph node frozen entirely as FX#2, now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled Medb Sichko, #309-01-69 and "right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.9cm tan-pink soft tissue with a long stitch designating the lateral aspect and a short stitch designating the superior aspect. The specimen is oriented with a long axis medial to lateral and is inked as follows: anterior - blue, posterior - black, superior - green, inferior - yellow. The specimen is received with the wire removed. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a white-tan firm tissue that takes up the entire specimen and abuts all margins. There are multiple small focal hemorrhages. The specimen is submitted entirely as follows: Section code:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral aspect, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Serial sections from lateral to medial.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial aspect, en face. Received fresh, labeled Medb Sichko, #309-01-69 and "right breast superior final shaved margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm piece of yellow-tan soft tissue with a stitch designating the new margin. The new margin is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable yellow-tan soft tissue. It is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled Medb Sichko, #309-01-69 and "right breast inferior final shaved margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm piece of yellow-tan soft tissue with a stitch designating the new margin. The new margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable tan-yellow soft tissue submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received formalin, labeled Medb Sichko, #309-01-69 and "right breast medial final shaved margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm piece of yellow-tan soft tissue with a stitch designating the new margin. The new margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable tan-yellow soft tissue submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled Medb Sichko, #309-01-69 and "right breast lateral final shaved margin", are two fragments of yellow-tan soft tissue with a stitch designating the new margin. The new margin is inked black. The REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm fragment is sectioned to reveal unremarkable tissue and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm fragment is sectioned to reveal unremarkable tissue and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled Medb Sichko, #309-01-69 and "right breast anterior final shaved margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm piece of yellow-tan soft tissue with a stitch designating the new margin. The new margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable soft tissue submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled Medb Sichko, #309-01-69 and "right breast deep final shaved margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm piece of yellow-tan soft tissue with a stitch designating the new margin. The new margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable soft tissue submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled Medb Sichko, #309-01-69 and "right axillary sentinel lymph node #3", is a 0.4cm potential lymph node with a small amount of attached fat. The specimen is bisected and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1; (RIGHT SENTINEL LYMPH #1): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. FROZEN SECTION #2; (RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE #2): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: #1 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals (118) to chromosome 17 signals (103) in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. Results at or near the cutoff point (ranging from REMOVED_DATE - 2.2) should be interpreted with caution. Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART : LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLARY, SENTINEL, #1), EXCISIONLYMPH NOD 
