 axis in the following manner: anterior-blue, posterior-black, superior-green, interior-yellow. The two smaller portions are inked black entirely. The large portion of the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a tan-yellow and focally hemorrhagic cut surface, and is submitted from medial to lateral in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (at least 90% submitted with only a small fragment of fat remaining). The two smaller portions of this specimen are bivalved to reveal a tan firm cut surface. These two portions of the specimen are submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  respectively. Gross Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART : BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION 
