excision" only, are 2 portions of fibrofatty breast tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm and a REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm portion of tan skin, excised up to a depth of 1.0cm  The skin surface displays a 2.5cm well-healed linear scar. The larger portion of breast tissue is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm gray-white, focally hemorrhagic nodule, which abuts the margin. The smaller portion of breast tissue is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm well-defined, gray-white, focally hemorrhagic area. Representative sections are submitted as:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Larger portion of breast tissue.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One end, enface.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Center, nodule in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Opposing end containing nodule, perpendicularly sectioned.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2nd portion of breast tissue, submitted entirely.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative cross-sections of skin. Received in formalin, labeled Hao Banh, #311-19-23 and "right breast final lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue, with a stitch designating 1 aspect, which is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal areas of firm, gray-white, fibrous tissue, which abuts the ink. Also received is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm aggregate of unoriented fibrofatty breast tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Oriented portion of breast tissue, submitted sequentially.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional aggregate of breast tissue. INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1; LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL): CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED. AWAIT SENTINEL NODE WORKUP. Final Diagnosis by Ritu Ghai M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 17,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 07:05:10PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Lymph Node (Right Axilla, "Sentinel"), Excision PART B: Breast (Right), Re-Excision PART C: Breast (Right Lateral, Final Margin), Excision PART D: Cryostat Frozen Section (slide only) [report_end] 
