VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: UpdatedType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist: Ben Zion Pilch, M.D. Frozen Section Resident: Norma Rodriguez, M.D. Frozen Section Consultant(s): None Consulting Pathologist(s): None Assigned Resident/Path: Rosalynn M Nazarian, M.D. Reports To: MICHELE ANNETTE GADD, M.D. ********** Addended Report *********** Reason for Addendum #1: Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA: Left breast invasive ductal carcinoma by core biopsy (3/05). FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT, "6:00"), EXCISION: INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU. FIBROADENOMA. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. SEE NOTE. SEE TABLE #1. NOTE: The tumor cells stain for the E-cadherin. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  Grade: 2. Lymphatic vessel invasion: Not identified. Blood vessel invasion: Not identified. Margin of invasive carcinoma: Positive at the inferior margin of the specimen along a broad front. Location of ductal carcinoma in-situ: Within the region of the mass Grade of ductal carcinoma in-situ: 1. Margin of ductal carcinoma in-situ: The distances to all margins measure 0.2cm or greater. Stains for receptors: Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (Her-2 only). BREAST (LEFT, "INFERIOR HALF, 6:00"), EXCISION: INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, REMOVED_DATE CM, EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE FINAL MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). SEE NOTE. NOTE: The lobular carcinoma cells do not stain for E-cadherin. BREAST (LEFT, "SUPERIOR HALF, 6:00"), EXCISION: UNREMARKABLE FAT. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, "FINAL MARGIN"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, "1:00"), EXCISION: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). FIBROADENOMA. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. SEE NOTE. NOTE: The tumor cells do not stain for E-cadherin. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION: METASTATIC CARCINOMA, SINGLE CLUSTER OF A FEW CELLS IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE. SEE TABLE #2. TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS #2 SENTINEL LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES: 1 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED: 1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0.02cm or less (isolated tumor cells): 1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases >0.02cm to 0.2cm (micrometastases): 0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases >0.2cm (macrometastases): 0 Method of detection: Cytokeratin immunohistochemistry Extracapsular extension: None. Other forms of axillary involvement: None. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left axillary sentinel lymph node" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm yellow-tan fragment of soft tissue, which is bivalved and entirely frozen as FX#1. Cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  = FX#1. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and " left breast 6:00" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm fragment of pink-tan soft tissue oriented with the long stitch lateral and short stitch superior. On the posterior surface, there is a thin fibrous smooth capsule. The superior medial portion of the tissue has palpable nodules within. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior - blue, posterior - black, superior - green, inferior - yellow. There is a firm white mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm abutting the inferior margin. Section code:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of the mass. The closest margin appears to be in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections away from the nodular area. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and " left breast 1:00" is an unoriented fragment of pink-yellow unremarkable breast measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm  The specimen is inked black, serially sectioned, and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast inferior half 6:00" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm fragment of fibrofatty soft tissue oriented with a long stitch lateral, two short double stitches indicating the new inferior margin and a single short stitch indicating superior. On the side opposite the two short double stitches, the tissue is red-tan-brown and has two staples with irregularity. The surface oriented by the two short double stitches is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The sections in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  have a firm, white cut surface. The remainder of the parenchyma is bright yellow-tan and unremarkable. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast superior half 6:00" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm fragment of soft yellow-red tissue, which is unoriented. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast, 1:00, final margin" are multiple fragments of yellow-pink soft tissue which are unoriented, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm in aggregate. The mass is serially sectioned to reveal focal poorly defined, firm, fibrous areas and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION# 1; (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Gross Dictation by Rosalynn M Nazarian M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Rosalynn M Nazarian M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Rosalynn M Nazarian M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER-2/c-erbB-2 Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Addendum #1 by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (LEFT, "6:00"), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (LEFT, "1:00"), EXCISION PART D: BREAST (LEFT, "INFERIOR HALF, 6:00"), EXCISION PART E: BREAST (LEFT, "SUPERIOR HALF, 6:00"), EXCISION PART F: BREAST (LEFT, "FINAL MARGIN"), EXCISION 
