) consist of individual cells scattered throughout the lymph node, present on all three cytokeratin stained slides. The tumor cells are not identified on the frozen section slide or the hematoxylin and eosin stained slide. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received are three containers which are all labeled Marilynn Forti, #315-80-93. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled "left axilla sentinel node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm tan-yellow lymph node. The lymph node is bisected and entirely submitted for frozen as FX#1, now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled "left mastectomy, short stitch ? superior, long stitch ? lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm left simple mastectomy specimen with a long suture designating the lateral and a short suture designating the superior aspect. On the anterior surface is a REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm tan-white skin ellipse with an eccentrically located, unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm nipple. No scar is identified. The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm well-delineated tan-pink firm mass located within the lower inner quadrant, coming to 0.5cm from the posterior and 1.0cm from the blue-inked anterior margin. The surrounding parenchyma is stained blue and the mass on cut surface contains a metal clip. The remaining uninvolved parenchyma is tan-yellow to pink, lobulated fibrofatty tissue. The fibrous tissue contains multiple cystic structures filled with dark brown cloudy fluid. Within the upper outer quadrant, a possible lymph node is identified. Representative sections are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire lower inner quadrant mass to closest posterior and anterior soft tissue margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of fibrous tissue.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Possible lymph node. Received fresh, labeled "additional anterior superior margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm aggregate of tan-yellow lobulated unoriented fibrofatty soft tissue fragments. The fragments are serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1; (LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL NODE): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Final Diagnosis by Joshua Kish M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON #1: QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The invasive tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein. The invasive tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein. The invasive tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. The lobular carcinoma in-situ cells stain for estrogen receptor protein Some lobular carcinoma in-situ cells stain for progesterone receptor protein The lobular carcinoma in-situ cells focally show moderate (2+) overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. Note: Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) HER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation: The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows: Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) Show strong (3+) over overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) These