 Posterior margin en face. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "papilloma left breast", is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm tan piece of soft tissue, which is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "duct lower inner quadrant (left breast)", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm oriented breast tissue, with a short stitch designating anterior, and the papilloma, a long stitch designating lateral, and a bowtie designating cephalad. The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior, and is inked as follows: superior/blue, inferior/black, medial/green, lateral/yellow. There is a 0.2cm duct noted in the anterior surface and posterior surface. On the anterior surface, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm papilloma. A clip is not identified. The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior, and representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin en face including papilloma.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Full section cross section of tissue next to anterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Section of cross section including lateral, superior, inferior and medial margins.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section including superior, inferior and medial margins.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Full thickness section including lateral, medial, superior and inferior margins, which is bivalved into two parts.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section including superior and inferior margins.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Full thickness section including lateral, inferior, medial and superior margins, and bivalved into two parts.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin submitted en face. Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION PART B: PAPILLOMA BREAST (LEFT,), BIOPSY PART C: BREAST (LEFT DUCT LOWER INNER QUADRANT), EXCISION [report_end] 
