 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin on multiple tissue levels support the above interpretation. TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS #2 SENTINEL LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES: 1 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED: 2 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0.02cm or less (isolated tumor cells): 0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases >0.02cm to 0.2cm (micrometastases): 1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases >0.2cm (macrometastases): 0 Method of detection: Cytokeratin immunohistochemistry (levels 3 through 6). Extracapsular extension: None Other forms of axillary involvement: None BREAST (RIGHT), NIPPLE-SPARING SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: 1. ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA. 2. LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU. 3. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLA, SENTINEL # REMOVED_CASE_ID ), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 LYMPH NODES (0/2). NOTE: Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the above interpretation. SKIN (RIGHT MASTECTOMY FLAP), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. SKIN (LEFT MASTECTOMY FLAP), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled Kelly Dimillo, #318-52-71, "right axillary sentinel node # REMOVED_CASE_ID ", are 2 yellow-pink fragments of lobulated adipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm  From these fragments, 2 lymph nodes are identified. Both lymph nodes are bisected and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with 1 lymph node in each cassette. Received are 5 containers which are each labeled Kelly Dimillo, #318-52-71. Received fresh, labeled "right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.7cm mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The breast is devoid of skin, nipple and areola. The anterior margin is inked blue and the posterior is inked black. The specimen consists of dense tan-yellow to gray-white fibrofatty, nodular tissue with focal cystic areas consistent with fibrocystic change. Lymph nodes are not detected in the lateral tissue. The following representative sections are submitted:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper-inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper-outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower-outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower-inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central aspect of specimen.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Small nodule in central breast.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Small firm area in medial breast.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Area of clustered punctate yellow secretions in medial breast. Received fresh, labeled "left breast", is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The specimen is devoid of skin, nipple and areola. The anterior margin is inked blue and the posterior margin is inked black. The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm indurated, ill-defined focus within the lower inner quadrant to lower central breast, which extends to within 0.5cm of the posterior and focally to 0.3cm of the anterior margins. The surrounding tissue is tan-pink and feels nodular and gritty. The remainder of the specimen consists of lobulated tan-yellow fat with an abundant amount of interspersed nodular fibrous tissue. Lymph nodes are not detected in the lateral tissue. The following representative sections are submitted, including the indurated area in its entirety:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Indurated area and surrounding gritty fibrous tissue.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper-outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper-inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower-outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central aspect of specimen.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lactiferous ducts.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of indurated area to anterior margin. Received fresh, labeled "left axillary sentinel node # REMOVED_CASE_ID ", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm unoriented portion of lymph node-bearing fat, which contains 2 lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE and 1.9cm in greatest dimension. The specimen is submitted entirely as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 lymph node, bisected.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 lymph node, bisected.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of fat. Received fresh, labeled "right mastectomy flap", is a REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm unoriented white skin excised to a depth of 0.9cm  No masses or lesions are identified. Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left mastectomy flap", are 4 irregular portions of unremarkable white skin ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 28,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 08:53:50PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: #1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: - The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) - Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) - Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) - The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) HER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation; the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated v