one aspect designating the long lateral margin and a short suture designating the superior margin. A localization wire is in place. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior-blue, posterior-black, superior-green, and inferior-yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a cavity, consistent with a previous biopsy site measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  The cavity contains white packing indurated material and a metal clip. The cavity comes to <0.1cm from the superior, 0.1cm from the posterior, 0.2cm from the inferior, 0.3cm from the anterior, 0.5cm from the lateral and <0.1cm from the medial margins, respectively. The remaining parenchyma is tan-yellow-pink and grossly unremarkable. The specimen is entirely and sequentially submitted from lateral to medial in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with the lateral margin taken en face in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The entire cavity in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the medial margin taken radially in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION [report_end] 
