ior margin is inked blue and the posterior margin is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal focal areas of dense, white fibrous tissue, with no discrete masses or lesions identified. In particular, no discrete lesion is identified in the lower outer region, although there is some fibrous breast tissue in the region. No lymph nodes are identified. Representative sections of the dense, fibrous tissue are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant tissue which may represent lymph nodes. Received fresh, labeled "right breast," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.3-cm simple mastectomy specimen with a suture designating 12 o?clock. There is a REMOVED_DATE x 4.0-cm unremarkable nipple-areolar complex. The anterior margin is inked blue and the posterior margin is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal focal areas of dense, white fibrous tissue, with no discrete masses or lesions identified. No lymph nodes are identified. Representative sections of the fibrous tissue are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant tissue which may represent lymph nodes. Received in formalin, labeled "left non-sentinel axillary node," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5-cm aggregate of yellow, lobulated adipose tissue in which a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2-cm pink, rubbery lymph node is identified. The lymph node is submitted in its entirety as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remainder of the specimen is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1 (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART C: BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART D: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA), EXCISION PART E: CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION (SLIDE ONLY) [report_end] 
