ellipse contains a REMOVED_DATE x 4.5cm areola and a REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm flattened nipple. There is a 3.5cm curvilinear well-healed scar approximately between the 3 and 4 o'clock position, 6.0cm from the areola. The specimen is inked as follows: Anterior blue, posterior black. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral axis, to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm stellate scar which lies approximately between 3 and 4 o'clock position in the outer quadrant beneath the overlying well-healed scar on skin. The stellate tan-white fibrous scar lies 2.5cm from overlying skin and 2.0cm from posterior inked margin. The rest of the breast parenchyma contains tan-yellow lobulated cut surface interspersed with fibrous tissue. No evidence of another discrete mass or lesion is noted. No lymph nodes are identified in the specimen. Representative sections are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire scar, to include adjacent fibrous breast parenchyma, outer quadrant, with nearest posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section, fibrous breast tissue, inner lower quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section, fibrous breast parenchyma, inner upper quadrant. Received are two additional containers, which are all labeled Margaret Scandalis, #323-21-19. Received in formalin, labeled "left axillary sentinel node #253", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm tan-yellow lobulated soft tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left axillary sentinel node #105", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm tan-yellow lobulated portion of soft tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm lymph node. The lymph node is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Fellow Review by Christopher K Hysell M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Joshua Kish M.D., Electronically signed on 