VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE: 04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON: 04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13:35 CLINICAL DATA: Breast carcinoma and bilateral mastectomies. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), MASTECTOMY: 1. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES INCLUDING ADENOSIS, SCLEROSING ADENOSIS, APOCRINE METAPLASIA, CYST FORMATION, AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS. 2. BIOPSY SITE WITH FAT NECROSIS, CHRONIC INFLAMMATION, AND DENSE FIBROSIS. 3. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 13 OF 13 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES. 4. ANGIOMA INVOLVING SUPERFICIAL DERMIS. BREAST (RIGHT), MASTECTOMY: 1. LOBULAR CARCINOMA-IN-SITU, MULTIFOCAL, WITH A DOMINANT REMOVED_DATE CM IN DIAMETER NODULE, FOCALLY INVOLVING AREAS OF ADENOSIS. 2. BIOPSY SITE WITH FAT NECROSIS, CHRONIC INFLAMMATION, AND DENSE FIBROSIS. 3. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES INCLUDING GLANDULAR ADENOSIS, FIBROSIS, CYST FORMATION AND MICROCALCIFICATION. (SEE NOTE). NOTE: There is no unequivocal evidence of invasion. There is no vascular nor lymphatic invasion. Dr. B. Pilch has reviewed selected slides and agrees with the diagnosis. Diagnosis by: Volker Nickeleit, M.D. Signed On: 08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 20:04 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in two separate parts. Labeled with the patient's name and unit number and designated "left breast" is an 850 gram mastectomy specimen, 25 x 16 x 3.5cm with a REMOVED_DATE x 10.5cm skin ellipse with a central areola, 5cm in diameter, with an unremarkable 1.2cm in diameter nipple. At one end of the skin ellipse is an 8 x 6 x 2cm axillary tail. The axillary lymph nodes range from REMOVED_DATE to 2.0cm in diameter (none are grossly suspicious for carcinoma). 3.3cm superior to the areola is a 4mm in diameter, slightly raised, red-brown papule 5.5cm from the apex of the skin ellipse. Between the brown pigmented lesion and 0.9cm from the apex of the skin ellipse is a 3.5cm long, slightly hypertrophic scar with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm underlying biopsy site. The biopsy site consists of a fibrotic slit, surrounded by granular tan and yellow tissue, which is focally hemorrhagic. The biopsy site extends to 2.5cm from the closest deep margin and to 3.0cm from the skin surface. The remainder of the breast is unremarkable except for a 3 x 2 x 2mm dark red-brown nodule distant from the biopsy site, 3.5cm from the deep margin and 2.5cm from the skin surface. Section Code A-H - axillary lymph nodes. I - skin with scar J-M - representative sections of biopsy site and closest deep resection margin N - dark red-brown nodule distant from biopsy site O,P - representative sections of breast distant from biopsy site Q - section of nipple R - section of skin with red-brown papule. S - scar and closest lateral inked resection margin Separately received, labeled with the patient's name and unit number only and designated "right breast" is an 825 gram, 22 x 16 x 4cm right simple mastectomy specimen. The 21 x 11.5cm overlying skin ellipse shows an eccentric 5cm in diameter unremarkable areola with a central 1.3cm in diameter unremarkable nipple. The areola extends to 1.0cm from one edge of the skin ellipse. On the opposite edge of the skin ellipse is a 5cm long hypertrophic scar extending to 0.5cm from the margin. Deep to the scar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm biopsy cavity lined by smooth, tan-red tissue and surrounded by granular, tan-yellow (fat necrosis) tissue. The biopsy cavity extends to 2.0cm from the deep margin and to 2.0cm from the skin surface and to 1.5cm from the closest lateral margin. 2.5cm distant from the biopsy cavity and 2.0cm from the closest margin is a 1.5cm in diameter area of rubbery, firmer tan breast tissue. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable. Section Code T-V - representative sections of biopsy cavity with closest deep resection margin in T and closest lateral resection margin in U W - skin with scar and closest adjacent resection margin X - representative section of nipple Y,Z - representative sections of firm area of breast Resident: Jeoffry Brennick, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Leslie Wayne Ottinger, M.D. Neil T Chen, M.D. PART A: LEFT BREAST PART B: RIGHT BREAST \u000a[report_end] 
