renchyma is characterized by diffuse fibrocystic change and is otherwise grossly unremarkable. SECTION CODE F-K: Biopsy cavity submitted entirely (F contains deep margin). L-N: Firm nodule in upper outer quadrant. O-P: Representative parenchyma away from the biopsy cavity and the firm nodule. Labeled "right breast, additional superficial superior" is a 3 x 3 x 4cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue. Submitted entirely in Q through V. Resident: LISA A. GALLAGHER, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** GROSS DIAGNOSIS (BREAST, LEFT SIMPLE MASTECTOMY): NO LARGE AREA GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA. O.R. Resident: HONGMEI LI, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Lawrence R. Zukerberg, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. Ashby Carter Moncure, M.D. Lawrence T Geoghegan, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT),MASTECTOMY PART B: BREAST (RIGHT),MASTECTOMY PART C: BREAST (RIGHT, ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR), EXCISION \u000a[report_end] 
