at such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 07 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 14:04 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left axillary lymph node" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm lymph node largely replaced by fat. The lymph node is trisected, entirely frozen as FX #1-3, now submitted in cassettes A-C. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast biopsy" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm portion of breast tissue, inked and sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes D-G. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast simple mastectomy" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5.0cm simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 12.0cm skin ellipse containing a nipple, and a stitch designating superior 12 o'clock. At 3 o'clock, 3.0cm to the nipple is a 3.5cm linear well healed scar. The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1.5cm in diameter firm stellate area underneath the scar which is 2.0cm from the closest inferior margin, and 4.0cm from the deep margin. 2.0cm inferior to the nodule is a 0.5cm stellate rubbery area. No additional nodule or mass is present in the remaining breast parenchyma. The remaining breast parenchyma consists of 90% yellow lobulated fat and 10% fibrous tissue. No lymph node is identified. Representative sections are submitted as follows: SECTION CODES: H-K: 1.5cm stellate area entirely submitted. L: 0.5cm nodule entirely submitted. M: inferior margin, en face. N: deep margin. O: representative section of uninvolved area. P: representative section of unremarkable nipple. Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm fragment of breast tissue, with a REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm unremarkable attached skin ellipse. A representative section is submitted