VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE: 24 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON: 24 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 10:04 CLINICAL DATA: Prior diagnosis of left axillary tissue with focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia. Significant family history of breast cancer. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. SEE NOTE NOTE: An immunohistochemical stain for E-Cadherin shows a loss of membranous staining in the affected lobules, confirming the diagnosis of lobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ). LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on six  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. SKIN (LEFT BREAST), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES SEE NOTE. NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on six  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. SKIN (RIGHT BREAST), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 02 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 13:58 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left sentinel node biopsy axilla" are 2 fragments of adipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm  Each fragment is dissected to reveal 2 lymph nodes, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  Both lymph nodes are bisected, and the smaller is frozen as FX #1, now resubmitted in A. The larger is frozen as FX #1A, now resubmitted in B. Note that adipose tissue devoid of lymph node is not submitted. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right sentinel node biopsy axilla" are 2 fragments of adipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm  Both pieces are dissected to reveal 2 lymph nodes, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  Each lymph node is bisected and frozen as FX #2 and #2A, now resubmitted in C and D respectively. Note that adipose tissue devoid of lymph node is not submitted. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "extra skin right" is an irregular portion of tan unremarkable skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1.8cm  excised to a depth of 1.9cm  Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm portion of fibroadipose tissue. Serial sectioning of the subcutaneous tissue and fibroadipose tissue reveals no nodules or masses. Representative sections are submitted in E. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "extra skin left" is an irregular fragment of tan unremarkable skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm  excised to a depth of 1.0cm  The underlying subcutaneous tissue is serially sectioned and is found to be unremarkable, without nodules or masses. Representative sections are submitted in F. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm simple mastectomy with a short stitch designated by the surgeon as superior and a long stitch designated as lateral. The mastectomy contains a REMOVED_DATE x 6.0cm skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm nipple-areolar complex, which contains an inverted nipple, but is otherwise unremarkable. The area lateral to the nipple is previously dyed blue. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior-blue, posterior-black. Serially sectioning reveals multiple, ill-defined areas of rubbery fibrosis, comprising approximately 40% of the breast parenchyma, spanning a total area of REMOVED_DATE x 6.0cm and coming to 1.0cm of the closest posterior margin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is tan-yellow, lobulated and unremarkable. Sectioning in the region of the axilla reveals no lymph nodes. Representative sections from areas of fibrosis are submitted in G-P, from lateral to medial, with closest posterior margin represented in G and H. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm simple mastectomy specimen, containing an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6.5cm tan skin ellipse. The skin ellipse contains a REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm nipple-areolar complex. There is an area lateral to the nipple which is previously dyed blue. The skin is otherwise unremarkable. The specimen is oriented as follows: short stitch superior, long stitch lateral. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior-blue, posterior-black. Serial sectioning reveals multiple areas of tan-white rubbery fibrosis comprising approximately 50% of the breast parenchyma and spanning a region measuring REMOVED_DATE x 8.0cm  Fibrosis comes to 0.7cm of the closest posterior margin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is tan-yellow and lobular, without nodules or masses. Sectioning of the axillary area reveals no lymph nodes. Representative sections of fibrotic areas from lateral to medial are submitted in Q-Z, with closest posterior margin represented in R and Y. Resident: ALIYAH RAHEMTULLAH, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY, SENTINEL #1), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1A: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY, SENTINEL #2), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #2: LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLARY, SENTINEL #1), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #2A: LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLARY, SENTINEL #2), EXCISION" THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. O.R. Resident: STEWART M. KNOEPP, MD., Ph.D. O.R. Diagnosis by: Robert Henry Young, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE (SENTINEL LEFT AXILLA), EXCISION PART B: LYMPH NODE (SENTINEL RIGHT AXILLA), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART D: BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART E: SKIN (RIGHT BREAST), EXCISION PART F: SKIN (LEFT BREAST), EXCISION 
