. The specimen is serially bread-loafed to reveal predominantly tan-white, rubbery fibrous tissue interspersed with a moderate amount of tan-yellow lobulated adipose tissue. There is no discrete mass or lesion grossly appreciated. The upper-outer quadrant is dissected for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated. Representative sections are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section, fibrous breast parenchyma, upper-inner quadrant  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section, fibrous breast parenchyma, inner-lower quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section, fibrous breast parenchyma, outer-upper quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section, fibrous breast parenchyma, outer-lower quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section, central region of the breast. Received are 2 containers which are labeled Donna Casaletto, #332-89-57. Received in formalin, labeled "right breast skin", is a REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm piece of unoriented tan skin, excised to a depth of 0.7cm  No masses or lesions are identified. Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast skin", are 3 pieces of grossly unremarkable wrinkled tan skin, ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M.D., Electronically signed on Sunday REMOVED_MONTH 17,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11:34:21AM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Lymph Node (Right Axilla, "Sentinel"COUNT 353), Excision PART B: Breast (Right), Simple Mastectomy PART C: Lymph Node (Left Axilla, "Sentinel"COUNT  REMOVED_CASE_ID ), Excision PART D: Breast (Left), Simple Mastectomy PART E: Skin (Right breast), Excision PART 