, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "Left breast tissue" are two irregular portions of fibrofatty breast tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm  The smaller portion is predominantly unremarkable adipose tissue. The larger portion has an irregular, ill-defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm yellow-white firm focus which abuts one margin. The lesion is submitted in its entirely in cassettes G - K. Gross Description by: JANINE L. DUDAC Resident: ALEXANDER KRATZ, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FXDX #1, BREAST TISSUE (LEFT): SUSPICIOUS CALCIFIED FOCUS; FAVOR SCLEROSING ADENOSIS OVER CARCINOMA; AWAIT PERMANENTS. O.R. Resident: JAMES J. TIESINGA, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: G. Richard Dickersin, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), SPECIMEN #1 PART B: BREAST (LEFT), SPECIMEN #2 "LATERAL" \u000a[report_end] 
