VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: UpdatedType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist: None Frozen Section Resident: None Frozen Section Consultant(s): None Consulting Pathologist(s): None Assigned Resident/Path: Pavan K Auluck, M.D., Ph.D. Reports To: MICHELLE C SPECHT, M.D. ********** Addended Report *********** Reason for Addendum #1: Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum #2: Additional Tissue Processed Reason for Addendum #3: Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA: Status post left breast biopsy: DCIS, ER/PR positive, with strong family history. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, SCATTERED FOCI, ADJACENT TO AND AWAY FROM THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE. TINY CLUSTER OF ATYPICAL CELLS IN A LYMPHATIC VESSEL ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY SITE (SEE NOTE). FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. NOTE: There is a cluster of 3 atypical cells within a lymphatic space which is suspicious for but not diagnostic of carcinoma. The differential for these cells includes histiocytes, as there are other lymphatic vessels containing histiocytes in the same region. However, the atypical cells have a higher nuclear to cytoplasmic ratio and sharper cell borders, making them suspicious for epithelial cells. They are not present on the deeper section, and therefore, additional studies cannot be performed. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, SENTINEL), EXCISION: METASTATIC CARCINOMA CELLS IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES (ISOLATED TUMOR CELLS) (SEE NOTE). NOTE: There are scattered single cells and small clusters of cells (up to 6 cells) present in the lymph node sinuses which are evident on both HE and keratin immunostained sections, totalling about 45 cells. The cytologic features are consistent carcinoma; Dr. David Wilbur concurs with this interpretation. Studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and Her2/neu will be attempted and the results will be reported in an addendum. SKIN (LEFT BREAST ADDITIONAL), EXCISION: SKIN AND SUBCUTANEOUS FAT WITH FAT NECROSIS, HEMORRHAGE, AND FIBROSIS. BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: MILDLY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, COLUMNAR CELL TYPE, SCATTERED FOCI. MILD FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 3 OF 3 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES. LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLA, SENTINEL), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES (SEE NOTE). NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. SKIN (RIGHT BREAST ADDITIONAL), EXCISION: NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast", is an 850 gram, 26 x 18 x 3.5cm simple mastectomy specimen with axillary tail measuring 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm  There is a 4 x 3cm skin ellipse centered around the nipple on the anterior surface. The anterior surface is dark yellow, fatty with no areas of puckering. The posterior surface is yellow-red, smooth and glistening. The anterior resection margin is inked blue; the posterior resection margin is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal predominantly dense fibrous breast tissue surrounded peripherally by yellow unremarkable fat. No discrete lesions or otherwise suspicious areas are identified. The axillary tail is dissected to reveal three potential lymph nodes. Representative sections of the breast parenchyma including the deep margin are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The three potential lymph nodes are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast sentinel node", are two pieces of fibrous tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm respectively. The larger specimen is inked black. Both pieces of tissue are bisected to reveal fleshy pink cut surface. Both specimens are submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast", is an 840 gram, 24 x 17 x 3.8cm simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm axillary tail. On the anterior surface, there is a REMOVED_DATE x 3.1cm skin ellipse centered around the areola. Located 2.5cm medial to the skin ellipse, and 5.4cm from the medial edge, is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE biopsy cavity that is exposed on the anterior surface. The biopsy cavity extends 2.8cm deep. The remainder of the breast tissue on the anterior surface is dark yellow and fatty. The posterior surface of the breast is yellow and red, smooth and glistening. The anterior surface is inked blue, the posterior surface is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal that the biopsy cavity is 3.5cm deep and extends to 0.3cm of the posterior margin. The breast tissue medial to the biopsy cavity is predominantly fatty. The breast tissue surrounding the biopsy cavity is dense and fibrotic. There is a palpable area of dense tissue measuring 0.5cm in diameter located 0.5cm superior to the biopsy cavity. The breast tissue lateral to the biopsy cavity is dense, fibrous and unremarkable. The axillary tail is dissected to reveal no potential lymph nodes. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Firm nodule adjacent to biopsy cavity.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin with respect to biopsy cavity.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy cavity with respect to anterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional representative sections of the biopsy cavity.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional representative sections of breast parenchyma focusing on areas of increased density. This specimen was re-examined and additional sections submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with emphasis on tissue from the region of the prior biopsy site. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left axilla sentinel node and right axillary node" (Dr. Specht contacted, and the specimen is verified as left axilla sentinel node). The specimen is a piece of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm  The specimen is dissected to reveal two potential lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm respectively. The larger lymph node is inked blue and bisected to reveal yellow-tan cut surface. The smaller lymph node is not bisected. Both lymph nodes are submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remaining fatty tissue is submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional right breast tissue", are two triangular pieces of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm respectively. The surface of the skin is pink, smooth and unremarkable. The deep resection margins are red, smooth and glistening without any nodularity. The deep resection margins are inked black. Both specimens are radially sectioned, and the pieces are submitted in toto with one specimen as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the second as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional left breast tissue", are two pieces of tissue, one which is triangular measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  and the other irregularly shaped measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  The surface of the skin is pink, smooth and unremarkable. The deep resection margin is dark red, glistening and unremarkable. The deep resection margin is inked black. Both pieces are radially sectione