ating furthest from biopsy, medial aspect. The medial aspect is inked black and the opposing aspect is inked blue. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal tan-yellow to white fibrofatty tissue, with minimal cystic change. The specimen is submitted in its entirely in cassettes I-M. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast final shaved margins-lateral aspect" are 2 tan-yellow to white, irregular fibrofatty tissues measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm  each with a suture designating the lateral aspect. The lateral aspect of each is inked black and the opposing aspect is inked blue. Each portion is serially sectioned to reveal a tan-yellow to white fibrofatty tissue. The specimens are submitted in their entirety as N-S, with the smaller portion in N-P and the larger in Q-S. Gross Description by: BRAD MOSBURG Resident: JOHN BISSONNETTE, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST(RIGHT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST (RIGHT MEDIAL), FINAL SHAVED MARGINS PART C: BREAST (RIGHT LATERAL), FINAL SHAVED MARGINS 
