s extends to 5.5cm to the deep resection margin, 9.0cm to the inferior resection margin, and 13.0cm to the superior margin. There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ill-defined area, underneath the superior surgical scar, with fat necrosis which extends to 7.0cm to the deep resection margin, 12.0cm to the superior resection margin, and 14.0cm to the inferior resection marign. The remaining breast parenchyma is mostly fatty and contains focal fibrous areas. Section code: A-D: the inferior biopsy cavity E-H: superior biopsy cavity I,J: fibrous areas K-O: axillary lymph nodes Labeled "additional axillary tissue" are multiple fragments of adipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm in aggregate; submitted entirely in cassette P. The third specimen, labeled "left breast" weighs 875 grams in toto and consists of three parts. Labeled "left lateral breast" are four fragments of fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6.5cm in toto. The largest fragment displays an attached REMOVED_DATE x 7.0cm piece of unremarkable skin. Sectioning of the breast parenchyma reveals unremarkable fibrofatty surfaces. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes Q, R,U and V. Labeled "left medial breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm piece of unremarkable fibrofatty tissue over-lined by a REMOVED_DATE x 5.0cm unremarkable piece of skin. Representative section is submitted in cassette S, W, and X . Labeled "left central breast" are two fragments of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm  respectively. Representative sections from each are submitted in cassette T, Y and Z. Resident: CHIN-LEE WU, MD, PhD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. Michael J Yaremchuk, M.D. PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B: SOFT TISSUE (AXILLARY) PART C: BREAST (LEFT), REDUCTION \u000a[report_end] 
