n cassettes B-E from superior to inferior and the inferior end is submitted in cassette F. Please note that greater than 90% of the specimen is submitted. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "intramammary lymph nodes from biopsy cavity" are two gray lymph nodes with a moderate amount of attached focally cauterized soft tissue, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  Each is bisected and submitted in its entirety in cassettes G-H. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number and "right axillary contents" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm portion of adipose tissue from which multiple lymph nodes are identified ranging from 0.3cm in greatest dimension up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm  Representative sections of these lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes I-O. Gross Description by: JANINE L. DUDAC Resident: STUART HOUSER, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), RE-EXCISION PART B: LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLA), EXCISION PART C: LYMPH NODES (INTRAMAMMARY), EXCISION \u000a[report_end] 
