 the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Atul Kumar Bhan, M.D. Signed On: 31 AUG 00 at 14:31 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and no designation as to site, is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm portion of breast with a long suture designating lateral margin, a short suture designating superior margin and a thick portion of a needle localization wire, inked as follows: anterior inked blue, posterior inked black, medial in red and lateral in yellow. Sections from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm  ill-demarcated irregular shaped, tan-white firm mass with two foci of calcification measuring 0.1cm in diameter, which comes to the inked anterior margin and within 0.5cm of the closest medial margin. Also identified is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ill-demarcated, tan-white rubbery lesion which comes to the inked posterior margin. During sectioning, the incision is noted from the anterior margin to the specimen and held together by an additional suture. The specimen is submitted entirely and serially in cassettes A-H. (Firm mass in cassettes C-E, rubbery lesion in cassette H). Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left breast final shaved margin" are five fragments of fibrofatty tissue measuring from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm to REMOVED_DATE x2.8 x 0.8cm  Two of them are inked black and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm cyst which comes to within 0.1cm of the closest inked margin. The specimen is submitted entirely and serially in cassettes I-O and P and remaining fragments are submitted in cassettes Q-R. Resident: Mari Mino, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-OUTPATIENT (OFF.P/CLINIC) REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (FINAL MARGIN), EXCISION 
