h marks 12 0'clock. Specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm poorly circumscribed yellow tan firm area which is 1.5cm from the inferior margin and abuts the anterior skin ellipse. The firm area is more than 4.0cm from all other resection margins. Multiple cysts ranging in size from 0.2cm to 0.7cm in diameter are identified within the firm area. Representative tissue is submitted. SECTION CODE: A: Posterior deep margin. B: Inferior resection margin. C: Firm area in relation to skin. D: Representative sections of nipple. E-L: Representative sections of the firm area (cystic in G-J). Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "modified radical mastectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 12.0cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 25 x 11cm tan skin ellipse and intact nipple. A REMOVED_DATE x 5.5cm scar with a REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm surface defect exposing an underlying cavity is present on the posterior resection margin. A stitch marks 12 o'clock. The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm biopsy cavity abutting the posterior margin. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5.0cm tan firm ill defined area is present beneath this cavity, which is more than 3.0cm from all inked margins. Representative tissue is submitted. SECTION CODE: M-N: Biopsy cavity in relation to the posterior resection margin. O-Q: Anterior wall of biopsy cavity. R-T: Representative sections of the mass. U: Representative sections of well circumscribed firm area at the superior margin, midline. V: Lymph node isolated from the lateral end of the specimen. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left inferior additional margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm tan skin ellipse, excised to a depth of 3.0cm  Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm fragment of adipose tissue. The specimen is serially sectioned and unremarkable. Representative sections are submitted in W-FF. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left axillary sentinel node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm tan-red soft tissue fragment, containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm lymph node. The lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and submitted in GG and HH. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left axilla sentinel node #2", are 2 lymph nodes, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in II. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left additional axillary content", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm adipose tissue. Dissection of the specimen reveals one lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm which is bisected and entirely submitted in JJ. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right axillary tail", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm adipose tissue, which is bisected to reveal multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm  Small lymph nodes are entirely submitted in cassette KK, two larger lymph nodes are bisected and entirely submitted in LL and MM. Resident: SONER ALTIOK, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS 1: LYMPH NODE, SENTINEL, LEFT AXILLARY: METASTATIC CARCINOMA. GROSS DIAGNOSIS 1: BREAST, RIGHT: NO OBVIOUS GROSS TUMOR. O.R. Resident: Mari Mino, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Robert Henry Young, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B: BREAST (LEFT, INFERIOR ADDITIONAL MARGIN) PART C