ectomy specimen with a short stitch superior and a long stitch lateral. The attached REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm skin ellipse contains a 3.1cm areola with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm unremarkable nipple. There is a 7.0cm linear scar on the skin surface, 0.1cm from the superior/medial edge. The anterior is inked blue and the posterior is inked black. Sectioning reveals dense, tan-pink rubbery fibrous tissue within the lateral one half of the specimen. The remaining breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable. No masses or lesions are identified. Representative sections of breast parenchyma are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  from lateral to medial ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  includes posterior margin and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  includes anterior margin). Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional superficial tissue left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm aggregate of tan-yellow lobulated soft tissue. The specimen is sectioned and no lesions or masses are identified. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional inferior tissue left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm unoriented portion of tan-pink and yellow lobulated soft tissue. The specimen is sectioned to reveal a homogenous tan-pink-yellow lobulated cut surface with no lesions or masses identified. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left axillary sentinel node # REMOVED_CASE_ID ", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a 1.5cm lymph node. The lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX#1 and now submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remaining tissue is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right modified radical mastectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6.0cm right modified radical mastectomy specimen with a short stitch superior and a long stitch lateral. The attached REMOVED_DATE x 3.8cm skin ellipse contains a 3.8cm areola with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm unremarkable nipple. The anterior is inked blue, the posterior is inked black. The specimen is sectioned to reveal dense, tan-white, rubbery fibrous tissue within the lateral one half of the specimen. This dense tissue comes to within 1.0cm from the closest anterior margin and 1.5cm from the closest posterior margin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of tan-yellow lobulated adipose tissue and white fibrous tissue. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Small nodular area near axillary tail.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of the dense fibrous tissue from the lateral half of the specimen submitted from lateral to medial ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  includes representative sections of the posterior margin and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains representative sections of the anterior margin).  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of fibrous tissue from the medial aspect of the specimen.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lymph nodes from the axillary tail. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional right axillary tissue", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm tan-pink-yellow soft tissue. Two possible lymph nodes are dissected from the specimen and submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remaining adipose tissue is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1; LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL), BIOPSY: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Gross Dictation by Aashiyana F Koreishi M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Aashiyana F Koreishi M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B: BREAST (LEFT ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (LEFT ADDITIONAL INFERIOR), EXCISION PART D: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"# REMOVED_CASE_ID ), EXCISION PART E: BREAST (RIGHT), MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART F: BREAST (RIGHT ADDITIONAL AXILLA), D [report_end] 
