VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE: 05 REMOVED_MONTH 99 ACCESSIONED ON: 05 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 15:09 CLINICAL DATA: 53 year old woman with known 8mm focus of invasive ductal carcinoma with positive margins and lymphovascular invasion (specimen reviewed at Brigham and Women's Hospital). Re-excision right breast lesion with axillary node biopsies. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), RE-EXCISION: LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, PRESENT AT THE INFERO-LATERAL RESECTION MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN. (SEE NOTE). HEALING BIOPSY SITE. NOTE: Invasion of the stroma, lymphatic vessels and blood vessels is not present. BREAST (RIGHT, ADDITIONAL MARGIN), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWO OF TWO LYMPH NODES. (SEE NOTE). NOTE: No keratin positive tumor cells are present on immunoperoxidase-stained serial level sections. LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLA, "NON-SENTINEL"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE. Diagnosis by: EDI BROGI, MD, PhD Signed On: 12 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 08:33 Consulting Pathologist(s): Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right sentinel node" are two fragments of yellow fatty tissue, REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0.5cm and 1 x 1 x 0.9cm  Two lymph nodes are dissected from this tissue and entirely frozen as FX #1 and #2, now cassettes A and B. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right axillary non-sentinel node" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm portion of adipose tissue containing a possible lymph node, entirely submitted in cassette C. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast, re-excision, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.4cm portion of yellow/pink fibroadipose tissue. A short stitch marks the superior margin and a long stitch marks the lateral margin. The specimen is inked black overall with additional colors as follows: blue, anterior; yellow, medial; and green, lateral. Serial sections show predominantly white fibrous tissue with no discrete mass. Entirely submitted. D : Superior margin E-S: Cross sections of specimen superior to inferior T: Inferior margin Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right breast, additional margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue. The suture placed by the surgeon marks the aspect furthest from the tumor. This aspect is inked black. Serial sections show white fibro-glandular tissue admixed with smaller amounts of yellow adipose tissue with no grossly suspicious areas. Entirely submitted in cassettes U-W. Resident: STACEY L. MIKESELL, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** Frozen section diagnoses #1,2 (Sentinel lymph nodes, right axilla): There is no evidence of malignancy. O.R. Resident: GARY LETTS, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Andrew Eric Rosenberg, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE, RIGHT AXILLA PART B: NON-SENTINEL LYMPH NODE, RIGHT AXILLA PART C: RIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION PART D: RIGHT BREAST, ADDITIONAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
