VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: UpdatedType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery, WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist: None Frozen Section Resident: None Frozen Section Consultant(s): None Consulting Pathologist(s): None Assigned Resident/Path: Melinda J Lerwill, M.D. Reports To: BARBARA LYNN SMITH, M.D. ********** Addended Report *********** Reason for Addendum #1: Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum #2: Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA: Left breast DCIS, residual calcifications, MRI densities on lateral aspect. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION: 1. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU. SEE TABLE #1. 2. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). 3. ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, FOCAL. 4. SCLEROSING PAPILLOMA. 5. PROLIFERATIVE FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. 6. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU TUMOR SIZE: Involving 8 of 10 sequential blocks and thus estimated to span about 6cm  GRADE: 1 and 2. CALCIFICATIONS: In the carcinoma in-situ and in benign changes. MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU: Ductal carcinoma in-situ extends to less than 0.1cm from the medial and anterior margins of the specimen, to 0.15cm from the superior margin, and to 0.17cm from the posterior margin. STAINS FOR RECEPTORS: Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . BREAST (LEFT, INFERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU. BREAST (LEFT, MEDIAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). BREAST (LEFT, SUPERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). BREAST (LEFT, DEEP FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU. BREAST (LEFT, LATERAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), EXCISION: DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU. LOBU