IA. 4. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. 5. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. NOTE: Evidence of invasive carcinoma is not identified. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU TUMOR SIZE: Involving 9 of 22 blocks. GRADE: 1 to focal 2. MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU: The distances to all margins measure 0.2cm or greater. STAINS FOR RECEPTORS: Not indicated; see specimen  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right axillary nodes, hot & blue, #543 and #468," is a tan-pink \u005c yellow, lobulated soft tissue with two lymph nodes, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm  Each lymph node is frozen separately as FX#1 & 1A and now submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , respectively. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left axillary sentinel node, hot & blue, # REMOVED_CASE_ID  and #660," is a single REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5-cm lymph node which is bisected and frozen entirely as FX#2 and now submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left axillary sentinel nodes, blue," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7-cm lymph node which is entirely frozen as FX#3 and now submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.5-cm simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 11.5-cm tan-pink skin ellipse containing a REMOVED_DATE x 3.5-cm areola with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2-cm, grossly unremarkable nipple. On the skin surface adjacent to the areola is a 3.5-cm curved scar that extends from 6