e with a needle localization wire in place. The tissue is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a poorly demarcated, soft, white and blue fibrous area with surrounding hemorrhagic foci. The largest dimension of this area is 0.6cm  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes A-C, E. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "B, skin tag, right chest", is a tan REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.1cm piece of tissue. The entire specimen is submitted in cassette D. Resident: TRACY L. DAVIS, MD., Ph.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: BREAST(RIGHT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: SKIN(RIGHT CHEST),EXCISION 
