losest posterior margin to first nodule and representative section of fibrous parenchyma. C: second firm nodular area to posterior margin D-J: representative sections of parenchyma from medial to lateral with posterior margin in G and anterior margin in H. Within the small portion of axillary fat rare lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0.3cm in greatest dimension, and they are submitted in their entirety in K, along with a representative portion of skin. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.8cm mastectomy with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm portion of axillary fat. There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 16.5cm tan wrinkled skin ellipse with a eccentric 2.8cm unremarkable nipple. There is a short stitch on the superior aspect and a long stitch on the axillary sampling. The skin is notable for a 3.5cm linear well healed scar in the lateral, inferior portion. This overlies a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm fibrotic area within the parenchyma that is 0.3cm from the inferior deep margin. The remainder of the parenchyma is moderately fibrous but contains no discrete masses. The entire fibrous area beneath the scar is submitted in L-P with posterior margin in L-O and anterior margin in P. Representative sections of fibrous parenchyma are submitted from lateral to medial in Q-W with posterior ink in Q-R and anterior ink in S. Within the small segment of axillary fat several lymph nodes are identified ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1.1cm in greatest dimension. Whole nodes are in X-Y, representative sections of nodes are in Z. Resident: MELINDA J. FAN, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** GROSS DIAGNOSIS #1: BREAST (LEFT): NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS SEEN. O.R. Resident: TAN A. INCE, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Ben Zion Pilch, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNO