VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE: 15 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON: 15 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 11:58 CLINICAL DATA: DCIS - LCIS on right biopsy, left prophylactic mastectomy. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY and AXILLARY LYMPH NODE SAMPLING: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA). FIBROADENOMA AND MILD FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. SEE NOTE. NOTE: No lymph nodes are identified in the axillary sample. BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY and AXILLARY LYMPH NODE SAMPLING: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU). MILD FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 3 EXAMINED AXILLARY LYMPH NODES. Diagnosis by: Dennis Sgroi, M.D. Signed On: 22 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 15:42 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, and "left" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm mastectomy with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm fragment of axillary fat. There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 5.5cm tan wrinkled skin ellipse with an eccentric unremarkable 3.0cm nipple. There is a short stitch on the superior aspect and a long stitch on the lateral aspect and a stitch on the axillary tail. In the medial portion of the specimen there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm tan white rubbery well circumscribed, nodule that is 0.7cm from the posterior-inferior margin. There is a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm tan white round, well circumscribed firm area that is 0.5cm from the superior posterior margin. The remainder of the parenchyma is grossly unremarkable. Representative sections are submitted as follows: A: first nodule in its entirety B: closest posterior margin to first nodule and representative section of fibrous parenchyma. C: second firm nodular area to posterior margin D-J: representative sections of parenchyma from medial to lateral with posterior margin in G and anterior margin in H. Within the small portion of axillary fat rare lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0.3cm in greatest dimension, and they are submitted in their entirety in K, along with a representative portion of skin. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.8cm mastectomy with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm portion of axillary fat. There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 16.5cm tan wrinkled skin ellipse with a eccentric 2.8cm unremarkable nipple. There is a short stitch on the superior aspect and a long stitch on the axillary sampling. The skin is notable for a 3.5cm linear well healed scar in the lateral, inferior portion. This overlies a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm fibrotic area within the parenchyma that is 0.3cm from the inferior deep margin. The remainder of the parenchyma is moderately fibrous but contains no discrete masses. The entire fibrous area beneath the scar is submitted in L-P with posterior margin in L-O and anterior margin in P. Representative sections of fibrous parenchyma are submitted from lateral to medial in Q-W with posterior ink in Q-R and anterior ink in S. Within the small segment of axillary fat several lymph nodes are identified ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1.1cm in greatest dimension. Whole nodes are in X-Y, representative sections of nodes are in Z. Resident: MELINDA J. FAN, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** GROSS DIAGNOSIS #1: BREAST (LEFT): NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS SEEN. O.R. Resident: TAN A. INCE, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Ben Zion Pilch, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNO