ostained levels. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, ?SENTINEL # 3, COUNT 620?), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE (0/1) (SEE NOTE AND SEE TABLE # 2). NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, ?SENTINEL # 4, COUNT 138?), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE (0/1) (SEE NOTE AND SEE TABLE # 2). NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS # 2 SUMMARY OF THE LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES: 1. TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED: 4. Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0.02cm or less (isolated tumor cells): 1. Number of lymph nodes with metastases >0.02cm to 0.2cm (micrometastases): 0. Number of lymph nodes with metastases >0.2cm (macrometastases): 0. Method of detection: Cytokeratin immunohistochemistry. Extracapsular extension: None. Other forms of axillary involvement: None. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled Dale Dennen, #378-00-91 and "left breast lumpectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm portion of gray-white to tan-pink fibrofatty tissue with a localization wire in place. A short black stitch designates the anterior margin, a long black stitch designates the lateral margin and a bowtie stitch designates the cephalad margin. The posterior margin is inked black, the anterior margin is inked blue, the superior/cephalad margin is inked green, and the inferior margin is inked yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm indurated gray-white mass at the level of the localization wire and silver metal clip. The mass is 0.3cm from the superior margin, 0.7cm from the posterior margin, 0.8cm from the anterior margin, and greater than 2.0cm from the other resection margins. The remaining breast parenchyma cut surface displays diffuse dense gray-white fibrous tissue with no other discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities. Representative sections of the specimen are submitted from medial to lateral as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with the medial end margin (en face) as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , the lateral end margin (en face) as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the entire mass as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received are 4 containers, which are all labeled Dale Dennen, #378-00-91. Received in formalin, labeled "left axillary sentinel node #1, count 358", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm tan-pink lymph node with 0.5cm attached tan-yellow lobulated adipose tissue. The lymph node is dissected, serially sectioned, and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left axillary sentinel node # 2, count 139", is a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm single lymph node with minimally attached tan-yellow lobulated adipose tissue. The lymph node is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left axillary sentinel node #3, count 620", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm tan-pink lymph node with minimally attached tan-yellow lobulated adipose tissue. The node is trisected and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left axillary sentinel node #4, count 138", is a 1 x 1 x 0.3cm aggregate of tan-yellow lobulated adipose tissue from which a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm single lymph node is dissected, then bisected and submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: Breast (Left), Excision PART B: Lymph Node (Left Axilla, "Sentinel" count 358), Excision PART C: Lymph Node (Left Axilla, "Sentinel" count 139), 