e nodules or masses, however much of the breast parenchyma is replaced by diffuse fibrous bands which traverse the specimen, aggregating approximately to REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm and grossly abutting the black inked resection margin on the anterior superior aspect of the upper outer quadrant. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm focally hemorrhagic area is encountered in the inner lower quadrant and adjacent to this area is a diffuse blue tinged parenchyma and a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm cystic cavity, located in the upper outer quadrant. Representative sections are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE: B: anterior skin and fibrous area in upper inner quadrant. C-D: additional representative sections of parenchyma and upper inner quadrant. E: biopsy cavity in lower inner quadrant. F-G: additional sections of lower inner quadrant. H: additional section of biopsy site. I: blue tinged parenchyma in upper outer quadrant. J-K: additional sections of upper outer quadrant with J containing ? biopsy cavity. L-N: representative sections of lower outer quadrant. O-R: ? biopsy cavity. Resident: CHRISTINE GARCIA, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1, LYMPH NODE (AXILLARY SENTINEL): CARCINOMA NOT IDENTIFIED. O.R. Resident: LAN WANG, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Ben Zion Pilch, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. Michael J Yaremchuk, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, SENTINEL) PART B: BREAST (LEFT), MASTECTOMY 
