VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Updated Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery, WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-2 Results To: MICHELLE C SPECHT, M.D. Frozen Section Pathologist: Joshua Kish, M.D. Frozen Section Resident: Adriana Dionigi, M.D. Signed Out by: Melinda J Lerwill, M.D. ********** Addended Report *********** Reason for Addendum #1: Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA: Left breast cancer. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION: 1. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU WITH FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR MICROINVASION. SEE NOTE AND TABLE #1. 2. INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMAS. 3. PROLIFERATIVE FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. 4. RADIAL SCAR. 5. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. NOTE: A small gland in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  raises concern for microinvasion, but due to its proximity to the biopsy site, the possibility it represents mechanically-displaced epithelium cannot be entirely excluded. The focus is no longer present on deeper immunostained sections or levels. Immunostains for p63, calponin, SM-MHC, and cytokeratin support that the remainder of the carcinoma is in-situ. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU TUMOR SIZE: Spanning at least 1.9cm  GRADE: 3. CALCIFICATIONS: In the carcinoma in-situ and in benign changes. MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU: The distances to all margins measure 0.2cm or greater. STAINS FOR RECEPTORS: Requested (as there is concern for microinvasion, Her-2/neu will be requested on the DCIS in addition to ER and PR). BREAST (LEFT, FINAL ANTERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL LATERAL MARGIN), EXCISION: 1. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, GRADE 1, SPANNING ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM AND >0.2 CM FROM THE NEW MARGIN. SEE NOTE. 2. MILDLY ATYPICAL APOCRINE HYPERPLASIA. 3. MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED. NOTE: The ductal carcinoma in-situ involves a fibroadenoma. As this focus of ductal carcinoma in-situ is morphologically distinct from the high-grade ductal carcinoma in-situ in the main excision, ER/PR studies will be separately requested and reported in an addendum. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN), EXCISION: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). BREAST (LEFT, FINAL POSTERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA AND 2 LYMPH NODES WITH NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION: ISOLATED TUMOR CELLS IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE, SEE TABLE #2. NOTE: Tumor is not present on the frozen section slide. TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS # 2 SENTINEL LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES: 1 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED: 1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0.02cm or less (isolated tumor cells): 1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases >0.02cm to 0.2cm (micrometastases): 0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases >0.2cm (macrometastases): 0 Method of detection: Cytokeratin immunohistochemistry highlights a small cluster of tumor cells present on 2 levels; rare suspicious cells are seen on the permanent H&E. Extracapsular extension: None. Other forms of axillary involvement: None. NOTE: The resection margins of the specimens were inked and microscopically evaluated. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled Forouz Brooks, #411-86-81 and "left breast", is a ragged, yellow, lobulated, focally friable portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm  received with a needle localization wire in place and accompanied by a radiograph. There is a short suture denoting the "superior" aspect and a long suture denoting the "lateral" aspect of the specimen, as per the surgeon. The specimen is inked for orientation as follows: superior- green, inferior- yellow, anterior-blue, and posterior- black. Sectioning reveals a ragged, hemorrhagic cavity (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm ) containing white, gritty material, consistent with packing material. This area is consistent with a previous biopsy site and is located 0.4cm from the anterior aspect, 1.0cm from the superior aspect, 0.6cm from the posterior aspect, 1.0cm from the medial aspect, and focally abutting the inferolateral aspect of the specimen. The remaining cut surfaces consist of fibrous, focally nodular tissue with a scant amount of yellow, lobulated adipose tissue. The specimen is submitted in toto in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial end.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body, submitted sequentially from medial to lateral (each cassette contains one half of a full thickness section).  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, serially sectioned. Received are six containers, which are all labeled Forouz Brooks, #411-86-81. Received in formalin, labeled "left breast anterior final margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm portion of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the "new" margin. The surface containing the stitch is inked black; specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast final lateral margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm portion of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the "new" margin". The surface containing the stitch is inked black; specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast final medial margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm portion of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the "new" margin. The surface containing the stitch is inked black, serially sectioned to reveal tan-white, rubbery fibrous tissue with occasional cystic spaces filled with clear fluid. The entire specimen is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast final posterior margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm portion of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the "new" margin. The surface containing the stitch is inked black, specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast final inferior margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm portion of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the "new" margin. The surface containing the stitch is inked black, specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast final superior margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm portion of portion of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the "new" margin. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled Forouz Brooks, #411-86-81 and "left axillary sentinel node", is a 1.3cm lymph node, bisected and entirely submitted for frozen as FX#1, now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION # 1; (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA. Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: # 1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The ductal carcinoma in-situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein. The ductal carcinoma in-situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein. The ductal carcinoma in-situ tumor cells show strong (3+) overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Breast (Left, Final Lateral Margin, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The ductal carcinoma in-situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The ductal carcinoma in-situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. See note. Note: Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) HER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation; the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows: Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) Show strong (3+) overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test?s accuracy and precision. Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (LEFT, FINAL ANTERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (LEFT, FINAL LATERAL MARGIN), EXCISION PART D: BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN), EXCISION PART E: BREAST (LEFT, FINAL POSTERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION PART F: BREAST (LEFT, FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN), EXCISIO [report_end] 
