sentative sections of lower inner quadrant. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast scar tissue", are three tan-white rubbery irregular fragments of fibrous-fatty tissue, ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm  The tissues are inked black, and the specimens are serially sectioned. No lesions or masses are appreciated. The specimen is submitted in its entirety as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Two smaller tissues.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Larger tissue. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left peri-areolar skin", are two strips of gray tan skin, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm  The margins are inked black, and the fragments are submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Gross Dictation by Tara A Shea, on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B: BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART C: SOFT TISSUE (LEFT BREAST), EXCISION PART D: SKIN (LEFT PERIAREOLAR), EXCISION 
