VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE: 29 AUG 01 ACCESSIONED ON: 29 AUG 01 at 13:17 CLINICAL DATA: Biopsy left breast-density. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH APOCRINE MACROCYST; THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST ("RIGHT BREAST MASS"), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU), INVOLVING A SINGLE LOBULE. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. Diagnosis by: Dennis Sgroi, M.D. Signed On: 05 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 14:13 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left breast" are two sections of yellow fatty tissue the first is a round 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm oriented specimen with a guide wire through the middle. A long stitch demarking the lateral position and the short stitch marking the superior position. The second tissue piece is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm nodule with attached fat. The oriented specimen was inked as followed: anterior-black, posterior-blue, inferior-green. The specimen was serially sectioned from lateral to medial revealing ill-defined fibrofatty white tissue abutting all inked margins. It was submitted in toto in cassette B-D. The second smaller unoriented tissue was bisected to reveal a fluid filled fleshy white anterior and the specimen was entirely submitted in cassette A. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right breast mass", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm red-yellow fatty section of tissue with no unorientation. The specimens surface is inked black and the specimen was bisected revealing fluid filled microcysts. The specimen was submitted in toto in cassette E. Resident: DAVID COON, MD ================