SION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Additional sections in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast", is a 530 grams, 24 x 14 x 5cm aggregate of multiple portions of fibroadipose breast tissue partially surfaced by light tan grossly unremarkable skin. The tissue is serially sectioned to reveal approximately 20% fibrous tissue and 80% adipose tissue. The breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable. Representative sections of the fibrous tissue are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Additional sections in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Gross Dictation by Julia Turbiner M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: Additional tissue sections were submitted for histologic examination. In the left breast, a focus of severely atypical ductal hyperplasia bordering on low-grade ductal carcinoma in-situ is identified ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), spanning just over 0.1cm  Additional sections of the right breast are non-contributory. Additional section code:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Right breast  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Left breast Addendum #1 by Kristina Braaten M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), MAMMOPLASTY PART B: BREAST (LEFT), MAMMOPLASTY 
