VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: UpdatedType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  CALNAN Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist: Melinda J Lerwill, M.D. Frozen Section Resident: Norma Rodriguez, M.D. Frozen Section Consultant(s): None Consulting Pathologist(s): None Assigned Resident/Path: Darryl A Oble, M.D., Ph.D. Reports To: JANEY SUE PRATT, M.D. ********** Addended Report *********** Reason for Addendum #1: Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA: Left breast lumpectomy. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION: PHYLLODE TUMOR, HIGH GRADE, WITH EXTENSIVE STROMAL OVERGROWTH AND NECROSIS AND EXTENDING TO BETWEEN REMOVED_DATE AND REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERIOR AND INFERIOR MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN IN SMALL FOCI. NOTE: The tumor cells stain for vimentin. The do not stain for wide spectrum keratin, keratin 903, keratin, smooth muscle actin, desmin, HMB-45, MART-1, or S-100 protein. Electron microscopy is non-contributory. BREAST (LEFT, "FINAL SHAVED MARGIN"), EXCISION: ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF PHYLLODES TUMOR. SEE NOTE. NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast mass", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5.0cm round, firm, tan-pink soft tissue mass. A short stitch has been placed to designate the superior resection margin, and a long stitch has been placed to designate the lateral resection margin of the specimen. A bow-tie stitch has been placed; however, the suture was received unattached to the specimen. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior-black, posterior-blue, superior-green, inferior-yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a well circumscribed partially gelatinous, partially necrotic cut surface. A 0.15cm rim of fibrous tissue encapsulates the mass. The mass is located 0.3cm from the blue inked margin, <0.1cm from the green inked margin, 0.1cm from the black inked margin, and 0.5cm from the yellow inked margin. An expansion of the fibrotic capsule surrounding the tumor brings this structure in direct opposition to the yellow inked surgical margin. Representative sections of two separate areas of the mass are frozen as FX#1 and FX#1A. FX#1 is resubmitted cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . FX#1A is kept frozen. SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : FX#1 Representative section of tumor.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sections through tumor demonstrating proximity to black inked surgical margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections through the tumor demonstrates proximity to blue inked surgical margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections through tumor demonstrating proximity to yellow inked surgical margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections through tumor demonstrating proximity to green inked surgical margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional sections of the tumor Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast mass-final shaved margins", is a hollow shell of fibrofatty tissue which measures 12 x 9 x 8cm in overall dimension which has numerous sutures placed to designate the outer aspect of the specimen which represents the true surgical margin of the resection bed. The new true surgical margin is inked black and the specimen is serial sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty tissue. Representative sections of the tissue involving the black inked surgical margin are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1: LEFT BREAST MASS: MALIGNANT NEOPLASM AWAIT PERMANENTS FOR CLASSIFICATION. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1A: LEFT BREAST MASS: MALIGNANT NEOPLASM AWAIT PERMANENTS FOR CLASSIFICATION. Gross Dictation by Darryl A Oble M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Darryl A Oble M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Addendum by Atul K Bhan M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (LEFT, "FINAL SHAVED MARGIN"), EXCISION 
