VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  CALNAN Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery, WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist: None Frozen Section Resident: None Frozen Section Consultant(s): None Consulting Pathologist(s): None Assigned Resident/Path: Aleksandr Vasilyev, M.D. Reports To: JANEY SUE PRATT, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: Simple mastectomy for malignant phyllodes tumor. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: HEALING BIOPSY SITE CHANGES, INCLUDING FIBROUS SCAR. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES AND COLUMNAR CELL CHANGE. CENTRAL INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL PHYLLODES TUMOR. BREAST (LEFT, DEEP), MARGIN), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. SKIN (LEFT BREAST), EXCISION: FOCAL HEALING BIOPSY SITE. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and " left breast", is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6.0cm  837 grams, simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 4.5cm unremarkable central skin ellipse; a short stitch indicates superior and a long stitch indicates lateral. In the area just superior to the areolar skin there is an 8.0cm in largest dimension slit-like cavity extending to approximately half of the depth of the tissue. The anterior is inked blue, the posterior, black. The area of exposed cavity on the anterior aspect is inked yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a diffuse area of fibrosis in the subareolar location with interspersed small gritty nodularities. The area of fibrosis surrounds the aforementioned cavity, with focal extension to the anterior blue inked margin and to within 0.1cm from the posterior margin. The lateral and medial margins appear to be uninvolved. Representative sections of the fibrous areas are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , including a section towards the skin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , sections towards the nearest anterior margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and sections towards the nearest posterior margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Sections  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contain biopsy site. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast deep margin", are multiple fragments of unoriented tan-yellow soft tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast excess skin" are two fragments of triangular skin, REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm and REMOVED_DATE x 2.2cm  The fragments are unoriented. The skin surface and soft tissues are grossly unremarkable. A representative section of the larger fragment is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; a representative section of the smaller fragment is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B: BREAST (LEFT,DEEP MARGIN), EXCISION PART C: SKIN (LEFT BREAST), EXCISION 
