 to within 0.1cm from the posterior margin. The lateral and medial margins appear to be uninvolved. Representative sections of the fibrous areas are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , including a section towards the skin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , sections towards the nearest anterior margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and sections towards the nearest posterior margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Sections  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contain biopsy site. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast deep margin", are multiple fragments of unoriented tan-yellow soft tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast excess skin" are two fragments of triangular skin, REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm and REMOVED_DATE x 2.2cm  The fragments are unoriented. The skin surface and soft tissues are grossly unremarkable. A representative section of the larger fragment is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; a representative section of the smaller fragment is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B: BREAST (LEFT,DEEP MARGIN), EXCISION PART C: SKIN (LEFT BREAST), EXCISION 
