 assessed visually and reported as follows: - The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) - Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) - Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) - The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) HER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation; the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows: - Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) - Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) - Show strong (3+) overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 30% of tumor cells) These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test?s accuracy and precision. Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 04,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11:57:37AM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON #2: RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals (100) to chromosome 17 signals (96) in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. The results at or near the cutoff point (ranging from REMOVED_DATE - 2.2) should be interpreted with caution (Equivocal Amplification). Reference: Journal of Clinical Oncology 25:118-145,  REMOVED_CASE_ID . Addendum #2 by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 13,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12:44:42PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART : Breast (Left), Core biopsy [report_end] 
