m the lateral aspect, 7cm from the superior, 8cm from the inferior aspect, and 3.0cm from the closest posterior margin. There are other foci of smaller nodules (0.1 to 0.3cm ) adjacent to this nodule scattered within the lower inner quadrant. There is also an independent firm white nodule in the central breast measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm hemorrhagic cavity in the mid to lateral lower part of the breast. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nodule #1(largest) to margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Aggregate of smaller nodules to margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Tiny nodule to margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Aggregate of tiny nodules to margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous area to margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nodule #2 (central) to margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous area to margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of cavity.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Closest posterior margin to cavity. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left mastectomy flap", are two strips of skin measuring 25 x 2cm excised to a depth of 0.5cm and REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm excised to a depth of 0.5cm  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right mastectomy flap", are two portions of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm  Representative sections are submitted  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B: SKIN(LEFT BREAST FLAP), EXCISION PART C: SKIN (RIGHT BREAST FLAP), EXCISION [report_end] 
