ed to reveal grossly unremarkable yellow-tan lobulated tissue. The smaller fragment is submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the larger fragment entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh and labeled "final margin, anterior", is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm yellow lobulated soft tissue fragment, which is serially sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable yellow lobulated tissue. The specimen is submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh and labeled "final margin, posterior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm yellow-tan and focally hemorrhagic lobulated soft tissue fragment, which is serially sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable yellow lobulated tissue. The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh and labeled "re-excision left breast, short stitch - new inferior margin, long stitch - lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1.1cm friable fibroadipose tissue fragment with 2 orienting sutures: the short stitch designating the new inferior margin and the long stitch designating the lateral one. There is a central REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm friable and focally hemorrhagic cavity, consistent with prior surgical site: this gapping cavity communicates with the lateral, superior, and medial margins and focally communicates with the inferior margin. The specimen is reapproximated and is oriented with a medial-lateral long axis. The anterior surface is inked blue, the posterior surface is inked black, the superior surface is inked green, the inferior surface is inked yellow, and the internal cavitary surface is inked red. The specimen is sectioned to reveal focally hemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is submitted entirely as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Specimen, entirely submitted, medial to lateral (clip removed from section in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: Breast (Left), Re-Excision; Anterior/Superior margin PART B: Breast (Left, Final Margin,Inferior), Excision PART C: Breast (Left, Final Margin, Anterior), Excision PART D: Breast (Left, Final Margin, posterior), Excision PART E: Breast (Left), Re-Excision;-Anterior/Inferior/Posterior [report_end] 
