iopsy site, measuring approximately 0.2cm diameter with peripheral fat necrosis and a metal clip is found. The remainder of the specimen consists primarily of hemorrhagic fibrous breast tissue with more adipose tissue present medially. Also received in the same container is a separate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm portion of fibroadipose breast tissue which is entirely inked black externally. The specimen is entirely submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, radially.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body of the specimen; area of metal clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, radially.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Separate detached fragment, entirely. Received fresh, labeled "left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE (M-L) x REMOVED_DATE (A-P) x REMOVED_DATE (S-I)cm breast excisional biopsy specimen oriented with a short stitch superior, and a long stitch left lateral. An additional stitch with no tail is present in the anterior aspect of the specimen and holds closed a defect in the anterior surface. The external surface of the specimen consists of partially cauterized fibrous and adipose breast tissue with no focal lesions. A needle localization wire passes into the lateral aspect of the specimen, through the middle and exits through the medial aspect of the specimen. Correlation with the specimen radiograph reveals a metal clip present in the middle of the specimen approximately REMOVED_DATE of the way from the lateral to the medial margin. The specimen is inked per protocol as follows: Anterior - blue, posterior - black, superior - green, inferior - yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the long medial-lateral axis from lateral to medial. The entire middle portion of the specimen is occupied by a REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm cross-section biopsy cavity with hemorrhagic rim and peripheral fat necrosis peripheral to the biopsy affected area are small amounts of unremarkable-appearing fibroadipose 