 fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled Lisa Stoeckle, #423-91-53 & "right axillary sentinel node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  tan-pink lymph node, which is bisected and entirely frozen as FX#1 and FX#1A. The entire frozen section material in FX#1 is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and FX#1A in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled Lisa Stoeckle, #423-91-53, "right breast simple mastectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.8cm simple mastectomy specimen, partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 10.9cm irregularly-shaped fragment of tan-pink, wrinkled skin. The skin surface is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm well-healed scar, as well as a REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm everted nipple with focal white-pink areas. The specimen is received with a suture at 1 aspect denoting the 12 o'clock position. The specimen is inked for orientation as follows: Anterior - blue, posterior - black. Serial sectioning from lateral to medial reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.4cm cavity, located at the 12 o'clock position in the mid breast, subjacent to the aforementioned skin scar. This cavity comes to 3.6cm from the posterior margin and to 3.5cm from the anterior margin. Dense, nodular parenchyma with multiple clustered small cysts surrounds the biopsy site and extends beyond the biopsy site, particularly in the lateral direction. A lateral intraparenchymal lymph node and several axillary lymph nodes are identified. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative biopsy cavity with surrounding parenchyma.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative posterior margin nearest biopsy cavity.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue away from biopsy site, upper outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue away from biopsy site, upper inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, coronal section.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Axillary lymph nodes, whole.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One axillary lymph no