VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery, WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-1 Results To: BARBARA LYNN SMITH, M.D. Resident: James E. Davis, M.D. Signed Out by: Kristina Braaten, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: Pregnancy-like hyperplasia versus DCIS on biopsy, patient not pregnant. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (RIGHT), RE-EXCISION: ATYPICAL PREGNANCY-LIKE AND CYSTIC HYPERSECRETORY HYPERPLASIA, INCLUDING FEW FOCI WITH SEVERE CYTOLOGIC ATYPIA BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, WITH AND WITHOUT CALCIFICATIONS (SEE NOTE). HEALING BIOPSY SITE. HYALINIZED FIBROADENOMA. NOTE: The atypical foci are present in 13 of 20 blocks, involving about 1 lobule per tissue block, except for one identified focus which involves several adjacent lobules. This is in contrast to the prior specimens (MS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and MS-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ), in which many adjacent lobules were involved in multiple sections. So the volume of disease in the current material is significantly decreased. Atypical foci are <0.1cm from the medial margin, <0.05cm from the posterior margin, 0.1cm from the lateral margin, and 0.2cm or less from the inferior margin. However, the most severely atypical foci appear 0.2cm or more from the margins. Careful clinical follow-up seems prudent. Selected foci reviewed in consultation with Dr. Koerner. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast re-excision," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0-cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue. There is a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The long axis of the specimen is superior-inferior. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior blue, posterior black, medial green, lateral yellow. Sectioning of the specimen reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2-cm biopsy cavity with a red-brown, granular surface lining. The cavity is located 0.2cm from the closest medial margin, 0.5cm from the closest posterior margin, 0.7cm from the closest anterior margin, and >1cm from the lateral, superior, and inferior margins. SECTION CODES:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy cavity submitted entirely from superior to inferior, with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the closest medial margin, and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the closest posterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains the enface superior margin, and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains the enface inferior margin. The specimen was re-examined, and additional sections submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART : BREAST (RIGHT), RE-EXCISION [report_end] 
