opsy cavity comes within 0.6cm of the anterior margin, 0.8cm from the posterior margin, 0.9cm from the inferior margin, 0.4cm from the medial margin and 0.2cm from the lateral margin. Subjacent to the biopsy cavity there is an ill-defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm tan-yellow area, which comes within 0.2cm from the inferior margin, 1.1cm from the superior margin, 0.5cm from the anterior margin, 0.4cm from the posterior margin and 0.6cm from the lateral margin. The remaining cut surfaces are predominantly glistening yellow lobulated adipose tissue. The specimen is submitted sequentially from medial to lateral in its entirety as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin to include firm area, sectioned radially.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy cavity to include firm area in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin en face. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and " left breast additional superior tissue" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm portion of tan-pink to red fibroadipose tissue with no orientation. The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable fibrofatty cut surface. The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and " additional posterior tissue left breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm portion of tan-red fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable fibrofatty cut surface. The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and " left breast posterior cavity" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm irregular portion of fibroadipose tissue, which is not oriented. The remnant of a previously opened biopsy cavity is noted along one surface. The opposing surface is marked with black ink. On sectioning there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x0.5cm well circumscribed nodule with a soft, white cut surface, which abuts the inked margin. The remainder of tissue consists mainly of cystic, white fibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with the nodule in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Gross Dictation by Jennifer Nash, on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (LEFT, "ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR"), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (LEFT, "ADDITIONAL POSTERIOR"), EXCISION PART D: BREAST (LEFT, "POSTERIOR CAVITY"), EXCISION 
