in with green ink, and the inferior margin with yellow ink. The specimen is serially sectioned from the lateral to medial to reveal a 0.5cm in diameter cyst, 0.4cm from the lateral end. No other masses or nodules are grossly identified. The tissue consists mainly of soft, white fibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , from the lateral to the medial ends, with the cyst in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and " left breast biopsy (re-excision)" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm yellow-white ovoid fibrofatty tissue, with a localization wire, a short stitch designating superior, and a long stitch designating lateral. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior blue, posterior black, medial green, and lateral yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a cut surface consisting of yellow lobulated adipose tissue and white rubbery fibrous tissue, which is focally cystic. The cysts are filled with bloody serous fluid. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm yellow-tan granular area, within which a clip is identified. No additional lesions are appreciated. Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with area of clip within cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Note:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is the en face superior margin. Gross Dictation by Tim Robinson, on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Michael R Tan, on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The ductal carcinoma in-situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The ductal carcinoma in-situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Addendum by Atul K Bhan M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION 
