 "right breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm lobular fibrofatty breast tissue with two needle localization wires and a short stitch indicating the superior aspect and a long stitch indicating the lateral aspect. The specimen is inked as follows: medial aspect-green, lateral aspect-yellow, superior aspect-blue and inferior aspect-black. The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior. Cross section reveals predominately soft yellow lobulated fat interspersed with a small amount of firm white fibrous tissue. There are multiple foci of hemorrhage corresponding the needle-localization wires. There is a 0.1cm spherical tan-blue cyst which is 0.5cm from the lateral margin. No other discrete lesions are identified. Representative sections are submitted sequentially from the anterior margin to the posterior margin with the cyst in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the area corresponding to the calcifications in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Additional sections of fibrous areas in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm yellow-pink fibrofatty tissue, with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm white skin ellipse. There is short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral. There are four undesignated localization wires in place. This specimen is inked as follows: anterior-blue, posterior-black, medial-green, and lateral-yellow. The specimen is sequentially sectioned from inferior to superior to reveal a cut surface consisting of yellow lobulated adipose tissue and white dense fibrous tissue, with multiple cysts filled with bloody serous fluid. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm tan finely granular firm area within the tissue, which abuts the medial margin, comes to within 0.2cm of the posterior margin, comes to within 1.2cm of anterior margin, and is greater than 2cm to the remainder margins. This firm area surrounds a clip and is adjacent to a wire. No additional lesions or masses are appreciated. Representative sections are submitted sequentially from inferior to superior, with area of clip within blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Additional sections of biopsy cavity in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Sections away from biopsy cavity in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and " right breast" is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm irregular lobule of fibrofatty breast tissue. Cross section reveals predominately soft yellow lobulated fat interspersed with a small amount of dense to soft white fibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Gross Dictation by Holly A Brunner, on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Holly A Brunner, on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The in-situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The in-situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Addendum by Atul K Bhan M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (RIGHT DEEP), EXCISION 
