VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist: None Frozen Section Resident: None Frozen Section Consultant(s): None Consulting Pathologist(s): None Assigned Resident/Path: Matthew M Johnson, M.D. Reports To: MICHELLE C SPECHT, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: 31 year old female with DCIS in the left breast. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (RIGHT), MASTECTOMY: 1. FLORID FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA, APOCRINE CYSTS AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS. 2. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. (SEE NOTE). Note: Dr. F Koerner has reviewed selected slides and concurs. LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLA," SENTINEL" #696), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 3 LYMPH NODES. (SEE NOTE). Note: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on six  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. BREAST (LEFT), MASTECTOMY: 1. FLORID FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA, APOCRINE CYSTS AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS. 2. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. 3. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). 4. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU. 5. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE. NOTE: Dr. Koerner has renewed selected slides and concurs. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL" " REMOVED_CASE_ID ), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 LYMPH NODES. SEE NOTE NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on six  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and " right breast" is a 19 x REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm simple mastectomy specimen, with a grossly unremarkable nipple measuring 3.0cm in diameter, and a separate portion of circular skin measuring 3.4cm in diameter. The mastectomy is oriented with a stitch on the axillary tail, and is inked black posteriorly and blue anteriorly. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a cystic cavity containing clear to mucoid fluid. The cyst measures approximately REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm  and comes to within 1.9cm of the posterior margin. There are multiple areas of firm nodularity throughout the specimen. In the outer lower quadrant there is a small area of hard nodularity that measures 1.5cm from the posterior margin. A second firm area is also identified in the outer lower quadrant, and it is also 1.5cm in posterior margin. Some other nodular areas are identified in the central portion of the breast, >2.0cm from the posterior margin. There is another firm small area of nodularity superior to the cyst, and 2.0cm from the black inked margin. A nodular area inferior to the cyst and 2.5cm from posterior margin is identified. There is another small firm area, 1.5cm from the posterior margin and inferior to the cystic area. Representative sections are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nodularity from outer lower quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nodular areas from central aspect of the specimen.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Cystic area to posterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nodularity superior to cyst.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nodularity inferior to cyst. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and " right sentinel lymph node" is a portion of orange-pink hemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  No lymph node is grossly identified. The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and " left breast" is a 20 x 15 x 3.9cm left mastectomy specimen, with an overlying nipple measuring 3.4cm in diameter, and a separate ring of skin measuring 3.9cm in diameter. The stitch indicates the axillary tail. The specimen is inked blue anteriorly and black posteriorly. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a smooth-lined cystic cavity measuring 1.4cm in diameter, and 2.0cm from the posterior margin. The cyst contains clear fluid, and surrounding tissue shows blue ink. There are some areas of nodularity in the upper outer quadrant that measure 0.5cm or more from the posterior margin. There is another area in the lower outer quadrant of firm nodularity that measures at least 1.0cm from the black inked posterior margin. There are some nodular areas directly posterior to the nipple in the lateral aspect. A firm region is identified 1.0cm from the posterior margin in the lower inner quadrant. Further areas of nodularity are identified superior to the cyst close to the anterior margin. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nodularity from upper outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nodularity from lower outer quadrant to posterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nodularity from lower outer quadrant to anterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nodularity to nipple.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nodularity and lower inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nodularity above cystic area to anterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional sections of nodular areas. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and " left sentinal node" are two portions of orange-red hemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm  No lymph nodes are grossly identified. The larger portion is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the smaller portion in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Gross Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), MASTECTOMY PART B: LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLA, "SENTINEL" #696), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (LEFT), MASTECTOMY PART D: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL" # REMOVED_CASE_ID ), EXCISION 
