ED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm tan-yellow lymph node. The specimen is bisected and submitted entirely as FX#1, now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "sentinel lymph node #2 (blue)", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm piece of tan-pink soft tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm lymph node. The fatty tissue is removed and the lymph node is bisected and submitted entirely as FX#2, now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remaining soft tissue is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast lump", is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.4cm yellow to tan-white fibrofatty piece of breast tissue with a short stitch on the superior aspect and a long stitch on the lateral aspect. There are multiple firm nodules in the lateral and inferior aspects. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior-blue, posterior-black, superior green, inferior-yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.6cm firm, circular, tan mass which is 0.2cm from the superior margin, 1.5cm from the anterior margin, 0.9cm from the inferior margin, 2.1cm from the posterior margin, 1.5cm from the lateral margin, and 1.0cm from the medial margin. There are no other masses or lesions appreciated. Gross photos are taken. Sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, radially sectioned.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of mass from lateral to medial, showing relation to closest margins.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative tissue away from mass.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Possible nodule at the posterior-inferior-lateral aspect of specimen (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ). INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1; SENTINEL LYMPH NODE (RIGHT, 202): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF METASTATIC CARCINOMA. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #2; SENTINEL LYMPH NODE (RIGHT, BLUE): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF METASTATIC CARCINOMA. Gross Dictation by Miriam D Post M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Miriam D Post M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells show moderate (2+) overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Addendum by Atul K Bhan M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals (74) to chromosome 17 signals (68) in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. Addendum by Atul K Bhan M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Addendum #2 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION PART B: LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION PART D: CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION (SLIDE ONLY) PART E: CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION (SLIDE ONLY) 
