VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist: Gregory Y Lauwers, M.D. Frozen Section Resident: Adam J Saenz, M.D. Frozen Section Consultant(s): None Consulting Pathologist(s): None Assigned Resident/Path: Joshua Kish, M.D. Reports To: MICHELE ANNETTE GADD, M.D. JONATHAN MICHAEL WINOGRAD, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: Left breast CA. History of invasive mammary carcinoma, favored ductal type. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). HEALING BIOPSY SITE SEE NOTE. NOTE: The tumor cells do not stain for E-cadherin. Stains for calponin, p63 protein, keratin, and myosin heavy chain do not reveal invasive carcinoma. BREAST (LEFT, ?FINAL ANTERIOR MARGIN?), EXCISION: HEALING BIOPSY SITE. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. SEE NOTE. NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. SKIN (?MASTECTOMY FLAP?), EXCISION: HEALING BIOPSY SITE. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. SKIN (?MASTECTOMY SCAR?), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, ?SENTINEL?), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, ?SENTINEL?), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left sentinel lymph node", is a yellow-red to brown REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm soft tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm lymph node. The lymph node is entirely submitted for frozen section as FX#1, which is now re-submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "sentinel lymph node left axilla", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm tan-pink lymph node, which is submitted in its entirety for frozen as FX#2, now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast tissue", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm yellow-white ovoid left simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating the 12 o'clock aspect. On the anterior aspect is a REMOVED_DATE x 2.2cm ovoid white portion of skin with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm everted nipple. At the 12 o'clock aspect is a 8.0cm linear defect, extending to a depth of 3.0cm  which is partially covered by a flap of breast tissue. The defect has a pink-red granular lining. On section, the tissue surrounding this defect displays yellow chalky area of fat necrosis and focally tan-white stellate fibrous areas. This area is consistent with previous biopsy site. These fibrous areas extend to the anterior margin and are covered by the flap of breast tissue. These stellar areas come to within 1.5cm of the deep margin. No definite tumor is appreciated. The remainder of the parenchyma consists of yellow lobulated adipose tissue and white rubbery fibrous tissue. The anterior aspect is inked blue (with the exception of the area of the defect), and the posterior aspect is inked black. No lymph nodes are identified. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrotic - yellow chalky area near anterior aspect.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Closest posterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior aspect of flap.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Uninvolved section from lower outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Uninvolved tissue from lower inner quadrant. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final anterior margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm yellow-white irregular fibrofatty tissue, with two stitches designating the new margin (inked black). The specimen is submitted in its entirety in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "mastectomy flap", are two tan-white irregular portions of skin, measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm and REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm  Both tissues are excised to a depth of 1.0cm  The smaller tissue has a short stitch designating the superior and a long stitch designating the lateral aspect. The superior aspect is inked blue, the inferior aspect is inked green, and the posterior aspect is inked black. On the superior-mid aspect of the specimen the subcutaneous tissue is focally dense, white and fibrotic. The remainder of the subcutaneous tissue is yellow and fatty. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential sections of oriented portion skin from medial to lateral.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section from second portion of skin. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "mastectomy scar", is a REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm tan-white irregular, unoriented portion of skin, excised to a depth of 0.9cm  There is a focal REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm tan-yellow firm area. No additional lesions or masses are identified. Representative sections are submitted in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1; LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. FROZEN SECTION # 2; LYMPH NOES (SENTINEL), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Gross Dictation by Paul Talusan, on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Christine Garcia M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Joshua Kish M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION PART B: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART D: BREAST (LEFT, "FINAL ANTERIOR MARGIN"), EXCISION PART E: SKIN ("MASTECTOMY FLAP"), EXCISION PART F: SKIN ("MASTECTOMY SCAR"), EXCISION PART G: CRYOSTAT 
