r, and "right breast lumpectomy, one stitch superior, two stitch medial", is a 7 x 5 x 2.5cm lumpectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm skin ellipse. The skin ellipse contains a centrally located 5.4cm linear well healed scar. The remaining skin is tan and wrinkled. A suture denotes the superior portion, and two sutures denote the medial portion. The long axis is from medial to lateral. The specimen is inked as follows: posterior - black, superior - green, and inferior - yellow. The specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm defect surrounded by pink-red hemorrhagic tissue and soft discolored yellow tissue. This lesion (including the surrounding yellow tissue), is 0.6cm from the posterior margin, 2.0cm from the medial margin, 0.6cm from the lateral margin, 0.6cm from the superior margin, and 0.5cm from the inferior margin. The remaining breast parenchyma is unremarkable. The specimen is submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, radially.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, radially.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of biopsy cavity and surrounding tissue, to nearest margins, from medial to lateral.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Grossly uninvolved breast, medial to biopsy cavity. INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1 AND #1A; LYMPH NODE (RIGHT BREAST SENTINEL): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY BUT AWAIT PERMANENTS AND CYTOKERATIN. Gross Dictation by Joshua Kish M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Joshua Kish M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Micro/Dx Dictation by Joshua Kish M.D., on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION PART C: CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION (SLIDE ONLY) 
