oma in-situ cells to be positive ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR), EXCISION: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR), EXCISION: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL MARGIN LATERAL), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL MARGIN MEDIAL ANTERIOR), EXCISION: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received are multiple containers, which are all labeled Lucinda Lanzilli, #436-01-78. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled "right axilla sentinel node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm tan-pink-yellow soft tissue that is inked black, bisected, and entirely frozen as FX #1, which is now  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled "right breast lumpectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm lumpectomy with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral. The long axis is medial to lateral. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior blue, posterior black, superior green and inferior yellow. Specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a firm white-red REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm lesion located 1.1cm from the lateral end margin, 1.0cm from the medial end margin, 0.1cm from the anterior margin, 0.3cm to the posterior margin, 0.7cm to the closest superior margin, and 1.5cm from the closest inferior margin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is diffusely firm and fibrous with no other lesions or masses identified. SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral end margin, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial end margin, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Section of lesion to closest inferior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Section of lesion to closest posterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One whole section to closest superior and anterior margins.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of breast parenchyma away from the lesion. Received fresh, labeled "superior final margin", is a yellow-tan REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm portion of fibrofatty tissue which is unoriented and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled "inferior final margin", is a yellow-tan REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm portion of fibrofatty tissue which is unoriented, entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled "final margin, lateral", are two yellow REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm portions of fibrofatty tissue which are unoriented and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled "medial/anterior final margin", are multiple REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm portions of yellow fibrofatty tissue which are unoriented and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION # 1; LYMPH NODE, RIGHT AXILLA SENTINEL NODE: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR), EXCISION PART D: BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR), EXCISION PART E: BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL MARGIN LATERAL), EXCISION PART F: BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL MARGIN MEDIAL ANTE [report_end] 
