spect inked green and rounded aspect inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted. The specimen is submitted entirely as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire larger portion of tissue submitted sequentially from medial to lateral, with the medial end in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the lateral end in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Smaller portion of tissue submitted with the ends in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the body in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The specimen is received in formalin, labeled "left breast final inferior medial margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm irregular portion of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch designating final margin. The final margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The specimen is received in formalin, labeled "left breast superior final margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm irregular portion of tan-yellow to gray-white fibroadipose tissue with a stitch designating final margin. The final margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The specimen is received in formalin, labeled "left breast inferior margin, calcs", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm irregular portion of tan-yellow, focally hemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue with a stitch designating final margin. The final margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The specimen is received in formalin labeled "left breast final inferior margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm irregular portion of tan-yellow to gray-white fibroadipose tissue with a stitch designating final margin. The final margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1; (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE): TH