ht breast inferior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm unoriented portion of yellow-tan breast parenchyma with a guide wire localizing a firm region. The outer surface of the specimen is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ill-defined fibrous region next to the guide wire that abuts the black inked margin. The entire specimen is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with the fibrous region in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled "right breast superior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm portion of yellow-tan breast tissue that is unoriented and contains a guide wire localizing a firm region. The outer portion of the specimen is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm ill-defined white-tan fibrous region that abuts the inked margin. The entire specimen is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with the fibrous region in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received are an additional five containers, which are all labeled Anne Speicher, #452-52-93. Received in formalin, labeled "right breast inferior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm portion of yellow-tan soft tissue with a stitch designating one aspect. The stitched aspect is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal no masses or lesions. The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast deep", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm portion of yellow-tan soft tissue with two stitches designating one aspect. The opposing aspect is white-tan fibrous tissue with focal hemorrhage. The stitched end is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal fibrocystic change that abuts the inked margin. The specimen is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast lateral", are two portions of yellow-tan soft tissue with a stitch designating one aspect measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast superior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm portion of yellow-tan soft tissue with a stitch designating one aspect. The stitched aspect is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned. The entire specimen is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast medial", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm portion of yellow-tan soft tissue with a stitch designating one aspect. The stitched end is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned. The specimen is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (RIGHT, INFERIOR), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (RIGHT, SUPERIOR), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION PART D: BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL DEEP MARGIN), EXCISION PART E: BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL LATERAL MARGIN), EXCISION PART F: BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN), EXCISIO [report_end] 
