VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Updated Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery, WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-2 Results To: MICHELE ANNETTE GADD, M.D. Frozen Section Pathologist: Judith A Ferry, M.D. Frozen Section Resident: Michael H Roehrl, M.D., Ph.D. Signed Out by: Melinda J Lerwill, M.D. ********** Addended Report *********** Reason for Addendum #1: Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA: R - Calc, LCIS. L - Calcs and re-excision. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION: 1. FOCAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU ARISING IN A BACKGROUND OF MULTIFOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA/FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA, SEE TABLE #1. 2. EXTENSIVE LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). 3. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. 4. MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED. NOTE: Immunostains for p63, SM-MHC and calponin do not reveal evidence of invasive carcinoma. The ductal carcinoma in-situ is positive for E-cadherin, and the lobular carcinoma in-situ is negative. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU - RIGHT BREAST TUMOR SIZE: Involving 1 of 5 blocks. GRADE: 1. CALCIFICATIONS: In the carcinoma in-situ, atypical changes, and focally in benign changes. MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU: Ductal carcinoma in-situ focally extends to 0.1cm from the inked margin, but severely atypical ductal hyperplasia that may in fact represent flat ductal carcinoma in-situ is present at the margin. STAINS FOR RECEPTORS: Requested on  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, SENTINEL), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 LYMPH NODE. NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, NON-SENTINEL), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 LYMPH NODE. BREAST (LEFT), NEEDLE-LOCALIZED EXCISION: 1. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, SEE TABLE #2. 2. BLUNT DUCT ADENOSIS WITH CALCIFICATIONS. 3. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. 4. FOCAL HEALING BIOPSY SITE. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #2 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU - LEFT BREAST TUMOR SIZE: Involving 2 of 10 blocks. GRADE: 1. CALCIFICATIONS: Limited to benign changes. MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU: Ductal carcinoma in-situ extends to <0.1cm from the inferior and anterior margins of the specimen. STAINS FOR RECEPTORS: Not indicated. BREAST (LEFT), RE-EXCISION: HEALING BIOPSY SITE; RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: HEALING BIOPSY SITE; RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: 1. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, GRADE 1, PRESENT AT THE FINAL MARGIN. 2. INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA. 3. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN), EXCISION: 1. FOCAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, GRADE 1, <0.1 CM FROM THE FINAL MARGIN. 2. MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL LATERAL MARGIN), EXCISION: HEALING BIOPSY SITE; RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL ANTERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: HEALING BIOPSY SITE; RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL DEEP MARGIN), EXCISION: HEALING BIOPSY SITE; RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED. NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled Kay Campbell, #453-46-92 and "right breast tissue", are three un-oriented portions of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissues ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm  The largest fragment contains a needle localization wire in place. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph. All three fragments are inked black, serially sectioned to reveal a tan-white, focally hemorrhagic fibrous breast parenchyma with focal nodularity in the smallest fragment. The entire specimen is submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Smallest fragment, serially sectioned.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Second fragment, serially sectioned.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Largest fragment, serially sectioned (containing needle localization wire). Specimen is received in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled Kay Campbell, #453-46-92, and "left axillary sentinel node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm tan-pink possible lymph node which is entirely as submitted as FX#1, now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh, labeled with the patient name Kay Campbell, #453-46-92, and "left breast needle loc", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm portion of breast tissue with a needle localization wire in place. The specimen is inked as follows: Anterior-blue, posterior-black, superior-green, inferior-yellow. Cut section reveals a tan-yellow fibrofatty surface with no masses or lesions identified. The specimen is serially sectioned, sequentially submitted from medial to lateral in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (medial margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , lateral margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and calcifications in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). Received are eight containers, which are all labeled Kay Campbell, #453-46-92. Received in formalin, labeled "left axillary non-sentinel node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm tan-pink intact lymph node, bisected and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast re-excision", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm oriented portion of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a short stitch designating superior, long stitch designating medial margin. On the anterior surface, there is a REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm tan-brown, linear skin ellipse, which contains a 1.5cm linear well-healed scar. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior - blue, posterior - black, superior - green, inferior - yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial to lateral axis to reveal a diffuse tan-white, fibrous, focally hemorrhagic cut surface with occasional foci of fat necrosis. No discrete mass or lesion is noted. The entire specimen is sequentially submitted from medial to lateral as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with en face section medial margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and en face section lateral margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "final inferior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm portion of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the new margin. The surface containing the stitch is inked black, specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "final superior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm portion of tan-white, rubbery soft tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the new margin. The surface containing the stitch is inked black, specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "final medial", is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm portion of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the new margin. The surface containing the stitch is inked black, specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with "final lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm portion of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one surface designating the new margin. The surface containing the stitch is inked black, the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with "final anterior", are four un-oriented portions of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled with "final deep", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm un-oriented portion of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue, serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1; (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE): NO CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED. Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON #1: QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The ductal and lobular carcinoma in-situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The ductal and lobular carcinoma in-situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein. See note. Note: Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Addendum #1 by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION PART B: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION PART C: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION PART D: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA), EXCISION PART E: BREAST (LEFT), RE-EXCISION PART F: BREAST (LEFT, FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION PART G: BREAST (LEFT, FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION PART H: BRE [