e is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm vaguely stellate area with a peripheral REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm nodule which is 2.5cm from the posterior margin. 1.0cm lateral to the stellate area is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm cavity with a tan-pink irregular lining, which is 4.0cm from the posterior margin. Inferior to the larger cavity is a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm cavity site with a tan-pink glistening lining, which is 3.5cm from the posterior margin. The remaining parenchyma is predominantly dense, gray-white fibrous tissue admixed with yellow lobulated adipose tissue. Dissection of the axillary tail reveals multiple tan-pink to tan-white soft to rubbery possible lymph nodes, ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1.8cm in greatest dimension. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire subareolar nodule.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire vaguely stellate area.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire biopsy cavity.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative fibrous breast parenchyma lateral to biopsy cavity.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Largest nodule, bisected.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 intact nodules.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 bisected nodules, 1 inked.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Multiple intact nodules.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous breast parenchyma, adjacent to subareolar nodule.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous breast parenchyma, adjacent to larger cavity site.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous breast parenchyma, lateral to larger cavity site.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous breast parenchyma, adjacent to subareolar nodule.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous breast parenchyma, containing smaller cavity site.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous breast parenchyma, adjacent to larger cavity site.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous breast parenchyma, lateral to larger cavity site. Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART : Breast (Right), Modified Radical Mastectomy [report_end] 
