his case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received are 2 containers, which are all labeled Carole S. Rowell, #461-98-75. Received fresh, labeled "left breast", is a 28 x 27 x 7.5cm breast with attached 15 x 10 x 2cm axillary tail. The breast is partially surfaced by a 24 x 14.5cm portion of skin with a 1.5cm nipple, 3.5cm from the nearest skin margin. The inferior edge of the areola displays a 5cm semicircular healed scar consistent with previous biopsy. The specimen is inked anterior - blue, posterior - black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm poorly delineated tan-white focally brown indurated area in the lower outer quadrant consistent with previous biopsy site that is 0.7cm from the skin, 1.5cm from the anterior margin, and >2cm from the posterior margin. The remaining uninvolved breast tissue is yellow lobulated and fatty with moderate white fibrous breast tissue. Dissection of the axillary tail reveals 30 possible lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Biopsy site to anterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire biopsy site to skin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin closest to biopsy site.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Uninvolved breast tissue from upper inner quadrant and mid breast, respectively.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Two possible lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Multiple possible lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Multiple possible lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One potential lymph node.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Two potential lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Two potential lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One lymph node bisected.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One possible lymph node bisected.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One possible lymph node bisected. Received fresh, labeled "right breast", is a 28 x 24 x 4cm breast surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 15cm portion of skin with a 6 x 5.5cm nipple areolar complex with a central REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm circular nipple, 2.2cm from the nearest skin margin. There is a suture marking the axillary tail. Specimen is inked anterior - blue, posterior - black and serially sectioned to reveal lobulated yellow adipose tissue with sparse fibrous tissue without obvious mass. Sectioning of the upper outer quadrant reveals 3 possible lymph nodes averaging REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mid breast.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 3 possible lymph nodes, each in 1 cassette. Received are 3 additional containers, which are all labeled Carole S. Rowell, #461-98-75. Received in formalin, labeled "right sentinel node #137", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm tan-pink lymph node with a moderate amount of attached tan-yellow adipose tissue. The lymph node is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right sentinel node #424", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm gray-pink lymph node with a moderate amount of attached tan-yellow adipose tissue. The lymph node is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right axillary sentinel node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm aggregate of tan-pink fibrofatty tissue which is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm tan-pink lymph node. The lymph node is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A: Breast (Left), Modified Radical Mastectomy PART B: Breast (Right), Modified Radical Mastectomy PART C: Lymph Node (Right Axilla, "Sentinel" 137), Excision PART D: Lymph Node (Right Axilla, "Sentinel" 424), Excision PART E: Lymph Node (Right Axilla, "Sentinel"), Excision [report_end] 
