rgin. The remainder of the cut surface consists of lobulated tan-yellow fat with a moderate amount of interspersed dense gray-white fibrous tissue. No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified. The specimen is entirely submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior end, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body of specimen, submitted sequentially from superior to inferior, with the section containing the clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and section containing the cystic cavity in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior end, en face. Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART : Breast (Left), Excision [report_end] 
