VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-1 Results To: BARBARA LYNN SMITH, M.D. Resident: Madelyn Lew, M.D. Signed Out by: Dennis Sgroi, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: 61 year old female with prior right breast excision, positive for lobular carcinoma in situ, focal flat epithelial atypia and fibrocystic change with focal ductal hyperplasia. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION: 1. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU) (SEE NOTE). 2. FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA WITH CALCIFICATIONS. 3. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS. 4. MYXOID FIBROADENOMA. NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MARGIN MEDIAL), EXCISION: 1. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU), (SEE NOTE.). 2. BENIGN GLANDS HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS. NOTE: Focal lack of e-cadherin staining supports a diagnosis of LCIS (slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR), EXCISION: BREAST TISSUE WITH FOCAL CALCIFICATIONS; THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR), EXCISION: BENIGN GLANDS HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS (SEE NOTE.). NOTE: Immunostains for e-cadherin demonstrate intense membrane staining. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MARGIN LATERAL), EXCISION: BREAST PARENCHYMA, THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received are 5 containers, which are all labeled Phyllis Kooyoomjian, #465-07-92. Received in formalin and labeled "left breast, final margin - superior", is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0.4cm fragment of unoriented fragment of tan-brown soft tissue. The specimen is serially sectioned, perpendicular to its longest axis, and submitted in its entirety and sequentially from  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, and labeled "left breast, final margin - inferior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm unoriented fragment of tan-pink soft tissue. The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to its longest axis to reveal a predominantly homogenous tan-white, firm, fibrous cut surface that comprises approximately 95% of the cut surface. The specimen is submitted in its entirety and sequentially from  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, and labeled "left breast, final margin - medial", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm unoriented fragment of tan-white soft tissue. The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to its longest axis to reveal a homogenous tan-fibrofatty cut surface with no obvious lesions. The fibrous component comprises approximately 80-90% of the cut surface. The specimen is submitted in its entirety and sequentially from  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, and labeled "left breast, final margin - lateral", are 2 fragments of tan-brown soft tissue measuring 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm and 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  The fragments are serially sectioned perpendicular to their longest axis to reveal a fibrofatty cut surface with the fibrous component comprising approximately 5-10% of the cut surfaces. The larger fragment is submitted in its entirety and sequentially from  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The smaller fragment is serially sectioned and submitted in its entirety in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh and labeled "left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm fragment of fatty soft tissue. The specimen is oriented with a short suture designating the superior aspect and a long suture designating the lateral aspect. The longest axis runs medial to lateral and the specimen is inked as follows: Anterior - blue, posterior - black, superior - green and inferior - yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 2.2cm tan-white, firm, fibrotic area extending from the medial margin. The fibrotic area abuts the medial margin, and measures 1.1cm from the lateral margin, and <0.1cm from the anterior, posterior, superior and inferior margins. No other masses or gross abnormalities are noted. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is yellow-tan, lobulated, and otherwise unremarkable. The specimen is submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, radially sectioned.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of fibrotic area and uninvolved unremarkable breast parenchyma.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of grossly normal breast parenchyma. Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 26,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05:13:57PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Breast (Left, Final Margin superior), Excision PART B: Breast (Left, Final Margin inferior), Excision PART C: Breast (Left, Final Margin medial), Excision PART D: Breast (Left, Final Margin lateral), Excision PART E: Breast (Left), Excision [report_end] 
