ozen as FX #1A, now resubmitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The rest of the fat is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh and labeled "right breast tissue", is a 30 x REMOVED_DATE x 7cm right mastectomy specimen surfaced by a 30 x 1.5cm of pink-slightly tan skin with an areolar-nipple complex with not very well demarcated borders measuring REMOVED_DATE x 4.5cm  the nipple is everted and measures REMOVED_DATE x 1cm and is at the level of the areola. The skin around the areola is slightly more erythematous. No puckering is identified. The areolar-nipple complex is located up to 12cm from the closest superior margin, 15cm from the closest lateral margin, 10cm from the closest medial margin, and 5.5cm from the closest inferior margin. A short suture stitch designates the superior aspect of the specimen and a long suture stitch, the lateral aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked as follows: Anterior - blue, posterior - black. The specimen is then serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a yellow, lobulated, unremarkable parenchyma, and a REMOVED_DATE x 6cm irregular area of pink-white fibrous tissue which is focally firmer. A tumor mass is not grossly identified nor a previous biopsy cavity. The fibrous dense area is located up to 4cm from the closest posterior black-inked margin, to 2cm from the closest areolar-nipple complex, 10cm from the superior aspect, 8cm from the inferior aspect of the specimen, 10cm from the closest lateral aspect of the specimen and 9cm from the closest medial aspect of the specimen. Another irregular area of tan-pink fibrous tissue, slightly firm, is identified, located 8cm from the previously described firm area, 2cm from the closest posterior margin, and 2.5cm from the closest anterior (skin) margin. No other lesions are grossly identified. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of the dense fibrous area.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Section of the closest posterior margin to the dense fibrous area.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Section of the 2nd area of dense fibrous tissue.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Section to include areola/nipple complex.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sections away from the fibrous dense areas previously described in the inferior inner quadrant of the breast.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional tissue adjacent to remote biopsy site. Received fresh and labeled "left breast tissue", is a 26 x REMOVED_DATE x 6cm left mastectomy specimen surfaced by a pink skin ellipse measuring 26 x 22cm with an areola-nipple complex measuring 5 x 3cm and the nipple measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm which is everted . The areola-nipple complex is located 10cm from the closest superior aspect of the specimen, 6cm from the closest inferior aspect, 15cm from the closest lateral aspect of the specimen and 11cm from the closest medial aspect of the specimen. The skin is unremarkable and non-hair-bearing. The specimen is inked as follows: Posterior - black, anterior - blue. The specimen is then serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal yellow lobulated unremarkable parenchyma and areas of pink-white fibrous tissue. There are no areas of grittiness or lesions grossly identified. No lymph nodes are identified. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Middle of the specimen.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior outer quadrant. Received fresh and labeled "right axillary contents", is an 11 x 10 x 2.5cm yellow fibroadipose tissue containing candidate lymph nodes. Candidate lymph nodes are identified measuring from 0.2cm to 2cm  SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 lymph node (2cm ), bivalved.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Candidate lymph node, submitted each 1 entirely. Received fresh and labeled "additional right axillary contents", are 2 fragments of fibroadipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0.5cm  containing candidate lymph node which is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The rest of the adipose tissue is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1 & #1A; (SENTINEL NODE, LEFT AXILLA #225): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M.D., Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 13,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04:05:44PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Lymph Node (Left Axilla, "Sentinel" #225), Excision PART B: Breast (Right), Simple Mastectomy PART C: Breast (Left), Simple Mastectomy PART D: Lymph Nodes (Right Axilla Contents), Dissection PART E: Lymph Node (Additional Right axilla Contents), Excision PART F: Cryostat Frozen Section (slide o [report_end] 
