itted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial end margin, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body of the specimen, sequentially submitted from medial to lateral.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral end margin, en face. Received fresh, labeled "additional cephalad aspect, left breast", is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm portion of fibroadipose tissue, which is partially cauterized on one aspect. This aspect of the specimen is inked blue, and the remainder of the specimen is inked black. Sectioning reveals predominantly gray-white dense fibrous tissue with no masses or lesions grossly identified. The specimen is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Ends of the specimen.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body of the specimen, sequentially submitted from one end to the other. Received in formalin, labeled Joanne Greig, #467-47-65 and "left breast additional tissue #2", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm fragment of tan-white rubbery fibroadipose tissue, which is inked black, serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday May 12,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05:24:30PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Breast (Left), Excision PART B: Breast (Left Additional), Excision PART C: Breast (Left Additional #2), Excision [report_end] 
