VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Updated Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery, WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-1 Results To: MICHELE ANNETTE GADD, M.D. Resident: Russell Ryan, M.D. Frozen Section Pathologist: Richard L Kradin, M.D. Frozen Section Resident: Sarah Chiang, M.D. Signed Out by: Melinda J Lerwill, M.D. ********** Addended Report *********** Reason for Addendum #1: Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum #2: Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization (FISH) Results CLINICAL DATA: Invasive carcinoma. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION: 1. INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA. SEE TABLE #1. 2. FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. 3. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm  GRADE: 2. LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION: Not identified. BLOOD VESSEL INVASION: Not identified. MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA: Positive at the posterior margin of the specimen in one focus and 0.12cm from the superior margin. STAINS FOR RECEPTORS: Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, SENTINEL), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE (0/1). NOTE: Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the above interpretation. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR), EXCISION: 1. FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA. 2. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MARGIN MEDIAL), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MARGIN LATERAL), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MARGIN ANTERIOR), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MARGIN DEEP), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received are 2 containers, which are both labeled Patricia Regan, #467-83-84. Received fresh, labeled "left breast lumpectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE (M-L) x REMOVED_DATE (S-I) x REMOVED_DATE (A-P)cm breast excision specimen oriented with a short stitch superior and a long stitch lateral. A needle location wire is present in the specimen passing into the lateral aspect and exiting through the medial-anterior aspect. The external surface of the specimen consists primarily of yellow fibroadipose tissue, however, there is a firmer, more fibrous area posteriorly, beneath which a mass can be palpated. The specimen is inked per protocol as follows: Anterior - blue, posterior - black, superior - green, inferior - yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned into 10 slices from lateral to medial. The central portion of the specimen consists of an ill-defined tan-white mass with a hemorrhagic center which approaches to within 0.1cm of the posterior margin, with other margins more distant, but difficult to grossly determine. The specimen is entirely submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #1 (lateral margin), radially, entirely.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Serial sections from lateral to medial.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #10 (medial margin), radially. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled "sentinel node, left axilla", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm tan-yellow lymph node, which is frozen entirely as FX #1, now  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received are 6 containers, which are all labeled Patricia Regan, #467-83-84. Received in formalin, labeled "left breast final margin, inferior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm portion of fibroadipose breast tissue, oriented with a stitch. The stitched margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast final margin superior", are 2 portions of fibroadipose breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  respectively. Both specimens are oriented with a stitch, and the stitched aspect is inked black. Specimens are serially sectioned with the first entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the second entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast final margin, medial", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm portion of fibroadipose breast tissue oriented with a stitch. The stitched margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast final margin lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm portion of fibroadipose breast tissue with a stitch. The stitched margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast final margin anterior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm portion of fibroadipose breast tissue with a stitch. The stitched margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast final margin deep", are 2 unoriented portions of fibroadipose breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  which are serially sectioned and entirely submitted with the larger in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the smaller specimen in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1; (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 14,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02:29:42PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON #1: QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) HER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation: The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows: Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) Show strong (3+) over overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Addendum #1 by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 15,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01:18:27PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON #2: RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals (94) to chromosome 17 signals (94) in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. Results at or near the cutoff point (ranging from REMOVED_DATE - 2.2) should be interpreted with caution. Addendum #2 by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 21,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06:28:18PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Breast (Left), Excision PART B: Lymph Node (Left Axilla, "Sentinel"), Excision PART C: Breast (Left, Final Margin inferior), Excision PART D: Breast (Left, Final Margin superior), Excision PART E: Breast (Left, Final Margin medial), Excision PART F: Breast (Left, Final Margin lateral), Excision [report_end] 
