VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-2 Results To: BARBARA LYNN SMITH, M.D. Frozen Section Pathologist: Ben Zion Pilch, M.D. Frozen Section Resident: Michiya Nishino, M.D. Signed Out by: John H Eichhorn, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: Invasive lobular cancer, right breast. Right mastectomy and invasive lobular cancer, right breast. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. NO RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES. LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLARY, SENTINEL), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. SEE NOTE. THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED. NOTE: Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the above interpretation. LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLARY, ADDITIONAL), REGIONAL DISSECTION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES. SKIN (RIGHT BREAST), EXCISION: NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled Kimberly Bakopolus, #467-92-62 and "right axillary sentinel node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm brown lymph node with attached fat. The fat is removed and the lymph node is entirely frozen as FX#1, now  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remaining fat is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received are 3 containers, which are all labeled Kimberly Bakopolus, #467-92-62. Received fresh, labeled "right breast", is a 20 x 19 x 2cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen with a short stitch designating superior, long stitch designating lateral margin. The anterior surface bears a 4 x 3.5cm tan-brown skin ellipse with a 3 x 3cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm nipple, which are grossly unremarkable. The anterior surface also contains a REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm tan-brown skin ellipse, located approximately between 9 and 11 o'clock position, 6.5cm from the areola and bears a 2.4cm linear well-healed scar. The specimen is inked as follows: Anterior blue, posterior black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm biopsy cavity in the outer quadrant, approximately between 8 and 10 o'clock position beneath the overlying tan-brown skin ellipse with a linear scar. The biopsy cavity is packed with dark red hemorrhagic material and lies 0.3cm from posterior black-inked and 3cm from anterior blue-inked margin. The breast parenchyma surrounding the biopsy cavity is dense, white and has a nodular feel and contains a foci of fat necrosis. The remaining breast parenchyma contains large amount of dense tan-white rubbery fibrous tissue interspersed with tan-yellow lobulated adipose tissue. There is no additional discrete mass or lesion noted. 2 whole lymph nodes dissected from the upper outer quadrant tissue which measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section, biopsy cavity to include closest posterior inked margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section, fibrous breast parenchyma, central quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section, fibrous breast parenchyma, inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Single whole lymph node.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Single whole lymph node. Received in formalin, labeled "additional right axillary tissue", is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm aggregate of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue from which a single whole lymph node is dissected which measures 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  The entire specimen is submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Single bisected lymph node.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining fibroadipose tissue. Received in formalin, labeled with "right breast skin", are 2 irregular unoriented fragments of tan-brown skin which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm and 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  The smaller fragment is inked blue, larger fragment is inked black. The entire smaller fragment and a representative section of the larger fragment is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1; (LYMPH NODE, RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL): MALIGNANCY IS NOT IDENTIFIED. Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 27,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11:27:46AM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Lymph Node (Right Axilla, "Sentinel"), Excision PART B: Breast (Right), Simple Mastectomy PART C: Lymph Nodes (Additional Right Axilla), Dissection PART D: Skin (Right Breast), Excision PART E: Cryostat Frozen Section (slide only) [report_end] 
