n in conjunction with the final medial margin. GRADE: 1. LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION: Present, multifocal (present in main excision and final medial margin). BLOOD VESSEL INVASION: Not identified. MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA: Positive at the anterior margin of the specimen along a broad front, < 0.1cm from the superior margin, and 0.15cm from the posterior margin in the medial half of the specimen. LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU: Beyond the region of the mass. GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU: 1. MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU: Ductal carcinoma in-situ extends to < 0.1cm from the anterior margin of the specimen in one focus. STAINS FOR RECEPTORS: Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . BREAST (LEFT, FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN), EXCISION: 1. INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA. GRADE 1, BROADLY PRESENT AT THE FINAL MARGIN AND WITH ASSOCIATED LYMPHATIC INVASION. SEE NOTE. 2. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. NOTE: The tumor appears to have been bisected between the main excision specimen and the final medial margin. See table #2 (above) for overall tumor size estimate. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL LATERAL MARGIN), EXCISION: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). BREAST (LEFT, FINAL ANTERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). BREAST (LEFT, FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: 1. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). 2. FOCAL FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA. BREAST (LEFT, FINAL DEEP MARGIN), EXCISION: 1. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). 2. FOCAL MINIMAL FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA. BREAST (LEFT ADDITIONAL), EXCISION: 1. ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA. 2. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received are 9 containers which are labeled Wendy Mcvey, #479-39-41. Received fresh in the Frozen Section 