teral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm fragment of tan-white fibrous tissue, oriented as follows: A stitch indicates the final margin. The final margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast final margin anterior", are 3 fragments of fibroadipose tissue, unoriented, aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  which are entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast final margin superior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue, oriented as follows: A stitch indicates the final margin. The final margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast final inferior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm fragment of tan-white predominantly fibrous tissue, oriented as follows: A stitch indicates the final margin. The final margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast final deep", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm fragment of tan-white fibrous tissue, with focal hemorrhage, oriented as follows: A stitch indicates the final margin. The final margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "left breast additional lumpectomy", are 2 unoriented fragments of tan-white fibrous tissue admixed with fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  Each fragment is inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable tan-white fibrous tissue with scant admixed adipose tissue, and no focal lesions or abnormalities. The specimen is entirely submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_