VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : REMOVED_CASE_ID  Report Status: Signed \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS: \u000aRight breast, excision: \u000aFibroadenoma. \u000aFibrocystic changes with ductal hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis and \u000amicrocalcifications. \u000aSlight atypical ductal hyperplasia of columnar type, single microscopic focus \u000a(see note). \u000aNOTE: The slides were sent in consultation to Dr. Frederick C. Koerner at \u000aMassachusetts General Hospital who concurs and states the following in \u000ahis consultation letter: \u000a"The tissue in the background of this excision specimen shows \u000afibrocystic changes and a small focus of adenosis. I agree that the \u000anodule in question represents a fibroadenoma. The epithelium within it \u000alooks stratified in several areas, but I attribute most of this \u000aappearance to tangential sectioning. One small region on slide "9", \u000awhich I dotted, probably does display genuine ductal hyperplasia, which \u000alooks similar to the foci of ductal hyperplasia in the surrounding \u000atissue. I would not regard either focus as atypical. The region of \u000aslide "7" that caught your attention looks a bit different: these \u000aproliferative cells have columnar shapes, atypical nuclei, and abundant \u000aapical cytoplasm. Because of these findings, I would classify this tiny \u000afocus as atypical ductal hyperplasia of columnar cell type. The degree \u000aof proliferation strikes me as minimal, though, and the atypicality as \u000asubtle. I do not think that such a minuscule lesion would require \u000afurther investigation or treatment unless the clinical details of the \u000acase suggest otherwise." \u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Daniel D. Koelliker, M.D. \u000aClinical diagnosis & history: \u000aRight breast mass \u000aTissue-Designation: \u000aBreast, excision (without margins) - right \u000aGross description: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled "right breast mass" and consists \u000aof a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm  aggregate of multiple irregular portions of fibroadipose \u000atissue. Each of the portions is primarily rubbery, pink and white-tan fibrous \u000atissue with a small amount of surrounding adipose tissue. No grossly \u000asuspicious areas are seen. The entire specimen is sectioned. Focally, there \u000ais a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm  bulging, pink-tan area. The entire specimen is \u000asubmitted in REMOVED_DATE 9 agg. all. \u000aDictated by: DDK____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE (Final) \u000a____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE (Final) \u000a[report_end] 
