V REMOVED_CASE_ID  FISKE,KATHLEEN A 61/F <REG REF 05/17> ( REMOVED_CASE_ID ) WIC SKORNIK,RONEE A. M.D.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------Specimen:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : REMOVED_CASE_ID  SOUT Received: 05/17/05- REMOVED_CASE_ID  Spec Type: - Clinical diagnosis & history: 8mm  cluster of indeterminate microcalcifications of left lower inner breast; tiny cluster of calcifications left breast; ? ductal carcinoma in situ versus fibrocystic changes Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD Gross description: The specimen is received in formalin in one container, labeled "stereotactic breast biopsy, left breast calcifications" and is contained in two cassettes. The first cassette is purple and designated "left lower inner quadrant with calcifications" and consists of a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  aggregate of yellowish-pink, firm needle biopsies each measuring 0.3cm  in diameter. Submitted in cassette REMOVED_DATE agg. all. The second cassette is aqua in color, designated to container "the remainder of the tissue" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0.4cm  aggregate of yellowish-pink, firm needle biopsies each measuring 0.3cm  in diameter. Submitted in cassette REMOVED_DATE agg. all. Dictated by: LV Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD DIAGNOSIS: Left breast, lower inner quadrant, needle core biopsies: Microcalcifications identified and associated with atypical ductal hyperplasia (see note). Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.MURJ DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT: NOTE: This case was sent to Dr. Frederick Koerner at Massachusetts General Hospital. He concurs with the above diagnosis of atypical ductal hyperplasia. He adds: "I agree with those in your department who favor the diagnosis of atypical ductal hyperplasia and I believe that the region of slide "1 1L" marked with red and blue demonstrates the atypicality most clearly. A population of atypical ductal cells fills and distends a small duct. They appear slightly enlarged and they possess ample, eosinophilic cytoplasm and nuclei containing homogeneous chromatin. Atypical columnar cells growing in a single layer and forming stubby small papillae distend a collection of glands, but distortion of the tissue makes it difficult to evaluate this focus. I acknowledge that the degree of proliferation in these areas seem slight and the nature of the cytological atypicality subtle; nevertheless, I would urge the patient and her physicians to consider an excision of this region of the left breast. Examination of a larger sample would provide a more secure evaluation of the extent and the significance of the atypical ductal hyperplasia." Final Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D. Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.MURJ Notes: REMOVED_DATE  Received all 6 slides and report from MGH via mail. NAM/mi (CR) REMOVED_DATE  Rec'd MGH path report via fax /dg REMOVED_DATE  Report faxed from MGH /jam REMOVED_DATE  Per NAM, sent for opinion to MGH, Dr. Koerner, sent (6) slides labeled (1 1L-3L, 2 1L-3L) NAM/dg CO Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.MURJ REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.INDMCODES:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - Left breast, NO-Needle BREANBX- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - -BREANBX-Atypical hyperp Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.MURJCOPIES TO: SELLAND,DONNA-LEE M.D. NEWTON-WELLESLEY RADIOLOGY NEWTON, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  (617)243- REMOVED_CASE_ID  SKORNIK,RONEE A. M.D. 173 WORCESTER ST. WELLESLEY, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  (781)237- REMOVED_CASE_ID MARKERS: Breast Disease Related, Presented at Breast CA Conf., Consult Case Out, Consult Case Return Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.INDM REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.MURJPROCEDURES:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (05/18/05- REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD) Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.MURJTISSUES: Breast, needle biopsy - left lower inner quadrant Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILDFinal: SAMPSON,RICHARD J MD * REMOVED_DATE <05/18/05- REMOVED_CASE_ID > by MD.SAMR MIHOK,NICOLE MD***** * REMOVED_DATE <05/20/05- REMOVED_CASE_ID > by MD.MIHN -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
