V REMOVED_CASE_ID  DELVECCHIO,SUSAN A (P) 49/F <REG REF 08/03> ( REMOVED_CASE_ID ) WIC LAJOIE,ROBIN JOAN M.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------Specimen:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : REMOVED_CASE_ID  SOUT Received: 08/03/07- REMOVED_CASE_ID  Spec Type: - Clinical diagnosis & history: Right lump at prior biopsy site, MRI showed suspicious enhancement of right outer breast and left fibroadenoma, right fibrocystic changes, doubt cancer, left fibroadenoma Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.DORD Gross description: The specimen is received in formalin in two containers. Specimen A labeled "guided breast biopsy, right breast" designated "right breast at 9 o'clock" and consists of eight firm, reddish-pink, glistening needle biopsies with a moderate amount of attached blood clot ranging in size from 0.5cm  in length x 0.2cm  in diameter to 1.5cm  in length x 0.2cm  in diameter. Entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . 8X all. Specimen B labeled "guided breast biopsy, left breast" designated "left breast at 3 o'clock" consists of eight firm, greyish-pink, glistening needle biopsies with a moderate amount of attached blood clot ranging in size from 0.5cm  in length x 0.2cm  in diameter to 2cm  in length x 0.2cm  in diameter. Entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . 8X all. Dictated by: LV Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.DORD DIAGNOSIS: A. Right breast, 9 o'clock, needle biopsy: Lobular carcinoma in situ with focal reactive stromal changes. See note. B. Left breast, 3 o'clock, needle biopsy: Fibroadenoma. Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD.MATAN DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT: NOTE: The right breast needle biopsies (A), show lobular carcinoma in situ. One core exhibits adjacent reactive stromal changes along with some irregularity of the epithelial cell nests. Immunohistochemical stain for E-Cadherin is negative in the lobular process. Stains for calponin and smooth muscle myosin highlight an intact myoepithelial cell layer throughout the LCIS. No areas diagnostic of invasive carcinoma are identified, although the stromal changes suggest that an adjacent area of invasion cannot be excluded. Excision is recommended. Final Diagnosis by: Anthony R. Mattia, M.D. Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT: (Continued) REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD.MATANCODES:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - Right breast, N-Lobular carcino  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - Left breast, NO-Fibroadenoma, N BREANBX - -BREANBX Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.DORD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD.MATANMARKERS: Breast Disease Related, Tumor case Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.DORD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILDPROCEDURES: IMMUNOCYTO (08/08/07- REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD)  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (08/08/07- REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD) Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.DORD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.GILDTISSUES: A. Breast, needle biopsy - right 9 o'clock B. Breast, needle biopsy - left 3 o'clock Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.DORDFinal: ROSS,MICHAEL J. M.D. * REMOVED_DATE <08/08/07- REMOVED_CASE_ID > by MD.ROSMJ MATTIA,ANTHONY R.MD * REMOVED_DATE <08/08/07- REMOVED_CASE_ID > by MD.MATAN -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
