VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : REMOVED_CASE_ID  Report Status: Signed \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT \u000aAddendum #1 Entered: 09/03/03- REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION *** \u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing \u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged. \u000aImmunohistochemical studies performed on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  reveal the following results \u000afor the infiltrating carcinoma: \u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE \u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): NEGATIVE for overexpression \u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed FEEN,DENNIS J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. Right axillary sentinel lymph node #1, biopsy: \u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized. \u000aNo metastatic carcinoma present on H&E and immunostaining with \u000apankeratin. \u000aB. Right axillary sentinel lymph node #2, biopsy: \u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized. \u000aNo metastatic carcinoma present on H&E and immunostaining with \u000apankeratin. \u000aC. Left axillary lymph node, dissection: \u000aAll four axillary lymph nodes are negative for metastatic carcinoma. \u000aD. Right partial mastectomy, excision: \u000aPoorly differentiated invasive lobular carcinoma, two foci \u000asuperior/lateral, 0.7cm  and superior/medial, 0.5cm  (near previous \u000abiopsy site. \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, focal. \u000aLobular carcinoma in situ, multifocal. \u000aFibrocystic changes with microcalcifications and extensive intraductal \u000ahyperplasia. \u000aIntraductal papilloma, small. \u000aFibroadenoma, small. \u000aSingle intramammary lymph node with no diagnostic abnormalities \u000arecognized (no metastatic carcinoma identified). \u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: \u000aINVASIVE TUMOR: \u000a-histologic type: lobular \u000a-histologic grade: poorly differentiated \u000a-size (greatest dimension): two foci, largest 0.7cm  and \u000aresidual focus near previous biopsy \u000asite, 0.5cm  \u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: none identified \u000a-perineural invasion: none identified \u000a-microcalcification in invasive tumor: present \u000a-margins for invasive tumor: 0.1cm  for the 0.7cm  focus in the \u000asuperior/lateral portion of the \u000aspecimen; 0.1cm  from the mid-deep \u000amargin for the residual foci (0.5 \u000acm.) near the previous biopsy site. \u000a-immunohistochemical stains for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor and \u000afor  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu will be performed on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and reported in an addendum \u000ato follow. \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (LCIS): present, multifocal; foci of \u000alobular carcinoma in situ are \u000apresent within 0.1cm  of inked \u000amargins \u000aLYMPH NODES: \u000aA total of six lymph nodes sampled are all negative for malignancy \u000a(0/2 sentinel lymph nodes; REMOVED_DATE non-sentinel lymph nodes). \u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Dennis J. Feen, M.D. \u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION: \u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (TISSUE EXAMINATION): \u000a#1 Sentinel lymph node #1: No gross tumor seen. \u000a#2 Sentinel lymph node #2: No gross tumor seen. \u000aMJR \u000aClinical diagnosis & history: \u000aRight breast carcinoma \u000aTissue-Designation: \u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - right axilla #1 \u000aB.Sentinel lymph node - right axilla #2 \u000aC.Lymph nodes, dissection - axillary \u000aD.Breast, partial mastectomy - right \u000aGross description: \u000aThe specimen is received in four parts. \u000aSpecimen A is labeled "sentinel node, right axilla #1" and consists of a 1 x 1 \u000ax 1cm  blue stained nodule of partly yellow adipose, partly firm tissue with \u000aattached fat measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm  The entire lymph node \u000ais serially sectioned and submitted. 5X. \u000aSpecimen B is labeled "sentinel node #2" and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  \u000anodule of partly yellow adipose, partly pink and blue stained firmer tissue. \u000aThe specimen is bisected. 2X all. \u000aSpecimen C is labeled "axillary nodes" and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1cm  \u000aaggregate of fat containing four nodules of firm, tan-pink tissue ranging in \u000adiameter from REMOVED_DATE to 1.0cm  \u000aSECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - bisected single lymph node, 2X \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - bisected single lymph node, 2X \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - two lymph nodes, 2X \u000aSpecimen D is labeled "right partial mastectomy" and consists of a 102 gram, \u000a12.7 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm  portion of partly yellow adipose, partly firm, tan-pink \u000atissue. A short suture marks the superior margin, and a long suture marks the \u000alateral margin. The superior margin is inked blue; the inferior margin, green; \u000athe remainder of the specimen with black ink. Sectioning of the lateral/mid \u000aportion of the specimen shows a previous biopsy site with a hematoma REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is firm but unremarkable. \u000aSection code:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - lateral margin (superior to inferior) \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - superior margin \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - medial margin \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - inferior margin \u000aDictated by: MJR____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE (Final) \u000a____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE (Final) \u000a[report_end] 
