000aoverall dimensions are 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm  The anterior surface is concave. The \u000asuperior surface is marked with a short green suture; the lateral surface with \u000aa long green suture. The deep surface is marked with black ink. The superior \u000asurface is marked with blue ink. The superior portion of the specimen is \u000asubmitted in its entirety proceeding from medial to lateral margin designated \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remainder of the specimen is also submitted from medial to lateral \u000adesignated  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The second portion of the specimen also consists of an oval \u000afragment of firm, yellowish-grey fibroadipose and fibrocollagenous tissue. \u000aThere are no orienting suture markings. The outer margins are inked. The cut \u000asurface reveals a hemorrhagic, irregular cavity-like area 2 x 1cm  The entire \u000aspecimen is embedded designated  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . 21X. \u000aDictated by: DJF____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE (Final) \u000a____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE (Final) \u000a[report_end] 
