VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : REMOVED_CASE_ID  Report Status: Signed \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. Right sentinel lymph node, 88 count, excision: \u000aNo tumor seen in one lymph node (0/1). \u000aB. Right non-sentinel lymph node, excision: \u000aNo tumor seen in one lymph node (0/1). \u000aC. Right breast, simple mastectomy: \u000aOne focus of atypical lobular hyperplasia. \u000aRare microcalcifications seen and are associated with benign breast \u000atissue and sclerosing adenosis. \u000aSkin with no diagnostic abnormalities recognized. \u000aNipple with hemangioma, 0.3cm , benign. \u000aFibrocystic changes. \u000aD. Left sentinel lymph node, 208 count, excision: \u000aBenign squamous subcapsular inclusions; no tumor seen in one lymph node \u000a(0/1). \u000aE. Specimen designated "supernumerary nipple", excision: \u000aSkin with dermal ducts consistent with supernumerary nipple. \u000aF. Left breast, simple mastectomy: \u000aFocal ductal hyperplasia with reactive changes. \u000aNo residual ductal carcinoma in situ seen (see note). \u000aFibrocystic changes. \u000aHealing excision site changes. \u000aSkin with scar. \u000aNipple with no diagnostic abnormalities recognized. \u000aIntraductal papillomas, 0.7cm  and 0.2cm  \u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: \u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (Massachusetts General \u000aHospital  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) was reported as: \u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained) \u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE, focal (1-10% of nuclei stained) \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (c-erb- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): NEGATIVE (0) (no membrane staining) \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (4 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , Ventana Medical Systems, FDA approved) is assessed by \u000aquantitation of the percent and intensity of tumor cells staining. \u000aLYMPH NODES: \u000aAll lymph nodes sampled are negative for malignancy (0/3) \u000a(0/2 sentinel lymph nodes; REMOVED_DATE non-sentinel lymph nodes). \u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph nodes, specimens A and D, is examined at multiple \u000alevels with H&E stains and immunohistochemical stains for keratin. \u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED: \u000aLeft breast needle localized excision; Massachusetts General Hospital \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; REMOVED_DATE  \u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pTis p REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (sn)(i-) pMX \u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information \u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D. \u000aClinical diagnosis & history: \u000aLeft breast carcinoma \u000aTissue-Designation: \u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - right, 88 count \u000aB.Lymph node, biopsy - right \u000aC.Breast, simple mastectomy - right \u000aD.Sentinel lymph node - left, 208 count \u000aE.Specimen designated as - supernumerary nipple \u000aF.Breast, simple mastectomy - left \u000aGross description: \u000aThe specimen is received in six containers. \u000aSpecimen A labeled "right sentinel lymph node, 88 count" is received in \u000aformalin and consists of a single REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm  lymph node. The lymph \u000anode is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in one cassette. 1 agg. all. \u000aSpecimen B labeled "right non sentinel lymph node" is received in formalin and \u000aconsists of a single lymph node that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm  The specimen \u000ais trisected and entirely submitted in one cassette. 3X all. \u000aSpecimen C labeled "right breast" is received fresh from the Operating Room and \u000aconsists of a 557 gram simple mastectomy with a stitch said to designate the \u000aaxillary tail. The breast measures up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm  On the surface \u000aof the breast is an ellipse of skin containing unremarkable skin and a nipple \u000awith areola. The skin with nipple and areola is up to REMOVED_DATE x 5.7cm  and the \u000anipple is up to 1.5cm  in greatest height. The skin is unremarkable. The \u000aareola shows a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm  slightly reddish nodule on the surface. The \u000abreast is inked as follows: upper outer quadrant, blue; lower outer quadrant, \u000agreen; upper inner quadrant, red; lower inner quadrant, yellow; deep margin, \u000ablack. The specimen is serially sectioned and no abnormalities are identified. \u000aThe breast parenchyma is yellowish-white and without lesions. Representative \u000asections are submitted. \u000aSection code:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - skin and the small nodule described \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - nipple with areola \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - underneath nipple \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - upper outer quadrant \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - lower outer quadrant \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - upper inner quadrant \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - lower inner quadrant \u000aSpecimen D labeled "left sentinel lymph node 208" is received in formalin and \u000aconsists of a single lymph node with attached adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.5 x 0.9cm  The node is trisected and submitted entirely in cassette D. 3X \u000aall. \u000aSpecimen E labeled "left supernumerary nipple" is received in formalin and \u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  portion of skin excised to a depth of 0.7cm  The \u000asurface of the skin shows slightly wrinkled beige skin. The specimen is \u000abisected and submitted entirely in cassette E. 2X all. \u000aSpecimen F labeled "left breast" is received fresh from the Operating Room and \u000aconsists of a 582 gram simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating the \u000aaxillary tail. The breast measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x up to 4.0cm  On the \u000asurface, there is an ellipse of skin with a scar and a nipple and areola in \u000aplace. The ellipse of skin is up to REMOVED_DATE x 6.5cm  The nipple is up to REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. in height. The nipple and areola are unremarkable. The skin shows a well \u000ahealed scar that is 3.1cm  and is towards the lateral end of the skin ellipse. \u000aThe breast is inked as follows: upper outer quadrant, green; lower outer \u000aquadrant, blue; upper inner quadrant, red; lower inner quadrant, yellow; deep \u000amargin, black. The specimen is serially sectioned and the cut surface shows a \u000ahealing biopsy cavity with adjacent area of scarring. The biopsy cavity is REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. in greatest dimension and the area of scarring around it is up to 2.0cm  \u000aSlightly inferior to the area of prior biopsy change is a slightly gritty, \u000ayellow focus that is 0.5cm  in greatest dimension. The cavity, scar and \u000ayellowish area are all widely clear of the surgical margin. They are located \u000aslightly lateral, underneath the nipple and at the 3 o'clock area of the \u000ajunction of the upper outer quadrant and lower outer quadrants. The remainder \u000aof the breast shows an area consistent with an intraductal papilloma in the \u000aupper inner quadrant. The specimen is sectioned and submitted as follows. 15 \u000aagg. \u000aSection code:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - nipple, areola and skin with scar \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - random sections from upper outer quadrant \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - random sections from lower outer quadrant \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - random sections from upper inner quadrant \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - random sections from lower inner quadrant \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - sections of entire biopsy cavity and area of fibrosis \u000aaround the area of biopsy cavity ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains the \u000aslightly gritty, yellowish area) \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - deep margin closest to the prior biopsy site \u000aTotal fixation time is 28 hours. \u000aDictated by: NAM____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE (Final) \u000a____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE (Final) \u000a[report_end] 
