locks of tissue have been completely leveled through. The pools of mucin are worrisome for mucinous carcinoma; however, a diagnosis of mucinous carcinoma cannot be made on this material given the lack of atypical epithelial cells within the mucin. Radiographic pathologic correlation is recommended and repeat biopsies may be indicated, especially if a mass lesion is identified. Final Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D. DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT: (Continued) Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.MURJ REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD.MIHN Notes: REMOVED_DATE  In addition to the cosigner Dr. Abbott, Dr. Mattia has reviewed the case and concurs with the diagnosis. NAM Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.MURJCODES:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - Epithelium, NOS  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - Right breast, N-Needle  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - Right breast, N-Mucin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - Adipose tissue BREANBX - -BREANBX BREANBX- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - -BREANBX-Separation, NOS Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.DORD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.MURJ REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.MURJ REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.MURJ REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.MURJCOPIES TO: CAHILL,TERESA M.D. NWH-RADIOLOGY DEPT. NEWTON, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  (617)243- REMOVED_CASE_ID  NEWTON-CHEH,EMILY M.D.  REMOVED_CASE_ID  WASHINGTON ST. NEWTON, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  (617)965- REMOVED_CASE_ID MARKERS: Breast Disease Related Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.DORDPROCEDURES:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  (10/28/08- REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.MURJ) Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.DORD REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.MURJ REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.MURJTISSUES: Breast, needle biopsy - right Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.DORDFinal: ABBOTT,TODD MD * REMOVED_DATE <10/28/08- REMOVED_CASE_ID > by MD.ABBT MIHOK,NICOLE MD***** * REMOVED_DATE <10/28/08- REMOVED_CASE_ID > by MD.MIHN -----------------------------------