hows a largely firm, \u000afibroglandular tissue with some adipose tissue admixed. Sections are taken as \u000afollows: \u000aSection code:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - four quadrants in a clockwise fashion \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - subareolar area \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - random breast, 8X \u000aSpecimen C labeled "inferior left breast chest wall skin" is received fresh \u000aand consists of a REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm , excised to a depth of 0.7cm  strip of \u000abluish-tan, ink-tinged skin. The specimen is sectioned and entirely submitted \u000ain cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . 3X all. \u000aSpecimen D labeled "left breast, stitch at 6 o'clock" consists of a 154 gram, \u000apiece of breast tissue without skin or nipple. It measures 13 x 10 x 0.8cm  \u000aTwo sutures are present. The suture at the edge is designated "6 o'clock" \u000aand a suture towards the middle of the specimen is superficially designated \u000a"subareolar". The specimen is inked. Multiple sections are largely composed \u000aof fibroglandular tissue with some fat admixed. Sections are taken from the \u000aedges in a clockwise fashion from 12 o'clock, labeled REMOVED_DATE The specimen \u000abeneath the nipple area is labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and random sections are labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aDictated by: RJS/LV____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE (Final) \u000a____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE (Final) \u000a[report_end] 
